                        "file": "27973-subject-2472.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3053\u306e\u3064",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3089-subject-2472.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since all of the \"number of things\" words all follow the same pattern (number plus {span:lang=ja:\u3064}), you really just have to remember the part before the {span:lang=ja:\u3064} (and then remember that the {span:lang=ja:\u3064} is in all of these). All of the readings are the kun'yomi reading, which means we'll have to use a mnemonic to remember them (you know the on'yomi reading of the kanji portion).\n{splitParent}What thing do you have nine of? The {tooltip:Vocabulary:nine things} that you have are nine {tooltip:Reading:coconu}ts ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3053\u306e}). Imagine yourself juggling nine coconuts in the air. Try counting them while you're doing this, arriving at nine things.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u3087\u3046\u306e\u30c6\u30b9\u30c8\u306b\u306f\u3001\u3058\u3057\u3087\u3092\u3064\u304b\u3046\u3082\u3093\u3060\u3044\u304c\u4e5d\u3064\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "There are nine questions that require a dictionary on today\u2019s test."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u306d\u3053\u306b\u306f\u4e5d\u3064\u306e\u3044\u306e\u3061\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3063\u3066\u307b\u3093\u3068\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "Is it true that a cat has nine lives?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c9\u30fc\u30ca\u30c4\u3092\u4e5d\u3064\u3064\u304f\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I made nine donuts."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "As is the case with most vocab words that consist of a single kanji, this vocab word has the same meaning as the kanji it parallels, which is {tooltip:Vocabulary:one}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "One",
                "Word Type": "numeral"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3061"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "27959-subject-2467.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3061",
