                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since all of the \"number of things\" words all follow the same pattern (number plus {span:lang=ja:\u3064}), you really just have to remember the part before the {span:lang=ja:\u3064} (and then remember that the {span:lang=ja:\u3064} is in all of these). All of the readings are the kun'yomi reading, which means we'll have to use a mnemonic to remember them (you know the on'yomi reading of the kanji portion).\n{splitParent}What thing do you have seven of? The {tooltip:Vocabulary:seven things} that you have are seven {tooltip:Reading:Nana}s ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u306a}). These are your grandmas, cloned. Just think, \"It's lucky to have seven nanas. They can all cook my favorite foods for me!\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u306f\u3053\u306e\u306a\u304b\u306b\u308a\u3093\u3054\u304c\u4e03\u3064\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
