                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}When a vocab has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) it is probably going to be the kun'yomi reading. Since you learned the on'yomi reading with the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u5927}, we'll have to use a mnemonic to remember this word.\n{splitParent}When you saw the size of (pick something surprising), you said \"{span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a} *#$@!\" Really imagine something surprising. Say the {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a} part out loud, as well. Think about the size of whatever you're looking at, too, and how big it is.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30c6\u30fc\u30d6\u30eb\u306e\u5927\u304d\u3055\u306f\u3001\u3088\u3053100\u30bb\u30f3\u30c1\u3001\u305f\u3066120\u30bb\u30f3\u30c1\u3067\u3059\u3002",
