                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to use the kun'yomi reading, which you didn't learn with the kanji. Here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to raise something}, and that something is {tooltip:Reading:a}ardvark ({span:lang=ja:\u3042}) above your head. Why? Because even though aardvarks have long tongues, they can't reach the ants in the trees. But when you raise this aardvark it can get at those yummy ants!\n"
