                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine two teams (black and {tooltip:Kanji:white}), wearing their team colors, working really hard on hacking the iPhone. It is a huge contest, and people are watching with a lot of tension, to see who will hack the {tooltip:Kanji:white} iPhone first. Feel that tension, and see the colors separating them so vividly. The colors are important, and the excitement of the winner holding up the {tooltip:Reading:hack}ed iPhone is too.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:white} team was the first to be able to {tooltip:Reading:hack} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u304f}) the {tooltip:Kanji:white} iPhone."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the radical are the same, so remembering the meaning of this kanji is as simple as making sure you know the radical for {tooltip:Radical:writing} first! If you know the radical, you know this kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:writing} as well.",
