                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Words that count days use an exceptional reading. Even though this is a jukugo word, it uses kun'yomi readings for both the kanji. Think about this word this way:\n{splitParent}Every {tooltip:Vocabulary:eighth day} you have to buy {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt to fuel your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046\u304b}). Your car runs on yogurt, but it needs to be refilled every {tooltip:Vocabulary:eight days} to keep running. It's really inconvenient because it's just ONE day more than a week. And a week just feels better. Oh well.\n"
