                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30531-subject-2584.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. {tooltip:Vocabulary:\u76ee\u7389}, however, is an exception. Perhaps this is because it includes a body part (the eye) in it, which often makes a word switch to kun'yomi readings. Either way, it doesn't matter too much. Both the readings you learned for the kanji in this word are the kun'yomi, meaning you should know how to read this one. Just make sure you watch out for the rendaku.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3058\u3083\u304c\u3044\u3082\u3092\u3001\u3086\u304d\u3060\u308b\u307e\u306e\u76ee\u7389\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019ll use these potatoes for the snowman\u2019s eyeballs."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u738b\u5973\u306f\u76ee\u7389\u3092\u30b3\u30ec\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u3059\u308b\u3057\u3085\u307f\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The princess' hobby is to collect eyeballs."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u3046\u304b\u3044\u306e\u76ee\u7389\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u3076\u3069\u3046\u3060\u3068\u304a\u3082\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "I think these grapes look like monster eyeballs."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji {span:lang=ja:\u6708} means both month and moon (because moon cycles take about a month, presumably). So, what is the number two month? It's not January... it's not March... it's {tooltip:Vocabulary:February}!",
