                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Words that count days use an exceptional reading. Even though this is a jukugo word, it uses kun'yomi readings for both the kanji. Think about this word this way:\n{splitParent}On the {tooltip:Vocabulary:fifth day} I have to {tooltip:Reading:eat} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3064}) five {tooltip:Reading:ca}rs ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). Now imagine yourself eating five cars. How did you manage to get past the first one? I'm impressed.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e94\u65e5\u3082\u3057\u3054\u3068\u3092\u3084\u3059\u307f\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I took five days off from work."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u516d\u6708\u4e94\u65e5\u306f\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061\u306e\u305f\u3093\u3058\u3087\u3046\u65e5\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "June 5th is my friend's birthday."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e94\u65e5\u3081\u306b\u3001\u300c\u3053\u308c\u3067\u304a\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3002\u300d\u3068\u3044\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "On the fifth day I said, \"That's it!\""
                }
            ],
