{
            "mnemonic": "Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana stuck in the middle you can guess that it is like putting two separate words that you've learned together into one word. This hiragana is {span:lang=ja:\u306e}, a particle that makes something possessive. In this case, the {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} is of the {span:lang=ja:\u5973}. Basically, this suggests that the woman is a child, aka a {tooltip:Vocabulary:girl}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Girl",
                "Alternatives": "Young Girl, Young Lady, Young Woman",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3093\u306a\u306e\u3053"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3093\u306a\u306e\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21259-subject-2512.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3093\u306a\u306e\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30542-subject-2512.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since there's hiragana in here, you can bet that these kanji will use the kun'yomi readings. You already know the kun'yomi reading for {tooltip:Vocabulary:\u5973}. The only thing I have to make sure that you know is {span:lang=ja:\u5b50}. When you need to remember the kun'yomi reading of {span:lang=ja:\u5b50}, just think about you fighting a child (you're a jerk, apparently!). When you hit him in the face, he flies to the floor, and the ref calls out \"{tooltip:Reading:KO}!\" because you just knocked the poor kid out.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ea\u30dc\u30f3\u3092\u3064\u3051\u3066\u3044\u308b\u5973\u306e\u5b50\u304c\u306f\u306a\u5b50\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The girl wearing the ribbon is Hanako."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3068\u3066\u3082\u304b\u308f\u3044\u3044\u5973\u306e\u5b50\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "She is such a cute girl, isn't she?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u307c\u304f\u306e\u306f\u3064\u3053\u3044\u306e\u5973\u306e\u5b50\u306f\u3001\u306b\u3093\u3058\u3093\u304c\u304d\u3089\u3044\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The girl who was my first love didn\u2019t like carrots."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

