                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it uses the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word:\n{splitParent}You see a child and walk up to him. Then, you punch him in the face (oh no, how could you!!?). He flies through the air, and he's knocked out. A ref nearby yells that it was a \"{tooltip:Reading:KO}!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3053}). That's a knock out.\n{splitParent}Make sure you learn this reading pretty well too. Both readings for {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} are going to show up a lot, and this is how you're going to learn the kun'yomi one.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u3001\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u307b\u3093\u3068\u3046\u306e\u5b50\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "You aren\u2019t my real child."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u30ed\u30b7\u30a2\u4eba\u306e\u5b50\u306f\u3001\u5927\u4eba\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3001\u3055\u3051\u3088\u308a\u3082\u4e0a\u624b\u306b\u5ddd\u3092\u4e0a\u308c\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "When that Russian kid grew up she got better than a salmon at swimming upstream."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u5b50\u3001\u30d3\u30e8\u30f3\u30bb\u306b\u306b\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u304a\u3082\u308f\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "Don\u2019t you think my kid looks similar to Beyonc\u00e9?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

