                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21244-subject-2542.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word:\n{splitParent}Look up at that big, bright moon. You have to open it up and take what's inside. To do that, you are required to have {tooltip:Reading:two key}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304d}), and they have to be turned at the same time. Imagine you and a friend both turning your keys on opposite sides of the moon to open up the center.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3093\u3084\u306f\u6708\u304c\u304d\u308c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "The moon is beautiful tonight."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u3082\u305d\u306e\u6708\u306b\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u304d\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I also came to Japan that month."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d4\u30f3\u30af\u306e\u6708\u304c\u51fa\u305f\u3089\u3001\u51fa\u3071\u3064\u306e\u3042\u3044\u305a\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "If the pink moon comes out, that\u2019s our signal to leave."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
