                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Words that count days use an exceptional reading. Even though this is a jukugo word, it uses kun'yomi readings for both of the kanji. You learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4e5d} when you learned {span:lang=ja:\u4e5d\u3064}, so you should be able to read this one too!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e5d\u65e5\u306b\u3001\u3044\u3063\u3057\u3087\u306b\u30b5\u30c3\u30ab\u30fc\u3092\u307f\u306b\u3044\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Would you like to go watch some soccer with me on the ninth?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u4e5d\u65e5\u3082\u30cb\u30c3\u30ab\u306b\u3042\u3063\u3066\u3044\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u3055\u3073\u3057\u304f\u3066\u3057\u306b\u305d\u3046\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "Since Koichi hasn't seen Nikka for nine days, he feels so lonely he could die."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30df\u306e\u305f\u3093\u3058\u3087\u3046\u65e5\u306f\u56db\u6708\u4e5d\u65e5\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "Mami\u2019s birthday is April ninth."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji for \"moon\" and \"month\" are the same, probably because a moon cycle takes approximately a month to occur. So, what is the tenth moon cycle of the year? That would be the awesome month {tooltip:Vocabulary:October}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "October",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
