                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Even though this is a jukugo word, it doesn't use the on'yomi readings. Both the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} and {span:lang=ja:\u72ac} often favor kun'yomi readings, and this word is no exception. The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u72ac} is the one you already know, and the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} as {span:lang=ja:\u3053} is a really common one (perhaps you've already learned that reading?). If not, just think about punching a puppy in the face, and giving it a {tooltip:Reading:KO} (That's a knock out).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3051\u3055\u3001\u5b50\u72ac\u304c\u3046\u307e\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The puppies were born this morning."
                },
                {
