                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it uses the kun'yomi reading. Here's a mnemonic to help you to remember it: \n{splitParent}You look through the soil. You're trying to find something. As you dig and sift, you come across not one but {tooltip:Reading:two chee}ses ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3061}). Pull them out of the ground and put them in your mouth. How do the two cheeses taste and compare?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
