                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "27922-subject-2492.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}{span:lang=ja:\u4e0a\u308b} consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, so it will use the kun'yomi reading of the kanji. For {span:lang=ja:\u4e0a}, there are multiple kun'yomi readings, and you didn't learn this one yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to climb} the mountain, but a gruff old man grabs your shoulder and says \"{tooltip:Reading:No bo}y, you ain't climbing that thing, not today.\" If you're not a boy, think about how weird it is that he called you a boy. If you are a grown man, think how you wish he called you \"dude\" or something, not \"boy.\" If you're a boy, well... think about how appropriate it is that he said \"no boy.\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u304c\u3084\u306d\u306b\u4e0a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "I can go up to the roof."
