                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}After you correct something for someone, you yell out {tooltip:Reading:ta da} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3060}) very excitedly. Go ahead and imagine yourself doing this a few times to help you to remember.\n"
