                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You want to exit the room you're in. Why? Because it has a {tooltip:Reading:de}ad ({span:lang=ja:\u3067}) body in it. Seriously. You should exit now. It's a {tooltip:Reading:de}ad ({span:lang=ja:\u3067}) {tooltip:Reading:roo}m ({span:lang=ja:\u308b})!\n"
