            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "White",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u308d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u308d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21304-subject-2581.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u308d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30446-subject-2581.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word:\n{splitParent}{tooltip:Vocabulary:White} surrounds you. The {tooltip:Reading:sheer} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u308d}) amount of white is overwhelming.  \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c6\u30fc\u30d6\u30eb\u306b\u3001\u767d\u306e\u304a\u3055\u3089\u3092\u306a\u3089\u3079\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Can you put the white dishes on the table?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e03\u3064\u306e\u77f3\u306e\u3046\u3061\u3001\u4e09\u3064\u306f\u767d\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Three out of seven stones were white."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u304a\u3068\u3053\u306f\u3001\u3086\u304d\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u767d\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u767d\u3086\u304d\u304a\u3068\u3053\u3068\u306a\u3065\u3051\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The man was as white as snow, so he was named \"Snow White.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Writing",
                "Alternative": "Sentence",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3076\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3076\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30459-subject-2540.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3076\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21238-subject-2540.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses one of the readings you learned for the kanji: {span:lang=ja:\u3076\u3093}. You can remember this by thinking how whenever you're working on your writing, you get hungry and want to eat a {tooltip:Reading:bun}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u306f\u3084\u304f\u6587\u3092\u3088\u3093\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please read the sentence faster."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u3069\u308d\u3044\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3001\u305d\u306e\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4eba\u306e\u6587\u306f\u30a4\u30ae\u30ea\u30b9\u4eba\u306e\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u6587\u3088\u308a\u3048\u3044\u3054\u304c\u4e0a\u624b\u306b\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "To my surprise, that American's English writing was written better than mine, and I'm British."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u306a\u3057\u3044\u6587\u3092\u3088\u3080\u3068\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u306a\u307f\u3060\u304c\u4e8c\u3075\u3093\u4e8c\u5341\u3073\u3087\u3046\u3060\u3051\u3068\u307e\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Whenever I read a sad story I can\u2019t stop crying for exactly two minutes and twenty seconds."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Although this word consists of one kanji that is all alone, it doesn't share its meaning with the parent kanji. The meanings are similar in a way, though. This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:years old} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:age}. With more years comes more {tooltip:Kanji:genius}, right? That's why this word means \"years old\" and not \"genius,\" like the parent kanji. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Years Old",
                "Alternative": "Age",
                "Word Type": "suffix"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3055\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30460-subject-2519.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3055\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20721-subject-2519.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the one you learned for the kanji, meaning you should already know it! Don't try to type the {span:lang=ja:\u301c} part though.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u4e94\u624d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I am five years old."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3089\u3044\u6708\u4e8c\u65e5\u306b\u3001\u516d\u5341\u4e03\u624d\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'll turn 67 on the 2nd of the next month."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3061\u3061\u306e\u4e94\u5341\u4e94\u624d\u306e\u305f\u3093\u3058\u3087\u3046\u65e5\u306b\u3001\u30db\u30b0\u30ef\u30fc\u30c4\u3078\u3057\u3087\u3046\u305f\u3044\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "On my dad\u2019s fifty-fifth birthday, I was invited to Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a really big gun. Why? Because only big guns will be able to shoot {tooltip:Radical:arrow}s! Bullets are pretty small, so the guns that shoot them can be any size. But you need a big gun if you want to shove an arrow in it and then shoot it at your enemies.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Arrow"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a {tooltip:Radical:canopy}. See the cloth draping down and the little point at the middle holding it up? You could sit under here and enjoy a bright, summer day without getting any sun!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Canopy"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks like a dude running off to the right. He's heading in a very distinct {tooltip:Radical:direction}. Which direction was it again?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Direction"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Where does a flag usually go? It goes over a {tooltip:Radical:door}. I know the {span:lang=ja:\u4e00} radical usually means ground, but in this case we're going to say the flag is in the doorway (where the {span:lang=ja:\u4e00} is the top of the door).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Door"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have two on a stick. Two what? Well, you can't tell because they're too {tooltip:Radical:dry}. Someone put two somethings on this stick to dry, but they seem to have left them out for way too long. Was it meat? Fish? Cucumbers? You have no clue, but they're two very dry somethings, that's for sure.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dry"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are fins covering the treasure making up this radical. You pull away the fins and start digging where the X is (because \"X\" marks where the treasure is, right?). When you dig down, instead of finding treasure, you find your {tooltip:Radical:father}. The shock of this in your imagination should help you to remember the meaning of this radical!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Father"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This looks like the hand ({span:lang=ja:\u624b}) radical, but smaller. That's because it's just the {tooltip:Radical:fingers}. You don't always have room for a whole hand to be in a kanji, but there's always space for a few fingers.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fingers"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Do you remember the hair radical? This is like that, except now the hair is attached to a tail. Animals don't usually have hair, though. Instead, they have {tooltip:Radical:fur}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fur"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Do you know those rice paddy hats? The ones shaped just like this radical? That's why this radical is a {tooltip:Radical:hat}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hat"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take a good look at this one. It kind of looks like a {tooltip:Radical:heart} (not the stereotypical Valentine\u2019s Day heart, though). Think of a real heart. Basically, there\u2019s a lump (the heart) in the middle, and three lines which make up the arteries that go in and out of the heart to keep you alive. This radical shows up a lot, so it shouldn\u2019t be too hard to learn it as you go along. Remember, lump (heart) plus arteries equals a heart\u2026 like, a real heart, not the fake, pretty kind.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Heart"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical consists of a cow radical with the ground radical below it. If you have cows on solid ground, then you really do have a good {tooltip:Radical:life}, I think. Sometimes this radical will show up without the slide part on the side too, though we'll treat them both as \"life.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Life"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a hat on top of the katakana for \"ra.\" Think of Ra, the Egyptian god. When is Ra wearing a hat? Right {tooltip:Radical:now}! It's always now, because he never takes it off. No really, look it up, it's true.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Now"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a cross on a mouth\u2014that's a pretty religious mouth. Who speaks the most about religion? {tooltip:Radical:Old} people, mostly. Also, think about the teachings of religion itself - also pretty old, age-wise. No matter how you look at it, everything about this radical is kind of \"old.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Old"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have two legs making up this radical. Between two legs is where you came from, no matter how you look at it. These two legs are your {tooltip:Radical:origin}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Origin"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's something sticking out of you while you're in private. It's {tooltip:Radical:poop}! You can't just poop in public, that's illegal and gross in this day and age. So the next time something starts to come out of you when you're in private, think, \"Ah yes, it's poop.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Poop"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks like a {tooltip:Radical:spoon}! Well, a spoon that's been bent a lot by an angry person or a psychic. Go grab a spoon and try to bend it into this shape. Then hold on to it so you'll never forget that this is the spoon radical!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Spoon"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This looks a bit like a calendar with spaces for you to write in your {tooltip:Radical:task}s for the day. See those blank sections? Make sure you write down your daily tasks, so you don't forget to do something important!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Task"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's something draped over that stick. It's a {tooltip:Radical:towel!}! Imagine taking a wet towel and hanging it over a railing or a stick so it won't get all musty and gross. It would look just like this.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Towel"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The three horns represent the {tooltip:Radical:triceratops}, one of the most awesome dinosaurs ever.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Triceratops"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks like the evening radical but has an extra long stroke. That's because evenings are long in the {tooltip:Radical:winter}. It gets dark super early.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Winter"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:arrow} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:arrow} kanji are the same. Sort of a \"straight\" shot to memorizing this kanji, you know?",
            "hints": "Just know your radicals and you'll know this kanji!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Arrow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the arrow as a human-sized living thing with legs, arms, and clothes, though. Strangely, it\u2019s able to walk around even though it's an arrow. It has some kind of agenda. Make it a bit evil, if you can. What a strange thing\u2026",
                "mnemonic": "To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3084} we use the word \u201cYankees\u201d (like the evil baseball team, go M\u2019s!)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You lift the {tooltip:Radical:lid} off a manhole and there's a {tooltip:Radical:towel} with the name of a {tooltip:Kanji:city} on it.",
            "hints": "Picture this towel with the name of a city on it. Any city you like. Maybe it's your city!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "City"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a city that has a sheep for its mascot. This city was built on sheep, don't you say a bad word about sheep when you're there.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:city} must have a lot of {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) because there is a sheep monogram on the towel. It's the sheep city."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:cow} are exactly the same! That makes it easy to remember, so long as you know your radicals well enough.",
            "hints": "The radicals are important to know, so make sure you're studying them. They'll come back again, you know!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I hope you know what {span:lang=ja:\u308f\u304e\u3085\u3046} beef is, otherwise this will be a difficult one to learn.",
                "mnemonic": "Have you ever heard of {span:lang=ja:\u308f\u304e\u3085\u3046} beef? That {span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3085\u3046} is this {span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3085\u3046}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you have {tooltip:Radical:seven} {tooltip:Radical:swords}, there's only so much you can do with them. The main thing? Probably using them to {tooltip:Kanji:cut} something.",
            "hints": "Take these seven swords and swing them around. {tooltip:Kanji:Cut} everything in your path, including yourself. Then, think about how dumb it was to try to use seven swords at once, and then feel the pain of the cut you gave yourself. Ouch, ouch ouch.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cut"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Just make sure you think about how you need to give them away in {tooltip:Reading:sets}, and not anything else. This is the most important thing to think about in your head as you're trying to establish the mnemonic for your kanji reading memory. It's gotta be sets.",
                "mnemonic": "Because having seven swords for yourself is too much, you decide to take the swords and divide them up amongst pairs of people. You {tooltip:Kanji:cut} them into pairs, and give {tooltip:Reading:sets} ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3064}) to everyone who needs them in the village."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:direction} are the same! Huzzah!",
            "hints": "The only direction you need to go in is forward, it's always the right way.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Direction",
                "Alternative": "Way"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Close your eyes and picture your home in your mind. Can you tell which direction it is from where you are?",
                "mnemonic": "What {tooltip:Kanji:direction} do you always know? Which direction do you always want to go? {tooltip:Reading:Ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}). Something about your home always stays with you, no matter how far away you go. So if you're lost and you don't know which direction to go, just think of home!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:door} are the same!",
            "hints": "Time to open the door to the reading part of this mnemonic.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Door"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel the pain of your toe going away. Think about the other side of the {tooltip:Kanji:door}, where your {tooltip:Reading:toe} is probably rolling around after it blasted off your foot.",
                "mnemonic": "You open the {tooltip:Kanji:door} and immediately get it closed back on your {tooltip:Reading:toe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068}), literally causing your toe to explode. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:big} guy here, with an extra {tooltip:Radical:drop} of something below his thigh, hanging down. That's {tooltip:Kanji:fat} right there. He's so fat he has things of fat hanging off his fat.",
            "hints": "Maybe you should touch the {tooltip:Kanji:fat} below his leg just to see what it is... feel it, and squeeze it. It'll help you to remember that this kanji means \"fat.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fat"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3044, \u305f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine him trying to tie the {tooltip:Reading:tie} but he can't lift his hands around to do it. You have to help him out. Another thing that might help you to remember this kanji's reading is that it's the same reading as {span:lang=ja:\u5927} (or, one of the same readings). Similar kanji often have similar readings, which is a good thing to know when you have to guess (it's true with this one, anyways!).",
                "mnemonic": "This poor {tooltip:Kanji:fat} guy has trouble with a lot of things. One of the things he has the most trouble with is tying a {tooltip:Reading:tie} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3044})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:father} are the same.",
            "hints": "No, I am not your father... but this kanji / radical set is!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Father",
                "Alternative": "Dad"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3061, \u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hopefully you know who they are. If not, think about your father laughing like this: {span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3061\u3061\u3061\u3061\u3061\u3061\u3061\u301c\uff01}",
                "mnemonic": "Imagine your father is {tooltip:Reading:Cheech} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3061}) from Cheech and Chong."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:small} {tooltip:Radical:slide}. The thing about small slides is that they can only fit a {tooltip:Kanji:few} people at a time.",
            "hints": "Imagine a small slide (how could you not, after you see the radicals?) with only a few people on it, trying to move forward. Only a few people are required to create a slide traffic jam, though. :(",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Few",
                "Alternative": "A Little"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3053, \u3059\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine this in your head. A traffic jam on a little slide, all because the shogun is using it. Picture some caution tape, orange cones, and Japanese secret service members all making sure no one gets close to the shougun while he slides. A few people are crying. They want to slide, they want to leave.",
                "mnemonic": "Why is there {tooltip:Kanji:a little} traffic jam on the slide? Because the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) is using the slide and he loves little things. He's forcing everyone to stop and watch, even though there are people backed up behind him. How inconsiderate."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:narwhal} sitting on a {tooltip:Radical:stool} is your {tooltip:Kanji:friend}.",
            "hints": "Imagine that narwhal sitting there. It waves its flipper and says \"hi friend\" to you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Friend"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3082",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your narwhal friend goes on to warn you about all those youths, and how they will try to take away your friendship with their good looks and young ages.",
                "mnemonic": "\"Hi {tooltip:Kanji:friend},\" says the narwhal. \"I must warn you about all the {tooltip:Reading:you}ths.\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3046})"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Fur} and {tooltip:Radical:fur} are the same as each other, so the meaning of this kanji should be simple. This can also mean {tooltip:Kanji:hair}, too, though more like furry hair.",
            "hints": "Just make sure you're studying your radicals, otherwise it won't be as simple as I'd hoped.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fur",
                "Alternative": "Hair"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Smell the {tooltip:Kanji:fur} as you {tooltip:Reading:mow} it down. Feel it flying everywhere. It's giant, so it must be pretty intense. Make it more intense to help yourself to remember the reading of this kanji better.",
                "mnemonic": "With {tooltip:Kanji:fur}, wisp your imagination to a land where there are stalks of fur all around, just like a big tall grassy field (except instead of grass, it\u2019s fur). You\u2019re surrounded by the black fur, the wind is blowing. Imagine yourself touching the long fur and smelling it. What does it feel / smell like? Now it\u2019s time to get rid of it. There\u2019s just too much {tooltip:Kanji:hair}! To get rid of it, you\u2019ll need to {tooltip:Reading:mow} ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3046}) it down with a lawn mower. Imagine yourself starting up the lawn mower, and taking it around, mowing down the hair. Hear the sound of the mower in your head (they\u2019re loud and distinct). The important thing is to imagine yourself mowing everything. Key is to think \u201cfur \u2192 In the fur \u2192 getting rid of the fur \u2192 mow the fur,\u201d in that order. That\u2019ll get you to mow, which will help you to remember the on\u2019yomi."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} is laying out to {tooltip:Radical:dry}. But it's so big, and it's laying on its side, so only {tooltip:Kanji:half} of it gets dry.",
            "hints": "Imagine the triceratops on its side, then imagine it getting up. When it stands up normally, half of its body is soaking wet still. It's a half-n-half triceratops right now.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Half"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine him using his blaster to shoot the poor triceratops in half, perfectly down the wet-dry line of its body.",
                "mnemonic": "\"You're half wet and half dry! I will cut you in {tooltip:Kanji:half} with my laser blaster so you're proper again,\" a voice says. It is  {tooltip:Reading:Han} Solo ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}), the anti-establishment guy who hates when things aren't even."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:heart} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:heart} are the same. Rejoice and let your heart be free!",
            "hints": "Also, make sure you know the radicals by heart, it'll help you to learn more effectively, just like with this kanji.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Heart"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3053\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This is when I start kicking you in the shin and you imagine feeling the pain of getting kicked there. As I kick you in the shin, you grab your chest... all this stress is giving you a heart attack (though your shin hurts a ton too).",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:heart}, where is it stored in your body? Most people thought it was in the chest, but in reality, your {tooltip:Kanji:heart} is stored in your {tooltip:Reading:shin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:person} {tooltip:Kanji:inside} your {tooltip:Radical:head}.",
            "hints": "And, you have no idea how to get them out. They're {tooltip:Kanji:inside} for good, and it's freaking you out. As in, there's a little person in there, running around, controlling your brain. People think you're crazy, but you know better... He's {tooltip:Kanji:inside} there, doing evil things.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Inside",
                "Alternative": "Within"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine him holding the knife out, threatening to stab your brain. You\u2019re in a conundrum here. If you don\u2019t take him out, you\u2019re in trouble, but if you do try to take him out, he might stab you in the brain with his knife. Try to think a way around this situation, focusing mainly on his knife.",
                "mnemonic": "You know this kanji means inside, so you can keep thinking about the person that\u2019s inside you, running around. You finally discover him, and try to take him out, but before you can, he pulls out a {tooltip:Reading:kni}fe ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3044}) and threatens to cut you if you do anything irrational."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:life} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:life} kanji are the same, so hopefully you now just know them both.",
            "hints": "Study your radicals and you'll read good.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Life"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044, \u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044, \u306a\u307e, \u3046, \u306f, \u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine having someone's life in the palm of your hands. It's up to you whether you protect it with your saber or... well... do the other thing sabers are for.",
                "mnemonic": "You can save {tooltip:Kanji:life} or take it away with your new {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}). This is the saber you got from doing the correct thing (remember?), and now you need to figure out how to use it with this life. So what do you do?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:private} {tooltip:Radical:mouth} that's a {tooltip:Kanji:machine}. But you have to keep your machine mouth private because it would scare all the non-machine people around you.",
            "hints": "Doesn't this kanji look like a machine mouth? Now wouldn't you want to keep that private from the people you know?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Machine"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u3044, \u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being so afraid that people will find out about your machine mouth that you have to dye it to match a normal human mouth. Oh, when will this discrimination against machine-kind end?!",
                "mnemonic": "To make sure they can't tell what's {tooltip:Kanji:machine} and what's human, you {tooltip:Reading:dye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3060\u3044}) the mouth to make it look like skin. You find dye the same shade as your normal mouth and just slap it on there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} lets out one {tooltip:Radical:drop}, and then another {tooltip:Radical:drop}. The drops dance together in the air, combine, and when they hit the ground, up sprouts your {tooltip:Kanji:mother}!",
            "hints": "Picture these two drops of the sun morphing before your very eyes until they look exactly like your dear ol' mum. She's bright and shining like the sun, and she's looking down at you, her big drop-eyes full of tears.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mother",
                "Alternative": "Mom"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u306f, \u304b\u3042",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You thought your mother was going to say something sweet or profound or motherly, and instead she's pointing and saying, \"Haha,\" over and over.{splitParent}Yeah. That sounds like my mom.",
                "mnemonic": "Suddenly your {tooltip:Kanji:mother} points at you and laughs, \"{tooltip:Reading:Haha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u306f})!\" She keeps laughing, haha haha haha, over and over. You start to feel uncomfortable."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:slide} is {tooltip:Radical:dry} at {tooltip:Kanji:noon}. The sun is brightest at noon, so it dries the morning dew off the slide, making noon the perfect time to slide.",
            "hints": "Picture all the kids out sliding on the slide at noon during their lunch break. It's hot and dry and they're very happy.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Noon"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054",
