                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Genji's origin story is pretty important when it comes to mnemonics and Japanese literature. He's going to keep popping up on your kanji journey, so make sure you remember him!",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:origin} of everything can be found in {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}). Genji is the name of the main character in the world's first ever novel, \"The Tale of Genji.\" "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're known to get the ailment {tooltip:Radical:evening} {tooltip:Radical:toe}, which is when your toe catches on fire after getting really, really hot (imagine this happening, ouch!). The only way to fix it is to cool your toe down, and the best way to do that is to go {tooltip:Kanji:outside}.",
            "hints": "After imagining your {tooltip:Radical:evening} {tooltip:Radical:toe} overheating, rush {tooltip:Kanji:outside} to fix it. It's the best way to prevent fire toe, which is way worse. In the evening it's nice and cold outside too, so feel this on your skin, and feel the cold air on your toe, which is starting to get some relief.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Outside"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3068, \u306f\u305a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you don\u2019t know Guy Fawkes, you should do a little reading up on him to make this mnemonic make sense. Also, Anonymous People wear a Guy Fawkes mask, if that helps any.",
                "mnemonic": "You go {tooltip:Kanji:outside} (you\u2019re not supposed to be out there at night!) and you\u2019re accosted by a couple of guys. Then, all of a sudden, {tooltip:Reading:Guy} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3044}) Fawkes jumps from the roof above you and takes them out, then starts running. \u201cGuy Fawkes!\u201d you yell after him!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:fins} that fell onto my {tooltip:Radical:sword} were sliced into two {tooltip:Kanji:part}s.",
            "hints": "The logic of this story makes a lot of sense - even in the kanji itself the fins are falling onto the sword from above. What happens to things that fall onto swords? They become more than one {tooltip:Kanji:part}.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Part",
                "Alternatives": "Minute, Separate, Understand"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3076\u3093, \u3075\u3093, \u3076",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Think about the {tooltip:Reading:bun}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3076\u3093}) as absolutely delicious things you want to eat really bad. If you want to eat the buns, and you taste the buns in your imagination, you'll surely remember that the reading for this kanji is {span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3093} as well.",
                "mnemonic": "Now that you've cut the fish, it's time to cut something else into {tooltip:Kanji:part}s. Next on your list is the {tooltip:Reading:bun}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3076\u3093}) which need to be split up amongst the people. If you'd like to learn the second reading, just think about how {tooltip:Reading:fun} ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3093}) it will be to do this task."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have {tooltip:Radical:fins} in {tooltip:Radical:private}. But, you want the world to see them, so you take them {tooltip:Kanji:public}.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself in private, with fins. You wish others could see them. \"That's it,\" you decide. \"It's time to show the world. I'm going to make my fins public!\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Public"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Remember, whenever we see the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046}, think of {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, a founder of WaniKani. We'll keep it consistent, so over time you should develop a character around {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} that you learn to love or hate.{splitParent}How long have you been hiding in private with your fins? The public areas have changed, and all the people have become {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s. One mother {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}--pushing a baby {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}--looks up and stares at your fins. Now you remember why you never go out in public.",
                "mnemonic": "You head out into the {tooltip:Kanji:public} where everyone can see your fins, but... things have changed. All people are the same. There are thousands of {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s walking around, and they all stare at you (though they pretend like they aren't)."
            }
        }

{
