                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u3053\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32951-subject-2607.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Did you know that this word created an English word you probably already know? Have you ever heard someone say \"just a skosh\"? That's {tooltip:Vocabulary:\u5c11\u3057}! Hopefully you know this English word and therefore know this Japanese word as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304e\u3085\u3046\u306b\u3085\u3046\u306f\u3001\u5c11\u3057\u3057\u304b\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "There is only little milk."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c11\u3057\u3057\u304b\u306e\u3053\u3063\u3066\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "There are only a few left."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u306e\u30d7\u30ed\u30dd\u30fc\u30ba\u306f\u5c11\u3057\u3042\u3044\u307e\u3044\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "His proposal was a little vague."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {span:lang=ja:\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab} part is pretty easy so long as you know katakana. It's the word for \"America.\" You know that {tooltip:Kanji:\u4eba} means \"person,\" so you can figure out that America + Person = {tooltip:Vocabulary:American}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "American",
                "Alternative": "American Person",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3081\u308a\u304b\u3058\u3093"
                    },
                    {
                        "primary": false,
                        "reading": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u3058\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3081\u308a\u304b\u3058\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3154-subject-2478.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3081\u308a\u304b\u3058\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "27989-subject-2478.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Often times when two kanji come together to form a combo kanji you use the on'yomi readings. This is similar to that, though instead of another kanji it's a foreign word. So, the reading of {span:lang=ja:\u4eba} is the on'yomi reading {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093}, which you learned already in the kanji. This pattern works with almost any location as well. Just add a country name + {span:lang=ja:\u4eba} and you've described the people who live there. You'll see more of these before you're finished here.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u308c\u306f\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4eba\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Am I American?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4eba\u304c\u4e8c\u4eba\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "There are two American people."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4eba\u306e\u5973\u3068\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I made friends with an American girl."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

