                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32800-subject-2619.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it uses the kun'yomi reading. Here's a mnemonic to help you to remember it: \n{splitParent}You're leading the cows around the field. To get them to move, you yell out \"{tooltip:Reading:USH}, USH, USH!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3057}) because you have a speech impediment and want to say \"MUSH MUSH MUSH.\" Go ahead and say this out loud, yelling it if you can.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3053\u3055\u3093\u306f\u725b\u3092\u304b\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3089\u3057\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Apparently Kyoko is raising a cow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c7\u30a4\u30d6\u306f\u3001\u725b\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Dave is a cow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u306e\u5973\u306f\u3001\u725b\u304c\u3089\u306e\u30c9\u30ec\u30b9\u3092\u304d\u3066\u3001\u725b\u3069\u3093\u3084\u306b\u884c\u3063\u3066\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "She came to a gyudon restaurant in a cow-spot patterned dress."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Do you remember the words {span:lang=ja:\u51fa\u53e3} (exit) and {span:lang=ja:\u5165\u308a\u53e3} (entrance) from previous levels? The {span:lang=ja:\u53e3} can be a doorway of some kind. This word is literally \"door mouth\" but I bet you can figure out that this actually means {tooltip:Vocabulary:doorway}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Doorway",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3050\u3061"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3050\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "12976-subject-2611.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3050\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32890-subject-2611.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this one is mixed. You get the kun'yomi readings for both kanji, even though it's a combo (jukugo) kanji. Since {span:lang=ja:\u6238}'s only reading is the kun'yomi reading you should know it. Also, you should know the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u53e3} as well from level 1. That means as long as you remember that this is a kun'yomi fest over here, you should be able to read this word. Also watch out for the rendaku (also known as sequential voicing). That just means the {span:lang=ja:\u304f} becomes the voiced {span:lang=ja:\u3050}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6238\u53e3\u306b\u624b\u3076\u304f\u308d\u304c\u304a\u3061\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "A glove was dropped in the doorway."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305f\u307e\u305f\u307e\u3001\u6238\u53e3\u3067\u306c\u3059\u307f\u304e\u304d\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I  eavesdropped it at the doorway by accident."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6238\u53e3\u306b\u4e09\u679a\u306e\u30c8\u30fc\u30b9\u30c8\u304c\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "There were three pieces of toast in my doorway."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u5c71} means mountain. Add the hiragana {span:lang=ja:\u3073\u3053} to the end and this gives you {tooltip:Vocabulary:echo}. That's because bee children (bee {span:lang=ja:\u5b50}) love echos, especially {tooltip:Vocabulary:mountain echo}s! Imagine baby bees buzzing as loudly as they can and hearing their voices echoing back at them through the mountains.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Echo",
                "Alternative": "Mountain Echo",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3084\u307e\u3073\u3053"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u307e\u3073\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "44138-subject-8957.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u307e\u3073\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "43676-subject-8957.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You learned this kanji reading when you learned the vocabulary {span:lang=ja:\u5c71}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c71\u3073\u3053\u304c\u805e\u3053\u3048\u308b\uff01",
                    "en": "I can hear an echo!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c71\u3073\u3053\u304c\u3072\u3073\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The echos reverberated."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30e4\u30c3\u30db\u30fc\u300d\u3068\u8a00\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u300c\u30e4\u30c3\u30db\u30fc\u300d\u3068\u5c71\u3073\u3053\u304c\u8fd4\u3063\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I said \"yoo-hoo\" and \"yoo-hoo\" came echoing back at me."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji {tooltip:Kanji:\u5916} alone means \"outside.\" This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:extremity}. How can you remember this? Just think of the {span:lang=ja:\u308c} as a \"ray of sunshine.\" Where you are, in the extremity of space, even the {span:lang=ja:\u308c}s of the sun cannot be seen. So, when {span:lang=ja:\u5916} is combined with {span:lang=ja:\u308c} just think of this.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Extremity",
                "Alternatives": "Furthest Point, End, Outskirts, Outer Limits, Edge, Miss, Failure",
                "Word Type": "noun, suffix"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u305a\u308c"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u305a\u308c",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "12908-subject-2633.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u305a\u308c",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32814-subject-2633.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Let's continue the previous story: You're off in the {tooltip:Vocabulary:extremity} of space and your friend is running low on Vitamin D. He {tooltip:Reading:has} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u305a}) to get some sun {span:lang=ja:\u308c}s on his skin! How's that supposed to happen with those spacesuits on, though?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u306f\u307e\u3061\u5916\u308c\u306e\u5c0f\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3048\u306b\u3059\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "He lives in a small house in the outskirts of town."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u738b\u5973\u306f\u3001\u304d\u305b\u3064\u5916\u308c\u306e\u30c9\u30ec\u30b9\u3092\u304d\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The princess was wearing a dress that doesn't suit the season."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3042\u305f\u308a\u304c\u51fa\u308b\u3068\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u672c\u300d\u3068\u304b\u304b\u308c\u305f\u30a2\u30a4\u30b9\u3092\u304b\u3063\u305f\u304c\u3001\u305c\u3093\u3076\u5916\u308c\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I bought some ice cream that had, \"If you hit, you get another\" written on them, but they were all misses."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of the {tooltip:Kanji:fat}? It's the same: {tooltip:Vocabulary:fat}.",
