{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. This is the polite and humble form of {tooltip:Vocabulary:father}. You use this when you're talking about your own father to other people, especially if you aren't very close to them.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Father",
                "Alternative": "Dad",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
