{
            "mnemonic": "This word begins with an honorific ({span:lang=ja:\u304a}), making whatever comes after it more elevated. Then there's {span:lang=ja:\u7236}, which you know means {tooltip:Kanji:father}. Lastly, we have the honorific name ender {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093}. So this is a nice way to say {tooltip:Vocabulary:father}. You use it when you're talking to your own {tooltip:Vocabulary:dad} or talking about him with friends. You can also use this when you're talking about your friends' dads.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Father",
                "Alternatives": "Dad, Papa",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3068\u3046\u3055\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3068\u3046\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "13009-subject-2618.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3068\u3046\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32884-subject-2618.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The part you have to learn to read is the {span:lang=ja:\u7236} portion. This uses the kun'yomi, which you didn't learn when doing the kanji. \n{splitParent}Imagine you are taking your venerable {tooltip:Vocabulary:father} to {tooltip:Reading:\u3068\u3046}\u304d\u3087\u3046. He's always wanted to go and this is the trip of a lifetime! Imagine walking through the streets of Tokyo with your Dad, taking in all the sights.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u306f\u307e\u3044\u65e5\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u305f\u3079\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My father eats an apple every day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u306b\u3060\u3063\u3066\u5206\u304b\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Even your father has something he doesn't understand."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u306e\u306d\u3053\u306f\u304b\u308f\u3044\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "My dad\u2019s cat is adorable."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
