                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You can treat this word and the {span:lang=ja:\u4eba} kanji on the end like jukugo (combo kanji). Usually, in the case of jukugo, you use the on'yomi reading. So here you'll want to remember to use the on'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4eba}. If you want, you can add {span:lang=ja:\u4eba} to the end of any place name to describe the people that live there!\n"
            },
