                    "en": "My younger sister is getting to look like our mother more and more."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bcd\u306f\u3068\u3046\u3075\u3068\u3075\u3050\u304c\u3059\u304d\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "My mother likes tofu and fugu."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word starts with {span:lang=ja:\u304a} which makes it more polite. Then, there's the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:\u6bcd} which you know means mother. Last, there's the honorific {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093} which further adds respect (to the mother). So, this is the nice way to say {tooltip:Vocabulary:mother}. You use it when you're talking to your own {tooltip:Vocabulary:mom} or talking about her with friends. You can also use this when you're talking about your friends' moms.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mother",
                "Alternative": "Mom",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
