                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it uses the kun'yomi reading. You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3042} portion. Here's a mnemonic to help you to remember it: \n{splitParent}What does your super nice {tooltip:Vocabulary:mother} do for you (this is why you're so polite to her!)? She drives you all around in her {tooltip:Reading:car} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3042}) taking you wherever you need to go... soccer, kendo, whatever. What a nice mother you have!\n\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u306f\u3069\u3053\uff1f",
                    "en": "Where\u2019s mom?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3072\u3053\u3046\u304d\u4ee3\u306a\u3089\u3001\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u304c\u51fa\u3057\u3066\u3042\u3052\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm your mother, so I can pay for your flight for you."
                },
