{
            "mnemonic": "When you see this on a number, for example {span:lang=ja:\uff17\u4eba} or {span:lang=ja:\uff13\u4eba}, you're using it to count people. Just remember, both {span:lang=ja:\u4e00\u4eba} and {span:lang=ja:\u4e8c\u4eba} have alternative readings. From 3 and up it's just the number plus {span:lang=ja:\u306b\u3093}, like this. {span:lang=ja:\uff15\u4eba} is {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u306b\u3093}, {span:lang=ja:\uff11\uff10\u4eba} is {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3046\u306b\u3093}, etc. This is the counter for people, which makes this word the {tooltip:Vocabulary:number of people}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Number Of People",
                "Alternatives": "People, Counter For People",
                "Word Type": "counter"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
