{
            "mnemonic": "First we have a katakana word, so it's safe to assume that it's a loan word. Like many loan words, it comes from English. Say it out loud and what do you have? That's right, \"table\". Then comes the particle {span:lang=ja:\u306e}, which joins two nouns together. Finally we have {span:lang=ja:\u4e0a}, which you learned means \"up\" or \"above\". Put all of these pieces together and we have a phrase meaning {tooltip:Vocabulary:on the table} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:tabletop}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "On The Table",
                "Alternative": "Tabletop",
                "Word Type": "expression"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
