                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32865-subject-7519.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}When a vocab word is a single kanji with no okurigana, it usually uses the kun'yomi reading. Numbers are an exception to this. Numbers use the on'yomi reading, which you've already learned by learning the kanji's reading! How nice!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u3078\u306e\u3072\u3053\u3046\u304d\u3060\u3044\u306f\u3001\u5341\u4e07\u4e94\u5343\u5186\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The plane ticket to Japan cost 105,000 yen."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u307e\u3044\u3068\u3057\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u30d0\u30ec\u30f3\u30bf\u30a4\u30f3\u30c7\u30fc\u306b\u4e07\u305f\u3093\u3044\u306e\u30c1\u30e7\u30b3\u30ec\u30fc\u30c8\u3092\u3082\u3089\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Every year Koichi receives tens of thousands of chocolates on Valentine's Day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3054\u3057\u3085\u3046\u304e\u306e\u305d\u3046\u3070\u306f\u5927\u305f\u3044\u4e09\u4e07\u5186\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The estimate on a congratulatory gift is approximately 30,000 yen."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

