                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be a kun'yomi reading. You haven't learned this one yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}If you're going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to disconnect something}, it {tooltip:Reading:has} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u305a}) to be the right thing! Don't go disconnecting the wrong plug, you'll cause no end of trouble!\n"
