                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u6bcd\u306e\u3044\u3048\u306b\u306f\u3001\u30d4\u30a2\u30ce\u304c\u4e8c\u53f0\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "There are two pianos at Koichi's mom's house."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u30c8\u30a4\u30ec\u306b\u306f\u30c6\u30ec\u30d3\u304c\u4e8c\u53f0\u3057\u304b\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "There are only two televisions in our bathroom."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This starts with another katakana word, so you can assume that it's a loan word. This one also comes from English. Can you figure out what it means? That's right, \"bed\". Then comes the particle {span:lang=ja:\u306e}, which joins two nouns together. Finally, we have {span:lang=ja:\u4e0b}, which you learned means \"down\" or \"below\". Put these elements together and you get {tooltip:Vocabulary:below the bed}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:under the bed} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:beneath the bed}. What's under your bed?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Under The Bed",
                "Alternatives": "Below The Bed, Beneath The Bed",
                "Word Type": "expression"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3063\u3069\u306e\u3057\u305f"
                    },
                    {
                        "primary": false,
                        "reading": "\u30d9\u30c3\u30c9\u306e\u3057\u305f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3079\u3063\u3069\u306e\u3057\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "44560-subject-8960.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3079\u3063\u3069\u306e\u3057\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "44152-subject-8960.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}{span:lang=ja:\u4e0b} is a standalone word here, so it uses the same reading that you learned when you learned the vocabulary.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d9\u30c3\u30c9\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u306f2000\u3055\u3064\u306e\u30de\u30f3\u30ac\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "There are 2000 manga under my bed."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d9\u30c3\u30c9\u306e\u4e0b\u306f\u307e\u3063\u305f\u304f\u305d\u3046\u3058\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "You never clean under your bed, do you?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d9\u30c3\u30c9\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u304b\u304f\u308c\u3066\u305c\u3093\u305c\u3093\u51fa\u3066\u3053\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm going to hide under the bed and never come out."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

