                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading, but it can be either that or the on'yomi reading, depending on the context. You haven't learned the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u65b9} yet, so there's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You need to go a certain {tooltip:Vocabulary:direction}. How do you get there? By jumping into a {tooltip:Reading:cata}pult ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u305f}) and shooting yourself the right {tooltip:Vocabulary:way}. Need to get a particular direction fast? Consider the catapult next time.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3061\u3089\u306e\u65b9\u304c\u3059\u304d\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
