{
            "mnemonic": "What is the {tooltip:Radical:evening} {tooltip:Radical:mouth}? Imagine a mouth that\u2019s up in the night sky. It\u2019s just there, talking, and only comes out at night. It only appears in one area of the world (what area would you choose? Imagine yourself going to that place to see the \u201cnight mouth.\u201d), and appears only one month out of the year (more on this in a second). The \u201cevening mouth\u201d is the most famous thing in the _____ area (this is the area you choose). He\u2019s so {tooltip:Kanji:famous} that everybody knows his {tooltip:Kanji:name} (\u201cEvening Mouth.\u201d).",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself going to the area you chose, and watching \u201cEvening Mouth\u201d speak. There are thousands of others there, wanting to see the giant floating mouth in the night sky. \u201cEvening Mouth\u201d then says \u201cEveryone, what\u2019s my {tooltip:Kanji:name}!?\u201d and everyone shouts back \u201cEvening Mouth!\u201d in unison. \u201cEvening Mouth\u201d has certainly gotten really {tooltip:Kanji:famous}.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Name",
                "Alternative": "Famous"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3044, \u307f\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You know what they say. April showers bring May Flowers. What do {tooltip:Reading:May} Flowers bring? They bring \u201cEvening Mouth,\u201d baby.",
                "mnemonic": "So, when does \u201cEvening Mouth\u201d appear? Turns out, \u201cEvening Mouth\u201d only comes out to talk in {tooltip:Reading:May} ({span:lang=ja:\u3081\u3044}). You know this because it\u2019s just starting to be spring, and when you look around (you\u2019re watching \u201cEvening Mouth\u201d again) you see some spring flowers come up."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:not} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:not} are the same thing! That makes it easy... Not!",
