                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u305a",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15256-subject-2648.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. In fact, the reading for this word is very rare, and kind of an exception. We'll use a mnemonic that uses both the kanji part and the hiragana attachment part. \n{splitParent}{tooltip:Vocabulary:First of all} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:to start with}, you have to make it through this {tooltip:Reading:maze} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u305a}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5148\u305a\u3001\u4e0b\u3054\u3057\u3089\u3048\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "First, we do the prep work."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5148\u305a\u3001\u305d\u306e\u4e94\u5341\u306d\u3093\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3042\u3064\u3081\u305f\u5207\u624b\u30b3\u30ec\u30af\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u304b\u3089\u3060\u3093\u3057\u3083\u308a\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "Why don't you declutter the stamp collection you've been working on for fifty years first?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5148\u305a\u306f\u3001\u30c1\u30ad\u30f3\u306e\u7fbd\u3092\u3080\u3057\u308a\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3001\u305d\u308c\u305e\u308c\u306e\u7fbd\u306b\u540d\u524d\u3092\u3064\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "First you need to pluck the chicken and then name each of the feathers."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
