                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20837-subject-2566.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. The only exception to this is {span:lang=ja:\u56db}, which uses the kun'yomi reading, since the on'yomi reading sounds too much like the word for \"death.\" Luckily you know these reading already, so there's nothing new to learn!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "T\u30b7\u30e3\u30c4\u3092\u56db\u5341\u307e\u3044\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I have forty T-shirts."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u5929\u624d\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4eba\u306f\u56db\u5341\u624d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "That genius American is 40 years old."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u56db\u5341\u3060\u3044\u306b\u3082\u306a\u308b\u3068\u3001\u305c\u3093\u3057\u3093\u304c\u304b\u3086\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Since reaching my forties, my entire body has been itchy."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you have {tooltip:Kanji:four} {tooltip:Kanji:hundred}s, you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:four hundred}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Four Hundred",
                "Word Type": "numeral"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3093\u3072\u3083\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3093\u3072\u3083\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "35220-subject-2681.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3093\u3072\u3083\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15311-subject-2681.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word has number four in it, and uses the kun'yomi reading for that kanji ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3093}). The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u767e} though, is the on'yomi reading ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3083\u304f}). This is pretty normal when it comes to words containing four in Japanese. You know both of these readings already. Hooray!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3057\u308a\u3087\u3046\u3092\u56db\u767e\u679a\u30b3\u30d4\u30fc\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please make four hundred copies of this document."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u306e\u30b7\u30a2\u30c8\u30eb\u5e02\u3067\u3001\u4e00\u3084\u306b\u3057\u3066\u56db\u767e\u4eba\u304c\u3057\u3063\u305d\u3046\u3059\u308b\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3058\u3051\u3093\u304c\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "There was an incident where 400 people went missing overnight in the city of Seattle in the US."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3063\u305f\u3044\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u56db\u767e\u30c9\u30eb\u3082\u4e00\u672c\u306e\u722a\u694a\u679d\u3092\u8cb7\u3046\u306e\u306b\u4f7f\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "How did you spend four hundred dollars on a toothpick?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Vocabulary:Fourth day} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:day four}. No matter how you look at this combination of kanji, the meaning of the word makes a lot of sense!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fourth Day",
                "Alternatives": "Day Four, Four Days",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3063\u304b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3063\u304b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30429-subject-2563.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3063\u304b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20826-subject-2563.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. Counting days, however, is an exception (at least up to ten). You need to use the kun'yomi readings to read this word. You already know the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u56db}, so that's fine (the {span:lang=ja:\u3093} gets turned into a small {span:lang=ja:\u3063}, though). Think of it this way:\n{splitParent}On the fourth day you pour {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3063}) all over your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}) because on the fifth day you're going to have to eat ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3064}) it. ({span:lang=ja:\u4e94}'s kun'yomi reading is {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3064}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3089\u3044\u6708\u306e\u56db\u65e5\u306b\u3001\u308f\u305f\u3057\u3068\u4e00\u3057\u3087\u306b\u3084\u304d\u3085\u3046\u3092\u307f\u306b\u3044\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Why don\u2019t you come watch baseball with me on the fourth of next month?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e03\u6708\u56db\u65e5\u306f\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u306e\u3069\u304f\u308a\u3064\u304d\u306d\u3093\u65e5\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "July 4th is Independence Day in America."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u304f\u307e\u306b\u51fa\u3042\u3063\u3066\u56db\u65e5\u3054\u3001\u307c\u304f\u306e\u305b\u306a\u304b\u306b\u304b\u3073\u304c\u306f\u3048\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Four days after I met that bear, my back started growing mold."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

