                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15261-subject-2659.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this word is just the jukugo, but the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u6587} is a little bit modified. Instead of the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3093}, which you learned with the kanji, it's just {span:lang=ja:\u3082}. You can remember this because you're shortening this word in a way as well. The \"writing letter\" is shortened to \"letter.\" So, think of {span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3093} being shortened to {span:lang=ja:\u3082}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6587\u5b57\u306f\u304d\u3044\u308d\u306b\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Make this letter yellow, please."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30a4\u30b1\u30eb\u306f\u516b\u3058\u304b\u3093\u304b\u3051\u3066\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3051\u3044\u6587\u5b57\u3067\u624b\u304c\u307f\u3092\u3057\u305f\u305f\u3081\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Michael took eight hours to write a letter to Koichi in hieroglyphics."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304b\u3089\u306e\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u3001\u6587\u5b57\u5316\u3051\u3057\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u307f\u305f\u3044\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u4f55\u3066\u66f8\u3044\u3066\u305f\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "It looks like that email from you contained corrupted characters, what did you write?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

