                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji with some hiragana, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}So, do you want a {tooltip:Vocabulary:rest} from work or school? You should say \"{tooltip:Reading:Yes!}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3084\u3059}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u3068\u3046\u3055\u3093\u306e\u3064\u304e\u306e\u4f11\u307f\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "When is Kato\u2019s next day off?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3072\u308b\u4f11\u307f\u306b\u30ab\u30d5\u30a7\u3067\u304b\u304d\u6c37\u3092\u305f\u3079\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "During lunch break, I ate shaved ice at a cafe."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u660e\u65e5\u306f\u4f11\u307f\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u4e00\u65e5\u4e2d\u4e00\u4eba\u3067\u30de\u30ea\u30aa\u30ab\u30fc\u30c8\u3092\u3059\u308b\u4e88\u5b9a\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Tomorrow is my day off, so I\u2019m planning to play Mario Kart by myself for the entire day."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

