                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. This word, however, uses the kun'yomi readings. This is possibly because of {span:lang=ja:\u624b}, because body parts often use kun'yomi. You learned both readings with the individual words, so you should be able to read this.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c71\u4e0b\u3055\u3093\u306f\u3001\u53f3\u624b\u306b\u304f\u308d\u3044\u304b\u3055\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Ms. Yamashita has a black umbrella in her right hand."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c0f\u3055\u3044\u5973\u306e\u5b50\u304c\u3001\u53f3\u624b\u306b\u30d3\u30fc\u7389\u3092\u306b\u304e\u308a\u3057\u3081\u3066\u7acb\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "There was a little girl holding a marble in her right hand."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3001\u8d64\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306e\u53f3\u624b\u306e\u3072\u3058\u306b\u30db\u30af\u30ed\u304c\u3042\u308b\uff01",
                    "en": "Oh, the baby has a mole on the elbow of his right arm."
