{
            "mnemonic": "It's kind of like you're saying {tooltip:Kanji:say} {tooltip:Kanji:say}. This is what you say when you answer or greet someone on the telephone. There's a strange story about this. One reason you say {span:lang=ja:\u7533\u3057\u7533\u3057} is because it's hard for foxes to say. So, you're confirming that the other person isn't a fox. The other explanation is that operators would say this, letting the person know on the other line that they're talking by saying \"say say\" but in a humble way. Either way, this is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:telephone hello}, so say it next time you talk to someone on the phone who is Japanese... just to make sure they aren't a fox.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
