{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:leg} or {tooltip:Kanji:sufficient}, and we're going with the \"sufficient\" meaning for this word! This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be enough}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Enough",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Sufficient, To Suffice",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u308a\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u308a\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "35115-subject-2706.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u308a\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15199-subject-2706.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u305f} portion. Whenever we need to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u305f} we use the word \"taco.\" \n{splitParent}What do you have enough of? What is sufficient? Turns out it's {tooltip:Reading:ta}cos ({span:lang=ja:\u305f}). Your bunker is filled with them and it's going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be enough} to last the winter.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u308c\u3060\u3051\u3067\u3001\u8db3\u308a\u308b\u306e\u304b\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "I wonder if this much will be enough."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30e2\u30ca\u30b3\u306e\u738b\u5973\u306f\u305b\u3051\u3093\u3057\u3089\u305a\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u8eca\u3092\u304b\u3046\u306e\u306b\u5341\u4e07\u5186\u3082\u3042\u308c\u3070\u8db3\u308a\u308b\u3068\u304a\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Because the princess in Monaco is ignorant to most things, she thinks that 100,000 yen is enough to buy a car."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u591c\u3001\u30ef\u30a4\u30f3\u30b3\u30eb\u30af\u3067\u4f55\u304b\u5de5\u4f5c\u3092\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306b\u8db3\u308a\u308b\u3060\u3051\u306e\u30ef\u30a4\u30f3\u3092\u98f2\u3080\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a93\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I vow to drink enough wine to make something crafty with the corks tonight."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:enter} into the {tooltip:Kanji:energy}. When you entering into (positive) energy, you are going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be pleased}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be satisfied} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be happy} with something. Just imagine yourself entering into some happy energy when you see something you're pleased with. Smile and feel pleased as well!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Pleased",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Satisfied, To Be Happy",
                "Word Type": "expression, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u306b\u3044\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u306b\u3044\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "35134-subject-2671.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u306b\u3044\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15244-subject-2671.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The {span:lang=ja:\u6c17} portion is pretty straight forward. The {span:lang=ja:\u5165\u308b} reading is the same as the one you learned with the vocabulary {span:lang=ja:\u5165\u308a\u53e3}. Just imagine you're really, really, reeeally pleased with your lovely new pet {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044})! You're so satisfied and happy with it. Feel the good energy your eagle is bringing you.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u307c\u3046\u3057\u3001\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3082\u6c17\u306b\u5165\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m very happy with this hat."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7389\u306d\u304e\u738b\u5b50\u306b\u6c17\u306b\u5165\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3046\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4e2d\u306e\u7389\u306d\u304e\u3092\u304b\u3044\u3057\u3081\u3066\u7389\u306d\u304e\u3054\u3066\u3093\u3092\u305f\u3066\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "In order to please Prince Onion, I bought all the onions in America and built an onion palace."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u541b\u306e\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u5b50\u72ac\u304c\u6c17\u306b\u5165\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3048\u308b\u3068\u3044\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "I hope you\u2019re happy with your new puppy."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:copy} so you know this means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to copy}. You know this word means \"to copy\" because it ends with {span:lang=ja:\u3059}. You're copying the documents you need to {tooltip:Reading:sue} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059}) someone who screwed you over.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
