                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3064} part. To remember that, think of yourself as a beatboxer. You're saying {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064} over and over again. Thing is, the other beatboxer is going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to copy} everything you do. That's why you're suing him.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3068\u306a\u308a\u306e\u30da\u30fc\u30b8\u306b\u3001\u3053\u306e\u5b57\u3092\u5199\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please copy the characters onto the next page of your workbooks."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306e\u5199\u3059\u5199\u3057\u3093\u306e\u5927\u30d5\u30a1\u30f3\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm a big fan of the photos Viet takes."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7d4c\u3092\u66f8\u304d\u5199\u3059\u306b\u306f\u3001\u5343\u5186\u652f\u6255\u3046\u5fc5\u8981\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "You must pay 1,000 yen in order to transcribe a sutra by hand."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:exit} but you do it with {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3051\u308b} added to it. Just think of that {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3051\u308b} as you are exiting while being \"cocky\" about it. You do this when you want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to go out} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to leave}. You go out in a cocky way!",
