                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use a kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn the {span:lang=ja:\u3044} reading with this kanji though, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}What does it mean {tooltip:Vocabulary:to live}? Life is pretty {tooltip:Reading:icky} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u304d} ... the {span:lang=ja:\u304d} comes from the hiragana part), but you have to take that ickiness and roll with it if you want to have a good life... if you want to live!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3057\u3064\u308c\u3093\u3067\u751f\u304d\u308b\u304d\u529b\u3092\u3046\u3057\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I lost the will to live from heartbreak."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u3001\u304b\u308c\u304c\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3059\u3089\u5206\u304b\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I don't even know if he's alive now."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u5927\u597d\u304d\u306a\u30a2\u30cb\u30e1\u30ad\u30e3\u30e9\u304c\u3001\u4eca\u751f\u304d\u308b\u304b\u3057\u306c\u304b\u306e\u305b\u3068\u304e\u308f\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "My favorite anime character is currently in a critical moment between life and death."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've already learned that {span:lang=ja:\u53e3} means \"mouth\" and here it's followed by the particle {span:lang=ja:\u306b}, which pinpoints a location. The verb {span:lang=ja:\u3059\u308b} means \"to do\" so you're doing something to your mouth! Logically enough, this expression is used to describe lots of actions that you do with your mouth. It's often used to mean {tooltip:Vocabulary:to mention} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to say}, but with an added descriptive nuance that you've said something accidentally or unexpectedly, maybe something you shouldn't have said! \ud83d\ude4a",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Mention",
                "Alternatives": "To Say, To Eat, To Drink",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, expression"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
