                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}This {tooltip:Vocabulary:year} you plan on {tooltip:Reading:tossi}ng ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3057}) out all your old stuff as a New Year's resolution. You pronounce it \"toshing\" though, because it has more vigor that way.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u305e\u3088\u3044\u304a\u5e74\u3092\u304a\u3080\u304b\u3048\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "I hope you have a happy New Year!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u5e74\u3082\u3076\u3058\u306b\u5e74\u3092\u3068\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Once again, I was able to age this year without issue."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u304f\u308b\u5e74\u3001\u30a8\u30ea\u30ab\u306f\u767d\u3044\u725b\u306b\u4e57\u3063\u305f\u738b\u5b50\u69d8\u306b\u51fa\u4f1a\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The next year, Erika met a prince riding a white cow."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "It's the 2011 {tooltip:Kanji:year}. I think the meaning is pretty obvious. This just means {tooltip:Vocabulary:year 2011} or simply {tooltip:Vocabulary:2011}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Year 2011",
                "Alternatives": "2011, The Year 2011",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306b\u305b\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3046\u3044\u3061\u306d\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u305b\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3046\u3044\u3061\u306d\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15364-subject-2662.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u305b\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3046\u3044\u3061\u306d\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "35259-subject-2662.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is a little trickier. You start with two thousand ({span:lang=ja:\u4e8c\u5343\uff0f\u306b\u305b\u3093}), then you need to add eleven to it ({span:lang=ja:\u5341\u4e00\uff0f\u3058\u3085\u3046\u3044\u3061}). Then, you simply add the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5e74} which you already know. You can assume it's the on'yomi reading because it's attached to something else, like a jukugo. From there, you get the entire reading.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\uff12\uff10\uff11\uff11\u5e74\u306b\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u3044\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I went to Japan in 2011."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e3b\u4eba\u306f\u3001\uff12\uff10\uff11\uff11\u5e74\u304b\u3089\u706b\u305b\u3044\u3067\u306f\u305f\u3089\u3044\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My husband has been working on Mars since 2011."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7236\u306f\u3001\uff12\uff10\uff11\uff11\u5e74\u306b\u3088\u3046\u3084\u304f\u30c9\u30e9\u30c3\u30b0\u306e\u4f7f\u7528\u3092\u8a8d\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My father finally admitted to drug use in 2011."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:year} {tooltip:Kanji:middle} sounds like it should be something like \"the middle of the year,\" but it's not. Think of something that happens in the middle of the year and then all other parts of the year. It's just referring to everything within this year, which is how we get {tooltip:Vocabulary:year round}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Year Round",
                "Alternatives": "All Year, Whole Year, Throughout The Year",
                "Word Type": "adverb, noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306d\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306d\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15303-subject-2664.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306d\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "35204-subject-2664.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings for the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. {span:lang=ja:\u4e2d} does have a strange reading, though, which is {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3046}. This is basically just {span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3085\u3046} changing to {span:lang=ja:\u3062\u3085\u3046}, but since {span:lang=ja:\u3062} is very rare it just switches to {span:lang=ja:\u3058} and you end up with {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3046}. That's called rendaku.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u753a\u306e\u305d\u3089\u306f\u3001\u5e74\u4e2d\u3069\u3093\u3088\u308a\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The sky in this town is dull all year."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u3057\u3083\u3044\u3093\u306f\u3001\u4e8c\u5341\u56db\u3058\u304b\u3093\u5e74\u4e2d\u3080\u304d\u3085\u3046\u3067\u306f\u305f\u3089\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu employees work twenty four seven, year round."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u56fd\u3067\u306f\u4e00\u5e74\u4e2d\u96e8\u304c\u964d\u308b\u3093\u3060\u304c\u3001\u59bb\u3082\u307e\u305f\u5e74\u4e2d\u305d\u306e\u6587\u53e5\u3092\u8a00\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "It rains year round in this country and my wife complains about it year round as well."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a strange looking axe, I know. But think of it this way: the letter \"T\" is in the cliff. What is the \"T\"? Of course it has to be Mr. T, who's super awesome. Think of Mr. T wielding a terrifying axe, running after you screaming, \"I pity the fool!\" while trying to chop you down. That makes for a pretty terrifying {tooltip:Radical:axe}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Axe"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have life on top of the moon (ignore that life is missing its little slide on the left side). What would life on the moon look like? Well, first of all, they have no air, so they probably look pretty {tooltip:Radical:blue} from asphyxiation. When you meet them, it turns out you're right. They're a civilization of blue people. Imagine them all living up there, being blue and Smurfy.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Blue"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "See the slide going into the dirt? That's where they throw your body when you die. It's actually a {tooltip:Radical:coffin}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Coffin"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The bed you get in prison is the only thing with {tooltip:Radical:color} you'll see while you're there. Picture a dark, dank cell. Maybe a toilet too. Now picture a bright, colorful bed against the wall. This is the only joy you have.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Color"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical already looks like a pair of wings, right? What are on wings? Well, usually lots of {tooltip:Radical:feathers}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Feathers"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have the radicals for loiter, two, and barb. Someone who uses two barbs on you while you're loitering really wants you to {tooltip:Radical:GO}!! GO on, stop loitering outside of my convenience store, ya dang kids!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Go"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's two sets of spikes underneath that hat. It's actually a trap, to prevent anyone from coming in and stealing your {tooltip:Radical:gold}. Why else would you make a trap? Everyone likes to protect their gold.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gold"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Remember the radical for drop (of liquid)? This is two drops instead of one. When you see two drops, you should think, \"the next stage of water.\" What is the next stage? Why, that is {tooltip:Radical:ice}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ice"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a very oddly shaped {tooltip:Radical:key}, but it's a key nonetheless.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Key"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "These are legs that are bending funny. They're bending so they can {tooltip:Radical:kick} you! Imagine someone doing a flying kick at you. Look at their legs and, ah yes, it looks just like this!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Kick"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Think of an old-style {tooltip:Radical:lantern}. It's on top of a few legs (you can only see two from this angle) and it's in a box shaped holder at the top. You can imagine these lining the streets before electricity, right? That's why this radical is a lantern.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lantern"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's something hooked going into a mouth. Rather than a hook, though, it's a {tooltip:Radical:lip ring}. They used to use fish hooks and nails in the old days. (Glad we don't live in those times anymore!)",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lip Ring"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Inside your head, you can only think about people, people, and more people. This is bad, because really all you want is their {tooltip:Radical:meat}, because you're some kind of sick cannibal... you monster. When you think of \"people\" in your head, you're really just thinking about more meat you can eat.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Meat"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under the hat there are two people {tooltip:Radical:meet}ing in private. Look at them huddled up in there. They must have a reason to want to meet in such a private place, but that's not for you to judge. Maybe next time you have to meet with someone you'll hide under a hat with them too.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Meet"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "See the {tooltip:Radical:mustache} going around the mouth? I wish I could grow a sweet mustache like this.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mustache"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The towel is getting soaked with drops of liquid. That's because it's {tooltip:Radical:rain}ing. Get your towels and other clothes inside before they get soaked through from this rain!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rain"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "See the person {tooltip:Radical:run}ning? Don't confuse this with foot ({span:lang=ja:\u8db3}), though. The head is just a streak because this person is running so fast.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Run"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are a bunch of sound waves coming out of a mouth. Those waves represent the things you {tooltip:Radical:say}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Say"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is a {tooltip:Radical:scooter}. See the handlebars and the little light? And there's a platform at the bottom you can stand or sit on (if it's one of those nice motorized ones).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Scooter"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "That little fleck / drop on your eye is what makes you unique. It's what makes you your {tooltip:Radical:self}. It's you, you know?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Self"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen one drop ({span:lang=ja:\u4e36}), but what happens when you triple this and have three drops, which happens to be the maximum number of drops you can have? You end up with a devastating {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}, because there's too much water and nowhere for it to go. Just think of this as a lot of water. When you have a lot of water, you have a tsunami.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tsunami"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have {span:lang=ja:\u5341} plus {span:lang=ja:\u5341}... what do you get when you add these two kanji together? You get {tooltip:Radical:twenty}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Twenty"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a roof with extra spikes / horns on it. Who was famous for having spiked roofs, spiked helmets, spiked boats?! The Vikings! That's why this is the {tooltip:Radical:Viking} radical.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Viking"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a rice paddy with dirt around it. This is the perfect place to set up a {tooltip:Radical:village}. You have a place to farm and some dirt to live on. What else could you need?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Village"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have pi coming out of a mouth. \"3.14,\" it says. We must take the secret of the circle with us, away from here. We must go to a magical place where nobody will persecute us for our math... a place to the {tooltip:Radical:West}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "West"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "See the criss-cross in the pseudo-square shape? That's the frames of a big {tooltip:Radical:window} you can look out of. It's not perfectly shaped like a rice field, it's more artistic. That's why this is a window and {span:lang=ja:\u7530} is not.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Window"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know {tooltip:Radical:Wolverine} from the X-Men? He has three claws that come out of his hand whenever he needs to fight, not at all unlike the radical you see here.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wolverine"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:task} in {tooltip:Radical:prison} is to bend things into different {tooltip:Kanji:angle}s and then put them in the {tooltip:Kanji:corner}. No one will tell you why you're doing this, but you get a couple cents an hour to do it, so you aren't going to complain.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself sitting in a corner, bending pieces of metal and scrap to fit the angle of that corner.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Angle",
                "Alternatives": "Corner, Antler"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3069, \u3064\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine cocking your head to different angles and hearing cocks crow every time you do. Prison isn't as fun as you thought it would be. Manual labor and loud chickens aren't what you expected.",
                "mnemonic": "To get the {tooltip:Kanji:angle} right you find that you have to {tooltip:Reading:cock} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304f}) your head to the side a lot. After cocking your head at weird angles so much you also start to hear cocks crowing in your head. Cock-co-cock-co-caww!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:axe} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:axe} kanji are exactly the same, with one minor difference. This kanji is also used as the {tooltip:Kanji:bread loaf counter}, probably because bread was so big and hard in the past that they had to use axes to slice them.",
            "hints": "Imagine you've gone back in time a good hundred years, and you're trying to count loaves of bread after each swing of your axe. Axes and bread loaves will become intertwined in your brain.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Axe",
                "Alternative": "Bread Loaf Counter"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being stuck using an axe on bread while the King of England glares down at you, munching and spilling crumbs everywhere.",
                "mnemonic": "You imagined being back in time too good and now you're stuck using an {tooltip:Kanji:axe} to be a {tooltip:Kanji:bread loaf counter} for the {tooltip:Reading:Kin}g ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3093}) of England. You aren't sure which king he is or when in time you are, but he's mean and keeps eating all the bread you cut up with your axe."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:blue} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:blue} kanji are exactly the same.",
            "hints": "Don't feel blue, you should know this kanji automagically!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Blue"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044, \u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You aren't sure how you or the saber turned blue, but you're pretty sure the Shougun had something to do with it. At least you match now, I guess.",
                "mnemonic": "You've been feeling really {tooltip:Kanji:blue}. Mostly because your skin, hair, and eyes have all turned blue. The {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) found out and now he's back. He places his hand on your shoulder and then points at your {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}). It's blue too! You aren't alone!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} has a {tooltip:Radical:book} all about the human {tooltip:Kanji:body}. Knowing about bodies is a privilege. One that only leaders get\u2014it helps them control all their subjects, like you.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking down at your body and thinking, huh, I wonder what all that junk is? Oh well, I'm sure the leader has it all figured out in that book of hers.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Body"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3089\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the leader, reading a book, putting a tie on her body. Look around at you and your family and your neighbors. You don't know what your body meat-bags do and you don't know how to tie a tie. Womp womp.",
                "mnemonic": "The leader's {tooltip:Kanji:body} book also taught her about something very body specific: how to tie a {tooltip:Reading:tie} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3044}). You can't have a tie on your body, no no. Those are for the leader and her smart body."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:color} radical and {tooltip:Kanji:color} are the same in looks as well as in meaning.",
            "hints": "Color me pink! This kanji's super easy if you know your radicals.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Color"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u304d, \u3057\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u308d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You can even have someone ask you about your ear... \"Is your ear okay? I think it's the color blue...\"",
                "mnemonic": "You already have {tooltip:Kanji:color} on the mind because you know the meaning of this kanji, so think of something colorful about yourself. Imagine your {tooltip:Reading:ear} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u308d}) being a weird color... green, purple, red, whatever. Just make it really bright and standing out."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's {tooltip:Radical:rice} spread out all over the {tooltip:Radical:ground}. This will cause the Predator to {tooltip:Kanji:come} because he loves kome (rice). Then once he's gone, the {tooltip:Kanji:next} Predator will come to eat.",
            "hints": "Also imagine everyone else coming to the rice next. When rice spills, people come from all around to line up and grab a handful of it to take home. Who's next? Come forward!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Come",
                "Alternative": "Next"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3089\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you love rye grains, on the other hand, imagine everyone being really happy that they came to get the rice. They're so lucky it's rye!",
                "mnemonic": "When they come, though, everyone is disappointed. It turns out it's {tooltip:Reading:rye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3089\u3044}) grains, and rye grains taste terrible. Yuck."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Plant a {tooltip:Radical:spirit} in the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} before you start your {tooltip:Kanji:company} and it will be successful. That's what all the great, old Japanese companies did back in the olden days. That's why companies like Mitsubishi have been around for hundreds of years. They planted a spirit in the dirt to help their company grow, and grow it did!",
            "hints": "Picture a young person way back in old-timey history times burying the spirit of one of their ancestors in the dirt. Now watch as an old-timey time lapse plays out in front of your eyes and a company is born!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Company"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3083",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u3057\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine going to a shaman and having them tell you that for your company to be successful you need to bury a spirit in the dirt so it can help the company grow. You should probably listen.",
                "mnemonic": "Where did you learn about this method of {tooltip:Kanji:company} growing? From a {tooltip:Reading:sha}man ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3083}), of course. Shamans aren't just spouting nonsense, they know what they're talking about. And spirits are right up their shaman alley."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} and a {tooltip:Radical:wolverine}. What are they doing together? You'd think they'd fight, but they took their battle to another venue... they're competing in a game show! One of them answers a question, and the host says, \"{tooltip:Kanji:Success}! You're {tooltip:Kanji:correct}!\"",
            "hints": "Feel free to think through several questions and answers, but make sure they're all right, because that's what we're focusing on. Also make sure to focus on the triceratops and the wolverine themselves. You want to make sure that when you see these two radicals you automatically know they're playing in a game show, not doing anything else, like fighting or racing or something.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Correct",
                "Alternatives": "Right, Success"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Wow, that was a pretty easy answer to get right. {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} is what pretty much everyone would guess, and they'd be correct.",
                "mnemonic": "When we need to remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046}, we use the Japanese city Tokyo. The last question in the game show match is the following: \"What is the capital of Japan.\" The triceratops and the wolverine scream the {tooltip:Kanji:correct} answer at the same time: {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:treasure}s are in the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} where there\u2019s {tooltip:Radical:ice}. How cryptic! You want to find the treasure, that\u2019s for sure (treasure is great!). It is somewhere where there is ice, so maybe the arctic? What you are looking at is a {tooltip:Kanji:diagram} which will guide you there.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking at a diagram or map \u2013 and it has pictures of treasure in an area where ice is. This is where you will find the mystical treasure. This diagram will show the way. You're so excited that you found this map!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Diagram"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305a, \u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048, \u306f\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine dragging a wooly mammoth back with you to the town or city you live in, then throwing it in a zoo to be kept. People are quite amazed by this mystical creature you\u2019ve found, though, which is pretty cool.",
                "mnemonic": "What will you do when you find these treasures that are shown on the {tooltip:Kanji:diagram}? Well, you get there, and you find that the treasure is actually a wooly mammoth! What will you do with this wooly mammoth? You grab it and put it in your {tooltip:Reading:zoo} ({span:lang=ja:\u305a})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see some {tooltip:Radical:windows}... you have a {tooltip:Radical:gun}. What do you think you're going to do with this gun? Of course, you're going to shoot the windows... {tooltip:Kanji:every} single one of them. {tooltip:Kanji:Each} and every one.",
            "hints": "Make a point to make sure you get {tooltip:Kanji:every} one, and don't miss any of them. Actually search around in your imagination for any more windows, because you want to stress it's important you hit {tooltip:Kanji:each} and every window with your gun.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Every",
                "Alternative": "Each"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you need to shoot every one of the mice that came through those broken windows. You can't let any survive. You have to get every last one out of here!!",
                "mnemonic": "Now that {tooltip:Kanji:each} and {tooltip:Kanji:every} window is broken you feel pretty stupid because a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:mi}ce ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u3044}) come pouring in through them. You've made a way for them to get into your house. That wasn't smart."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:feather} radical and {tooltip:Kanji:feather} are the same in looks as well as in meaning.",
            "hints": "Have you been studying your radicals? If so, this'll be easy!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Feather",
                "Alternatives": "Feathers, Wing, Wings"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u306d, \u306f, \u308f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Taste the honey, feel it all over your feathers. Go ahead and plummet towards the ground (because you were jumping off a building to fly when someone doused you with honey). At least it's a tasty way to go, no?",
                "mnemonic": "All these {tooltip:Kanji:feather}s. You're a bird man / woman, and you're getting ready to fly. Just as you're about to take off, someone dumps you with {tooltip:Reading:honey} {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u306d} and you're all goopy, unable to go anywhere."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:tree} and another {tooltip:Radical:tree}. You basically have yourself a {tooltip:Kanji:forest}!",
            "hints": "Follow the logic of this one and you should be okay.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Forest",
                "Alternative": "Grove"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3084\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Obviously that didn't work well - you'll want to focus on your battle cry plus indecent swearing right afterwards to remember this reading.",
                "mnemonic": "So, now you have this {tooltip:Kanji:forest} and you want to cut it down (so much money!). But, you don't have any tools, only your hands. You think... I've done karate for a while, so I can probably chop it down that way. You get in a chopping stance, then do your battle cry and hit: \"{tooltip:Reading:HAYA ... .SHI******}!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:go} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:go} kanji are exactly the same!",
            "hints": "If you know your radicals well enough (and you do), you'll know this kanji.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Go"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046, \u304e\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044, \u304a\u3053\u306a, \u3086",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You try to go another direction, and he just yells and points louder: \"GO!\"",
                "mnemonic": "\"{tooltip:Kanji:Go}!\" someone is telling you. \"Go! Go! Go!\" That person is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. He is holding his finger out, and pointing at your WaniKani reviews. \"Go! Go!\" Then, he over-enunciates the word \"go\" by saying \"{tooltip:Reading:GYOU!}!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3087\u3046})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:gold} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:gold} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "Just know your radicals and you'll be golden, so to speak.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gold"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u306d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the King on a huge pile of gold. Gold coins, gold candelabras, gold ponies. He's laughing and pointing at all of it while making very strong eye contact with you.",
                "mnemonic": "The most {tooltip:Kanji:gold} in the land belongs to the {tooltip:Reading:Kin}g ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3093}) of England. In fact, you've never actually met someone with gold, it all goes straight to the King whenever someone finds some. You just have a few pennies to work with."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You plant your {tooltip:Radical:flowers} in the light of the {tooltip:Radical:sun} in the shape of a {tooltip:Radical:cross}, but it's too hot\u2014the sun is too strong\u2014and you end up with {tooltip:Kanji:grass}. Flowers can't grow in these conditions.",
            "hints": "Think of how disappointed you are. You wanted a beautiful cross of flowers, and now you just have a big overgrown patch of thick grass. It isn't even pretty green grass, it's a little brown and damaged from the sun.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Grass",
                "Alternative": "Weed"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine using your cool saw to saw off the heads of all of this grass. You made the cross pretty big, so there is a ton of grass to get through. The sun is beating down on you and the grass too, which isn't making it any easier.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:grass} on top is brown and burned from the sun, so you need to take a {tooltip:Reading:cool saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3055}) and hack the tops off. The saw is actually physically cool to the touch, to help heal the grass' sunburned bits. It just happens to look cool too."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:village} you always think of first is your {tooltip:Kanji:hometown}. ",
            "hints": "Why would you ever talk about the village where someone else was born? Answer: you wouldn't. Everything is always about you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hometown",
                "Alternative": "Village"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Close your eyes and imagine being on a saddle, heading back to your hometown right now. Feel your butt and legs chafing. Eh... that's not such a great memory, now that you think about it.",
                "mnemonic": "You go back to your {tooltip:Kanji:hometown} in a {tooltip:Reading:saddle} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3068}). You can't take a car or a train there, it's really in the middle of nowhere. So you have to ride a horse, so break out that old saddle and go visit your parents."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader}'s {tooltip:Radical:key} is the key that {tooltip:Kanji:make}s all the other keys. It's sort of like the one ring to rule them all, the one ring to bind them... except with keys.",
            "hints": "Imagine the leader taking his key to open up a safe that has a button to make other keys for the underlings. No key is as great as this key, though.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Make"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u304f, \u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel angry about this. Maybe you should kick your foot in his mouth and make him {tooltip:Reading:suck} on that.{splitParent}Also keep in mind that there's another reading that pops up too that's {span:lang=ja:\u3055}. It's similar to {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u304f}, though, and I think you'll be able to learn both the readings via the vocabulary.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:make} a key for an underling, and he looks at it disapprovingly (even though you're their leader!). He simply says, \"this key {tooltip:Reading:sucks}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u304f}) and then walks off. How could this be?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "How many {tooltip:Radical:evenings} are there? There are {tooltip:Kanji:many}.",
            "hints": "If you accidentally think \"a lot\" or something similar, that's okay too. It's the basic meaning that counts, and all these things are pretty close, though eventually you want to get to the point where you know that this kanji does in fact mean {tooltip:Kanji:many}.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Many",
                "Alternatives": "Much, Lots Of"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The tacos pelt you and knock you off your feet. Hard shell, soft shell, meat, lettuce, tomatoes, cheese... it's terrible. And there are so many of them, flying from the sky to drown you in tacos. This is absolutely absurd (and you should think that too, so you remember the reading).",
                "mnemonic": "To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u305f} we use the word \"Taco\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:meat} radical and {tooltip:Kanji:meat} are the same in looks as well as in meaning.",
            "hints": "Study those radicals, and perhaps we'll eat some meat tonight.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Meat"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Do you know someone named {tooltip:Reading:Nick} you can imagine? There's celebrities too, if you don't have someone. Someone like {tooltip:Reading:Nick} Cage would do the trick.",
                "mnemonic": "You know there's people-eating going on here, with this kanji. So, when you think of this {tooltip:Kanji:meat}, you'll have to think about whose meat it is. In this case, it's {tooltip:Reading:Nick}'s ({span:lang=ja:\u306b\u304f}) meat."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:meet} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:meet} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals, yo!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Meet",
                "Alternative": "Meeting"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"I met my soulmate in a kayak,\" said Koichi.",
                "mnemonic": "What better way to {tooltip:Kanji:meet} new people than to start {tooltip:Reading:kay}aking ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044})! Get into your kayak and just float out into the water. You'll eventually bump into someone else in a kayak and boom, you're meeting someone new!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You put a {tooltip:Radical:lid} on your {tooltip:Radical:father}. But, he won't taste good alone, so you {tooltip:Kanji:mix} in some other ingredients. They {tooltip:Kanji:mingle} inside the pot with him.",
            "hints": "This may seem traumatic, but actually your father is surprisingly into it. Imagine him mixed in with all kinds of other things. It's important to note that this kanji is about things being mixed in, not so much about the action of mixing. That's another kanji. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mix",
                "Alternative": "Mingle"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3058, \u307e, \u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"I love mixing in with potatoes and tomatoes,\" your father {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} states. \"Turn up that temperature. I like to mingle with a bit more tingle.\"",
                "mnemonic": "With a {tooltip:Kanji:mix} of your father and other ingredients {tooltip:Kanji:mingl}ing in your cooking pot, you lift up the lid... your father pops up. Your father is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. He stares back at you with a big smile."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Someone on a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} has an {tooltip:Radical:axe}, and they're getting {tooltip:Kanji:near} to you really fast! Oh no, they're so {tooltip:Kanji:close} now, you need to get out of here!",
            "hints": "Picture a scooter coming toward you in the dark. You see the gleam of the axe as it looms nearer and nearer.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Near",
                "Alternative": "Close"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3093, \u3053\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The King is now so near to you his nose and mustache are tickling your face. He's holding the axe high above his head and saying, \"I can get as close to you as I want and you can't stop me because I'm the King. I can get sooooo close. Look, I'm not touching you though!\"",
                "mnemonic": "As they draw {tooltip:Kanji:near}, you recognize who is riding the scooter: the {tooltip:Reading:Kin}g ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3093}) of England! Behind him, a bunch of his guards also on scooters and wielding axes appear and move {tooltip:Kanji:close} to you. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Who's someone who's just a {tooltip:Radical:mouth} with {tooltip:Radical:legs}? That's your know-it-all {tooltip:Kanji:older brother}, who won't shut up about anything.",
            "hints": "To help this mnemonic along, literally imagine your older brother as someone that's just a giant mouth with a pair of legs walking around. It talks and talks and talks, too, irritating you. Feel the irritation specifically at your older brother. He's older than you, so you can't beat him up... yet.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Older Brother",
                "Alternatives": "Big Brother, Elder Brother"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046, \u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u306b, \u306b\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hmm... don't you want to go to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} someday? Maybe you should have sent your brother somewhere less cool.",
                "mnemonic": "You wish you could box your loud-mouth {tooltip:Kanji:older brother} up and send him far away to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} is super far away from where you currently live, so just ship your older bro off so he can never bother you again."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical for {tooltip:Radical:rain} and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:rain} are the same thing.",
            "hints": "Make sure you know your radicals!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rain"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3081, \u3042\u307e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a world where each rain drop had to choose a target to aim for. How strange would rainfall be? Also, {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3081} and \"aim\" don't really sound too much alike, but the goal is to use \"aim\" to get to {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3081}, so make sure to take note of that in your mind as you learn the reading.",
                "mnemonic": "What if the {tooltip:Kanji:rain} actually tried to {tooltip:Reading:aim} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3081}) for you? As in, drops would move out of their normal flight path just to hit you on your head? You'd be a lot wetter, that's for sure."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:rice} radical and {tooltip:Kanji:rice} are the same in looks as well as in meaning. This also refers to \"America,\" maybe because America is covered in rice or fields or something?",
            "hints": "Aren't radicals nice? They make things so much easier... if you've been studying them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rice",
                "Alternative": "America"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3044, \u307e\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3081",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "In your mind, bulldoze the rice into the bay, watching it fill it up, then pile high. It's not particularly good looking land, but it'll do, and it's already full of seeds, so that's pretty good. The important thing is that you think you have way too much of the stuff, so the only way to get rid of it is to dump it in a large body of water, and that large body of water is a bay.",
                "mnemonic": "You've got tons of dry grains of {tooltip:Kanji:rice}. You have no idea what you're going to do with it. Then, you come up with a solution. All this dry rice could go towards filling up the {tooltip:Reading:bay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3079\u3044}), so you have more land to farm on!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:run} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:run} are exactly the same!",
            "hints": "Make sure you know your radicals!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Run"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Running really takes it out of you. In this case, it takes your soul out of you. Don't worry, when you stop your soul will collide with you again and everything will be okay. (Probably.)",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:run} and run and run and suddenly you feel your {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) leave your body. Still running, you turn around and see your soul running a few steps behind you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:mustache} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground}. Upon closer inspection, you see that the mustache on the ground is exactly the {tooltip:Kanji:same} as yours!",
            "hints": "Pick up the mustache, hold it up next to your face in front of a mirror. It's unbelievable, but it's the same in every way, down to the last hair.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Same"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3069\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If it helps, imagine hundreds or thousands of doughnuts all around you with the same exact mustache. First of all, it's terrifying to be surrounded by thousands of mutant doughnuts. Secondly, it's really weird they all have the same mustache as you.",
                "mnemonic": "When we need to remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3069\u3046}, we use the word \"doughnut\"."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:say} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:say} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals, yo!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Say"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052\u3093, \u3054\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044, \u3053\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Genji is a real smooth talker. In fact, he can talk his way out of anything. If you can just stay calm and think \"What would Genji say?\" before saying anything, you'll probably end up saying something cool instead of something lame.",
                "mnemonic": "If you aren't sure what to {tooltip:Kanji:say}, just think about {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}) and ask yourself, \"What would Genji say?\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:self} radical and {tooltip:Kanji:self} are the same in looks as well as in meaning. ",
            "hints": "Radicals have self. Kanji has self. Kanji and radicals can sometimes be the same thing... so do they really have \"self\"? Only way to find out is to study both of them hard!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Self",
                "Alternative": "Oneself"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058, \u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u305a\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You can feel free to do some introspection here.",
                "mnemonic": "When we need to remember {span:lang=ja:\u3058} we use the word \"Jesus.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're walking at night when you discover a {tooltip:Radical:lantern} covered entirely in {tooltip:Radical:hair}, making it a very strange {tooltip:Kanji:shape}. In fact, this is a {tooltip:Kanji:form} you'd never expect a lantern to take.",
            "hints": "Picture all the different shapes this hairy lantern could take in your mind.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shape",
                "Alternatives": "Form, Appearance"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044, \u304e\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305f, \u304b\u305f\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the shape of this hairy, glowing cake.",
                "mnemonic": "You stare at the {tooltip:Kanji:shape} until you finally recognize it: {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044})! Well, it's hairy, glowing cake, but it's still shaped like a big slice of cake."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Slide} down a {tooltip:Radical:branch} and your {tooltip:Kanji:skin} will come off. Unlike what Tarzan will make you believe, you can't just slide around on branches, they're rough and painful and if you do it your skin will come sliding off and it will hurt.",
            "hints": "Imagine sliding down a slide made of a big, branch. The branch's bark digs into your skin and pulls it right off of your body.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Skin"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your skin protects you from really feeling lots of heat. It gets burned before you and it has many tiny layers to keep you safe from heat generating things like the sun. You really need your skin!",
                "mnemonic": "Without your {tooltip:Kanji:skin} to protect you, you feel the full {tooltip:Reading:he}at ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}) from the friction of your body going down the branch slide."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Giving a {tooltip:Radical:roof} {tooltip:Radical:legs} is the kind of {tooltip:Radical:construction} you do. You make it so a roof can be in the {tooltip:Kanji:sky}. In addition to meaning \"sky\", this kanji often means {tooltip:Kanji:\"empty\"}. Think about it - there's nothing more empty than the sky!",
            "hints": "Think about it. If you give a roof legs, it goes even higher up. What's higher up? The sky is!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sky",
                "Alternative": "Empty"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3089, \u3042, \u304b\u3089, \u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Say \"coooooties\" nice and long, just like a little kid, to emphasize the long vowel in {span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3046}.",
                "mnemonic": "The reason you want to put a roof in the {tooltip:Kanji:sky} is because it gets the roof away from all the {tooltip:Reading:coo}ties ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3046}) that are on the ground."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "For some reason, you are {tooltip:Radical:stand}ing on the {tooltip:Radical:sun}. It's obviously very hot, but the thing you notice most is the {tooltip:Kanji:sound} of you burning up.",
            "hints": "Imagine a super loud sizzling sound, drowning everything else out. It's ridiculously loud, and hurts your ears more than the sun's heat hurts your skin.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sound"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3068, \u306d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your burning body sounds just like sizzling, crispy onions being fried in a pan. Listen close. It's exactly the same! You can almost smell onions too! ",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:sound} isn't just loud, it's familiar. Finally you place it: {tooltip:Reading:on}ions ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3093})!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a wild {tooltip:Radical:viking} {tooltip:Radical:child} you have to take care of. He won't do anything but {tooltip:Kanji:study}, surprisingly. You can't get him to eat, use the bathroom, or anything else. He just wants to study.",
            "hints": "Of course, this isn't what you'd expect of a little viking child. It's the opposite. That's why it's so surprising! He loves to study!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Study",
                "Alternatives": "Learn, Learning"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You should tell the other vikings to stop gawking at this child. Just because he likes to study doesn't mean he's a bad viking...",
                "mnemonic": "This crazy viking child who prefers {tooltip:Kanji:study} over pillaging (and other viking activities)... the other vikings just stop and {tooltip:Reading:gawk} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u304f}) at him when they walk by."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} in the distance. But, it's odd. It's perfectly {tooltip:Radical:pi} shaped (that is, circular). Some kind of piceratops, if you will. The reason they are this shape is because they want to absorb as much {tooltip:Kanji:sunlight} (or just {tooltip:Kanji:light} is fine, too) as possible. They evolved to be round so they don't have any corners casting a shadow.",
            "hints": "Absorbing sunlight is natural for reptiles, after all. And a round one can absorb even more light. Imagine it sitting in a round spot of sun, enjoying the warmth. What a rare sight you've come across!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sunlight",
                "Alternative": "Light"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u304b\u308a, \u3072\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine many different (but also kind of the same) {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s attacking and throwing spears at the piceratops. But, because it was able to charge up in the sunlight, it uses its powers to shoot light in all directions, rendering all the {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s momentarily blind, allowing it to escape.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch this majestic beast absorbing {tooltip:Kanji:sunlight}, suddenly several dozen feral ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061})s burst from various hiding spots, spears in hand. Oh no! Those {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s are hunting this rare piceratops!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In a {tooltip:Radical:coffin} is someone {tooltip:Radical:begging}. But, it won't work. You won't listen. So, the man in the coffin just begins to {tooltip:Kanji:think}: What could I have done better in my life? Why am I in this situation? How will I get out? Think, damnit, think!!",
            "hints": "Imagine him changing from a begging position to a stereotypical \"thinking\" position, hand on chin, eyebrows furrowed. Focus on the beggar's thinking. This is a pretty abstract idea to imagine, so it will be important to create a very vivid picture in your mind's eye.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Think",
                "Alternative": "Consider"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Then, the beggar realizes that he is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. You're burying {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} in a coffin alive and all he can think of is himself.",
                "mnemonic": "What is the beggar {tooltip:Kanji:think}ing of? A thought bubble pops up into existence near his head. In it is a picture of {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}! He's thinking that if {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} was here, he'd save him. Oh, if only {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} could save us all!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:mouth} inside a {tooltip:Radical:mouth}. But if you look even closer (not actually, but we're pretending), you can see another mouth inside that mouth... and another one inside of that one! It keeps going and going. Can you count the number of {tooltip:Kanji:times} there's a mouth inside a mouth? This kanji also means {tooltip:Kanji:revolve} too. Think of each \"time\" a thing happens, it loops back around and comes back to the beginning, revolving around again another time.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself counting and counting smaller and smaller mouths inside of each other, recording the number of times you can find a mouth inside another mouth. Dig deeper and deeper until it feels ridiculous how small the mouths are getting. Be sure to focus on the counting and the number of times you find one. Now, how many mouths is this times two, because your mouth is like this too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Times",
                "Alternative": "Revolve"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your kayak is slashing and dipping through the revolving mouths, going down and down more times than you can count!",
                "mnemonic": "If you're having a hard time wrapping your head around the infinite number of {tooltip:Kanji:times} these mouths {tooltip:Kanji:revolve}, just picture yourself in a little {tooltip:Reading:kay}ak ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044}) going around and down through the mouths."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:hat} decorated with {tooltip:Radical:fins} and (presumably fish) {tooltip:Radical:mouth}s on it. Who wears strange hats like this? Turns out, the {tooltip:Kanji:valley} people are the ones who wear these. I'm talking about the \"Valley Girls\" of California, Hollywood / LA. They're into the crazy fashion, and they'll wear anything if it's deemed \"cool\" or something like that.",
            "hints": "Imagine a bunch of Valley Girls walking around with these strange hats. Fins and fish mouths... what a strange new fad.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Valley"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u306b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u305b",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What a jerk he is. Imagine the deep tan lines on TAN-E as well. He's the epitome of robot laziness.",
                "mnemonic": "Hanging around with all the {tooltip:Kanji:Valley} Girls in the sunny area of LA is also a robot. It's WALL-E's distant (and lazy, lounging) relative, {tooltip:Reading:TAN-E} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u306b}). He sits around getting a tan in LA with the Valley Girls while his cousin picks up trash."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:samurai} with a {tooltip:Radical:flag} on a {tooltip:Radical:stick}. On his flag is this symbol, the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:voice}. Why does he have that there? He feels like his Shogun isn't giving him and his fellow Samurai a voice, so he's brought a flag with the word \"voice\" written on it to protest.",
            "hints": "Imagine him and other samurai with their flags on sticks waving them around shouting things like \"we want a voice in politics!\" etc., etc.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Voice"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3048",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Then you ask him out on a date. He still plays coy with you... one of those samurai, I guess.",
                "mnemonic": "Once you start asking the samurai more specific questions about how he wants more {tooltip:Kanji:voice} he starts playing {tooltip:Reading:coy} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3048}) with you. He doesn't really know what he wants, he's just here for the sake of protesting."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:west} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:west} kanji are the same. Isn't that nice?",
            "hints": "Make sure you know all those radicals, will make your life more pleasant.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "West"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044, \u3055\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself fighting your way West, your saber shining in the light of the sun as it sets in front of you. You'll protect your home from the West if it takes everything you and your saber have left!",
                "mnemonic": "People are attacking from the {tooltip:Kanji:West}, so you pull out your {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}) and beat them back. You keep pushing further and further West until you reach the ocean and there's nowhere left for them to run."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Our {tooltip:Radical:leader} has a {tooltip:Radical:lip ring}. Wait, our leader has a lip ring? {tooltip:Kanji:WHAT}??",
            "hints": "Think of our president (or your prime minister, or dictator, or whatever) and imagine this person appearing on television one morning with a big ol' lip ring. Feel surprised by it. Just say \"What??\" over and over again. You want to have the feeling of \"what\" in you when you imagine this - that'll help you to remember this kanji's meaning.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "What"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u306b, \u306a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Make this one vivid and scary. He's eating the naan (that's your {span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3093}), and then he screams at the naan but gets overwhelmed with pain (that's the {span:lang=ja:\u306a\u306b}). Smell the naan (you're there) and see the blood gushing out of his/her lip. It's terrifying. How did the naan even catch on his lip ring anyways?",
                "mnemonic": "The leader with his lip ring is now eating some {tooltip:Reading:naan} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3093}) and curry. It's delicious, of course... but then he gets it caught on his lip ring, and tears half his lip off. He screams: \"{tooltip:Reading:Nannnnn eeeeeeeeeehhh}!!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u306b}) in anger at the naan and curry."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:life} radical is without the slide (as it sometimes is), but when you combine that with the {tooltip:Radical:winter} radical, you have life during winter. What gives you life during the winter? It's the {tooltip:Kanji:wheat} you store away.",
            "hints": "Imagine you're starving. It's cold and you've run out of food. You don't know what you're going to do. If you don't find something, you'll lose your life. Then, you break open a barrel, and wheat pours out. It's beautiful. You just found some life in the middle of winter.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wheat",
                "Alternatives": "Barley, Oats"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080\u304e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the disappointment. You go from finding life to losing it all... now you have no hope for the winter :( Also, keep in mind that {span:lang=ja:\u3080\u304e} and mug aren't super-alike, so you'll have to use it to get  close enough to remember the actual reading, {span:lang=ja:\u3080\u304e}.",
                "mnemonic": "You found your {tooltip:Kanji:wheat}. Thank God. You'll survive. You have to take the wheat back to your house, though. On your way, you get {tooltip:Reading:mug}ged ({span:lang=ja:\u3080\u304e})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is someone with a {tooltip:Radical:bow} and a {tooltip:Radical:stick}, wearing {tooltip:Radical:horns}, going down a {tooltip:Radical:slide}. What type of person do you imagine? I'd say someone who's an immature boy. That would be your {tooltip:Kanji:younger brother}.",
            "hints": "Just pretend you have a younger brother for now, even if you don't. Also be sure to imagine this person really vividly. He is a stereotypical little boy, playing dress up with horns and a bow and stick (he can't have an arrow, that's dangerous), and he's going down a slide too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Younger Brother",
                "Alternative": "Little Brother"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u3044, \u3067, \u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3068\u3046\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the bright red, blue, green and purple dye in your younger brother's hair. He's put so much on that he's dyed half his face too. He's going to be in trouble when he gets home!",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:younger brother} loves playing dress up so much that he's now started {tooltip:Reading:dye}ing his hair all kinds of colors. Imagine the bright red, blue, green and purple dye in his hair."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:rest} from {tooltip:Kanji:school} you are {tooltip:Vocabulary:absent from school}. This is only for very long absences though, not a day or a week, but months or years. Think about it like taking an extended leave of absence from school.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Absent From School",
                "Alternatives": "Absence From School, School Absence, Leave Of Absence",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046\u304c\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3085\u3046\u304c\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "17516-subject-2793.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
