                        "file": "37429-subject-2806.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You have your body. It's nice - looking good! What would really mess up your body? It would be a {tooltip:Reading:car raider} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3089\u3060}). I'm talking about a dude who is a raider of some kind driving a car. If he runs into your body, you're done for, so watch out for the car raider. \n{splitParent}Of course, this mnemonic is only meant to get you close to the reading. Hopefully it is close enough to get you to the actual reading, {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3089\u3060}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u3075\u308d\u306b\u5165\u308b\u3068\u3001\u306f\u3058\u3081\u306b\u4f53\u3092\u3042\u3089\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When I take a bath, I wash my body first."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b8\u30e3\u30de\u30eb\u3063\u3066\u4f55\u3067\u305d\u3093\u306a\u306b\u4f53\u304c\u3084\u308f\u3089\u304b\u3044\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "Jamal, why is your body so flexible?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u306a\u305c\u3060\u304b\u3001\u4f53\u4e2d\u304c\u304b\u3086\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "My entire body is so itchy for some reason."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

