{
            "mnemonic": "You have the {tooltip:Kanji:below} {tooltip:Kanji:town}. Does this sort of sound familiar? We have another word for it in English, but it's essentially the same thing: {tooltip:Vocabulary:downtown}. It isn't the downtown you might be used to though. In Japan, this is an old word that was used for the commercial districts literally, physically down (lower than) the main city. So picture an old, urban Japanese area!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Downtown",
                "Alternative": "Backstreets",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
