{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:skin} on the {tooltip:Kanji:meat} is kind of like the outer shell. It's not very nice, and people who eat only meat skin tend to use {tooltip:Vocabulary:sarcasm} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:irony}. That being said, Japanese people don't really understand sarcasm. So, maybe that's why \"meat skin\" means \"sarcasm.\" Is this ironic? Now I'm not even sure.",
