                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "17694-subject-2743.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You have a ton of {tooltip:Vocabulary:sunlight} where you live. This creates heat. With this sunlight heat you're able to make your favorite food in the world: {tooltip:Reading:hickory} ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u304b\u308a}) smoked bacon. Mmm, taste that delicious bacon.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u592a\u3088\u3046\u306e\u5149\u304c\u307e\u3076\u3057\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u30ab\u30fc\u30c6\u30f3\u3092\u3057\u3081\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "The light from the sun is blinding, so please close the curtains."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6708\u306e\u5149\u306b\u3066\u3089\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3001\u304b\u306a\u3048\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306e\u6b6f\u304c\u307e\u308b\u3067\u30d1\u30fc\u30eb\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "In the moonlight, your teeth look just like pearls, Kanae."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5317\u671d\u9bae\u3067\u884c\u65b9\u4e0d\u660e\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5b50\u4f9b\u306b\u306f\u3001\u307e\u3060\u5fae\u304b\u306b\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u5149\u304c\u6b8b\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "There is still a slight glimmer of hope left for your child who was lost in North Korea."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What happens when {tooltip:Kanji:light} travels a {tooltip:Kanji:year}? You have a {tooltip:Vocabulary:light-year}.",
