{
            "mnemonic": "The {span:lang=ja:\u304a} is an honorific that makes this word a bit more fancy. When you're talking about money you gotta be fancy, after all. So, you're basically saying \"gold\" in a nicer way. What was gold back in the day? It was {tooltip:Vocabulary:money}.",
