                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}When you think of the word \"same\" think {tooltip:Vocabulary:same} {tooltip:Reading:owner} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u306a}). You're looking at a restaurant that has a sign that says, \"New owners!\" However, when you walk in you see it's the same terrible owner you remember from before. What a liar.\n"
