                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the on'yomi reading which you learned with the kanji. This is probably because this word gets attached to numbers usually, which makes it behave more like jukugo. So, you can have {span:lang=ja:\uff11\u56de}, {span:lang=ja:\uff12\u56de}, {span:lang=ja:\uff13\u56de}, or even {span:lang=ja:\uff11\uff10\uff10\u56de} if you're into that sort of thing.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u4e00\u56de\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
