{
            "mnemonic": "You know this is a verb because it ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound. The kanji for this word is {tooltip:Kanji:right} or {tooltip:Kanji:success}, so what's the verb form of that? Turns out it's a ton of things. Like, a crazy amount of things. I tried narrowing it down for you, but it will still be a lot. This word tends to be about getting an answer right. As in, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be right} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be on target}. It means many other things too, but I think these are the two meanings you'll see the most, so focus on those.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Right",
                "Alternatives": "To Be On Target, To Touch, To Hit",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305f\u308b"
