                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304f} portion. In order to do that let's think about something that you're going to make. Imagine something really awesome. You complete it and look at your masterpiece. It's amazing. You realize right then and there that it's {tooltip:Reading:too coo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304f}) for the general public to see. You proceed to smash it. It's way too cool.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3070\u3093\u3054\u306f\u3093\u306b\u3084\u304d\u305d\u3070\u3092\u4f5c\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
