                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3042} part but let's include the {span:lang=ja:\u3046} as well for this one. Who do you want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to meet} more than anyone? Think about it. Then, imagine meeting them. The first thing they do is grab your arm and pinch it. You yell out \"{tooltip:Reading:OW}!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3046}) and they laugh and run away.\n"
