                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u307e} portion. Who would mix things for you (like cakes and other goodies) growing up? That would be your {tooltip:Reading:Ma} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u30d7\u3092\u3088\u304f\u4ea4\u305c\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
