                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "37372-subject-2838.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3044} we use the word \"eagle.\" \n{splitParent}You're trying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to say} something, but every time you try to say anything an {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) swoops down and pecks at your face then flies away. Just imagine yourself saying tiny bits of words, then an eagle crashing down on your face. Then, you wait in silence. Nothing happens. You try to say something again, and the eagle swoops down on you again.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3086\u3063\u304f\u308a\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please say it slowly."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3042\u308a\u304c\u3068\u3046\u3063\u3066\u3048\u3044\u3054\u3067\u4f55\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "How can I say, \"Thank you always,\" in English?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b8\u30a7\u30a4\u30af\u306b\u3001\u8db3\u3092\u8e0f\u3093\u3067\u3054\u3081\u3093\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3064\u3082\u308a\u306a\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "Are you going to say sorry to Jake for stepping on his foot?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

