                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You are {tooltip:Vocabulary:to separate} a couple of children that really have fun together. When you separate them, they begin to cry and scream: {tooltip:Reading:WAAAAAAAAAHHHH} ({span:lang=ja:\u308f}). Poor kids.\n"
