                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u305f} portion. In order to do that, think of yourself standing up a huge sign. On it, written in big words:\n{linebreak}\"{tooltip:Reading:ta} ta ({span:lang=ja:\u305f})!\"\n"
