                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You come to a stop sign and decide {tooltip:Vocabulary:to stop} because the sign has a picture of a {tooltip:Reading:toe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068}) on it. This toe looks eerily like a toe your Ma ({span:lang=ja:\u307e}) has too... and your Ma always taught you to stop and look both ways before crossing her toes.\n"
