                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You look at your younger brother. He's a scheming one. He's smiling up at you. Why? Because he's lit a firecracker on your foot. It explodes, sending your toe flying. You yell {tooltip:Reading:\"OH. Toe? TOE!\"} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3068\u3046\u3068}) as you realize what's going on.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u5f1f\u306f\u3001\u30c6\u30ec\u30d3\u3092\u898b\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "My little brother doesn\u2019t watch TV."
                },
                {
