                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u9752\u5e74\u306f\u3001\u4e0b\u5fc3\u304c\u3042\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3084\u3089\u3057\u3044\u7b11\u307f\u3092\u6d6e\u304b\u3079\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u96a0\u305d\u3046\u3068\u3059\u308b\u306e\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Why do youths in Japan try to hide their nasty smiles when they\u2019re up to something?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "First of all, there's a cross making up the middle, which automatically makes this a religion-based radical. That cross is the frame of someone's body and the things coming off of it are wings. This is an {tooltip:Radical:angel}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Angel"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This looks like a tail with some hairs coming off of it. It shouldn't be confused with fingers though, because it's curved, and the things sticking out are more erratic, like hair or fur would be. That's why this radical is the {tooltip:Radical:animal} radical.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Animal"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a little speck of something on your plate ({span:lang=ja:\u76bf}). \"What is that?\" you ask. Oh no... that speck is {tooltip:Radical:BLOOD}!!! I hope it's blood from a nosebleed you suddenly have and not someone else's blood. (Your waiter is probably gonna get fired, btw.) At least your platelets should stop the bleeding soon. Haha, get it? PLATE-lets? Japanese blood jokes.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Blood"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks like the fire from the burner of a stove or the steam coming up off of a pot of water. That's because this is the {tooltip:Radical:boil} radical. You need to boil a bunch of water over some flames. This radical looks like all of those parts at once!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Boil"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:box} is open. There could be any number of things inside, but for now all you need to know is the meaning of this radical, which is box.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Box"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You already learned the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u5e02}, which means city. We're treating it as a radical too, since it pops up in many other kanji. When used as a radical, it still means {tooltip:Radical:city}. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "City"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a lid on a lion. And you're stuck under the lid with the lion, which means you will surely meet your {tooltip:Radical:death}. Or if you don't want to die, think of the poor lion. If you leave a lion under a lid for too long, death will come for it too. Either way, somebody's gonna die today.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Death"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You put on your hat and go outside to kick something white. It's a big white goose and you killed it with your kick. That's because you're going to cook and {tooltip:Radical:eat} it. Yum!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Eat"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Someone has a toe in their mouth. They are a fortune teller telling your {tooltip:Radical:fortune}. But for her to do it, she has to take one of your toes and taste it. This better be a good fortune for you to let someone put your foot in their mouth.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fortune"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a tree with a slide cutting off the top. What do you cut off the top of trees and plants? The {tooltip:Radical:grain}s. Imagine taking a sickle and slicing the grains off rice or wheat. The plant you leave behind will look like this radical. It's a sign that you got a grain of some sort from it.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Grain"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is like one of those {tooltip:Radical:jet}s that have the little nose-wings going on too. Imagine you're looking at the jet from the top down, this is what it would look like. It's also why this is the jet radical.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Jet"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a {tooltip:Radical:knife}. See how it has two sharp sides? And there's a little handle at the bottom for the... well the handle. Be careful you don't cut yourself!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Knife"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a person in a prison. Why is this person in prison? Because they {tooltip:Radical:lack} the stuff humans need to be around other humans. If you're lacking something (kindness, self-control, etc.) you may do something that makes other people put you in prison. Try to fix what you lack so this won't happen to you.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lack"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:ladle} scooping up two drops of liquid. See the handle and the scoop part of the ladle? Imagine ladling some water into your mouth. Mmm.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ladle"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This L-shaped radical is the {tooltip:Radical:lion} radical, because \"L is for Lion.\" It also looks like a lion's mouth being opened really, really wide. Imagine a lion opening its mouth to yawn. It looks like this radical!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lion"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a modified key radical on top of the kick radical. You kick the key as far as you can, then measure the distance. How {tooltip:Radical:long} did it travel? How long will it take you to find it? How long will you be in trouble for kicking a key into the woods?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Long"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is just like the katakana character \"ma\" ({span:lang=ja:\u30de}). So let's keep things simple and make the radical {tooltip:Radical:mama}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mama"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are some horns on the ground that you want for yourself. You pick them up and you attach them to your {tooltip:Radical:neck}. Imagine these horns sticking out of your neck. No one can slit your throat now that your neck is protected.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Neck"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a {tooltip:Radical:sheep} and you're looking at it from above. See the two ears and the body of the sheep going back (with all its wool poking out to the side) and then the little tail sticking out the back. What a cute sheep!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sheep"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Something is sticking out of a mouth. Something with a thousand little tastebuds on it. It's your {tooltip:Radical:tongue}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tongue"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The evening radical is under the ground. Who's doing things underground at night? The {tooltip:Radical:Yakuza}. Picture Yakuza members sneaking around in the subway, or in the sewers. They're definitely up to no good down there.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Yakuza"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Kings} with {tooltip:Radical:hats}. Did you know that {tooltip:Kanji:all} kings wear hats?",
            "hints": "Think of as many kings as you can think of. Guess what, every single one of them (aka {tooltip:Kanji:all} of them) wear hats! Think of strange hats, funny hats, and normal hats. Just make sure you're amazed by the fact they all are wearing them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "All",
                "Alternative": "Whole"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3079, \u307e\u3063\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "To add to this story and make it more memorable, you can imagine the other kings getting upset, saying things like \"{tooltip:Kanji:All} kings must wear hats! You are no king!\" The king of {tooltip:Reading:Zen} Buddhism just ignores them and begins to meditate.",
                "mnemonic": "But, as you're going through all the kings, it turns out not {tooltip:Kanji:all} of them have hats after all. The last one you come to does not have a hat. He is the king of {tooltip:Reading:Zen} ({span:lang=ja:\u305c\u3093}) Buddhism. He has simple clothes and a shaved head, unlike all the other fancy kings standing around nearby."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:loiter} around to {tooltip:Radical:poop} in {tooltip:Radical:winter} you never know what could be happening {tooltip:Kanji:behind} you. {tooltip:Kanji:After} you're done you could turn {tooltip:Kanji:back} to see something really crazy that you missed because you took so long to poop in the cold.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to loiter while you poop in the winter. You're just trying to take your time as you squat over the snow, but soon you hear things behind you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Behind",
                "Alternatives": "After, Back, Later"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054, \u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3057, \u3042\u3068, \u306e\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Godzilla and {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} were going at it behind you the entire time you were just lazily taking a poop in the snow?! Ahh, that's so embarrassing! And also dangerous, they could have crushed you! You should look behind you more.",
                "mnemonic": "You finally look {tooltip:Kanji:behind} you and see {tooltip:Reading:Go}dzilla ({span:lang=ja:\u3054}) and a giant {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} having a violent battle {tooltip:Kanji:back} there!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:blood} radical and {tooltip:Kanji:blood} are the same in looks as well as in meaning.",
            "hints": "There'll be some bad blood between us if you're not studying your radicals, especially when they're the same like this kanji!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Blood"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel the relief that you didn't just lick up someone's blood. Taste the ketsup taste, too. It's pretty good. Not quite ketchup, but not quite catsup. Yum!",
                "mnemonic": "To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3064}, we use the word \"ketsup.\" The perfect mix of ketchup and catsup!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under the {tooltip:Radical:ground}, which you dug into, you found two great finds. You found {tooltip:Kanji:both} a {tooltip:Radical:mountain} and a {tooltip:Radical:head}, two strange things to find underground.",
            "hints": "You'll want to focus on the part where you find {tooltip:Kanji:both}, not so much the things themselves. Think about how you can't believe you did so well finding both things at once. Usually you only find one or the other when you're searching.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Both"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Also think... \"What's that row boat doing here?\" But, it's your only hope, so you have to focus on it really hard.",
                "mnemonic": "But, you dig too deep and water flows into where you are. Your only hope is a {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat floating off in the distance."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} AND the {tooltip:Radical:moon} are out? With both their light-powers combined, it's incredibly {tooltip:Kanji:bright} outside.",
            "hints": "Look up at both of them, hanging out in the sky together. Make them super bright, so bright you have to shield your eyes.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bright"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042, \u3042\u304b, \u3042\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If your months don't match up with this too well (if you're down in the southern hemisphere, for example) then you'll have to imagine all this up in the Northern Hemisphere. Sorry about that, South Hemisphere folks.",
                "mnemonic": "When do things start to get {tooltip:Kanji:bright} outside? I'd say when things start getting sunny, and that is the month of {tooltip:Reading:May} ({span:lang=ja:\u3081\u3044})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a {tooltip:Radical:lid} covering all the {tooltip:Radical:mouth}s that are too {tooltip:Radical:small} to feed themselves, forming the {tooltip:Kanji:capital}. All of the small mouths come together and create a place where everyone can support each other.",
            "hints": "Picture the capital of your country. How many mouths have come together to support each other there? A thousand? A million? More?!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Capital"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3084\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "When you think of the capital, think of {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}!",
                "mnemonic": "To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046} we use the Japanese city, Kyoto, which is spelled {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. It was once the capital of Japan! It was soooo full of mouths that came together that it was the capital for a long, long time."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} with a {tooltip:Radical:spoon} is a powerful thing. Even something like a spoon when given to the right man or woman can make great {tooltip:Kanji:change} in the world.",
            "hints": "Imagine your leader-hero holding a spoon out, then doing something awesome with it to totally {tooltip:Kanji:change} everything for the better. It's amazing the change this person can do with such a blunt, small, device!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Change"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Of course, doing something like this is utterly amazing. Feel amazed in your imagination, because if you don't, then it'll be hard to remember the reading for this kanji. If you are amazed, you'll know that spoons going to cars = the reading is {span:lang=ja:\u304b}, so make sure you take the time to be amazed.",
                "mnemonic": "Then, this hero of yours takes their spoon and says some magic words into it, {tooltip:Kanji:changing} it into a {tooltip:Reading:car} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of the {tooltip:Radical:king} extends all the way around him (like in this kanji). Where his mouth reaches, that is his {tooltip:Kanji:country}, give or take a few {tooltip:Radical:drop}s.",
            "hints": "Imagine his talking taking physical form. As he talks, waves extend out from him, and stop right at the border of his country before getting to the next one.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Country"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u306b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Would you drink that much soda for breakfast? Now this king says he wants to pass a law requiring everyone in the country to drink nothing but Coke! That's crazy!",
                "mnemonic": "Turns out the king of this {tooltip:Kanji:country} loves drinking {tooltip:Reading:Coke} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u304f}). Every morning that big mouth of his swallows a whole 2-liter bottle of Coke for breakfast."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You scoop some {tooltip:Radical:grain}s into a {tooltip:Radical:ladle} to do {tooltip:Kanji:science}. You're doing experiments on these grains in your science {tooltip:Kanji:course}.",
            "hints": "Imagine carefully ladling grains into different piles so you can do science experiments on them. This course is going to make you an expert. You'll be the best in this department!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Course",
                "Alternatives": "Science, Department"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "From your science meddling, these grains grow huge, red, and sprout sports cars when they're ripe. This is the true power of science!",
                "mnemonic": "Using your {tooltip:Kanji:science} skills, the right temperatures and measurements, you manage to get these grains to grow into a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). This is the science {tooltip:Kanji:department}'s special car now!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:death} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:death} are the same.",
            "hints": "This thing is deceased. It ain't alive anymore.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Death",
                "Alternative": "Deceased"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You didn't want to know what would cause your death, you say? Well that's a shame. I guess you could try to avoid bowling from now on, but that won't do any good. Mark my words, your death will be bowling-related.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:death} will be because of a {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) accident. Oh, you didn't know? You're going to be hit by a giant bowling ball and crushed flat."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the {tooltip:Radical:yakuza} hands you a {tooltip:Radical:spoon}, {tooltip:Kanji:death} is coming for you. It's the death spoon, a sign that the yakuza is coming to cause your death.",
            "hints": "This spoon isn't for pudding, it's for death!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Death"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the death sheep. He looks like a black shadow, and he has a scar on his face. He's holding a bunch of spoons, from all the other people the yakuza marked for death!",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Death} comes in the form of a {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}). The death sheep works for the yakuza, and kills anyone who has their spoon."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a close-up of a {tooltip:Radical:leaf} in a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} inside of a {tooltip:Radical:box}. Wait, it's not a box, this whole thing is just a {tooltip:Kanji:drawing}.",
            "hints": "Look closely at this box-shaped drawing. See each little stroke, smell the paper and the lead.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Drawing",
                "Alternatives": "Picture, Painting"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c, \u304b\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the entire drawing. There's a cock sitting on a gargoyle, watching over this rice paddy. It's actually quite beautiful and idyllic.",
                "mnemonic": "The drawing seems to have something else in the rice paddy, behind the leaf. You realize the drawing is actually of a {tooltip:Reading:ga}rgoyle ({span:lang=ja:\u304c}) and a {tooltip:Reading:cock} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304f}). You see the cock sitting on top of the gargoyle, crowing into the sky."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:dirt} {tooltip:Radical:alligator} lives in the {tooltip:Kanji:earth}, not the water. They can swim through the earth itself! Which is pretty scary.",
            "hints": "Imagine seeing the earth moving as a dirt alligator rises out from the ground. You should run.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Earth",
                "Alternatives": "Ground, Land"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061, \u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you ever see someone throwing cheese on the ground, now you know why. They aren't crazy, they're saving us humans from what's lurking under the earth.",
                "mnemonic": "The only way to keep this dirt alligator from dragging you under the {tooltip:Kanji:earth} and eating you is to feed it {tooltip:Reading:chee}se ({span:lang=ja:\u3061}). That way it won't lead you to a horrific death under the earth by dragging you under and spinning you around until you eat dirt (literally)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Behind that {tooltip:Radical:tree} the {tooltip:Radical:sun} is rising in the {tooltip:Kanji:east}. The sun always rises in the east, so if you head that way, past the tree, you'll be going east too.",
            "hints": "Picture the sun behind the tree, don't picture the sun alone, you'll burn your eyes. It's slowly coming up behind it. Now think: where does the sun rise? In the east!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "East"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u304c\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "When you think about East Japan think about {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. And if you're bad at geography, just look at a map for a while. Or, stand outside in the morning, watch the sun rise behind the trees, and point that way. That's east, it's where {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} is!",
                "mnemonic": "You walk {tooltip:Kanji:east} for a few hours until you finally come to a city. It's {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. Oh! {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} is in the east. I get it now!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical for {tooltip:Radical:eat} and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:eat} are the same! Lucky you.",
            "hints": "If you know the radical, you basically know the meaning(s) of this kanji. There is a second meaning added to it, though, and that is {tooltip:Kanji:meal}. Just think about the things you eat? What are they? In the simplest form, they are just meals. So, if you know \"eat\" you should be able to remember \"meal\" as well.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Eat",
                "Alternative": "Meal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f, \u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "So, do you keep eating and keep getting shocked? Or do you not eat and continue to starve? What is worse? Obviously you're in one of the Saw movies, or something, too, so feel the fear. What will you choose? Life with shocks or death from hunger?",
                "mnemonic": "Thank goodness, you finally get to {tooltip:Kanji:eat} your {tooltip:Kanji:meal}. You're so hungry. Someone has been starving you and now they've finally given you food. Unfortunately, though, every time you take a bite, you get a {tooltip:Reading:shock} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u304f}) from somewhere."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You accidentally stab your {tooltip:Radical:cross} into the {tooltip:Radical:eye} of a {tooltip:Radical:lion}. This is a terrible thing you did and you need to {tooltip:Kanji:fix} it right now. I'll be {tooltip:Kanji:direct} with you, this is something you have to fix on your own.",
            "hints": "How will you fix this mistake though? Maybe if you build a time machine you can go back and stop yourself from throwing your cross around so carelessly. Whatever you do, focus on how important it is to fix the mistake, more than anything.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fix",
                "Alternative": "Direct"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u304f, \u3058\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You're relieved! You don't know how to fix a choking, eye-stabbed lion, but you can absolutely fix a ROBOTIC one. Robots are fixable.",
                "mnemonic": "As you try to {tooltip:Kanji:fix} the lion's eye, it starts to {tooltip:Reading:choke} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u304f}) and make what can only be described as a {tooltip:Reading:jiki}jikijiki sound ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u304d}). Through its choking jikijiki sounds, it coughs up a gear. Wait. Is this a machine lion?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are some {tooltip:Radical:horns} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} and a {tooltip:Radical:moon} {tooltip:Radical:knife} in {tooltip:Kanji:front} of you. When you try to move, they always rotate around with you, staying right in front. You can't escape these objects, for some reason.",
            "hints": "Perhaps it's some kind of magic, but you don't care. Why are these strange objects always in front of me? Why won't they stay put? This will get pretty freaky after a while. Try to run. Try to hide. Spin around. Do whatever you need to do. No matter what, these objects are always in front.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Front",
                "Alternative": "Before"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Go ahead and do some Zen Buddhist meditation. Maybe it'll help you to remember this kanji's reading better (and calm your mind so you're ready for the next kanji!).",
                "mnemonic": "You're going crazy with these things in {tooltip:Kanji:front} of you all the time. You finally seek the help of a {tooltip:Reading:Zen} ({span:lang=ja:\u305c\u3093}) master, who tells you that meditation will save you from this curse. You try it out, and sure enough, the objects are gone! It worked!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:narwhal} and a {tooltip:Radical:moon} is all you {tooltip:Kanji:have}. Imagine one of each under your arms.",
            "hints": "You don't have anything else. This is it. All you have. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Have"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3046, \u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "They came and took your things. Now they have all your stuff, and you only have the moon and a narwhal. You don't have much anymore, but at least you have these things still.",
                "mnemonic": "Everything you {tooltip:Kanji:have} (except the narwhal and the moon) were taken from you by a roving gang of {tooltip:Reading:you}ths ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3046})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:private} {tooltip:Radical:grain}s are meant to stay {tooltip:Kanji:private}! You shouldn't be sharing them with the whole town, they're just for you.",
            "hints": "Look at your private grains. Who are those for? Why, they're for I!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "I",
                "Alternative": "Private"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f\u305f\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The moral of the story is: don't let a sheep sneak into your private stash of things just for you (I). I'm sure this is a metaphor for something important...",
                "mnemonic": "You're getting into the zone, thinking about yourself ({tooltip:Kanji:I}) and how much you love having things that are {tooltip:Kanji:private} and just yours, when you realize there is a {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) in this grain bag. And it's eating all of your (I's) private grains. No!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Just before saying something important, you take an {tooltip:Radical:arrow} to the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} which seals your lips together, making it so you can't talk. Someone doesn't want you to share what you {tooltip:Kanji:know} with someone else.",
            "hints": "Imagine being so surprised by this arrow. Then, think of all the things you know that need to be said and told to everyone. Maybe you have information about nuke codes. Maybe you have information that will save the President. Whatever it is, make sure you know important things that need to be said (but also things that people want to prevent you from saying, even if it means shooting you in the mouth with an arrow).",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Know"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Try saying the words \"cheese\" with an arrow in your mouth. What would that sound like? Go ahead and pretend out loud.",
                "mnemonic": "To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3061} we use the word \"cheese.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} of {tooltip:Radical:tongue}s is coming at you. As it washes over you, you feel each individual tongue moving around on your body, licking you. They make you feel so... {tooltip:Kanji:lively}!",
            "hints": "Your entire body wakes up, you feel so lively! The tongues are making you more aware of yourself and your surroundings than you've ever been. You want to dance, you want to sing, you want to live your life.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lively"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You and the cats are running around playing together, because you can't seem to get the lively feelings to stop. You have to get the energy out, but the cats have sharp claws and they're scratching you.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:lively} feeling isn't just happening to you, the tongue tsunami is licking it into all of the {tooltip:Reading:cats} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3064}) in your neighborhood too!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:long} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:long} kanji are the same! ",
            "hints": "As long as you know the radical long, you know the kanji long as well.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Long",
                "Alternative": "Leader"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u306f",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "{tooltip:Kanji:Long} isn't an idea that's easy to imagine in any specific sense, but you can try some other things too, as long as it gets associated with Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou}. For the most part, when you see a kanji with the radical {span:lang=ja:\u9577} the reading will be {span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}.",
                "mnemonic": "You see a very {tooltip:Kanji:long} person. It's Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}), who has made herself long, like her street. \"I made myself long so I can watch more of the street, my domain. I'm the {tooltip:Kanji:leader} of these streets. Watch yourself not-long person,\" says Mrs. Chou."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Twenty} {tooltip:Radical:mouths} are together. That's a lot of mouths. What do they do? They sing beautiful {tooltip:Kanji:music} together.",
            "hints": "Listen to the twenty mouths. They sound great. Have them sing your favorite music. Also note that this kanji also means \"bend.\" Imagine the music coming out at you {tooltip:Kanji:bend}ing all around in strange shapes through the air.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Music",
                "Alternative": "Bend"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine how you feel as they cloak you with music. Feel the music all around you, enveloping you. Become the music itself.",
                "mnemonic": "The twenty mouths make so much {tooltip:Kanji:music} that they literally {tooltip:Reading:cloak you} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u304f}) with it. They cloak you with the music."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:neck} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:neck} are exactly the same!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Neck"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3073",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Look at yourself in a mirror as the cool beans make their way down your neck. You can see them, like little ants marching all the way down to your tummy.",
                "mnemonic": "The only thing you do with your {tooltip:Kanji:neck} is use it to swallow lots of {tooltip:Reading:coo}l {tooltip:Reading:bea}ns ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3073}). Mm mm. Feel those cool, cool beans sliding down your neck. You don't really taste them, but you know they're there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:lack} {tooltip:Radical:ice}. So you go to the store and see if they have any. Nope, no ice. So, now you go to the {tooltip:Kanji:next} store. Is there ice here? Nope. Next!",
            "hints": "Feel a little frustrated you can't find ice. Have the words \"{tooltip:Kanji:next} next next\" echoing through your head as you go from store to store, irritated.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Next"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine him coming down. Imagine your surprise. He hands you the ice, and it's cold. You thank him, and he flies away.",
                "mnemonic": "To remember the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3058}, we used the word \"Jesus\" - Finally, when you're at the last store in existence, you decide it's time to pray to {tooltip:Reading:Je}sus ({span:lang=ja:\u3058}), asking for a miracle. He comes down from the heavens with ice in his hands."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} is wearing a {tooltip:Radical:lid} and is standing outside in {tooltip:Radical:winter}. Plus it's raining and she's covered in {tooltip:Radical:drop}s of water. On top of all this, it's {tooltip:Kanji:night}.",
            "hints": "If it helps, you can come up with a reason why she's outside in the winter at night. Also, why is she wearing a lid on her head? Probably because she's protecting her people from something that comes at night.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Night",
                "Alternative": "Evening"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088, \u3088\u308b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the Yankees stomping towards the leader, baseball bats in hand, blood on their faces. They're here to eat, and nobody will stop them. Feel the fear of their approach. Will you survive another night with them on the prowl?",
                "mnemonic": "Question is, what is she protecting them from during the {tooltip:Kanji:night}? Turns out, it's the {tooltip:Reading:Ya}nkees ({span:lang=ja:\u3084}) baseball team. They're out for blood, and only the leader can protect us."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The only {tooltip:Radical:woman} in this {tooltip:Radical:city} is your {tooltip:Kanji:older sister}. She's the only woman surrounded by a bunch of men, but she's following her dreams in the big city.",
            "hints": "You want to go to the city someday, but you're not old enough yet, like your older sister is.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Older Sister",
                "Alternatives": "Big Sister, Elder Sister"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a, \u3042\u306d, \u306d\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture your older sister and her sheep walking through the city. Everyone turns to stare at them, because they're the only ones of their kind.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:older sister} may have moved to the city, but she kept her pet {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) with her. Now the only woman in the city is your older sister, and the only sheep is her pet."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:fortune} {tooltip:Radical:boil}s down to a single {tooltip:Kanji:point} in time. One point in time determines how the rest of your future will go.",
            "hints": "Imagine actually going somewhere to get your fortune told and watching a big boiling pot of goo. As it boils, it melts down to a single point at the very bottom. Where this point is determines your future.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Point"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Is the ten spot good? Are you going to live a long life or does this point mean you're only going to live ten more years?! Ahh!",
                "mnemonic": "As you stare at the {tooltip:Kanji:point}, you watch in awe as it moves to the {tooltip:Reading:ten} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3093}) spot in a long series of numbers."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "With a {tooltip:Radical:roof} over her head, a {tooltip:Radical:woman} can {tooltip:Kanji:relax}. She doesn't have to worry about rain or snow or finding a safe place to sleep. The roof also happened to be super {tooltip:Kanji:cheap}, so she can even relax about her finances.",
            "hints": "Picture the super relaxed woman lounging under her cheap but sturdy roof. Ah, she doesn't have a care in the world!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Relax",
                "Alternative": "Cheap"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Think about it: anchovies cost next to nothing, they come in cans, you don't have to cook them or cut them up. You just munch them down. There's nothing more cheap and relaxing than eating anchovies under your own roof.",
                "mnemonic": "As she {tooltip:Kanji:relax}es, she pulls out the {tooltip:Kanji:cheap}est, most relaxing food in the world {tooltip:Reading:an}chovies ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} you've made a {tooltip:Radical:roof} over the {tooltip:Radical:ground} where you can be in {tooltip:Radical:private}. This is your {tooltip:Kanji:room}! That's really all a room is, you know? A covered, private place where you can have some time to yourself.",
            "hints": "Imagine the room you live in now. Take away all the stuff and you're left with a roof and the dirt on the ground. It's your own little private place.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Room"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine watching the little shih tzu come into your room and lift its leg to all your things. This isn't fair. The shih tzu has its own room to pee in. Why does it have to ruin yours?",
                "mnemonic": "The only problem with your {tooltip:Kanji:room} is that you can't always be alone. Because of your dad's {tooltip:Reading:shih tzu} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3064}). The shih tzu likes to come into your room and pee everywhere. Ruining your privacy completely."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} is coming, so you point your {tooltip:Radical:gun} out the {tooltip:Radical:window} at it. \"You better turn back, {tooltip:Kanji:sea}, or I'll shoot!\"",
            "hints": "You'll have to think of the \"sea\" as its own entity, controlling the tsunami, otherwise you might confuse and combine the two. So when you point your gun out the window, aim it at the \"sea,\" not the \"tsunami.\" It's like aiming for the head of a zombie and not the arms or legs.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sea",
                "Alternative": "Ocean"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine paddling in your kayak, your gun still in one hand, as you chase the sea back to its home.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:sea} decides it doesn't want to die today, so it turns its tsunami around and goes the other way. You hop in your {tooltip:Reading:kay}ak ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044}) and chase after it with your gun, to make sure it actually returns to the sea and doesn't just drown someone else."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sheep} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:sheep} kanji are the same in looks as well in meaning.",
            "hints": "You are no sheep\u2014you study your radicals, unlike most Japanese learners. You'll learn sooo much faster!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sheep"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3064\u3058",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the taste of this yogurt. You're scared and tired from running, but it tastes great!",
                "mnemonic": "To remember {span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}, we use the word \"Yogurt.\" The {tooltip:Kanji:sheep} are after you. There are too many of them, and they're chasing you down, stalking you... because you stole their sheep's milk {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}). Now you're running and crying and trying to eat the yogurt before the sheep catch up and stomp you down with their hooves."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A long time ago, someone put up a {tooltip:Radical:canopy} over their {tooltip:Radical:fortune} telling booth and created the first {tooltip:Kanji:shop}. This {tooltip:Kanji:store} was fortune-based, but since then lots of different stores have popped up!",
            "hints": "Picture the very first store in history. A fortune teller decided enough was enough, they should be in some kind of structure where it's safe, official looking, and more permanent.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shop",
                "Alternative": "Store"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u305b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture ten shops, all made up of someone selling something under a canopy. The first one is the fortune teller, but the nine others are whatever you want them to be!",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:shop} quickly turned into {tooltip:Reading:ten} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3093}) shops! It was a good idea, after all, so all of the other people selling goods and services decided to copy it and create their own shops. The next day there were ten more."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:cross} you're holding above your {tooltip:Radical:head} to keep your {tooltip:Radical:horns} {tooltip:Radical:dry} keeps pulling you {tooltip:Kanji:south}. Probably because it's warmer and less damp down south.",
            "hints": "Look down and see the compass pointing south and feel the cross pulling you in that direction.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "South"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u306a\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being in the south and taking big bites of naan. It tastes good, but now your mouth is dry just like your horns. Too dry...",
                "mnemonic": "You finally make it down {tooltip:Kanji:south}, and it is dry, but you're really hungry. When you try to find southern food you realize every single store is only selling {tooltip:Reading:naan} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} that gives {tooltip:Radical:life} is our very own {tooltip:Kanji:star} (which we happen to call the sun). Of course, all the other stars are probably giving life to other planets as well.",
            "hints": "Imagine all sorts of stars all around the universe giving life to planets as suns. These are all the stars you see in the sky and there are billions of them. I hope you don't feel overwhelmed by how minuscule we really are when you look up at all of them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Star"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you're soaring through between the stars, swinging your saber through the silence of space, and... wait. No that was a dream. You roll over and pat your saber. The two of you are ready just in case the stars need your help.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:star} (the sun) and all of the others are yours to protect with your trusty {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}). If you could protect your land from the West, then you can certainly defend the stars too!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Think about Japan. Japan is a country made up of islands. They're basically three {tooltip:Radical:drop} {tooltip:Radical:drop} {tooltip:Radical:drop}s in the large {tooltip:Radical:river} that is the Pacific Ocean. These are Japan's {tooltip:Kanji:states} or {tooltip:Kanji:province}s.",
            "hints": "Also, another way to think of this is that the river radical is actually just three rivers, separating drops, which are capitals of various states. Rivers are usually great ways to divide up a country, and states are one way to do it!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "State",
                "Alternatives": "Province, County"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The state shoes also have things like the state birds, state flowers, and state fish printed on each of them. They're quite collectable, you should buy a pair for your favorite state!",
                "mnemonic": "Each {tooltip:Kanji:state} has its own {tooltip:Reading:shoe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}) to represent it. The bottom of each shoe is the shape of the state, so when you step it leaves a state-shaped imprint in the ground."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You come across an {tooltip:Radical:angel} wearing a {tooltip:Radical:hat} that's covered in {tooltip:Radical:flowers}. So, you do the only natural thing. You take this angel, chop him up into tiny pieces, and dry him out. Then, you make {tooltip:Kanji:tea} out of all the dried up angel bits. You wear the hat, though.",
            "hints": "How does this angel-flower tea taste? Be sure to imagine it. Probably heavenly *rimshot.*",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tea"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3083, \u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It gets kind of weird when you know their names... Usually you just make them into tea without knowing who they are (easier that way). This one... this one is Chad, and you remember it vividly, because now you feel kind of bad.",
                "mnemonic": "In your {tooltip:Kanji:tea} you find a little metal button. I guess you missed it while you turned the angel into tea. You look at the button - on the back it says \"To {tooltip:Reading:Cha}d, you'll make an awesome angel.\" Looks like you're drinking Chad the Angel."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} you find a {tooltip:Radical:heart} and it makes you {tooltip:Kanji:think}. You think a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:thought}s like, \"Whose heart is this? Why is it in a rice paddy? Why am I thinking out loud?\"",
            "hints": "Think, think, think. Think about this rice paddy heart.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Think",
                "Alternative": "Thought"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you don't know Moe from the Simpsons use a different Moe, perhaps the one from the Three Stooges? You should be able to come up with one. Think really hard about the Moe you know best and imagine them standing watching you from the edge of the rice field.",
                "mnemonic": "As you are {tooltip:Kanji:think}ing these {tooltip:Kanji:thought}s, you spot someone on the edge of the rice field. He really reminds you of someone. But who? That's it! He reminds you of that bartender on The Simpsons. What's his name? You think some more. What is it? {tooltip:Reading:Oh! Moe} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3082}) is his name!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:stop} at a {tooltip:Radical:small} {tooltip:Radical:slide}. What were you doing before you stopped here? You were {tooltip:Kanji:walk}ing.",
            "hints": "Question is, what made you stop? Imagine yourself walking at a nice casual pace... then imagine something that would make you stop that's incredibly interesting and strange. Maybe an alien is going down the slide? He would say \"keep walking, friend.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Walk"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u308b, \u3042\u3086",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Of course, imagine the pain of your face. Did your nose break? After bringing yourself together, look down at what hit you. It's a hoe! How did you manage to step on just the right spot to flip it up on you like that? Examine the hoe. Pay close attention to it. Whose hoe is this? etc.",
                "mnemonic": "So, you're {tooltip:Kanji:walk}ing around, minding your own business, when suddenly something flips up and whacks you in the face. You stepped on the head of a {tooltip:Reading:hoe} ({span:lang=ja:\u307b}) and it caused it to swing up from the ground and hit you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:drop} hits your {tooltip:Radical:mustache}. Where did it come from? \"Ah, it came from {tooltip:Kanji:yonder},\" you say, {tooltip:Kanji:facing} that way.",
            "hints": "Yonder is a bit of a weird word, but it fits the meaning of this kanji quite well. You'll have to trust me that it's more useful in Japanese than it is in English. When you imagine through this mnemonic, make sure the drop comes from the side and hits you in the mustache with quite a bit of force. That means it came from a far distance thus making you look over \"yonder.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Yonder",
                "Alternative": "Facing"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Who is that over yonder!\" you yell.\n{linebreak}\"It is I, ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}),\" he yells back. \"I shot at you over yonder because you weren't doing your kanji reviews often enough and you're taking up space on our database.\"\n{linebreak}\"But I'm paying you!\"\n{linebreak}\"Oh, that's true. Well, I'm going to walk over yonder and leave you alone, then.\"",
                "mnemonic": "Who shot this drop at you from {tooltip:Kanji:yonder}? You look over yonder, and see a figure. It is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Who's that {tooltip:Radical:woman} pretending to be a {tooltip:Radical:jet}? That's my {tooltip:Kanji:younger sister}. *Sigh*",
            "hints": "Imagine a little girl (your younger sister) running around with her arms out, pretending to be a jet, too. Prwoooooo!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Younger Sister",
                "Alternative": "Little Sister"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3082\u3046\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ew, gross. Your younger sister is such a weirdo! Why does she have mice on her back while pretending to be a jet?",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:younger sister} is giving some {tooltip:Reading:mi}ce ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u3044}) a ride on her back like a jet. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This shares one of the meanings you learned for the kanji: {tooltip:Vocabulary:after}. You can differentiate this one from {span:lang=ja:\u5f8c\u308d} (which you may or may not have seen yet) thanks to the {span:lang=ja:\u3067} on the end. Some people believe that after something's dead ({span:lang=ja:\u3067}), it goes to an afterlife.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "After",
                "Alternatives": "Afterwards, Later",
                "Word Type": "adverb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3068\u3067"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3068\u3067",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40523-subject-2912.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3068\u3067",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40549-subject-2912.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}{tooltip:Vocabulary:After}. Everything happens after. It's a cause and effect chain. One thing happens, and then another thing happens after. This is life. This is the universe. Everything is after. It's an {tooltip:Reading:auto}matic ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3068}) cycle that just keeps going and going and going.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f8c\u3067\u3044\u3063\u3057\u3087\u306b\u304a\u8336\u3067\u3082\u3057\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Why don\u2019t we have some tea together later?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f8c\u3067\u3001\u300c\u8a00\u308f\u3093\u3053\u3063\u3061\u3083\u306a\u3044\u300d\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u308f\u305b\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Don't make me say, \"I told you so,\" later."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u6620\u753b\u3092\u898b\u7d42\u308f\u3063\u305f\u5f8c\u3067\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u5ea6\u305d\u308c\u3092\u898b\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u9055\u3046\u6620\u753b\u9928\u3078\u5411\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After the movie, we headed across town to watch it again in another theater."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This has a little hiragana attached to it but nothing that suggests it's a verb or an adjective. That means you can assume this word has the same meaning as its parent kanji.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "All",
                "Alternatives": "Entire, Everything",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
