                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3079} part, which is an admittedly difficult sound to remember. You have to think of the concept of {tooltip:Vocabulary:all} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:entire}. When you think of that concept, think of someone's entire fortune. All their money. You want to get all of Beth's money, so you {tooltip:Reading:sue Be}th ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3079}) for {tooltip:Vocabulary:all} she has.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5168\u3066\u3046\u307e\u304f\u884c\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Everything went smoothly."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7533\u3057\u308f\u3051\u3054\u3056\u3044\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304c\u3001\u3052\u3093\u3056\u3044\u5168\u3066\u306e\u304a\u305b\u304d\u304c\u3046\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3058\u3087\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3067\u3057\u3066...\u3002",
                    "en": "I am sorry, but all the seats are fully occupied at the moment, so..."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u50d5\u304c\u5148\u3060\u3088\u3002\u30a6\u30a3\u30ad\u30da\u30c7\u30a3\u30a2\u304c\u50d5\u306e\u5bbf\u984c\u3092\u5168\u3066\u771f\u4f3c\u3057\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I was the first to do it. Wikipedia copied my entire homework assignment afterwards."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

