{
            "mnemonic": "The hiragana attached to this word doesn't suggest it's a verb or an adjective, so we can assume it's a noun. While {span:lang=ja:\u5f8c\u3067} (you may or may not have seen this word yet) means \"after,\" this one means all the other meanings you learned with the kanji: {tooltip:Vocabulary:behind}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:back}, and {tooltip:Vocabulary:rear}. Think of the {span:lang=ja:\u308d} as a hint. It's like saying you're on the \"road\" ({span:lang=ja:\u308d}) and you're driving so fast you're leaving everything \"behind.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Behind",
                "Alternatives": "Back, Rear",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3057\u308d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3057\u308d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39452-subject-2911.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3057\u308d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19526-subject-2911.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Continue to think you're driving on this road. You hit something, then look {tooltip:Vocabulary:behind} you, seeing you hit a cow. Know the word for cow in Japanese? It's {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3057}, which is also the reading for this word.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5f8c\u308d\u306e\u30c9\u30a2\u3092\u3057\u3081\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please close the door behind you."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c1\u30e3\u30a4\u30eb\u30c9\u30b7\u30fc\u30c8\u306f\u3001\u304b\u306a\u3089\u305a\u5f8c\u308d\u306e\u3056\u305b\u304d\u306b\u305b\u3063\u3061\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "You must install the child carseat on the rear seat of the car."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u632f\u308a\u8fd4\u3063\u3066\u5f8c\u308d\u3092\u898b\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u3055\u3089\u306b\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u5ea6\u632f\u308a\u8fd4\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u50d5\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304c\u898b\u3048\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "If you turn around to look behind you and then do it again, you\u2019ll see me."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

