                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304b} portion. What is {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304b} in Japanese? It is \"red.\" So, think of something that's really {tooltip:Vocabulary:bright}. Now, imagine it being totally red (aka {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304b}). In Japan, the color red is associated with the sun, and the sun is pretty bright. If you can remember this you can also remember the reading of this word.\n"
