{
            "mnemonic": "You know {span:lang=ja:\u5916\u4eba} the word that means \"foreigner,\" but that word is a bit informal and can come off as rude. The nicer, more politically correct version of the word is the one above. An {tooltip:Kanji:outside} {tooltip:Kanji:country} {tooltip:Kanji:person}. To differentiate this from \"foreigner\" we're going to use the more polite English version of this word as well (just like in Japanese): {tooltip:Vocabulary:Foreign Person}.",
