                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. But! Don't forget, {span:lang=ja:\u56db} uses the kun'yomi reading, since the on'yomi reading sounds too much like the word for \"death.\"\n"
