                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}If you're lucky, you already know this (very) common word's reading. It's the word for \"I,\" probably one of the first things you'd learn in Japanese. The reading for this is {span:lang=ja:\u308f\u305f\u3057}. If you don't know that already, just think: \"{tooltip:Reading:What, a \u3057}?\" referring to the reading of the kanji, which is {span:lang=ja:\u3057}.\n"
