                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "34232-subject-5846.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading uses the {span:lang=ja:\u5b9d} vocab reading, {span:lang=ja:\u305f\u304b\u3089}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u59b9\u304c\u5b9d\u304f\u3058\u306b\u5f53\u305f\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3088\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3059\u3054\u3044\u306d\uff01\u3067\u3001\u3044\u304f\u3089\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u4e00\u4e07\u5186\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"My little sister won the lottery.\" \"Oh cool! How much?\" \"10,000 yen.\""
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u307c\u3046\u3066\u304d\u304b\u3093\u305d\u304f\u3067\u306f\u3001\u6765\u5e74\u3042\u305f\u308a\u306b\u5b9d\u304f\u3058\u306b\u5f53\u305f\u308b\u306f\u305a\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "It's wishful thinking, but I'll probably win the lottery at some point next year."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7236\u89aa\u306e\u79d8\u66f8\u304c\u5b9d\u304f\u3058\u306b\u5f53\u305f\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3092\u30d5\u30a7\u30a4\u30b9\u30d6\u30c3\u30af\u306b\u66f8\u3044\u305f\u6642\u306b\u79d8\u66f8\u3092\u79d8\u5bc6\u3068\u66f8\u304d\u9593\u9055\u3048\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3001\u307f\u3093\u306a\u304c\u52d8\u9055\u3044\u3057\u3066\u305f\u304f\u3055\u3093\u304a\u3081\u3067\u3068\u3046\u30b3\u30e1\u30f3\u30c8\u3092\u6b8b\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My dad's secretary won the lottery, but I made a spelling mistake when I posted it on Facebook. Secretary was spelled secretly. It confused people and I got a lot of congrats."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u6587\u5b57} means \"letters\". So, what are \"small letters\"? That would be {tooltip:Vocabulary:lowercase letters}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lowercase Letters",
                "Alternatives": "Lowercase Characters, Lowercase",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3082\u3058"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3082\u3058",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39418-subject-3411.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3082\u3058",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19517-subject-3411.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5c0f} is an exceptional reading. You know it means \"small,\" so think about what else is small: a child. How do you say \"child\" in Japanese? {span:lang=ja:\u3053}. You also know how to say the {span:lang=ja:\u6587\u5b57} portion from the previous level, so combine those together and you have {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3082\u3058}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3084\u3063\u3066\u5c0f\u6587\u5b57\u3068\u5927\u6587\u5b57\u3092\u5207\u308a\u304b\u3048\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "How do you switch from lowercase to uppercase?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d1\u30b9\u30ef\u30fc\u30c9\u306b\u306f\u3001\u304b\u306a\u3089\u305a\u5927\u6587\u5b57\u3001\u5c0f\u6587\u5b57\u3001\u3059\u3046\u5b57\u3092\u4e00\u3064\u3044\u4e0a\u3064\u304b\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Passwords must contain at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter and a number."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u541b\u306eE\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u30a2\u30c9\u30ec\u30b9\u3063\u3066\u3001\u5168\u90e8\u5c0f\u6587\u5b57\u306a\u306e\uff1f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\uff1f\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u304a\u304b\u3057\u3044\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "Is your email address in all lowercase letters? Is it really? Are you crazy?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

