                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}Someone yells out \"NEXT!\" because the first thing didn't work on you. That was a single guillotine. Now they are going to try {tooltip:Reading:two gui}llotines ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304e}) and see how that works on your thick neck. NEXXXXT!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
