                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this one is an exception, because it uses kun'yomi readings even though it is a jukugo kanji. You already know the separate kun'yomi readings from the vocabulary of the last level, but you will have to remember to actually use this knowledge when this word comes up.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5e74\u4e0a\u306e\u4eba\u3068\u3001\u30c7\u30fc\u30c8\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306f\u306f\u3058\u3081\u3066\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This is my first date with an older person."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eba\u751f\u306f\u3088\u305d\u304f\u4e0d\u304b\u306e\u3046\u3060\u3002\u304a\u524d\u304c\u5e74\u4e0a\u306e\u3073\u4eba\u3068\u3051\u3063\u3053\u3093\u3059\u308b\u304b\u306e\u3046\u305b\u3044\u3060\u3063\u3066\u30bc\u30ed\u30d1\u30fc\u30bb\u30f3\u30c8\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Life is unpredictable. It's not a zero percent chance that you will get married with a beautiful older woman."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u304c\u3001\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u306e\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u306f\u30d4\u30e9\u30df\u30c3\u30c9\u3088\u308a\u3082\u5e74\u4e0a\u3060\u3068\u8a00\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "My dad says that my mom\u2019s mom is older than the pyramids."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {span:lang=ja:\u304a} makes the word more polite. You're elevating the \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:older sister}\" title because you're a good younger sibling. Otherwise, the meaning of this word is the same as the kanji - just the feeling is different. You can also use this word to refer to a youthful-looking woman that you don't know, as in \"Excuse me {tooltip:Vocabulary:miss}!\" ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Older Sister",
                "Alternative": "Miss",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u306d\u3048\u3055\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u306d\u3048\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39603-subject-2893.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u306d\u3048\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19693-subject-2893.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is different too. It has some hiragana attached to it, which is a clue that this uses a kun'yomi reading. Let's use a mnemonic to learn that reading. \n{splitParent}Imagine your {tooltip:Vocabulary:older sister} (even if you don't have one). She is, for some reason, a horse. Imagine petting her, giving her carrots, and doing other horse-related things with her. What do horses say? They say {tooltip:Reading:nehhhh} ({span:lang=ja:\u306d\u3048}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u307f\u3069\u308a\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306e\u304a\u59c9\u3055\u3093\u306f\u3081\u304c\u306d\u3092\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Midori\u2019s older sister is wearing glasses."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3001\u3066\u3063\u304d\u308a\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u304f\u3093\u306e\u304a\u59c9\u3055\u3093\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3061\u304c\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I totally thought you were Viet's older sister, but you aren't, eh?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u304a\u59c9\u3055\u3093\u306f\u3001\u30d0\u30a4\u30af\u3092\u8cb7\u3046\u3053\u3068\u304c\u5f7c\u6c0f\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u7e4b\u304c\u308b\u3068\u8003\u3048\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My older sister thinks that buying a motorcycle will help her get a boyfriend."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. This is your older sister, by the way. Not somebody else's.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Older Sister",
                "Alternatives": "Big Sister, Elder Sister",
