                        "file": "39414-subject-7526.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. You haven't learned this reading yet,  so here's a mnemonic to help you remember:\n{splitParent}Picture your {tooltip:Vocabulary:older sister} (even if you don't have one), her birthday is coming up and there's only one thing she wants from you. {tooltip:Reading:A ne}cklace ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u306d}). She's wanted a necklace for years and you're finally going to give her one. She'll be so happy.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u59c9\u306e\u3044\u3048\u306b\u884c\u304f\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m just about to go to my older sister\u2019s house."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u3001\u59c9\u306e\u4e94\u3070\u3044\u306e\u308a\u3087\u3046\u306e\u672c\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I have five times as many books as my older sister does."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u59c9\u306f\u30b9\u30c1\u30e5\u30ef\u30fc\u30c7\u30b9\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My big sister works as a stewardess."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If {tooltip:Kanji:\u6b69} is \"walk\" and you take {tooltip:Kanji:one} {tooltip:Kanji:walk}, then really you are just taking {tooltip:Vocabulary:one step}. When there's a number before {span:lang=ja:\u6b69}, it refers to the number of steps you're taking. The most common is this one, and you'll see it on urinals when they kindly ask you to please take one step forward because peeing isn't a game and somebody has to clean up after you.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "One Step",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3063\u307d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3063\u307d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19643-subject-7451.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3063\u307d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39548-subject-7451.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is pretty standard in its trickiness. The {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3061} shortens to an {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3063} and the {span:lang=ja:\u307b} rendakus to {span:lang=ja:\u307d}. One step at a time, right?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u3046\u3084\u304f\u3001\u3086\u3081\u306b\u5411\u304b\u3063\u3066\u4e00\u6b69\u3075\u307f\u51fa\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019ve finally taken one step forward toward my dream."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5343\u91cc\u306e\u9053\u3082\u4e00\u6b69\u304b\u3089\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3067\u3057\u3087\uff1f",
                    "en": "They say, a journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step, right?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6700\u521d\u306e\u4e00\u6b69\u3092\u8e0f\u307f\u51fa\u3059\u306e\u306b\u52c7\u6c17\u304c\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "It takes courage to take the first step forward."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:outside} of the {tooltip:Kanji:sea} is someplace {tooltip:Vocabulary:overseas}. It can also be {tooltip:Vocabulary:foreign} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:abroad} if those words are easier to remember for you.",
