                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u304d} portion: \n{splitParent}Something is {tooltip:Vocabulary:snap}ping. Turns out that something is your arm. Your arm is a {span:lang=ja:\u6728} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) that grew out of you one day. \"What's this ki doing here?\" you ask. Then it suddenly {tooltip:Vocabulary:break}s in half! \"OW OW OW! My ki! It's been cut!!\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
