{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:copy}, but what is a copy? It is basically a photograph, which is why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be photographed}. You know this one is \"to be photographed\" because it ends with a {span:lang=ja:\u308b}. Someone thinks you're \"{tooltip:Reading:ru}de\" so they're photographing you.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Photographed",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3064\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3064\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "15343-subject-2724.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3064\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "35257-subject-2724.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3064} part. You're being rude, right? That's why you got photographed. Why are you rude? You're doing beatboxing, constantly saying {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064} over and over again. Say it out loud, too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u304a\u5144\u3055\u3093\u306f\u3001\u3053\u306e\u3057\u3083\u3057\u3093\u306b\u5199\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Is your brother in these pictures?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u5e74\u3068\u3063\u305f\u4e94\u767e\u307e\u3044\u306e\u5199\u3057\u3093\u306e\u5185\u3001\u306a\u3093\u3068\u767e\u4e09\u307e\u3044\u306e\u5199\u3057\u3093\u306b\u53bb\u5e74\u3057\u3093\u3060\u7236\u306e\u3059\u304c\u305f\u304c\u5199\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Among the 500 pictures I took this year, 103 of them had my father who had died last year in them."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u5199\u771f\u306b\u5199\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u7537\u306e\u4eba\u306f\u3001\u79c1\u306e\u30d5\u30a1\u30fc\u30b9\u30c8\u30ad\u30b9\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The guy in this picture was my first kiss."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The meaning of this word is pretty strange, having very little to do with the kanji meaning you learned. This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to carry out}. Maybe you can think of it like someone is saying \"You ({span:lang=ja:\u3046}) {tooltip:Kanji:go} do that task!\" to get yourself {tooltip:Vocabulary:to carry out} that task. Whatever you do, just know this is a weird exception word, so you may have to do some extra work to remember it.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Carry Out",
                "Alternative": "To Perform",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3053\u306a\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3053\u306a\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "17578-subject-2776.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3053\u306a\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "37460-subject-2776.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is also a strange exception. You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3053\u306a} portion. Maybe this mnemonic will help: You have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to carry out} a task but you're not too excited about it. Then you find out the task will bring you to Kona, Hawaii. \"{tooltip:Reading:Oh, Kona!?}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3053\u306a}), you shout. In that case, you'll get right on it \ud83c\udfdd \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u3066\u3044\u3069\u304a\u308a\u3001\u65e5\u3088\u3046\u65e5\u306b\u3046\u3093\u3069\u3046\u4f1a\u3092\u884c\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We will perform in the athletic meet on Sunday as planned."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6765\u3057\u3085\u3046\u306e\u6708\u3088\u3046\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u5b66\u751f\u304c\u3001\u3048\u304d\u3067\u3046\u3061\u308f\u306e\u3080\u308a\u3087\u3046\u306f\u3044\u3075\u3092\u884c\u3046\u3088\u3066\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The students are scheduled to hand out free uchiwa fans at the station next Monday."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u75c5\u9662\u306b\u8c5a\u306e\u5fc3\u81d3\u3092\u904b\u3076\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3092\u4efb\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u3082\u3057\u79c1\u304c\u305d\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3092\u884c\u308f\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3001\u8ab0\u304b\u304c\u6599\u7406\u3092\u5b8c\u6210\u3055\u305b\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u306a\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019ve been entrusted with the job of delivering a pig heart to Tokyo hospital and if I don\u2019t carry out my task someone won\u2019t be able to finish the meal they\u2019re cooking."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
