                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u305f} portion if you want to be able to read this word, which uses the kun'yomi reading. Think about yourself {tooltip:Vocabulary:eat}ing some {tooltip:Reading:ta}cos ({span:lang=ja:\u305f}). Imagine yourself eating it, that raw beef taste in your mouth (either like it or hate it).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bce\u3042\u3055\u3001\u306a\u3063\u3068\u3046\u3092\u98df\u3079\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I eat natto every morning."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3001\u3051\u3093\u3053\u3046\u306b\u3044\u3044\u3082\u306e\u3092\u98df\u3079\u308b\u3058\u304b\u3093\u304c\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I never have enough time to eat healthy foods."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u3001\u5bdd\u306a\u304c\u3089\u98df\u3079\u308b\u306e\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3060\u3002\u5922\u904a\u75c5\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306a\u611f\u3058\u3067\u3001\u305d\u308c\u306f\u5922\u904a\u98df\u4e8b\u75c5\u3068\u547c\u3070\u308c\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "I like to eat while I\u2019m sleeping. It\u2019s just like sleepwalking, but it\u2019s called sleep-eating."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that the kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:yonder}, which is like \"over there.\" This is the verb version of \"yonder.\" That being said, \"to yonder\" isn't really a thing, so you have to think of what happens when you \"look yonder.\" This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to face} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to turn toward}. You're looking yonder, but you have to turn towards said yonder to look that way.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Face",
                "Alternative": "To Turn Toward",
                "Word Type": "godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3080\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3080\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19506-subject-3496.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3080\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39416-subject-3496.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You turn {tooltip:Vocabulary:to face} a new direction and look out into the distance. There is a single cow out there. It turns to face you too, and says {tooltip:Reading:moo} ({span:lang=ja:\u3080}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3063\u3061\u3092\u5411\u3044\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Turn this way, please."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3078\u3084\u306f\u3001\u5357\u3092\u5411\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3067\u65e5\u5f53\u305f\u308a\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "This room is facing South, so it gets very sunny."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u5ea6\u306f\u3001\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u306e\u65b9\u3092\u5411\u3044\u3066\u3001\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u8d64\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306e\u683c\u597d\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u304b\u805e\u3044\u3066\u307f\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "Now, let\u2019s turn toward your dad and ask him why he\u2019s wearing a baby costume."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:fix} so this vocab word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to fix}. This is when you're fixing something, as in doing the actual physical action of fixing.",
