                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to learn the {span:lang=ja:\u306a\u304a} part. Think of it this way. You need {tooltip:Vocabulary:to fix} something! It's urgent! You have to fix it {tooltip:Reading:now}! ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u304a}). This will also work with the similar word, {span:lang=ja:\u76f4\u308b}, which you'll learn soon if you haven't already.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d1\u30bd\u30b3\u30f3\u304c\u3053\u308f\u308c\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u76f4\u305b\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "My PC broke. Can you fix it?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8003\u3048\u76f4\u3057\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You'd better think it through again."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3057\u58ca\u308c\u3066\u3044\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3092\u76f4\u305d\u3046\u3068\u3059\u308b\u5fc5\u8981\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You don\u2019t need to fix something if it\u2019s not broken."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
