                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}When something starts {tooltip:Vocabulary:to grow} it also learns to laugh. Imagine a little plant growing out of the ground laughing. \"{tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f}) ha ha ha!\" it says, as it sprouts out of the ground.\n"
