{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. This word is actually two words put together, though. {span:lang=ja:\u4ea1\u304f} means \"be deceased.\" {span:lang=ja:\u306a\u308b} means \"to become.\" So put that all together and you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to pass away} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to become deceased}. It's basically a polite way to say something died ({span:lang=ja:\u6b7b\u306c}).",
