                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You learned that reading with this kanji, but here's a reminder of the mnemonic just in case: \n{splitParent}You have to remember the {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3082} part to read this word. To do this, though, you'll have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to think} about that guy... hmm... what was his name? He's on The Simpsons... he's the bartender? I think? {tooltip:Reading:Oh! Moe} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3082}) is his name! Thank you. Now I remember.\n{splitParent}If you don't know Moe from the Simpsons use a different Moe, perhaps the one from the Three Stooges? You should be able to come up with one.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u3082\u6765\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I think he\u2019s coming too."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30cf\u30ea\u30b1\u30fc\u30f3\u306e\u304d\u305b\u3064\u306f\u30e1\u30ad\u30b7\u30b3\u306b\u884c\u304f\u306e\u3092\u3055\u3051\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
