                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39488-subject-2661.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings for the kanji in this word are a bit strange. The {span:lang=ja:\u5927} portion is actually read using the kun'yomi, the same reading as you learned with {tooltip:Vocabulary:\u5927\u304d\u3044} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a\u304d\u3044}). Everything else is just on'yomi. So, you'll need to remember the one exception with {span:lang=ja:\u5927}. If you do, you should be okay.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3055\u3044\u3057\u3087\u306e\u5b57\u306f\u3001\u5927\u6587\u5b57\u3067\u304b\u3044\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please capitalize the first letter."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30bf\u30a4\u30c8\u30eb\u3092\u5927\u6587\u5b57\u3067\u304b\u304d\u76f4\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please rewrite the title in uppercase letters."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f55\u6545\u3060\u304b\u308f\u304b\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u5c0f\u6587\u5b57\u3088\u308a\u5927\u6587\u5b57\u306e\u65b9\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "For some reason I like uppercase more than lowercase."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

