                        "file": "19699-subject-2892.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}Your {tooltip:Vocabulary:younger sister} is really into {tooltip:Reading:emote}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3082\u3046\u3068}). Look up this word if you're not a teenage girl. Just imagine her sending you these on your phone over and over. You tell your younger sister: \"HEY, STOP SENDING ME EMOTES.\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u7530\u4e2d\u3055\u3093\u306e\u59b9\u306f\u3069\u306e\u4eba\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Who is Tanaka\u2019s younger sister?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u59b9\u306b\u3046\u3089\u5207\u3089\u308c\u305f\u6c17\u5206\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I feel betrayed by my little sister."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u59b9\u306f\u3001\u30d0\u30fc\u30d3\u30fc\u4eba\u5f62\u306b\u30a6\u30a3\u30c3\u30b0\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u3066\u3042\u3052\u305f\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3068\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u9aea\u306e\u6bdb\u3092\u5207\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My younger sister just cut off all of her hair so she could make wigs for her Barbie dolls."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "See the cool wing on the bottom? See the head with the neat feather coming out of the top? This is a {tooltip:Radical:bird}. Tweet tweet!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bird"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you boil a village everything will turn {tooltip:Radical:black}. Mostly because you're a crazed murderer, but more so because when you boil a village all the roads melt and coat everything in black tar. Picture it! It looks like Pompeii. (Oof, too soon?)",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Black"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This looks like a {tooltip:Radical:boat} coming toward you in the water. See the billowing sail and the reflection off the water? That's what boats look like.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Boat"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put some dirt around your head and in your mouth to figure out your head's {tooltip:Radical:circumference}. When you pull your head out you'll have the perfect shape of your head, making measuring the circumference easy. Oh, and the dirt in your mouth? That's just for the taste.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Circumference"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This looks like a little tamagotchi or (if you aren't a 90s kid) a duck. What do both of these critters have in common? They have really crazy {tooltip:Radical:clan} followings. And the people who enjoy them (tiny pocket games or watching quacking duckies) create clans that get together and share their experiences. Which clan are you a part of?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Clan"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In a prison on a rice paddy they're boiling something. What do you think it is? {tooltip:Radical:Fish}! What goes better with rice? What's easy to find, making it cheap prison food? Fish, of course!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fish"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical already looks like a {tooltip:Radical:gate}, right? Just imagine a big gate with two pillars, one on either side. Then, up above are the doors, which can come down at any moment.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gate"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radicals ground and big make up this radical. There's a big guy on the ground... who is that big guy? Embarrassingly, it's your {tooltip:Radical:husband}. Feel the shame that he got knocked down on the ground. By what? Who? How? (It doesn't matter.)",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Husband"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This looks a bit like a backwards S. S for Self. But it's backwards because you didn't want to mix yourself up with any of the other selves out there, so you flipped it. That's why it means {tooltip:Radical:oneself}. (That's you!)",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Oneself"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have the animal radical in this already, that should be a clue. What kind of animal is it? It's in the ground, covered in mud. Also, there are toes laying around with it, because this animal will eat anything (good way to get rid of bodies... I hear). So what's this animal that's covered in mud and eats toes because it will eat anything? It's a {tooltip:Radical:pig}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pig"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your mama is carrying some kind of elaborate weapon. You look closely and see that it's a {tooltip:Radical:spear}. The pointy end is to the right, and there are some decorations hanging off it. It's a very fancy spear, and you wonder where your mama got it.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Spear"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks a little like the letter P, right? It's a P printed onto something... wait, it's not printed, it's a {tooltip:Radical:stamp} that's been put on the paper. Peter Parker likes to use stamps instead of pens.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Stamp"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What happens when you put a flat surface on top of a pair of legs? You get a {tooltip:Radical:table}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Table"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is made up of coffin and child. To keep a child out of a coffin they'll need a good {tooltip:Radical:teacher} to make sure they know not to stick forks in outlets or dance in traffic. That's why this radical is a teacher.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Teacher"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks kind of like a {tooltip:Radical:temple} on a hill, don't you think? With all the layers, n' stuff? Just picture that first horizontal line as the base of the ornate temple balancing on that hill underneath it and you'll have no problem remembering this radical.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Temple"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical looks just like a top hat. That's why it's {tooltip:Radical:top hat}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Top Hat"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "See the {tooltip:Radical:wing}? It's kind of like a bat wing with webbing. Either way, it's just a wing.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wing"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Flowers that grow out of the ground of a rice paddy after you bury fins there will grow {tooltip:Radical:yellow}. Why? Because yellow is the color of a fish's soul, so planting flowers over their fins will turn them into a nice, pretty yellow. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Yellow"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "While riding your {tooltip:Radical:scooter}, you take your {tooltip:Radical:sword} and cut out an {tooltip:Kanji:area} on the ground. This whole place is your area now!",
            "hints": "Imagine riding your scooter around in a really large circle, pressing your sword into the ground as you do. Once you close the circle, you claim to everyone around that this is YOUR area, and they aren't allowed in.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Area"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305f, \u3079",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine doing everything you can to get this hen out of your area, but it manages to dodge and outwit you at every turn. You even slash at it with your sword and try to run it over with your scooter, but the hen can't be stopped. This is the hen's area now. You have been defeated.",
                "mnemonic": "As you look down at your {tooltip:Kanji:area}, you suddenly realize there is a {tooltip:Reading:hen} ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3093}) pecking at the ground in there. \"Um, excuse me, hen, I believe I said this is MY area?!\" You try to kick it out, but it hops over your leg."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have to take the measurement of a leader. Imagine yourself measuring that leader's height and then coming up short. This is not good, you think. Leaders need to be at least six feet tall. So, to make the leader tall enough, you {tooltip:Kanji:attach} another head to the top of the leader's head.",
            "hints": "Make sure you really feel like the person can\u2019t be a leader because they\u2019re too short when you measure them (I know this isn\u2019t true, but we\u2019re remembering kanji here, anything goes!). As long as you feel disconcerted that the leader isn\u2019t tall enough, you should be able to remember that you need to attach something to the leader to make them tall enough. The fact that you\u2019re attaching another head to the top of the leader's head is pretty weird too, and should help you to remember the meaning.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Attach"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Just focus on how attaching requires two things to remember this reading.",
                "mnemonic": "You have to remember the kun'yomi reading of this kanji, and the part you need to remember is {span:lang=ja:\u3064}. So, think of {tooltip:Kanji:attach}ing something to something else. What would you need? You'd need {tooltip:Reading:two} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064}) things to put together!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:tree} has an {tooltip:Radical:umbrella}, and it's holding it over his head, which is strange, because trees normally like water... turns out, it's not water falling on him, but dollar {tooltip:Kanji:bills} floating down.",
            "hints": "The sick part of this is that those dollar {tooltip:Kanji:bills} were once this tree's friends. The tree is sobbing uncontrollably as pieces of his friends fall on him and all around him - which is why he's using the umbrella to protect himself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bill",
                "Alternatives": "Tag, Label, Note"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What else could he do? He couldn\u2019t move, so he sat. It\u2019s weird imagining a tree trying to sit\u2026",
                "mnemonic": "The tree couldn\u2019t take the body parts of his friends falling down on him, so he {tooltip:Reading:sat} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3064}) down, and began crying uncontrollably."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:bird} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:bird} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "As long as you know the radical bird you know the kanji bird.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bird"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
