{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:slide} coming out of the patient's {tooltip:Radical:heart} is there because a mad scientist is testing to see if it's a good way to drain the body of blood. The patient is alive now... but they are definitely slated for {tooltip:Kanji:certain} death.",
            "hints": "As you imagine the mad scientist drawing blood out of the patient's heart with a small slide, also imagine a little meter hooked up to him as well. On one end is \"SURVIVE!\" on the other end is \"CERTAIN DEATH.\" Right now the finger is pointing close to {tooltip:Kanji:certain} death, though :(",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Certain"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u306a\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Maybe imagine yourself running in there too, just trying to {tooltip:Reading:hit} the patient back to life, because the patient was your friend.",
                "mnemonic": "As the beeping heart thing starts to do one long continuous beeeeeeeeeeeeeep, the doctor puts his hands together and {tooltip:Reading:hits} ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3064}) the dead patient over and over, attempting to bring him back."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This kanji uses a modified {tooltip:Radical:jet} radical. The front area of the wing is wider than the middle area of the wing. This may seem counterintuitive, but by doing this they can fit so much more jet fuel. The jet zooms off and keeps going for a long, long time, until it reaches the {tooltip:Kanji:end} of the earth.",
            "hints": "Imagine the end of the earth being like how they imagined it pre-Columbus era. Just a big drop going off into space, giant waterfalls plummeting down. Your crazy jet has made it to the very end! Congratulations!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "End"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's surprisingly dirty down here, because all the water takes the garbage this way. That's why you sit on these mats you brought.",
                "mnemonic": "When you get to the {tooltip:Kanji:end} of the world, you land your jet and put out a few {tooltip:Reading:mats} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u3064}) to sit on so you can view the sights. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:clan} is where you get your name. But not your given name, your {tooltip:Kanji:family name}. That's why people have names that mean \"in a rice paddy\" and \"near the ferry crossing.\" The location of your clan determined your {tooltip:Kanji:surname}! Hope your ancestors didn't live on \"Poo Lake\" or something.",
            "hints": "Think about your own surname in your language. Where did it come from? Were you a clan of village dwellers? Maybe you made shoes! You should look it up and find out!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Family Name",
                "Alternatives": "Last Name, Surname"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3058",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine your ancestors, herding sheep. Thanks to them your name means \"sheep people.\" Thanks great great great great great grand pappy.",
                "mnemonic": "Don't worry, I'll tell you where your {tooltip:Kanji:family name} came from. Your family used to herd {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}). You read that right, your family was of the sheep clan because you took care of sheep all day."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "That {tooltip:Radical:slide} is your {tooltip:Radical:husband}'s only {tooltip:Kanji:fault}. He loves that slide, more than you, and it's the only thing you don't like about him.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking out the window of your house and watching your husband slide down his slide over and over. He's not even good at it, he falls off the side halfway down most of the time. You want to complain, but he's pretty decent otherwise. This is his only fault.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fault"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3057\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You run outside and yell, \"AHA! It's your fault that shih tzu died! You and that stupid slide!\"",
                "mnemonic": "You try to come up with another {tooltip:Kanji:fault} of his so you can complain when you see a tiny {tooltip:Reading:shih tzu} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3064}) trotting by. Oh no! Before you can call out, your husband has fallen off the slide and crushed the poor thing. You hear a sharp yelp and then nothing."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:fish} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:fish} are exactly the same!",
            "hints": "Nothing fishy about that, right?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fish"
            },
