{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:lion} drops a {tooltip:Radical:drop} of saliva onto this {tooltip:Radical:person} {tooltip:Kanji:from} above. The person is in a much worse place {tooltip:Kanji:compared with} where they were before, {tooltip:Kanji:since} they only just recently fell into this pit.",
            "hints": "Picture the person, the lion is leaning over them, the drop of spit dangling from their mouth. \"I-I want to go back where I came from,\" the person gasps, shaking.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "From",
                "Alternatives": "Since, Compared With, With, By Means Of"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The eagle came from the sky and technically rescued him, but compared to where he was before, it may not be a better situation. I think this person is going to be eaten either way.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:From} above there is a loud caw, and a giant {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) swoops down, forcing the lion to back off. The eagle grabs the person with its talons, bringing him into the air! But now he's... in the air being carried by a giant eagle, {tooltip:Kanji:compared with} where he was before, is this really better?!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Sew {tooltip:Radical:thread} through your {tooltip:Radical:top hat} and to the top hats of other people you know and you'll turn into a {tooltip:Kanji:group} of top hat wearing people. You're all connected by the thread now, so everyone will assume you're a group, even if that's all you guys have going for yourselves.",
            "hints": "Picture a group of people threaded together by their top hats. Don't you want to be part of a cool group like that? Your own top hat team.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Group",
                "Alternatives": "Association, Team"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being in a group of soap makers. Picture the soap bubbles floating between all of you.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:group} decides to make {tooltip:Reading:so}ap ({span:lang=ja:\u305d}) together. You take off your top hats and use them as soap molds, mixing together all of your favorite smells and colors."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under this {tooltip:Radical:roof} is a {tooltip:Radical:pig}. Your pig, because it's your {tooltip:Kanji:house}! You keep your pig inside where it's nice and warm. He's a member of your family, so he deserves to live in your {tooltip:Kanji:home} too.",
            "hints": "Picture the little pig, prancing around happily under the roof of your house.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "House",
                "Alternative": "Home"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b, \u3051",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3048, \u3084, \u3046\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the pig again, but this time sitting in your car, which is also in your house. The three of you are warm and cozy and safe together in your home.",
                "mnemonic": "Also in your {tooltip:Kanji:house}, is your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). Your pig and your car are safe under your roof."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This kanji is the same as the radical it comes from. {tooltip:Radical:Lack} becomes {tooltip:Kanji:Lack}!",
            "hints": "If you know the radical you know this.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lack"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine having to use regular, ordinary ketchup, or just old, boring catsup on your burger. Or even worse, an actual tomato. BLEH!",
                "mnemonic": "To remember {span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3064}, we use the word \"ketsup.\" It's the perfect blend of ketchup and catsup!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're flying in a Jet. Even though it's one of the fastest things on earth, your child is sitting in the back asking, \"Are we there yet? Are we there yet?\" You have to keep responding. \"{tooltip:Kanji:Not yet}! Not yet! NOT YET!\"",
            "hints": "Feel the irritation of this. How irritating is this kid going to be the whole flight over? The jet is going as fast as it can!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Not Yet"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e, \u3044\u307e, \u3072\u3064\u3058",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Go ahead and pretend to listen to the kid asking if we're there yet. Then in your mind go \"me me me me me me me\" quietly.",
                "mnemonic": "What a selfish kid, right? Well, all he thinks about is \"{tooltip:Reading:Me} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f}) me me me me me me me me me me.\" Hate kids like that."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:thread} that ties you to your {tooltip:Radical:clan} is {tooltip:Kanji:paper}. Your papers, that is.",
            "hints": "The paper itself was also made by your clan using thread woven really tightly together.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Paper"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u307f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a big guard coming up to you and asking to see your papers so they can see what clan you belong to. Well you're from the Commi clan, so you really hope this guard is okay with that.",
                "mnemonic": "You need this specific {tooltip:Kanji:paper} to prove that you aren't a {tooltip:Reading:Commi} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u307f}), aka a Communist. Or that you are. It really depends on where you want to go and what decade this is."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} with your {tooltip:Radical:mama} carrying a {tooltip:Radical:task} she needs to get done. You see her {tooltip:Kanji:pass through}, hurrying by to get that task done.",
            "hints": "Imagine your mama passing through your house on a scooter, not stopping because she needs to get her task done urgently. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pass Through"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u304a, \u304b\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Why do you have to do the task too? Because there are two tasks, so the two of you have to do them.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch your mama {tooltip:Kanji:pass through} the house, she yells, \"YOU HAVE TO DO THIS TASK {tooltip:Reading:TOO} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3046})!\" Too?! Oh no, now you have to do it too. Hurry up!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:mouth} {tooltip:Radical:clan} are a group of {tooltip:Kanji:people}. They are the {tooltip:Kanji:people} of a {tooltip:Kanji:nation}.",
            "hints": "The mouth clan are distinct peoples. They do, of course, use their mouths.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Peoples",
                "Alternatives": "People, Nation"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "That's why they're the mouth clan. This nation of people are known for mouthing off and saying mean things. Imagine them, as a nation, saying mean things to you. How awful! All being from the same place, they're all into it too. In a way, they're not the mouth clan, they're the mean clan.",
                "mnemonic": "The mouth clan {tooltip:Kanji:peoples} are a {tooltip:Kanji:nation} of {tooltip:Kanji:people} who use their mouths to say {tooltip:Reading:mean} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3093}) things to other peoples."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:king}'s {tooltip:Radical:village} is the {tooltip:Kanji:reason} he's king. Without the village there would be no reason to have a king in the first place.",
            "hints": "If a king has no one to rule then he has no reason to exist.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reason"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3068\u308f\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Just like you can't have a king without a village, you can't have reason without re.",
                "mnemonic": "You can't have {tooltip:Kanji:reason} without {tooltip:Reading:re} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A giant {tooltip:Radical:cross} with a {tooltip:Radical:mouth} stands above you. \"I am {tooltip:Kanji:reason}!\" it says to you. It is the Cross of Reason.",
            "hints": "Because it's a cross with a mouth, it thinks that it is reason in all the chaos.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reason"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3046, \u3086, \u3086\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3057, \u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Those youths just do things for no reason! That's why I, the Cross of Reason is here! I will knock some reason into those youths.\"",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:reason} that this Cross of Reason exists is to combat the {tooltip:Reading:you}ths ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3046}) of the world, who just bring chaos into everything."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Next to the {tooltip:Radical:tree}, a {tooltip:Radical:lid} is put on your {tooltip:Radical:father}. \"Hello child,\" he says. \"This is your new {tooltip:Kanji:school}.\" ",
            "hints": "He goes on to explain that he changed your school to here because there is a tree to block the satellite's view. Also, he wears a tin foil lid on his head so they can't track him. The regular school was no good because \"they were watching.\" So now you have this new school, taught under a tree by your father who's wearing a lid on his head.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "School"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "On your first day of school, imagine walking under the tree and seeing all your classmates. They're all {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}\u2013similar to each other, but with some variation. Your father explains these {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s escaped from a government research facility, and they come to this school to receive a better education.  \"These poor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s need a school that will teach them more than just kanji and Japanese vocabulary.\"",
                "mnemonic": "Your new {tooltip:Kanji:school} has other students too. They are all {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s, though."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:rain} is hated so much by {tooltip:Radical:wolverine}s, so they always want to live in the {tooltip:Kanji:snow}.",
            "hints": "Imagine rain falling on a wolverine and how much they hate it, so the wolverine moves up north to somewhere with lots of snow. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Snow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "He keeps saying \"Yucky yucky yucky\" over and over again. Imagine him doing this with an accent that would bring the word closer to {span:lang=ja:\u3086\u304d}.",
                "mnemonic": "You ask the wolverine, \"Why do you want this {tooltip:Kanji:snow} so bad?\" He replies quickly: \"Because the rain is {tooltip:Reading:yucky}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u304d})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:private} {tooltip:Radical:bow} made of {tooltip:Radical:insect}s that's extremely {tooltip:Kanji:strong}. Insect bodies are really durable, so they make for strong bows. You also have to be strong to use it, since it was made just for strong arms.",
            "hints": "Imagine holding this strong bow in your strong arms. Look closer at the little insect bodies that make it up. Thanks for your help, little guys.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Strong",
                "Alternative": "Strength"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine all the strong people who live in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} and make strong things. You should go there someday!",
                "mnemonic": "You had this {tooltip:Kanji:strong} bow made especially for you in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} is famous for their strong bows, so if you ever want another, you know where to go."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:eye} {tooltip:Radical:leaf} grows only in the {tooltip:Radical:winter}. Every other leaf, however, will do the opposite, which is to grow in the {tooltip:Kanji:summer}.",
            "hints": "Just think of the eye leaf as weird (it is weird, after all). It grows in the winter. Now, think of any normal leaves. They do the exact opposite, which is to grow in the summer.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Summer"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052, \u304b, \u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Think about summer. Now think about yourself tying knots. Now think about summer again. Now think about tying knots again. Now think about your mother getting upset at you because all you do is tie knots all summer long. Go play video games like a normal kid!",
                "mnemonic": "Now it's summertime! What do you do during the {tooltip:Kanji:summer}? You just sit around with your favorite string tying {tooltip:Reading:knots} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3064}) in it over and over again."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:lid} on your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} and {tooltip:Radical:mustache}, covering up all your talking holes. This is because you kept saying how {tooltip:Kanji:tall} and {tooltip:Kanji:expensive} you are.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself saying how tall and expensive you are to everyone in the room. Then they use a lid to cover your mouth so you can't talk to anyone anymore. But, then your mustache starts talking, saying the same thing. That's why this lid covers both your mustache and your mouth. Now you can't say that you are tall or expensive.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tall",
                "Alternatives": "Expensive, High"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s finally get tired of your shenanigans, and lid up your mouth and mustache so you can't say that you're tall or expensive. ",
                "mnemonic": "\"I am {tooltip:Kanji:tall}er and more {tooltip:Kanji:expensive} than you.\" "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:teacher} in {tooltip:Radical:winter} is happiest because they get to {tooltip:Kanji:teach}! The kids can't go out and play because it's too cold. They all have to come in and stay warm as the teacher teaches!",
            "hints": "Picture a teacher excitedly teaching, bundled up in the cold. Snow falling outside. Grumpy children being taught inside.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Teach"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3057, \u304a\u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the teaching teacher teaching you about Japan in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} in winter. You've always wanted to go to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}!",
                "mnemonic": "Teachers can teach the most about Japan in winter by going to {tooltip:Reading:\u304d\u3087\u3046}{span:lang=ja:\u3068}. {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} is where all the old temples and history of Japan is centered. And it's really gorgeous when it snows."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} is used in a {tooltip:Radical:temple} to tell {tooltip:Kanji:time}. They don't have clocks or cell phones, they have sun dials and good old fashioned \"looking up and seeing where the sun is right now.\"",
            "hints": "Imagine being in a temple and realizing you don't know what time it is. Never fear! Look on up at the sun. Ah, yes. Blinding noon.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Time",
                "Alternatives": "O'clock, Hour"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine him going to all kinds of different times and also make sure you're specifically imagining Jesus doing all these things. Put these two together and you'll remember the reading in no time. (Haha, get it?)",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Time} in a temple makes you think of {tooltip:Reading:Je}sus ({span:lang=ja:\u3058}). Specifically, Jesus being able to perform time travel magic. He winks at you, goes back to the dinosaur ages, where he wrestles a T-rex. Then, he goes to WWII era and punches Hitler in the mouth."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have two {tooltip:Radical:bow}s but they're both covered in {tooltip:Radical:ice}. This has made them very {tooltip:Kanji:weak}.",
            "hints": "Just look at these weak, iced over bows. If you tried to draw back their strings they'd snap into a million pieces.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Weak"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3083\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you're stuck with two weak broken bows and no jack. Ice is lame.",
                "mnemonic": "You give up on your trip and bring the {tooltip:Kanji:weak} bows back to your car, but it's stuck in the ice and snow. You decide to use the bows as a {tooltip:Reading:jack} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3083\u304f}) to try to get your car unstuck. Unfortunately, they're just too weak and they break in half."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Use a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} to travel the {tooltip:Radical:circumference} of the world and it will take you a full {tooltip:Kanji:week}. Seven whole days!",
            "hints": "A week in earth time is also known as a \"full scoot\" in scooter lingo. ;)",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Week"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You can't ride a scooter for a week barefoot, are you nuts?! Get some shoes!",
                "mnemonic": "If you want to scoot for a {tooltip:Kanji:week}, you'll need {tooltip:Reading:shoe}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}). Good shoes too, not sandals or high heels or boots. Solid, high quality shoes, so you don't fall off the scooter and hurt yourself."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is an {tooltip:Radical:insect} {tooltip:Radical:slid}ing around under your {tooltip:Radical:table}, being blown by the {tooltip:Kanji:wind}. You try to grab the insect but it keeps sliding past your hand because the wind is so strong. It\u2019s going to start blowing you around under the table too!",
            "hints": "Picture an insect, on its back, being blown around under a table. Feel the wind pushing you as you try to save the poor thing.{splitParent}This kanji also means {tooltip:Kanji:style} too. You can think of the wind blowing one style in fashion one moment and then another the next. It blows your clothes off and blows new style clothes onto you, over and over again. Imagine this happening. Are you embarrassed when all the clothes are off? Pleased when you get new style clothes on?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wind",
                "Alternative": "Style"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3046, \u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Try to stuff food in your mouth in the wind. Food tastes even better when you have to fight for it!\n",
                "mnemonic": "The only way you can distract yourself from the {tooltip:Kanji:wind} and the insect sliding around under your table is by eating lots of {tooltip:Reading:foo}d ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3046}). That\u2019s why you were at the table in the first place. It\u2019s your dining room table and it\u2019s dinner time!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What you {tooltip:Radical:say} to {tooltip:Radical:oneself} (yourself), you decide to {tooltip:Kanji:write down}. Whether this is in the form of a journal, diary, or blog, you feel the need to {tooltip:Kanji:record} these important thoughts in some way.",
            "hints": "Just imagine writing in a diary and saying everything to write aloud to yourself in your head. {splitParent}\"Dear me, today I learned a lot of new kanji on WaniKani. It was the best. I love the crabigator sooooo much. Love, me.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Write Down",
                "Alternative": "Record"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
