{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Group",
                "Alternatives": "Team, Class",
                "Word Type": "noun, suffix"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304f\u307f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304f\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39885-subject-2975.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304f\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19986-subject-2975.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You're part of a special {tooltip:Vocabulary:group}. It is the {tooltip:Reading:cumi}n group, and they deal with all things cumin (the spice / seed). Smell the cumin. Touch it. Taste it. You live and breathe the stuff, because you are the president of this cumin group.\n{splitParent}P.S. This can also be spelled {span:lang=ja:\u7d44\u307f} (same overall reading: {span:lang=ja:\u304f\u307f}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u308c\u304b\u3089\u3001\u307f\u306a\u3055\u3093\u3092\u4e8c\u7d44\u306b\u5206\u3051\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "After this, we\u2019ll be splitting into two teams."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30aa\u30ec\u305f\u3061\u306e\u7d44\u306f\u3053\u306e\u8fba\u3058\u3083\u6709\u540d\u306a\u3093\u3060\u305c\u3002",
                    "en": "Our group is famous around here."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e09\u5e74\u4e8c\u7d44\u306e\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304f\u3093\u3001\u307e\u305f\u3053\u304f\u767d\u3055\u308c\u305f\u3089\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I heard Koichi in grade 3 class 2 was asked out again."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When something is {tooltip:Kanji:hand} {tooltip:Kanji:made}, it is {tooltip:Vocabulary:handmade}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
