                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}What do you do in your {tooltip:Vocabulary:home}? You {tooltip:Reading:ea}t {tooltip:Reading:e}ggs ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3048}), that's what. You eat eggs three times a day, every day. You really love eating eggs in your {tooltip:Vocabulary:house}!\n"
