                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Someone's telling you \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:not yet}... not yet.... not yet...\" you have some food on your nose, but you're not allowed to eat it until your {tooltip:Reading:ma} says it's okay. \"Not yet... Not yet...\" Why would your mom treat you like a dog like this? Oh well... maybe she'll let you eat the food soon, at least.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u672a\u3060\u4e8c\u767e\u624d\u307e\u3067\u751f\u304d\u305f\u4eba\u3052\u3093\u306f\u3044\u306a\u3044\u3002",
