{
            "mnemonic": "This word starts with an {span:lang=ja:\u304a} to make it more polite. Then it has the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:\u5144} which you already know. Lastly, it has {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093} which is an honorific to elevate people and be polite. This is basically the formal way of saying {tooltip:Vocabulary:older brother} (versus plain old {span:lang=ja:\u5144}). It can also be used to refer to a {tooltip:Vocabulary:guy} that you don't know who has a youthful appearance. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Older Brother",
                "Alternative": "Guy",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u306b\u3044\u3055\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u306b\u3044\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "13006-subject-2621.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u306b\u3044\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "32900-subject-2621.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this one is pretty tricky, and I'd consider it an exception. To remember it, you have to learn the {span:lang=ja:\u5144} part, and everything else will fall into place. Here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}Your (kind) {tooltip:Vocabulary:older brother} pushes you down on the ground. You stand up and look at your {tooltip:Reading:knee} ({span:lang=ja:\u306b\u3044}), which is all bloody. \"Why'd you do that to my knee!?\" you ask. \"You're supposed to be a nice older brother, that's why I call you {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u5144\u3055\u3093}!\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u308c\u304c\u305f\u304b\u3057\u306e\u304a\u5144\u3055\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Which one is Takashi\u2019s older brother?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306e\u305f\u3063\u304d\u3085\u3046\u3073\u3093\u306e\u304a\u5144\u3055\u3093\u306e\u304b\u304a\u304c\u30bf\u30a4\u30d7\u3059\u304e\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The delivery guy today had exactly the type of face I go for."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u5144\u3055\u3093\u306e\u306f\u306a\u3052\u304c\u304d\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3057\u304b\u305f\u304c\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "I can\u2019t help thinking about my older brother\u2019s nose hair."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

