                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. You haven't learned this reading yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You really want to eat food that's in neat {tooltip:Vocabulary:shape}s, so you decide to use a {tooltip:Reading:cutter} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u305f}) on your {tooltip:Reading:chee}se ({span:lang=ja:\u3061}) to make it a new shape. Square cheese is so boring. After you cut it up you have mouse shaped cheese! It just tastes better like that.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3064\u307e\u3068\u305d\u3046\u3060\u3093\u3057\u3066\u3001\u5f62\u3088\u308a\u5185\u3088\u3046\u3092\u304a\u3082\u3093\u3058\u305f\u3051\u3063\u304b\u3001\u3053\u306e\u5f62\u306b\u304d\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
