                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Ra, the Egyptian god asks you: \"Can you do it? Are you {tooltip:Vocabulary:certain} you can build the pyramids?\" \n{splitParent}\"Yes I {tooltip:Reading:can ra} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u306a\u3089}). Yes I can,\" you reply.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u306f\u5fc5\u305a\u3082\u3069\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001\u5927\u3058\u3087\u3046\u3076\u3067\u3059\u3002",
