                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19993-subject-2968.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}There's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:tall} dude trying to sell you something really {tooltip:Vocabulary:expensive}. He's really going off on how great this item is and how you should buy it. This guy is a real salesman. A real {tooltip:Reading:talker} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u304b}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u5e97\u306f\u3001\u9ad8\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304c\u304a\u3044\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This restaurant is expensive, but delicious."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306b\u306f\u9ad8\u3059\u304e\u3066\u3068\u3069\u304b\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u305b\u304c\u9ad8\u3044\u30b8\u30a7\u30fc\u30e0\u30ba\u30fb\u30b9\u30c6\u30e5\u30a2\u30fc\u30c8\u3092\u5929\u56fd\u304b\u3089\u3088\u3093\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "That is too high for me to reach, so I've brought James Stewart, who is very tall, down from Heaven."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3001\u300c\u30d3\u30c3\u30b0\u30a2\u30f3\u30c9\u30c8\u30fc\u30eb\u300d\u306e\u30b9\u30fc\u30c4\u306f\u3042\u3093\u306a\u306b\u5024\u6bb5\u304c\u9ad8\u3044\u3093\u3060\uff1f",
                    "en": "Why are suits from the \"Big and Tall\" store so expensive?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. Throw a \"the\" in there if you'd like, as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "The End",
                "Alternative": "End",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3048"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39756-subject-2947.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "19850-subject-2947.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You've reached {tooltip:Vocabulary:the end} of the universe. Nothing is there. You step out, and you're surprised because you get greeted by an old Canadian man. {tooltip:Reading:Sue, eh?}({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3048}) he asks you, over and over. The poor man is looking for his wife Sue, and he's searched to the end of the universe. That's true love. As he walks off into the distance, you hear him calling out, \"Sue, eh? Sue, eh? Sue, eh?\" \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3093\u306a\u3042\u305d\u3073\u304c\u306f\u3084\u308b\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4e16\u3082\u672b\u3060\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "If this kind of game is popular, then it\u2019s the end of the world."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u305f\u304f\u306e\u3080\u3059\u5b50\u3055\u3093\u306f\u672b\u304c\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u305f\u306e\u3057\u307f\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "You must be looking forward to seeing what your son might end up being in the future."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6fc0\u3057\u3044\u53e3\u8ad6\u306e\u672b\u3001\u672b\u606f\u5b50\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u91d1\u3092\u3069\u3053\u304b\u306b\u57cb\u3081\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u51fa\u3066\u884c\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After a heated discussion, my youngest son left to bury my gold somewhere."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Okay, so this one is really weird, sorry. Each of us only get {tooltip:Kanji:one} {tooltip:Kanji:body} in our lifetimes, right? Well what {tooltip:Vocabulary:the heck}! What if I want more than one body. Let's all be mad about this together. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "The Heck",
                "Alternatives": "In The World, On Earth",
                "Word Type": "adverb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
