                        "file": "19683-subject-2903.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have to learn the {span:lang=ja:\u306a\u304a} part. Think of it this way. Something needs {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be fixed}. It's urgent! You have to fix it {tooltip:Reading:now}! ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u304a}). This will also work with the similar word, {span:lang=ja:\u76f4\u3059}, which you'll learn soon if you haven't already.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3057\u305f\u8eca\u304c\u76f4\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "When can I get my broken car fixed?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u308c\u3067\u30a2\u30e4\u306e\u6c17\u3052\u3093\u304c\u76f4\u308b\u306a\u3089\u3001\u304a\u308c\u306f\u305c\u3093\u305c\u3093\u304b\u307e\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "If it makes you feel better, then I don't mind at all, Aya."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8fb2\u592b\u306e\u58ca\u308c\u305f\u30c8\u30e9\u30af\u30bf\u30fc\u306f\u76f4\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The farmer\u2019s broken tractor was fixed."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
