{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji portion means {tooltip:Kanji:fault}, so you would think the verb version is \"to fault.\" It's a little different, though. Think of it this way, if you \"fault\" something, you're messing up. What's a great way to mess up? By losing something. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to lose}. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Lose",
                "Alternatives": "To Part With, To Lose Something, To Part With Something",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
