                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine buying an entire car's worth of shellfish. Mmm delicious.",
                "mnemonic": "You decide to {tooltip:Kanji:buy} as many shellfish as you can fit in your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). You keep buying until your car is completely full of shellfish before you stop. Cars are totally a realistic unit of measure."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:rain} {tooltip:Radical:cloud} is still a {tooltip:Kanji:cloud}! It's probably going to rain on you soon though, so I hope you have a jacket or an umbrella.",
            "hints": "Picture all of the different types of clouds in the sky. There are puffy white ones, heavy dark ones, and wispy thin ones. But they're all clouds.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cloud"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3082",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You look at each cloud and each one is a different cool mom. They're each doing different cool mom things. You suddenly don't want to look at the clouds anymore.",
                "mnemonic": "You lie down and try to figure out what the {tooltip:Kanji:cloud}s are shaped like. The first cloud is shaped... like a {tooltip:Reading:coo}l {tooltip:Reading:mo}m ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3082}). She's wearing high pants, and holding a kid on each hip, but she's also listening to the latest music and using slang. Huh. You look to the next cloud and see... wait, another cool mom?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:white} {tooltip:Radical:ice} {tooltip:Radical:tree} is a magical tree. When you eat its ice flowers it gives you incredible amounts of {tooltip:Kanji:comfort}, {tooltip:Kanji:ease}, and {tooltip:Kanji:pleasure}.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself picking the white ice flowers off the tree. Then, put it in your mouth. Make it taste comforting... It puts you at ease. Then, swallow it. Feel your head go nuts with comfort. This is the greatest drug in the world when it comes to comfort. So much pleasure!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Comfort",
                "Alternatives": "Ease, Pleasure"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3089\u304f, \u304c\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine setting up the rack. Make it look beautiful. Shift around the flowers. Fill up the entire rack. Of course, your focus should be on the rack portion.",
                "mnemonic": "You want more of this, You gather as much as you can, and create an entire {tooltip:Reading:rack} ({span:lang=ja:\u3089\u304f}) at your store with this tree. You sell out immediately, and have to refill your rack."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:winter}, the {tooltip:Radical:woman} has to go through all the {tooltip:Radical:rice} and {tooltip:Kanji:count} each individual grain. Once she's counted all of them, she'll have an {tooltip:Kanji:amount} / {tooltip:Kanji:number} so that she can split them up accordingly.",
            "hints": "She has to count each grain out in order to divvy up the supply to last through the winter. Imagine yourself getting just a few grains today for food. It's not a good time for you guys :(",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Count",
                "Alternatives": "Number, Amount"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305e, \u304b\u305a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Come up with a story about why your farm got sued for everything. Go to the court  case. Listen to the judge come up with your verdict. Be angry. This has ruined everything.",
                "mnemonic": "Why are you so low on rice? It's because someone {tooltip:Reading:sue}d your farm and took everything you owned. So, you had barely enough rice (or not enough)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have at your disposal a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} and a {tooltip:Radical:hook} to assassinate this {tooltip:Radical:person}. Which weapon will you choose. {tooltip:Kanji:Decide} now!",
            "hints": "Have trouble with the decision. Which one? Tsunami will be big and cool, but a hook will be more discreet. How can you decide? Can you think of a neat way to decide this, like Two-Face on Batman?",
