                "mnemonic": "You are looking at a horse. It's looking at you. You try making horse noises at it, to get a reaction. Instead of reacting with a normal horse noise, it just makes sheep noises: \"{tooltip:Reading:Baaa},\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3070}) it says. \"Baaaaa.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:gate} that the {tooltip:Radical:sun} goes through at a regular {tooltip:Kanji:interval}. There is an {tooltip:Kanji:interval of time} in the sense that the sun goes through it at the same time every day. And there is an {tooltip:Kanji:interval of space} in the sense that it has to go through the space between the gate posts.",
            "hints": "\"Interval\" is a weird word to remember, but just think of the sun going around the earth and through the gate like clockwork. Every 24 hours it passes through the gate, and each interval is exactly the same.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Interval",
                "Alternatives": "Interval of Time, Interval of Space"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093, \u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3044\u3060, \u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Genghis Khan ordering his most skilled inventors and builders to create this special sun gate so they can harness the power of intervals, and all people under his rule can benefit from the accurate telling of time.",
                "mnemonic": "This method of keeping track of {tooltip:Kanji:interval}s of time was invented by the great Khans of Mongolia, specifically the most famous Khan of all: Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Dirt} makes it {tooltip:Radical:easy} to identify your {tooltip:Kanji:location}. If you know that, you can go from {tooltip:Kanji:place} to place.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking at the dirt. It's a distinct color and texture, and you're able to identify your location just from that alone.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Location",
                "Alternative": "Place"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Remember Jourm? He's our local farmhand who only has nine toes (from the {span:lang=ja:\u4e0a} mnemonic). Imagine that guy explaining to you how to know your location from dirt. He may be a bit clumsy, but the man really does know his dirt.",
                "mnemonic": "Knowing your {tooltip:Kanji:location} from dirt is quite a feat! Who taught you that? It was {tooltip:Reading:Jou}rm ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087\u3046}), the big local farmhand. Despite being a bit weird, he does really know his dirt and can tell you the {tooltip:Kanji:place} from which any dirt came."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're in a {tooltip:Radical:cage} and you've been shot by an {tooltip:Radical:arrow}. Obviously things are looking pretty bad. You need some {tooltip:Kanji:medicine} if you hope to live.",
