{
            "mnemonic": "Do you remember the word {span:lang=ja:\u601d\u3046}? It means \"to think.\" What you are {tooltip:Kanji:think}ing is {tooltip:Kanji:exit}ing\u2014it's coming out of your head! You're recalling {tooltip:Vocabulary:a memory} and/or {tooltip:Vocabulary:memories}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "A Memory",
                "Alternatives": "Memories, Memory",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082\u3044\u3067"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3082\u3044\u3067",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20153-subject-3433.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3082\u3044\u3067",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40063-subject-3433.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are both kun'yomi, but based off of previous experience with the two separate words that make up this word, you should be able to read it. Just remember that it's kun'yomi. One hint is the hiragana sticking out of the {span:lang=ja:\u601d}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3063\u3066\u3001\u3080\u306d\u306b\u305d\u3063\u3068\u3057\u307e\u3063\u3066\u304a\u304f\u3082\u306e\u306a\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "Aren\u2019t memories things you lock safely away in your chest?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u306e\u3053\u308d\u3001\u65e5\u304c\u304f\u308c\u308b\u307e\u3067\u53cb\u3060\u3061\u3068\u3042\u305d\u3093\u3067\u3044\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4eca\u3068\u306a\u3063\u3066\u306f\u3068\u3066\u3082\u306a\u3064\u304b\u3057\u3044\u3044\u3044\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3067\u3059\u3002\u4eca\u306f\u3082\u3046\u304b\u3093\u5168\u30dc\u30c3\u30c1\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3089\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I used to play with my friends until it got dark. It's a really great, nostalgic memory now especially because I don't have any friends anymore."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u304c\u6bce\u9031\u65e5\u66dc\u65e5\u306e\u671d\u306b\u30c1\u30e7\u30b3\u30ec\u30fc\u30c8\u3067\u30b3\u30fc\u30c6\u30a3\u30f3\u30b0\u3055\u308c\u305f\u30d9\u30fc\u30b3\u30f3\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u306e\u306f\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u3044\u3044\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My dad making chocolate covered bacon for us every Sunday morning is such a good memory of mine."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you stick this onto the end of another word that talks about an {tooltip:Kanji:interval of time} in some way, you're indicating the {tooltip:Vocabulary:amount of time} that has gone past. For example, {span:lang=ja:\u4e8c\u5e74\u9593} is \"two years.\" {span:lang=ja:\u4e00\u6642\u9593} is \"one hour.\" Any amount of time + {span:lang=ja:\u301c\u9593} will make it an \"amount of time\" instead of just a specific time.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Amount Of Time",
                "Alternatives": "Interval Of Time, Time Interval, Period Of Time",
                "Word Type": "noun, suffix"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093"
