                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji (on'yomi), probably because it usually is attached to other words (aka names, like {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061\u541b}) making it act more like jukugo words do.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u5e74\u306e\u590f\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u5c71\u7530\u541b\u3068\u3001\u30c7\u30a3\u30ba\u30cb\u30fc\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3042\u308b\u30db\u30c6\u30eb\u306b\u3068\u307e\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "This summer, I stayed in a hotel in Disney Land with Yamada."
