{
            "mnemonic": "Remember how {span:lang=ja:\u5165\u308a\u53e3} means entrance and {span:lang=ja:\u51fa\u53e3} means exit? This is just the {span:lang=ja:\u53e3} part with a direction on it. That means it can be both entrance or exit. So when you have {tooltip:Kanji:East} up there this word can mean both {tooltip:Vocabulary:East exit} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:East entrance}. This is a great word to know if you need to know which side of a train station you need to leave on to go somewhere or meet someone!",
