                        "file": "20132-subject-3008.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u305b\u3093\u5f8c\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u5bfe\u5916\u305b\u3044\u3055\u304f\u306f\u3069\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u304b\u308f\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "How did Japan\u2019s foreign policy change postwar?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u5bfe\u5916\u305b\u3044\u3055\u304f\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u306e\u30dd\u30c3\u30c9\u30ad\u30e3\u30b9\u30c8\u3092\u30ec\u30b3\u30fc\u30c7\u30a3\u30f3\u30b0\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We are recording a podcast about Japan's foreign policy."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u306e\u5bfe\u5916\u50b5\u52d9\u304c5000\u5104\u30c9\u30eb\u3092\u7a81\u7834\u3057\u305f\u6642\u306b\u3001\u4ffa\u306e\u500b\u4eba\u8ca0\u50b5\u304c500\u4e07\u30c9\u30eb\u3092\u7a81\u7834\u3057\u305f\u306e\u306f\u3001\u5358\u306a\u308b\u5076\u7136\u306a\u306e\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Is it just a coincidence that my personal debt shot past $5 million when America\u2019s foreign debt shot past $500 billion?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:pleasure}? Well, you could say it's \"pleasurable,\" but I'm afraid that's not what we're going for here. In this case, this word is a little more innocent. It just means {tooltip:Vocabulary:fun}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fun",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u306e\u3057\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u306e\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40180-subject-3071.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u306e\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20278-subject-3071.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}How much {tooltip:Vocabulary:fun} did you have? You just had a {tooltip:Reading:ton o'} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u306e}) fun!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30b2\u30fc\u30e0\u306f\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u697d\u3057\u304f\u3066\u3001\u304a\u3082\u767d\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This game is really fun and interesting."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c6\u30ec\u30d3\u3092\u898b\u306a\u304c\u3089\u98df\u3079\u308b\u65b9\u304c\u3001\u3057\u3083\u3079\u308a\u306a\u304c\u3089\u98df\u3079\u308b\u3088\u308a\u697d\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "It's more fun to eat while watching TV than it is to eat while chatting."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u98db\u884c\u6a5f\u304b\u3089\u98db\u3073\u964d\u308a\u308b\u3063\u3066\u3001\u7269\u51c4\u304f\u697d\u3057\u3044\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "Jumping out of an airplane is so much fun!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:north} {tooltip:Kanji:sea} {tooltip:Kanji:road} is the road you take to get to the northern sea. That is an area of Japan, actually. That area is known as {tooltip:Vocabulary:Hokkaido}. It's a very nice place, be sure to visit it if you can for some of the freshest seafood around.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hokkaido",
                "Alternative": "Hokkaidou",
