                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u307e",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20231-subject-2990.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}Imagine someone riding a horse. Who is that person? It's {tooltip:Reading:Uma} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u307e}) Thurman, the famous actress.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u99ac\u306b\u3001\u30cb\u30f3\u30b8\u30f3\u3084\u30ea\u30f3\u30b4\u3092\u3042\u3052\u3066\u3082\u3044\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Is it okay to give that horse carrots and apples?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u99ac\u306f\u3001\u307e\u305f\u4e00\u3064\u3053\u3093\u306a\u3093\u3092\u306e\u308a\u3053\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My horse has overcome yet another difficulty."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u5e74\u5bc4\u308a\u305f\u3061\u304c\u6b21\u304b\u3089\u6b21\u3078\u3068\u99ac\u304b\u3089\u843d\u3061\u305f\u306e\u3001\u3081\u3061\u3083\u304f\u3061\u3083\u9762\u767d\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u301c\uff01",
                    "en": "I find it unreasonably funny when old people fall off of horses one after another."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word was probably made pretty recently. A {tooltip:Kanji:horse}'s {tooltip:Kanji:power}? That is {tooltip:Vocabulary:horsepower}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Horsepower",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3070\u308a\u304d"
