                        "file": "39974-subject-2991.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3070\u308a\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20065-subject-2991.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. \n{splitParent}Take note that the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u529b} is the {span:lang=ja:\u308a\u304d} version of the reading. You can remember this by thinking about how it's {tooltip:Reading:Ricky} who drives the high {tooltip:Vocabulary:horsepower} cars. Vroom vroom Ricky!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u3069\u3046\u8eca\u306e\u99ac\u529b\u3092\u4e0a\u3052\u308b\u306b\u306f\u3001\u3069\u3046\u3059\u308c\u3070\u3044\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "What\u2019s the best way to increase a car\u2019s horsepower?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30b5\u30d2\u306e\u3058\u3044\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3063\u3066\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u99ac\u529b\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Asahi, your grandpa is such an energetic person, isn't he?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7d04\u56db\u5e74\u9593\u3044\u3058\u304f\u308a\u56de\u3057\u305f\u304a\u304b\u3052\u3067\u3001\u4eca\u4ffa\u306e\u829d\u5208\u308a\u6a5f\u306f450\u99ac\u529b\u3082\u3042\u308b\u3093\u3060\u305c\u3002",
                    "en": "I tinkered with my lawnmower for about four years and now it has 450 horsepower."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:person} {tooltip:Kanji:interval}. Just think of different intervals each with a different type of species. The raccoon interval... the dog interval... the person interval... they are the {tooltip:Vocabulary:human}s.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Human",
                "Alternative": "Human Being",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306b\u3093\u3052\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u3093\u3052\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40067-subject-3061.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u3093\u3052\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20158-subject-3061.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. For {span:lang=ja:\u4eba} that's okay. For {span:lang=ja:\u9593} it's something weird, something you didn't learn with the kanji. To remember this, think of the {tooltip:Vocabulary:human}s, living on this earth. They are only a small part of this earth's existence, though. This human {tooltip:Reading:gen}eration ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}) is hopefully going to be a long one, but we'll see how that goes.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3055\u3063\u304d\u30ab\u30d5\u30a7\u3067\u3001\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3092\u306e\u3093\u3067\u308b\u3057\u3070\u72ac\u3092\u898b\u304b\u3051\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "A while ago I saw a shiba inu drinking coffee like a human at a cafe."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u3059\u304d\u306a\u3057\u306f\u3001\u3042\u3044\u7530\u307f\u3064\u3092\u306e\u3001\u300c\u3064\u307e\u3065\u3044\u305f\u3063\u3066\u3000\u3044\u3044\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3000\u306b\u3093\u3052\u3093\u3060\u3082\u306e\u300d\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3057\u3067\u3059\u3002\u4eba\u9593\u3068\u3044\u3046\u304b\u3093\u5b57\u304c\u3072\u3089\u304c\u306a\u3067\u304b\u304b\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3053\u308d\u304c\u3059\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My favorite poem is Mitsuo Aida's, \"It\u2019s ok to stumble, isn\u2019t it,\nwe are humans after all.\" I like this because the kanji for humans is written in hiragana."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eba\u9593\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u4eba\u751f\u306e\u76ee\u7684\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u60a9\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3002\u3067\u3082\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u305d\u306e\u7b54\u3048\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u305f\u6c17\u304c\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002Tofugu\u3067\u52c9\u5f37\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\uff01",
