                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "41277-subject-3058.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3044\u3060",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40023-subject-3058.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3044\u3060",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20105-subject-3058.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it uses the kun'yomi reading. {span:lang=ja:\u9593} has two common kun'yomi readings, {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044\u3060} and {span:lang=ja:\u307e}. You haven't learned these readings yet, so here's an explanation of each reading and mnemonics to help you remember them: \n{splitParent}When {span:lang=ja:\u9593} refers to a longer interval of time, it's generally read as {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044\u3060}. For a short burst of time, it's read as {span:lang=ja:\u307e}. When it means an interval of space, it's usually read as {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044\u3060}. \n{splitParent}You can remember this because time feels longer in {tooltip:Reading:Ida}ho ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044\u3060}). Any interval of time you spend there feels so long, because Idaho life moves so slowly. As soon as you cross the border and enter a new state, you call your {tooltip:Reading:ma} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e}) to tell her you're finally out of that slooooow state, and the intervals of time feel shorter. \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u305f\u3044\u3066\u3044\u3001\u306d\u3066\u3044\u308b\u9593\u306f\u3001\u3060\u3093\u307c\u3046\u3092\u5207\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Usually, I turn off the heater while I\u2019m sleeping."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u9593\u306b\u3001\u3044\u305d\u3044\u3067\u3072\u308b\u3054\u306f\u3093\u3092\u304b\u304d\u3053\u307f\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Meanwhile, I shoved my lunch in my mouth."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7b4f\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u9593\u306b\u3001\u4ffa\u9054\u307f\u3093\u306a\u9913\u6b7b\u306b\u3057\u3061\u307e\u3046\u3088\uff01\u6cf3\u3044\u3067\u5ddd\u3092\u6e21\u3063\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u7121\u96e3\u306a\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "In the time it takes to build a raft we\u2019ll die of starvation! Wouldn\u2019t it be safer to just swim across the river?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
