{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen the word {span:lang=ja:\u51fa\u6765\u308b} (to be able to do), which is the first part. Then the second part, {span:lang=ja:\u4e0a\u304c\u308b} means \"to rise.\" So, think about it this way: once you're able to do something, you rise because you're finished. That's why this verb means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be finished}.",
