{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u4ea4\u305c\u308b} means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to mix} and that the kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:mix} as well. So, this probably has something to do with mixing things. This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be mixed}. This is when something is mixed but it's not mixed by you. It's just being mixed. Think of it this way - the {span:lang=ja:\u3058} in {span:lang=ja:\u4ea4\u3058\u308b} is Jesus, who just uses Jesus magic to mix something. So, you're not mixing it. It's just when something is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be mixed}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Mixed",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Blended With, To Join",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
