                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u305f\u3044\u3068\u4e0d\u5b89\u304c\u4ea4\u3058\u3063\u305f\u6c17\u3082\u3061\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My anxiety is mixed with excitement."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u3055\u3044\u3075\u3092\u3059\u3063\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u305d\u306e\u30b9\u30ea\u306f\u3059\u65e9\u304f\u4eba\u3054\u307f\u306b\u4ea4\u3058\u3063\u3066\u304d\u3048\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After snatching my wallet, the pickpocket quickly blended in with the crowd and disappeared."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a verb because it ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound. What does the kanji mean? It's {tooltip:Kanji:music} and {tooltip:Kanji:bend}. In the case of this word, we're going with the \"bend\" version. The verb of that is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to bend}. This is when you're doing the bending. You can remember this because {span:lang=ja:\u3052} is the {tooltip:Reading:gen}tleman you're bending. He looked good before you bent him in half.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Bend",
                "Alternative": "To Bend Something",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3052\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
