{
            "mnemonic": "Because this word ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you can tell it's probably a verb. The kanji portion means {tooltip:Vocabulary:near}. The verb version of that is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to draw near}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to get close} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to approach}. Essentially, the general idea is that you're getting closer to something. You're becoming more nearby. You're approaching.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Get Close",
                "Alternatives": "To Approach, To Draw Near, To Near, To Bring Near",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
