                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3066\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40017-subject-3465.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3066\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20110-subject-3465.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading can be remembered via the word {span:lang=ja:\u5f53\u305f\u308b} which you learned a few levels ago. Use that knowledge to remember that this word is read as {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3066\u308b}. The important part is the {span:lang=ja:\u3042}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u8c9d\u304c\u3089\u3001\u8033\u306b\u5f53\u3066\u308b\u3068\u306a\u307f\u306e\u97f3\u304c\u3059\u308b\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "Put this shell to your ear and you\u2019ll hear the sound of the waves."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3072\u308b\u4f11\u307f\u306b\u3001\u3060\u308c\u304c\u3046\u305d\u3092\u3064\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3092\u5f53\u3066\u308b\u30b2\u30fc\u30e0\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We played a game trying to guess who was lying during lunch break."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30dc\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u30d0\u30c3\u30c8\u306b\u4e0a\u624b\u304f\u5f53\u3066\u305f\u3068\u8a00\u3044\u305f\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u9593\u9055\u3048\u3066\u304a\u5c3b\u306b\u5f53\u3066\u305f\u3068\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I wanted to say, \"I hit the ball really well with my bat,\" but I accidentally said butt."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:help} so the verb version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to help}. Don't confuse this with {span:lang=ja:\u52a9\u304b\u308b} which means \"to be helped.\" You know that {span:lang=ja:\u52a9\u3051\u308b} is \"to help\" because you're doing the helping. You know that you're doing the helping because you {tooltip:Reading:care} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u308b}).",
