                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "41293-subject-5934.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307f\u3087\u3046\u306b\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "41292-subject-5934.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3057\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40176-subject-5934.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3057\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20271-subject-5934.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading makes no sense at all. You have to learn it straight up, and can't rely on the kanji it's made from. Why is {tooltip:Vocabulary:tomorrow} going to be such a bright and awesome day? Because you're making {tooltip:Reading:ash ta}cos for dinner, and that's your favorite. Imagine imagining tomorrow, full of ash tacos and deliciousness. Maybe you could use some of those Dorito taco shells?\n{splitParent}A note about the other two readings {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3059} and {span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3087\u3046\u306b\u3061}: {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3059} is used in the news and in weather reports, and {span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3087\u3046\u306b\u3061} is really only used in business, so you should really only be using {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3057\u305f} for now. But it's good to know that the other two readings exist!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u660e\u65e5\u3001\u3073\u3087\u3046\u3044\u3093\u3078\u884c\u304d\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "Let\u2019s go to the hospital tomorrow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u660e\u65e5\u306f\u660e\u65e5\u306e\u98a8\u304c\u3075\u304f\u3002",
                    "en": "Tomorrow is another day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e00\u30f6\u6708\u30a4\u30bf\u30ea\u30a2\u306b\u884c\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u77e5\u3089\u305b\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u660e\u65e5\u5b66\u6821\u306b\u96fb\u8a71\u3057\u306a\u304f\u3066\u306f\u3044\u3051\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I need to call the school tomorrow to inform them that I\u2019m going to Italy for a month."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know the word {span:lang=ja:\u76f4\u3059} from a couple levels ago. It means \"to fix.\" So, when you fix what you see, what are you doing? You're reevaluating something. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to reevaluate}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Reevaluate",
                "Alternatives": "To Look Again, To Reassess",
                "Word Type": "godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307f\u306a\u304a\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
