                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You need {tooltip:Vocabulary:to support} someone. In order to support them, you grab two saws. One saw and another saw. A {tooltip:Reading:saw saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3055} combination good enough to do all the supporting you need - and maybe cut some supports too).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3084\u3063\u3071\u308a\u3001\u304a\u308c\u306e\u3057\u3085\u3046\u5165\u3060\u3051\u3067\u3001\u4e00\u5bb6\u3092\u652f\u3048\u308b\u306e\u306f\u304d\u3073\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002",
