                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached, so you can bet it uses the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn this reading with the kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You're at a baseball game watching people {tooltip:Vocabulary:throw} balls around. But you're hungry so you call for a snack from a vendor. You raise your hand and they throw some {tooltip:Reading:na}chos ({span:lang=ja:\u306a}) at you. Oh no! Oh ouch! The nachos are hot and they hit you in the face. The vendor just threw a bunch of hot, sauced nachos at you! WHY?!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3042\u305f\u3089\u3057\u3044\u30dc\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u6295\u3052\u3084\u3059\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This new ball is very easy to throw."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3042\u306e\u4eba\u305f\u3061\u306f\u3001\u304b\u3093\u305d\u3046\u3057\u305f\u5927\u305a\u3092\u6295\u3052\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Why are those people throwing dried soy beans?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d4\u30c3\u30c1\u30e3\u30fc\u304c\u30dc\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u6295\u3052\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3046\u3069\u30d0\u30c3\u30bf\u30fc\u306e\u524d\u3092\u98db\u3093\u3067\u3044\u305f\u9ce9\u306b\u5f53\u305f\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "The pitcher threw the ball and it struck a pigeon flying in front of the batter."
