                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39958-subject-3029.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the kun'yomi reading, but that's the reading you learned with the kanji so you should be able to read this one too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u571f\u3088\u3046\u65e5\u306b\u3001\u68ee\u3067\u30d4\u30af\u30cb\u30c3\u30af\u3092\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "On Saturday, we had a picnic in the woods."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u306f\u6728\u3092\u898b\u3066\u68ee\u3092\u898b\u305a\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "You can't see the wood for the trees, mom!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8d64\u305a\u304d\u3093\u3061\u3083\u3093\u304c\u68ee\u306e\u4e2d\u3092\u6b69\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3001\u6b7b\u3093\u3060\u72fc\u306b\u51fa\u304f\u308f\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u8d64\u305a\u304d\u3093\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306f\u305d\u306e\u5834\u3092\u7acb\u3061\u53bb\u308a\u3001\u8a2a\u308c\u305f\u304a\u3070\u3042\u3055\u3093\u306e\u5bb6\u3067\u7d20\u6674\u3089\u3057\u3044\u6642\u9593\u3092\u904e\u3054\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Little Red Riding Hood was walking through the forest when she came upon a dead wolf. Then she went on her way and had a lovely visit with her grandmother."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {span:lang=ja:\u304a} is added to elevate someone in {tooltip:Kanji:front} of you. What do you call someone in front of you? That's right, {tooltip:Vocabulary:you}. Over time, this word has lost its sense of politeness, and nowadays it sounds very rough and often rude. This \"you\" is a good way to show anger, and some people also use it in very casual situations to show affection.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "You",
                "Word Type": "pronoun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u307e\u3048"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u307e\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40026-subject-7531.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u307e\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20104-subject-7531.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u524d} is the kun'yomi, like the reading for the vocabulary word {span:lang=ja:\u524d}. So long as you know that word, you'll be able to read this one too. \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e00\u751f\u304a\u524d\u3068\u3044\u3063\u3057\u3087\u306b\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u304d\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I want to live my whole life with you."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5973\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304a\u524d\u3063\u3066\u3088\u3076\u7537\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u304d\u3089\u3044\u3060\u308f\u3002",
                    "en": "I really hate men who call women \"you.\""
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u524d\u306e\u4f5c\u308b\u9903\u5b50\u306f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u7f8e\u5473\u3057\u3044\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "The gyoza you make is really tasty."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Okay, so the kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:buddy} and so does the word, but it also means {tooltip:Vocabulary:you} as well. This is one of the several ways to say \"you\" in Japanese, and this one is kind of an \"affectionate\" you. Maybe you'd say it with someone you're close to. Maybe you'd say it with a girlfriend or boyfriend. You wouldn't want to use it with your boss or teacher, though. Make sure to keep that in mind. It's kind of like saying \"hey buddy\" or \"hey you,\" after all.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "You",
                "Alternative": "Buddy",
                "Word Type": "pronoun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u307f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39969-subject-3005.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20055-subject-3005.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}Who's your {tooltip:Vocabulary:buddy}? It's {tooltip:Reading:Kimmy} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u307f})! If you know a Kimmy, imagine her. If you don't, find a famous Kimmy or make up a Kimmy to imagine. You ask... is it you?? Wait, you're my buddy?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u541b\u3068\u307c\u304f\u306f\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3044\u3063\u3057\u3087\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You and I will always be together."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u541b\u306f\u3051\u3063\u3053\u3046\u305b\u304c\u3072\u304f\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3001\u30b7\u30e3\u30ef\u30fc\u30d8\u30c3\u30c9\u3092\u30d5\u30c3\u30af\u304b\u3089\u5916\u305b\u308b\u304b\u5fc3\u3071\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "You're pretty short, so I'm worried if you'll be able to reach the shower head and take it off the hook."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u541b\u306f\u3001\u30a8\u30ec\u30d9\u30fc\u30bf\u30fc\u3067\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u9589\u3058\u8fbc\u3081\u3089\u308c\u305f\u304f\u306a\u3044\u4eba\u30ca\u30f3\u30d0\u30fc\u30ef\u30f3\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "You are the worst person to be stuck with in an elevator."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
