                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you have to try to make some other fool lose. Otherwise you'll be the loser fool forever.",
                "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Kanji:lose}, you're a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}). All you had to do was not hold the prison shellfish. It really shouldn't have been that hard to not lose, ya fool."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You need to look a {tooltip:Radical:tree} in the {tooltip:Radical:eye} to gain a {tooltip:Kanji:mutual} respect for each other. Stand up straight, look the tree directly in its eye(s). If it looks right back, you know things are mutual.",
            "hints": "It's the same with humans, you know? If you want to have a mutual relationship you need to be able to look each other in the eyes. If you're too embarrassed, or you look down on them, then that isn't mutual respect!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mutual"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
