                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now the nori is going for a ride too, woohoo!",
                "mnemonic": "You decide the grain is probably lonely on this {tooltip:Kanji:ride} alone, so you add some {tooltip:Reading:no}ri ({span:lang=ja:\u306e}) seaweed, so it has a friend."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Some of your {tooltip:Radical:private} {tooltip:Radical:dirt} is on the {tooltip:Radical:ground}, so you stick a {tooltip:Radical:flag} into it. Then on this private land you claimed, you build a {tooltip:Kanji:roof}. Under the roof you also build some {tooltip:Kanji:shop}s and {tooltip:Kanji:store}s.",
            "hints": "That's the natural next progression of claiming some land. Building a roof upon it and building some shops and stores inside. You'll see why in a moment.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Roof",
                "Alternatives": "Shop, Store"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You have yourself a whole Yankees stadium, and all it took was a roof and some shops / stores! If you build it, they will come.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:roof} covering the dirt is there so that the {tooltip:Reading:Ya}nkees ({span:lang=ja:\u3084}) can play baseball year round. The {tooltip:Kanji:store}s and {tooltip:Kanji:shop}s are there to sell hot dogs and Yankees memorabilia."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There\u2019s a {tooltip:Radical:samurai} with (just) his {tooltip:Radical:forehead} and {tooltip:Radical:legs}. Everything in between is missing. What happened to everything in between? He was low on money, so he had to {tooltip:Kanji:sell} it all, leaving him with only the top and the bottom.",
            "hints": "Imagine this terrifying samurai. You have legs\u2026 okay, that\u2019s normal. But, then you have just a giant forehead on the top of everything else, walking around. It's pretty scary that someone would sell such important parts of their body.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sell"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine saying, \"Bye,\" loudly into the forehead of a samurai trying to sell you the rest of their face. If you say it loud enough it will distract them while you run away.",
                "mnemonic": "If you see a samurai trying to {tooltip:Kanji:sell} all their body parts here's what you should say, \"{tooltip:Reading:Bye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u3044})!\" and just get the heck out of there. Actually, if anyone tries to sell you a body part you should probably say bye over and over until you can get away from them."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On its {tooltip:Radical:scooter}, a {tooltip:Radical:horn}ed creature from {tooltip:Radical:heaven} will take things you want to {tooltip:Kanji:send} there.",
            "hints": "Picture the horned thing on its scooter, a big messenger bag over its shoulder with the kanji for heaven on it. \"You got somethin' you want me to send?\" it mutters.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Send"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
