                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3067\u3082\u3001\u305d\u308c\u306f\u305f\u3093\u306a\u308b\u4eee\u5b9a\u306e\u8a71\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "But that\u2019s just an assumption, right?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305f\u3068\u3048\u3070\u3001\u4e00\u30c9\u30eb\u767e\u5186\u3068\u4eee\u5b9a\u3059\u308b\u3068\u3001\u4e00\u672c\u4e00\u30c9\u30eb\u306e\u30b3\u30ab\u30b3\u30fc\u30e9\u306f\u767e\u5186\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3088\u306d\uff1f",
                    "en": "For example, if we say one dollar is one hundred yen, then one can of $1 coca cola is one hundred yen, right?"
