{
            "mnemonic": "This word contains the words {span:lang=ja:\u6c17} (energy) and {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u3051\u308b} (to attach). So, when you {tooltip:Kanji:attach} {tooltip:Kanji:energy} to something you're focusing in on it, right? This word is a sort of \"order\" as well, since it's te-form there at the end. It's a set phrase people say to other people who are doing dangerous things. It's kind of like saying \"Attach energy to what you're doing! Stay focused!\" A simpler way to translate this would be to say this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:be careful} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:take care}, though. Learn this word so that you can always show that you're caring for your friends!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Be Careful",
                "Alternative": "Take Care",
                "Word Type": "expression"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
