                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20563-subject-3127.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the kanji reading you learned. When writing out the answer to this reading, omit the {span:lang=ja:\u301c} as it's only there to let you know that some other word should come before it.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f1f\u306f\u3001\u304b\u305c\u306738\u5ea6\u306e\u306d\u3064\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My brother has a cold and a fever of 38 degrees Celsius."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a8\u30a2\u30b3\u30f3\u306e\u304a\u3093\u5ea6\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u4f55\u5ea6\u3050\u3089\u3044\u306b\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "What temperature do you usually set the AC to?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\uff12\uff14\u5ea6\u3050\u3089\u3044\u304c\u3061\u3087\u3046\u3069\u3044\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "I think about 24 degrees is just right for me."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
