                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3082\u3066",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40416-subject-7573.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. You haven't learned this reading yet though, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You're standing in front of a building, staring at its {tooltip:Vocabulary:front}. You spend some time gazing at it before you realize what it is. \"{tooltip:Reading:Oh}, {tooltip:Reading:motel} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3082\u3066})\", you say aloud. A little time looking at the {tooltip:Vocabulary:exterior} and you're able to figure it out.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u8868\u306f\u30d4\u30f3\u30af\u8272\u306b\u306c\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please paint the front pink."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u8868\u306e\u304b\u304a\u306f\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u793e\u9577\u3067\u3042\u308b\u304c\u3001\u3046\u3089\u306e\u304b\u304a\u306f\u4e16\u754c\u3067\u3082\u6709\u6570\u306e\u30b8\u30e3\u30b0\u30ea\u30f3\u30b0\u305b\u3093\u624b\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi's public face is the president of Tofugu, but his private face is the most well-known juggler in the world."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5341\u5186\u7389\u306e\u8868\u306f\u3069\u3061\u3089\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Which side of a ten yen coin is the face?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": [
                {
                    "en": "to go outside",
                    "ja": "\u8868\u306b\u51fa\u308b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "the front and back of a coin",
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a4\u30f3\u306e\u8868\u3068\u88cf",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "the front of a card",
                    "ja": "\u30ab\u30fc\u30c9\u306e\u8868",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                }
            ]
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:house} {tooltip:Kanji:tools} aren't the tools you use to build a house. They're more like the things that are a part of your house that you use like tools. Those things would be your {tooltip:Vocabulary:furniture}. So, remember, your house tools are just furniture.",
