                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u9031\u672b\u306f\u3001\u65b0\u304d\u3087\u306e\u5bb6\u5177\u3092\u8cb7\u3044\u306b\u884c\u304f\u4e88\u5b9a\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I plan to go buy furniture for my new house this weekend."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u738b\u5973\u306e\u5bb6\u5177\u306f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u3059\u3070\u3089\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3059\u306d\uff01\u3055\u3059\u304c\u3067\u3059\uff01",
                    "en": "You have such wonderful furniture, Princess! Very impressive."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5bb6\u5177\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u5bb6\u306b\u304a\u904b\u3073\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u3082\u3046\u5c11\u3057\u8170\u3092\u8efd\u304f\u3057\u3066\u6249\u3068\u7a93\u3092\u65e9\u304f\u53d6\u308a\u4ed8\u3051\u308b\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u306e\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We moved the furniture to your new house but you should act quickly to get the doors and windows installed."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093} on the end is the name honorific {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093}. It's there to show some respect. It's like saying \"Mr. Guest!\" or something like that. But that sounds dumb in English. We'll just call this word {tooltip:Vocabulary:guest}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:visitor}, or {tooltip:Vocabulary:customer}. You'll hear this word a lot when you're at a store or you're a customer somewhere in Japan. You are the {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u5ba2\u3055\u3093}, in that situation. Alternatively, you'll also hear {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u5ba2\u3055\u307e} which is a more polite version of this word (because it ends in {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u307e} and not {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093}).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Guest",
                "Alternatives": "Visitor, Customer",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304d\u3083\u304f\u3055\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u304d\u3083\u304f\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20424-subject-3115.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u304d\u3083\u304f\u3055\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40332-subject-3115.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the reading you learned with the kanji. Just add the hiragana on the end and you'll be good to go.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u5ba2\u3055\u3093\u304c\u5165\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308b\u3068\u3001\u3053\u306e\u30d9\u30eb\u304c\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When customers come in, this bell rings."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u3048\u304d\u3067\u3001\u304a\u5ba2\u3055\u3093\u3068\u4f1a\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I met up with my guest at Tokyo Station."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u5ba2\u3055\u3093\u3092\u7372\u5f97\u3059\u308b\u306b\u306f\u3069\u3046\u3059\u308c\u3070\u3044\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "What do you think I should do to get customers?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

