                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You're lifting something that's really {tooltip:Vocabulary:heavy}. Oof! You lift it above your head. You're so awesome. You scream: \"{tooltip:Reading:OH! MO}RE!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3082}) they put more. You yell it again: \"OH, MORE!\" and again: \"OH, MORE!\" Go ahead and act this out wherever you are, pretending like you're holding a couch or two or three over your head, saying \"OH MORE!\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u306b\u3082\u3064\u306f\u91cd\u305d\u3046\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "That luggage looks heavy."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u8eca\u3001\u91cd\u3059\u304e\u3066\u3046\u3067\u304c\u3082\u3052\u305d\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "This car is so heavy that my arm is about to fall off."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u8db3\u3092\u8e0f\u3093\u3067\u3057\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3054\u3081\u3093\u306a\u3055\u3044\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u91cd\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3069\u3046\u3063\u3066\u3053\u3068\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"I\u2019m sorry I stepped on your foot.\" \"No problem. It was a little heavy, but no harm done.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen the word {span:lang=ja:\u9ad8\u3044} from a couple levels ago. This word is related to that. It's like {span:lang=ja:\u5927\u304d\u3044} versus {span:lang=ja:\u5927\u304d\u3055}, where one describes the other. In this case, the {span:lang=ja:\u9ad8\u3055} is the {tooltip:Vocabulary:height} of something (while {span:lang=ja:\u9ad8\u3044} is tall). This word isn't \"price\" though. For that you'd ask {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u304f\u3089\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f} (how much is it?).",
