                {
                    "ja": "\u548c\u98df\u30a4\u30b3\u30fc\u30eb\u5bff\u53f8\u3063\u3066\u308f\u3051\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Japanese style food doesn\u2019t always mean sushi."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:Japanese style} {tooltip:Kanji:room} tends to be pretty small. This mainly refers to the kind of room that's covered in tatami mats, though. If you're looking for places to stay in Japan, a {span:lang=ja:\u548c\u5ba4} will be something like that. You'll pull the futon out of the closet and sleep on the floor. So comfy, these {tooltip:Vocabulary:Japanese style room}s!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Japanese Style Room",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
