                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji (except for {span:lang=ja:\u540d} and {span:lang=ja:\u5c4b}, which are kun'yomi here). If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. For {span:lang=ja:\u306a} just think to {span:lang=ja:\u540d\u524d} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u307e\u3048}) which uses the {span:lang=ja:\u306a} reading. The \"name\" ({span:lang=ja:\u540d\u524d}) of this city is what? It's {tooltip:Reading:Na}goya. Watch out for rendaku changing {span:lang=ja:\u3053} to {span:lang=ja:\u3054} too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u540d\u53e4\u5c4b\u306b\u306f\u304a\u3044\u3057\u3044\u3082\u306e\u304c\u305f\u304f\u3055\u3093\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
