                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You visit the {tooltip:Vocabulary:sea}. Strangely, it asks you who is visiting. You're so full of yourself (even in front of the sea/ocean) that you reply: \"{tooltip:Reading:um, me}?\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u307f}). Imagine yourself feeling this full of yourself.\n"
