{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:mutual} {tooltip:Kanji:hand} is someone else's hands (or just someone else, if you remembered that {span:lang=ja:\u624b} can also refer to a person as well). Whose hands are these? These are your {tooltip:Vocabulary:partner}'s hands. That's why everything is mutual.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Partner",
                "Alternative": "Companion",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3044\u3066"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3044\u3066",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20511-subject-3138.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3044\u3066",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40422-subject-3138.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are the kun'yomi readings. For {span:lang=ja:\u624b}, that's no problem for you. For {span:lang=ja:\u76f8}, that's more of an issue since you learned the on'yomi reading for it. Think of it this way: \n{splitParent}Your partner wouldn't be your partner without you. Your partner is: {tooltip:Reading:I} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044}) and you. Remember that as you gaze into your partner's eyes. \"I and you.\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u307e\u305a\u306f\u3001\u76f8\u624b\u306e\u8a71\u3092\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3068\u304d\u3044\u3066\u3042\u3052\u3088\u3046\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "First, you will listen closely to what your partner has to say."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3089\u306a\u3044\u306b\u3088\u308b\u3068\u3001\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u3051\u3063\u3053\u3093\u76f8\u624b\u306f\u3069\u3053\u304b\u306e\u56fd\u306e\u738b\u5b50\u3055\u307e\u3060\u305d\u3046\u3067\u3059\u3002\u672c\u5f53\u304b\u306a\uff1f",
                    "en": "According to my fortune, my future partner is a prince in some country. I wonder if it's true."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u99ac\u9e7f\u306a\u8a71\u3057\u76f8\u624b\u306f\u6b32\u3057\u304f\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "I don\u2019t want a stupid talking companion."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

