{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. Besides {tooltip:Vocabulary:thing}, it has the related meanings of {tooltip:Vocabulary:object} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:item}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Thing",
                "Alternatives": "Object, Item",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3082\u306e"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u306e",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20582-subject-3107.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u306e",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40221-subject-3107.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading, but you haven't learned it yet. Here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}What game has the most {tooltip:Vocabulary:thing}s in it? {tooltip:Reading:Mono}poly ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u306e}). You can choose from a bunch of random things to play as, you know? And no one actually knows what those things are. What's a thimble anyway? Just call it a thing.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30b5\u30eb\u3055\u3093\u304c\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u7269\u306f\u4f55\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "What is that thing Masaru has?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u30ef\u30f3\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3092\u7269\u3042\u3064\u304b\u3044\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\uff01",
                    "en": "Don't treat my dog like a thing!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u597d\u304d\u306a\u7269\u3092\u4e09\u3064\u6319\u3052\u308b\u306a\u3089\u3001\u30c1\u30ad\u30f3\u3068\u63da\u3052\u7269\u3068\u3054\u98ef\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My three favorite things are chicken, fried foods, and rice."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. Additionally on top of {tooltip:Vocabulary:thing} there are the meanings {tooltip:Vocabulary:matter} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:action} as well. Like the kanji, this word has to do with action things... things that you do, for example, rather than physical things.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Thing",
                "Alternatives": "Matter, Action",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3068"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3068",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20488-subject-3082.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3068",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40397-subject-3082.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}It's hard to start a mnemonic with the word \"thing\" or \"action,\" so let's continue off the kanji mnemonic where you've put a cross in the mouth of a wolverine.  Why did you do it? You knew that feisty wolverine was going to eat your {tooltip:Reading:coat} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3068}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b9\u30e2\u30e2\u3055\u3093\u304c\u3001\u30d4\u30f3\u30af\u8272\u306e\u3044\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3092\u304d\u308b\u4e8b\u304c\u591a\u3044\u306e\u306f\u306a\u305c\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Why do you think Ms. Sumomo wears so many pink clothes?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f8c\u306f\u3044\u304c\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u4e8b\u304c\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3088\u304f\u5206\u304b\u3089\u306a\u304f\u3066\u3053\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I often have trouble understanding what my junior colleague is saying."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3059\u307e\u306a\u3044\u304c\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u4eca\u306f\u3059\u308b\u4e8b\u304c\u305f\u304f\u3055\u3093\u3042\u3063\u3066\u3001\u5fd9\u3057\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m sorry but I\u2019ve been busy recently because I have a lot of things to do."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Kanji:now} {tooltip:Kanji:occurrence} you'll learn your kanji, no? This word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:this time}. Despite being \"this time\" it has the feeling of {tooltip:Vocabulary:next time}, though. It's like saying \"okay, this time we'll get it\" where \"this time\" really means \"next time,\" making it a little bit different from {span:lang=ja:\u4eca\u56de}.",
