                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You lose your tournament/soccer game/whatever (you decide something applicable to you). You're sad about this. Who's there to comfort you? Your {tooltip:Reading:Ma} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e}). She's a nice lady.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3059\u304d\u306a\u30c1\u30fc\u30e0\u304c\u8ca0\u3051\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3001\u304f\u3084\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My favorite team lost, so I\u2019m frustrated and heartbroken."
