                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}{tooltip:Reading:Two car}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304b}), are what you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to use} because you're so huge you don't fit into one. You've got a British car on your left and an American car on your right, and you're driving them both at the same time.\n"
