                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e8b\u5b9f\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u306a\u3063\u3068\u304f\u306f\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "That may be true, but I'm still not convinced."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u305b\u3044\u3058\u5bb6\u306e\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4e8b\u5b9f\u306b\u53cd\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "What that politician has been saying contradicts the facts."
