                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30af\u30fc\u30dd\u30f3\u306e\u4f7f\u7528\u306e\u4ed5\u65b9\u304c\u5206\u304b\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I don't know how to use this coupon."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u660e\u65e5\u3001\u4e5d\u6642\u304b\u3089\u4f1a\u304e\u5ba4\u3092\u4f7f\u7528\u3057\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u7a7a\u3044\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "I want to use the meeting room at nine tomorrow. Is it available?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3078\u30fc\uff01\u4f7f\u7528\u4eba\u3063\u3066\u88ab\u96c7\u7528\u8005\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3082\u8a00\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3002\u3066\u3063\u304d\u308a\u53ec\u4f7f\u3044\u3063\u3066\u610f\u5473\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3002\u300d\u300c\u305d\u3046\u3060\u3088\u3002\u4f7f\u7528\u8005\u3082\u3001\u5229\u7528\u8005\u3060\u3051\u3058\u3083\u306a\u304f\u3066\u96c7\u7528\u4e3b\u3063\u3066\u610f\u5473\u3082\u3042\u308b\u3057\u306d\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Oh! Shiyounin is used for an employee too? I always thought it just meant servant.\" \"Yup. And shiyousha not only means user, but employer too.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:weak} {tooltip:Kanji:insect}. This is what people call {tooltip:Vocabulary:weakling}s in Japan. This is a good word to know if you're a bully, or something.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Weakling",
                "Alternative": "Coward",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306a adjective, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3088\u308f\u3080\u3057"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u308f\u3080\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20504-subject-3477.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u308f\u3080\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40413-subject-3477.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this one is a weird one. It uses the kun'yomi readings for both, meaning you'll have to pull your knowledge of the word {span:lang=ja:\u5f31\u3044} from earlier and apply it here. {span:lang=ja:\u866b} should be okay, though, as this is the reading you learned with the kanji.\n{splitParent}Just remember, only weak bugs use kun'yomi, and that weak bug is you in this instance.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3093\u306a\u306b\u5f31\u866b\u3067\u306a\u304d\u866b\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3080\u3059\u5b50\u3082\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u4eba\u524d\u306e\u5927\u4eba\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My son, who was such a weakling and a crybaby, is already an adult."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u591a\u304f\u306e\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u4eba\u306f\u306a\u3063\u3068\u3046\u3054\u3068\u304d\u304c\u98df\u3079\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u5f31\u866b\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Many Americans are cowards who can't even eat a bit of natto."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f31\u866b\u6bdb\u866b\u306f\u3001\u631f\u3093\u3067\u6368\u3066\u308d\uff01",
                    "en": "Cowards should be treated like hairy caterpillars - picked up and thrown out!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Something that is double {tooltip:Kanji:weak} is probably pretty weak. You also know that this is an adjective because it ends with {span:lang=ja:\u3044}. You know that {span:lang=ja:\u5f31\u3044} is weak, so it probably isn't that. Instead, this one is {tooltip:Vocabulary:weak looking} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:frail}. If you know the grammar {span:lang=ja:\u3089\u3057\u3044} you can kind of use that as a hint. The {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3044} on the end reminds me of {span:lang=ja:\u3089\u3057\u3044} which is like \"seems to be.\" So, \"seems to be weak\" = \"weak looking.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Weak Looking",
                "Alternatives": "Frail, Weak Seeming, Seemingly Weak",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3088\u308f\u3088\u308f\u3057\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u308f\u3088\u308f\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40450-subject-3478.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u308f\u3088\u308f\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20541-subject-3478.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is double kun'yomi, as you can probably guess due to all the hiragana involved. So, you double up on {span:lang=ja:\u3088\u308f} and then add the {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3044} to read this vocabulary word.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u306a\u3093\u304b\u3001\u5f31\u3005\u3057\u3044\u3046\u305f\u3054\u3048\u3060\u3063\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u5fc3\u3071\u3044\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was starting to worry about you because you had such a weak singing voice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3080\u304b\u3057\u306f\u5f37\u304f\u898b\u3048\u305f\u7236\u304c\u5e74\u3068\u3068\u3082\u306b\u3060\u3093\u3060\u3093\u5f31\u3005\u3057\u304f\u898b\u3048\u3066\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My father, who used to look strong, gradually began looking weaker year after year."
                },
                {
