                "mnemonic": "You wave as the turkey {tooltip:Kanji:advance}s into the street at top speeds, collides with a car, and scrapes up its {tooltip:Reading:shin}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}) almost immediately. Ah!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} is an {tooltip:Radical:alcohol}ic beverage containing a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:alcohol}. It\u2019s 3 different kinds of rums, pineapple juice, and grenadine. It\u2019ll hit you like a tsunami though. This alcoholic drink has a kick to it.",
            "hints": "It\u2019s made with spiced rum, coconut rum, and dark rum. Imagine yourself on a sandy beach drinking this cocktail. Feel the sun on your face and the wind in your hair as you sip on this fruity and rummy alcoholic beverage known as a tsunami. You could even picture an actual tsunami in the water coming right for you. I wouldn\u2019t recommend it though\u2014actual tsunami are scary, not drinkable and delicious.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Alcohol"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3051, \u3055\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the alcohol flowing down this long chute from somewhere far away. You try to see where it's coming from, but all you can see is this long, long chute stretching along the entire beach, until it disappears into the distance. You should probably be concerned that you're nonstop drinking alcohol from a random chute, but it tastes so good!",
                "mnemonic": "As you lay on this beach, the {tooltip:Kanji:alcohol} keeps coming down a {tooltip:Reading:chu}te ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085}), straight into your mouth. You can feel the sand in your toes and the alcohol sliding down your throat from this special tsunami chute."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you give a {tooltip:Radical:woman} a {tooltip:Radical:machine} she'll {tooltip:Kanji:begin} learning how to use it right away. She'll also get it to {tooltip:Kanji:start} before anyone else could. Women are really good at starting up new machines!",
            "hints": "Picture a woman seeing a new machine and beginning work on it right away to see how she can start it up.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Begin",
                "Alternative": "Start"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3058",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a machine starting up as the woman begins to shear the sheep. Picture the sheep staring at you, staring at it.",
                "mnemonic": "Actually, before she can {tooltip:Kanji:begin}, she has to shear the {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) over there. The machine is going to turn wool into yarn, but you can't just start that process by shoving the sheep in there. You have to keep the little sheep safe!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:sheep} is having trouble trying to eat a fish with {tooltip:Radical:spikes} on its {tooltip:Radical:fins}, then the sheep probably has no {tooltip:Kanji:business} trying to eat it in the first place. Don\u2019t sheep usually eat like, grass and stuff? What is this sheep doing trying to eat a fish with spikes on its fins? What silly business this is.",
            "hints": "Imagine this crazy sheep. Why is it trying to eat this fish? This sheep is blood crazed. Blood crazed for fish meat, especially the meat from fish with spikes on their fins. This crazed sheep means business.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Business"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine you\u2019re at an Asian style restaurant and you just ordered a big plate of gyoza dumplings. Next thing you know, this crazy sheep busts through the front door and starts devouring all your gyoza! Where did this sheep come from and why does he love gyoza so much!?",
                "mnemonic": "What\u2019s this? The sheep is also trying to eat some {tooltip:Reading:gyo}za ({span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3087\u3046}) dumplings! Where will this sheep\u2019s madness end? First spikey finned fish and now gyoza? This is some crazy {tooltip:Kanji:business}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you get stabbed in the {tooltip:Radical:eye} {tooltip:Radical:twenty} times with {tooltip:Radical:bamboo}, you\u2019re going to have a hard time beginning to {tooltip:Kanji:calculate} where anything is. Taking a bamboo shoot to the eye is no pleasant experience, especially if done twenty times. You\u2019d be blinded for sure. And a newly blinded person is going to have one heck of a time calculating where everything is without the power of sight.",
            "hints": "Imagine getting jabbed with a bamboo shoot. Now imagine getting jabbed in the eye with a bamboo shoot. It\u2019s going to hurt. Try and calculate exactly how painful this would be and imagine it happening to you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Calculate",
                "Alternative": "Calculation"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this evil Asian Santa-san, clad in blood red garments and brandishing pointed bamboo shoots in each hand. He\u2019s a cold and calculating madman! You\u2019d better start studying! Santa-san is watching!",
                "mnemonic": "Do you know how {tooltip:Reading:San}ta-san ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093}) punishes naughty boys and girls in Asia? He doesn\u2019t give them coal, Santa-san tortures them with twenty bamboo jabs to the eye. Yikes. Do you know how Santa-san {tooltip:Kanji:calculate}s who is naughty and who is nice? By their school grades, of course."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "While riding your {tooltip:Radical:scooter}, you bang your {tooltip:Radical:forehead} on the {tooltip:Radical:car} in front. Your scooter's wrecked, so you have to {tooltip:Kanji:carry} it home. You'll need a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:luck} to get that scooter home safely.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to carry your scooter down a busy road, with all the cars whizzing past. Your forehead is still hurting from that nasty bang. Good luck!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Carry",
                "Alternative": "Luck"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's hard enough to carry a scooter in heavy traffic, but now you have to try to keep yourself and it dry with an umbrella too. ",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:carry} the scooter, your {tooltip:Kanji:luck} turns, and it starts to rain, so you pull out your {tooltip:Reading:um}brella ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3093}). Now you're holding your scooter, your forehead, and an umbrella."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hit ancient {tooltip:Radical:China} and formed the {tooltip:Kanji:Chinese} country we know now as... {tooltip:Kanji:China}!",
            "hints": "Picture the world way far away, from space. You see a giant tsunami carve out a massive chunk of land to the west of Japan on the main continent. Slowly the tsunami waters recede, leaving the outline of China.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chinese",
                "Alternative": "China"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
