                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as the Khan takes China for himself. A tiny little flag with a horse on it is raised in the middle, for all of the Chinese people to see. Hmm, this could be a problem.",
                "mnemonic": "You peer closer at {tooltip:Kanji:China} and realize the borders are inching inward, even though the tsunami is already gone. You look even closer and see the Mongols, being led by Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) moving in to conquer all of the Chinese people living in China!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:bird} opens its {tooltip:Radical:mouth}, you\u2019re most likely to hear a {tooltip:Kanji:chirp}. This is how birds communicate. They open their mouths and let out a series of chirps. Chirp chirp chirp!",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself out in the wilderness on a sunny spring day. The weather is perfect and the scenery is beautiful. The only sound you can hear is the chirp of birds throughout the woods around you. It\u2019s very peaceful.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chirp"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself surrounded by birds of all kinds, handing out nachos. Just listen to their happy chirping. They're sitting on your arms, shoulders, and even your head, trying to get closer to the nachos. That chirping is so loud!",
                "mnemonic": "The best way to experience the {tooltip:Kanji:chirp} chirping of birds is to offer them {tooltip:Reading:na}chos({span:lang=ja:\u306a}). Birds love nachos so much, it's a guaranteed way to make the chirp with delight."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You chase a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} up a {tooltip:Radical:tree} to {tooltip:Kanji:collect} it. At least, you will once you've {tooltip:Kanji:gather}ed enough turkeys into this one tree.",
            "hints": "Collect another turkey, send it flying and gobbling up into the tree next to the other one.",
