{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:thread} of {tooltip:Radical:winter} splits in {tooltip:Radical:two} when the year comes to an {tooltip:Kanji:end}. One half symbolizes the year you were just in, and the other symbolizes the new year beginning, cutting winter in half and {tooltip:Kanji:finish}ing off the year.",
            "hints": "Picture the threads that symbolize winter splitting in two to mark the end of the year. Winter isn't finished though, it's only half done.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "End",
                "Alternative": "Finish"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
