                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's the end of the year, so it's time for new shoe laces!",
                "mnemonic": "Right as winter {tooltip:Kanji:end}s you grab the two threads and lace them into your {tooltip:Reading:shoe}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}). Oh, you thought these were metaphorical? No they're real threads, although, they're technically shoe laces now."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Here you {tooltip:Radical:stand}, a {tooltip:Radical:hair}\u2019s breadth away from the edge of a {tooltip:Radical:cliff}, when out of nowhere a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} slaps you right in the {tooltip:Kanji:face}. Geoducks are gross, and you back away from the edge of the cliff you were standing but a hair\u2019s breadth away from just before. Your face is all gooey from the geoduck\u2019s slimy residue.",
            "hints": "Imagine being slapped in the face with a geoduck. It\u2019s probably one of the worst things that could ever happen to someone. Those things are disgusting. Now you have geoduck goo all over your face. It\u2019s sticky and slimy and gross.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Face"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Cows are big animals. So you probably got hit in the face with that geoduck pretty hard. Feel the geoduck shaped welt starting to form on the side of your face. It\u2019s very painful and stings a lot.",
                "mnemonic": "But where did that geoduck come from anyway? As you turn around from the cliff edge, wiping the goop from your {tooltip:Kanji:face} and out of your eyes, you see an angry {tooltip:Reading:cow} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304a}). This cow is the one who hit you in the face with this geoduck. I know not the reason, but this cow is most definitely not happy with you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A violent {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} causes {tooltip:Radical:flowers} to be ripped from the branches of trees and they swirl around and {tooltip:Radical:kiss} your face gently as they {tooltip:Kanji:fall}. With the tsunami came a great windy storm that blew many flowers all about. It\u2019s a pretty sight amongst all the destruction.",
            "hints": "Imagine being out in this tsunami induced storm. You can feel the rain and wind on your skin \u2013 you\u2019re wet, cold, and scared. But you see some flowers being blown to the ground and you are mesmerized by the dance they do on the wind before they finally fall to the ground.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fall"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3089\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine running around catching the flowers as they fall. Imagine placing each little petal onto the rack to keep it safe and dry.",
                "mnemonic": "You want to save these flowers you see {tooltip:Kanji:fall}ing in around you, so you take out a drying {tooltip:Reading:rack} ({span:lang=ja:\u3089\u304f}) and place them carefully on it. Now whenever you feel scared, you can look at the flowers on this rack and you won't be scared anymore."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You blast your {tooltip:Radical:music} loud so it causes a {tooltip:Radical:landslide}, revealing the perfect soil for {tooltip:Kanji:farming}! Musically moved dirt is perfect for {tooltip:Kanji:agriculture}.",
            "hints": "Imagine slowly turning up your big boombox until your ears hurt and the ground beneath your feet is vibrating with the beat. Soon you and the boombox are sliding with all of the earth down the hill and onto your farmland. Hooray, now the farming can begin!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Farming",
                "Alternative": "Agriculture"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Nostradamus flailing his arms and trying to explain his vision to the farmers at the time. He knows that if they listen their farming techniques will improve, but they're looking at him like he's nuts.",
                "mnemonic": "The first person to come up with this {tooltip:Kanji:farming} method was {tooltip:Reading:No}stradamus ({span:lang=ja:\u306e\u3046}), the famous seer and prophecy man. He predicted humans of the future would use special \"yell cubes\" to \"move that good earth.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You jump on your {tooltip:Radical:scooter} with a big {tooltip:Radical:bundle} to go as {tooltip:Kanji:fast} as you can! You have a bundle of pizzas in here, and they need to be delivered as fast as you can get them there!",
            "hints": "Imagine how fast you can go on your scooter holding this bundle. It's way faster than trying to go on foot, that's for sure!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fast"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine riding the scooter as fast as you can in just your socks. You can feel the wind pulling them off your feet!",
                "mnemonic": "You were going so {tooltip:Kanji:fast}, you only put on {tooltip:Reading:sock}s ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u304f}). So now you're barreling down the street at top speeds in just your sad, white socks."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} eats lots of {tooltip:Radical:beans}, its {tooltip:Kanji:head} will grow larger. To a geoduck, beans are a brain food, so by eating beans, a geoduck\u2019s head will grow incredibly large. Geoducks already look strange enough as it is, let alone with engorged heads.",
            "hints": "Imagine, if you will, a geoduck. Now imagine that same geoduck with a massive head. It looks ridiculous, and more disgusting than ever. It\u2019s actually really creeping you out, because the head keeps getting larger as the geoduck eats more beans. Ew.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Head"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305a, \u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305f\u307e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Remember how gross geoducks are? Of course you do. Now imagine one exploding right in front of you. You\u2019ve got geoduck mess all over yourself. It\u2019s gross, slimy, sticky, and covering you from head to toe. It\u2019s wretched.",
                "mnemonic": "As the geoduck eats more and more beans, its {tooltip:Kanji:head} gets bigger and bigger until finally the geoduck\u2019s head explodes like an {tooltip:Reading:atomi}c ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u305f\u307e}) bomb. BOOM! Geoduck parts go flying everywhere and pieces of the geoduck\u2019s massive head float to the ground as atomic fallout."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you press your {tooltip:Radical:ear} up to a {tooltip:Radical:gate}, you\u2019re likely to {tooltip:Kanji:hear} what\u2019s going on on the other side. The other people on the other side won\u2019t know you are listening to their conversation because you are so sneaky and clever. They\u2019ve no idea you\u2019re on the other side of the gate hearing every word they say.",
            "hints": "I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve pressed your ear up against a wall, door, or gate at sometime to hear what\u2019s going on on the other side of it. Remember back to a time you did this and how sneaky you felt listening in on people without them knowing. You sneaky frood, you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hear"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3076\u3093, \u3082\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I\u2019m sure many of you were forced to play the recorder in school at some point and were made to play the song known as hot cross buns. Picture yourself playing this song and remember the melody when you see this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "From the other side of the gate, you {tooltip:Kanji:hear} one of the people on the other side start to play a song on a recorder. You recognize the song as \u201cHot Cross {tooltip:Reading:Bun}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3076\u3093}).\u201d You haven\u2019t heard this song in a long time. \u201cHot cross buns\u2026 hot cross buns~\u201d"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:building} has a {tooltip:Radical:roof} and will teach you about the {tooltip:Radical:origin} of many things. It's an {tooltip:Kanji:institution}!",
            "hints": "Institutions are places of learning, but they have to be a physical place with a roof and all that. If you're learning out in a field somewhere, that's probably not a proper institution.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Institution"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Just remember, it's an IN-stitution, and you'll know this reading easy-peasy.",
                "mnemonic": "What does {tooltip:Kanji:institution} start with? In ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3093})!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:say} something about the {tooltip:Radical:circumference} of this area. You've looked around this whole area, making a big circle around it, because you are trying to {tooltip:Kanji:investigate} something that happened here. You also say this thing in a really quiet {tooltip:Kanji:tone} of voice, because you don't want the person or thing you're investigating to know you're on to them.",
            "hints": "Because the radical {tooltip:Radical:circumference} is in play, you can think of the crime scene you're investigating as a statue of a giant globe, and you're doing a circumference around it. Then, in the reading, we'll think about what you'll {tooltip:Radical:say}.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Investigate",
                "Alternative": "Tone"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "From what you know about evil Mrs. Chou, you probably could have guessed it was her. The \"Circumference Investigation\" is now over, though you do still have to catch the perp, Mrs. Chou.",
                "mnemonic": "\"I came here to {tooltip:Kanji:investigate} this place, and I did indeed find out who the criminal is... it's none other than Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046})!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You look at some {tooltip:Radical:gold} and notice a {tooltip:Radical:fault} in it. You scrape at the fault and see that it's just sprayed with gold paint. It's not gold, it's (comparatively) worthless {tooltip:Kanji:iron}!",
            "hints": "You think you've found a ton of gold bars! Imagine being so happy about this. Then, imagine your heart dropping in your chest when you notice the fault. Then, it dropping down even farther when you figure out it's merely iron.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Iron"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch a trailer on YouTube for Tetsuo the Iron Man. Go ahead, do it now \u2013 I\u2019ll wait. Did you watch it? Remember that nonsense every time you see this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "Do you know that movie, {tooltip:Reading:Tetsu}o ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3064}) the {tooltip:Kanji:Iron} Man? We talked about it on Tofugu a while back. It\u2019s one of the wackiest Japanese movies of all time. If you don\u2019t know about Tetsuo the Iron Man, you should definitely look it up (if you aren't averse to horror/violent films). Tetsuo is one of the most insane movies in the history of ever."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What you {tooltip:Radical:say} between {tooltip:Radical:five} {tooltip:Radical:mouth}s is a {tooltip:Kanji:language}. As long as there are five different people saying these same words with their five mouths, it's considered its own language.",
            "hints": "Picture these five mouths saying the same language to each other. They can understand each other! The mouths are smiling and laughing too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Language"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Godzilla speaks a language some people understand! You wish you knew this earlier, then you might have been able to stop some of his destruction. Try to say, \"Hey Godzilla, please stop destroying my city,\" in his language. It's a lot of growling and yelling. He doesn't seem to understand you. You better practice your pronunciation.",
                "mnemonic": "Another mouth joins in speaking the {tooltip:Kanji:language}, but it's green and scaled and... it's {tooltip:Reading:Go}dzilla's ({span:lang=ja:\u3054}) mouth! Godzilla speaks this language too."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:world} of {tooltip:Radical:flowers} and {tooltip:Radical:tree}s, the most important thing is the {tooltip:Kanji:leaf}. {tooltip:Kanji:Leaves} are how flowers and trees get their nutrients from the sun! ",
            "hints": "Leaves, no matter how little, are the most important thing in the world for them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Leaf",
                "Alternative": "Leaves"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f, \u3070",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "{span:lang=ja:\u306f} is the sound of a leaf coming into existence. Whenever you see a plant from now on, hear the little ha sound it makes when each leaf pops out of its body.",
                "mnemonic": "Picture a little flower working really hard to grow its first leaf. The {tooltip:Kanji:leaf} pops out and it shouts, \"{tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f})!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You find some {tooltip:Radical:white} {tooltip:Radical:feathers} and you want to {tooltip:Kanji:learn} more about where they came from and what they're made of.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself in a library poring through huge tomes on birds, feathers, and the history of white birds. You want to learn everything you can!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Learn"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh geez, oh no. You better learn how to control these shoes before you\u2014CRASH!!! Welp, you just shot through a plane. You need to learn more before you act next time.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:learn} that you should tie these white feathers to your {tooltip:Reading:shoe}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}). You do it before you learn what it will do, and then suddenly you're jump-flying out of the building."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tombstone} may be heavy for a human, but to a {tooltip:Radical:car}, they\u2019re relatively {tooltip:Kanji:lightweight}. Cars are very strong, you see, so something heavy like a tombstone is no match for them. All cars find tombstones to be lightweight and easy to transport.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself trying to move a huge slab tombstone. It\u2019s difficult, no? I bet you wish you had a car or some other vehicle to make the process much less painful. Your arms are getting sore from carrying the tombstone and you\u2019re getting sweaty and hot from all the work. What you would do for a car with air conditioning.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lightweight",
                "Alternatives": "Light, Light Weight"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u308b, \u304b\u308d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Remember all that hard work you were doing before and how you got all sweaty and gross? Now imagine yourself inside of a nice car with air conditioning, and the tombstone in the trunk. It feels great doesn\u2019t it? The air conditioning is perfect, and driving a car is much easier than carrying a tombstone around.",
                "mnemonic": "What do you wish you had to transport this tombstone? Oh, that\u2019s right \u2013 a {tooltip:Reading:car} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u308b}). If you had a car, this tombstone moving business would be no problem. To cars, tombstones are naught but {tooltip:Kanji:lightweight} pebbles!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If someone falls overboard while you're {tooltip:Radical:white} {tooltip:Radical:water }rafting, you can use a long piece of {tooltip:Radical:thread} as a life {tooltip:Kanji:line}. Sure it might be thin, but a line of thread is better than nothing. Throw them a line and drag them back aboard! Those white water rapids are vicious.",
            "hints": "Imagine you're the person who fell overboard. The white water is rushing violently and it is deathly cold. Feel the water and freezing temperature on your skin. But look! Someone has thrown you a line of thread! You're saved!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Line"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Coming out of the rushing water, this centaur is like an angel sent from heaven. He's just saved your life. Imagine the happiness and gratitude you feel towards this centaur as you are pulled to safety by that line of thread.",
                "mnemonic": "The person who threw you that {tooltip:Kanji:line} of thread is actually a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}). How kind of him. After you are safe you hop on the centaur's back and ride around to get the wind to dry you off."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Let the {tooltip:Radical:sun} shine into your {tooltip:Radical:ear} while sitting on a {tooltip:Radical:stool} and make sure {tooltip:Kanji:most} of it gets in your head. You want to fill your brain with the most sun anyone has ever.",
            "hints": "Most of the sun is getting into your ear, but not all of it. Darn, maybe you should try angling yourself a different way. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Most"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3063\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Install the part into your cyborg. As long as most of the sun gets into its human ear, most of its cyborg bits will have power.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Most} of this is for your {tooltip:Reading:cy}borg ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044}). You're testing out a new way to power it, but if you can't get most of the sun into your ear, it won't be enough to power most of the cyborg's robo-parts."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:gate} with a {tooltip:Radical:lantern} is {tooltip:Kanji:open} for you. That's convenient, since it's pretty dark out and you might not have seen the open gate without the lantern's help.",
            "hints": "Imagine being a traveler, walking around the outside of a huge walled city. You really need to get inside but all of the gates are closed. Finally, you see a single, bright lantern marking the open gate! What a relief.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Open"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042, \u3072\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine kayaking in the dark toward an open gate. Finally, you've made it!",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:open} gate is in the water though, so you'll need a {tooltip:Reading:kay}ak ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044}) to get in. Luckily, you've been carrying your kayak with you just in case."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:see} a {tooltip:Radical:tree} that you want to {tooltip:Radical:stand} under to take a break while hiking, a good {tooltip:Kanji:parent} will stand under the tree with you. This is a kind and caring parent who can see that you are tired and want to relax by standing in the shade of this tree.",
            "hints": "Imagine that you\u2019re on a long mountain hike and so far you\u2019ve been hiking all in the sun with no shade. Feel the sun beating down on your back, the sweat getting in your eyes. Finally you see a tree to seek refuge under. It\u2019s like an oasis in a desert. You\u2019re saved!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Parent"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3084, \u3057\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Busting your shins on things really hurts. I'm sure you've hit your shins on coffee tables and the like all your life. Remember that pain and think how much worse it would be banging your bare shins on pointy tree roots after you've been hiking all day in the hot sun. Not enjoyable.",
                "mnemonic": "Once you get closer to the tree, you and your {tooltip:Kanji:parent} see that it has some pretty crazy roots coming out of it. While making your way into the shade, you manage to bang your {tooltip:Reading:shin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}) on one of these roots. Your shins already hurt from walking so much, and this is just icing on the cake."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have to {tooltip:Radical:say} what you\u2019re {tooltip:Radical:sell}ing because people don\u2019t like to {tooltip:Kanji:read}. If they walk right by and don\u2019t read, you better say what you have for sale so they\u2019ll know! Read it out loud to them.",
            "hints": "Imagine reading what you have for sale out loud to people walking by because they\u2019re too lazy to read it for themselves.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Read"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046, \u3069\u304f, \u3068\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine reading through your list of yo-yo tricks. Do you know how to pronounce those weird yo-yo names?",
                "mnemonic": "What are you forced to {tooltip:Kanji:read} aloud to sell? {tooltip:Reading:Yo-}yo ({span:lang=ja:\u3088}) instructions! You\u2019d think they\u2019d be self explanatory, but there are actually a lot of rules and tricks that you have to read to get good at yo-yoing. Read all of these out loud so you can sell them."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On the {tooltip:Radical:ground} is a {tooltip:Radical:water} {tooltip:Radical:drop} you spilled, so I {tooltip:Kanji:request} you wipe it up. I would do it myself, but you're the one who spilled it, so I'm requesting you do it and take responsibility for your mistake.",
            "hints": "It's a simple request, really. Just wipe up that water drop off the ground.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Request"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
