{
            "mnemonic": "If your {tooltip:Radical:car} runs into a {tooltip:Radical:cloud} you'll {tooltip:Kanji:revolve} around it instead of going straight through. Clouds are really hard to see through, so even though you're trying not to, you revolve in a tight circle up and around the cloud anyway.",
            "hints": "Imagine driving your car around and around the cloud, instead of going through it. At least it's soft and cool.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Revolve"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Unfortunately, not long after you get through that cloud another one comes down and gets in your way. Now you're counting each revolution, one... two... three... all the way up to ten.",
                "mnemonic": "You have to {tooltip:Kanji:revolve} around the cloud {tooltip:Reading:ten} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3093}) times before it disappears and you're able to go through."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you\u2019ve been walking all day, nobody is going to want to {tooltip:Radical:kiss} your {tooltip:Radical:foot} if you\u2019ve been walking barefoot down a dirt {tooltip:Kanji:road}. Your feet are filthy, sweaty, and stinky. Nobody is going to want to kiss those feet.",
            "hints": "Imagine kissing someone\u2019s foot. Now imagine kissing someone\u2019s foot after they\u2019ve been walking down a dirt road for hours. It\u2019s disgusting. Smell the stench of dirt and sweat wafting up into your nostrils as the foot approaches your lips. It\u2019s wretched.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Road"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058, \u307f\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Walking down a dirt road barefoot like this is a sure way to dirty up your feet. Feel the dirt, rocks, and twigs under your feet. The road is hard and dry and is not making your journey very comfortable at all.",
                "mnemonic": "What was this person walking down again? Oh, that\u2019s right \u2013 a {tooltip:Reading:ro}ad ({span:lang=ja:\u308d}). They were walking down a dirt {tooltip:Kanji:road}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:sick} stick of {tooltip:Radical:dynamite} is going to be {tooltip:Kanji:sick} forever. Unfortunately there are no medicines that are effective on sticks of dynamite, so once they contract a sickness, they\u2019re sick for good.",
            "hints": "Imagine if you were a sick stick of dynamite. Every time you sneezed you ran the risk of blowing up. It would be a terrifying way to live. Just imagine it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sick",
                "Alternatives": "Sickness, Ill, Illness"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084, \u3084\u307e\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this as your life. You could explode at any moment, you\u2019re sick, and you have B.O. Nobody wants to be around you because you might explode and kill them, and you stink. What a terrible way to live!",
                "mnemonic": "Being nervous all the time about spontaneously exploding would probably make you sweat profusely. And you know what sweating causes? {tooltip:Reading:B.O.} ({span:lang=ja:\u3073\u3087\u3046}). You\u2019d be one smelly stick of dynamite. B.O. is a very unpleasant smell, and being {tooltip:Kanji:sick} is no excuse."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:tree} marked with a {tooltip:Radical:yellow} X on the {tooltip:Kanji:side} of the house is going to get cut down. You\u2019ve marked it with a yellow X so the hired help knows which tree to cut down. There are a lot of trees on the side of the house, but the tree marked with a yellow X is the only one in danger of causing damage to your roof in the event of a storm.",
            "hints": "Picture the scene of a woman with a chainsaw cutting down this tree marked with a yellow X. Hear the sound of the chainsaw buzzing and the grinding of wood as it meets the side of the trunk. It\u2019s very loud. Woodchips go flying everywhere.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Side",
                "Alternative": "Horizontal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3053",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now picture the same scene as before only imagining Yoko Ono wielding that chainsaw. Maybe she\u2019s dancing. Maybe there\u2019s some Beatles music playing in the background. Either way it\u2019s a strange sight \u2013 remember it.",
                "mnemonic": "Wait, that woman with the chainsaw is {tooltip:Reading:Yoko} ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3053}) Ono! Yes, the same Yoko Ono who\u2019s married to John Lennon of the Beatles. What\u2019s she doing chopping down trees on the {tooltip:Kanji:side} of your house? Who can say. Silly Yoko."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:lack} a {tooltip:Radical:lip ring} (or two in this case) it's going to make it way easier for you to sing a {tooltip:Kanji:song}.",
            "hints": "Imagine a song with lip rings. Then imagine one without. Sing them, pretending you have lip rings. It doesn't work as well.",
