                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself getting hit by this car. All the air flies out of you as you sing your {tooltip:Kanji:song}. You think \"I shouldn't have tried to sing a song with all these lip rings...\"",
                "mnemonic": "You're singing a {tooltip:Kanji:song} with all these lip rings in your mouth and you sound terrible. You're on the side of the road singing. People are freaking out. Finally, someone drives into you with their {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Run} into {tooltip:Radical:oneself} in a dream and you'll definitely {tooltip:Kanji:wake up}.",
            "hints": "If you run into yourself, it really messes you up, you know? You won't be able to handle what you're seeing so you have to wake up.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wake Up"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your obi is like a special object you only have in dreams. If you have your obi, it's okay, it's a dream and you can wake up now! Make sure you memorize exactly how it feels so dream-you can't trick you or something.",
                "mnemonic": "If one runs into oneself and you don't {tooltip:Kanji:wake up}, just look down at your waist. If you're wearing an {tooltip:Reading:o}bi ({span:lang=ja:\u304a}) you know it's a dream and you'll eventually wake up. If you aren't wearing an obi then it isn't a dream and you don't have anything to wake up from."
            }
        }

