                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28064-subject-3160.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this one is strange. The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u901f} ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u304f}) is what you'd expect (on'yomi), but {span:lang=ja:\u65e9} gets a reading you haven't seen before, meaning you should treat this as an exception. Just think about how you're learning this word {tooltip:Vocabulary:at once} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:without delay} so there's no time for any {tooltip:Reading:sa}ss ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3063}), just kanji learning.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e9\u901f\u4f7f\u308f\u305b\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3060\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I used it immediately."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e9\u901f\u306e\u3054\u3078\u3093\u3057\u3093\u3001\u3042\u308a\u304c\u3068\u3046\u3054\u3056\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Thank you for your immediate response."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u305d\u306e\u8304\u5b50\u3092\u65e9\u901f\u5f7c\u306b\u9001\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I will send the eggplants to him at once."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:distribute} your {tooltip:Kanji:heart} around you, it's like your heart is everywhere at once, but not in your body. You feel frantic, you don't know what to do because your heart is out there. This represents the feeling you have when you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:a worry} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:concern}. {span:lang=ja:\u5fc3\u914d\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u306d\uff01}",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "A Worry",
                "Alternatives": "Concern, Anxiety, Worry",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb, \u306a adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093\u3071\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3093\u3071\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3387-subject-3564.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3093\u3071\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28089-subject-3564.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Take note that the {span:lang=ja:\u3071\u3044} in {span:lang=ja:\u914d} got rendaku'd from {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3044}, as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u304c\u5143\u6c17\u304c\u306a\u3044\u306e\u306f\u3081\u305a\u3089\u3057\u3044\u306e\u3067\u5fc3\u914d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m worried because it\u2019s unusual for him to be so down."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u8239\u306e\u9032\u884c\u65b9\u5411\u304c\u897f\u306a\u306e\u304b\u6771\u306a\u306e\u304b\u5fc3\u914d\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I got worried about whether the ship was heading east or west."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5fc3\u914d\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002\u3059\u3079\u3066\u4e0a\u624b\u304f\u3044\u304f\u3088\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u8a00\u3046\u3053\u3068\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u3066\u3002",
                    "en": "Don\u2019t worry, everything is going to be fine. You can believe what I say."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:self} {tooltip:Kanji:revolving} {tooltip:Kanji:car}. You'd think this would be a regular car, but {tooltip:Vocabulary:bicycles} were probably introduced before cars were, meaning the self revolving car is the bicycle, not the car. Just imagine yourself on a bike, and you don't even have to move the pedals. They revolve themselves, but now you're going too fast and it's scary.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bicycle",
                "Alternatives": "Bike, Pushbike",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3066\u3093\u3057\u3083"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3058\u3066\u3093\u3057\u3083",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3375-subject-3173.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3058\u3066\u3093\u3057\u3083",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28071-subject-3173.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u81ea\u8ee2\u8eca\u3067\u4f1a\u793e\u306b\u884c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I go to work by bike."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u8ee2\u8eca\u3092\u8cb7\u3063\u3066\u3042\u3052\u308b\u3088\u3002\u304a\u8fd4\u3057\u306f\u8981\u3089\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3089\u306d\uff01",
                    "en": "I'll buy you a new bicycle, no strings attached."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3054\u3081\u3093\u3002\u3066\u3063\u304d\u308a\u541b\u304c\u50d5\u306e\u81ea\u8ee2\u8eca\u3092\u58ca\u3057\u305f\u306e\u304b\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3088\u3002\u300d \u300c\u4f55\u305d\u308c\uff01\u3072\u3069\u3044\u3002\u79c1\u304c\u305d\u3093\u306a\u3053\u3068\u3059\u308b\u306f\u305a\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"I\u2019m sorry. I thought for sure you were the one who broke my bike.\" \"What? That\u2019s awful. You know me better than that.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji for {span:lang=ja:\u82e6} means {tooltip:Kanji:suffer}. This word, however, is a bit different, but you'll see how it's related. It means {tooltip:Vocabulary:bitter tasting}. Think of putting the most bitter thing in the world in your mouth. You feel sick, your mouth gets all weird, and you try to spit it out but the bitterness remains. Obviously eating {tooltip:Vocabulary:bitter tasting} things will cause you to suffer.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bitter Tasting",
                "Alternative": "Bitter",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306b\u304c\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u304c\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20495-subject-3110.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u304c\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40407-subject-3110.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This reading of the kanji is unique to this meaning of the word, so here's a mnemonic to help you out!\n{splitParent}The taste is so {tooltip:Vocabulary:bitter} that you fall to your knees really, really hard. Luckily, you were wearing your {tooltip:Reading:knee gua}rds ({span:lang=ja:\u306b\u304c}). Feel the relief that you were wearing them. Ack, no relief now. It's still bitter in your mouth.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30d9\u30fc\u30b3\u30f3\u3001\u306a\u3093\u304b\u82e6\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "This bacon is a little bitter."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u304f\u3059\u308a\u306f\u3059\u3063\u3054\u304f\u82e6\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3001\u6c17\u3092\u3064\u3051\u3066\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "This medicine is very bitter, so brace yourself!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ab\u30e9\u30e1\u30eb\u306f\u3001\u7126\u304c\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u306b\u6c17\u3092\u4ed8\u3051\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u3067\u306a\u3044\u3068\u3001\u82e6\u3044\u5473\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Be careful not to let the caramel burn or it will taste bitter."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is only one place in Japan that has a {tooltip:Kanji:thousand} {tooltip:Kanji:leaves} and that's {tooltip:Vocabulary:Chiba}. Picture all of those leaves swirling around you on your vacation to Chiba. Beautiful.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chiba",
                "Word Type": "proper noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3070"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3061\u3070",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3537-subject-7534.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3061\u3070",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28135-subject-7534.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a place name and it uses the kun'yomi. You haven't learned kun'yomi for {span:lang=ja:\u5343} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you remember it:\n{splitParent}While you're admiring all of the leaves in {tooltip:Vocabulary:Chiba}, you realize you're craving something. What goes well with watching leaves? Why, {tooltip:Reading:chee}se ({span:lang=ja:\u3061}) of course. Delicious Chiba cheese.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u306f\u5343\u8449\u770c\u4eba\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "He\u2019s from Chiba."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u6bcd\u306f\u3001\u5343\u8449\u770c\u3055\u3093\u306e\u843d\u82b1\u751f\u304c\u5927\u3059\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My mom loves peanuts made in Chiba."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3053\u304b\u3089\u5343\u8449\u307e\u3067\u3060\u3068\u3001\u7247\u90531\u6642\u959330\u5206\u304b\u30892\u6642\u9593\u306f\u3050\u3089\u3044\u304b\u304b\u308a\u307e\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "It usually takes an hour and a half to two hours for a one way trip from here to Chiba."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:friend} who is like one of your {tooltip:Kanji:parent}s is someone who will look out for you. They are like family, in fact! That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:best friend} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:close friend}. Just imagine someone who watches over you like a parent would. This is the way to describe them.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Close Friend",
                "Alternatives": "Best Friend, Good Friend",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093\u3086\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3093\u3086\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3386-subject-3226.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
