{
            "mnemonic": "Just like the meaning of the kanji ({tooltip:Kanji:fast}) this adjective also means {tooltip:Vocabulary:fast}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fast",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3084\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3084\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3648-subject-7472.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3084\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28172-subject-7472.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Remember how {span:lang=ja:\u65e9\u3044} means \"early\"? If you are early to something, it probably means you moved {tooltip:Vocabulary:fast} to get there. These two words share a reading (and have similar meanings, in a way, as well!).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65b0\u304b\u3093\u7dda\u306f\u3075\u3064\u3046\u306e\u96fb\u8eca\u3088\u308a\u901f\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The shinkansen is faster than a normal train."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u304b\u3089\u6771\u4eac\u307e\u3067\u3001\u3060\u308c\u304c\u4e00\u756a\u901f\u304f\u6cf3\u3052\u308b\u304b\u304d\u3087\u3046\u305d\u3046\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We had a competition to see who could swim from Portland to Tokyo the fastest."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u5bb6\u65cf\u306f\u3001\u3054\u98ef\u3092\u98df\u3079\u308b\u306e\u304c\u3068\u3066\u3082\u901f\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "In my family, we eat dinner really fast."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen {span:lang=ja:\u4e00\u756a} (number one), so what in the world is this eye on the end? This eye ({span:lang=ja:\u76ee}) signifies the order. So, add this to \"number one\" and you have the {tooltip:Vocabulary:first thing} / {tooltip:Vocabulary:the first}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "First Thing",
                "Alternative": "The First",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3061\u3070\u3093\u3081"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3061\u3070\u3093\u3081",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3764-subject-3481.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3061\u3070\u3093\u3081",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28238-subject-3481.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this word is just the vocab word {span:lang=ja:\u4e00\u756a} plus the word {span:lang=ja:\u76ee}. If you know both of those readings you'll be able to read this one as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3054\u3046\u304b\u306a\u671d\u98df\u3092\u98df\u3079\u7d42\u308f\u3063\u3066\u3001\u4e00\u756a\u76ee\u306e\u304b\u3093\u305d\u3046\u306f\u3001\u3084\u3063\u3071\u308a\u30d9\u30fc\u30b3\u30f3\u306f\u304a\u3044\u3057\u3044\u3001\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The first thing that comes to mind after finishing this wonderful breakfast is that bacon is delicious, as we all know."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e00\u756a\u76ee\u306e\u3089\u3093\u306b\u306f\u3001\u3059\u304d\u306a\u4eba\u306e\u540d\u524d\u3092\u304b\u3044\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please write down the name of the person you like in the first column."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u50d5\u306f\u6bce\u671d\u4e00\u756a\u76ee\u306b\u30015\u30ad\u30ed\u306e\u30e9\u30f3\u30cb\u30f3\u30b0\u3092\u3059\u308b\u3093\u3060\u305c\u3002\u300d\u300c\u5927\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306a\u3044\u3088\uff01\u50d5\u306f10\u30ad\u30ed\u8d70\u308b\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"The first thing I do every morning is run five kilometers.\" \"Big deal! I run ten!\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know the word {span:lang=ja:\u5916\u6765} to mean \"imported.\" So, combine that with the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:language} and you have an imported word, aka a {tooltip:Vocabulary:borrowed word}. There are a lot of these in Japanese, which makes this word important. Almost everything in katakana is a {span:lang=ja:\u5916\u6765\u8a9e}, in fact.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
