                    "ja": "\u5de5\u696d\u30c7\u30b6\u30a4\u30ca\u30fc\u306e\u4e2d\u5c71\u3055\u3093\u306f\u3001\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u3092\u30b9\u30c8\u30ec\u30b9\u767a\u3055\u3093\u306b\u4f7f\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The industrial designer, Mr. Nakayama, uses WaniKani for stress relief."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u5de5\u696d\u6280\u8853\u30d7\u30ed\u30b8\u30a7\u30af\u30c8\u306e\u9032\u307f\u5177\u5408\u306f\u3069\u3046\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u4eca\u306e\u3068\u3053\u308d\u306f\u9806\u8abf\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"How is your industrial technology project going? \" \"So far, so good.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:parent}s are very close to you, most likely. They are your closest relatives. They are the ones who are {tooltip:Vocabulary:intimate} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:friendly} with your affairs. They want to know everything!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Intimate",
                "Alternatives": "Friendly, Close",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u305f\u3057\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u305f\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3695-subject-3224.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u305f\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28195-subject-3224.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Those who are most {tooltip:Vocabulary:intimate} with you hang out with you even when you're doing gross things, like sitting on the {tooltip:Reading:sh*tter} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u305f}). Gross, your family is.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u307e\u3060\u89aa\u3057\u3044\u53cb\u4eba\u306b\u3057\u304b\u8a71\u3057\u3066\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "I've only told this to close friends."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u89aa\u3057\u304d\u4ef2\u306b\u3082\u793c\u304e\u3042\u308a\u300d\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3067\u3057\u3087\uff1f\u3044\u304f\u3089\u89aa\u3057\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3063\u3066\u30c8\u30a4\u30ec\u306f\u306e\u305e\u304b\u306a\u3044\u3067\uff01",
                    "en": "They say, \"A hedge between keeps friendship green,\" right? We're good friends, but don't peek at me when I'm on the toilet."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3002\u843d\u3061\u7740\u3044\u3066\u3088\u3002 \u89aa\u3057\u3044\u53cb\u4eba\u305f\u3061\u306b\u8ab0\u304b80\u30bb\u30f3\u30c8\u8cb8\u3057\u3066\u3042\u3052\u308c\u308b\u4eba\u304c\u3044\u306a\u3044\u304b\u805e\u3044\u3066\u307f\u3066\u3042\u3052\u308b\u304b\u3089\u3002",
                    "en": "Oh Koichi. Calm down. I\u2019ll ask my close friends if anyone can lend you the 80 cents."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know {span:lang=ja:\u65e5\u672c} is \"Japan.\" So, when you add {tooltip:Kanji:language} onto the end of that you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:Japanese language}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Japanese Language",
