                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word ({span:lang=ja:\u756a\u53f7}) with a single-word kanji added. That means you have two on'yomi readings from the jukugo word and the kun'yomi reading from the single kanji ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3060}). Put them all together and you have the reading of this kanji!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u756a\u53f7\u672d\u3092\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3001\u304a\u5f85\u3061\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please take a numbered ticket and wait your turn."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3059\u307f\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3001\u3053\u306e\u8fba\u308a\u306b\u756a\u53f7\u672d\u306f\u843d\u3061\u3066\u3044\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3067\u3057\u305f\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Excuse me, wasn't there a number tag left around here?"
                },
