                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. It will also help if you know the reading of {span:lang=ja:\u7814\u7a76} already. Also note that {span:lang=ja:\u6240} is normal for one reading, but also gets the rendaku treatment, meaning {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087} becomes {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087}, for the secondary reading.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3068\u3042\u308b\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u306e\u7814\u7a76\u6240\u304c\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u304c\u30da\u30e9\u30da\u30e9\u306b\u306a\u308b\u304f\u3059\u308a\u3092\u958b\u767a\u3057\u305f\u305d\u3046\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I heard that a certain American lab has made a pill that will make you fluent in Japanese."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u307f\u305d\u3057\u308b\u7814\u7a76\u6240\u3067\u3001\u307c\u3046\u3055\u3044\u304f\u3093\u308c\u3093\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "There is an emergency drill in the Miso Soup Research Facility today."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u30d0\u30fc\u30ac\u30fc\u30ad\u30f3\u30b0\u7814\u7a76\u6240\u3067\u50cd\u3044\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u79c1\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u306f\u3001\u30d5\u30e9\u30a4\u30c9\u30dd\u30c6\u30c8\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3001\u305d\u306e\u5f8c\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u4f53\u91cd\u3092\u6e2c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I work for the Burger King Research Institute. My job consists of eating french fries and then having my body weighed."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:revolve} X number of {tooltip:Kanji:times}. Really, the times isn't so important, but the revolving is. That's why this word is {tooltip:Vocabulary:revolve} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:rotate}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rotation",
                "Alternatives": "Revolution, Revolve, Rotate",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044\u3066\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3044\u3066\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3438-subject-3176.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3044\u3066\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28109-subject-3176.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. P.S. Ever heard of \"{span:lang=ja:\u56de\u8ee2\u305a\u3057}?\" That's the kind of sushi that's on conveyer belts, rotating around and around, bringing you delicious plates of things.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30da\u30c3\u30c8\u306e\u30cf\u30e0\u30b9\u30bf\u30fc\u304c\u3082\u306e\u3059\u3054\u3044\u3044\u304d\u304a\u3044\u3067\u56de\u3057\u8eca\u3092\u56de\u8ee2\u3055\u305b\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My pet hamster is vigorously rotating his hamster wheel."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u305d\u3053\u306e\u56de\u8ee2\u305a\u3057\u3001\u3082\u3046\u884c\u3063\u305f\uff1f\u306a\u3093\u304b\u3001\u305d\u3053\u306e\u3059\u3057\u3057\u3087\u304f\u4eba\u306f\u76bf\u304c\u304d\u3089\u3044\u3089\u3057\u304f\u3001\u3059\u3057\u304c\u56de\u8ee2\u3057\u3066\u3042\u3064\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u308b\u30b3\u30f3\u30d9\u30a2\u30d9\u30eb\u30c8\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u76f4\u3067\u304a\u304b\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3089\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Have you been to the conveyer belt sushi restaurant over there? Apparently their sushi chefs hate plates there, so the sushi is directly on the rotating, hot conveyor belt."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6708\u306f\u5730\u7403\u306e\u5468\u308a\u56de\u8ee2\u3057\u3066\u3044\u3066\u3001\u5730\u7403\u306f\u592a\u967d\u306e\u5468\u308a\u3092\u56de\u8ee2\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "The moon revolves around the earth and the earth revolves around the sun."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is just the noun version of the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u9152} - it has an {span:lang=ja:\u304a} there to be nice. This word can mean both {tooltip:Vocabulary:alcohol} (like the parent kanji) or {tooltip:Vocabulary:sake} (the main kind of Japanese alcohol, at least back in the kanji days).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sake",
                "Alternative": "Alcohol",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3055\u3051"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3055\u3051",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3262-subject-3163.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3055\u3051",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28027-subject-3163.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is kun'yomi, which isn't what you learned with the kanji. But, it should be pretty easy. You know what Japanese alcohol is called already, right? It's {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3051}, simple as that. So long as you've heard of sake you should be A-Okay with this reading.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u30d1\u30fc\u30c6\u30a3\u30fc\u3067\u304a\u9152\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I drank alcohol at the party."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u3001\u305d\u306e\u304a\u9152\u306f\u30b7\u30fc\u30ba\u30f3\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u7533\u3057\u308f\u3051\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304c\u3054\u7528\u3044\u3067\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "That sake is out of season now, so I'm afraid it's not available."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u5272\u308a\u52d8\u306b\u3057\u3088\u3046\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3044\u3084\u3002\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u4ffa\u306e\u5962\u308a\u3060\u3088\u3002\u3057\u304b\u3082\u3001\u4ffa\u306f\u304a\u9152\u3092\u305f\u304f\u3055\u3093\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u304a\u524d\u306f\u4e00\u6ef4\u3082\u98f2\u307e\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Let\u2019s split the bill.\" \"No, it\u2019s on me this time. I drank a lot of alcohol, but you didn\u2019t drink anything\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Taking the {tooltip:Kanji:nearby} {tooltip:Kanji:road} will get you to your destination more quickly (because it's more close by!). This is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:shortcut}, aka the {tooltip:Vocabulary:short way}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shortcut",
                "Alternative": "Short Way",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3061\u304b\u307f\u3061"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3061\u304b\u307f\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3674-subject-3487.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3061\u304b\u307f\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28188-subject-3487.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is a bit weird in this one. It uses the kun'yomi reading for both kanji, even though it looks just like it should be all on'yomi reading. It's like you're taking a {tooltip:Vocabulary:shortcut} with your kanji readings and doing the native Japanese readings (kun'yomi) instead of the more intellectual Chinese ones (on'yomi). Luckily, you've hopefully seen both of these kanji as vocab already. You have {span:lang=ja:\u3061\u304b} for {span:lang=ja:\u8fd1} (short for {span:lang=ja:\u8fd1\u3044}) and you have {span:lang=ja:\u9053} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3061}), just like the word \"street\" you learned before. Combine these together and you have the reading for this word. Perhaps it's like this because you're combining a couple concepts together into one word, at least when it comes to \"short + way.\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e0a\u624b\u306a\u7d75\u3092\u3082\u5199\u3059\u308b\u4e8b\u306f\u3001\u4e0a\u305f\u3064\u306e\u8fd1\u9053\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Tracing a good picture is a shortcut for improvement."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u3067\u6f22\u5b57\u3092\u304a\u307c\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u7fd2\u3068\u304f\u306e\u8fd1\u9053\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Do you really think memorizing kanji on WaniKani is actually a shortcut to Japanese acquisition?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3042\u308a\u3048\u306d\u3047\uff01\u304a\u524d\u3063\u3066\u672c\u5f53\u8133\u307f\u305d\u7121\u3044\u306e\u306a\u3002\u306a\u3093\u3067\u4e00\u65b9\u901a\u884c\u3092\u9006\u8d70\u3057\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d\u300c\u8fd1\u9053\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Oh my God! You are such an airhead! Why are we going down a one-way street?\" \"I thought it would be a shortcut!\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Kanji:energy} is that of {tooltip:Kanji:sick}ness, you are probably {tooltip:Vocabulary:sick}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sick",
                "Alternatives": "Illness, Sickness, Disease",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3087\u3046\u304d"
