                        "file": "28008-subject-3230.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bcd\u306e\u75c5\u6c17\u306f\u3001\u307e\u3060\u3088\u304f\u306a\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "My mother\u2019s illness still hasn\u2019t improved."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u3057\u308a\u304b\u3089\u304a\u306a\u3089\u304c\u6b62\u307e\u3089\u306a\u3044\u75c5\u6c17\u306b\u304b\u304b\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3001\u5916\u306b\u51fa\u3089\u308c\u306a\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I got a disease that makes me fart all the time, so I've haven't been able to go outside."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u5148\u751f\u3001\u50d5\u306e\u30de\u30de\u306e\u75c5\u6c17\u3001\u76f4\u305b\u308b\u306e\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3084\u3063\u3066\u307f\u308b\u3051\u3069\u3001\u5f53\u3066\u306b\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u306d\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Can you fix my mom\u2019s illness, doctor?\" \"I\u2019ll give it a try, but don\u2019t count on it.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:person} who is {tooltip:Kanji:sick} is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:sick person}. They are also a {tooltip:Vocabulary:patient}, at least we can hope they are, for their sake.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sick Person",
                "Alternative": "Patient",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3087\u3046\u306b\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3073\u3087\u3046\u306b\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3420-subject-3232.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3073\u3087\u3046\u306b\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28082-subject-3232.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Note that this uses the {span:lang=ja:\u306b\u3093} reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4eba}. This is because every sick person enjoys laying in bed playing {tooltip:Reading:nin}tendo.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3064\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3044\u3084\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3001\u75c5\u4eba\u306b\u306f\u8fd1\u3088\u308a\u305f\u304f\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "If you don\u2019t want to catch something, you shouldn\u2019t go near sick people."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3057\u306b\u3001\u524d\u4e16\u306f\u75c5\u4eba\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The fortuneteller told me that my previous life was as a sick person."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u8abf\u5b50\u306f\u3069\u3046\u3060\u3044\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u7d76\u597d\u8abf\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d\u300c\u305d\u308c\u306f\u826f\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002\u75c5\u4eba\u304b\u3089\u305d\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u805e\u3051\u308b\u3068\u306f\u601d\u3063\u3066\u3082\u307f\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u304c\u306a\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"How\u2019s it going?\" \"Couldn\u2019t be better.\" \"Good. I\u2019m surprised to hear that from a sick person though.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. Please note that this word refers to \"the side of something.\" Not \"the right side,\" for example. That would be {span:lang=ja:\u53f3\u5074}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Side",
                "Alternatives": "Beside, Next To, Horizontal",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3053"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3185-subject-3219.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28006-subject-3219.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this vocab is the same as the one you learned with the kanji, lucky you!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u3063\u8336\u5e97\u306e\u6a2a\u306b\u3001\u98df\u3069\u3046\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "There is a diner next to the cafe."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3057\u5f37\u3068\u3046\u304c\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u306b\u3084\u3063\u3066\u6765\u305f\u3089\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u30c7\u30b9\u30af\u307e\u3067\u8d70\u3063\u3066\u305d\u306e\u6a2a\u306b\u3057\u3083\u304c\u307f\u3053\u3080\u3093\u3060\u3002\u305d\u3053\u304c\u6700\u3082\u5b89\u5168\u306a\u5834\u6240\u3060\u304b\u3089\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "If a robber breaks into the Tofugu office, just run to Koichi's desk and crouch down next to it because it's the safest spot."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5348\u5f8c\u306e\u4eee\u7720\u306e\u9593\u306b\u6a2a\u5411\u304d\u306b\u5bdd\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "During my afternoon nap I sleep on my side."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Remember how {span:lang=ja:\u624b} can sometimes refer to a person? In this case, we have a {tooltip:Kanji:song} {tooltip:Kanji:person} (or perhaps a \"person who handles songs\"). What is a song person also known as? A {tooltip:Vocabulary:singer}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Singer",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3057\u3085"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3057\u3085",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3546-subject-3205.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3057\u3085",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28123-subject-3205.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are on'yomi readings. You've learned them both already (you learned {span:lang=ja:\u624b}'s on'yomi reading with word {span:lang=ja:\u6295\u624b}), so you should be able to read this like a {tooltip:Vocabulary:singer} sings with a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:cashew}s {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3057\u3085} in their mouth. FAST AND LOUD!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6b4c\u624b\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u306e\u306f\u3001\u6bcd\u306e\u3048\u3044\u304d\u3087\u3046\u304c\u5927\u304d\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My mother had a large influence in my becoming a singer."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u6b4c\u624b\u3001\u304b\u306a\u308a\u65e5\u3084\u3051\u3057\u305f\u306d\u3002",
