{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Song",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u305f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3632-subject-3204.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28168-subject-3204.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}Think about a song... but not just any song... think about the {tooltip:Reading:utter} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u305f}) song, and make it up right now and sing it out loud. What does the utter song sound like? Why do you love utterances so much that you made a song about them?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3067\u3082\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u6b4c\u306f\u3042\u307e\u308a\u77e5\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "But I don\u2019t know Japanese songs very well."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u308c\u306f\u305f\u3093\u306a\u308b\u6b4c\u3058\u3083\u306a\u304f\u3001\u3072\u307f\u3064\u306e\u3042\u3093\u53f7\u3067\u3082\u3042\u308b\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3068\u3044\u3046\u6c17\u304c\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "It feels like this isn't just a song, but a secret code too."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30b8\u30a7\u30a4\u30bd\u30f3\uff01\u3042\u3093\u305f\u3001\u30a2\u30de\u30f3\u30c0\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u6b4c\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u306e\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3048\u30fc\u3068\u3001\u3053\u308c\u306f\u305d\u3046\u3044\u3046\u306e\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3082\u3046\uff01\u3068\u307c\u3051\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Jason! You made a song for Amanda?\" \"Ah, this isn\u2019t what it looks like.\" \"Come on! Don\u2019t give me that.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You can probably figure out that {span:lang=ja:\u30b9\u30da\u30a4\u30f3} is \"Spain\" just by reading it. Add the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:language} on there and you have the {tooltip:Vocabulary:Spanish language} (or just {tooltip:Vocabulary:Spanish}), if you'd like.",
