                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28179-subject-8744.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5f15} and the on'yomi for {span:lang=ja:\u7b97}. And the {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3093} reading is rendaku'd into {span:lang=ja:\u3056\u3093}. This is the same for all the math-ish words (addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division), so try to remember that, because you'll see it again!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3061\u308d\u3093\u3001\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u5f15\u304d\u7b97\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\uff01",
                    "en": "Of course I can do subtraction!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u5f15\u304d\u7b97\u306e\u3058\u3085\u304e\u3087\u3046\u306f\u9577\u3059\u304e\u3066\u3001\u3042\u304f\u3073\u304c\u6b62\u307e\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "Subtraction class is so long that I can't stop yawning."
