                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4ed5\u4e8b\u7d42\u308f\u308a\u306e\u30d3\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u6700\u9ad8\u3060\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "Beer when work ends is the best."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u308f\u3093\u306e\u591c\u3051\u3044\u3092\u898b\u306a\u304c\u3089\u6700\u9ad8\u306e\u4e00\u6642\u3092\u697d\u3057\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm enjoying the best moment, looking at the night view of Tokyo Bay."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3046\u308f\uff01\u3042\u3093\u305f\u306e\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3001\u4eca\u307e\u3067\u3067\u6700\u9ad8\u306e\u30c1\u30e7\u30b3\u30ec\u30fc\u30c8\u30b1\u30fc\u30ad\u3060\u308f\u3002\u3067\u3082\u3001\u4e00\u4f53\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u306e\uff1f\u304a\u83d3\u5b50\u4f5c\u308a\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u3002\u300d\u300c\u5225\u306b\u3002\u4f55\u304b\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3057\u3066\u307f\u305f\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3060\u3051\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Wow, you made the best chocolate cake. But, what\u2019s gotten into you? You\u2019ve never baked before.\" \"Nothing, I just wanted to do something new.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is the adverb version of the kanji, so it has the same meaning, basically. You can say this is {tooltip:Vocabulary:the most} or just {tooltip:Vocabulary:most}. You can also use it as {tooltip:Vocabulary:extremely}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "The Most",
                "Alternatives": "Most, Extremely",
                "Word Type": "adverb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3063\u3068\u3082"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u3063\u3068\u3082",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3733-subject-3233.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u3063\u3068\u3082",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28211-subject-3233.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this is a reading you didn't learn with the kanji (the kun'yomi reading). To learn it, let's look at a mnemonic. \n{splitParent}Think of {tooltip:Vocabulary:the most} ridiculous {tooltip:Reading:motto} ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3063\u3068}) you've ever heard. Now imagine a motto that's even more ridiculous. Here are some actual totally real mottos that are the most ridiculous: \"What Can Brown Do for You?\" \"It's Not for Women\" \"If It Doesn't Get All Over the Place, It Doesn't Belong in Your Face\" and of course, \"Why Not Enjoy the Go?\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3052\u3057\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4e00\u5e74\u3067\u6700\u3082\u591c\u304c\u307f\u3058\u304b\u304f\u306a\u308b\u65e5\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "The summer solstice is the shortest night of the year."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3075\u3058\u5c71\u306f\u65e5\u672c\u3067\u6700\u3082\u9ad8\u3044\u5c71\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Mt. Fuji is the tallest mountain in Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f7c\u3001\u4eca\u65e5\u306e\u591c\u4f55\u98df\u3079\u305f\u304b\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u308b\uff1f\u713c\u304d\u8089\u98df\u3079\u653e\u984c\u306b\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002\u6700\u3082\u81ed\u3044\u304a\u306a\u3089\u306b\u5099\u3048\u3066\u304a\u3044\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u8eab\u306e\u305f\u3081\u3060\u3088\u3002\u7528\u5fc3\u306b\u8d8a\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",
                    "en": "Do you know what he ate tonight? He went to an all you can eat yakiniku restaurant. We\u2019d better prepare for the smelliest farts imaginable. Better safe than sorry."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Now} {tooltip:Kanji:morning} is just another way of saying {tooltip:Vocabulary:this morning}. It's the closest morning to right now!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "This Morning",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3055"
