                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3051\u3055",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3544-subject-8703.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3051\u3055",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28134-subject-8703.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This reading is an exception. Let's use this mnemonic to remember it:\n{splitParent}{tooltip:Vocabulary:This morning} you want a {tooltip:Reading:quesa}dilla ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3055}) for breakfast. You can't wait until tomorrow morning, you NEED it this morning! Imagine eating a delicious quesadilla first thing this morning. Mmm!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u671d\u3001\u304f\u3059\u308a\u3092\u98f2\u3080\u306e\u3092\u308f\u3059\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I forgot to take my medicine this morning."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u671d\u304b\u3089\u4e21\u8db3\u304c\u3044\u305f\u304f\u3066\u601d\u3046\u3088\u3046\u306b\u6b69\u3051\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "My legs have been hurting since I woke up this morning, so I can't move as much as I'd like."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u671d\u3053\u3053\u3067\u7389\u7a81\u304d\u4e8b\u6545\u304c\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "This morning there was a multi-vehicle accident here."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:advance} so the verb vocab version means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to advance}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Advance",
                "Alternatives": "To Go Forward, To Progress",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3059\u3080"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u3059\u3080",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3273-subject-3177.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u3059\u3080",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28022-subject-3177.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}In order {tooltip:Vocabulary:to advance}, you must {tooltip:Reading:sue Sue} for her misdeeds against you. Imagine her standing in your way, literally. She keeps saying, \"You'll have to sue me if you want to get past me!\" So you do. You sue Sue. Now tell her to {tooltip:Reading:mo}ve ({span:lang=ja:\u3080}). \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4ed5\u4e8b\u306f\u9032\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Are you making any progress in your work?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u4e00\u6b69\u5148\u3092\u9032\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu always goes one step ahead, doesn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u5b22\u3055\u3093\u306f\u4ed6\u306e\u5b66\u751f\u3088\u308a\u305a\u3063\u3068\u9032\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Your daughter is advancing faster than the other students."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen the word {span:lang=ja:\u6c7a\u3081\u308b} before, hopefully. This is similar, except for instead of doing the action of deciding, something has just been decided (by something or someone else). You are not the decision maker, here. That's why this word is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be decided}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Decided",
                "Alternative": "To Be Settled",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u307e\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u307e\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3206-subject-3492.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u307e\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28012-subject-3492.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as {span:lang=ja:\u6c7a\u3081\u308b}, so make sure you know that word so you can apply that knowledge over here.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4ed5\u4e8b\u304c\u6c7a\u307e\u3063\u3066\u304b\u3089\u306f\u3001\u304d\u3087\u3046\u307f\u304c\u306a\u304f\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Since I got the job, I\u2019ve lost interest."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u6bce\u671d\u304b\u307f\u304c\u305f\u304c\u6c7a\u307e\u3089\u306a\u3044\u305b\u3044\u3067\u4f1a\u793e\u306b\u3061\u3053\u304f\u3059\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Every morning Koichi is late for work because he hasn't decided on a hairstyle yet."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u305d\u308c\u306f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u3044\u3044\u8003\u3048\u3060\u306d\u3002\u305d\u3046\u3057\u3088\u3046\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3088\u3057\u3001\u3058\u3083\u3042\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3067\u8a71\u306f\u6c7a\u307e\u308a\u3060\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"That\u2019s a really good idea. Let\u2019s do that.\" \"Okay, then it\u2019s been decided.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:begin} or {tooltip:Kanji:start}, and the verb version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to begin}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to begin something}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to start}, or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to start something}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Begin",
                "Alternatives": "To Start, To Begin Something, To Start Something",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3058\u3081\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3058\u3081\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20414-subject-3097.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3058\u3081\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40320-subject-3097.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be the kun'yomi reading, which you didn't learn with the kanji. Here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}Right now it's time {tooltip:Vocabulary:to begin} {tooltip:Reading:Haj} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3058}). (Haj is the fifth pillar of Islam, and is a pilgrimage to Mecca during the month of Dhu al-Hijja). You need to start Haj right now!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f55\u304b\u3089\u59cb\u3081\u308b\u306e\u304c\u3044\u3044\u306e\u304b\u3001\u5206\u304b\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I don\u2019t know what to start from."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3080\u3059\u3081\u3055\u3093\u3001\u56db\u5e74\u751f\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u4f55\u304b\u306a\u3089\u3044\u4e8b\u3092\u59cb\u3081\u308b\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "Will your daughter start any extracurriculars when she reaches fourth grade?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u751f\u5730\u3092\u30d5\u30e9\u30a4\u30d1\u30f3\u306b\u6d41\u3057\u59cb\u3081\u308b\u524d\u306b\u3001\u6750\u6599\u3092\u5168\u3066\u6df7\u305c\u308b\u5fc5\u8981\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "You need to mix all the ingredients together before you can start transferring the batter to the pans."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u52a9\u3051\u308b} means \"to help\" - so, this is a different version of that. This is when someone is helping someone else, or something is helping you, but you're not doing the action of helping someone. Use the {span:lang=ja:\u304b} to help you remember: The \"car\" helps you to drive around. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be helped}. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Helped",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Saved, To Be Rescued",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
