                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You need {tooltip:Vocabulary:to hear} something very important, but you can't. In order to hear, you have to take a {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) and unlock the doors covering your ears. Go ahead and imagine yourself doing that, focusing on the key.\n"
