                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28187-subject-3171.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to learn} about {tooltip:Reading:Nara}, the city of deer... lots and lots of deer. If you don't know about it, how about learning about it?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u6765\u3066\u304b\u3089\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u3092\u7fd2\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019ve learned Japanese since coming to Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u59c9\u306f\u3001\u30d4\u30a2\u30ce\u3092\u7fd2\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My older sister is taking piano lessons."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u4e16\u754c\u4e00\u306e\u30d5\u30b0\u30af\u30c3\u30ad\u30fc\u306e\u4f5c\u308a\u65b9\u3092\u7fd2\u3044\u306b\u884c\u304f\u306e\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m going to learn how to make the world\u2019s best fugu cookies today."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:exit} your house and you {tooltip:Kanji:meet} someone. You didn\u2019t mean to meet them, but it happened anyway. That\u2019s why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to meet by chance}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Meet By Chance",
                "Alternatives": "To Meet Unexpectedly, To Come Across, To Encounter, To Run Into",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3067\u3042\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3067\u3042\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3671-subject-3506.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3067\u3042\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28186-subject-3506.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is that of the word {span:lang=ja:\u51fa\u308b} and the word {span:lang=ja:\u4f1a\u3046}, both of which you've hopefully seen. The {span:lang=ja:\u51fa} portion may be confusing, but you can usually assume that if one part of the word is kun'yomi / vocab reading, the other part is too, which is why {span:lang=ja:\u51fa} uses the vocab reading.\n{splitParent}Oh by the way, this word can be written like this too: {span:lang=ja:\u51fa\u5408\u3046}. It\u2019s not as common, but you may come across it every now and then, so it\u2019s good to know! \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u305f\u3061\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u51fa\u4f1a\u3046\u306e\u304c\u65e9\u3059\u304e\u305f\u307f\u305f\u3044\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "It looks like we happened to run into each other a little too early."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u306e\u3046\u306e\u591c\u3001\u30af\u30e9\u30d6\u3067\u3001\u308c\u3093\u3042\u3044\u304b\u3093\u3058\u3087\u3046\u306c\u304d\u3067\u305f\u3060\u697d\u3057\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3046\u7537\u306b\u51fa\u4f1a\u3063\u3066\u3055\u3001\u30cf\u30de\u3063\u3061\u3083\u3044\u3051\u306a\u3044\u306e\u306f\u5206\u304b\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3081\u3061\u3083\u304f\u3061\u3083\u30bf\u30a4\u30d7\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Last night, I met a guy who's looking for no strings attached fun at a club and I know I shouldn't be into him, but he was really my type."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30cb\u30b3\u30fc\u30eb\u3063\u3066\u3001\u4eca\u3001\u4ed8\u304d\u5408\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u4eba\u3044\u308b\u306e\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3048\u3048\u3002\u30a8\u30ea\u30c3\u30af\u30681\u5e74\u9593\u4ed8\u304d\u5408\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u308f\u3002\u300d\u300c\u305d\u3046\u306a\u3093\u3060\uff01\u5f7c\u3068\u306f\u3001\u3069\u3053\u3067\u51fa\u4f1a\u3063\u305f\u306e\uff1f\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Are you seeing anyone now, Nicole?\" \"Yes, I\u2019ve been seeing Eric for a year.\" \"Wow, where did you guys meet?\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Kanji:mouth} makes {tooltip:Kanji:tone}s we call it your {tooltip:Vocabulary:tone} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:tone of voice}. They're different kinds of sounds you make with your mouth that make you sound happy, sad, mean, etc.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tone",
