                        "file": "28013-subject-3185.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You go {tooltip:Vocabulary:to open} the door. When you do, a huge scream comes out: \"{tooltip:Reading:AAAHHH}!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3042}). Imagine giant {span:lang=ja:\u3042} characters flying out of the door you opened as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u3058\u3057\u3087\u3092\u958b\u3051\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please open your Japanese dictionary."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u304b\u308c\u6c0f\u306f\u3001\u8eca\u306b\u4e57\u308b\u6642\u306f\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u30c9\u30a2\u3092\u958b\u3051\u3066\u304f\u308c\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "My boyfriend always opens the car door for me when I get in."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u306d\u3047\u3001\u3053\u306e\u30ef\u30a4\u30f3\u30dc\u30c8\u30eb\u3092\u958b\u3051\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3048\u306a\u3044\u304b\u306a\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3044\u3044\u3088\u3002\u671d\u98ef\u524d\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Can you open this bottle of wine for me?\" \"Of course. Piece of cake.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
