{
            "mnemonic": "This is a ceremony radical with a slide radical. Why would someone be sliding on the floor at a ceremony? If they're a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard}, that's why! People love to drink at ceremonies. And there's always at least one drunkard who takes it too far and slides across the floor doing the worm.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Drunkard"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Do you remember stairs ({span:lang=ja:\u4e43})? This radical is a lot like that, but it has extra bits and pieces. It's still stairs... but it's more complicated. And faster! That's why it's an {tooltip:Radical:escalator} instead!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Escalator"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is the same as the kanji. It means {tooltip:Radical:few}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Few"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is the same as the kanji you learned earlier, but the meaning is a little different. It's not just for saying things humbly, it's for being {tooltip:Radical:humble} in general. When you see this radical, think about being humble.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Humble"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is the same as the kanji. It means {tooltip:Radical:older brother}.",
            "hints": "",
