                "Primary": "Older Brother"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The \"Hat-Ground\" stamp is on this envelope. That can only mean one thing: {tooltip:Radical:Orders} from HQ. Imagine this stamp on some orders for you\u2014read the orders out loud to help yourself remember that this hat-ground stamp means \"orders\" and nothing else.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Orders"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the sun is out and you kick the ground, you'll hit a {tooltip:Radical:root}. Roots try to come up when the sun is bright. But if you kick too hard, the root will trip you, so watch out!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Root"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's some stuff growing out of this rice paddy and there is a cross guarding over it. This rice paddy is owned by a {tooltip:Radical:simple} family that lives the simple life. They grow their rice, pray to their god, and everything is nice and simple. Ahh, I'm jealous.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Simple"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is the same as the kanji. It means {tooltip:Radical:skin}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Skin"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is the same as the kanji. It means {tooltip:Radical:sound}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sound"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's a lid on top of something you're trying to keep private. It's your {tooltip:Radical:trash}. You wouldn't want people going through your private trash, which is why we put lids on our trash cans. It's also illegal to look through someone's trash, so make sure you never do that.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Trash"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Using your {tooltip:Radical:construction} {tooltip:Radical:power} you build something great. A true {tooltip:Kanji:achievement} built for the achievement of making kanji learning easier!",
            "hints": "Just constructing this thing was an achievement. Feel proud like it was, well, an achievement.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Achievement",
                "Alternative": "Accomplishment"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Thanks {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. Now everyone will know of your achievements around kanji learning and inside-out earth theory.{splitParent}Hint: When you see {span:lang=ja:\u5de5} in a kanji it will often take the {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046} reading. Remember that, because it comes up quite a bit!",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:achievement} was made possible by {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, so of course this construction project is a giant statue of the man himself. What an achievement of a statue. What an achievement of an achievement."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} holds a {tooltip:Radical:sword} it {tooltip:Kanji:becomes} something else. The drunkard doesn't become a swordsman, they're still just a drunkard. But the sword in their hands does.",
            "hints": "Picture the drunkard standing in front of you. He picked up the sword and is holding it above his head. It's becoming... becoming...",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Become"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If a sword becomes a saber in the hands of a drunkard... then what are you? Geez this became pretty deep.{splitParent}You slice down the drunkard with your saber and become a little more depressed than you were before.",
                "mnemonic": "The sword has {tooltip:Kanji:become} a {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044})! It's just like the saber you have! Hey, wait."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:mountain} on top of the {tooltip:Radical:cliff} is {tooltip:Radical:dry} from the {tooltip:Kanji:coast} below. Just from looking at the raging {tooltip:Kanji:shore} below, you'd think everything would be wet, it's splashing everywhere!",
            "hints": "You're on top of the mountain and the entire coast is stretching out below. The shore goes as far as your eyes can see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Coast",
                "Alternative": "Shore"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Sit down next to Gandhi and close your eyes. You can hear the water hitting the shore below. The coastal birds are screaming. You crack open an eye and see Gandhi still sitting perfectly still. ",
                "mnemonic": "Sitting up there, watching the {tooltip:Kanji:coast} with you, is {tooltip:Reading:Gan}dhi ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3093}). The world famous Gandhi, is just hanging out up here with you, looking down at what you now realize must be a coast in India."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Stand}ing next to your {tooltip:Radical:older brother} is another {tooltip:Radical:stand}ing {tooltip:Radical:older brother} of yours. They're trying to {tooltip:Kanji:compete}, to see which of them can stand the straightest and tallest.",
            "hints": "Picture your two older brothers competing like this. Are you going to root for one of them? That's not very nice, you shouldn't have a favorite older brother.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Compete"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046, \u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Look really closely at your older brothers. They're competing pretty hard for your attention. They really want to go to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}... but which one do YOU want to spend time with the most?",
                "mnemonic": "Your older brothers are trying to {tooltip:Kanji:compete} to see which of them gets to go to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} with you. You won a free trip to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}, but there's only one other ticket, so now your brothers are competing for you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you keep a {tooltip:Radical:wolverine} in a {tooltip:Radical:prison} with {tooltip:Radical:barb}s, you\u2019re likely to get into a {tooltip:Kanji:conflict} with animal rights groups. Wolverines aren\u2019t meant to be kept in cages, let alone barbed prisons. There\u2019s going to be some sort of conflict here, and animal activist groups are not going to be happy with you.",
            "hints": "Imagine you\u2019re the wolverine in this barbed prison. There\u2019s hardly enough room for you to even turn around in here. The barbs keep poking you as well. Have you ever run into a barbed wire fence? It\u2019s not pleasant.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Conflict"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3089\u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Pretend you're the wolverine once again. You're already in pain from gouging yourself in this barbed prison. But now you can feel a conflict within yourself. Your soul can't take this. You have to hold on, but it's so hard to keep fighting.",
                "mnemonic": "When the wolverine cuts itself inside the barbed prison (which is inevitable), the conflict changes. Now there is a {tooltip:Kanji:conflict} between the wolverine and its {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}). Does it lose it and become a shell of its former self? Or does it keep fighting and try to hang onto what's left of its soul?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} stands upon the {tooltip:Radical:ground} of the {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy}. She is searching for {tooltip:Radical:treasure}. It is said that this treasure here in this rice field will make things much easier for the leader (that's what leaders really want, after all). If she gets this treasure, it will be a great {tooltip:Kanji:convenience} for her, because convenience is everything when you're the leader.",
            "hints": "Imagine the leader looking around the rice paddy. She keeps saying, \"Ugh, it would be convenient if I didn't have to walk around out here looking for the treasure that's going to make things more convenient for me. Ugh.\" Go ahead and say this phrase out loud, too, pretending to be the leader in the rice paddy. Feel the cold and the wet, making it less convenient for you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Convenience",
                "Alternative": "Convenient"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3093, \u3073\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel the happiness that the leader would feel at this revelation. It will make everything much more convenient for her, since she's not the one doing all the manual labor. She won't have to eat out of a bento, that's for sure.",
                "mnemonic": "She finds a place to dig in the ground. It looks like there's some fresh dirt here. Finally, the treasure of {tooltip:Kanji:convenience} that will make this leader's life so much easier. She digs into the ground and pulls out a box. When she opens it, she finds out it's a {tooltip:Reading:ben}to ({span:lang=ja:\u3079\u3093}). My god, she thinks. This really will make my life more convenient. My people can take their lunches with them now instead of coming back to base to eat, which will waste way less time!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "By the time you finish digging a {tooltip:Radical:coffin} hole with nothing but a {tooltip:Radical:spoon}, you\u2019ll be an old {tooltip:Kanji:elderly} person. Digging with nothing but a spoon takes a long time, especially when the hole needs to be big enough for a coffin. You might as well be digging it for yourself at this rate. By the time you finish, you\u2019ll be all wrinkled and elderly and just about ready to keel over.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself digging a coffin hole with nothing but a spoon. Your hands get all cramped, your wrist starts to hurt, and you get painful blisters on your hands. It takes forever to dig a hole big enough for a coffin!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Elderly"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You hated roe when you were still young, but now that you\u2019re an elderly old fart you really want to eat it. Roe is for old people, you guess, as you slurp it up.",
                "mnemonic": "Now that you\u2019re {tooltip:Kanji:elderly} (and probably about to die) you suddenly crave some delicious {tooltip:Reading:roe} ({span:lang=ja:\u308d\u3046}). Salmon roe, sea urchin roe, tofugu roe, doesn\u2019t matter. Your old, tired bones need roe after all that hard work!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Orders} coming from your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} will determine the {tooltip:Kanji:fate} of your men. You are a commanding officer and orders from your mouth are law. Your orders alone determine the ultimate fate of your soldiers.",
            "hints": "Pretend you are a high ranking officer and imagine yourself giving orders to your underlings. Imagine all the power and influence you have. It feels good.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3044, \u307f\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u306e\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Students of American history are very familiar with the Mayflower. Recall learning about it in school whenever you see this kanji. Or look it up on Wikipedia if you don\u2019t know about it. The Mayflower is a big deal!",
                "mnemonic": "You are the commanding officer on the {tooltip:Reading:May}flower ({span:lang=ja:\u3081\u3044}). You give orders to colonize America. The orders spewing from your mouth hole determine the {tooltip:Kanji:fate} of the settlers and the fate of America and the fate of the world! You and the Mayflower have changed everything forever."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Try to use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to {tooltip:Radical:spoon} out some of the {tooltip:Radical:sun} and you'll come back with just one {tooltip:Kanji:finger}.",
            "hints": "Look down at your finger and the burned stumps where the rest of your fingers used to be. It hurts. And you're sad. But at least you still have one finger left.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Finger"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3073, \u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture sitting with a sheep. It's right across from you, staring into your eyes. It reaches out its sheep finger hoof and you reach out with your finger. They touch. It's magical.",
                "mnemonic": "Don't worry, you aren't the only one out there with just one {tooltip:Kanji:finger}, {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) only have one finger too. I mean, they're hooves, which are really just a single animal finger. It's just big and kind of flat."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you want a {tooltip:Radical:spirit} {tooltip:Radical:sword}, you have to be the {tooltip:Kanji:first} one to find it. Do you really think the first person to come across a spirit sword wouldn't want it?! No. So if you're any place but first, you're not getting anything.",
            "hints": "Imagine it like commenting on Youtube or Facebook. If you can say FIRST, first, well congrats. You win the internet spirit sword.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "First"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3058, \u306f\u3064, \u305d, \u305e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This is the first show of this type, anywhere in the world!",
                "mnemonic": "If you were lucky enough to be the {tooltip:Kanji:first} one to find the spirit sword, you should open up a small {tooltip:Reading:show} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087}) to show it off! And then you can make yourself the first in line every day to see the show."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What is the {tooltip:Radical:jet} of your {tooltip:Radical:mouth}? It's {tooltip:Kanji:flavor}. It's what shoots your mouth off, which explains why it hurts so much when you eat something awesome.",
            "hints": "Imagine how your favorite food tastes. Imagine a jet taking off in your mouth because of it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Flavor",
                "Alternative": "Taste"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3058",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Of course, if you're vegetarian imagine the flavor of the meat being terrible. Up to you. Make the mnemonic work for your lifestyle.",
                "mnemonic": "And what has more {tooltip:Kanji:flavor} than a big slab of {tooltip:Reading:me}at ({span:lang=ja:\u307f})? You love meat and its flavor nearly as much as you love the flavor of its juice. So many good things to put in your mouth! "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} there is a {tooltip:Radical:bear} trying to {tooltip:Kanji:follow} and {tooltip:Kanji:chase} you! You're on your own scooter, luckily, but that doesn't make this any less terrifying.",
            "hints": "Picture the bear on its scooter, following really closely behind your scooter. You can almost feel his bear breath on your neck!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Follow",
                "Alternative": "Chase"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the bear chasing you on its scooter, trying to reach out and grab the obi off your waist. Woah, it's getting a little too close!",
                "mnemonic": "The bear is trying to {tooltip:Kanji:follow} you because it wants your {tooltip:Reading:o}bi ({span:lang=ja:\u304a}). The obi is waving in the wind behind your scooter, and the bear is reaching out with its teeth to try and grab it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You should have a {tooltip:Radical:spirit} that's {tooltip:Radical:humble} when before a {tooltip:Kanji:god}. You never really have to act all nice and humble before anyone else, but if you meet a god... well... you should probably lower yourself appropriately. They can smite you and all that.",
            "hints": "Imagine a spirit appearing before you. It's a god. You should be as humble as possible. Out of respect and also because you don't want to be cursed or something.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "God"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093, \u3058\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you don't get down on your shins before god, they could take them away. Even your jeans couldn't protect you then. You don't want to live a shin-less life, do you?",
                "mnemonic": "When you see a {tooltip:Kanji:god}, you need to get down on your {tooltip:Reading:shin}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}). Get down on your ankles? No, not low enough. Knees? No, no, get your shins flat on the ground to show how humble you really are. Luckily, you're wearing {tooltip:Reading:jean}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093}), so at least that will stop your poor shins getting chafed!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:drop} of water to a {tooltip:Radical:root} is {tooltip:Kanji:good}. It's good for the roots to grow and live and thrive. And what's good for roots is good for our plants and us humans too.",
            "hints": "Imagine putting a little drop of water over a root you want to grow. Doing this is good for the plant and also good for your soul.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Good"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088, \u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Rowing even feels good on your arms and back. Probably just as good as all these roots will feel.",
                "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:good} way to get a lot of drops of water for your roots is to buy a {tooltip:Reading:row} boat ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}). Then just row out to the middle of the lake and plonk all the roots right into the source!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sound} of your {tooltip:Radical:heart} gives me an {tooltip:Kanji:idea}. The methodic thump thump thumping of a heart puts me in a trance that gives me great ideas. It\u2019s a very inspirational sound, the sound of a heart is. It gives me an idea. ",
            "hints": "Put your hand over your heart, or on your wrist, or somewhere you can feel your pulse. Your heart is pumping blood through your body, hear the sound of your heart beat and try to picture and get an idea for how all the blood flows through your body.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Idea"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the majestic animal that is the bald eagle. Imagine the sound of an eagle screeching as it zooms through the air, flapping its wings in the wind. It\u2019s pretty impressive.",
                "mnemonic": "The heart of an {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) is very strong. The person who knew this probably came up with the {tooltip:Kanji:idea} to make the bald eagle a symbol of the United States. Eagles are always flying around and doing things, so their hearts are very strong."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:Viking} in a position of {tooltip:Radical:power} does not need to {tooltip:Kanji:labor} in the fields. Labor is for the weak! A Viking of power takes what he wants, and need not labor for it. A powerful Viking plunders all and takes what he wants!",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself as a powerful Viking. You have the power to take anything you want, pillaging and plundering to your heart\u2019s content. Imagine all the things you would acquire with this sort of power.{splitParent}Note - there are a few other kanji that have a similar meaning to this one. This kanji is used in words related to physical, or manual labor, with an emphasis on how darn tiring it is!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Labor"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u305f\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this powerful Viking laying siege on a small fishing village and taking all the roe and stuffing it into his bearded face. So much labor went into harvesting that roe! Vikings are so mean!",
                "mnemonic": "It takes a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:labor} to harvest {tooltip:Reading:roe} ({span:lang=ja:\u308d\u3046}) so that\u2019s what the Viking decides to take first! Roe is delicious, but it\u2019s small and delicate. Vikings don\u2019t labor for their own roe! They take it and eat it!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are pieces of {tooltip:Radical:thread} on each {tooltip:Radical:escalator} showing you what {tooltip:Kanji:level} they go to in your school. Each escalator takes you to a different {tooltip:Kanji:grade}, so make sure you follow the right thread or you'll end up in a class that's either way above or way below your level.",
            "hints": "When you level up your Japanese skills, you'll take this escalator to rank up too!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Level",
                "Alternatives": "Grade, Rank"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "A teacher comes over and says, \"Excuse me, this is advanced level cucumber studies. I don't think you're at this level yet... please take the escalator down and follow the threads to find your level.\"",
                "mnemonic": "You want to see what the highest {tooltip:Kanji:level} is, so you go up the wrong escalator. At the top you find a giant {tooltip:Reading:cu}cumber ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3085\u3046})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a {tooltip:Radical:woman} and a {tooltip:Radical:child} in front of you. You {tooltip:Kanji:like} them very much.",
            "hints": "Imagine a woman and a child you like very much. Just appreciate them, and think about how much you like those two. The reading mnemonic definitely won't ruin your image of them or anything.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Like"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059, \u3053\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "And you DO like them. You have always been a fan of {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}'s kanji learning methods, and you feel so lucky to have married a woman who looks just like {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} and then (this is the real miracle!) gave birth to a child that looks like {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} too. Hashtag blessed.",
                "mnemonic": "\"I {tooltip:Kanji:like} you two,\" you say to the woman and child. They both turn their heads 180 degrees back towards you. They both have faces that look just like {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}'s. \"We like you too,\" they say in unison."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You\u2019ve been playing {tooltip:Radical:blackjack} in the {tooltip:Radical:sun} since {tooltip:Kanji:long ago}. This is the longest game of blackjack you\u2019ve ever played and it feels like ages since you started. You\u2019ve been sitting out in the sun playing blackjack since long, long ago.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself playing a never-ending game of blackjack out in the hot sun. You\u2019re sticky, sweaty, and tired. But all you can do is continue to play your game of blackjack. It\u2019s miserable.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Long Ago",
                "Alternative": "Long Time Ago"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u304d, \u3057\u3083\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080\u304b\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine your muck ashi, all dirty and muddy from walking on that old road from long ago. Feel the muck between the toes of your ashi, squishing with every step. Hear the sound the mud makes as it slides between your sweaty mucky toes.",
                "mnemonic": "Once you finally finish the game, you walk the long walk back home, in the sun, barefoot, on a dirt road that hasn\u2019t been maintained since {tooltip:Kanji:long ago}. Your feet are all sweaty from being out in the sun, and walking on this dirt road gives you {tooltip:Reading:muck ashi} ({span:lang=ja:\u3080\u304b\u3057}). Your ashi (feet) are all mucky and muddy from the combination of dirt and sweat. Your muck ashi are really gross, man."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} of your {tooltip:Radical:clan} wants to live close to the {tooltip:Radical:ground} so he demands you get {tooltip:Kanji:low}. Low, low, with your belly to the ground. That way you're always below him, since he's the leader.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself, face smooshed into the ground, and you can hear the leader shouting above you, \"GET LOW!\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Low"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Get low to the ground right now and ask your mom or dad to roll some tater tots towards your face. Eat them up, mm mm.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Low} people like you can only eat low food like potatoes. But that's boring, so you low people learned to make {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots. You roll them to each other and eat them without lifting your heads."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Give {tooltip:Radical:trash} to the {tooltip:Radical:moon} and it will {tooltip:Kanji:nurture} and {tooltip:Kanji:raise} that trash like it's its own little moon baby.",
            "hints": "Picture the moon raising this ball of trash, giving it love and attention.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Nurture",
                "Alternative": "Raise"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3060, \u306f\u3050\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as the little trash ball {span:lang=ja:\u884c\u304f}s up into the sky and floats around its moon mama. If you raise your child right it will want to {span:lang=ja:\u884c\u304f} wherever you go too.",
                "mnemonic": "The moon {tooltip:Kanji:nurture}s the trash ball until one day, it speaks! \"{tooltip:Reading:\u884c\u304f} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u304f}), {span:lang=ja:\u884c\u304f\uff01}\" it says. It wants to go live with mom moon!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you know the radical meaning {tooltip:Radical:orders} you know the kanji meaning {tooltip:Kanji:orders} as well!",
            "hints": "Here's an order: study your radicals.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Orders"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine an authority figure giving you this order as an official order. Ray guns don't really exist, so you think it's a pretty strange order.{splitParent}Hint: when you see the {tooltip:Radical:orders} radical, the reading will often be {span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3044}. The mnemonic will likely involve orders to get a ray gun of some kind.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:orders} are to get a {tooltip:Reading:ray} ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3044}) gun."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see something that would {tooltip:Radical:suit} you so you use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} and {tooltip:Kanji:pick up} the thing you want. You can pick up anything you think suits you. A shiny rock. A new pair of pants. Anything!",
            "hints": "Imagine something that would suit your life and your style. Now pick up that thing. Hold it in your fingers. Feel it. It's yours now.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pick Up"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u308d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You picked up the hero sword and now you're the new hero. Time to go kill a dragon. Good luck, try not to die hero person!",
                "mnemonic": "You're walking around looking for something to {tooltip:Kanji:pick up} when you see a sword in a rock. Yes, this will suit you. You pick up the sword and people jump out around you and tell you that you are the new {tooltip:Reading:hero} ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u308d})! Uh oh. Maybe you shouldn't have picked this up."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} {tooltip:Radical:master} has the power to {tooltip:Kanji:pour} water wherever he pleases. Tsunami masters are masters over the most powerful water force in the universe, so it makes sense that they have the ability to pour water at will, wherever they please. Best not tick off the master, unless you want a tsunami poured on your head.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself as this tsunami master. You\u2019re like a water bender from Avatar, only more awesome. Feel the cold wet water pouring out of your fingertips as you create water out of nothing. Imagine what it would be like to have this power.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pour"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u305d, \u3055, \u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine Chewbacca soaking wet. All his fur is matted down and he looks pretty depressed. He smells like wet dog too. Smell this smell in your nostrils as you imagine how pathetic this drenched Chewbacca feels.",
                "mnemonic": "If {tooltip:Reading:Chew}bacca ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3085\u3046}) was trying to attack you, you\u2019d be able to defend yourself easily. Simply {tooltip:Kanji:pour} a tsunami on him and Chewbacca would surrender in a heartbeat. Chewbacca doesn\u2019t like having water poured on him, especially not all the water from a tsunami."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Cut {tooltip:Radical:grain}s with a {tooltip:Radical:knife} to make them smaller and you'll make a great {tooltip:Kanji:profit}. By cutting them, now you can get three grains worth of money for what was once a single grain. ",
            "hints": "Imagine buying some rice. Now cut all the grains with a knife into smaller grains. Now sell them for two, three, four times the profit!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Profit",
                "Alternatives": "Benefit, Advantage"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture all of your reeds full of grains in a row. The entire world will benefit from your crafty invention. And you'll turn a great profit too, which certainly doesn't hurt.",
                "mnemonic": "To make an even better {tooltip:Kanji:profit}, you decide to cut up {tooltip:Reading:ree}ds ({span:lang=ja:\u308a}) too. You stuff the grains in the reeds and sell that as \"self-cooking\" sets."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} {tooltip:Radical:stand}s at the highest {tooltip:Kanji:rank} in an organization. The leader is of the highest rank and stands above all others.",
            "hints": "Picture this great leader. Imagine him actually standing on the shoulders of his supporters who are a lower rank than he is. He\u2019s standing atop this great pyramid as a fearless leader.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rank"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3089\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the same ranking pyramid from before, only all the members are boy scouts, and the leader at the top is an eagle. Hear the piercing screech of the eagle with your ears.",
                "mnemonic": "This great leader is actually the leader of the boy scouts. And as we all know, the highest {tooltip:Kanji:rank} in boy scouts is the rank of {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) scout. This great leader has attained the rank of eagle scout and stands above all other scouts."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:middle} of the road {tooltip:Radical:leader} is likely to have an average {tooltip:Kanji:relationship} with everyone. He doesn\u2019t really take sides in matters, and just stays in the middle. This makes him seem like sort of a wishy washy people pleaser, and as such his relationships with people are rarely anything more than average.",
            "hints": "I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve heard of \u201cflip-floppers\u201d in politics, or people who try and take both sides of an issue, always staying in the middle ground and never really taking a stand. Imagine one of these people to represent this kanji.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Relationship"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine your favorite flip-flopper from before. Now imagine that there\u2019s a knocker on his forehead and you get to knock that knocker as hard as you like. Sounds like fun, doesn\u2019t it? Imagine yourself doing this.",
                "mnemonic": "This kanji is pronounced exactly like the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u4e2d} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u304b}). It's one of those kanji where you can figure out the reading from one of the radicals."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When {tooltip:Radical:winter} comes your {tooltip:Radical:direction}, the trees must {tooltip:Kanji:release} their leaves for the coming cold.",
            "hints": "Picture winter heading straight for you and frosting everything over. Now picture the leaves being released by the trees.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Release"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u306a, \u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Release my home from this leaf prison!\" you shout at the now bare trees.",
                "mnemonic": "The trees {tooltip:Kanji:release} all of their leaves onto your {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}). Slowly, you watch in horror as your home is consumed by the released leaves. They enter in through the windows, doors, and the chimney."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You only got a {tooltip:Radical:few} {tooltip:Radical:grain}s on your plate. It only takes you a  {tooltip:Kanji:second} to eat them. It can't take any longer because there were so few.",
            "hints": "Count how many seconds it takes for you to eat the few grains you have. One... oh, they're gone.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Second"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Whenever you eat a few grains, even if only for a second, you get a terrible reaction seconds later that causes some pretty terrible B.O.",
                "mnemonic": "And also, a {tooltip:Kanji:second} is how long it takes for your awful {tooltip:Reading:B.O.} ({span:lang=ja:\u3073\u3087\u3046}) to appear. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} you put a {tooltip:Radical:sword} and a {tooltip:Radical:knife}. Now that you have them in there, you have to make them {tooltip:Kanji:separate} from each other.",
            "hints": "Anyone can put a sword and knife in their mouth. But not everyone can make them separate while still in your mouth.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Separate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"I bet you can't separate the sword and knife,\" they say in an annoying voice. Alright, time for you to show them. Nobody bets you anything without you blindly trying to do it!",
                "mnemonic": "Why are you trying to make a sword and knife {tooltip:Kanji:separate} in your mouth? Because someone {tooltip:Reading:bets you} ({span:lang=ja:\u3079\u3064}) can't do it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:cow} {tooltip:Radical:temple} is {tooltip:Kanji:special}. This cow must have been very important to have an entire temple dedicated to it.",
            "hints": "Picture a temple dedicated to a single cow. All of the people who come and worship here have a special place in their hearts for the cow.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Special"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You walk up to a statue of the special cow in the temple and see a collar around its neck with that says \"Tokugawa Moo Moo\" on it. How... special!",
                "mnemonic": "This cow is {tooltip:Kanji:special} because it belonged to {tooltip:Reading:Toku}gawa ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u304f}) Ieyasu, the first sh\u014dgun of the Tokugawa shogunate and uniter of Japan! He's a super important figure in Japanese history. You should absolutely look him up and read a bit about him (when you're caught up on these lessons, that is)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The card game fish are best at is {tooltip:Radical:blackjack} because they can easily hold the cards with their {tooltip:Radical:fins} {tooltip:Kanji:together}. In blackjack you don't have to have a huge hand, full of cards. It's just a few, so fish fins can keep them together and just hit or stay.",
            "hints": "Imagine a fish trying to hold a full hand of cards together. Impossible! Fish don\u2019t have fingers to keep them spread properly. Now imagine a fish trying to hold two cards together and nodding to hit. It's much easier to keep things together this way!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Together"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3082",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a bunch of fish gathering together in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} to participate in this blackjack tournament. With so many fish all together in one place, it probably smells pretty fishy.",
                "mnemonic": "Once a year trillions of fish get {tooltip:Kanji:together} in {tooltip:Reading:\u304d\u3087\u3046}{span:lang=ja:\u3068} to play blackjack. They have a huge tournament there once a year."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:woman} of {tooltip:Radical:power} sits on a {tooltip:Radical:stool} while her servants {tooltip:Kanji:toil} away in the kitchen. They are toiling away preparing a feast for this woman of power while she kicks back on her cozy stool. She\u2019s a queen and deserves to be pampered.",
            "hints": "Imagine you are in a position of power and can relax on a stool while your minions toil away in the kitchen to prepare you a feast. It\u2019s good to have money! You\u2019ve got it made. Imagine how smug you feel.{splitParent}Note - there are a few other kanji that have a similar meaning to this one. This kanji is used in words that refer to doing work, with a focus on making a concerted effort.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Toil"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3069",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine eating all this food with your dog. Hear your dog barking as it woofs up the food next to you as you do the same.",
                "mnemonic": "The servants are making lots of food for you and your {tooltip:Reading:do}g ({span:lang=ja:\u3069}). You're really hungry, so you encourage your minions to {tooltip:Kanji:toil} away faster so that you might feast a bit sooner."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} has a {tooltip:Radical:cloud} that he uses to {tooltip:Kanji:transmit} all of the messages he needs to send to his people. The cloud floats above him and when he wants to tell people something he just whispers into the cloud and it transmits his message really, really loudly to all of them.",
            "hints": "Picture this special cloud floating above your leader. It's probably just a speaker attached to a drone covered in cotton balls.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Transmit",
                "Alternative": "Tell"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3067\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u305f, \u3064\u3066",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You highly doubt this is a magical cloud that can transmit messages. You inch closer to the big dent and try to poke it. Your finger goes right in! Hmm, you're still pretty sure there's a trick to this thing.",
                "mnemonic": "As the leader {tooltip:Kanji:transmit}s his latest series of messages to you and the others, you notice a pretty large {tooltip:Reading:den}t ({span:lang=ja:\u3067\u3093}) in it. That dent is probably a clue to what this cloud is really made of."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Even a {tooltip:Radical:simple} {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} can start a {tooltip:Kanji:war}. In fact, it's really common for one simple drunk person to offend an entire country into declaring war.",
            "hints": "Think about all of the people you know. You can picture at least one of them getting drunk and, I dunno, sending out a simple drunk tweet that starts the next world war. \u00af\\_({span:lang=ja:\u30c4})_/\u00af",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "War",
                "Alternative": "Battle"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
