                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the war of humans vs centaurs. Do you really think the humans will win? Centaurs are really powerful and they have all of the same high tech weapons as us AND horse legs.",
                "mnemonic": "Welp, you woke up this morning and now you're at {tooltip:Kanji:war} with the {tooltip:Reading:cen}taurs ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}). This is especially unfortunate, because the centaurs are really good at {tooltip:Kanji:battle}s because they're all automatically cavalry troops."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits your {tooltip:Radical:skin} and creates smaller {tooltip:Kanji:wave}s. Those hit you too!",
            "hints": "If you\u2019ve ever been to the ocean or a large lake, you know what kind of forces even small waves can hit with. Now imagine the force with which a tsunami wave would strike you. You\u2019d have the wind knocked out of you for sure.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wave"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The waves are basically punching you in the gut, forcing the air out of your lungs, and making you shout HA!",
                "mnemonic": "When each {tooltip:Kanji:wave} hits your body, you shout, \"{tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f})!\" It's not like it's on purpose. When the wave crashes into you, the wind gets knocked right out of your mouth, making a HA sound."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:sheep} rides a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} in classic {tooltip:Kanji:Western style}. And by Western style I mean the sheep is dressed in a cowboy outfit and has put a saddle atop the tsunami wave to ride it. It\u2019s a tsunami rodeo and this crazy sheep is riding that tsunami wave in classic Western style. ",
            "hints": "Imagine how ridiculous a sheep would look all decked out in Western style cowboy gear. Now imagine it riding a tsunami wave as it screams, \u201cBaa~ baa~ baa~!\u201d",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Western Style",
                "Alternative": "Ocean"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself eating this Western style apple pie yogurt. It tastes just like apple pie only creamier and fruitier. Taste the sweet yogurt in your mouth as you imagine yourself scarfing some down.",
                "mnemonic": "After a whole day of riding this tsunami, the sheep is hankerin\u2019 for some {tooltip:Kanji:Western style} food. This sheep loves {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}). And its favorite flavor is Western style apple pie yogurt. America loves its apple pie and this sheep loves Western style apple pie flavored yogurt."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} with a lot of {tooltip:Radical:power} can move {tooltip:Radical:heavy} things with hardly any {tooltip:Kanji:work}. By power, I mean a lot of strength because this leader is very strong and moving heavy things is no problem for her. Her power allows the leader to move heavy things with little to no work at all.",
            "hints": "Picture this powerful leader, muscles flexing as she picks up heavy things and casually tosses them aside. How does she maintain so many muscles?{splitParent}Note - there are a few other kanji that have a similar meaning to this one. This kanji is used in words that refer to doing work, with a focus on movement or physical operation of a device.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Work"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3069\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u305f\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself eating one of these power doughnuts. It\u2019s delicious. Doughnuts are fantastic. Taste the fresh doughnut in your mouth as it crumbles and melts on your tongue. It\u2019s the best doughnut you\u2019ve ever had.",
                "mnemonic": "Where does this leader\u2019s power come from? {tooltip:Reading:Dou}ghnuts ({span:lang=ja:\u3069\u3046}). She eats nothing but doughnuts. She has a special crew of bakers that {tooltip:Kanji:work} for her in his castle and they work all day to make the leader doughnuts of power. They are imbued with many secret ingredients that give the leader the power to move anything, no matter how heavy it is."
            }
        }

