                        "file": "28431-subject-3289.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun'yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you to remember: \n{splitParent}What do you use your {tooltip:Vocabulary:finger} for the most? For pointing, of course! Imagine going up to people and saying, \"What will {tooltip:Reading:you be} ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3073}) when you grow up?\" Point your finger at the next person, \"What will you be?\" Keep going until you're just saying, \"You be? You be?\" with your finger out.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6307\u304c\u304d\u308c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "You have such beautiful fingers."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3048\u3048\u3063\u3001\u3053\u306e\u9593\u6307\u306e\u3048\u304c\u304d\u65b9\u306e\u30ec\u30c3\u30b9\u30f3\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u3066\u304b\u3089\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u30f6\u6708\u3082\u305f\u3063\u305f\u306e\uff01\uff1f",
                    "en": "Wow. It's already been a month since I took the lesson of drawing fingers last time, huh?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7a81\u7136\u4e2d\u6307\u304c\u75db\u304f\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "I just had a sudden pain in my middle finger."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
