{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:return} the {tooltip:Kanji:doing}s of another person, you're doing it to {tooltip:Vocabulary:get even} (whether it's a nice thing or a mean thing).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Getting Even",
                "Alternatives": "Getting Back At, Retaliation, Revenge",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u304b\u3048\u3057"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u304b\u3048\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3887-subject-3482.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u304b\u3048\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28283-subject-3482.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are a bit weird, here. {span:lang=ja:\u4ed5} gets its on'yomi reading... you should be okay with that. {span:lang=ja:\u8fd4\u3057} gets the kun'yomi reading, though, which is the reading you saw with the word {span:lang=ja:\u8fd4\u3059} in level 9. You can tell this part uses the kun'yomi vocab reading because it has that hiragana attached to it. Just remember to distinguish between the two parts of the word to remember the readings.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304f\u3084\u3057\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3001\u306a\u3093\u304b\u4ed5\u8fd4\u3057\u3057\u305f\u3044\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "It was mortifying, so I wanna get even."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ad\u30e3\u30c3\u30c8\u30a6\u30fc\u30de\u30f3\uff01\u3042\u3093\u305f\u3063\u3066\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u6700\u4f4e\u306e\u5973\u3060\u306d\uff01\u3044\u3064\u304b\u4ed5\u8fd4\u3057\u3057\u3066\u3084\u308b\u308f\uff01",
                    "en": "Catwoman! You are so evil! I\u2019ll get you back soon!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d7\u30ea\u30f3\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3089\u308c\u305f\u4ed5\u8fd4\u3057\u306b\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u5927\u3059\u304d\u306a\u30e8\u30fc\u30b0\u30eb\u30c8\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3066\u3084\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I ate Koichi's favorite yogurt to get back at him for eating my pudding."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "God",
                "Alternative": "Gods",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u307f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4097-subject-3297.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28381-subject-3297.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}Do you know the word \"Kamikaze\"? Also, do you remember the word {span:lang=ja:\u98a8} from a previous level? Kamikaze means \"divine winds\" or \"godly winds.\" If you know the word \"Kamikaze\" you can apply it to this single word, that means \"god\" or \"gods.\" Use your prior knowledge to remember this reading.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u795e\u3092\u3057\u3093\u3058\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Do you believe in gods?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u795e\u3092\u3044\u3064\u307e\u3067\u5f85\u305f\u305b\u308b\u3064\u3082\u308a\u306a\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "How much longer will you make God wait?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u795e\u69d8\u306f\u6c34\u306e\u4e0a\u3092\u6b69\u3051\u308b\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u4ffa\u306f\u9678\u306e\u4e0a\u3092\u6cf3\u3050\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3093\u3060\u305c\u3002",
                    "en": "God may be able to walk on water. But I can swim on land."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

