                        "file": "28481-subject-3499.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from the vocab words {span:lang=ja:\u4f7f\u3046} and {span:lang=ja:\u65b9}. So long as you're okay with those you can apply that knowledge over here.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3046\u5c11\u3057\u3001\u8a00\u8449\u306e\u4f7f\u3044\u65b9\u306b\u6c17\u3092\u4ed8\u3051\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3002",
                    "en": "You should be more careful about how you use language."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30a4\u30d5\u30a9\u30f3\u306e\u4f7f\u3044\u65b9\u304c\u5206\u304b\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I don't know how to use iPhones."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u4ed5\u4e8b\u304c\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u4ffa\u306e\u72ac\u306b\u91d1\u69cc\u306e\u4f7f\u3044\u65b9\u3092\u8a13\u7df4\u3057\u3066\u307f\u3088\u3046\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m going to train my dog how to use a hammer and bring him to work with me."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8} means {tooltip:Kanji:attach} and words like {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u304f} mean \"to be attached.\" This has the same idea. When you see this attached to another word, for example, you might know that something is attached to something else, or perhaps {tooltip:Vocabulary:included} with it. For example, if you stay at a hotel room, maybe it is a breakfast{span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u304d}, i.e. \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:including} breakfast.\"",
