{
            "mnemonic": "You know the kanji part means {tooltip:Kanji:begin}. The {span:lang=ja:\u306b} on the end refers to a direction. So, think of this like \"the direction of the beginning\" which would be where things all started. That's why this word/phrase means \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:in the beginning}.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "In The Beginning",
                "Alternatives": "To Begin With, To Start With",
                "Word Type": "expression"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3058\u3081\u306b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3058\u3081\u306b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20407-subject-3099.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3058\u3081\u306b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40316-subject-3099.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is kun'yomi (look at all that hiragana!) but that's the reading you learned with the word {span:lang=ja:\u59cb\u3081\u308b}, so have no fear, you got it!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3082\u3093\u3060\u3044\u3067\u306f\u3001\u59cb\u3081\u306b\u3057\u3064\u3082\u3093\u3092\u304d\u3044\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "For this problem, please begin by listening to the question."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u59cb\u3081\u306b\u30ab\u30ca\u30a8\u304c\u305f\u3093\u751f\u65e5\u30b1\u30fc\u30ad\u306b\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3086\u3092\u3053\u307c\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u4ee5\u5916\u306f\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u30b5\u30d7\u30e9\u30a4\u30ba\u30d0\u30fc\u30b9\u30c7\u30fc\u30d1\u30fc\u30c6\u30a3\u30fc\u306f\u5927\u305b\u3044\u3053\u3046\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi's surprise birthday party went really well except that Kanae spilled soy sauce on his birthday cake in the beginning."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8056\u66f8\u306e\u4e00\u756a\u59cb\u3081\u306b\u306f\u4f55\u304c\u66f8\u304b\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "What are the first words at the beginning of the Bible?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your \"{tooltip:Kanji:doing} {tooltip:Kanji:action}s\" are the things you do. What do you say when someone asks \"what you do\"? You tell them what your {tooltip:Vocabulary:job} is.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Job",
                "Alternatives": "Work, Occupation",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3054\u3068"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3054\u3068",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3816-subject-3500.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3054\u3068",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28254-subject-3500.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses the on'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4ed5} and the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4e8b}. Please note that {span:lang=ja:\u4e8b} uses the reading {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3068}, which you didn't learn with the kanji, but you have come across it once or twice by now, and because of the way rendaku works, it's changed to the voiced {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3068}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u306f\u3001\u4ea4\u901a\u3072\u3053\u307f\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Does this job reimburse transportation costs?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8d64\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u306f\u6ce3\u304f\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The business of a baby is to cry."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u6642\u9593\u5185\u306b\u3001\u3053\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3092\u7d42\u3048\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3046\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3055\u3042\u3001\u305d\u308c\u306f\u3069\u3046\u304b\u306a\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Do you think we can finish this work in time?\" \"Well I wouldn\u2019t bet on it.\""
