                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28465-subject-3272.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u793e\u9577\u306f\u3001\u8089\u4f53\u52b4\u50cd\u8005\u306e\u4e0d\u8db3\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u3069\u3046\u304a\u8003\u3048\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "What does president Koichi think about the shortage of blue-collar workers?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e00\u4f53\u3001\u304a\u524d\u3068\u52b4\u50cd\u8005\u305f\u3061\u306e\u9593\u306b\u3001\u4f55\u304c\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "What happened between you and all the laborers?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u30b3\u30d4\u30fc\u6a5f\u4f7f\u308f\u305b\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3044\u3044\uff1f\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u52b4\u50cd\u8005\u3092\u96c7\u3046\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u30c1\u30e9\u30b7\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "Can I use the photocopier? I\u2019m making up flyers to try to get new laborers."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji for this means {tooltip:Kanji:fate}... but what is your fate, really? Your fate is to live out your life the way you're being fated to live out your life. Then, when your {tooltip:Vocabulary:life} runs out, your fate runs out.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Life",
                "Word Type": "independent noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u306e\u3061"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u306e\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28443-subject-3273.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u306e\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4174-subject-3273.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word:  \n{splitParent}The Book of {tooltip:Reading:Enoch} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u306e\u3061}) has passed down your fate and told you how to use your {tooltip:Vocabulary:life}. You must read the book of Enoch and find out what you're supposed to do.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u308f\u305f\u3057\u305f\u3061\u307f\u3093\u306a\u306e\u547d\u306e\u304a\u3093\u4eba\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We all owe our lives to Koichi."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u306d\u304c\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3089\u3001\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u3067\u304b\u3093\u5b57\u3092\u3079\u3093\u5f37\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3088\u308a\u3082\u3054\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u547d\u3092\u5927\u5207\u306b\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please, please value your life more than learning kanji on WaniKani."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30bb\u30fc\u30e9\u30fc\u30e0\u30fc\u30f3\u306e\u547d\u304c\u5371\u306a\u3044\uff01",
                    "en": "Sailor Moon\u2019s life is in danger!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u597d} means {tooltip:Kanji:like} and this vocab word means the same thing: {tooltip:Vocabulary:like} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:love}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Like",
                "Alternatives": "Love, Likable, Lovable",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306a adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3059\u304d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4196-subject-3250.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28435-subject-3250.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Who do you {tooltip:Vocabulary:like} more than anyone? Your friend {tooltip:Reading:Sue}. If you know someone named Sue, pretend you like her. If you don't, think of a famous person you know named Sue and use her, pretending you're good friends that like each other a lot.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002\u3067\u3082\u3001\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u306f\u3082\u3063\u3068\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I like Tofugu, but I looove WaniKani."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u597d\u304d\u306a\u4eba\u3068\u5bb6\u3067\u30b4\u30ed\u30b4\u30ed\u3059\u308b\u306e\u304c\u5927\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I love just staying home and doing nothing with someone I love."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u307e\u307e\u306e\u541b\u304c\u597d\u304d\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3002\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3001\u4ed6\u306e\u3084\u3064\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u81ea\u5206\u3092\u304b\u3048\u3088\u3046\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u308c\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I like you just the way you are. So please don\u2019t try to change yourself for anyone."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Remember how you learned the words {span:lang=ja:\u6587\u5b57} and {span:lang=ja:\u901a\u308a}? Well an \"avenue\" made of \"letters\" is {tooltip:Vocabulary:literally} {tooltip:Vocabulary:to the letter}. Wink.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Literal",
                "Alternatives": "Literally, To The Letter",
                "Word Type": "adverb, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3058\u3069\u304a\u308a"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u3058\u3069\u304a\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28453-subject-7632.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u3058\u3069\u304a\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4278-subject-7632.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a combination of the words {span:lang=ja:\u6587\u5b57} and {span:lang=ja:\u901a\u308a}, which you learned already, so you should be able to read this one. Just make sure you remember that {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u304a\u308a} becomes {span:lang=ja:\u3069\u304a\u308a} because of rendaku.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u306f\u6587\u5b57\u901a\u308a\u3001\u300c\u5929\u624d\u300d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "He\u2019s literally a genius."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u793e\u3044\u3093\u306b\u306a\u308b\u306b\u306f\u3001\u6587\u5b57\u901a\u308a\u3068\u3046\u3075\u3068\u30d5\u30b0\u304c\u597d\u7269\u3067\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "In order to become an employee at Tofugu, you literally have to like tofu and fugu."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c4\u30f3\u30c7\u30ec\u3068\u306f\u3001\u6587\u5b57\u901a\u308a\u300c\u4eba\u524d\u3067\u306f\u30c4\u30f3\u30c4\u30f3\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3051\u3069\u4e8c\u4eba\u306e\u6642\u306f\u30c7\u30ec\u30c7\u30ec\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u300d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "\"Tsundere\" literally means \"when in public, he/she is cold but in private, he/she suddenly become love struck.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. This is a good way to start stories, by the way: {span:lang=ja:\u6614\u3005\u306b\u2026} (Long, long ago).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Long Ago",
                "Alternative": "Long Time Ago",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3080\u304b\u3057"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3080\u304b\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3818-subject-3279.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3080\u304b\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28231-subject-3279.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji. {span:lang=ja:\u3080\u304b\u3057} sounds like a kun'yomi reading, doesn't it? It's so long.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u6614\u306f\u3051\u3093\u3051\u3093\u3092\u3059\u308b\u306e\u304c\u3068\u304f\u610f\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi used to be good at hopping on one leg a long time ago."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6614\u3001\u4e00\u56de\u3060\u3051\u3001\u53f3\u8db3\u306b\u9b5a\u306e\u76ee\u304c\u3067\u304d\u305f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I got a corn on my right foot once a long time ago."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3001\u4eca\u591c\u306e\u4e88\u5b9a\u306f\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u6614\u306e\u98f2\u307f\u4ef2\u9593\u3068\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u51fa\u304b\u3051\u3066\u304f\u308b\u4e88\u5b9a\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"What are your plans for tonight Darling?\" \"I\u2019m going out with my old drinking buddies.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've hopefully come across {span:lang=ja:\u8ca0\u3051\u308b} by now, which means \"to lose.\" So, you can figure out this word means \"losing dog.\" Well, calling someone a dog isn't so nice, so you're probably just calling them a {tooltip:Vocabulary:loser}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Loser",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3051\u3044\u306c"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u3051\u3044\u306c",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3981-subject-3502.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u3051\u3044\u306c",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28343-subject-3502.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are kun'yomi, but you should be familiar with {span:lang=ja:\u8ca0\u3051\u308b} and of course {span:lang=ja:\u72ac} well enough to learn the reading here.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u3001\u4e00\u65e5\u4e2d\u5bb6\u306b\u3044\u3066\u3001\u30c6\u30ec\u30d3\u3070\u3063\u304b\u308a\u307f\u3066\u308b\u8ca0\u3051\u72ac\u3060\u3063\u3066\u3053\u3068\u306f\u81ea\u304b\u304f\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm aware that I'm a loser who loves to just stay home and watch TV all day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u8ca0\u3051\u72ac\u304c\u660e\u65e5\u304b\u3089\u304a\u308c\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3092\u5f15\u304d\u3064\u3050\u3068\u304b\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u304c\u307e\u3093\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I can't stand the fact that the loser is taking over my job tomorrow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u8ca0\u3051\u72ac\u3081\uff01\u30ad\u30e2\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "You are a loser and really creepy!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:low}? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:low}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Low",
                "Alternative": "Short",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3072\u304f\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3072\u304f\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4212-subject-3258.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3072\u304f\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28439-subject-3258.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You look down and very {tooltip:Vocabulary:low} to the ground is a man, looking up at you. Your friend is there too, but you don't know this little man. Your friend says \"{tooltip:Reading:He coo'}, he coo,\" referring to the low to the ground man.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f4e\u3044\u58f0\u306e\u7537\u306e\u4eba\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I like a guy with a low voice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u3080\u3059\u3081\u306f\u3001\u5e73\u304d\u3093\u3088\u308a\u3084\u3084\u8eab\u9577\u304c\u4f4e\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Our daughter is a little shorter than average."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u306d\u3047\u3001\u3086\u304d\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3002\u3042\u3093\u305f\u3001\u3042\u307e\u308a\u5143\u6c17\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3055\u305d\u3046\u306d\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3046\u3093\u3002\u305d\u3046\u306a\u306e\u3002\u4f4e\u8840\u5727\u75c7\u3063\u3066\u8a3a\u65ad\u3055\u308c\u305f\u308f\u3002\u300d\u300c\u4f55\u305d\u308c\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3064\u307e\u308a\u3001\u79c1\u306e\u8840\u5727\u304c\u3081\u3061\u3083\u304f\u3061\u3083\u4f4e\u3044\u3063\u3066\u3053\u3068\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3069\u308c\u304f\u3089\u3044\u4f4e\u3044\u306e\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3048\u3063\u3068\u3001\u4eca\u671d\u306f\u4e0a\u304c80\u3067\u4e0b\u304c40\u3050\u3089\u3044\u3060\u3063\u305f\u304b\u306a\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Hey, Yuki. You don\u2019t look so good.\" \"Yeah, I know. I was diagnosed with hypotension.\" \"What\u2019s that?\" \"It just means that my blood pressure is really, really low.\" \"How low is that?\" \"Well, this morning was about 80/40.\""
