{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:idea} you {tooltip:Kanji:see} in your head is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:opinion}. As the dude once said... \"That's just, like, your {span:lang=ja:\u610f\u898b}, man.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Opinion",
                "Alternative": "View",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3051\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3051\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4118-subject-3317.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3051\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28390-subject-3317.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is all on'yomi, meaning {span:lang=ja:\u610f} is just fine. {span:lang=ja:\u898b}'s on'yomi ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) is a reading you didn't learn with the kanji because it's so much less useful, but you do have to know it here. You've seen it with {span:lang=ja:\u767a\u898b} a couple levels ago, so that should help. Still, here's a mnemonic to help you remember:\n{splitParent}In this case, just think about how {tooltip:Reading:Ken} the samurai has an {tooltip:Vocabulary:opinion} on everything. Ken is such a know-it-all, and you're better off agreeing with his opinions. He's a samurai after all!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u610f\u898b\u306e\u51fa\u3057\u304a\u3057\u307f\u306f\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u4e0b\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Don't hold your opinions back, please."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u304f\u3089\u4ef2\u306e\u826f\u3044\u53cb\u3060\u3061\u3067\u3082\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u6b63\u76f4\u306b\u306f\u610f\u898b\u3057\u3065\u3089\u3044\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Even though they were my close friends, I would probably have difficulty openly telling them about this."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u308c\u306f\u4ffa\u306e\u500b\u4eba\u7684\u306a\u610f\u898b\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u305f\u307e\u306b\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u306f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u5909\u308f\u3063\u305f\u56fd\u3060\u306a\u3041\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "This is just my personal opinion, but I sometimes think that Japan is a really weird country."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:pour} {tooltip:Kanji:writing} onto a form. You're filling out this form to {tooltip:Vocabulary:order} something new for yourself. It's a formal {tooltip:Vocabulary:request} to get this new thing (imagine it being something you're excited about ordering right now, and imagine yourself ordering it by pouring writing onto an order form).",
