                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28269-subject-7578.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5ea6} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you remember them together:\n{splitParent}In {tooltip:Vocabulary:preparation} for getting sheared, a {tooltip:Reading:shee}p will sit on a {tooltip:Reading:tack} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u305f\u304f}). This sheep tacking makes it so that the shearing part is nothing! Imagine watching some sheep {tooltip:Vocabulary:getting ready} by sitting on tacks. Yikes. You want to tell them being sheared doesn't hurt and that sheep tacking is worse, but something makes you think they won't listen to you.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5b66\u6821\u3078\u884c\u304f\u652f\u5ea6\u304c\u3067\u304d\u305f\u3089\u3088\u3093\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please call me when you've gotten ready for school."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bcd\u306f\u53f0\u6240\u3067\u5915\u306f\u3093\u306e\u652f\u5ea6\u3092\u3001\u7236\u306f\u90e8\u5c4b\u3067\u308a\u3087\u884c\u306e\u652f\u5ea6\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Mom is preparing dinner in the kitchen and dad is making arrangements for a trip in his room."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3064\u307e\u3067\u5bdd\u3066\u308b\u306e\uff01\u65e9\u304f\u8d77\u304d\u3066\u652f\u5ea6\u3057\u306a\u3055\u3044\uff01\uff01",
                    "en": "How long are you sleeping? Get up now and get ready!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

