                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. The {span:lang=ja:\u306f} from {span:lang=ja:\u6ce2} rendakus to {span:lang=ja:\u3071}, so be careful. Maybe it's your {tooltip:Reading:pa} who has bad reception every time you try to call him?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30d3\u30eb\u306f\u30b3\u30f3\u30af\u30ea\u3067\u3067\u304d\u3066\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001\u3080\u7dda\u306e\u96fb\u6ce2\u306f\u3068\u3069\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "This building is made of concrete, so it can't be penetrated by radio waves."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u516c\u304d\u3087\u3046\u306e\u96fb\u6ce2\u3067\u305d\u3093\u306a\u4e8b\u8a00\u3046\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3001\u6700\u4f4e\u3060\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "How could he say such things on public radio! Nasty jerk."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3054\u3081\u3093\u3001\u3088\u304f\u805e\u3053\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002\u3053\u3053\u306f\u96fb\u6ce2\u304c\u60aa\u3044\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Sorry, you sound kind of choppy. It seems like I\u2019ve got bad reception here."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Imagine someone {tooltip:Kanji:accept}ing something and then {tooltip:Kanji:attach}ing something. This person is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:receptionist}, because they are accepting the call, writing down the information, and then attaching said information to a sticky note for you to read. You say, \"No, I'm not available.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Receptionist",
                "Alternative": "Reception",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3051\u3064\u3051"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3051\u3064\u3051",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3946-subject-3511.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3051\u3064\u3051",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28342-subject-3511.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}For this reading you have to think back to the verb words that get used with this kanji, namely {span:lang=ja:\u53d7\u3051\u308b} and {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u3051\u308b}. Then just drop off the {span:lang=ja:\u308b}s and put them together. {span:lang=ja:\u53d7} becomes {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3051} and {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8} becomes {span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3051} and you're left with {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3051\u3064\u3051}. This is what's called a compound word. And now you know it. Nice!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u53d7\u4ed8\u306e\u5973\u305b\u3044\u3001\u5de6\u8db3\u306b\u5927\u304d\u306a\u9b5a\u306e\u76ee\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3089\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I heard that receptionist lady has a big corn on her left foot."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u660e\u65e5\u304b\u3089\u3001\u30b7\u30e5\u30ef\u3061\u3083\u3093\u304c\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u53d7\u4ed8\u3092\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Arnold Schwarzenegger will be Tofugu's receptionist starting tomorrow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3048\uff1f\u77e5\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3002\u53d7\u4ed8\u3067\u805e\u3044\u3066\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "Huh? I don\u2019t know. Didn't someone at reception explain it to you?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
