                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28274-subject-3276.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u82b1\u706b\u5927\u4f1a\u306e\u65e5\u306b\u3001\u3086\u304b\u305f\u3092\u304d\u3066\u6d77\u5cb8\u305e\u3044\u3092\u6b69\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u30ab\u30c3\u30d7\u30eb\u3092\u898b\u308b\u306e\u304c\u3059\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I like seeing couples walk along the seashore in yukata on days when there are fireworks."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6d77\u5cb8\u306b\u3042\u308b\u3044\u3044\u30ab\u30d5\u30a7\u3092\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3088\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3089\u4e00\u3057\u3087\u306b\u304a\u8336\u3057\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "I know a good cafe at the coast. Do you wanna get tea with me?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u4eca\u65e5\u3001\u79c1\u9054\u3068\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u6d77\u5cb8\u306b\u884c\u304b\u306a\u3044\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u307e\u305f\u306e\u6a5f\u4f1a\u306b\u3059\u308b\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Do you want to go to the seashore with us today?\" \"I\u2019ll go with you next time.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well - that is the unit of time, {tooltip:Vocabulary:second}.",
