                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "37393-subject-2819.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses the kun'yomi readings for both kanji, but you know them both now, so you should be able to read this too! One hint that this is a kun'yomi reading word is the hiragana in the center. It's like two separate words combined together, and when a word is a single kanji / a single kanji with hiragana attached it is usually kun'yomi. This is like two of those, combined.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u58f2\u308a\u624b\u306b\u3060\u307e\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was cheated by that vendor."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7a7a\u305c\u3093\u306e\u58f2\u308a\u624b\u5e02\u5834\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "This's the hottest seller's market ever."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u5bb6\u306e\u58f2\u308a\u624b\u306f\u3001\u300c\u8fd1\u6240\u306e\u4eba\u304c\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u3072\u3069\u3044\u3084\u3064\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u5bb6\u3092\u624b\u653e\u3059\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3057\u305f\u3093\u3060\u300d\u3068\u3001\u79c1\u306b\u8a71\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The guy selling that house told me he\u2019s selling it because his neighbor is a real jerk."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {span:lang=ja:\u306e} is there to indicate that it is the difference of something. For example this is like saying \"the {tooltip:Vocabulary:separate} ______\" or \"the {tooltip:Vocabulary:different} _____\" or \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:another} ______\". {span:lang=ja:\u5225} by itself just means separate, different, or another.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Separate",
                "Alternatives": "Different, Another, Separate Thing, Different Thing, Another Thing",
                "Word Type": "\u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3064\u306e"
