                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3042\u306e\u30e8\u30c3\u30c8\u306f\u7d20\u6575\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002\u7530\u4e2d\u3055\u3093\u306e\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f\u300d \u300c\u5144\u8cb4\u3068\u5171\u6709\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"That is a very nice yacht. Is that yours, Mr. Tanaka?\" \"I'm a co-owner with my brother.\""
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30ef\u30f3\u30d4\u30fc\u30b9\u306e\u30d5\u30a3\u30ae\u30e5\u30a2\u306f\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3068\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306e\u5171\u6709\u306e\u3056\u3044\u3055\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "These One Piece figures are the shared assets of Koichi and Viet."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5b50\u80b2\u3066\u306f\u3001\u3075\u3046\u3075\u9593\u3067\u3058\u3087\u3046\u307b\u3046\u3092\u304d\u3061\u3093\u3068\u5171\u6709\u3057\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u4e0a\u624b\u304f\u884c\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Raising a kid works better when husbands and wives share information properly."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:way}/{tooltip:Kanji:road} of the {tooltip:Kanji:god}(s) is, as you can probably guess, a big Japanese religion. There's two, and I'll give you a hint, this one isn't Buddhism (that would probably have the kanji for Buddha in it, no?). So what's the other big one? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:Shinto}. If you're having trouble remembering this because you've never heard of it before, skip to the reading. The reading will help.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shinto",
                "Alternative": "Shintou",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093\u3068\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3093\u3068\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4208-subject-3298.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3093\u3068\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28428-subject-3298.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is a bit wonky. {span:lang=ja:\u795e} should be no problem. {span:lang=ja:\u9053} on the other hand is almost the one you learned ({span:lang=ja:\u3069\u3046}) but now it's {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046} for some reason. Perhaps the gods took away the dakuten to make it {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046}, who knows. All I know is that it's best not to question said gods. If you already know of Shinto in English, though, this reading should be really easy. If you don't, perhaps you can use this reading to help you to remember Shinto the religion.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u308c\u306f\u3001\u795e\u9053\u306e\u304e\u3057\u304d\u306e\u4e00\u3064\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This is one Shinto ritual."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u306e\u3046\u306e\u591c\u3001\u3072\u305f\u3059\u3089\u795e\u9053\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u8a9e\u308b\u3086\u3081\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Last night, I had a dream that I was just explaining Shinto to Koichi forever."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u795e\u9053\u306b\u306f\u7d76\u5bfe\u7684\u306a\u795e\u304c\u3044\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Why doesn\u2019t Shinto have an absolute God?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:God} {tooltip:Kanji:company}... think of this as \"what 'company' does the god's work?\" Well, the answer to that is a shrine, probably. In this case a {tooltip:Vocabulary:Shinto Shrine} because of the {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093} in the {span:lang=ja:\u795e}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shinto Shrine",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3093\u3058\u3083"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3058\u3093\u3058\u3083",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4127-subject-3299.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3058\u3093\u3058\u3083",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28395-subject-3299.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}But wait! {span:lang=ja:\u795e} is read {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093} in this word for some reason. Darn them gods, always messing around, adding dakuten. Maybe this will help, though: Imagine yourself at a Shinto Shrine. You are praying to the Gods, asking for food. Out from the sky rains {tooltip:Reading:Ginger} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093\u3058\u3083}). You are pelted with it and not sure if you should be happy or upset.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u795e\u793e\u306b\u521d\u3082\u3046\u3067\u306b\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3068\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u304c\u306a\u3050\u308a\u5408\u3044\u306e\u3051\u3093\u304b\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "When I visited a shinto shrine at the beginning of the new year, I saw Koichi and Viet having a fist fight."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u795e\u793e\u3067\u8cb7\u3063\u305f\u304a\u307e\u3082\u308a\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3001\u3059\u3063\u304b\u308a\u308f\u3059\u308c\u3066\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I totally forgot about the charm I bought at a shinto shrine in Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u3049\u3001\u4e2d\u3005\u30a4\u30b1\u3066\u308b\u81ea\u64ae\u308a\u3058\u3083\u3093\u3002\u3067\u3082\u3001\u304a\u524d\u3001\u306a\u3093\u3067\u5b66\u6821\u3058\u3083\u306a\u304f\u3066\u795e\u793e\u306b\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\uff1f",
                    "en": "Yo! Very cool selfie, but why were you in a shinto shrine instead of at school?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've hopefully seen {span:lang=ja:\u8cb7\u3046} by now and know it means \"to buy.\" So, {span:lang=ja:\u8cb7\u3044} is going to be similar to that. Add that to {tooltip:Kanji:thing} and you have a \"buying things\" sort of word. What does \"buying things\" describe? It describes {tooltip:Vocabulary:shopping}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shopping",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044\u3082\u306e"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3044\u3082\u306e",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28084-subject-3512.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3044\u3082\u306e",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3439-subject-3512.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are the kun'yomi, which is usually the case when there's hiragana in the middle. You learned the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u8cb7\u3044} when you learned the kanji, as well as the word {span:lang=ja:\u8cb7\u3046}, and you learned this reading of {span:lang=ja:\u7269} in the word {span:lang=ja:\u7269}!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u30b9\u30fc\u30d1\u30fc\u3067\u8cb7\u3044\u7269\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m shopping at the grocery store."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8cb7\u3044\u7269\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u30cd\u30c3\u30c8\u30b7\u30e7\u30c3\u30d4\u30f3\u30b0\u3067\u3059\u307e\u305b\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "As for shopping, I usually just do it online."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u30af\u30ea\u30b9\u30de\u30b9\u306e\u8cb7\u3044\u7269\u306b\u884c\u304f\u306e\uff01\u3059\u3054\u304f\u30ef\u30af\u30ef\u30af\u3059\u308b\u308f\uff01",
                    "en": "We\u2019re going Christmas shopping today! I\u2019m so excited!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

