{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:language} about {tooltip:Kanji:thing}s. This is a confusing one. Just think of it more like someone talking about things, anything, really. Someone who just talks about things is someone who tells stories. So, this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:tale} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:story} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:legend} (not the Tom Cruise one, though).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tale",
                "Alternatives": "Story, Legend",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3082\u306e\u304c\u305f\u308a"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u306e\u304c\u305f\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3754-subject-3213.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3082\u306e\u304c\u305f\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28224-subject-3213.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Both kanji take the kun'yomi here. For {span:lang=ja:\u7269}, that's {span:lang=ja:\u3082\u306e}, which you learned with the vocabulary {span:lang=ja:\u7269}. You learned the kun'yomi for {span:lang=ja:\u8a9e} with the verb {span:lang=ja:\u8a9e}\u308b, but here it becomes {span:lang=ja:\u304c\u305f\u308a} because of rendaku, and the {span:lang=ja:\u308a} is tucked inside the kanji.\n{splitParent}Maybe you've already heard the word {span:lang=ja:\u3082\u306e\u304c\u305f\u308a} too. It's in some film and book names. If you haven't, and you find this reading hard to remember, think of a story about an infamous {tooltip:Reading:Gatling} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u305f\u308a}) gun that wandered the land, mowing everything down in its path. It's a terrible legend, but what if it were true???\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u7269\u8a9e\u306e\u4e3b\u4eba\u516c\u306b\u3067\u3082\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3064\u3082\u308a\u3067\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3060\u308d\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "I think she's acting like she's the main character of a story."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7af9\u3068\u308a\u7269\u8a9e\u306f\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u6709\u540d\u306a\u7269\u8a9e\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter is a famous Japanese legend."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u7269\u8a9e\u3092\u66f8\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002\u60b2\u3057\u3044\u5b50\u72ac\u30d5\u30a7\u30c1\u306e\u7537\u306e\u8a71\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m writing a story right now. It\u2019s about a sad guy who is obsessed with puppies."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

