                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: \n{splitParent}You may have the ability to {tooltip:Vocabulary:taste} things now, but just wait until you get up there in {tooltip:Reading:age} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3058}). You'll find that the tastes and flavors you once liked will become bland, and you'll need a lot of Sriracha to make things taste better.\n"
