                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "44084-subject-8939.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be the kun'yomi reading, which you didn't learn with the kanji. Here's a mnemonic to help:\n{splitParent}You are moving your lawsuit forward against Sue. But now she says that YOU'RE the problem. \"{tooltip:Reading:Sue, sue me},\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3059\u3081}) you say as you continue to advance the lawsuit. Make sure to say \"me\" like \"mehh,\" in a really snobbish way.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u7814\u7a76\u3092\u9032\u3081\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306e\u52a9\u8a00\u3092\u3057\u3066\u4e0b\u3055\u3063\u3066\u3001\u3042\u308a\u304c\u3068\u3046\u3054\u3056\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Thank you for giving us advice on advancing our research."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u96ea\u3058\u3083\u3001\u3053\u308c\u4ee5\u4e0a\u5de5\u4e8b\u3092\u9032\u3081\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "With this snow, we can't move the construction forward anymore."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30da\u30fc\u30b9\u3067\u4f5c\u696d\u3092\u9032\u3081\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please move your work forward at the current pace."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
