{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:attempt} or {tooltip:Kanji:try}. The verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to attempt} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to try out}. Why don't you try out the meaning of this verb, while you're at it?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Attempt",
                "Alternatives": "To Try Out, To Test, To Test The Limits, To Try",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3081\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3081\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20742-subject-4148.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3081\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30118-subject-4148.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Okay. Here's the deal. We have this wild animal. I want you {tooltip:Vocabulary:to attempt} to {tooltip:Reading:tame} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3081}) it. Now, imagine trying to tame this wild animal. Yeehaw!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u85ac\u3092\u8a66\u3057\u3066\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'll try out this medicine."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u306e\u304f\u3089\u3044\u901f\u304f\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u65e9\u53e3\u8a00\u8449\u3092\u8a00\u3048\u308b\u304b\u3001\u8a66\u3057\u3066\u307f\u3088\u3046\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Let's try to see how fast we can say Japanese tongue twisters."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8098\u3092\u8210\u3081\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3069\u3046\u304b\u306f\u5206\u304b\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u8a66\u3057\u306b\u3084\u3063\u3066\u307f\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I don\u2019t know if I can lick my elbow, but I\u2019ll give it a try."
