                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}When you were raised, you were raised completely on {tooltip:Reading:soda} ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3060}). That's all you drank. No water, no juice... just tons and tons of soda. Imagine this.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u6771\u4eac\u3067\u751f\u307e\u308c\u80b2\u3061\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was born and raised in Tokyo."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306f\u3068\u3066\u3082\u304d\u3073\u3057\u3044\u5bb6\u3066\u3044\u3067\u3001\u30d9\u30fc\u30b3\u30f3\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3066\u80b2\u3061\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was raised on bacon in a very strict household."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u660e\u6cbb\u795e\u5bae\u304c\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3082\u597d\u304d\u306a\u306e\u3002\u68ee\u304c\u3001\u81ea\u7136\u306e\u68ee\u3068\u3057\u3066\u80b2\u3064\u3088\u3046\u306b\u8a08\u7b97\u3057\u3066\u9020\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u3057\u3001\u81ea\u7136\u7684\u306a\u7a7a\u9593\u306a\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "I really like the Meiji Shrine because its forest was carefully designed to mimic a natural forest and because of that it\u2019s beautiful and has a very natural atmosphere."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You hopefully know the word {span:lang=ja:\u8fd4\u3059}, which means \"to return\" (as in, you're doing the direct action of returning something). This word, on the other hand, is the version where something just returns (and you're not doing the action of returning). Use the {span:lang=ja:\u308b} to help you to remember this. {span:lang=ja:\u308b} the Kangaroo is returned to you. You don't do any of the returning, it just happens or someone else does it. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be returned}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Returned",
                "Alternatives": "To Return, To Come Back",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3048\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4162-subject-3490.ogg"
