{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:pass through} but we already know the word {span:lang=ja:\u901a\u308b} which means to pass through. This word means a different kind of passing through, like how you pass through the halls of your school everyday. But we don't say to pass through school, we say {tooltip:Vocabulary:to attend} school, or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to commute} to school.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Commute",
                "Alternatives": "To Attend, To Go Back And Forth",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3088\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3088\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3868-subject-7514.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3088\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28262-subject-7514.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use one of the kun'yomi readings. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You live in the middle of three different school districts so you need to decide which of the three schools you want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to attend}. You decide you don't mind that you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to commute} to the farthest of the three because their mascot is Wile E. {tooltip:Reading:Coyo}te ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3088}). He's your favorite Looney Toon because he always has the energy {tooltip:Vocabulary:to go back and forth} after that road runner.\n\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3048\u3063\u3001\u5317\u6d77\u9053\u304b\u3089\u304a\u304d\u306a\u308f\u307e\u3067\u6bce\u65e5\u901a\u3063\u3066\u308b\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "What!? Are you going back and forth between Hokkaido and Okinawa every day?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u307e\u3067\u30cf\u30fc\u30ec\u30fc\u3067\u901a\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi commutes to the Tofugu office on a Harley\u2010Davidson."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u59b9\u306f\u3001\u56db\u6708\u304b\u3089\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u5b66\u5712\u306b\u901a\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My younger sister will attend Tofugu Academy starting in April."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:compete} so the verb vocab version means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to compete}.",
