                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28261-subject-3287.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji. Nicely done!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3059\u3066\u308b\u795e\u3042\u308c\u3070\u62fe\u3046\u795e\u3042\u308a\u3002",
                    "en": "When one God gets rid of you, another picks you up."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u3048\u308a\u306b\u3042\u305d\u3053\u306e\u6b69\u9053\u3067\u4e94\u767e\u5186\u7389\u3092\u62fe\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I found a 500 yen coin on that sidewalk on the way back home."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3060\u308c\u304b\u304c\u9053\u7aef\u306b\u30bd\u30d5\u30a1\u3092\u6368\u3066\u3066\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u307e\u3060\u4f7f\u3048\u305d\u3046\u3060\u3063\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3001\u62fe\u3063\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Someone threw a couch away on the side of the road, but it still looked useful, so I picked it up."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:finger}. So, if you \"to finger\" something, what are you doing? You're pointing. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to point}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Point",
                "Alternative": "To Point At",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
