                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You are pointing at something in fear. It is a {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}). Thing is, you're pointing at this saw with a missing finger. It just cut off your finger and you're freaking out, trying to point with a bloody non-finger.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u77e2\u3058\u308b\u3057\u306f\u3001\u3069\u3061\u3089\u306e\u65b9\u5411\u3092\u6307\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Which way is the arrow pointing?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eba\u3092\u6307\u3067\u6307\u3059\u306e\u306f\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u3067\u306f\u5931\u793c\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "In Japan, it's rude to point at people with your finger."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3042\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u8272\u76f2\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u3069\u3063\u3061\u304c\u8d64\u8272\u3067\u3069\u3063\u3061\u304c\u7dd1\u8272\u304b\u3092\u6307\u3059\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3067\u304d\u307e\u305b\u3093\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Oh, you\u2019re color blind, eh? So that means you can\u2019t point at which one is red and which one is green, then."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
