                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You are going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to pour} some {tooltip:Reading:sauce} ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u305d}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3057\u304b\u3057\u3066\u3001\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u30b3\u30fc\u30e9\u306b\u725b\u306b\u3085\u3046\u6ce8\u3044\u3060\uff1f",
                    "en": "Did you pour milk in my coke by any chance?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u4eca\u5e74\u306fAKB48\u3092\u304a\u3046\u3048\u3093\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u5168\u529b\u3092\u6ce8\u3044\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi is pouring all of his energy into supporting AKB48 this year."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3082\u3046\u5c11\u3057\u30ef\u30a4\u30f3\u3092\u6ce8\u3044\u3067\u3044\u305f\u3060\u3051\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3082\u3061\u308d\u3093\u3002\u201c\u305d\u3053\u307e\u3067\u201d\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u306d\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3042\u3001\u305d\u3053\u307e\u3067\uff01\u305d\u308c\u304f\u3089\u3044\u3067\u7d50\u69cb\u3067\u3059\u3002\u6709\u96e3\u3046\u3054\u3056\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Can you pour some more wine for me, please?\" \"Sure. Just say when.\" \"Yes! There! That\u2019s perfect. Thank you.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:attach} your {tooltip:Kanji:energy} (imagine someone suddenly looking up at something, attaching their energy to it), you have noticed or realized something. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to realize} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to notice}. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Realize",
                "Alternative": "To Notice",
                "Word Type": "godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3065\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3065\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4242-subject-3508.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3065\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28442-subject-3508.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from the {span:lang=ja:\u6c17} kanji (which you know) and the word {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u304f} which you should know by now. Combine these together and you have the ability to read this word. Take note that the {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u304f} part is rendaku'd, though, so it is a tiny bit different.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c17\u4ed8\u304b\u306a\u3044\u3075\u308a\u306f\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Don't pretend like you didn't notice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u5b50\u3078\u306e\u304a\u3082\u3044\u306b\u6c17\u4ed8\u3044\u305f\u306e\u306f\u304b\u306e\u5973\u3068\u51fa\u4f1a\u3063\u3066\u4e09\u65e5\u76ee\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I think I realized my feelings for Koichiko three days after we met."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3093\u305f\u304c\u79c1\u306b\u30a2\u30a4\u30b9\u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30e0\u3092\u304f\u308c\u308b\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002\u3042\u3093\u305f\u304c\u305d\u3093\u306a\u306b\u512a\u3057\u3044\u306a\u3093\u3066\u4eca\u307e\u3067\u6c17\u4ed8\u304b\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u308f\uff01",
                    "en": "I can\u2019t believe you gave me your ice cream. I didn\u2019t realize that you were so kind until now."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:release} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to release}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Release",
                "Alternatives": "To Let Go, To Release Something, To Let Go Of Something",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u306a\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u306a\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4230-subject-3277.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u306a\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28427-subject-3277.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Imagine you are going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to release} something. It is a {span:lang=ja:\u82b1} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u306a}). You release it from your hand and it falls, hitting the ground in slow motion. You have the power to release and you are doing the releasing (versus {span:lang=ja:\u653e\u308c\u308b} where something is just released). You can remember this because even though you did the releasing of the flower, you're going to sue the pavement company for breaking your flower. It's all a big scam you're running.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u653e\u305b\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "Let go of me!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e09\u5341\u5206\u5f8c\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3064\u3044\u306b\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306e\u624b\u3092\u653e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi finally released Viet's hand after thirty minutes."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d5\u30b0\u3092\u6d77\u306b\u653e\u3059\u3068\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3001\u6cf3\u3044\u3067\u9003\u3052\u3061\u3083\u3063\u3066\u3001\u79c1\u304c\u547c\u3093\u3067\u3082\u77e5\u3089\u3093\u3077\u308a\u3059\u308b\u306e\u3002\u3069\u3046\u3059\u308c\u3070\u9003\u3052\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u306b\u6559\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u308b\u306e\u304b\u3057\u3089\u3002",
                    "en": "Every time I let Fugu loose in the sea, he swims off and when I call him he doesn\u2019t listen. What should I do to teach him to not run away?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:revolve}, and the verb version is when you make something revolve. You roll it. That's why this verb is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to roll something}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Roll Something",
                "Alternative": "To Turn Something Over",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u308d\u304c\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u308d\u304c\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "43575-subject-8932.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u308d\u304c\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "44098-subject-8932.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You learned this reading when you learned {span:lang=ja:\u8ee2\u304c\u308b}, but here's a mnemonic anyway just in case:\n{splitParent}When you try {tooltip:Vocabulary:to roll something}, the outside bits may be moving, but its {tooltip:Reading:core} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u308d}) stays still. Picture yourself making the earth roll across the floor. The outside parts where the people live are spinning round and round, but the earth's core is in exactly the same place.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ab\u30f3\u30b8\u30e5\u30fc\u30b9\u3092\u8ee2\u304c\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I rolled a can of juice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8d64\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306f\u4eba\u5f62\u3092\u304a\u3057\u3066\u8ee2\u304c\u3059\u306e\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "The baby likes pushing the doll to turn it over."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "Dung beetle\u306f\u3001\u30d5\u30f3\u3092\u8ee2\u304c\u3059\u3053\u3068\u304b\u3089\u300c\u30d5\u30f3\u30b3\u30ed\u30ac\u30b7\u300d\u3068\u8a00\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Dung beetles are called \u201cpoop rollers\u201d because they roll poop."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know the words {span:lang=ja:\u898b\u308b} and {span:lang=ja:\u9001\u308b} by now, hopefully. Here you're \"seeing\" the \"sending.\" You're seeing someone off, so this verb is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to see off}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To See Off",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307f\u304a\u304f\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307f\u304a\u304f\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3937-subject-3509.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307f\u304a\u304f\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28305-subject-3509.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from the vocab words {span:lang=ja:\u898b\u308b} and {span:lang=ja:\u9001\u308b}. Make sure you know those and you'll know this word's reading as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u7a7a\u3053\u3046\u307e\u3067\u898b\u9001\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I'll go to the airport to see you guys off."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u898b\u9001\u308b\u65b9\u3068\u898b\u9001\u3089\u308c\u308b\u65b9\u3063\u3066\u3001\u3069\u3063\u3061\u306e\u65b9\u304c\u3064\u3089\u3044\u3093\u3060\u308d\u3046\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I wonder which is harder, being the person who sees someone off or being one who is seen off by someone."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u5f7c\u3089\u3092\u898b\u9001\u3063\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u3069\u3063\u3068\u6d99\u306e\u96e8\u3092\u6d41\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi burst into tears after seeing them off."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've already been introduced to the word {span:lang=ja:\u82e6\u3057\u3044}. That word means painful, or agonizing. So, if you turn that into a verb, you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to suffer} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to struggle}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Suffer",
                "Alternative": "To Struggle",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304f\u308b\u3057\u3080"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304f\u308b\u3057\u3080",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4261-subject-3507.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
