                        "file": "28288-subject-3245.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be the kun'yomi reading, which you didn't learn with the kanji. Here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to transmit} a signal to the {tooltip:Reading:sta}rs ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u305f})! Trying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to tell} your message to anyone on earth would be too boring and too easy. Aim your message at the nearest star and transmit it into space!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u767a\u97f3\u3092\u305d\u306e\u307e\u307e\u30c0\u30a4\u30ec\u30af\u30c8\u306b\u306e\u3046\u306b\u4f1d\u3048\u308b\u304d\u304b\u3044\u3092\u767a\u660e\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu invented a machine that transmits Japanese pronunciation directly to your brain."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5148\u751f\u306b\u306f\u3001\u6388\u696d\u4e2d\u306b\u306d\u3080\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3046\u3050\u3089\u3044\u3064\u304b\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3063\u3066\u4e8b\u524d\u306b\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3068\u4f1d\u3048\u3066\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I told my teacher that I was so tired that I could have fallen asleep in his class earlier."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7236\u69d8\u3068\u304a\u6bcd\u69d8\u306b\u3082\u3001\u3088\u308d\u3057\u304f\u304a\u4f1d\u3048\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Please give your mother and father my regards."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:work}, and the verb version means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to work}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to labor}, and sometimes {tooltip:Vocabulary:to commit} (a crime).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Work",
                "Alternatives": "To Labor, To Commit",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u305f\u3089\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u305f\u3089\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3953-subject-3316.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u305f\u3089\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28299-subject-3316.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: If you are as mad as a {tooltip:Reading:hatter} you'll need {tooltip:Vocabulary:to work} very hard to regain your sanity. You know The Hatter from Alice in Wonderland? Imagine how hard he would have to work to be considered \"normal\".\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u982d\u306f\u30ac\u30f3\u30ac\u30f3\u3059\u308b\u3057\u3001\u304a\u306a\u304b\u306f\u30da\u30b3\u30da\u30b3\u3060\u3063\u305f\u304c\u3001\u4e00\u65e5\u4e2d\u50cd\u304b\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3044\u3051\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I had to labor through the day with a headache and an empty stomach."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u3067\u50cd\u304f\u305f\u3081\u306b\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u3092\u3079\u3093\u5f37\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm studying Japanese to work in Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u91d1\u66dc\u65e5\u3001Tofugu\u306e\u8a18\u4e8b\u3092\u8aad\u307f\u306b\u6765\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u884c\u304d\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u91d1\u66dc\u65e5\u306e\u591c\u306f\u9045\u304f\u307e\u3067\u50cd\u304b\u306a\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3051\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002\u300d\u300c\u305d\u308c\u306f\u6b8b\u5ff5\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3067\u306f\u3001\u307e\u305f\u4eca\u5ea6\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Would you like to come read Tofugu articles on Friday?\" \"I\u2019d like to but I have to work late Friday night.\" \"That\u2019s too bad. Maybe some other time.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know the kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:profit}. When you make it into a verb, though, it means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to work well}. If you think about it, when something works well it makes you a profit.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Work Well",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Possible, To Be Effective",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3788-subject-3267.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28228-subject-3267.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}What works so well? Your special {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) that can unlock anyone and anything's potential. Imagine putting it into a key slot in someone's back. Someone who's a good for nothing can't-do-anything is now an effective member of society! Go around using your key on other non-effective things and show them that anything is possible!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u8ee2\u8eca\u306e\u30d6\u30ec\u30fc\u30ad\u304c\u5229\u304b\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "My bike's brakes don't work well."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u3046\u3067\u306e\u5229\u304f\u308a\u3087\u3046\u308a\u4eba\u306b\u308a\u3087\u3046\u308a\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I had a skilled cook make food for me today."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u4e2d\u3005\u878d\u901a\u306e\u5229\u304f\u7537\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi is a pretty flexible man."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
