                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun'yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you to remember: You jump on a wave and ride around the world on it. It doesn't drop you off anywhere, until you reach a certain location: Viet{tooltip:Reading:nam} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u307f}). You jump off the wave and look at Vietnam. Imagine the most Vietnamese things you can think of to help you to make this wave-Vietnam association.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306e\u6ce2\u3001\u3059\u3054\u304f\u9ad8\u3044\u306d\u3002",
