{
            "mnemonic": "Imagining one\u2019s {tooltip:Radical:self} without a {tooltip:Radical:heart} can make it hard to draw {tooltip:Kanji:breath}. Without a heart, you\u2019d have no blood pumping and you would start to die. This would make it increasingly harder to draw breath and get oxygen to stay alive.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to live without a heart. You couldn\u2019t. Your blood stops flowing and your body shuts down. You would no longer be able to draw breath.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Breath"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine smelling this smelly sock. Imagine the smelly stench of the dirty sock wafting up into your nostrils and filling your lungs with its odor. Gross.",
                "mnemonic": "You know how when people are unconscious and their {tooltip:Kanji:breath} slows or comes to a stop, they use smelling salts to revive them? Well a smelly {tooltip:Reading:sock} ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u304f}) can work just as well. Socks get really stinky and their stench is powerful enough to revive someone who isn\u2019t drawing breath."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:stand} at a podium {tooltip:Radical:early} in the morning to practice reading the {tooltip:Kanji:chapter} from your latest book.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself, standing tall in the light of the early morning. You hold your head up high, open to your bookmark, and read the name of the chapter aloud: \"Chapter 42: The Most Important Number.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chapter"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself in a line with other authors, standing in the early morning, waiting to read chapters from your respective books. You really hope the Shougun likes yours. If he does, you'll be famous! If he doesn't, you might be beheaded.",
                "mnemonic": "You're practicing this specific {tooltip:Kanji:chapter} because you've been asked to read it for the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). There will be a bunch of other authors reading chapters of their books to him too, and you want to make a good impression."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're in a {tooltip:Radical:tent} eating {tooltip:Radical:beans} because you're trying to {tooltip:Kanji:climb} a mountain! When you climb, you sleep in a tent and eat only beans (the ultimate climbing food).",
            "hints": "Imagine climbing slowly and carefully up a cliff on the side of this mountain. Your tent and your beans are tied to your back, and you're letting out little farts with each step from all the beans you've been consuming.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Climb"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046, \u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e\u307c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh, what was the name of the {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} mountain you just worked so hard to climb? Mount Takao. (You should go climb it with your real body and see {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} with your real eyes sometime!)",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:climb} and climb and climb until you finally reach... {tooltip:Reading:\u3068\u3046}{span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046}! At the top of this mountain you've been climbing you can see all of {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. It's beautiful! It's breathtaking! All your climbing makes this view of {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} even more worthwhile!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:roof}, even though it's almost {tooltip:Radical:spring}, is still covered in {tooltip:Radical:ice} so it's {tooltip:Kanji:cold}. Inside the house is cold, outside the house is cold. Everything is cold!",
            "hints": "Picture the entire roof covered in ice. It's supposed to be spring right now, but it's too cold for the ice to melt off your roof.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cold"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
