                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The samurai isn't doing a good job stopping the cold, and soon he and his sword have frozen into your ice roof. So now it's cold and you have a dead samurai stuck to your house. Great.",
                "mnemonic": "You can't stand the {tooltip:Kanji:cold} anymore, so you hire a {tooltip:Reading:samu}rai to come try to hack the ice off of your roof with his sword. You stand outside shivering, and watching as the samurai tries to stab the ice off of your roof."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The force of a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} is enough to put a gash in a {tooltip:Radical:tree} about {tooltip:Radical:pi} (3.14) feet {tooltip:Kanji:deep}. Tsunamis are pretty powerful, so the force of the water alone is enough to cut into a tree several feet deep.",
            "hints": "Picture this tsunami wave hitting the tree. It\u2019s like a lumberjack axe of water, cutting deep into the tree with the force of a thousand lumberjacks.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Deep"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being deep in the woods and banging your shin on a stump you didn\u2019t see. It hurts to bang your shin, so imagine this pain and the awful sensation it brings.",
                "mnemonic": "Some tsunamis cut so {tooltip:Kanji:deep} that they flat out chop the tree right off its stump. In areas like this, you have to be careful not to bang a {tooltip:Reading:shin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}) on them. These stumps are right about shin height, so you want to be cautious when walking around them as to not injure yourself."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} who hires his own personal {tooltip:Radical:clown} will likely {tooltip:Kanji:double} his entertainment. Clowns are funny and make people laugh, so the leader decided to hire one. Since that time, the leader\u2019s amount of mirth has doubled. ",
            "hints": "Picture a clown and all the ridiculous funny things they do. Imagine the clown throwing a pie at someone\u2019s face and how funny that is. Chuckle to yourself and remember this kanji.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Double",
                "Alternatives": "Times, Multiply"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This clown has served its purpose. Wave your hand in the air and say bye-bye to this worthless clown.",
                "mnemonic": "When the clown stops being funny, it\u2019s time to say {tooltip:Reading:bye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u3044}). At first, the clown {tooltip:Kanji:double}d the leader\u2019s entertainment, but now the clown is just annoying. It\u2019s time to say bye-bye."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You\u2019ll have to {tooltip:Radical:excuse} me, having all this {tooltip:Radical:power} puts a lot of strain and {tooltip:Kanji:exertion} on my body. My power comes from exertion of muscle, so please excuse me if I start to perspire.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself under great exertion. You\u2019re attempting to use your power to move something and it\u2019s really requiring a lot of exertion to move. Picture yourself doing this action and imagine how difficult it is.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Exertion"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this Ben in your head. Ben always uses lots of exertion to do tasks. Imagine him using an unnecessary amount of power and exertion in carrying out normal everyday tasks.",
                "mnemonic": "Excuse me, I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve introduced myself yet. My name is {tooltip:Reading:Ben} ({span:lang=ja:\u3079\u3093}) and I use powerful muscle {tooltip:Kanji:exertion} to accomplish every task. Ben knows what Ben wants and how to get it. Remember that, kids."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A long time ago a huge {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} swept a {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} up into the {tooltip:Radical:moon} and {tooltip:Kanji:extinguish}ed its life.",
            "hints": "I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve heard many theories on how dinosaurs went extinct. Well, this is the real story. Imagine this poor triceratops and all his friends being extinguished by this powerful tsunami, sweeping them up into the moon where there's no air to breathe or leaves to eat.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Extinguish"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d, \u3051",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch the Shougun's eyes light up as an actor dressed like a tsunami crashes into an actor dressed as a triceratops and all of the lights on the stage are extinguished. Spooky...",
                "mnemonic": "This famous event where almost all life was {tooltip:Kanji:extinguish}ed is reenacted every year for the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). He's got a bit of an unhealthy obsession with extinguishing life..."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:tent} with a {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer} in it for the {tooltip:Kanji:festival}! Festivals need booths where people can do activities. In this tent, festival goers can use a jackhammer and make a lot of noise, perfect for a festival!",
            "hints": "Imagine being at a festival and waiting in line to ride the jackhammer. You don't want to eat candy apples or ride rides, you want to wait for the jackhammer tent.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Festival"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3064\u308a, \u307e\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine your cyborg going to this festival. Everyone here has some type of cyborg enhancement, like robotic arms, legs, or braces. Your cyborg is really excited to be around its people and play with jackhammers.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:festival} is for {tooltip:Reading:cy}borgs ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044}) only. Picture the cyborg you made getting excited that you're taking it to the festival. That's why all of the activities have to do with heavy machinery. The rides are mostly just cyborgs letting other people ride them, but it's still pretty fun."
            }
        }

{
