                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now Ryu is punching and kicking and tatsumaki senpukyaku-ing all of the trash into burnable and non-burnable piles. But the stream doesn't end. Now he's trying to get his other Street Fighter pals to help him beat it back!",
                "mnemonic": "Next to the trash {tooltip:Kanji:stream} you suddenly see {tooltip:Reading:Ryu} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3085\u3046}) from Street Fighter and he looks pissed. He's furious that so many people throw their trash in the river and it causes streams like this."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical {tooltip:Radical:suit} and the kanji {tooltip:Kanji:suit} are exactly the same! This kanji can also mean {tooltip:Kanji:join} which makes sense. When something suits you well, like a hat or something, it joins together with you quite well too. Join me, my hat! You suit my head well. It just {tooltip:Kanji:fit}s, you know?",
            "hints": "Just remember that this \"suit\" means \"to suit you\" - not the thing you wear, okay!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Suit",
                "Alternatives": "Fit, Join"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054\u3046, \u304c\u3063",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042, \u3042\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine you two standing next to each other, posing for a photograph. You two suit each other well. {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3046\u3044\u3061} with his gray beard, and you with your [well, you have to fill in this part by yourself].",
                "mnemonic": "You need someone who will {tooltip:Kanji:suit} you. Someone who can {tooltip:Kanji:join} you on your life journey. So you call Grandpa Koichi ({span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3046\u3044\u3061})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:building} has {tooltip:Radical:easy} access to {tooltip:Kanji:sunshine}. It's big and tall, so the {tooltip:Kanji:sunlight} shines right onto its roof.",
            "hints": "You're standing on top of the building as the sunshine comes down. Its warm light fills your entire body as it covers the building with ease.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sunshine",
                "Alternative": "Sunlight"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
