                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ha! Wouldn't you like to know why there are teeth in there? Ha. Ha ha. HA HA HA HA!",
                "mnemonic": "Why do I have a rice box full of {tooltip:Kanji:teeth}? {tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f})! Wouldn't you like to know. Ha! I definitely have an answer that isn't weird or creepy. Ha... ha ha..."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If someone with a {tooltip:Radical:gun} is headed your {tooltip:Radical:direction}, nock an {tooltip:Radical:arrow} in your bow and gather your {tooltip:Kanji:tribe} behind you because it\u2019s about to get real! This cretin with a gun is headed your direction and he doesn\u2019t even know what you and your tribe are gonna do to him. If he gets any closer, you\u2019re likely to shoot that arrow right at him.",
            "hints": "This guy headed your direction with his gun doesn\u2019t look friendly at all. Hear the sound of the bowstring as you nock your arrow and prepare your shot to defend yourself. Then imagine the sound of everyone in your tribe doing the same.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tribe",
                "Alternative": "Family"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305e\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You remember what a bosozoku is, right? We wrote about them on Tofugu a while ago. They\u2019re bike gang members and the \u201czoku\u201d in bosozoku means tribe. Remember that article when you see this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "When he starts to get closer, you notice that this guy is a boso{tooltip:Reading:zoku} ({span:lang=ja:\u305e\u304f}) bike gang member. Bosozoku means \u201crunning {tooltip:Kanji:tribe}\u201d and this guy is running right at you. With a gun. So gather your own tribe behind you and prepare to defend yourself against this bosozoku member."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If your friendly neighborhood {tooltip:Radical:tofu} takes a {tooltip:Radical:gun} and points it in your {tooltip:Radical:direction}, you might want to take a {tooltip:Kanji:trip}. This tofu obviously has something wrong with it. If it\u2019s taking a gun and pointing it in your direction, now\u2019s probably a good time to get away and take that trip you\u2019d been talking about.",
            "hints": "Imagine this menacing block of tofu threatening you with a gun. Guns are scary so you want to get away. Use images of your trip to make the thoughts of the big bad tofu and his gun fade away.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Trip",
                "Alternative": "Travel"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3073",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being stuck on a trip with a block of tofu that took your robe and is wearing it around, still pointing the gun in your face. This vacation has been ruined.",
                "mnemonic": "Your plan didn't work and the tofu went on your {tooltip:Kanji:trip} with you. And now it's wearing your hotel {tooltip:Reading:ro}be ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087})! It looks so comfortable, wrapped up in the robe. That's the best part of going on trips, and he stole it from you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "People who {tooltip:Radical:loiter} around the {tooltip:Radical:temple} are probably just trying to {tooltip:Kanji:wait}. They don't mean to look like they're up to no good, but it's hard to wait without looking suspicious when you're waiting outside a temple.",
            "hints": "Imagine waiting outside a temple. People are giving you looks. People think you're loitering, not just waiting innocently.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wait"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3044",
