                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself frying onions on this plate warmed by the sun. Smell the onion smell as the onion fumes get into your eyes and your sinuses. It makes your eyes water as you are very sensitive to onions.",
                "mnemonic": "The plate starts to get so {tooltip:Kanji:warm} that you could fry an {tooltip:Reading:on}ion ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3093}) on it. Who doesn\u2019t love fried onions? That plate sure is warm enough, so start cookin\u2019 \u2018em!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are {tooltip:Radical:sheep} right before your {tooltip:Radical:eye}s, because they just love what you {tooltip:Kanji:wear}. It's a little known fact that sheep are fashionistas, and they {tooltip:Kanji:arrive} daily to admire your style. These sheep are so stylish they wear their tail to one side - in the latest fashion (check out the sheep radical - the tail is sweeping stylishly to the left!).",
            "hints": "Imagine all the chic sheep lining up to check out your style, with their carefully coiffed left-hanging tails!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wear",
