            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u52d5\u7269\u306f\u82e6\u624b\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I don't like animals."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f55\u304b\u52d5\u7269\u306f\u304b\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Do you have any animals?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304c\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u52d5\u7269\u5712\u306b100\u5339\u306e\u91cd\u8981\u306a\u52d5\u7269\u3092\u96c6\u3081\u3066\u30d1\u30fc\u30c6\u30a3\u30fc\u3092\u958b\u50ac\u3057\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u4f55\u6545\u304b\u79c1\u306f\u62db\u5f85\u3055\u308c\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002\u79c1\u3082\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u306e\u91cd\u8981\u52d5\u7269\u306e\u4e00\u5339\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi hosted a party at the Tofugu Zoo for one hundred very important animals and for some reason, I wasn\u2019t invited. I thought I was one of the VIA to him too."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:chirp} {tooltip:Kanji:voice} is a sound an animal makes. Sure, it works for birds (which chirp), but it also works with most other animals as well. So, we call this an {tooltip:Vocabulary:animal cry}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Animal Cry",
                "Alternatives": "Animal Sound, Animal Noise, Chirp, Tweet, Roar, Bark, Meow",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304d\u3054\u3048"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306a\u304d\u3054\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4834-subject-3517.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306a\u304d\u3054\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28730-subject-3517.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are those that you learned with the kanji. {span:lang=ja:\u58f0} gets changed to {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3048}, though, so take note of that in your head. Perhaps you can imagine an animal that does a \"GOEEEEE\" cry.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u308a\u3093\u306e\u9cf4\u304d\u58f0\u3092\u805e\u3044\u305f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Have you ever heard what a giraffe sounds like?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5916\u304b\u3089\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u58f0\u304c\u805e\u3053\u3048\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u5c0f\u9ce5\u306e\u9cf4\u304d\u58f0\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I thought I heard Koichi outside, but it was a little bird's chirps."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u52d5\u8ca9\u58f2\u6a5f\u306e\u4e0b\u304b\u3089\u5b50\u72ac\u306e\u9cf4\u304d\u58f0\u304c\u805e\u3053\u3048\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I hear a puppy barking under the vending machine."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:hand} (or person, as you know {span:lang=ja:\u624b} often refers to a person) that {tooltip:Kanji:win}s gets to do {tooltip:Vocabulary:as one pleases}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "As One Pleases",
                "Alternatives": "One's Own Convenience, One's Own Way, One's Way",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306a adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
