                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3063\u3066",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28525-subject-3567.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this is weird. It's all kun'yomi, which luckily you've seen before, but still strange. I guess when you do {tooltip:Vocabulary:as one pleases} you can read kanji however you want, in this case the kun'yomi readings. Do note that there's a small {span:lang=ja:\u3063} in there before, presumably to connect the two readings of the two kanji together.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u307b\u3093\u3068\u3001\u52dd\u624b\u3060\u3088\u306d\uff01",
                    "en": "You are so selfish!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u52dd\u624b\u306a\u3053\u3068\u3070\u3063\u304b\u308a\u8a00\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "Don't say whatever you want."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30b5\u30fc\u30e2\u30f3\uff01\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u4e94\u56de\u3082\u6d6e\u6c17\u3057\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002\u305d\u3093\u306a\u7537\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3001\u4fe1\u3058\u3061\u3083\u30c0\u30e1\u3060\u3063\u3066\u3070\u3002\u300d\u300c\u5206\u304b\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3067\u3082\u3001\u5f7c\u3001\u79c1\u304c\u3044\u306a\u3044\u3068\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u3051\u306a\u3044\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u306e\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3058\u3083\u3042\u3001\u3082\u3046\u3001\u52dd\u624b\u306b\u3059\u308c\u3070\uff01\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Salmon! Fugu cheated on you five times. Never trust a guy like that.\" \"I know\u2026 but he says he can\u2019t live without me.\" \"Well, suit yourself then!\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:bad}? It's also {tooltip:Vocabulary:bad}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bad",
                "Alternatives": "Poor, Wrong",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u308f\u308b\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u308b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4786-subject-3357.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u308b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28706-subject-3357.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Do you know how in the Mario universe all the {tooltip:Vocabulary:bad} versions are called \"{tooltip:Reading:WARU}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u308f\u308b})? For example: \"WARUIJI\" and \"WARIO.\" That's because they are bad. They come from this kanji. So, if you ever need to remember this reading, just think back to Wario and Waruigi.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u98df\u3079\u653e\u3060\u3044\u306e\u3059\u3057\u5c4b\u306e\u305b\u3063\u5ba2\u306f\u3001\u3057\u3093\u3058\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u307b\u3069\u60aa\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "This all-you-can-eat sushi restaurant's customer service is unbelievably bad."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u60aa\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3053\u306e\u91ce\u3055\u3044\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u84b8\u3057\u3068\u3044\u3066\u304f\u308c\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "Sorry to bother you, but can you steam these veggies for me?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u725b\u4e73\u306f\u60aa\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3051\u3069\u3001\u4ffa\u306f\u6c17\u306b\u3057\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The milk went bad, but I didn\u2019t care."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

