                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28556-subject-3521.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u97f3} is the {span:lang=ja:\u97f3\u8aad\u307f}. {span:lang=ja:\u8aad\u307f} uses the kun'yomi, though, strangely. Way to mess up the one word that should be all on'yomi, Japan. Way. To. Go.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u6f22\u5b57\u306e\u97f3\u8aad\u307f\u3063\u3066\u4f55\u3060\u3063\u3051\uff1f",
                    "en": "What was the on'yomi for this kanji again?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u521d\u3081\u3066\u898b\u305f\u5730\u540d\u306f\u3075\u901a\u306f\u97f3\u8aad\u307f\u3057\u3061\u3083\u3046\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "We usually read place names that we see for the first time with on'yomi."
