                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3064\u304b\u306f\u3051\u3063\u3053\u3093\u3057\u3066\u3001\u3042\u305f\u305f\u304b\u3044\u5bb6\u5ead\u3092\u304d\u305a\u304d\u305f\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I want to get married and build a loving home someday."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u3057\u3085\u5473\u306f\u3001\u304b\u304f\u5bb6\u5ead\u304b\u3089\u51fa\u308b\u30b4\u30df\u3092\u3059\u624b\u3067\u3057\u3085\u3046\u96c6\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My hobby is to pick up each household member's waste with my bare hands."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u5973\u6027\u3068\u6bd4\u3079\u308b\u3068\u3001\u5916\u56fd\u306e\u5973\u6027\u306f\u5bb6\u5ead\u306e\u6642\u9593\u3068\u4ed5\u4e8b\u306e\u6642\u9593\u3092\u5206\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u306f\u3001\u304b\u306a\u308a\u53b3\u683c\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Compared to Japanese women, foreign women tend to be pretty strict about separating family time and working time."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:house} {tooltip:Kanji:tribe} is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:family}. They live in the same house as you and they're part of your \"tribe.\" This is closer than family, though (depending on how you look at family). This is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:immediate family} because these are the people you live with and give birth to, etc.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Family",
                "Alternative": "Immediate Family",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305e\u304f"
