{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:breath} {tooltip:Kanji:child} (that lets you release your breath when it's born) is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:son}. Nowadays it's cool to have a girl, but back in the day you wanted a son to carry on your underwater basket weaving legacy. That's why this is a son.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Son",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3080\u3059\u3053"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3080\u3059\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4425-subject-3324.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3080\u3059\u3053",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28552-subject-3324.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading of this is messed up. {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} is {span:lang=ja:\u3053}, that should be okay. {span:lang=ja:\u606f} is {span:lang=ja:\u3080\u3059} for some reason though. Why? Because you gave birth to a son, but he was a {tooltip:Reading:moose} ({span:lang=ja:\u3080\u3059}). You better hold that breath again, because this is not what you wanted.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u606f\u5b50\u304c\u660e\u65e5\u306e\u3057\u3051\u3093\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u4e00\u591c\u3065\u3051\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u305f\u3081\u3001\u4eca\u591c\u306f\u3068\u3066\u3082\u3057\u305a\u304b\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "Tonight is very quiet because my son is cramming for the exam tomorrow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u606f\u5b50\u306f\u3001\u3053\u3046\u308a\u3064\u3066\u304d\u306b\u50cd\u3044\u3066\u3060\u308c\u3088\u308a\u3082\u65e9\u304f\u305f\u3044\u793e\u3059\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "My son works efficiently and goes home earlier than anyone else."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5168\u304f\u3072\u3069\u3044\u606f\u5b50\u3092\u3082\u3063\u305f\u3082\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002\u3042\u3044\u3064\u306f\u6628\u591c\u4ffa\u306e\u30b1\u30fc\u30ad\u306e\u6b8b\u308a\u3092\u3053\u3063\u305d\u308a\u76d7\u307f\u98df\u3044\u3057\u3084\u304c\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "I have the most beastly son. He sneakily ate up the rest of my cake last night."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. Another meaning I'm going to add is {tooltip:Vocabulary:sports ball} because this is the word used for balls in various sports (soccer, baseball, etc).",
