                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28533-subject-3389.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are both the readings you learned with the kanji. Now you can spend a little more time drinking tea at a tea ceremony and a little less time trying to remember kanji readings.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u8336\u306e\u6e6f\u306e\u9053\u5177\u304c\u8cb7\u3048\u308b\u304a\u5e97\u3092\u3055\u304c\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm looking for a shop where I can buy tools for tea ceremonies."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u6c34\u306f\u3001\u8336\u306e\u6e6f\u306b\u3066\u304d\u3057\u305f\u6c34\u3068\u3057\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This water is known to be good for tea ceremony."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8336\u306e\u6e6f\u306e\u4e16\u754c\u306b\u306f\u3001\u300c\u4e00\u3064\u4e00\u3064\u306e\u51fa\u4f1a\u3044\u3092\u5927\u5207\u306b\u300d\u3068\u3044\u3046\u610f\u5473\u306e\u300c\u4e00\u671f\u4e00\u4f1a\u300d\u3068\u3044\u3046\u8a00\u8449\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\u3053\u306e\u8a00\u8449\u306f\u3001\u6620\u753b\u300c\u30d5\u30a9\u30ec\u30b9\u30c8\u30fb\u30ac\u30f3\u30d7\u300d\u306e\u526f\u30bf\u30a4\u30c8\u30eb\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3082\u4f7f\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "In the world of tea ceremonies there is a saying, \"Ichi-go ichi-e,\" which means \"to treasure every encounter.\" This saying was also used as the subtitle for Japan\u2019s release of Forrest Gump."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:warm} {tooltip:Kanji:degree}s is how many degrees warm it is in here. Of course, there can be very few warm degrees as well, making it very cold. What is all this? It's the {tooltip:Vocabulary:temperature}.",
