{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:stream}, but what in the world could \"to stream\" be (remember, there weren't streams of StarCraft II games back in the day when this word was made up)? Well, let's think water. If you're streaming water, it's going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to flow}. Alternatively, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to flush} works too.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Flow",
                "Alternatives": "To Flush, To Drain, To Pour, To Float, To Wash Away, To Set Afloat",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304c\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306a\u304c\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4771-subject-3333.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306a\u304c\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28700-subject-3333.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: What do you do with someone who is a {tooltip:Reading:nagger} (one who nags)? You have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to flush} them down the toilet. Imagine someone nagging you to do your chores so you flush them down the toilet, somehow.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30a4\u30ec\u306e\u6c34\u3001\u6d41\u3059\u306e\u308f\u3059\u308c\u305f\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "You forgot to flush the toilet, didn't you?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3042\u306e\u4eba\u305f\u3061\u304c\u306c\u307e\u5730\u306b\u3042\u3076\u3089\u3092\u6d41\u3057\u3066\u308b\u304b\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Do you know why they are pouring oil over the swamp?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u98a8\u7fd2\u306b\u3001\u6cb3\u8c5a\u306e\u5f62\u306b\u5207\u308a\u3068\u3063\u305f\u7d19\u3092\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u8a95\u751f\u65e5\u306b\u5ddd\u306b\u6d41\u3059\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3082\u306e\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "A Tofugu custom involves cutting paper into the shape of fugu and setting them afloat down a stream on Koichi\u2019s birthday."
