{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:Tokyo} {tooltip:Kanji:Metropolis} is, of course, the {tooltip:Vocabulary:Tokyo Metropolis}. Technically this is one of Japan's prefectures, but it's called a \"Metropolis\" instead. It's the capital and the largest city in all of Japan! ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tokyo Metropolis",
                "Alternatives": "Tokyo Metro, Tokyo Metropolitan Area, Tokyo Metro Area",
                "Word Type": "proper noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4856-subject-3350.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28723-subject-3350.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is just {span:lang=ja:\u6771\u4eac} and {span:lang=ja:\u90fd} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068}). Really it's all just the reading you learned with the kanji, too, so you can think of it that way as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u90fd\u306b\u306f\u3001\u4e00\u6d41\u306e\u30ec\u30b9\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u304c\u305f\u304f\u3055\u3093\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "There are a lot of first-rate restaurants in the Tokyo Metropolitan Area."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u90fd\u306e\uff13\uff10\u4ee3\u4f1a\u793e\u54e1\u3001\u5c71\u7530\u592a\u308d\u3046\u3055\u3093\uff08\u4eee\u540d\uff09\u306f\u3001\u3052\u304d\u3080\u3068\u9577\u6642\u9593\u308d\u3046\u3069\u3046\u3067\u77e5\u3089\u308c\u308b\u304e\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3044\u3067\u50cd\u3044\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Taro Yamada (pseudonym), who is in his 30s and a salaryman in the Tokyo Metropolis, is working in an industry that is notorious for its hard work and long working hours."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b9\u30ab\u30a4\u30c4\u30ea\u30fc\u304c\u305d\u3073\u3048\u7acb\u3064\u6771\u4eac\u90fd\u58a8\u7530\u533a\u3067\u306f\u3001\u4eca\u5e74\u306f\u6628\u5e74\u3088\u308a\u3082\u65e9\u304f\u6728\u306e\u8449\u304c\u843d\u3061\u59cb\u3081\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The leaves started falling earlier this year than last year in Tokyo Metro\u2019s Sumida Ward, where the Tokyo Sky Tree stands."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:move} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to move}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Move",
                "Alternative": "To Operate",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3054\u304f"
