                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28696-subject-3352.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Someone is telling you {tooltip:Vocabulary:to move}. They are saying \"{tooltip:Reading:you go} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3054}) over there. Move! Move!\" If it helps, have them pronounce \"You go\" more like \"Ugo.\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u305d\u3053\u3067\u4f55\u304b\u52d5\u3044\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Something moved over there."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u30b5\u30fc\u30d0\u30fc\u306f\u4e8c\u5341\u56db\u6642\u9593\u52d5\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3067\u3082\u30a2\u30af\u30bb\u30b9\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu's servers operate twenty-four hours a day, so it can always be accessed."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304f\u305d\u301c\u3002\u30d1\u30bd\u30b3\u30f3\u304c\u52d5\u304b\u306a\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u305c\u3002\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3053\u3046\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u308d\u3046\uff1f\uff01",
                    "en": "Shoot! My computer doesn\u2019t work. How did this happen?!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u8d77\u304d\u308b} means \"to wake up.\" This word, however, means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to occur}. Think of it this way. When an action \"wakes up\" in a way it is occurring as well. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to occur}. Just imagine a {tooltip:Reading:core} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u308b}) of uranium just occurring out of nowhere to help you to remember this word.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Occur",
                "Alternatives": "To Happen, To Take Place",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3053\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3053\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4793-subject-3562.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3053\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28719-subject-3562.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as what you learned with the kanji and the same as {span:lang=ja:\u8d77\u304d\u308b} too, meaning you should be able to put together the reading on your own.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u307e\u3055\u304b\u3053\u3093\u306a\u3053\u3068\u304c\u8d77\u3053\u308b\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3001\u601d\u3063\u3066\u3082\u307f\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I never expected something like this would happen."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u8d77\u3053\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u3001\u843d\u3061\u7740\u3044\u3066\u3088\u304f\u8003\u3048\u3066\u307f\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please calm down and think carefully about what's taken place."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u306d\u3047\u3001\u50d5\u306b\u30ad\u30b9\u3057\u305f\u3044\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3042\u308a\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3002100\u4e07\u5e74\u7d4c\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3042\u3093\u305f\u3068\u30ad\u30b9\u306a\u3093\u3066\u7d76\u5bfe\u306b\u3057\u305f\u304f\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3002\u5929\u5730\u304c\u3072\u3063\u304f\u308a\u8fd4\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3001\u8d77\u3053\u308a\u3063\u3053\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Hey, do you want to kiss me?\" \"Absolutely no way would I ever want to kiss you in a million years. That would never happen even if heaven and earth were turned upside down.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You should know {span:lang=ja:\u958b\u3051\u308b} by now. This word is similar to that, except it has to do with when things are just open. It's the same thing, though. The meaning is also {tooltip:Vocabulary:to open}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Open",
                "Alternative": "To Be Open",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4313-subject-3561.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28491-subject-3561.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Do you remember the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u958b\u3051\u308b}, which you learned in level 10? That's right, it's {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3051\u308b}! So if you know the reading of that word (I hope you do!) then you can apply that knowledge here.\n{splitParent}Just a quick side note \u2014 {span:lang=ja:\u958b\u304f} can also be read as {span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3089\u304f}, but we're going to focus on the {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304f} reading here. Since {span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3089\u304f} has slightly different meanings, we won't accept it as a reading for this word, so be sure to enter {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304f}!\n\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u304a\u5e97\u306f\u4f55\u6642\u306b\u958b\u304d\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "What time does this shop open?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u793e\u4f1a\u306e\u307e\u3069\u304c\u958b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Your fly is open."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3059\u307f\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u535a\u7269\u9928\u306f\u660e\u65e5\u306f\u958b\u3044\u3066\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u958b\u3044\u3066\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Excuse me, is the Tofugu Museum open tomorrow?\" \"Yes, it's open.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

