                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u5b66\u3092\u305d\u3064\u696d\u3059\u308b\u524d\u306b\u3001\u6771\u5357\u30a2\u30b8\u30a2\u3092\u65c5\u884c\u3057\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I want to travel around Southeast Asia before graduating from university."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u65c5\u884c\u306e\u8a71\u3092\u805e\u304d\u305f\u3044\u306e\u306f\u5206\u304b\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3088\u308a\u3001\u307e\u305a\u306f\u79c1\u304c\u3044\u306a\u3044\u9593\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u305f\u306e\u304b\u6559\u3048\u3066\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I know you want to ask about my trip, but first things first, how have you been while I've been away?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:warm}? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:warm}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Warm",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305f\u305f\u304b\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u305f\u305f\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4843-subject-3385.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u305f\u305f\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28741-subject-3385.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Touch something that's warm... too warm! You pull your hand back and go \"{tooltip:Reading:AH ta ta!} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u305f\u305f}). People make this noise when they touch something that's hot, I hear. It's almost like saying \"hot hot hot\" while dropping the \"h\" sound.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f55\u304b\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u3082\u306e\u304c\u98f2\u307f\u305f\u3044\u306a\u3041\u3002",
                    "en": "I want to drink something warm."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u521d\u5fc3\u8005\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u3069\u3046\u304b\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u76ee\u3067\u898b\u307e\u3082\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm a beginner, so please go easy on me."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30c7\u30b6\u30fc\u30c8\u306b\u6e29\u304b\u3044\u30a2\u30a4\u30b9\u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30e0\u306f\u3044\u304b\u304c\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f\u300d \u300c\u3044\u3044\u3048\u3001\u3082\u3046\u7d50\u69cb\u3067\u3059\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Would you like some warm ice cream for dessert?\" \"No, we\u2019re all set.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:water} {tooltip:Kanji:deep}ness is the {tooltip:Vocabulary:water depth}. You should check this before diving into the water so you don't hit your face.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
