                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c34\u6df1100\u30d5\u30a3\u30fc\u30c8\u307e\u3067\u3082\u3050\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I've dived to depths of one hundred feet before."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30d7\u30fc\u30eb\u306e\u6c34\u6df1\u306f\u3042\u3055\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3001\u5fc3\u914d\u3057\u306a\u304f\u3066\u3044\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You don't have to worry because this pool is very shallow."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c0\u30a4\u30d3\u30f3\u30b0\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u969b\u306b\u3001\u6c34\u6df1\u5341\u30e1\u30fc\u30c8\u30eb\u306e\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3067\u8679\u8272\u306e\u6d77\u85fb\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "While diving at a depth of ten meters, I found rainbow-colored seaweed."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:way} of {tooltip:Kanji:speak}ing is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:way of speaking} (or it could be your {tooltip:Vocabulary:speaking style}). This is how someone talks. Some people have an interesting speaking style, after all.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Way Of Speaking",
                "Alternatives": "Speaking Style, Way Of Talking, Talking Style",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u306a\u3057\u304b\u305f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u306a\u3057\u304b\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4865-subject-3555.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u306a\u3057\u304b\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28750-subject-3555.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from {span:lang=ja:\u8a71\u3059} and {span:lang=ja:\u65b9}. By now you should have seen these words separately and should be able to read this word too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u8a71\u3057\u65b9\u304c\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u30a4\u30e9\u30a4\u30e9\u3059\u308b\u306e\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "The way he talks makes me really annoyed."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u8a71\u3057\u65b9\u3063\u3066\u3001\u304b\u306a\u308a\u3057\u3076\u3044\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi's style of conversation is very cultured, eh?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u308f\u3041\uff01\u541b\u306e\u8a71\u3057\u65b9\u3001\u307e\u308b\u3067\u6bcd\u56fd\u8a9e\u304c\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u4eba\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3060\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Wow! The way you talk sounds just like a native Japanese person."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:leaf} of the things you {tooltip:Kanji:say} is like a leaf from a tree of speaking. That leaf is a part of the whole language, it is a single {tooltip:Vocabulary:word}, though it can add up to be a {tooltip:Vocabulary:language} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:manner of speech}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Word",
                "Alternatives": "Language, Manner Of Speech",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3068\u3070"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3068\u3070",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "4814-subject-7492.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3068\u3070",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28718-subject-7492.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u8a00} is one you haven't learned. It's kind of an exception, in fact, though you might see it from time to time. You'll want to imagine yourself playing a {tooltip:Reading:koto} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3068}). Each strum of the instrument sends forth several {tooltip:Vocabulary:word}s from its strings, flying at the person you're talking to. You speak your {tooltip:Vocabulary:word}s via music, specifically the koto (so think about using other instruments as well to communicate... they just don't work).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a8\u30eb\u30d5\u3092\u3084\u3068\u3044\u305f\u3044\u306e\u306f\u5c71\u3005\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u8a00\u8449\u306e\u304b\u3079\u304c\u3042\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3080\u305a\u304b\u3057\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I'd like to hire elves if I could, but It's difficult because of the language barrier."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u307e\u304f\u8a00\u8449\u306b\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3059\u3054\u304f\u7279\u5225\u306a\u4eba\u306a\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "It's hard to put into words, but Koichi is a very special person to me."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u8a00\u8449\u306b\u8a70\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was at a loss for words."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:writing} {tooltip:Kanji:chapter} on its own is more like an {tooltip:Vocabulary:article} or something like that. Even if it's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:sentence} long. So it covers just about every type of {tooltip:Vocabulary:writing} there is.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
