                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u6587\u7ae0\u3092\u304b\u3044\u305f\u306e\u306f\u3060\u308c\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Who wrote this article?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u6587\u7ae0\u304c\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u4e0a\u624b\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi is such a good writer."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u3001\u6751\u4e0a\u6625\u6a39\u306e\u6c17\u969c\u3067\u6c17\u53d6\u3063\u305f\u6587\u7ae0\u304c\u3042\u307e\u308a\u597d\u304d\u3067\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I don\u2019t like Haruki Murakami\u2019s cheesy, pompous writing style very much."
                }
