{
            "mnemonic": "Legs appear between two lumps of dirt. This is the earth's version of a {tooltip:Radical:womb}. Imagine a tiny baby growing under the ground and then sprouting out, legs first, into the world. Imagine being inside this dirt womb. It's warm and damp. You feel safe.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Womb"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:compare} {tooltip:Radical:white} light to the other colors you'll realize... white consists of {tooltip:Kanji:all} the colors in one. It contains all the colors in the spectrum in one color. It is the one color that is {tooltip:Kanji:everything}.",
            "hints": "Just look at the color white. Compare it to other colors. Now look at white again. Split it up into all the colors, creating a beautiful spectrum. Wow, it's {tooltip:Kanji:all} the colors!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "All",
                "Alternatives": "Everyone, Everything, Everybody"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u306a, \u307f\u3093\u306a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine everything covered in white. Everything in the world. Then, you see a dark splotch. It's the miners, they're all covered in coal, ruining all your ambitions. Walk up to them and see all the dirt on the perfectly white uniforms you gave them just a few minutes earlier. Feel enraged at them. How could they ruin all this white you made for {tooltip:Kanji:all} the people of the world!?",
                "mnemonic": "You decide white light is the ultimate color. You decide you want to put it on {tooltip:Kanji:all} things to make everything white. \"What a great idea,\" you think. You try to put it on everything and you nearly succeed... except, the {tooltip:Reading:miners} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u306a}). They keep getting dirty doing all their mining things. NOOO, your plan is ruined!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You thought it would be a good idea to {tooltip:Radical:say} the {tooltip:Radical:body} {tooltip:Radical:measurement}s of everyone in your village and now you have to {tooltip:Kanji:apologize}.",
            "hints": "When you do a bad thing you should apologize. And saying everyone's private body measurements is definitely something you should not have done. So it's apology time.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Apologize"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3083",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3084\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"What do we say?\" the shaman says, poking you in the back. \"Ugh, I'm sorry I told everyone how tiny your socks are, I guess.\" \"And?\" \"Annnddd I'll never do it again.\"",
                "mnemonic": "You were told you had to {tooltip:Kanji:apologize} by the village {tooltip:Reading:sha}man ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3083}). At first you didn't even know why everyone was glaring at you, but the shaman took you aside and explained. And now she's standing behind you with her arms crossed as you apologize to everybody."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Putting your wood in {tooltip:Radical:bundle}s for {tooltip:Radical:winter} is the {tooltip:Radical:correct} way to {tooltip:Kanji:arrange} it. You want to make sure you {tooltip:Kanji:organize} all of your wood before winter comes, or the loose logs could get blown away in the first winter storm.",
            "hints": "Picture all of the bundles, neatly arranged and organized, as the first snowflakes begin to fall.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Arrange",
                "Alternative": "Organize"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3068\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You can't just throw an entire bundle of logs onto a fire, you have to saber them into smaller chunks. And it's easier to arrange them first, saber them all in half, and then you have two nicely arranged rows!",
                "mnemonic": "Right after you've finished {tooltip:Kanji:arrang}ing the bundles, you take out your {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}) and do one final slice. All of the bundles are now perfectly organized AND cut."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tree} from {tooltip:Radical:heaven} with a {tooltip:Radical:mustache} above his {tooltip:Radical:mouth} valiantly crosses a {tooltip:Kanji:bridge}. This holy tree from heaven was sent down to earth to cross this very bridge. It is the tree\u2019s angelic mission. Also the tree has a mouth and a mustache.",
            "hints": "Picture this majestic tree as it crosses the bridge. Its mustache is very distinguished. Hear its roots and branches swaying, creaking, and cracking in the wind.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bridge"
            },
