{
            "mnemonic": "You want to get a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} so you have one of {tooltip:Radical:yourself} ({tooltip:Radical:oneself}) and another self working {tooltip:Radical:together} to {tooltip:Kanji:choose}. The two tiny yous sit on each of your shoulders and argue about which scooter you should choose.",
            "hints": "The white self says you should choose the safest scooter. The red self says safety is for suckers, and you should buy one that's loud and dangerous and covered in flames.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Choose"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The white self says, I choose this centaur scooter because of its strong arms. The red self says, I choose this scooter because it looks like a badass horse monster, wooh!",
                "mnemonic": "Suddenly your selfs both gasp and {tooltip:Kanji:choose} the scooter in front of you that looks like a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}). The scooter is designed like a human on the top, the bars are its arms, and the bottom with the seat and the wheels are all horse. This centaur is what you choose to ride."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On this {tooltip:Radical:tree} there is an {tooltip:Radical:eye} inside a {tooltip:Radical:heart} that was drawn trying to express some sort of {tooltip:Kanji:concept}. Unfortunately, concepts like this, especially concept art, has never been your strong suit.",
            "hints": "You sit down in front of the tree with its eye heart and stare at it, trying to understand the concept it's trying to express. Concepts are too abstract. This is hard.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Concept"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046, \u305d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The soul of the tree or symbol or whoever granted the ability to understand complicated concepts to YOUR soul. Groovy.",
                "mnemonic": "After a few hours of contemplating this {tooltip:Kanji:concept}, suddenly it becomes clear and a {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) pops out of the tree. It leans forward and touches your forehead and your head fills with new concepts and ideas you've never considered before."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Big} {tooltip:Radical:products} need to be put in a big {tooltip:Kanji:container}. A small container just won\u2019t do. These products are big and they need a big container to be contained in.",
            "hints": "Imagine having all these big products. How will you contain them all!? Imagine yourself stuffing all of these big products into their respective containers.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Container",
                "Alternative": "Vessel"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3064\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the size of these big keys you have to use to lock these containers. It\u2019s a really big key. Picture yourself straining to turn the key in the lock.",
                "mnemonic": "Once you get the big products into a {tooltip:Kanji:container}, you then lock it with a {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}). You wouldn\u2019t want these products to bust out of their containers, so it\u2019s best to lock them up with a key."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you yourself are a {tooltip:Radical:sun}, and you {tooltip:Radical:stand} next to another {tooltip:Radical:sun}, no area around you will be {tooltip:Kanji:dark}. The two suns are very bright and standing right next to each other, so all the area will be lit up and nothing will be dark.",
            "hints": "Think of how bright the sun is. Now multiply that by two. Suns are especially bright right after you come out of a dark area. Imagine yourself looking at these suns and feeling the pain as your eyes are blinded by the bright light.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dark"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3089, \u304f\u308c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself eating anchovies. The anchovies taste particularly fishy and salty. Taste the anchovies on your tongue as you eat them in darkness.",
                "mnemonic": "Since the sun has blinded you, your vision is now very {tooltip:Kanji:dark}. You can\u2019t see anything, but you are hungry so you reach around for some food and eat it. Yuck! It\u2019s {tooltip:Reading:an}chovies ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3093}). You don\u2019t even like anchovies, how did they get in your house?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you get home from school, your {tooltip:Radical:mama} says to hang your {tooltip:Radical:spoon}s and {tooltip:Radical:arrow}s on the {tooltip:Radical:coat rack}. That doesn't sound like something your mama would say, and you begin to {tooltip:Kanji:doubt} that she's your mama at all! She usually takes them and washes them in the sink. You doubt you could hang them on the coat rack even if you tried.",
            "hints": "Your mama is acting weird. You doubt she's really your mama. What are you going to do?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Doubt"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u305f\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch the doubt wash over her face as she looks up at you from her position in the guillotine. Finally she mutters, \"Well, this is disappointing, and I doubt you hung up your spoons and arrows on the coat rack before trying to murder your ol' mum.\"",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:doubt} is growing really strong, so you decide to test your mama by putting her head in a {tooltip:Reading:gui}llotine ({span:lang=ja:\u304e})! Oh come on, don't feel bad, you're preeettty sure this isn't your real mama."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:rice} {tooltip:Radical:ladle} that's specifically for paying the rice {tooltip:Kanji:fee}. Each scoop of something has an extra fee tacked on, so when you use a {tooltip:Kanji:material}, there's a fee you have to pay in that material as well.",
            "hints": "Imagine ladling up a nice big scoop of rice and then seeing the little fee ladle next to it. Ugh. The material fee.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fee",
                "Alternative": "Material"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "That's a lot of material you have to give up every time you want to eat some rice. Maybe you should take this row boat oar ladle and row out into the ocean where no one can tax you.",
                "mnemonic": "One day, the {tooltip:Kanji:fee} ladle is suddenly the size of row ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat oars! What! You're supposed to pay a row boat sized fee now?!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:soul} is {tooltip:Radical:blue}. As in, it's sad and not feeling well. Your soul changes colors depending on what it's {tooltip:Kanji:feeling} or what {tooltip:Kanji:emotion} you're expressing.",
            "hints": "Start with a blue soul. What feeling is that? Now a red soul. What emotion is that? Go through as many colors as you can think of, focusing on the fact that each color represents a different emotion or feeling.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Feeling",
                "Alternative": "Emotion"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
