                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine playing in the water in the summer. It\u2019s crazy hot outside in the summer, so going in the water feels nice. Imagine the coolness of the refreshing water around your body.",
                "mnemonic": "This sheep with the {tooltip:Kanji:formal name title} of Sir Wilburt Coddington III only likes to play outside in the water during the {tooltip:Reading:summer} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u307e}). Summer is the best season for this fancy sheep. The other seasons just can\u2019t compare."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Sheep} {tooltip:Radical:fins} are {tooltip:Radical:good} for {tooltip:Kanji:foster}ing children. The sheep have been genetically combined with fish, so the sheep have fins (and they've lost their tails - which is why the tail part of the sheep radical is missing in this kanji!). These sheep fins are very rich in nutrients and as such are very good for foster children that need to grow up big and strong.",
            "hints": "Imagine eating a fish fin with sheep wool on it. It tastes fishy like the ocean but the wool tastes like clothes. It\u2019s probably the worst thing ever. Imagine eating something like this and taste its flavor on your tongue.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Foster"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u3057\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Remember how bad those sheep fins tasted? Now imagine eating your favorite yogurt flavor instead. This yogurt is delicious.",
                "mnemonic": "The best way to {tooltip:Kanji:foster} a better relationship with these foster kids would be to give them some {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}). Maybe they can dip the sheep fins in the yogurt to help mask the strange taste. Yogurt is also very nutritious, so it\u2019s a good supplement to the foster kids\u2019 diet."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you see a {tooltip:Radical:wolverine} in the {tooltip:Radical:water} playing with a piece of {tooltip:Radical:thread}, there\u2019s no doubt that it\u2019s {tooltip:Kanji:green}. Wolverines love green thread. Almost as much as they love the water.",
            "hints": "Picture this wolverine playing with the green thread. It\u2019s like a little kitten with yarn. That wolverine loves that green thread. Picture how cute it is as it plays with the thread and coos in happiness.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Green"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u304f",
