                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you\u2019ve ever had Midori before, imagine that taste. It\u2019s also green, so that\u2019s an easy way to remember this kanji. If you haven\u2019t had it, just picture the taste of melon and imagine that flavor on your tongue.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Reading:Midori} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3069\u308a}) is a {tooltip:Kanji:green} colored melon liqueur with a sweet, fruity taste. This wolverine is too young to drink alcohol like Midori, so he just sticks to drinking water."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:womb} spins in a {tooltip:Radical:circle} and starts to {tooltip:Radical:boil} with {tooltip:Kanji:heat}. Uh oh, I think you have a {tooltip:Kanji:fever}.",
            "hints": "Even if you don't have a womb, just picture one anyway: it's turning around in a circle faster and faster, as the heat bubbles and boils in you. You can feel this heat spread through your entire body as you burn up with a fever.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Heat",
                "Alternative": "Fever"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306d\u3064",
