                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the dog kneeling in front of the pot of concentrated nature and breathing deeply as it practiced Zen. You kind of wish you could join it, considering how peaceful it looks.",
                "mnemonic": "Destroying {tooltip:Kanji:nature} like this is the dog's way of practicing {tooltip:Reading:Zen} ({span:lang=ja:\u305c\u3093}) Buddhism. As it breathes in the fumes from all of the different pieces of nature being boiled down, the dog gets really zen and chill."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What you {tooltip:Radical:say} at a {tooltip:Radical:temple} is a {tooltip:Kanji:poem}. It has to be a poem, because if you say anything else it's just plain disrespectful. All of the monks and priests at this temple have to read and recite poems all day, and if they can do it forever, you can while you're visiting.",
            "hints": "Picture all of the people at the temple reciting poems together. You join in too, and it's a really powerful moment!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Poem"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You turn to the person next to you and realize you have to say everything in poem form.{splitParent}Excuse me\n{linebreak}I'm not a creep\n{linebreak}so hear my plea\n{linebreak}is that a sheep?",
                "mnemonic": "As you recite a long {tooltip:Kanji:poem} at the temple you see a {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) in the crowd. It's opening and closing its mouth like it wants to say the poem too."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Pointing a {tooltip:Radical:thread} to the {tooltip:Radical:east}, you {tooltip:Kanji:practice} your navigation skills. You\u2019ve discovered a method to tell direction using just a thread, so you point it to the east in order to find your way. The method takes practice though, so you\u2019re sure to practice every day.",
            "hints": "East is the land of the rising sun, so imagine yourself practicing this method, pointing the thread to the east as the sun rises up. Feel the heat of the sun\u2019s rays and see the bright light as the sun shines up over the horizon.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Practice"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you\u2019ve ever seen the show Ren & Stimpy, imagine what it would be like to be Ren. If not, watch a clip on YouTube and pretend you are Ren when you practice doing things, like studying kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "Also, you are {tooltip:Reading:Ren} ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3093}), from Ren & Stimpy the TV show. Since you\u2019re not in the TV business anymore, you\u2019ve decided to {tooltip:Kanji:practice} your other skills. How mature of you, Ren."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Shoot a {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} that's in the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of a {tooltip:Radical:Viking} at the fair and you'll win a {tooltip:Kanji:prize}. The game is to shoot the shellfish in the Viking's mouth and knock it over.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking at a big Viking with a shellfish in its mouth. You want to knock it over. You want this prize.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Prize"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You want this prize. You want to meet the Shougun. Soon you'll both be eating shellfish together!",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:prize} you're working so hard to win is lunch with the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). This is a pretty huge prize, considering all you're doing is knocking something over."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you run into a {tooltip:Radical:gate} {tooltip:Radical:mouth} first, you\u2019re going to have a {tooltip:Kanji:problem}. Smashing your mouth into a gate is going to hurt. A lot. The problem you\u2019re now in is one of getting to a hospital and having your mouth sewn back on. The {tooltip:Kanji:question} is, how are you going to get to the hospital?",
            "hints": "Imagine having your mouth bashed into a gate. It\u2019s going to hurt. Imagine how painful this would be and how problematic it is. Imagine that the only question in your mind is how to get to the hospital as quickly as you possibly can.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Problem",
                "Alternative": "Question"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068, \u3068\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Monsters are scary. Maybe you\u2019ve had a dream where you were being chased by one. Remember how scary that is when you see this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "The reason you ran mouth first into this gate was because you were being chased by a {tooltip:Reading:mon}ster ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3093}). A monster in and of itself is a big enough {tooltip:Kanji:problem} as is, let alone smashing your mouth into a gate. You poor, hapless soul."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Eat}ing on this {tooltip:Radical:roof} is a {tooltip:Radical:bear}, which is how you know this is a {tooltip:Kanji:public building}. The law says that all bears are allowed to eat on the roofs of public buildings. In Japan at least, I don't know where bears are supposed to eat in wherever you're from.",
            "hints": "Picture a public building, like a museum or a library, and look at the roof. There's a bear eating up there! And it's smiling and waving to you!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Public Building"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The next time you see a public building, think, \"Thank you Genghis Khan.\" Because of him bears are free to go up to the roof and eat whatever they please whenever they please. ",
                "mnemonic": "All {tooltip:Kanji:public building}s must serve bear needs thanks to the monumental law passed by Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}). Genghis Khan knew that bears weren't treated well by humans, so he made sure all public buildings were at least partially bear accessible."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} in the {tooltip:Radical:center} of the sky gives off its light, which {tooltip:Kanji:reflect}s off of everything around it.",
            "hints": "Look around you, everything you see is reflecting the light of the sun. Unless it's night time, then the tiny sun in the center of your lightbulb is creating the light that reflects there.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reflect",
                "Alternative": "Reflection"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3064, \u306f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the light of the sun reflecting off a single acorn on the forest floor. So much symbolism!",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:reflect}ed light is important for {tooltip:Reading:a}corns ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3044}), in particular. Without light reflecting off everything, the sun's light would never make it down to the ground where they've fallen. They would never grow into trees. And we'd all suffocate."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:original} {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} had a {tooltip:Kanji:request}. He wants there to be more geoducks in the world!",
            "hints": "Remember, this is the OG = original geoduck. There are no other geoducks yet.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Request"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306d\u304c, \u306d\u304c\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "People listened when Gandhi said, \"My friends. We must stop trying to eat the geoduck, and instead allow it to breed. Join me in this fast!\"{splitParent}And that's why we have so many geoducks on the earth today. Thanks Gandhi.",
                "mnemonic": "The only person that would even hear the geoduck's {tooltip:Kanji:request} was {tooltip:Reading:Gan}dhi ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3093}). Gandhi closed his eyes, sat down, and spread the geoduck's request to the rest of the world."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:samurai} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:samurai} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals, yo!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Samurai"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
