                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself driving a car and salivating over the fruit waiting for you in the fruit section. Imagine your favorite fruit as you put the pedal to the metal in your awesome car.",
                "mnemonic": "To get to the fruit {tooltip:Kanji:section}, you have to go to the store. To get to the store you have to drive a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). Driving a car is the fastest way to get to the fruit section at the store."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:tree} with a {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} and a {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer} tied to it. You look closer, because this is an odd sight, and realize that there is a sign here too. It's telling you to beware of helicopters and jackhammers in this woods. It's a poorly made {tooltip:Kanji:signpost}!",
            "hints": "This is not the best signpost you've ever seen, but it's better than nothing at all, you suppose.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Signpost"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u308b\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Press it a few more times and hear the sound in your head. Also spell it out in kana as you hear it as a nice little additional visual.",
                "mnemonic": "As you look at this weird {tooltip:Kanji:signpost} you notice a button. You press it because it will supposedly tell you more about these dangerous helicopters and jackhammers. Instead, it just yells out in a loud obnoxious voice: {tooltip:Reading:HEYO} ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3087\u3046})!!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "At the {tooltip:Radical:root} of {tooltip:Radical:gold}, there is {tooltip:Kanji:silver}. Gold is basically just silver leveled up. That's why gold is first place, and silver is second. If you just scratch gold really good, you'll find that at its root, there's silver hidden just underneath.",
            "hints": "Imagine taking a gold coin and rubbing it with some soap and water. As you rub, you slowly see that it's really silver underneath. Huh!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Silver"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Guinea pigs are to silver as normal pigs are to truffles.",
                "mnemonic": "If you want to hunt for some {tooltip:Kanji:silver} for yourself, all you need is a {tooltip:Reading:gui}nea ({span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3093}) pig. Guinea pigs can smell silver, so get a couple and set them loose in the woods and they'll lead you straight to it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:horse} and a {tooltip:Radical:shrimp} are sitting next to each other. They are both at the train {tooltip:Kanji:station}, waiting for a train to come and take them home.",
            "hints": "Imagine the horse and the shrimp sitting next to each other on a small bench. There is nobody else at the train station. It is awkward.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Station",
                "Alternative": "Train Station"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Instead of saying \"a key\" he says \"eh key.\" How strange. Imagine the station master saying it like this with his weird accent. You ask him if he has \"a key\" and he replies with, \"What is a key?\" Then you say \"eh key.\" He totally understands you now.",
                "mnemonic": "The train pulls into the {tooltip:Kanji:station}. They walk up to the train doors, but they don't open. \"Perhaps {tooltip:Reading:a key} ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u304d}) would help?\" asks the station master, as he goes over to open the door to the train."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} of the {tooltip:Radical:elephant}s was so great, they made a {tooltip:Kanji:statue} of him. This {tooltip:Kanji:image} of him looks down on all the other elephants at all times.",
            "hints": "For now, just imagine the leader of the elephants being told they're getting a statue. Don't think about what the statue looks like, because that's next.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Statue",
                "Alternative": "Image"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305e\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "But this is exactly what the leader of the elephants asked for. For you see, the leader of the elephants was a big fan of zombies. Imagine the elephant leader being so excited to have a zombie version of the statue.",
                "mnemonic": "When they unveil the {tooltip:Kanji:statue} of the leader elephant, everyone gasps. It's a statue of the leader, but they are a {tooltip:Reading:zo}mbie ({span:lang=ja:\u305e\u3046}). Gasp!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you use the {tooltip:Radical:sun}, you can find the {tooltip:Radical:correct} {tooltip:Radical:geoduck}. That's the {tooltip:Kanji:topic} of today's lecture.",
            "hints": "Picture a teacher pointing to a chalkboard with a big pointer, and it says \"TOPIC.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Topic"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
