{
            "mnemonic": "For your {tooltip:Radical:car} you use a {tooltip:Radical:hat}, some {tooltip:Radical:ground} and a {tooltip:Radical:bookshelf} to build a new {tooltip:Kanji:wheel}. I mean, it's generally {tooltip:Kanji:ring} and {tooltip:Kanji:loop} shaped, so it should work, right?",
            "hints": "Imagine this wheel you made out of a hat, some ground (presumably to keep it all together), and a bookshelf. You install it on your car and hope for the best. This is why you should buy wheels from professional wheel makers.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wheel",
                "Alternatives": "Ring, Loop"
            },
