                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28828-subject-3568.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses the kun'yomi, which you didn't learn with the kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you out. What are you beginning? You are beginning {tooltip:Reading:Haj} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3058}). (Haj is the fifth pillar of Islam, and is a pilgrimage to Mecca during the month of Dhu al-Hijja).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u307e\u305a\u521d\u3081\u306b\u725b\u8089\u3092\u30b9\u30e9\u30a4\u30b9\u3057\u3066\u3001\u305d\u308c\u304b\u3089\u30d5\u30e9\u30a4\u30d1\u30f3\u3067\u3044\u305f\u3081\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "To begin with, please first slice the beef and then pan fry it."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u521d\u3081\u306b\u8a00\u308f\u305b\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u30a2\u30c9\u30ea\u30d6\u3048\u3093\u305d\u3046\u306f\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "First of all, please don't improvise."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "Tofugu\u3088\u5b89\u3089\u304b\u306b\u7720\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308c\u3002\u4eca\u6708\u521d\u3081\u306b\u3001\u50d5\u306e\u4e00\u756a\u597d\u304d\u306a\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u5b66\u7fd2\u30b5\u30a4\u30c8\u304c\u5012\u7523\u3057\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "R.I.P. Tofugu. At the beginning of this month my favorite Japanese learning site went bankrupt."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
