{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:like} {tooltip:Kanji:alcohol} a lot, you're probably a heavy {tooltip:Vocabulary:drinker}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Drinker",
                "Alternative": "Alcoholic",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306a adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3051\u305a\u304d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3055\u3051\u305a\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5071-subject-3515.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3055\u3051\u305a\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28862-subject-3515.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is all kun'yomi vocab reading here as you can probably guess from the hiragana sticking out on the end. You should know the readings of these as separate words already ({span:lang=ja:\u9152} and {span:lang=ja:\u597d\u304d}) which means all you need to pay attention to is the rendaku of {span:lang=ja:\u3059\u304d} to {span:lang=ja:\u305a\u304d}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u308c\u6c0f\u306f\u9152\u597d\u304d\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3001\u5fc3\u914d\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "My boyfriend is a drinker, so I'm worried."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u9152\u597d\u304d\u3001\u4eca\u65e5\u3082\u671d\u304b\u3089\u5f15\u3063\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3084\u304c\u308b\u305c\u3002",
                    "en": "That alcoholic is drinking in the morning again today."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u59bb\u306f\u9152\u597d\u304d\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u30a2\u30eb\u4e2d\u306b\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u304b\u5fc3\u914d\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "My wife is a drinker and I\u2019m worried about her becoming an alcoholic."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u98f2\u3080} is drink, so this has to do with {tooltip:Kanji:drink}ing. Also, {span:lang=ja:\u4f1a} means {tooltip:Kanji:meet}, so when you meet to drink you're getting together with others to drink. It's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:drinking party}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Drinking Party",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306e\u307f\u304b\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306e\u307f\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5032-subject-3548.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306e\u307f\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28820-subject-3548.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from the {span:lang=ja:\u98f2\u3080} vocabulary word and the regular kanji reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4f1a}. Hopefully you know both of those by now so you can apply them to the reading of this word, too!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u4e3b\u3055\u3044\u306e\u98f2\u307f\u4f1a\u306f\u3068\u3066\u3082\u697d\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "Drinking parties hosted by Tofugu are so fun!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6700\u8fd1\u3001\u98f2\u307f\u4f1a\u3067\u4e00\u6c17\u98f2\u307f\u3092\u5f37\u8981\u3055\u308c\u3066\u6025\u305b\u3044\u30a2\u30eb\u30b3\u30fc\u30eb\u4e2d\u3069\u304f\u3067\u6b7b\u307c\u3046\u3059\u308b\u5b66\u751f\u304c\u3075\u3048\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3088\u3046\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "These days there seems to be an increase in the number of students who are forced to chug drinks at parties and die of acute alcohol poisoning."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u888b\u304c\u98f2\u307f\u4f1a\u306b\u306f\u884c\u3063\u3061\u3083\u30c0\u30e1\u3060\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002\u304a\u524d\u3093\u3068\u3053\u306e\u89aa\u304c\u30a2\u30eb\u30b3\u30fc\u30eb\u3068\u304b\u306b\u5bfe\u3057\u3066\u53b3\u3057\u304f\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3001\u7fa8\u307e\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "My mom says that I can\u2019t go to the drinking party. Your parents are really chill about stuff like alcohol. I\u2019m jealous."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Kanji:heart} is {tooltip:Kanji:fever}ish and hot about something, it is obviously something you have a lot of {tooltip:Vocabulary:enthusiasm} about. Think about the things you've enthusiasm for. Then, imagine your heart beating and getting all hot from thinking about it. Why else would people get so upset when talking about religion and politics. It's their feverish heart! Their enthusiasm!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Enthusiasm",
                "Alternatives": "Passion, Zeal",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306a adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306d\u3063\u3057\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306d\u3063\u3057\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
