                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u65c5\u884c\u306b\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3089\u65c5\u9928\u306b\u3068\u307e\u3063\u3066\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When I travel to Japan, I would like to stay at a Japanese-style hotel."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6765\u6708\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u65c5\u884c\u306b\u884c\u304f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u65c5\u9928\u3068\u30db\u30c6\u30eb\u3068\u3069\u3063\u3061\u306b\u3068\u307e\u3063\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "I'm traveling to Japan next month. Where do you think I should stay: a Japanese-style inn or a hotel?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3053\u306e\u65c5\u9928\u3001\u3053\u3093\u306a\u306b\u30b4\u30ad\u30d6\u30ea\u304c\u51fa\u308b\u306e\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u6700\u8fd1\u96e8\u3070\u3063\u304b\u308a\u964d\u3063\u3066\u308b\u304b\u3089\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\uff1f\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Why are there so many cockroaches in this Japanese inn?\" \"I think it\u2019s because of all the rain we\u2019ve been getting.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Wind} of the {tooltip:Kanji:gods}. These are {tooltip:Vocabulary:divine winds}. More popularly, this is a word known as {tooltip:Vocabulary:kamikaze}, which became known because of the kamikaze pilots during WWII. This was used before WWII, though, when the entire Mongol fleet was destroyed by a storm, preventing an invasion of Japan. How lucky.",
