{
            "mnemonic": "You have your {tooltip:Kanji:feeling}s... these are the feelings humans have. When you ask someone to have feelings (Have feelings, {tooltip:Reading:KAY}?? ({span:lang=ja:\u3051} at the end)), you are asking them to {tooltip:Vocabulary:pity} or have {tooltip:Vocabulary:mercy} on you. Please! Have those human feelings that people have, like {tooltip:Vocabulary:sympathy} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:pity}. Don't kill me, man!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pity",
                "Alternatives": "Sympathy, Mercy, Compassion",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3055\u3051"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306a\u3055\u3051",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5169-subject-3541.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306a\u3055\u3051",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28894-subject-3541.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Who are you begging to have pity on you? It's {tooltip:Reading:NASA}. They have you hanging outside of the space station and they're going to push you towards earth where you'll burn up in the atmosphere. You don't want that, so you beg mission control for some {tooltip:Vocabulary:pity}. What will they do? You decide.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u5b50\u306f\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304c\u60c5\u3051\u306e\u304b\u3051\u3089\u3082\u306a\u3044\u7537\u3060\u3068\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3001\u5225\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichiko broke up with Koichi after she learned Koichi is a man without even a shred of sympathy."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306b\u306f\u3001\u300c\u65c5\u306f\u9053\u3065\u308c\u4e16\u306f\u60c5\u3051\u300d\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3053\u3068\u308f\u3056\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "In Japanese there is a proverb, \"It is important for us to be compassionate toward each other as we travel through this world.\""
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c6\u30b9\u30c8\u306f70\u70b9\u304c\u5408\u683c\u70b9\u3060\u3063\u305f\u304c\u3001\u79c1\u306f69\u70b9\u3060\u3063\u305f\u306e\u306b\u3082\u95a2\u308f\u3089\u305a\u304a\u60c5\u3051\u3067\u5408\u683c\u3055\u305b\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3048\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I needed a 70 to pass the test, and even though I got a 69, I was given a pity pass."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a tricky word that doesn't really have a good translation. The best ways I've seen it done in terms of getting a meaning across are {tooltip:Vocabulary:please} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:please help me}. When you say this word you're kind of saying \"please help me out and I'm relying on you and you're kind of awesome too.\" Anyways, {tooltip:Vocabulary:please} is a pretty good way to do it. So, when you see this word you'll notice it has the {tooltip:Kanji:request} kanji in it. You can guess you're requesting something. What is that thing? It's help ({tooltip:Vocabulary:please help me}) and you're asking very nicely too ({tooltip:Vocabulary:please}).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Please Help Me",
                "Alternatives": "Please, If You Would Be So Kind",
                "Word Type": "expression"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u306d\u304c\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u306d\u304c\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5306-subject-3637.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u306d\u304c\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28972-subject-3637.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You ask for help by saying {tooltip:Vocabulary:please help me}, and that person does try to help you... but the amount they do for you is so {tooltip:Reading:neg}ligible that it hardly does anything to help you at all. Please try to help me again, this time better?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u795e\u69d8\u3001\u304a\u9858\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059\uff01\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u304c\u4e0a\u624b\u304f\u306a\u308a\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Please God! I want to be fluent in Japanese."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3086\u3046\u308c\u3044\u4f1a\u54e1\u3067\u3082\u304b\u307e\u308f\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u304a\u9858\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "If you aren't an active member, please join!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u901a\u8def\u5074\u306e\u5e2d\u3092\u304a\u9858\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u7a93\u304b\u3089\u5916\u306e\u666f\u8272\u3092\u773a\u3081\u308b\u306e\u304c\u5acc\u3044\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Could I have an aisle seat, please? I hate looking out the window."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
