                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28858-subject-3619.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e00\u5e74\u9593\u7df4\u7fd2\u3057\u3066\u3001\u3088\u3046\u3084\u304f\u6709\u6c17\u97f3\u3068\u3080\u6c17\u97f3\u3092\u805e\u304d\u5206\u3051\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After practicing for one year, was finally able to distinguish between aspirated and unaspirated sounds."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u3005\u306e\u7df4\u7fd2\u304c\u5b9f\u3092\u3080\u3059\u3073\u3001\u30a2\u30c9\u30ea\u30d6\u3067\u30ae\u30bf\u30fc\u304c\u3072\u3051\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My daily practice bore fruit and now I can improvise on the guitar."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u50d5\u304c\u4e16\u754c\u30e9\u30f3\u30ad\u30f3\u30b0\u4e00\u4f4d\u3092\u7dad\u6301\u3057\u7d9a\u3051\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u3092\u6bce\u65e5\u4e03\u6642\u9593\u7df4\u7fd2\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304b\u3089\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I believe the reason I continue being ranked number one in the world is that I devote seven hours a day to practicing Japanese."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Remember that {span:lang=ja:\u624b} can refer a \"person\" in some words? Well this is one of them. In this case, we have {tooltip:Kanji:choose} {tooltip:Kanji:person}, or perhaps a better way to think of it is like \"chosen person.\" One situation in which you'd choose a person to do something is in sports, like in a schoolyard pick. Keep that in mind and you should be able to remember that this means {tooltip:Vocabulary:pro athlete} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:sports player}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pro Athlete",
                "Alternatives": "Sports Player, Professional Athlete",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093\u3057\u3085"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305b\u3093\u3057\u3085",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5163-subject-3629.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305b\u3093\u3057\u3085",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28914-subject-3629.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u9078} is what you'd expect. {span:lang=ja:\u624b} is the on'yomi reading as it is every once in a while, especially when it has to do with representing a person, so you'll have to remember that. I think you've seen {span:lang=ja:\u624b} using this reading enough to be able to remember it, though.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u30cf\u30f3\u30b5\u30e0\u306a\u9078\u624b\u306f\u3060\u308c\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Who is that handsome pro athlete?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6700\u8fd1\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u4eba\u306e\u30d7\u30ed\u91ce\u7403\u9078\u624b\u304c\u30e1\u30b8\u30e3\u30fc\u30ea\u30fc\u30b0\u3067\u3082\u30d7\u30ec\u30a4\u3059\u308b\u3059\u304c\u305f\u304c\u3088\u304f\u898b\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "These days, we can often see Japanese professional baseball players play in the major leagues."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u7d20\u6674\u3089\u3057\u3044\u5263\u9053\u306e\u9078\u624b\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi is magnificent pro kendo player."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:problem} {tooltip:Kanji:topic} is the {tooltip:Vocabulary:problem} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:question} you have to answer. If you think about it, topics as problems tends to be a school-related thing. So, when you have to answer a problem in school, that's {span:lang=ja:\u554f\u984c}.",
