                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own. The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5b9f} gets changed to {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3063} so be careful!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u58f2\u308a\u4e0a\u3052\u8868\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3068\u3001\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u304c\u58f2\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3060\u306a\u3068\u5b9f\u611f\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When I look at this revenue chart I really feel like WaniKani is selling well."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bcd\u304c\u6b7b\u3093\u3060\u3068\u3044\u3046\u77e5\u3089\u305b\u3092\u805e\u3044\u3066\u3082\u3001\u3059\u3050\u306b\u306f\u5b9f\u611f\u304c\u308f\u304b\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Even when I heard the news that my mother died, it didn't feel real at first."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u3078\u884c\u3063\u3066\u521d\u3081\u3066\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u306f\u306a\u3093\u3068\u5c0f\u3055\u3044\u56fd\u304b\u3068\u5b9f\u611f\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Only after I went to America did I realize how small Japan really is."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've hopefully seen {span:lang=ja:\u597d\u304d} by now, which is \"to like.\" So, what happens when you have a {span:lang=ja:\u5927} (big) like? You {tooltip:Vocabulary:really like}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:like a lot}, or {tooltip:Vocabulary:love} something.",
