                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading comes from {span:lang=ja:\u597d\u304d} which you've hopefully seen. Then, {span:lang=ja:\u5927} is the reading you learned with the kanji.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I love you."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u306a\u3093\u3060\u304b\u3093\u3060\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3001\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304c\u5927\u597d\u304d\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "No matter what he says, Fugu still likes WaniKani a lot."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5929\u7136\u30dc\u30b1\u3067\u3001\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u3044\u3066\u3044\u3064\u3082\u697d\u3057\u3044\u306a\u3063\u3066\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3002\u304a\u524d\u306e\u3053\u3068\u5927\u597d\u304d\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You\u2019re kind of goofy and that makes you fun to hang out with. I really like you."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You think about the {tooltip:Kanji:concept} of a certain number of {tooltip:Kanji:times}, each time thinking of each time you've thought about this concept before. Each time you look back, that is {tooltip:Vocabulary:retrospection} on that concept. You look back more and more times until there are no more times to look back on.",
