                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Just be sure to note the shortened {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u304f}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u98df\u5668\u3092\u30c6\u30fc\u30d6\u30eb\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u306a\u3089\u3079\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Can you arrange these plates and utensils on the table, please?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u304c\u6c60\u306b\u843d\u3068\u3057\u305f\u306e\u306f\u3053\u306e\u91d1\u306e\u98df\u5668\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3001\u305d\u308c\u3068\u3082\u3053\u306e\u9280\u306e\u98df\u5668\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Which utensils did you drop in the pond, the gold ones or the silver ones?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3001\u98df\u5668\u304c\u4e00\u5f0f\u591a\u3044\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "How come we have one extra place setting?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have {tooltip:Kanji:feeling}s of {tooltip:Kanji:apologizing}. Strangely, this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:thanks} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:gratitude}, though. Perhaps someone did something so nice for you that you want to apologize for how many nice things they're doing for you. You are this grateful to them!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
