                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: When you say you're sorry {tooltip:Vocabulary:to apologize}, you'd probably start with: \"{tooltip:Reading:I am} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3084\u307e}) sorry!\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306b\u4eca\u3059\u3050\u8b1d\u308a\u306a\u3055\u3044\uff01",
                    "en": "Apologize to Koichi right now!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f55\u3082\u60aa\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3057\u3066\u306a\u3044\u306e\u306b\u8b1d\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u304e\u3083\u304f\u306b\u3053\u3063\u3061\u304c\u3053\u307e\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "If you apologize even though you haven't done anything wrong it makes me uncomfortable."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u541b\u304c\u6e80\u8db3\u3059\u308b\u7d50\u679c\u304c\u5f97\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u306e\u306f\u304b\u308f\u3044\u305d\u3046\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u306e\u306b\u8b1d\u308b\u3064\u3082\u308a\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I feel bad that you won\u2019t get a satisfying result, but I refuse to apologize for something I didn\u2019t do."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word is tough, because there's another word in this level ({span:lang=ja:\u7740\u308b}) that means \"to wear\" that is so similar. This word, however, means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to arrive}. You should have seen that meaning with the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u7740} as well, so I hope that helps. To differentiate between this and {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u308b}, though, zoom in on the {span:lang=ja:\u304f}. You want to be {tooltip:Reading:coo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u304f}) so you arrive to the party late.",
