{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:reflect}. The verb vocab version means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be reflected}. You're not doing the reflecting directly. You can remember this by thinking how rude ({span:lang=ja:\u308b}) it is that someone's reflecting your image using a mirror for everyone outside the dressing room to see.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Reflected",
                "Alternative": "To Be Projected",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3064\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3064\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5218-subject-3594.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3064\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28929-subject-3594.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Your reflection is getting reflected onto the mirror. You don't like it, it doesn't look like you. Impostor reflection! You take a hammer and you {span:lang=ja:\u6253\u3064} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3064}) it as hard as you can, glass flying everywhere. Then some dubstep starts playing from the broken mirror: {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064\u3046\u3064}. \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b9\u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30f3\u306b\u793e\u5185\u7528\u3057\u308a\u3087\u3046\u304c\u6620\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The internal company document is being projected on the screen."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u93e1\u306b\u6620\u3063\u305f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u304b\u304a\u3092\u898b\u3066\u3001\u300c\u306a\u3093\u3066\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u3093\u3060\u300d\u3068\u6bce\u65e5\u601d\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Looking at my own face reflected in the mirror I feel \"how beautiful my face is\" every day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u6e56\u306e\u6c34\u9762\u306b\u6620\u308b\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u5c71\u306b\u611f\u52d5\u3057\u3001\u30db\u30ed\u30ea\u3068\u6d99\u3092\u6d41\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "A tear rolled down Koichi\u2019s cheek when he saw the beautiful mountains reflected on the surface of the lake."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:release} and the verb vocab version means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be released}. You can differentiate this one from {span:lang=ja:\u653e\u3059} (to release) by thinking that it's pretty {tooltip:Reading:rare} ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u308b}) for you to be released by your arch nemesis. He just let you go, strangely. How rare.",
