                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28923-subject-3628.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You have the opportunity {tooltip:Vocabulary:to choose}. You choose, and a bright sign lights up reading \"{tooltip:Reading:error}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3089}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3060\u308c\u3092\u6bba\u4eba\u3059\u308b\u304b\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3001\u9078\u3079\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I can't choose who to kill."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5148\u751f\u306e\u8a71\u3092\u805e\u304b\u305a\u306b\u3001\u305a\u3063\u3068\u3069\u3063\u3061\u306e\u5973\u306e\u5b50\u3092\u9078\u307c\u3046\u304b\u8003\u3048\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I stopped listening to my teacher and just kept thinking about which girl to choose."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u826f\u3044\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u30b3\u30b9\u30c1\u30e5\u30fc\u30e0\u3092\u304a\u9078\u3073\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "You chose a great Fugu costume."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:feeling} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to feel}.",
