{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u8ffd\u3046} is \"to follow.\" So, you're following something or someone, or something similar. Just think of the {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3051\u308b} as you being all \"cocky\" about it. You're not just following this person, you're chasing them, with the intent to catch them. So, this word is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to chase} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:to pursue}. Scary!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Chase",
                "Alternatives": "To Pursue, To Stalk, To Run After, To Follow",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3044\u304b\u3051\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3044\u304b\u3051\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28967-subject-3579.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3044\u304b\u3051\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5309-subject-3579.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading comes from {span:lang=ja:\u8ffd\u3046} as well as the kanji reading you learned too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u7530\u4e2d\u3055\u3093\u306f\u5c71\u7530\u3055\u3093\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304c\u5927\u3059\u304d\u3067\u3001\u6bce\u65e5\u8ffd\u3044\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Ms. Tanaka likes Mr. Yamada a lot, so she chases him every day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u3078\u3093\u3060\uff01\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3063\u305f\u3089\u30d1\u30b9\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u3092\u6301\u305f\u305a\u306b\u65e5\u672c\u3078\u51fa\u767a\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3088\u3002\u4eca\u3059\u3050\u8ffd\u3044\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3053\u306e\u30d1\u30b9\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u3092\u308f\u305f\u3057\u3066\u3042\u3052\u3066\u304f\u308c\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "OMG! Koichi left for Japan without his passport. Can you run after him and give him this passport?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b7\u30e3\u30c1\u306e\u7fa4\u308c\u3092\u8ffd\u3044\u304b\u3051\u3066\u308b\u30d5\u30b0\u3092\u898b\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I saw Fugu following a pod of killer whales."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:separate}, so you can guess the meaning is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to separate} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be divided}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Separate",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Divided, To Part From, To Break Up",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u308f\u304b\u308c\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u304b\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28970-subject-7495.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u304b\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5288-subject-7495.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Remember the word {span:lang=ja:\u5206\u3051\u308b}? That word means \"to separate\" too. The reading is similar, though not the same, but we can at least use it as a jumping off point. We go from {span:lang=ja:\u308f\u3051\u308b} to {span:lang=ja:\u308f\u304b\u308c\u308b}. It's like we've \"separated\" the {span:lang=ja:\u3051} and the {span:lang=ja:\u308b} and combined them in the middle. {span:lang=ja:\u3051}, making a {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u308c}, which gets you to {span:lang=ja:\u308f\u304b\u308c\u308b}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u5b50\u306f\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3068\u5225\u308c\u3066\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u3068\u4ed8\u304d\u5408\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichiko separated from Koichi and started going out with Viet."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30df\u30e5\u30cb\u30b1\u30fc\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u4e0d\u8db3\u304c\u3052\u3093\u3044\u3093\u3067\u5225\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We broke up due to a lack of communication."
                },
