                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Keys to houses are always made out of a piece of the foundation it was built upon. How else would they be unique from one another?",
                "mnemonic": "Remember, a good {tooltip:Kanji:foundation} is the {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) to a good house. No, literally. You have to use a piece of the foundation to make the key to your house."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Each {tooltip:Radical:life} has a {tooltip:Radical:soul}, and that soul determines what {tooltip:Kanji:gender} you are. It's not so much about your body parts, it's more about what's inside that matters.",
            "hints": "Picture your own soul and your own life. Listen to what your soul says about your gender and live your life to the fullest!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gender",
                "Alternatives": "Nature, Sex"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
