{
            "mnemonic": "This meaning is a little weird, but I'm going to try my best to help you remember. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Carrot",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306b\u3093\u3058\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u3093\u3058\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5509-subject-8805.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u3093\u3058\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29092-subject-8805.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u53c2} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You're craving a {tooltip:Vocabulary:carrot}, but you can't seem to find any. You look in your fridge, in your garden, and even in the trash. Finally you give up your carrot search and sit down when... ouch! The carrot was in your {tooltip:Reading:jean}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093}) the whole time!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u4eba\u53c2\u30b9\u30fc\u30d7\u306b\u306f\u5931\u671b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was disappointed with this carrot soup."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u9152\u597d\u304d\u306e\u738b\u69d8\u306b\u3001\u4eba\u53c2\u30ea\u30ad\u30e5\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u30d7\u30ec\u30bc\u30f3\u30c8\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u3088\u308d\u3053\u3070\u308c\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I gifted some carrot liqueur to the King, who loves alcohol, but he didn't like it."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u9858\u3044\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4f55\u3067\u3082\u98df\u3079\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001\u4eba\u53c2\u3060\u3051\u306f\u52d8\u5f01\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please. I'll eat anything else, just not the carrot. Please."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What {tooltip:Kanji:location} {tooltip:Kanji:suit}s a situation the best? That always depends on the {tooltip:Vocabulary:case} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:circumstance}. You can't know the suitability of the location until you have all the facts about the circumstances.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Case",
                "Alternatives": "Circumstance, Situation",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3042\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3070\u3042\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "39996-subject-3034.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3070\u3042\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20087-subject-3034.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses the kun'yomi readings for both kanji. You haven't learned this kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5408} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent} To know exactly what {tooltip:Vocabulary:case} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:circumstance} you're dealing with, you keep a close {tooltip:Reading:eye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044}) on things. Imagine your eye really close up to the circumstances, trying to figuring out exactly what's going on.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30bf\u30aa\u30eb\u3084\u77f3\u3051\u3093\u3001\u304a\u304b\u3057\u3001\u304a\u305d\u3070\u306a\u3069\u3092\u3082\u3063\u3066\u3044\u304f\u5834\u5408\u304c\u591a\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "In many circumstances, we take things like towels, soap, snacks, or noodles."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u51fa\u6765\u308b\u304b\u304e\u308a\u65e9\u304fE\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u306b\u3078\u3093\u3057\u3093\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3088\u3046\u52aa\u3081\u3066\u304a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3059\u3050\u306b\u3078\u3093\u3057\u3093\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u5834\u5408\u3082\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u306e\u3067\u3054\u308a\u3085\u3046\u3044\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "We try our best to respond your emails as soon as possible, but please note that we may not be able to respond immediately."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u5834\u5408\u306b\u306f\u8b66\u5bdf\u3092\u547c\u3093\u3060\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "In this case, I think it would be good to call the police."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
