                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}You really want to measure the {tooltip:Vocabulary:circumference} of something but there doesn't seem to be anything round around. That's when you remember, \"{tooltip:Reading:Mah Wa}lnuts! ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u308f}).\" The walnuts in your pocket have an easy {tooltip:Vocabulary:edge} to measure.\n"
