                    "en": "Leaders of companies need to have a sense for fine art, but Koichi doesn't have anything like that."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e4\u306f\u3001\u4eba\u9593\u306e\u5265\u88fd\u3068\u3044\u3046\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u7f8e\u8853\u4f5c\u54c1\u304c\u4e26\u3079\u3089\u308c\u305f\u30a2\u30b8\u30c8\u3092\u300cTofugu\u306e\u6050\u308d\u3057\u3044\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u300d\u3068\u540d\u4ed8\u3051\u305f\u3002\u305d\u3057\u3066\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3068\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u3082\u305d\u306e\u5265\u88fd\u306e\u4e00\u3064\u306b\u3055\u308c\u3088\u3046\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Aya named her hideout the \"Tofugu Terrible Art Gallery\" because it was filled with her beautiful artwork-stuffed corpses. Koichi and Viet were to join her collection."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This has almost the same meaning as the kanji it comes from. Instead of just simply being \"example,\" though, it's {tooltip:Vocabulary:for example}. So, you could start a sentence with this and be all like \"{span:lang=ja:\u4f8b\u3048\u3070}, I am using {span:lang=ja:\u4f8b\u3048\u3070} in a sentence.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "For Example",
                "Alternative": "For Instance",
                "Word Type": "adverb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3068\u3048\u3070"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3068\u3048\u3070",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5648-subject-3657.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3068\u3048\u3070",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29158-subject-3657.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Using all kinds of \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:for examples}\" like this, you were {tooltip:Reading:taught} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3068}) many things throughout your life. For example, you were taught about...\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f8b\u3048\u3070\u3001\u6614\u306f\u3059\u3054\u304f\u4eba\u6c17\u304c\u3042\u3063\u305f\u3051\u3069\u3001\u4eca\u306f\u843d\u3061\u3076\u308c\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u4eba\u304c\u3044\u305f\u3068\u3057\u307e\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "For example, let's say there was a person who used to be very popular but isn't at all anymore."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f8b\u3048\u3070\u3001\u820c\u3092\u304b\u307f\u305d\u3046\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u6642\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306a\u3089\u4f55\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3068\u601d\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "For instance, what do you think Koichi would say when he almost bit his tongue?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u306a\u3041\u3001\u3055\u304f\u3089\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3001\u4f8b\u3048\u3070\u3001\u9031\u306b\u4e00\u5ea6\u3084\u4e8c\u5ea6\u3050\u3089\u3044\u3001\u3046\u3061\u306b\u6765\u306a\u3044\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Hey, Sakura, why don\u2019t you come over to my house, like, once or twice a week or something?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:origin} of your {tooltip:Kanji:foundation} is where you have to work from when learning something new. For example, the {span:lang=ja:\u57fa\u672c} portions of WaniKani are the earlier levels, especially the radicals. They are the {tooltip:Vocabulary:foundation} you need to learn your kanji and vocab later on.",
