                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u56f3} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You {tooltip:Vocabulary:intentional}ly stub your {tooltip:Reading:toe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068}) all the time! If you hurt your toe {tooltip:Vocabulary:on purpose} you can get out of class and work! It's a really simple injury, but you can't do other stuff while it's hurt, so you always do it on purpose to get out of things.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u793e\u54e1\u306e\u57fa\u672c\u7d66\u3092\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u7684\u306b\u5f15\u304d\u4e0a\u3052\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi intentionally raised the base pay for Tofugu employees."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3067\u3082\u305d\u308c\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u3001\u610f\u56f3\u7684\u306a\u4f5c\u308a\u8a71\u3063\u307d\u304f\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "But don't you think it sounds a little like an intentionally made-up story?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u610f\u56f3\u7684\u306b\u60c5\u5831\u3092\u64cd\u4f5c\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u5974\u304c\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "There\u2019s a guy manipulating the news on purpose."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:thing}s you {tooltip:Kanji:wear} are your {tooltip:Vocabulary:clothes}. Oh, and Japanese clothes count too. We're talking {tooltip:Vocabulary:kimono}s. Way back when, these could just be called {tooltip:Vocabulary:clothes} because it's all people really wore, but nowadays we know they're specific to the stereotypical kimono you think of when you think \"Japan.\"",
