{
            "mnemonic": "This has the same meaning as the kanji. The little {span:lang=ja:\u308a} thrown on there is just a little {tooltip:Vocabulary:remainder} sticking off the end of the kanji. No need to pay attention to that.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Remainder",
                "Alternatives": "Remnant, Leftover, Residue",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306e\u3053\u308a"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306e\u3053\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5665-subject-3704.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306e\u3053\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29168-subject-3704.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: You're waiting inside. The {tooltip:Vocabulary:remainder} of your forces are out there, fighting. You don't know who will survive... or if they even will. You have a secret {tooltip:Reading:knock} ({span:lang=ja:\u306e\u3053}), though, that you use to find out if it's one of the remaining forces outside or the enemy, broken through. You hear a knock. What is it? Is it your men or theirs? Imagine it out, focusing on the knock conversation that happens between you and the remainder.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6b8b\u308a\u306e\u6c34\u306f\u3069\u3053\u306b\u884c\u3063\u305f\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "Where is the leftover water?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3055\u304f\u591c\u306e\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u30c4\u30a4\u30fc\u30c8\u306f\u3001\u4e00\u306b\u304e\u308a\u306e\u6b8b\u308a\u306e\u30d5\u30a9\u30ed\u30ef\u30fc\u3055\u3048\u3082\u304a\u3053\u3089\u305b\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi's tweet last night made even the small remainder of his followers very upset."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u591c\u306f\u30c7\u30fc\u30c8\u304c\u3042\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001\u6669\u5fa1\u98ef\u306f\u663c\u5fa1\u98ef\u306e\u6b8b\u308a\u3092\u6e29\u3081\u3066\u98df\u3079\u3066\u306d\u3002\u30de\u30de\u3088\u308a\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m going on a date tonight. You can heat up some leftovers from lunch to eat for dinner. Love, Mom."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

