{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:four} {tooltip:Kanji:season}s are {tooltip:Vocabulary:the four seasons}. For some reason many Japanese people think that Japan's the only place with four distinct seasons. Obviously they haven't been to half the places on their latitude around the world.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "The Four Seasons",
                "Alternative": "Four Seasons",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u304d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5571-subject-3671.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29132-subject-3671.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Note that {span:lang=ja:\u56db} is read using the on'yomi reading, which you've seen a few times over the course of WaniKani. Think of {span:lang=ja:\u3057} meaning \"death\" (like {span:lang=ja:\u6b7b}), and how with the four seasons there comes death every Fall and Winter.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306e\u3068\u3063\u305f\u5199\u3057\u3093\u306f\u3001\u56db\u5b63\u306e\u7f8e\u3057\u3055\u3092\u3068\u3066\u3082\u3088\u304f\u3073\u3087\u3046\u5199\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The photos Viet took depict the beauty of the four seasons very well."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u305f\u3057\u306e\u5f1f\u306f\u3001\u6614\u306f\u56db\u5b63\u3092\u901a\u3058\u3066\u4e0b\u305f\u3092\u306f\u3044\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My younger brother used to wear Japanese geta all year round."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u56db\u5b63\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u3068\u3001\u305d\u308c\u305e\u308c\u306e\u5b63\u7bc0\u306b\u3069\u3093\u306a\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3069\u3093\u306a\u3082\u306e\u3092\u98df\u3079\u308b\u306e\u304b\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u3001\u6559\u3048\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3048\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Can you tell me about Japan\u2019s four seasons and what people do and eat during them?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is an {tooltip:Kanji:interval} (of time) that you need \"to suit\" ({span:lang=ja:\u5408\u3046}). To suit that interval, you need to be there before the time in question. That's why this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be in time for}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to make it on time} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be on time for}.\n",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be In Time For",
                "Alternatives": "To Make It On Time, To Be On Time For",
                "Word Type": "godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307e\u306b\u3042\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u306b\u3042\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "3714-subject-3489.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u306b\u3042\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "28199-subject-3489.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u9593} when you learned {span:lang=ja:\u9593\u3082\u306a\u304f}. And the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5408\u3046} is just that of the word {span:lang=ja:\u5408\u3046}. If you remember them both, you'll remember this word!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u3059\u3050\u30bf\u30af\u30b7\u30fc\u306b\u4e57\u308c\u3070\u3001\u307e\u3060\u9593\u306b\u5408\u3046\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "If we get in a taxi right now, we might still make it on time."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3054\u3081\u3093\uff01\u3058\u3085\u3046\u305f\u3044\u306b\u306f\u307e\u3063\u3061\u3083\u3063\u3066\u3001\u5f85\u3061\u5408\u308f\u305b\u306b\u9593\u306b\u5408\u3044\u305d\u3046\u306b\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Sorry! I'm stuck in traffic, so I'm most likely not going to make it to the appointment on time."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u9593\u306b\u5408\u3046\u3068\u601d\u3046\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3082\u3046\u3059\u30507\u6642\u306a\u3093\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3001\u5f8c\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u3067\u8003\u3048\u308c\u3070\u308f\u304b\u308b\u3060\u308d\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Do you think we can make it in time?\" \"Well, it\u2019s almost seven o\u2019clock. Do the math.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Hey. {tooltip:Kanji:Drop} yourself down and {tooltip:Kanji:arrive} back to me. You're going nuts over there. Lower down. Come back. Arrive. You need to do these things {tooltip:Vocabulary:to calm down}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Calm Down",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3061\u3064\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3061\u3064\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5481-subject-3798.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3061\u3064\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29072-subject-3798.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from {span:lang=ja:\u843d\u3061\u308b} and {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u304f}. Hopefully you know these words so you can read this word as well! If you don't, just {span:lang=ja:\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304f} and everything will be okay.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u306e\u5973\u306f\u3068\u3089\u3048\u3069\u3053\u308d\u306e\u306a\u3044\u5973\u6027\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u4e00\u3057\u3087\u306b\u3044\u308b\u3068\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I have no idea what she's thinking, but I can relax when I'm with her."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u8d64\u3061\u3083\u3093\u306b\u30b9\u30b3\u30c3\u30c1\u3092\u3042\u3052\u3066\u843d\u3061\u7740\u304b\u305b\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet calmed down the baby by giving her some scotch."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3061\u304f\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3001\u4e0a\u53f8\u306e\u3084\u3064\uff01\u3082\u3046\u3001\u982d\u306b\u304d\u305f\uff01\u3053\u3093\u306a\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3001\u8f9e\u3081\u3066\u3084\u308b\u3002\u300d\u300c\u304a\u3044\u304a\u3044\u304a\u3044\u3001\u305d\u3046\u7126\u308b\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3002\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u843d\u3061\u7740\u3051\u3088\u3002 \u300d",
                    "en": "\"Damn him! I\u2019m sick of my boss. I\u2019m going to quit my job.\" \"Whoa, whoa, whoa. Don\u2019t be in such a hurry. Calm down.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:participate}, so you'd think this word would mean \"to participate\" but it doesn't (sorry!). It's a little more complex. Think of it as \"to participate\" but where you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:to come} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to go} in order to do it. This is the humble way to say those things, so you're going to these places with your tail between your legs, just happy you can participate more than anything.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Come",
                "Alternative": "To Go",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3044\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u3044\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5616-subject-3662.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u3044\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29141-subject-3662.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: You get {tooltip:Vocabulary:to come} to participate! \"It's {tooltip:Reading:my} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u3044}) lucky day!\" you exclaim.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3056\u3001\u53c2\u3089\u3093\uff01",
                    "en": "Let's go!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u9031\u672b\u306f\u3001\u6bcd\u306e\u304a\u306f\u304b\u306b\u53c2\u308b\u3064\u3082\u308a\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This weekend I'm planning to visit my mom's grave."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u6bce\u65e5\u795e\u793e\u306b\u53c2\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I visit a Shinto shrine every day."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know how {span:lang=ja:\u6d88\u5316} is \"digestion\"? Well, The verb form of that is this word, which is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to digest}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Digest",
                "Word Type": "\u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3059\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3059\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5512-subject-3880.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3059\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29102-subject-3880.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}If you know {span:lang=ja:\u6d88\u5316} you should be able to read this. Also, it uses the readings you learned with the kanji anyways, so no problemo there.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30cd\u30b3\u306f\u3001\u9b5a\u306e\u76ae\u3092\u3046\u307e\u304f\u6d88\u5316\u3067\u304d\u305a\u306b\u306f\u3044\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "It looks like this cat couldn't digest the fish skin and threw it up."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u3001\u5168\u793e\u54e1\u304c\u6709\u304d\u3085\u3046\u4f11\u304b\u3092\u5b8c\u5168\u6d88\u5316\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3059\u3044\u3057\u3087\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu recommends that all employees use all their paid days off."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u3001\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u523a\u3057\u8eab\u3092\u767e\u5207\u308c\u98df\u3079\u305f\u3088\u3002\u6d88\u5316\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306b\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u6642\u9593\u304c\u304b\u304b\u308a\u305d\u3046\u3002(\u30b2\u30c3\u30d7)",
                    "en": "I just ate 100 pieces of fugu sashimi. It\u2019s gonna take a while to digest. (Burp)"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen that {span:lang=ja:\u6d88\u3059} is \"to extinguish.\" So, this is another verb version of that. This time, you're not doing the extinguishing, it's just happening. Something is going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to disappear} on its own. How can you differentiate this from {span:lang=ja:\u6d88\u3059}? Well, {span:lang=ja:\u3048\u308b} allows you to notice how the object disappeared into thin {tooltip:Reading:air} ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u308b}). You know you didn't do it, so it disappeared on its own, making it {tooltip:Vocabulary:to disappear}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Disappear",
                "Alternatives": "To Go Out, To Turn Off",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3048\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5345-subject-3881.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29004-subject-3881.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is different from {span:lang=ja:\u6d88\u3059}, unfortunately, so you can't use that. Just think about how after the object in front of you disappears you use a {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) to open an invisible door. That's where everything's disappearing to! You see all your disappeared stuff on the other side of this invisible door which you opened with a magical {tooltip:Reading:key}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ef\u30cb\u30ab\u30cb\u306b\u3057\u3085\u3046\u5165\u306e\u5927\u534a\u304c\u6d88\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "WaniKani makes most of my income disappear."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u305b\u3067\u307e\u3086\u6bdb\u304c\u6d88\u3048\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My eyebrows have worn off from my sweat."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f7c\u306f\u3001\u5f7c\u5973\u304c\u8996\u754c\u304b\u3089\u5b8c\u5168\u306b\u6d88\u3048\u308b\u307e\u3067\u3001\u3055\u3088\u3046\u306a\u3089\u3068\u624b\u3092\u632f\u308a\u7d9a\u3051\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "He waved goodbye until she completely disappeared from view."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Hopefully you know the word {span:lang=ja:\u671f\u5f85} by now (expectation). This is the verb version, which makes it {tooltip:Vocabulary:to expect}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
