                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You should be able to read this on your own.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6298\u89d2\u82e6\u52b4\u3057\u3066\u5408\u683c\u3057\u305f\u306e\u306b\u3001\u4f55\u3067\u305d\u3093\u306a\u3059\u3050\u306b\u5927\u5b66\u3084\u3081\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u306e\uff1f",
                    "en": "You worked so hard to pass the exam, so why did you quit university so suddenly?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u671d\u306e\u6642\u70b9\u3067\u306f\u3001\u307e\u3060\u5408\u683c\u3057\u305f\u306e\u304b\u3069\u3046\u304b\u5206\u304b\u3089\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "As of this morning, I didn't know if I passed the exam yet."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8868\u5411\u304d\u306f\u5165\u5b66\u8a66\u9a13\u306b\u5408\u683c\u3059\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u5b66\u7fd2\u587e\u306b\u901a\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u5b9f\u306f\u53cb\u9054\u3068\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u3044\u305f\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3060\u3051\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I attended a cram school ostensibly to pass entrance exams, but I actually just wanted to hang out with my friends there."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Another verb for this kanji! Crazy! I know, I'm sorry. The previous ones were: {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u308b} (to wear), {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u304f} (to arrive), and now {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u3051\u308b} (to put on / to wear). At least it's similar to {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u308b}, right? In this case, this word is like {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u3051\u308b}, which means \"to attach.\" It's used for things you \"attach\" to your body to wear, like accessories, or a face mask. That's why this is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to put on} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to wear}. Same sound, different kanji, similar ideas.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Put On",
                "Alternative": "To Wear",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3051\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3064\u3051\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5622-subject-3885.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3064\u3051\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29164-subject-3885.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as {span:lang=ja:\u7740\u304f}'s reading, but it might be easier to think it shares a reading with {span:lang=ja:\u4ed8\u3051\u308b}, which has a similar meaning. Put on clothes, attach on clothes, etc!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e45\u3057\u3076\u308a\u306b\u30a4\u30e4\u30ea\u30f3\u30b0\u3092\u7740\u3051\u3066\u307f\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I wore earrings for the first time in a long time."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u3057\u3085\u5473\u306f\u3001\u591c\u306a\u591c\u306a\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u90e8\u5c4b\u306b\u3053\u3082\u3063\u3066\u4e16\u754c\u304b\u304f\u5730\u306e\u304a\u9762\u3092\u7740\u3051\u3066\u3042\u305d\u3076\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi has fun by secluding himself in his room and putting on masks from around the world every night."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u304a\u5b88\u308a\u3092\u808c\u8eab\u96e2\u3055\u305a\u8eab\u306b\u7740\u3051\u308b\u3068\u7d04\u675f\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u306a\u3044\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Could you promise me that you will wear this good luck charm all the time, please?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:remainder}, so the verb vocab version is \"to remainder.\" Let's make that sound better: {tooltip:Vocabulary:to remain behind}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Remain Behind",
                "Alternatives": "To Remain, To Stay Behind",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306e\u3053\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306e\u3053\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5651-subject-3705.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306e\u3053\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29153-subject-3705.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: You decide {tooltip:Vocabulary:to remain behind}. Everyone else leaves, and you think you're alone. Then, someone {tooltip:Reading:knock}s ({span:lang=ja:\u306e\u3053}) on the door. Your heart jumps in your throat. They knock again.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u30df\u30b9\u30c6\u30ea\u30a2\u30b9\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3046\u4eba\u306f\u3001\u3053\u3053\u306b\u6b8b\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please stay behind if you think you're mysterious."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u306b\u5411\u3051\u3066\u51fa\u767a\u3057\u305f\u304c\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u307e\u3060\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u6b8b\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We left for Portland, but Koichi remained behind in Japan."
                },
                {
