{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:stream}? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:to stream} (though it's also {tooltip:Vocabulary:to flow}, a very similar word). You can differentiate this from {span:lang=ja:\u6d41\u3059} because with {span:lang=ja:\u6d41\u3059} you flush something down the toilet, which causes it to overflow so you {tooltip:Reading:sue} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059}) the toilet maker. With {span:lang=ja:\u6d41\u308c\u308b} you find a {tooltip:Reading:rare} ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u308b}) jewel trying to flow down the river. You grab it, and see it's a rare diamond!",
