                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3053\u3080",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29006-subject-3666.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}People {tooltip:Vocabulary:surround} you. They circle around you, calling you a chicken. \"{tooltip:Reading:Cacko}! ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3053}) Cacko! Cacko!\" Wait, this isn't the sound a chicken makes, right? You laugh at them, thinking their way of making a chicken noise is weird. Go ahead and join in with them and say \"Cacko\" with them as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6642\u3005\u3001\u3082\u3046\u4e00\u5ea6\u8a18\u8005\u306b\u56f2\u307e\u308c\u305f\u3044\u306a\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "There are times when I wish I was surrounded by reporters again."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6b63\u304b\u3044\u306e\u756a\u53f7\u3092\u5168\u3066\u4e38\u3067\u56f2\u307f\u306a\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Circle the numbers on all of the correct answers."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306f\u6d77\u306b\u56f2\u307e\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3001\u5869\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3067\u3082\u624b\u306b\u5165\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Since Japan is surrounded by oceans, has salt always been available there?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've hopefully seen {span:lang=ja:\u65c5\u884c} by this point. This is the verb version of that. Instead of \"trip\" it's {tooltip:Vocabulary:to travel} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to take a trip}. These are fun to do. You should do them!",
