                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as {span:lang=ja:\u65c5\u884c}, but it also happens to use the reading you learned with the kanji anyways, so you should be able to read it.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e4\u306f\u304b\u3093\u56fd\u3092\u65c5\u884c\u3059\u308b\u3060\u3051\u3067\u306a\u304f\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u3082\u65c5\u884c\u3059\u308b\u4e88\u5b9a\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Not only is Aya traveling to South Korea, but she's also traveling to Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65c5\u884c\u3059\u308b\u524d\u306b\u7f8e\u3088\u3046\u9662\u306b\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u601d\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3088\u308a\u77ed\u304f\u5207\u3089\u308c\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I went to a hair salon before taking my trip, but it ended up shorter than I'd wanted."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30b8\u3001\u7d42\u308f\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3002\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u65c5\u884c\u3092\u3057\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u5f7c\u304c\u4e00\u9031\u9593\u3082\u96fb\u8a71\u3092\u6298\u308a\u8fd4\u3057\u3066\u3053\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3002\u304d\u3063\u3068\u3001\u79c1\u5bdd\u3063\u5c41\u3092\u3053\u304d\u307e\u304f\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3093\u3060\u308f\u3002",
                    "en": "Seriously, it\u2019s already been a week since our trip together and he hasn\u2019t called me back. I must have farted too many times while I was sleeping."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen {span:lang=ja:\u8d77\u304d\u308b} which is \"to wake up.\" This is similar, except you are doing the waking up, which makes the meaning of this word {tooltip:Vocabulary:to wake someone up}. How do you differentiate between this and {span:lang=ja:\u8d77\u304d\u308b}? Because of the {span:lang=ja:\u3059} on the end. You wake someone up violently, wrenching their neck. They turn around and {tooltip:Reading:sue} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059}) you, making you wish you never woke them up.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Wake Someone Up",
                "Alternatives": "To Wake Up, To Wake Someone",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3053\u3059"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3053\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5636-subject-3889.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3053\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29152-subject-3889.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as {span:lang=ja:\u8d77\u304d\u308b}, so as long as you know that word you should be able to read this one. Of course, you can also imagine them yelling \"OH!\" when you shake them awake too, if that helps.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6298\u89d2\u8d77\u3053\u3057\u3066\u3042\u3052\u305f\u306e\u306b\u3001\u610f\u5473\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I tried really hard to wake you up, but it didn't work."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8d64\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3092\u8d77\u3053\u3057\u305f\u304f\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u30a4\u30f3\u30bf\u30fc\u30db\u30f3\u306f\u9cf4\u3089\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "We don't want to wake our sleeping baby, so please don't buzz the intercom."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c3\u30c8\u304c100%\u6b63\u3057\u3044\u3088\u3002\u4eca\u3059\u3050\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u8d77\u3053\u3059\u3079\u304d\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You are absolutely correct, Viet! We should definitely wake Koichi up right now!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
