{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} is out, the sky is {tooltip:Radical:blue}, things have begun to {tooltip:Kanji:clear up}!",
            "hints": "Look into the blue sky and imagine the clouds parting as the weather clears up and you can see the sun. Gorgeous! The beauty is so great you have to squint.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Clear Up"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Say the \"ha ha ha\" part out loud while you imagine the weather clearing up. It'll help you to remember the reading of this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "Now that it's starting to {tooltip:Kanji:clear up} you can't help but laugh. \"{tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f})! Ha ha ha!\" you laugh up into the sky. The sun feels great on your face, making you feel lively! And that blue sky ain't too shabby either."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:saw} down a {tooltip:Radical:bamboo} {tooltip:Radical:tree} to {tooltip:Kanji:construct} and {tooltip:Kanji:build} a building. Bamboo trees are great for construction, so you saw down a bunch of bamboo trees to build this new building.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself sawing down this bamboo tree. Feel the saw in your hands as you slide through the bamboo, wood chips flying everywhere.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Construct",
                "Alternative": "Build"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u305a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine trying to construct the rest of this building covered in baby chicks. They're very cute, but this is dangerous! You have to build very carefully, so you don't accidentally hurt any of them.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:construct} and {tooltip:Kanji:build} this building, you hear a strange cheeping noise. Suddenly a {tooltip:Reading:chick} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u304f}) pops out of one of the bamboo pieces you are building with. Then another, and another. You're surrounded by chicks!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:mama} stands with a {tooltip:Radical:man}, it gives him {tooltip:Kanji:courage}.",
            "hints": "When all alone, though, the man has no courage. It helps when his mama is there to back him up. Imagine a man's mama standing there with him, saying \"you can do it, boy\" while giving him reassurance.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Courage",
                "Alternatives": "Bravery, Valor, Valour"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a courageous man (and his reassuring mama) standing against the youths. They tell him things about modern technology and avocado toast, but thanks to his mama the man can keep his courage.",
                "mnemonic": "A man needs {tooltip:Kanji:courage} to stand up to all the {tooltip:Reading:you}ths ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3046}) of the world. They are too numerous and difficult to understand. It's scary, but the man has courage thanks to his mom."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:stand} in front of a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}, you\u2019re going to {tooltip:Kanji:cry}. That tsunami is going to hit you hard, and rip you right off the ground on which you stand. Who wouldn't cry?",
            "hints": "Imagine getting hit with the full force of a tsunami. It slams into you and crushes every bone in your body. It hurts so much you cry.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cry"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine stuffing yourself with nachos. The tears stop. You're feeling bruised and wet, but much better.",
                "mnemonic": "Do you know the only way to stop yourself {tooltip:Kanji:cry}ing after a tsunami? That's right, {tooltip:Reading:na}chos ({span:lang=ja:\u306a})! Nachos are the only proven way to cheer people up after being hit by a tsunami."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:creeper} inside of a {tooltip:Radical:cape}, who are they? They\u2019re the {tooltip:Kanji:director} of a movie. They try to look all mysterious, but you know it\u2019s just so people go see their movies and think they\u2019re cool. Really they\u2019re just a creep deep down.",
            "hints": "Picture the creepiest director you know. Wearing a cloak and cackling as he directs your favorite actors.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Director"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304b\u3055\u3069",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The creep director gets really into whatever his current project is. Picture him wearing a sheep costume with the cape over it, petting and whispering to his sheep cast.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:director} is currently directing a movie about {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}). He keeps petting them and talking to them like they're humans."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:cage} with {tooltip:Radical:treasure} in it is actually a map of the {tooltip:Kanji:district} the treasure is in.",
            "hints": "Picture a big pirate map, and on it are a bunch of these markers for the districts where you can find the treasures you've been searching for.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "District",
                "Alternative": "Ward"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The treasure of the cookie district is cookies, which you want. And to be fair, even if you weren't a pirate, you'd probably want those cookies.",
                "mnemonic": "There is one {tooltip:Kanji:district} you're interested in, and that's the {tooltip:Reading:coo}kie ({span:lang=ja:\u304f}) district."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are many {tooltip:Radical:flowers} in the {tooltip:Radical:center} of {tooltip:Kanji:England}. It may seem rainy and gray at first, but if you walk right to the center you'll see all the flowers that grow there in the center of the country.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself in the center of England, speaking English to all of the beautiful flowers.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "England",
                "Alternative": "English"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine walking around the giant English acorn. Touch its smooth surface with your hand.",
                "mnemonic": "You keep walking to the very central center of {tooltip:Kanji:England} and see a giant {tooltip:Reading:a}corn ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3044}) planted in the middle of the ground. This acorn is the source of all the flowers and life in England."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:height} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:height} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "If you paid attention in radicals school, you'll be able to learn this kanji meaning easily.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Height",
                "Alternative": "Ten Feet"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3051",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Jourm really is a big guy. Look up at him, and try to measure him, but ten feet is too high for you to reach.",
                "mnemonic": "When you think of {tooltip:Kanji:height} think of our huge farmhand friend, {tooltip:Reading:Jou}rm ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087\u3046}). He's a big guy, and he has a lot of height to him. In fact, he's {tooltip:Kanji:ten feet} tall."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:husband} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:husband} kanji are the same. How useful, unlike some husbands, I'd imagine.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Husband"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
