                "mnemonic": "What do all {tooltip:Kanji:husband}s love? {tooltip:Reading:Foo}d ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3046})! Can you hear your future husband? He\u2019s saying,\u201d Fooooood! FOOOOOD!\u201d like some kind of food craving zombie. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you're {tooltip:Radical:anti}-{tooltip:Radical:eat} your {tooltip:Kanji:meal} will just sit in front of you, uneaten. Food is meant to be eaten! Stop trying to fast and take a bite.",
            "hints": "Look down at the huge meal in front of you. I guess there are plenty of reasons to be anti-eat right now, but you'll have to eat your food eventually.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Meal",
                "Alternative": "Food"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Han Solo slowly eating your whole meal! He's making constant eye contact with you, reaching down and shoving the entire meal into his mouth.",
                "mnemonic": "As you stare at the {tooltip:Kanji:meal}, {tooltip:Reading:Han} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}) Solo appears before you and takes a bite! This is what happens if you don't eat your food, someone else will eat it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you want to {tooltip:Radical:say} how big a {tooltip:Radical:cross} is, you have to {tooltip:Kanji:measure} it. You can't say the size of something without measuring it first.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to use your hands to show the size of this cross, but the other person shakes their head and says, \"Use your words!\" Ugh, okay, you'll have to measure it then.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Measure",
                "Alternative": "Measurement"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"This cross measures two cakes wide and three cakes long,\" you say.",
                "mnemonic": "You need to {tooltip:Kanji:measure} this cross but all you have is a {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}). Good enough! I'm sure all cakes are exactly the same size, so they're a reliable unit of measure."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Tsunami}s in the {tooltip:Radical:past} changed the {tooltip:Kanji:method}s and {tooltip:Kanji:law}s of today.",
            "hints": "Tsunamis used to come crashing into towns, just leveling them completely. Today we have new methods of building and protecting ourselves, and laws to keep them in place, so the past doesn't repeat itself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Method",
                "Alternative": "Law"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your home has strong walls and ceilings. You aren't allowed to leave the doors unlocked and open. These methods and laws are because of those past tsunamis and the damage they used to cause. Your home is safe thanks to them!",
                "mnemonic": "These {tooltip:Kanji:method}s and {tooltip:Kanji:law}s affected your own {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}) the most."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} has an {tooltip:Radical:excuse} for disappearing at {tooltip:Kanji:night}. The sun gets really tired, same as anyone else \u2013 so when night rolls around the sun excuses itself and goes to sleep. It\u2019s a valid excuse.",
            "hints": "Imagine you\u2019re the sun, working all day. Of course you get tired. This is a good excuse to go to bed at night and get some rest. Feel how sore and hot and sweaty and exhausted you are after a hard day\u2019s work of being the sun.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Night",
                "Alternative": "Evening"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You\u2019re a pretty cool dude. Ray-Bans are cool. You even wear them at night you\u2019re so awesome. Yeah.",
                "mnemonic": "Since you\u2019re the sun, it\u2019s pretty bright, so before you excuse yourself for the {tooltip:Kanji:night}, you\u2019re wearing Ray-{tooltip:Reading:Ban} ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u3093}) sunglasses. You keep these Ray-Ban sunglasses on all day to protect your eyes from being burned by yourself."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} rises from the {tooltip:Radical:ground}, and on top of it is a giant {tooltip:Radical:shrimp}. It doesn't do anything except for every day right at {tooltip:Kanji:noon}, when it tells you the time. \"Hey guyz, it's {tooltip:Kanji:noon}, mmk?\"",
            "hints": "Really try to imagine this giant shrimp on the sun as a normal thing that happens, without fail, every day. The shrimp also tells the time right at noon, every day (so important you stress remembering that it's noon, not some other time). Maybe you could have him sing a \"noon song\" in your imagination as well.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Noon"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u308b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Right after the shrimp's announcement, imagine it struggling to put on heels, while sitting on the sun. This shrimp is almost bigger than the sun, actually, so all its struggles with its heels are easy to see.",
                "mnemonic": "At {tooltip:Kanji:noon}, the shrimp also puts on its high {tooltip:Reading:heel}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u308b}) to get ready for the evening, where it wants to make sure it looks good for the other shrimp he/she meets later on."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "To throw {tooltip:Radical:life} out the {tooltip:Radical:window}, use {tooltip:Kanji:poison}.",
            "hints": "To keep life safely inside the window, put that poison down.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Poison"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3069\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Have you done Sudoku before? Imagine yourself completing these puzzles and concentrating really hard. They\u2019re fun, but also challenging.",
                "mnemonic": "If anything's worse than {tooltip:Kanji:poison} it's doing Su{tooltip:Reading:doku} ({span:lang=ja:\u3069\u304f}) puzzles."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "With the right {tooltip:Radical:key} you can unlock the {tooltip:Radical:sun} to {tooltip:Kanji:yesterday}, or a {tooltip:Kanji:previous} day. The sun is in charge of the day changes, so if you use a key to unlock it, you can control the flow of time and return to yesterday, or a previous day in the past. Behold the power of the sun.",
            "hints": "Imagine having the power to control time like this. Picture yourself unlocking the sun to go back in time. Feel the heat of the sun and the bright light in your eyes as you unlock the door to the past.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Previous",
                "Alternative": "Yesterday"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine wearing this sack as you\u2019re sucked through the vortex of time and space. Feel yourself spinning around as you hurtle back into yesterday.",
                "mnemonic": "Time traveling to a {tooltip:Kanji:previous} time, like {tooltip:Kanji:yesterday}, can be rough on the body. As such, you wear a small {tooltip:Reading:sack} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u304f}) to hold your valuables while you\u2019re ripped through the sands of time. The sack keeps your important stuff from getting lost. The sack holds your key to the sun as well."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:knife} got stuck in {tooltip:Radical:Wolverine}'s {tooltip:Radical:forehead}, and he has a {tooltip:Radical:towel} wrapped around it to stop the bleeding, but he really needs to {tooltip:Kanji:return home}.",
            "hints": "Everything is fun and games until someone gets hurt. And in this case, very hurt. If something like this happens, it's always best to return home.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Return",
                "Alternative": "Return Home"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3048",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as Wolverine climbs up onto car elephant and returns home. Well, this party was a failure.",
                "mnemonic": "Wolverine wants to {tooltip:Kanji:return home}, but he can't drive himself because there's a knife in his forehead and lots of blood, so he asks his friend the {tooltip:Reading:ca}r {tooltip:Reading:e}lephant ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3048}) to take him. Car elephant is just an elephant mutant that has a car on his back."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "To {tooltip:Radical:construct} a whole {tooltip:Radical:ceremony}, you can\u2019t just make it up on the spot. That is not a ceremony. A ceremony has a past. A ceremony is done a certain way because that\u2019s the way it\u2019s always been done. In short, to build a ceremony, you have to create a {tooltip:Kanji:ritual} first. Then, the ritual can be constructed into a bigger, more lavish ceremony.",
            "hints": "Ritual and Ceremony kind of mean the same things, sort of. Don't worry too much if you mix them up a little - both will help you to remember the other. There's a reason this kanji is made up of the ceremony radical already!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ritual",
                "Alternatives": "Ceremony, Equation"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It\u2019s good to practice making your own mnemonics up every once in a while. It\u2019ll help you to add on to the mnemonics already here and make better ones more personal to yourself!",
                "mnemonic": "So, you\u2019re at a {tooltip:Kanji:ritual}. Think of the most ridiculous ceremony you can think of. Give it a shot \u2013 I\u2019ll let you come up with the ridiculousness this time (it\u2019s good practice). When you think of your mnemonic, make sure to imagine it with a Sheikh (an Arabic leader). Have the sheikh do something ridiculous to help you to think of this sheikh ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u304d}) and then remember this on\u2019yomi."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take your {tooltip:Radical:yakuza} {tooltip:Radical:knife} and put it in a {tooltip:Kanji:row} with the others.",
