                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Just keep in mind that the reading of {span:lang=ja:\u4e0d} changes from {span:lang=ja:\u3075} to {span:lang=ja:\u3076}. If you're clumsy you'll get a lot of {tooltip:Reading:boo}-boos ({span:lang=ja:\u3076}), get it?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5341\u4ee3\u306f\u3001\u4e0d\u5668\u7528\u306a\u79c1\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u5927\u5909\u306a\u6642\u671f\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My teens were the hardest years for an awkward person like me."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e0d\u5668\u7528\u306a\u52a9\u624b\u304c\u3001\u4e0d\u5668\u7528\u306a\u624b\u3064\u304d\u3067\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u30af\u30bd\u4e0d\u5473\u3044\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3092\u3044\u308c\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My clumsy assistant made very disgusting coffee with his clumsy hands, as usual."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u4e3b\u4eba\u306f\u5805\u82e6\u3057\u304f\u3066\u4e0d\u5668\u7528\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u6b63\u76f4\u8005\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My husband is strict and clumsy, but he\u2019s an honest person."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
