                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: Think about your {tooltip:Vocabulary:husband} even if you don't have one. What's his name? It's {tooltip:Reading:Otto} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3063\u3068}), and he's always leaving you at home because he's working at the {tooltip:Reading:auto} ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3063\u3068}) shop.\n"
