                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6056-subject-7544.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3064\u3066",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29359-subject-7544.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}When a vocab word is a single kanji with no okurigana, it takes the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn this one yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you remember: \n{splitParent}When the {tooltip:Vocabulary:go-between} gets back and is about to tell you everything the other group said, it takes him {tooltip:Reading:two ta}kes ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3066}) to get it all right. The other group had a lot to say and he had trouble getting it all on the first take, but he totally nailed it on the second.\n{splitParent}Little side note: this word is actually more common in katakana, as in {span:lang=ja:\u30c4\u30c6}, or hiragana, as in {span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3066}. Still, you might see it in kanji too, and it's good if you can read it!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bcd\u304c\u4ea1\u304f\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u4f1d\u3048\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u304a\u3058\u3055\u3093\u306b\u306f\u308c\u3093\u3089\u304f\u3059\u308b\u4f1d\u304c\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I want to tell my uncle that my mom passed away, but I don't have a way to get in touch with him."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f1d\u3092\u305f\u3088\u3063\u3066\u3001\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306b\u3057\u3085\u3046\u3057\u3087\u304f\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I got a job at Tofugu through my connections."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8ab0\u304b\u306e\u4f1d\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3068\u3044\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "But I think some kind of intermediary would be good."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": [
                {
                    "en": "to have contacts",
                    "ja": "\u4f1d\u304c\u3042\u308b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "to rely on one's contacts",
                    "ja": "\u4f1d\u3092\u983c\u308b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "a connection via an acquaintance",
                    "ja": "\u77e5\u308a\u5408\u3044\u306e\u4f1d",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                }
            ]
        }

