{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. It also refers to {tooltip:Vocabulary:cooked rice}, because you gotta eat cooked rice with every meal, so it's basically synonymous with \"meal\" itself.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Meal",
                "Alternatives": "Cooked Rice, Food",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3057"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3081\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6040-subject-3795.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3081\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29350-subject-3795.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: You're eating a {tooltip:Vocabulary:meal}... MMmm, delicious! What are you eating? Well, it's a {tooltip:Reading:Mesh} ({span:lang=ja:\u3081\u3057}) net. Taste the mesh net. It tastes terrible. This is a bad meal. Feel it in your mouth. It's weird and meshy.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\uff01\u98ef\u3092\u305f\u304f\u306e\u3092\u308f\u3059\u308c\u3066\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Oh no. I forgot to cook rice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u4e09\u5ea6\u306e\u98ef\u3088\u308a\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3092\u3059\u308b\u306e\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi would rather work for Tofugu than eat."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u305d\u3053\u306e\u98ef\u306f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u81ed\u304b\u3063\u305f\u305c\u3002\u4e8c\u5ea6\u3068\u5840\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u623b\u308a\u305f\u304f\u306d\u3048\u306a\u3002",
