                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3086\u3073\u308f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29250-subject-3900.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from the individual vocab readings, {span:lang=ja:\u6307} and {span:lang=ja:\u8f2a}. In English we don't distinguish some other ring from a \"finger ring\" but in Japanese, you can think of this as two separate words coming together to form one word, which is why it uses the kun'yomi vocab readings like this. So, if you know the individual words, you should be able to figure out this word is read as {span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3073\u308f}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u4e8b\u306a\u6307\u8f2a\u3092\u5931\u304f\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3001\u6c17\u5206\u304c\u6674\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I lost my precious ring and I feel awful."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6307\u8f2a\u304c\u6307\u304b\u3089\u5916\u308c\u306a\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I can't get this ring off of my finger."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30dc\u30fc\u30ca\u30b9\u304c\u51fa\u305f\u3089\u3001\u30c0\u30a4\u30e4\u30e2\u30f3\u30c9\u306e\u6307\u8f2a\u3092\u8cb7\u3063\u3066\u3084\u308b\u3088\u3002\u300d\u300c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u53e3\u5148\u3070\u304b\u308a\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"When I get a bonus, I\u2019ll buy you a diamond ring.\" \"You always say that, but words are just words.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

