{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:strange} {tooltip:Kanji:action} that takes place is something that shouldn't have happened (but it did). This is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:strange incident}. The difference between this and {span:lang=ja:\u4e8b\u5909} is that while {span:lang=ja:\u4e8b\u5909} can also be used to describe a strange incident, it also can be used to talk about another type of incident as well. For example, the \"Manshuu Jihen\" is the \"Manshuu Incident.\" This word, {span:lang=ja:\u5909\u4e8b} is more just a strange or unusual incident.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Strange Incident",
                "Alternative": "Unusual Incident",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3093\u3058"
