                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Just note that {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u304f} changes to {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3063} as many K-column sounds do in situations like this.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6628\u4eca\u306f\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u69d8\u306a\u5927\u7269\u306b\u304a\u76ee\u306b\u304b\u304b\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3081\u3063\u305f\u306b\u306a\u304f\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3088\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3055\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "Nowadays it is very rare to meet somebody big like you, Mr. Koichi."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6628\u4eca\u306e\u6d41\u884c\u308a\u306b\u3042\u3084\u304b\u3063\u3066\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u3067\u3057\u3070\u72ac\u3068\u30c1\u30f3\u30c9\u72ac\u3092\u304b\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306b\u6c7a\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Owing to recent trends, Koichi decided to have a Shiba-inu and a Jindo in our office."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6628\u4eca\u306f\u5c31\u8077\u6c37\u6cb3\u671f\u3060\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304c\u3001\u4f1a\u793e\u3092\u9078\u3070\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3069\u3053\u304b\u306b\u306f\u5c31\u8077\u3067\u304d\u308b\u306f\u305a\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "They say it's been a hard time for job seekers these days, but I'm sure you should be able to find a job if you're not picky about the company you work for."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:arrange} something with {tooltip:Kanji:reason} you're arranging it. That's why this is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to arrange}.",
