                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u672c\u3060\u306a\u3092\u6574\u7406\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3001\u5927\u5909\u611f\u8b1d\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I really appreciate that you organized the bookshelf."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u66f8\u308b\u3044\u3092\u5168\u3066\u6574\u7406\u3059\u308b\u306b\u306f\u3001\u5927\u5909\u306a\u6642\u9593\u3068\u52b4\u529b\u304c\u5fc5\u8981\u3067\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "It takes a great deal of time and effort to arrange all of these documents."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u8a71\u3092\u6574\u7406\u3055\u305b\u3066\u306d\u3002\u3064\u307e\u308a\u3001\u7537\u306e\u4eba\u304c\u6d6e\u6c17\u3092\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3044\u3044\u3051\u3069\u3001\u5973\u306e\u4eba\u304c\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3060\u3081\u3063\u3066\u3053\u3068\uff1f\u305d\u308c\u304c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u8a00\u3044\u305f\u3044\u3053\u3068\uff1f",
                    "en": "So let me get this straight. It\u2019s okay for men to cheat, but not for women. Is that what you\u2019re trying to say?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:arrange}, and the verb version also means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to arrange} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to put in order}. This has to do with putting things in their rightful place, getting affairs in order, or even preparing equipment.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Arrange",
                "Alternative": "To Put In Order",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3068\u306e\u3048\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3068\u306e\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6101-subject-7754.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3068\u306e\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29393-subject-7754.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Everything in your room has finally been {tooltip:Vocabulary:put in order}. Just as you finish, you hear a crash and turn to see your dog has jumped up onto your desk. \"{tooltip:Reading:Toto no} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3068\u306e})!\" you yell as he knocks everything over. Guess you have  {tooltip:Vocabulary:to arrange}  it all over again. Dammit Toto.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u3001\u53e3\u3072\u3052\u304c\u4e09\u89d2\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u6bce\u65e5\u6574\u3048\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet arranges his mustache into a triangle every morning."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7236\u306e\u305d\u3046\u304e\u306e\u624b\u306f\u305a\u306f\u3001\u5144\u304c\u5168\u3066\u6574\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My older brother put all the things in order regarding our father's funeral."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30db\u30eb\u30e2\u30f3\u30d0\u30e9\u30f3\u30b9\u3092\u6574\u3048\u308b\u65b9\u6cd5\u3092\u3054\u7d39\u4ecb\u81f4\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We\u2019ll introduce you to methods for getting your hormone balance in order."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u597d\u304d} is \"like.\" Although {span:lang=ja:\u597d\u304d} is kind of like a verb already, this is definitely a verb. It can be {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be fond of} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to like}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Fond Of",
                "Alternative": "To Like",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u306e\u3080"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u306e\u3080",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6091-subject-3575.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u306e\u3080",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29378-subject-3575.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is a strange one, different from anything you've learned, kanji on'yomi or vocab kun'yomi. The reading is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u306e}, so think of this. What is it that you're particularly fond of? Getting a {tooltip:Reading:cone} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u306e}) with your ice cream (which you're also fond of, who isn't?). Think of all the different cones you can get: waffle cones, sugar cones, oreo cones, yum!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u65e5\u672c\u9152\u306f\u3001\u5927\u5909\u9152\u597d\u304d\u3060\u3063\u305f\u79c1\u306e\u7236\u304c\u751f\u524d\u306b\u597d\u3093\u3067\u98f2\u3093\u3067\u3044\u305f\u3082\u306e\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This Japanese sake is what my heavy drinker of a father liked when he was alive."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u9ed2\u30cb\u30f3\u30cb\u30af\u3092\u597d\u3093\u3067\u98df\u3079\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi likes eating black garlic."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3055\u3093\u3001\u7533\u3057\u8a33\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304c\u3001\u597d\u3080\u3068\u597d\u307e\u3056\u308b\u3068\u306b\u95a2\u308f\u3089\u305a\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u79d8\u5bc6\u306f\u66b4\u9732\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3046\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m sorry, Mr. Koichi. Whether you like it or not, your secrets might get revealed."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:believe} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to believe}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Believe",
                "Alternative": "To Trust In",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093\u3058\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
