                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29368-subject-3732.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4fe1} is {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093} no matter what! See, if you believe, good things will happen. You should be able to read this.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u306a\u3044\u304c\u3001\u5b9f\u306f\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u30b9\u30d1\u30a4\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Believe it or not, Viet turned out to be a spy."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u76ee\u306b\u3057\u305f\u3082\u306e\u4ee5\u5916\u306f\u4fe1\u3058\u306a\u3044\u4e3b\u304e\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm the type of person who only trusts what they can actually see."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u3082\u306f\u3084\u30b5\u30f3\u30bf\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30b9\u3092\u4fe1\u3058\u3066\u3044\u306a\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3001\u6700\u8fd1\u30a4\u30e9\u30a4\u30e9\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b...\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I guess I've been irritated lately by the fact that I no longer believe in Santa Claus."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:build} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to build}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Build",
                "Alternative": "To Construct",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3066\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3066\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6060-subject-3756.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3066\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29374-subject-3756.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Think about what happens when you build something. What are you doing? You're standing it up. How do you say \"to stand\" in Japanese? {span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3066\u308b}. That's the reading of this word as well. If you think about it they're similar!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u7537\u306f\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u4e08\u592b\u306a\u5bb6\u3092\u5efa\u3066\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3067\u6709\u540d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This man is well known for building very sturdy houses."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u738b\u306f\u3001\u5c71\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u307b\u3069\u7f8e\u3057\u3044\u304a\u3057\u308d\u3092\u5efa\u3066\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The king built an unbelievably beautiful castle on top of the mountain."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6211\u304c\u793e\u306f\u3001\u5916\u56fd\u306e\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u305f\u3061\u306b\u5b66\u6821\u3092\u5efa\u3066\u3066\u3042\u3052\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u8caf\u91d1\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Our company is saving money to build a school for children in another country."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji is {tooltip:Kanji:change}, but this verb is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to change}. If you change one thing for another thing, you are going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to change} it, after all. This word refers to changing one thing for a similar thing.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Change",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3048\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "5773-subject-5983.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3048\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29213-subject-5983.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}I don't like this car. I would like {tooltip:Vocabulary:to change} it for another {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u4eba\u306b\u306a\u308b\u3068\u3001\u8003\u3048\u65b9\u3092\u5909\u3048\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3080\u305a\u304b\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When you become an adult, it's difficult to change your way of thinking."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3063\u3001\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u304f\u3061\u3073\u308b\u306e\u5f62\u306f\u5909\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\u305d\u308c\u306f\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u597d\u7269\u306e\u30bf\u30e9\u30b3\u3092\u30e2\u30c1\u30fc\u30d5\u306b\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002\u5909\u3048\u305f\u3089\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304c\u60b2\u3057\u307f\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Oh, please do not change the shape of Fugu's lips. They were inspired by Koichi's favorite food, cod roe. If you change them, Koichi will be sad."
                },
                {
