                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29229-subject-3789.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this is pretty weird. {span:lang=ja:\u8a08} is all nice and normal, but {span:lang=ja:\u6642} is {span:lang=ja:\u3068} for some reason. It probably is coming from the vocab word {span:lang=ja:\u6642} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u304d}), is my guess. But even if it is, it's shortened, making it a step more complicated. Maybe it's just better to imagine that your {tooltip:Vocabulary:watch} is a walky {tooltip:Reading:talky} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3051\u3044}) and run with that?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306b\u3082\u3089\u3063\u305f\u6642\u8a08\u3092\u8239\u304b\u3089\u843d\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi dropped the clock Viet had given him from the ship."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6642\u8a08\u53f0\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u3001\u4e09\u6642\u306b\u5f85\u3061\u5408\u308f\u305b\u306d\uff01",
                    "en": "We're gonna meet at the clock tower at 3 p.m., okay?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u306d\u3047\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u6642\u8a08\u306b\u553e\u304c\u7740\u3044\u3066\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
