{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is the same as the kanji. It means {tooltip:Radical:valley}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Valley"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This radical has a figure reaching out both hands at you with some dirt on his head. This is a {tooltip:Radical:zombie}, and he must have just recently dug himself out of the grave by the looks of it.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Zombie"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits a {tooltip:Radical:valley}, filling it up with water. Lucky for you, you're a giant, so you just lay down in the valley and use it to {tooltip:Kanji:bathe}.",
            "hints": "Sure, there's a lot of water in the valley, but you're big too. It's the perfect place for you to bathe... and good thing too, you're getting smelly.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bathe"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine cooking egg yolks in the same water you bathe in.",
                "mnemonic": "You know what would make the {tooltip:Kanji:bath}ing experience even better? If you had some egg {tooltip:Reading:yolk}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u304f}) to eat. Just crack those yolks into the water you bathe in, and it'll cook to perfection. Yum!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Having a keen {tooltip:Radical:eye} for woodworking, you can tell that the {tooltip:Radical:bamboo} from that {tooltip:Radical:tree} over there will make an excellent {tooltip:Kanji:box}. Boxes made from bamboo trees are very sturdy and fashionable. You have an eye for fashion as well, you see.",
            "hints": "At some point in school, you most likely had some sort of woodshop class to take. Remember back to those times and imagine yourself crafting a bamboo box out of a bamboo tree you felled yourself. Don\u2019t forget to wear eye protection though! Wouldn\u2019t want anything to happen to those valuable eyes of yours.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Box"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3053",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the hawk landing in the box and grumpily trying to stuff it full of straw and twigs. At least your beautiful box will be put to good use.",
                "mnemonic": "While working on your wooden {tooltip:Kanji:box} you hear a strange cry from above. You look up and see an angry {tooltip:Reading:hawk} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3053}) flying overhead. Oh no! That bamboo you cut down must have been where the hawk lived. Imagine finishing up the box, climbing up some bamboo and tying the box securely up there as a replacement home for the hawk."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A psychic {tooltip:Radical:leader} can pick a {tooltip:Radical:thread} up off the {tooltip:Radical:ground} and make a {tooltip:Kanji:connection} with the person that it came from. This leader is very powerful, so even a thread is enough for them to make a psychic connection with the person who was wearing the thread.",
            "hints": "Imagine you are this leader and you just picked up this piece of thread from the ground. You get a jarring psychic connection with the owner of the thread. Your head spins, your heart races, and your hands tremble. Picture this happening to you as you pick up the thread from the ground.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Connection"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304b, \u304b\u304b\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Because the connection is so strong, you feel like you too are eating the cake. You taste the fluffy and creamy vanilla strawberry flavors washing over your tongue. Imagine yourself eating this delectable cake. It\u2019s fantastically delicious.",
                "mnemonic": "As you develop this psychic {tooltip:Kanji:connection} with the owner of the thread, you can tell that he is currently eating a {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}). Since the connection is so strong, you feel like you are eating the cake as well. It\u2019s vanilla strawberry."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "After a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}, use this {tooltip:Radical:machine} to {tooltip:Kanji:cure} the people and the country from the damage. {tooltip:Kanji:Heal}ing machines are all over Japan just in case a tsunami does way more damage than they can handle. ",
            "hints": "Imagine if you had your own machine to cure yourself if a tsunami came to where you live. It would be pretty convenient!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cure",
                "Alternatives": "Heal, Reign, Rule"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058, \u3061",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine getting Jesus to cure half the people and feeding the other half lots of cheese and their wounds miraculously healing on their own! You're a hero!",
                "mnemonic": "Alternative ways to {tooltip:Kanji:cure} yourself after a tsunami are either praying to {tooltip:Reading:Je}sus ({span:lang=ja:\u3058}) or eating your weight in {tooltip:Reading:chee}se ({span:lang=ja:\u3061}). I'm not sure if I have enough cheese for all the people that got hit though... Hmm, do you have cheese?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a {tooltip:Radical:prison} on a {tooltip:Radical:cliff} surrounded by {tooltip:Radical:snake}s. Now that's a {tooltip:Kanji:dangerous} place. If you try to escape the prison you either fall to your death off the cliff or get bitten/squeezed to death by the snakes. Can you think of anything more dangerous than this? I can't.",
            "hints": "Imagine a dangerous prison surrounded by cliffs and snakes. You wouldn't want to be here either, would you?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dangerous"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3076, \u3042\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine staring at the key dangling right outside of the dangerous prison you're trapped in. Would you take the chance and go for it?",
                "mnemonic": "Lucky for you, even though you're stuck in this {tooltip:Kanji:dangerous} place, there is hope. There is a {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}). All dangerous prisons have a key. You just have to find and steal it so you can avoid the cliffs and snakes!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When the {tooltip:Radical:sun} gets in your {tooltip:Radical:eye}, I {tooltip:Kanji:dare} you to stare at it. I dare you to look right at the sun. I dare you.",
            "hints": "Looking at the sun straight on hurts. It\u2019s bad for your eyes and burns your brain. Imagine how painful it is to stare at the sun.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dare"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself bowling without the power of sight. It would be awfully difficult to do well. You\u2019d just have to concentrate really hard on the sound of the pins and determine where you need to throw the ball.",
                "mnemonic": "After you\u2019ve blinded yourself from the {tooltip:Kanji:dare} of looking at the sun and losing sight in each eye, the guy dares you to go {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}). You\u2019re blind now, so bowling will be quite the challenge."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A group of {tooltip:Radical:private} {tooltip:Radical:sword} guys are in your {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy}. You must {tooltip:Kanji:detain} them at once! Private sword guys are people who work for private companies and use their swords on people. They're basically paid assassins. And you're going to detain them!",
            "hints": "Imagine running into the rice paddy and detaining the private sword holders one by one. They won't get away this time!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Detain"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308b, \u308a\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If Ryu hadn't shown up with this loophole you never would have detained all these private sword guys by yourself!",
                "mnemonic": "You're running out of steam and you're afraid you might not be able to {tooltip:Kanji:detain} all of these guys when {tooltip:Reading:Ryu} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3085\u3046}) from Street Fighter appears. He hates swords, and will only use fists because it's the honorable way to fight, so he starts helping you detain them!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you listened in to the {tooltip:Radical:private} lives of {tooltip:Radical:twenty} people, all of them would have different {tooltip:Kanji:dialect}s and ways of {tooltip:Kanji:speech}. Whether they actually use these dialects with you is another story. But when they're alone, or with other people who are from the same place, their speech will be different.",
            "hints": "Can you even imagine twenty different dialects in your head? Well I can tell you that there are definitely at least twenty of them in Japan alone.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dialect",
                "Alternative": "Speech"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It also helps that bento are delicious, and anyone with any dialect will love them.",
                "mnemonic": "The best way to learn someone's {tooltip:Kanji:dialect} is to buy them a {tooltip:Reading:ben}to ({span:lang=ja:\u3079\u3093}) from where they're from. Not only do these bento have writing in their dialect on them, but their speech will immediately shift to match. Then you'll be able to hear how they sound in their head and in private!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What I {tooltip:Radical:say} is {tooltip:Radical:correct} 100%! You may use it as {tooltip:Kanji:evidence} in this murder case.",
            "hints": "You convince the officials questioning you that your evidence can be trusted and it's {tooltip:Kanji:proof} that you definitely didn't have anything to do with any law breaking or murdering.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Evidence",
                "Alternative": "Proof"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304b\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You better hope the Shougun believes your evidence is accurate, because he's known to kill people willy-nilly when he thinks they're lying.",
                "mnemonic": "The officials force you to present this {tooltip:Kanji:evidence} in front of the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}), himself. Your knees quake, you feel like you're gonna be sick, but you try to stand up tall and tell him everything. After all, you know your {tooltip:Kanji:proof} is correct, so you shouldn't be so scared."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:narwhal} {tooltip:Radical:stick}s a {tooltip:Radical:child} with its horn then you have to admit that it {tooltip:Kanji:exist}s. We know some of you have been doubting narwhals and whether they're real. Well now your kid is a kabob, so do you believe they exist now? I {tooltip:Kanji:suppose} you do.",
            "hints": "Imagine needing this kind of horrible proof to believe something exists. Maybe you should have more faith in what we teach.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Exist",
                "Alternative": "Suppose"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3093, \u305e\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I suppose you'll never forget that narwhals exist now that your son has one permanently stuck in him.",
                "mnemonic": "Oh, and the child we had to narwhal stab to prove they {tooltip:Kanji:exist} - that's your {tooltip:Reading:son} ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3093}). Maybe you should have listened and kept your son out of the Narwhal Danger {tooltip:Reading:Zone} ({span:lang=ja:\u305e\u3093}) after we warned you about it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:face} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:face} kanji are the same! But this isn't just a face like the one you're looking at your computer/phone with. It's the {tooltip:Kanji:surface} kind of face too!",
            "hints": "The next time you look at your face, also notice how much surface area it has.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Face",
                "Alternative": "Surface"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082, \u304a\u3082\u3066",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Look at the face of all men put together. Measure how much surface area they all take up.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:face} you're looking at, that has a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:surface} area, belongs to {tooltip:Reading:men} ({span:lang=ja:\u3081\u3093}). Not a single man, but all men put together. It's hundreds of thousands of men's faces in a row."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} with a {tooltip:Radical:zombie} on it, going really {tooltip:Kanji:far} away. Someone tied that zombie to the scooter and now it's far off in the distance, groaning and growling.",
            "hints": "Picture the zombie, going far off into the distance. It's getting smaller and harder to see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Far"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I mean, to be fair, the zombie wasn't really alive to begin with. But going far enough to end it all? That's some serious distance!",
                "mnemonic": "The zombie goes so {tooltip:Kanji:far}, that its life {tooltip:Reading:en}ds ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3093}). Zombies need to eat to live (it's really all they need), but they go so far on their scooter trip, that they just give up and end it all."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You examine the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of a {tooltip:Radical:zombie} and find a small {tooltip:Kanji:garden} in there. There are even benches... it looks like a {tooltip:Kanji:park}.",
            "hints": "Zombies are dead, so I guess their mouths have all the things garden plants crave. Their mouths are like compost piles, if you think about it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Garden",
                "Alternative": "Park"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh. The zombie probably bit down on your head and now it's the end for you. At least you were looking at a nice garden at the end of it all...",
                "mnemonic": "You look closer at the {tooltip:Kanji:garden} and suddenly everything {tooltip:Reading:en}ds ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The radical for {tooltip:Radical:gate} and the kanji for {tooltip:Kanji:gates} are the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals or you won't be allowed to pass.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gates",
                "Alternative": "Gate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "They start pounding on the gate, and it begins to budge. Focus in on their moaning noises, because that's the reading of this kanji, but also feel the fear as well. When you start moaning too, it seems to calm them. Go ahead and pretend you're in front of this gate, and moan out loud for me a bit. Uwhhhhhh. Muhehwhhhhhhh.",
                "mnemonic": "You're standing in front of some {tooltip:Kanji:gates}. You can't get through them, but on the other side you hear all kinds of loud {tooltip:Reading:moan}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3093}). Are those zombie noises? Is this gate to keep the zombies out, or in?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:canopy} {tooltip:Radical:attach}ing your entire country is the {tooltip:Kanji:government}. They loom over you all and try to keep you all organized and together under their control.",
            "hints": "Picture a map of the world with actual canopies attached to each government, representing the ruling governments of each place.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Government"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Think of all the people who've been labeled as fools by the government because they try to detach themselves from under their reach. It's a pretty long list...",
                "mnemonic": "Try to get out from under this {tooltip:Kanji:government} canopy and you'll be labeled a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}). Unless... you can fool them!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put a {tooltip:Radical:lid} on something {tooltip:Radical:spicy} and you'll cook up pure {tooltip:Kanji:happiness}.",
            "hints": "Spicy foods literally do trigger happy chemicals in your brain. It wouldn't be too far off to say that putting a lid on a pot filled with something spicy could produce happiness.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Happiness"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3042\u308f, \u3055\u3044\u308f, \u3055\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "{span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} looks sad. But when you serve him happiness, he starts to perk up a bit. A couple more bites of happiness, and there's a smile on his face. Although when you found {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} he was depressed, down on his luck, and hiding from the government, cooking him some spicy foods seems to have brought him some happiness.",
                "mnemonic": "Out of spicy foods you made pure {tooltip:Kanji:happiness}. You give it to your sad friend {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, who waits at the table."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you're {tooltip:Radical:anti}-{tooltip:Radical:building}, you're probably afraid of {tooltip:Kanji:heights} and {tooltip:Kanji:slopes}. The only downside to a building is that they're high and if you fall off of them you could die. So if someone says they're anti-building, they're really just anti-heights.",
            "hints": "Imagine standing on the edge of a very high building. If you feel sick or upset, you may be one of these anti-height people!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Heights",
                "Alternative": "Slope"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine standing at the top of a tall building with Han Solo. He's very afraid of heights. They make him nervous. Like something bad will happen if he were to ever stand above a big pit, high up.",
                "mnemonic": "Another person you know who's afraid of {tooltip:Kanji:heights} is {tooltip:Reading:Han} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}) Solo. Now wait, you may be thinking, he flies a space ship! You're right, because he doesn't like to walk all the way up high buildings, it freaks him out. He flies up instead so he doesn't have to think about falling."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:wolverine}'s {tooltip:Radical:heart} is in {tooltip:Radical:prison}, so you need to {tooltip:Kanji:hurry} to set it free. If you don't hurry, its heart won't survive. And the wolverine's death will be on you.",
            "hints": "Imagine a dying wolverine, its heart trapped in a prison. Hurry, save it! You aren't going fast enough! Hurry, hurry!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hurry"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Cucumbers help you hurry to where you need to go. Something about the smell, crunch, and taste helps you hurry it up.",
                "mnemonic": "You're trying to {tooltip:Kanji:hurry} as fast as you can to save the wolverine. But you're losing strength, so you grab a {tooltip:Reading:cu}cumber ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3085\u3046}) from your bag and munch on it to get some of your hurrying power back."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Bamboo} {tooltip:Radical:heaven} is a place for {tooltip:Kanji:laugh}ing. Bamboo is a very jolly plant, and they love to laugh. Even after death in bamboo heaven, the bamboo continue to laugh joyfully. Bamboo heaven is truly a place of laughter.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself as a bamboo plant that laughs in heaven. What are you laughing about? Chuckle to yourself as you remember this kanji.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Laugh"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
