{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:roof} needs {tooltip:Radical:measurement}s done every year to make sure it will {tooltip:Kanji:protect} you properly.",
            "hints": "If you think about it, your roof protects you from a lot of things! Rain, snow, bird poop. But if your roof's measurements are off it won't be able to protect you properly.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Protect"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059, \u3057\u3085",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3082, \u3082\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Odds are, the roof collapsed or a tree fell on you and you died from lack of protection. So now your family and friends are going to sue on your behalf.",
                "mnemonic": "If the measurements are off, and your roof doesn't {tooltip:Kanji:protect} you, then you get to {tooltip:Reading:sue} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059})! If you're still alive, that is."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Radical:tongue} becomes too {tooltip:Radical:spicy} for you to bear, it\u2019s time to {tooltip:Kanji:quit} the jalape\u00f1o eating contest. You\u2019ve been eating them for three hours now and the spiciness from the peppers is really burning your tongue. Throw in the towel, it\u2019s time to quit the contest.",
            "hints": "You may have to quit eating but you never have to quit saying words. Especially if you're, well, trying to learn a whole new language full of them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Quit",
                "Alternative": "Word"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Jesus scarfing down jalape\u00f1o peppers. He never quits. And then he says some words about how the jalape\u00f1os gave up their lives for this contest, so we better appreciate them. Thanks Jesus!",
                "mnemonic": "Oh, you're probably wondering who won that spicy food contest after you {tooltip:Kanji:quit} and became obsessed with {tooltip:Kanji:word}s instead. It was {tooltip:Reading:Je}sus ({span:lang=ja:\u3058}). Who did you expect? He was great with words AND never quitting when things got spicy."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the {tooltip:Radical:pope} spends all day staring at {tooltip:Radical:fins} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground}, he\u2019s going to lose touch with {tooltip:Kanji:reality}. He should be focusing on his popish duties, but instead he\u2019s looking at the fish fins he dropped, and now can\u2019t eat because they\u2019re dirty. Silly pope. You can\u2019t let this one thing get you down. You have other things to do.",
            "hints": "Picture trying to get the pope to stop staring at the fins laying on the dirty ground. His eyes are all big. Yup, he\u2019s completely lost touch with reality, you think.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reality"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the pope angrily kicking your shin super hard. You fall over and pull it close. Feel how badly it aches. Who knew you\u2019d need shin guards to deal with a pope that\u2019s lost touch with reality just from dropping his dinner.",
                "mnemonic": "You\u2019re doing your best to bring the pope back to {tooltip:Kanji:reality} when he snaps and kicks you in the {tooltip:Reading:shin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}). Oww! What the heck, pope! But he\u2019s already back staring at the fins and your shin is throbbing where he kicked."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:gate} of {tooltip:Radical:horns} will take you to {tooltip:Radical:heaven}. These horns are {tooltip:Kanji:related} and {tooltip:Kanji:connected} to heaven in some way.",
            "hints": "Perhaps they are related to heaven because the devil has horns? Perhaps they are connected to heaven because these are the horns of heaven's enemies? The real reason they're connected will be revealed in the reading mnemonic.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Related",
                "Alternative": "Connected"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304b, \u305b\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine Genghis Khan taking horns off his enemies, and making a gate to heaven. The horn gate is connected to both heaven and Genghis Khan in that way.",
                "mnemonic": "They are {tooltip:Kanji:related} and {tooltip:Kanji:connected} to heaven because these are the horns that Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) made from his enemies. God said he could come into heaven if he made a gate of horns, so that's what he did."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Going into a {tooltip:Radical:building} made by a {tooltip:Radical:squid} is {tooltip:Kanji:risky}. First of all, squids only have tentacles, no bones, and they make all of their buildings out of risky materials like kelp and sharp coral.",
            "hints": "One squid got stuck in his own building, but no one could save him because going in would be too risky. Poor little squid.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Risky",
                "Alternative": "Steep"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The squid cries, \"I can build one that isn't so risky next time!\" Ken shakes his head, \"I'm not letting you do anymore risky things, you're coming with me from now on.\" Ken scoops up the squid into a bucket, hoists him over his shoulder, and walks off into the sunset.{splitParent}Who knows what adventures await our new duo. All we know is that they'll definitely be getting into some risky business.",
                "mnemonic": "\"It's too {tooltip:Kanji:risky}, leave me!\" the squid cries. \"I'll save you, underwater citizen! Nothing is too risky for {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai!\" The building is collapsing on the squid, the risk is so great, but Ken the samurai dives in and saves him!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you play {tooltip:Radical:music} with your {tooltip:Radical:fins}, one {tooltip:Kanji:rule} is that you must be a fish. You can\u2019t play music using fish fins that don\u2019t belong to you. That\u2019s the rule. And it\u2019s also rude.",
            "hints": "Imagine a fish playing music using his fins. What kind of a song is it? Imagine it in your head as you see a sign with the fish fin rule on it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rule"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a group of ten (as per the rule) fish playing music with their fins. Now the song can be louder and more intricate. Imagine it playing in your head.",
                "mnemonic": "There\u2019s also a {tooltip:Kanji:rule} in place to limit the amount of fish fin musicians. No more than {tooltip:Reading:ten} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3093}) are allowed to gather and play their music together. That\u2019s the rule. No more than ten."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Sticking a {tooltip:Radical:cross} into a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} to get its {tooltip:Radical:measurement}s is your {tooltip:Kanji:specialty}. Most people get really confused when they have to measure their rice paddies, but that's where you come in. You plant a cross right in the middle, look down it from one end to the other, and voila! You know the measurements immediately. That's why it's your specialty!",
            "hints": "Visualize yourself doing this. The numbers just come to you. It's just what you're good at. Your specialty is something no one else in the world is as good at as you!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Specialty"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3063\u3071",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself at a centaur funeral. Tons of centaurs standing around and stamping their hooves as you make your measurement and stick a cross into the ground.",
                "mnemonic": "Hearing of your amazing {tooltip:Kanji:specialty} and cross measurement abilities, a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}) from a far off land recruits you for a job. The centaur\u2019s father has just passed away and the centaur wants you to measure the rice paddies that have been left to him."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:forehead} {tooltip:Radical:table} is completely {tooltip:Kanji:superfluous}.",
            "hints": "Seriously, you don't need a forehead table. It's totally unnecessary to have a table made of foreheads and is a superfluous purchase. First of all, getting all those foreheads is a waste of people. Second, forehead tables aren't very strong. Superfluous, superfluous, superfluous.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Superfluous",
                "Alternatives": "Unnecessary, Uselessness"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
