                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u82b8\u8853\u5bb6\u306e\u4f5c\u54c1\u306b\u306f\u3001\u82e6\u7b11\u3044\u304c\u304b\u304f\u305b\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I can't hide my wry smile at this artist's works."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u82b8\u8853\u5bb6\u306f\u3001\u5f1f\u5b50\u306b\u7559\u5b88\u756a\u3092\u305f\u306e\u3093\u3067\u3001\u30e8\u30fc\u30ed\u30c3\u30d1\u306b\u7559\u5b66\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The artist asked his disciple to look after his house while he was away and left for Europe to study."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u518d\u6765\u6708\u306e\u30de\u30e9\u30bd\u30f3\u5927\u4f1a\u3001\u82b8\u8853\u5bb6\u9054\u3068\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u53c2\u52a0\u3059\u308b\u3063\u3066\u306e\u306f\u3069\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "How about running a marathon with a bunch of artists the month after next?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "An {tooltip:Kanji:automatic}{tooltip:Kanji:al} ({span:lang=ja:\u81ea\u52d5} + {span:lang=ja:\u7684}) thing of course isn't \"automatical.\" A better way to say it is to cut off the -al and call it {tooltip:Vocabulary:automatic}.",
