                        "pronunciation": "\u3052\u3072\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29591-subject-3818.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You haven't seen this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u4e0b} yet (sorry there's so many for this kanji!) so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}Those items are so {tooltip:Vocabulary:crude} that you can't even tell what they're supposed to be. Honestly they all just look like statues of lumpy {tooltip:Reading:ge}ckos ({span:lang=ja:\u3052}). That says it's a lamp but it looks more like a gecko looking at the sky. That chair? Definitely a bunch of geckos having a pool party. Are you sure you didn't get this stuff from a weird gecko artist?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u4e0b\u54c1\u306a\u82f1\u8a9e\u306e\u57fa\u672c\u3092\u30de\u30b9\u30bf\u30fc\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I've mastered the fundamentals of vulgar English."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u306f\u308b\u304b\u9060\u304f\u304b\u3089\u3001\u4e0b\u54c1\u306a\u7b11\u3044\u58f0\u304c\u805e\u3053\u3048\u3066\u304d\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I heard a vulgar laugh from the distance."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u4e0b\u54c1\u306a\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u306f\u4f1a\u793e\u306b\u623b\u3063\u3066\u304b\u3089\u3058\u3063\u304f\u308a\u8aad\u307e\u305b\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019ll carefully read your crude email for you when I get back to the office."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:dangerous}? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:dangerous}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dangerous",
                "Alternative": "Risky",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3076\u306a\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3076\u306a\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6592-subject-3816.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3076\u306a\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29629-subject-3816.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Someone is in danger! It's poor old {tooltip:Reading:abe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3076}) Lincoln. You try to save him, yelling out {span:lang=ja:\u5371\u306a\u3044\u3088\uff01\uff01\uff01\uff01}, but he gets shot in the back of the head anyways.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5371\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3089\u3001\u8eca\u306b\u8377\u7269\u3092\u3064\u3080\u306e\u306f\u529b\u306e\u5f37\u3044\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306b\u3084\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3089\u304a\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "It's dangerous, so just leave loading the baggage into the car to Viet, who's strong."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u56db\u3064\u8449\u306e\u30af\u30ed\u30fc\u30d0\u30fc\u3092\u898b\u3064\u3051\u305f\u3089\u5e78\u904b\u304c\u304a\u3068\u305a\u308c\u308b\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3051\u3069\u3001\u304e\u3083\u304f\u306b\u5371\u306a\u3044\u76ee\u306b\u3042\u3063\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "They say if you find a four-leaf clover, you'll have good luck, but I got in a dangerous situation instead."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5371\u306a\u3044\u4f1a\u793e\u306e\u3053\u3093\u306a\u306b\u5371\u306a\u3044\u8a08\u753b\u306b\u5dfb\u304d\u8fbc\u307e\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3001\u8ab0\u3082\u53cd\u5bfe\u3057\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u306a\u3093\u3066\u4fe1\u3058\u3089\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "I can\u2019t believe no one opposed getting involved in the risky plan of such a risky company."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:weekday} {tooltip:Kanji:day} is the {tooltip:Vocabulary:day of the week}, as in \"Monday\" or \"Tuesday.\" You'll be learning those on level 18, but first you should learn {span:lang=ja:\u66dc\u65e5} to get you prepared.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Day Of The Week",
                "Alternative": "Weekday",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046\u3073"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3046\u3073",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6237-subject-3948.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3088\u3046\u3073",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29453-subject-3948.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses the on'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u66dc} and the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u65e5}. You've learned both of these already, but be careful because {span:lang=ja:\u3072} of {span:lang=ja:\u65e5} changes to {span:lang=ja:\u3073} here.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c34\u66dc\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u30cd\u30a4\u30c6\u30a3\u30d6\u304c\u8a71\u3059\u30b9\u30d4\u30fc\u30c9\u3067\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u3092\u8a71\u3059\u65e5\u306b\u3057\u307e\u305b\u3093\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Why don't we make Wednesday the day we try speaking Japanese at the speed of native speakers?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u3063\u3066\u4f55\u66dc\u65e5\u3060\u3063\u3051\uff1f",
                    "en": "What day of the week is today?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u809d\u5fc3\u306a\u306e\u306f\u3001\u3053\u306e\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u8ab2\u984c\u3092\u91d1\u66dc\u65e5\u307e\u3067\u306b\u7d42\u308f\u3089\u305b\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3046\u3053\u3068\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "The bottom line is that we have to finish this Japanese assignment by Friday."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
