                        "file": "6204-subject-3875.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304c\u3044\u3081\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29448-subject-3875.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. This reading is usually for building exteriors and outside surfaces. The other reading {span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3068\u3065\u3089} is used when a person's personality comes to the surface and is a bit of an exception, so you'll probably see it less often. Just keep those differences in mind!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u5916\u9762\u306f\u3044\u3044\u4eba\u305d\u3046\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u5b9f\u306f\u3068\u3066\u3082\u304a\u305d\u308d\u3057\u3044\u4e00\u9762\u3092\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "On the surface, Viet looks like a nice guy, but he actually has a scary side."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5916\u9762\u3060\u3051\u304c\u3044\u3044\u7537\u6027\u3068\u3051\u3063\u3053\u3093\u3057\u3001\u5916\u9762\u306f\u7acb\u3071\u3060\u3051\u3069\u5185\u9762\u306f\u30dc\u30ed\u30dc\u30ed\u306e\u4e2d\u53e4\u4f4f\u305f\u304f\u3092\u8cb7\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3001\u4eca\u3068\u3066\u3082\u82e6\u52b4\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm married to a man who is an angel outside and a devil at home, and we bought an older home that has a fine exterior, but the interior is worn out, so I'm having a tough time right now."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f7c\u306e\u5916\u9762\u306b\u9a19\u3055\u308c\u306a\u3044\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002\u79c1\u304c\u30a4\u30f3\u30b9\u30c8\u30e9\u30af\u30bf\u30fc\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304c\u5acc\u3044\u3060\u3063\u305f\u306e\u306f\u3001\u4e0a\u53f8\u306b\u306f\u3044\u3044\u9854\u3092\u3057\u3066\u9670\u3067\u5f8c\u8f29\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3092\u5c0f\u7a81\u304d\u56de\u3057\u3066\u3044\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "You shouldn\u2019t be fooled by his outward appearance. I hated my instructor because he showed his superiors a nice face while he bullied subordinates, including me, behind their backs."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:face} of a {tooltip:Kanji:face} is a face, but more specifically the {tooltip:Vocabulary:face of a person}. Probably because the most face-like thing you can ever have is a human's face... at least in our eyes (by \"our\" I mean the human race's eyes, because I am totally with you guys on that one).",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Face Of A Person",
                "Alternatives": "Person's Face, Face",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3093\u3081\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304c\u3093\u3081\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6267-subject-7491.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304c\u3093\u3081\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29467-subject-7491.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u9854} isn't the one you learned with the kanji. But, we're going to learn that reading right now.\n{splitParent}The worst thing that can happen to a face is if a face disappears. If it becomes totally {tooltip:Reading:gone} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3093}). A man that is walking up to you with no face, is a man with a gone face. Those men are men who are a part of the {tooltip:Reading:gone men} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3093\u3081\u3093}). Faces, totally gone!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u793e\u54e1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u3001\u307f\u3093\u306a\u9854\u9762\u3078\u3093\u3055\u3061\u304c\u9ad8\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu workers' facial deviation values are all very high."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b9\u30c8\u30ec\u30b9\u304c\u539f\u56e0\u306e\u9854\u9762\u795e\u3051\u3044\u3064\u3046\u306b\u306a\u3084\u307e\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm suffering from facial neuralgia caused by stress."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u30a2\u30b9\u30d5\u30a1\u30eb\u30c8\u306b\u9854\u9762\u3092\u5f37\u6253\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I hit my face hard on the asphalt."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u5408\u683c\u3059\u308b} is \"to pass a test,\" so what's the opposite of that? {tooltip:Vocabulary:Fail a test} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:failure}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fail A Test",
                "Alternatives": "Failure, Rejection",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3054\u3046\u304b\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3075\u3054\u3046\u304b\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
