                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3044\u3044\u4eba\u3055\u3092\u524d\u9762\u306b\u51fa\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet always puts his good man-ness to the front."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u524d\u9762\u3082\u5f8c\u9762\u3082\u4e21\u65b9\u3068\u3082\u7dd1\u8272\u306e\u7bb1\u3092\u3055\u304c\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please find a box that has green on both the front and back sides."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u624b\u7d19\u3084\u5c0f\u5305\u3092\u9001\u308b\u6642\u306b\u306f\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u524d\u9762\u306bTofugu\u306e\u30b9\u30c6\u30c3\u30ab\u30fc\u3092\u8cbc\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Whenever we send a letter or a package, we put the Tofugu sticker on the front of it."
