                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u962a\u795e\u96fb\u8eca\u30ab\u30e9\u30fc\u306e\u30bc\u30ea\u30fc\u3092\u6c37\u3067\u3072\u3084\u3057\u3066\u56fa\u3081\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm setting the Hanshin Electric Railway colored jelly by cooling it with ice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u5ea6\u3001\u962a\u795e\u5730\u533a\u306b\u65b0\u7bc9\u306e\u5bb6\u3092\u8cb7\u304a\u3046\u3068\u601d\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u76f8\u5834\u306f\u3044\u304f\u3089\u3050\u3089\u3044\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "I am thinking about buying a newly-built house in the Hanshin district. About how much is the market price?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u308f\u3041\u3001\u962a\u795e\u30bf\u30a4\u30ac\u30fc\u30b9\u306e\u30d5\u30a1\u30f3\u305f\u3061\u3001\u6075\u6bd4\u5bff\u6a4b\u304b\u3089\u3042\u306e\u6c5a\u3044\u5ddd\u306b\u30c0\u30a4\u30d6\u3057\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3063\u3066\uff1f\u3059\u3052\u3047\u306a\u3001\u3042\u3044\u3064\u3089\u306e\u982d\u5927\u4e08\u592b\u304b\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "Oh my God! Hanshin Tigers fans dived off the Ebisu bridge down into the dirty river? Wow, they are nuts!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is the noun version of the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u5e78}. Kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:happiness} and the vocab word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:happiness}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Happiness",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306a adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3042\u308f\u305b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3042\u308f\u305b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6347-subject-3833.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u3042\u308f\u305b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29499-subject-3833.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}On your quest for true {tooltip:Vocabulary:happiness}, you meet a happiness guru. {tooltip:Reading:She always says} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3042\u308f\u305b}), \"just be happy!\" She always says that, and you always listen. You can't believe how simple yet profound her approach is! \n\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u672b\u306a\u304c\u304f\u304a\u5e78\u305b\u306b\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I wish you happiness for many years to come."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u3001\u3046\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3057\u304b\u3089\u4eca\u5e74\u4e2d\u306b\u5e78\u305b\u304c\u304a\u3068\u305a\u308c\u308b\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "A fortune teller told Viet that happiness will come to him within the year."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u79c1\u306f\u304a\u91d1\u3067\u5e78\u305b\u306f\u8cb7\u3048\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4f55\u6545\u306a\u3089\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u82b1\u706b\u3092\u898b\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u5e78\u305b\u306a\u6c17\u6301\u3061\u306b\u306a\u308b\u304b\u3089\u3067\u3059\u3002\u3082\u3057\u79c1\u304c\u5927\u91d1\u6301\u3061\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u6bce\u65e5\u82b1\u706b\u3092\u697d\u3057\u3093\u3067\u305a\u3063\u3068\u5e78\u305b\u306a\u6c17\u6301\u3061\u3067\u3044\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002\u300d\u5f7c\u5973\u306f\u5e78\u305b\u305d\u3046\u306a\u53e3\u8abf\u3067\u305d\u3046\u8a00\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "\"I think money can buy happiness because watching fireworks makes me happy. If I had a lot of money, I could enjoy fireworks every day and feel happy all the time,\" she said happily."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "With a little {tooltip:Kanji:luck} and {tooltip:Kanji:happiness} you can achieve {tooltip:Vocabulary:happiness}, though that goes without saying.",
