{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:face} of this object is so {tooltip:Kanji:white}! Why is it so white compared to everything else? This is so {tooltip:Vocabulary:interesting}...",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Interesting",
                "Alternatives": "Amusing, Funny",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082\u3057\u308d\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3082\u3057\u308d\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6544-subject-3878.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u3082\u3057\u308d\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29589-subject-3878.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is unlike what you've learned before, at least with the {span:lang=ja:\u9762} part ({span:lang=ja:\u767d\u3044} is just like the vocab word {span:lang=ja:\u767d\u3044}). When you look at the white face of the object you say to your friend Moe: \"{tooltip:Reading:Oh mo}!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3082}) because you want him to come over and look at this. Try to imagine someone you know named Moe, or at least a celebrity or something named Moe.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3044\u3064\u306f\u9762\u767d\u3044\u3084\u3064\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3050\u5207\u308c\u308b\u306e\u304c\u30cd\u30c3\u30af\u3060\u3088\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "He is an amusing guy, his only downside is that he gets angry over the smallest things."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u30de\u30f3\u30ac\u306f\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u4e0b\u54c1\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3068\u3066\u3082\u9762\u767d\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This manga is a bit crude but it's very interesting."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306f\u306f\u306f\u306f\uff01\u8d85\u30a6\u30b1\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002\u4eca\u307e\u3067\u805e\u3044\u305f\u4e2d\u3067\u3001\u4e00\u756a\u9762\u767d\u3044\u8a71\u3060\u308f\u3002",
                    "en": "Ahahaha! You crack me up, Fugu! That\u2019s the funniest thing I\u2019ve ever heard."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:discuss} something {tooltip:Kanji:superfluous} you aren't being serious, you're telling a {tooltip:Vocabulary:joke}.",
