                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29633-subject-3814.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3064\u307e\u3089\u306a\u3044\u5197\u8ac7\u306b\u4fc2\u308f\u3063\u3066\u308b\u3072\u307e\u306f\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I have no time to waste on a stupid joke."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u30dd\u30c3\u30c9\u30ad\u30e3\u30b9\u30c8\u3067\u5197\u8ac7\u3070\u304b\u308a\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u304c\u3001\u6642\u3005\u5197\u8ac7\u306e\u901a\u3058\u306a\u3044\u4eba\u304b\u3089\u3044\u304b\u308a\u306e\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u3092\u3082\u3089\u3046\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu likes joking on their podcast, but sometimes they get angry emails from people who don't get the jokes."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5197\u8ac7\u306f\u30e4\u30e1\u3066\u3088\uff01\u4f55\u3067\u30d5\u30ec\u30f3\u30c1\u30ec\u30b9\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u306a\u3093\u3066\u884c\u304d\u305f\u3044\u306e\uff1f\u79c1\u9054\u306e\u67c4\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u3063\u3057\u3087\u3002\u98f2\u3081\u308c\u3070\u3069\u3053\u3067\u3082\u3044\u3044\u3058\u3083\u3093\uff1f\u9055\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "Stop joking around. Why do you want to go to a French restaurant? We shouldn\u2019t break our pattern. If we\u2019re just going drinking, anywhere is fine, right?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Vocabulary:Kansai} region of Japan is the Southern Central part of Japan. It actually {tooltip:Kanji:connects} the East side of Japan (at least back in the day) to the West side, making it the \"connection to the west.\" For our purposes, though, we should call it \"Kansai.\"",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Kansai",
                "Word Type": "proper noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093\u3055\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3093\u3055\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6510-subject-3951.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3093\u3055\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29570-subject-3951.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Urgh, what a confusing reading! The {span:lang=ja:\u897f} is {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044} instead of {span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}. Readings like this just make you want to {tooltip:Reading:sigh} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044}), no?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30a4\u30b1\u30eb\u306f\u3001\u95a2\u897f\u4e00\u306e\u82b8\u4eba\u3068\u3057\u3066\u306e\u5730\u4f4d\u3092\u56fa\u3081\u3064\u3064\u3042\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Michael has been consolidating his position as the number one comedian in Kansai."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u95a2\u6771\u306e\u4eba\u3068\u95a2\u897f\u306e\u4eba\u3063\u3066\u6298\u304c\u5408\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3063\u3066\u805e\u3044\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u3067\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "I heard that people from Kanto and people from Kansai don't get along well. Is it true?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3044\u3064\u306f\u95a2\u897f\u306f\u5b8c\u5168\u306b\u521d\u5fc3\u8005\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3001\u4ffa\u3089\u304c\u6848\u5185\u3057\u3066\u3084\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3068\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "This guy is a total noob in Kansai, so we\u2019ll have to show him around."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:public building} where {tooltip:Kanji:writte}n things are all {tooltip:Kanji:diagram}ed out in a way that lets you find said written things? That sounds like a {tooltip:Vocabulary:library} to me!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Library",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3057\u3087\u304b\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3057\u3087\u304b\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6567-subject-3879.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3057\u3087\u304b\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29603-subject-3879.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The {span:lang=ja:\u66f8\u9928} part should be readable by you, but it's the {span:lang=ja:\u56f3} that's troublesome with an alternate reading from the one you learned. Imagine yourself at the library. You check out every single book you can about the human {tooltip:Reading:toe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068}). You have a giant stack of books on it, then you drop it... ironically on your toe. You decide to {tooltip:Reading:show Khan} (your buddy) your smashed toe.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u56f3\u66f8\u9928\u304b\u3089\u3001\u96fb\u5b50\u66f8\u305b\u304d\u3092\u304b\u308a\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3082\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3063\u3066\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Did you know that you can even borrow ebooks from the library?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u56f3\u66f8\u9928\u306e\u30c8\u30a4\u30ec\u306f\u3001\u3053\u3053\u3092\u771f\u3063\u76f4\u3050\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3068\u3053\u308d\u306e\u4e00\u756a\u304a\u304f\u306b\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "If you go straight, you'll see the library's bathroom at the end of this aisle ahead."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u5e74\u672b\u5e74\u59cb\u306e\u304a\u4f11\u307f\u3044\u3064\u304b\u3089\u3044\u3064\u307e\u3067\u306a\u306e\uff1f\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u56f3\u66f8\u9928\u306b\u884c\u3053\u3046\u3088\u3002\u300d\u300c\u5341\u4e8c\u6708\u4e09\u5341\u65e5\u304b\u3089\u4e94\u65e5\u9593\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u56f3\u66f8\u9928\u3082\u9589\u307e\u3063\u3066\u308b\u306f\u305a\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"When is your New Year's vacation? I want to go to the library with you.\" \"I have five days off starting December 30th, but I\u2019m afraid the library will be closed too.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Something that's {tooltip:Kanji:special} and in a {tooltip:Kanji:hurry} must be special indeed. This refers to {tooltip:Vocabulary:limited express train}s in Japan. They go fast, they stop at fewer stops (because they're special!) and they hurry. Look out for these if you want to get somewhere in a jiffy.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Limited Express Train",
                "Alternative": "Limited Express",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3063\u304d\u3085\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3063\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6318-subject-3851.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3063\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29488-subject-3851.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Just note that the {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u304f} goes to {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3063}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30ce\u30ea\u3067\u7279\u6025\u306b\u4e57\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u6c7a\u3081\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We decided, spur of the moment, to take the limited express."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3051\u3093\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3093\u3060\u3093\u3067\u3001\u5fc3\u96fb\u56f3\u306b\u7570\u5e38\u304c\u3042\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3001\u6708\u66dc\u65e5\u306b\u7279\u6025\u306b\u4e57\u3063\u3066\u5927\u962a\u306e\u5927\u5b66\u75c5\u9662\u307e\u3067\u884c\u3063\u3066\u3001\u305b\u3044\u307f\u3064\u3051\u3093\u3055\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3044\u3051\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "When I had my checkup, they found something unusual in my EKG, so I have to go back for a complete physical at a university hospital in Osaka via the limited express train on Monday."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7279\u6025\u5238\u3092\u5148\u306b\u8cb7\u3063\u3066\u304a\u3044\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3001\u4eca\u51fa\u308c\u3070\u4e09\u6642\u4e94\u5341\u5206\u306e\u7279\u6025\u306b\u9593\u306b\u5408\u3046\u3088\u3002",
