                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29638-subject-3916.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306b\u304b\u3056\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u305f\u30ce\u30a2\u306e\u7bb1\u3076\u306d\u306e\u7d75\u304c\u597d\u304d\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I liked the picture of Noah's ark that was displayed at the art gallery."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bcd\u304c\u6b8b\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u6307\u8f2a\u3092\u3001\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306b\u304d\u4ed8\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I donated the ring handed down to me from my mother to the museum."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3069\u3046\u3084\u3063\u3066\u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u306e\u30c4\u30a2\u30fc\u30ac\u30a4\u30c9\u306b\u306a\u308c\u308b\u306e\uff1f\u82b8\u8853\u306e\u5c02\u9580\u5bb6\u304b\u4f55\u304b\u3058\u3083\u306a\u304f\u3061\u3083\u3044\u3051\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u306e\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3044\u3044\u3084\u3001\u305d\u3046\u3067\u3082\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002 \u7f8e\u8853\u9928\u304c\u60c5\u5831\u3092\u5168\u90e8\u304f\u308c\u308b\u304b\u3089\u3001\u307e\u3041\u3001\u53f0\u8a5e\u3092\u899a\u3048\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306a\u3082\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"How can you be a tour guide in the museum? Don\u2019t you have to be an art expert or something?\" \"No, not really. They give you all the information, it\u2019s like memorizing a script.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u6298\u308b} is \"to fold,\" so what about \"to fold {tooltip:Kanji:paper}\"? Ever heard of something that involves lots of folding of paper that is Japanese? Most likely you have. This is {tooltip:Vocabulary:origami}, aka the {tooltip:Vocabulary:art of paper folding}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Origami",
                "Alternative": "Art Of Paper Folding",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u308a\u304c\u307f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u308a\u304c\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6578-subject-3917.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u308a\u304c\u307f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29601-subject-3917.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading comes from {span:lang=ja:\u6298\u308b} and the vocab word {span:lang=ja:\u7d19}. As long as you know those you should be able to read this. Also, you probably already know this reading because it's an English word, too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306e\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u5f01\u5f53\u7bb1\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u3001\u306a\u305c\u304b\u98df\u3079\u7269\u306e\u4ee3\u308f\u308a\u306b\u6298\u308a\u7d19\u304c\u5165\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Today, in Koichi's bento box, there were some origami instead of food."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u30d7\u30ed\u306e\u6298\u308a\u7d19\u30a2\u30fc\u30c6\u30a3\u30b9\u30c8\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm a professional origami artist."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3053\u306e\u6570\u5e74\u9593\u652f\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u307f\u306a\u3055\u3093\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u6709\u96e3\u3046\u3054\u3056\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u304a\u9670\u69d8\u3067\u3001\u3064\u3044\u306b\u6298\u308a\u7d19\u3067\u6cb3\u8c5a\u304c\u6298\u308c\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I want to thank everyone who has shown me support over the years. Thankfully, I\u2019ve finally mastered how to make an origami Fugu."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:big} {tooltip:Kanji:heights}. What a nice area to be, it's where everyone wants to live! This magical place is {tooltip:Vocabulary:Osaka}. Heard of it before? It's a city, and kind of the rival to Tokyo.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Osaka",
                "Alternative": "Oosaka",
                "Word Type": "proper noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304a\u3055\u304b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u304a\u3055\u304b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6437-subject-3952.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u304a\u3055\u304b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29517-subject-3952.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is pretty weird, but then again so are people from Osaka (just kidding, Osakazens!). The {span:lang=ja:\u5927} reads like {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a} from {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a\u304d\u3044}. Then, {span:lang=ja:\u962a} uses the kun'yomi reading as well, which you didn't learn. That being said, doesn't this kanji look like {span:lang=ja:\u5742}, which also means slope? Well, it shares a kun'yomi reading as well, so if you've seen {span:lang=ja:\u5742} you can apply that reading over to here, making {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a\u3055\u304b}. Then again, if you know this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:Osaka} you probably can figure out how to write it too. Don't forget the double {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304a} though!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u962a\u3067\u306f\u3001\u305b\u3044\u3052\u3093\u901f\u5ea6\u3092\u5b88\u3063\u3066\u8d70\u308b\u8eca\u306f\u5c11\u306a\u3044\u3068\u805e\u3044\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "I heard that not many cars obey the speed limit in Osaka, is that true?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u962a\u65c5\u884c\u304c\u697d\u3057\u307f\u3059\u304e\u3066\u3001\u52c9\u5f37\u304c\u3059\u3063\u304b\u308a\u304a\u7559\u5b88\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was so excited about the Osaka trip that I totally neglected my studies."
                },
                {
