{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:bathe} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to bathe}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Bathe",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3073\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3073\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6238-subject-3849.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3042\u3073\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29439-subject-3849.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You want to know the best way {tooltip:Vocabulary:to bathe}? With a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:a}ardvarks ({span:lang=ja:\u3042}) in the water. They use their sticky little tongues to clean all your cracks and crannies.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6669\u98ef\u306e\u524d\u306b\u3001\u3072\u3068\u3063\u98a8\u308d\u6d74\u3073\u3066\u304f\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I'll go take a bath before dinner."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u653e\u3057\u3083\u80fd\u3092\u6d74\u3073\u308b\u306e\u304c\u6016\u304f\u3066\u3001\u3053\u306e\u753a\u306b\u306b\u3052\u3066\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We were afraid of being exposed to radioactivity and we ran away to this town."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u79c1\u306b\u89aa\u53cb\u306e\u5929\u7136\u9bdb\u3092\u7d39\u4ecb\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u9bdb\u541b\u306f\u3001\u6df1\u6d77\u306b\u4f4f\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3067\u65e5\u5149\u3092\u3042\u307e\u308a\u6d74\u3073\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3068\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Fugu introduced me his best friend, Wild Red Sea Bream. He told me Sea Bream lives at great depths and is bathed in hardly any sunlight."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u95a2} means {tooltip:Kanji:connected}. So, when you add {span:lang=ja:\u3059\u308b} to it you make it a verb. Now it means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be connected to}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Connected To",
                "Alternative": "To Be Related",
                "Word Type": "\u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093\u3059\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u3093\u3059\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
