                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3051\u3093\u306b\u95a2\u3057\u3066\u306f\u3001\u59a5\u5354\u306e\u3088\u5730\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "There is no room for compromise on this matter."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30af\u30ea\u30b9\u30c6\u30f3\u306f\u3001\u65e5\u672c\u6587\u5b66\u306b\u95a2\u3059\u308b\u7814\u7a76\u3092\u884c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Kristen is doing research connected to Japanese literature."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u3001Tofugu\u306e\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u3067\u50cd\u3044\u3066\u3044\u308b\u6642\u306b\u3001\u30a2\u30b8\u30c8\u3067\u306e\u767a\u7832\u306b\u95a2\u3059\u308b\u96fb\u8a71\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "While working at the Tofugu office, Viet received a call related to a shooting at his hideout."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that the kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:connection}. This is a verb, so one meaning is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be connected with}. There are many other ways to say this too. This word is a bit full featured. You can say {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be involved with} or even {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be affected}. Basically things that have to do with being connected with something else.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Involved With",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Connected With, To Be Affected, To Have To Do With",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304b\u308f\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u304b\u308f\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6588-subject-3800.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u304b\u308f\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29630-subject-3800.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Who have you gotten involved with this time? The \"{tooltip:Reading:Kaw Kaw} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304b}) Crow Gang\" this time? They are bad news, always eating from garbage and squawking \"kaw kaw\" ... You don't want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be connected with} them.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u304c\u3084\u3070\u3044\u305d\u3057\u304d\u3068\u4fc2\u308f\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u306f\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3051\u3069\u3001\u305d\u306e\u306f\u3093\u3056\u3044\u306b\u4fc2\u308f\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3068\u306f\u3084\u3063\u3071\u308a\u601d\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "I know Viet is involved with a dangerous organization, but I still don't think that he has anything to do with the crime."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u308c\u3093\u4e2d\u306b\u306f\u4fc2\u308f\u3089\u306a\u3044\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Don't get involved with people like that."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3057\u6bd2\u629c\u304d\u3092\u305b\u305a\u306b\u6cb3\u8c5a\u3092\u98df\u3079\u305f\u3089\u3001\u547d\u306b\u4fc2\u308f\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "If you ate blowfish without taking the poison out, it would be a matter of life and death."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You already learned how {span:lang=ja:\u6298\u308b} means \"to fold.\" Well this is what happens after that. You folded it too far and now it's starting {tooltip:Vocabulary:to break}. ",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Break",
                "Alternatives": "To Snap, To Fracture",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u308c\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6575-subject-7755.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29584-subject-7755.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You learned this reading when you learned {span:lang=ja:\u6298\u308b}, so you should know this one too!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u3093\u306a\u3053\u3068\u3092\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3001\u5fc3\u304c\u6298\u308c\u308b\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "My heart breaks when you say that."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u91cd\u3044\u8377\u7269\u3092\u304b\u305f\u306b\u304b\u3064\u3044\u3067\u904b\u3093\u3067\u3044\u305f\u3089\u3001\u304b\u305f\u306e\u9aa8\u304c\u6298\u308c\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "When I was carrying a heavy load on my shoulders, my shoulder bone fractured."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u30c1\u30e5\u30fc\u30ea\u30c3\u30d7\u3001\u6bce\u5e74\u82b1\u304c\u54b2\u3044\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u6839\u5143\u304b\u3089\u30dd\u30c3\u30ad\u30ea\u6298\u308c\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Every year, our tulips snap at the roots after they bloom."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Come Off",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Removed, To Fall Off",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u308c\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30115-subject-4073.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21318-subject-4073.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be the kun'yomi reading.\n{splitParent}Lucky for you, the kanji readings for transitive and intransitive verbs are almost always the same. Once you learn one, you know them both! This reading is the same as {span:lang=ja:\u53d6\u308b}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30dc\u30bf\u30f3\u304c\u53d6\u308c\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "A button came off."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u3057\u307f\u306f\u53d6\u308c\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u306a\u3044\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "It might be difficult for this stain to be removed."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30b8\u30cd\u30b9\u8857\u306b\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u3092\u8a2d\u3051\u308b\u3068\u306a\u308b\u3068\u8cc3\u6599\u306f\u304b\u306a\u308a\u9ad8\u304f\u3064\u304d\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u6211\u3005\u306e\u30a4\u30e1\u30fc\u30b8\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u91cd\u8981\u306a\u4e8b\u3067\u3082\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3057\u3001\u4e00\u5e74\u3050\u3089\u3044\u3067\u5143\u306f\u53d6\u308c\u308b\u306e\u3067\u306f\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Renting an office in the business district will be considerably expensive, but it\u2019s important for our image and I think it will pay for itself in about a year."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u59a5\u5354} means {tooltip:Kanji:compromise}. So, what happens when you make it a verb? It becomes {tooltip:Vocabulary:to compromise}.",
