            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u5b66\u3092\u5352\u696d\u3057\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u3076\u4e8b\u306b\u7b2c\u4e00\u5e0c\u671b\u306e\u4f1a\u793e\u306b\u3057\u3085\u3046\u3057\u3087\u304f\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After graduating from university, I was able to, uneventfully, get a job at my company of choice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u51fa\u305b\u304d\u65e5\u6570\u304c\u8db3\u308a\u306a\u304f\u3066\u9ad8\u6821\u3092\u5352\u696d\u3067\u304d\u306a\u3044\u3060\u3063\u3066\uff1f\u5197\u8ac7\u3060\u308d\u3046\uff1f",
                    "en": "Are you saying that you can't graduate from high school because you haven't attended enough? Don't be ridiculous."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u5144\u306f\u969c\u5bb3\u3092\u4e57\u308a\u8d8a\u3048\u3001\u5927\u5b66\u3092\u5352\u696d\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u79c1\u306f\u5144\u3092\u3068\u3066\u3082\u8a87\u308a\u306b\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u5927\u5b66\u5352\u696d\u306f\u5f7c\u306e\u6c7a\u610f\u3068\u52aa\u529b\u306e\u8cdc\u7269\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My brother overcame his disability and graduated from college. I\u2019m very proud of him. His graduation is the result of his determination and effort."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:hurry} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to hurry}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Hurry",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u305d\u3050"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u305d\u3050",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6511-subject-3838.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u305d\u3050",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29587-subject-3838.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Someone who is trying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to hurry} is someone who is not at {tooltip:Reading:ease} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u305d}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u6025\u3044\u3067\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306b\u66f8\u304d\u304a\u304d\u3092\u6b8b\u3057\u305f\u5f8c\u3001\u30c8\u30a4\u30ec\u306b\u4e00\u6642\u9593\u3053\u3082\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi left a note for Viet in a hurry and stayed in the toilet for an hour."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u304c\u304b\u52b4\u3067\u305f\u304a\u308c\u305f\u3068\u805e\u3044\u3066\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u75c5\u9662\u3078\u6025\u304e\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi heard that Viet broke down from working too much, so he hurried to the hospital."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3082\u3046\uff01\u6025\u3044\u3067\u3088\uff01\u9045\u308c\u3061\u3083\u3046\u308f\u3002\u300d\u300c\u4eca\u8d77\u304d\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3001\u3059\u3050\u884c\u304f\u308f\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Hey, hurry up! We\u2019ll be late.\" \"I just woke up, I\u2019m coming.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is like a fancy and humble way of saying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to know}. Sure, the kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:suppose}, but think of it this way... When you say \"I suppose\" it's like a humble way of saying \"I know.\" You're not being as direct about it this way, and in Japanese, that makes you more humble and polite. So, that's why {span:lang=ja:\u5b58\u3058\u308b} means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to know}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Know",
                "Alternative": "To Be Aware Of",
                "Word Type": "ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305e\u3093\u3058\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305e\u3093\u3058\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6554-subject-3826.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305e\u3093\u3058\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29620-subject-3826.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as the one you learned with the kanji. If you remember the kanji reading, you'll have no problem remembering this vocabulary reading as well!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u793e\u54e1\u305f\u3061\u304c\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304d\u3085\u3046\u3092\u8981\u6c42\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306f\u5b58\u3058\u3066\u304a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I was aware that workers were making demands for a pay raise."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3064\u307e\u304c\u5f1f\u306b\u304a\u91d1\u306e\u8fd4\u3055\u3044\u3092\u8981\u6c42\u3057\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u5b58\u3058\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3067\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I didn't know that my wife had demanded that my brother pay the money back."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5e74\u672b\u3067\u304a\u5fd9\u3057\u3044\u3068\u306f\u5b58\u3058\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3053\u306e\u8a18\u4e8b\u3092\u8aad\u3093\u3067\u9802\u3051\u308c\u3070\u5b09\u3057\u304f\u5b58\u3058\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I know that the end of the year is really busy, but I would appreciate it if you could read this article."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u6771\u4eac} is {tooltip:Kanji:Tokyo}, and you know that {span:lang=ja:\u5f01} is {tooltip:Kanji:dialect}, so you have yourself {tooltip:Vocabulary:Tokyo dialect}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tokyo Dialect",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3079\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3079\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6426-subject-3836.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3079\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29526-subject-3836.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. It will help to know how to read {span:lang=ja:\u6771\u4eac} already, which you should.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u5f01\u306f\u5171\u901a\u8a9e\u3068\u307b\u3068\u3093\u3069\u540c\u3058\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Tokyo dialect is almost the same as standard Japanese."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u5f01\u3067\u3057\u3083\u3079\u3063\u3066\u307b\u3057\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3046\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u8981\u6c42\u3092\u3057\u308a\u305e\u3051\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I rejected Koichi's request that I speak in Tokyo dialect."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u306d\u3048\u3001\u7121\u6599\u3067\u6771\u4eac\u5f01\u306e\u30ec\u30c3\u30b9\u30f3\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002\u300d\u300c\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u805e\u3051\u3088\u3002\u30a2\u30a4\u30c4\u306f\u4f55\u3067\u3082\u3059\u308b\u305e\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"I need to get some free Tokyo dialect lessons.\" \"Ask Koichi. He\u2019ll do anything.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:laugh} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to laugh}.",
