                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine you have a hankering for your favorite fruit. You gotta get in your car and put the pedal to the metal! Feel the wind in your hair as your car speeds down the road and listen to that engine purr.",
                "mnemonic": "They sell {tooltip:Kanji:fruit} at the store, and you need to drive your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}) to get there. A car is the fastest way to fruit."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under this {tooltip:Radical:roof} is a {tooltip:Radical:bear} who works for the {tooltip:Kanji:government}. If you saw a bear out in the wild you might be afraid and try to run, but if you see a bear inside a building under a roof, don't be scared! It's just a government bear.",
            "hints": "Picture the government bear looking through government documents and snorting gruffly as it decides what to sign and what to reject. It has a little government sash and hat.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Government"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Genghis Khan patting the first bear government worker on the back as they start their first day working for the government.",
                "mnemonic": "The first {tooltip:Kanji:government} that allowed bears was set up by Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}). He was all about conquering people and then using them as efficiently as possible. He discovered that bears are incredibly useful in government buildings as government workers."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:net} is for {tooltip:Radical:someone} who works in a {tooltip:Kanji:government office}. You'll also take someone from a {tooltip:Kanji:political office}.",
            "hints": "Doesn't matter who, but you're going to catch someone from a government office using this net, it doesn't matter who.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Government Office",
                "Alternatives": "Political Office, Office"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the show they put on. You'll call your show \"Exactly 8 Hours of Bureaucracy.\"",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Government office} and {tooltip:Kanji:political office} people put on the best {tooltip:Reading:show}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087}). That's why you want to capture someone from there with your net."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you're on the {tooltip:Radical:roof} of the {tooltip:Radical:festival} you'll have to {tooltip:Kanji:guess} what's actually going on below you. You can kind of see that there are rides and maybe food? It smells like food. But you have to guess on the specifics because you're above it and not in it.",
            "hints": "Imagine being on the roof above a festival. Can you guess what's happening below you based on the sounds and smells?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Guess"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now imagine yourself just after you sat down. You close your eyes and open your ears and you can guess a lot better. You should have sat down earlier so you could concentrate on guessing better rather than endangering yourself.",
                "mnemonic": "You were trying to {tooltip:Kanji:guess} by leaning over the edge of the roof, but you almost slip, and {tooltip:Reading:sat} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3064}) down instead."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:Viking} will empty his {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of all its {tooltip:Radical:dirt} in the great {tooltip:Kanji:hall}. They all get together in some kind of {tooltip:Kanji:public chamber} and dish all the dirt (literal and figurative) that they've got.",
            "hints": "Picture a long Viking hall, with a big table and tons of chairs. All of the Vikings are gossiping and sharing all their dirt on their enemies.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hall",
                "Alternative": "Public Chamber"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3069\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now picture all of the Vikings in the hall spitting dirt with one breath and shoveling doughnuts in with the next. It's pretty gross!",
                "mnemonic": "While the Vikings gather to spill the dirt in their {tooltip:Kanji:hall}, they also stuff their faces with {tooltip:Reading:dou}ghnuts ({span:lang=ja:\u3069\u3046}). Ah yes, Vikings love to eat doughnuts when they talk trash."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You hide {tooltip:Radical:poop} in a {tooltip:Radical:cape} as part of the {tooltip:Kanji:illusion} in your magic show. Your acts are kind of gross and this one involves creating the illusion of disappearing poop by hiding it within the folds of your cape.",
            "hints": "Imagine having poop in your cape. It would smell bad and anyone close to you would be able to smell right through the illusion.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Illusion"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u307c\u308d\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Genji grabs the cape before you can stop him and he puts it on. You can see the illusion fade, he keeps smiling but more tears start streaming down his face. \"A wonderful illusion, the best I've ever seen,\" he chokes out and marches away, without looking back.",
                "mnemonic": "Somehow the poop cape {tooltip:Kanji:illusion} goes over really well. The crowd is giving you a standing ovation and right in the center is {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}). He marches up to you, wipes a tear from his eye, and says, \"Your illusion cape is wonderful. I must have it!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:criminal} has done an {tooltip:Kanji:injustice} on the world or other people. Being a criminal is a {tooltip:Kanji:negative} thing, and even if it was just a {tooltip:Kanji:mistake}, it was still a crime.",
            "hints": "Think of all the criminals you know. Even if what they did was a mistake, it was still some type of injustice, right? It was something the rest of the world sees as a negative thing.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Injustice",
                "Alternatives": "Negative, Mistake"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
