                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This is the heat of embarrassment, of knowing you did something negative or wrong.",
                "mnemonic": "When you commit an {tooltip:Kanji:injustice}, you'll know because {tooltip:Reading:hea}t ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}) fills your body. Maybe you've never done any kind of big thing, but when you make a {tooltip:Kanji:mistake} your face fills with heat and you turn red!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Putting on {tooltip:Radical:cleats} in the {tooltip:Radical:heart} of {tooltip:Radical:winter} and braving the harsh elements just to plant a kiss on your sweetheart\u2019s {tooltip:Radical:forehead} \u2013 that\u2019s {tooltip:Kanji:love}. Sure, you could see them another day, but you need to plant this smooch on their forehead today, so you get some cleats for better grip on the winter snow and you keep thoughts of your dear in your heart as you travel to see your love.",
            "hints": "Feel the joy of love in your heart as you travel out in the winter. It\u2019s cold outside, but the feeling of love in your heart keeps you warm. Feel this warm love emanating and heating your body.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Love"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine seeing your love with your own two eyes after a long time away from them. It feels great to be reunited and see eye to eye once again. Imagine this feeling.",
                "mnemonic": "Walking through the winter snows with your cleats on, you\u2019ve gotta keep your {tooltip:Reading:eye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044}) on the prize. It\u2019s a really hard journey, but you keep your eye on the prize, which is your {tooltip:Kanji:love} and the time you\u2019ll get to spend with them."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Flowers} can be used for {tooltip:Radical:comfort}, but also for {tooltip:Kanji:medicine}. Sure, it\u2019s a comfort to smell flowers because they smell nice, but one can also use them as medicine to heal people.",
            "hints": "Imagine having some medicine that smells and tastes like fresh cut flowers. Smell the smell in your nose and taste the taste on your tongue.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Medicine",
                "Alternatives": "Drug, Drugs"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
