                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3059\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a yak in your mind. Pretend you are riding atop the yak as it transports this medicine. Feel the fur of the yak in your hands as you cling on for dear life.",
                "mnemonic": "The best way to transport all the {tooltip:Kanji:medicine} on land is with a {tooltip:Reading:yak} ({span:lang=ja:\u3084\u304f}). Yaks are big, strong, and very capable of transporting flower medicine like these."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Viking} {tooltip:Radical:see}, Viking {tooltip:Kanji:memorize}. That\u2019s how Vikings learn things. They see something, and then they memorize it. Quite simple, really.",
            "hints": "How else would a Viking memorize something? Imagine having to memorize sea charts for your Viking navigation. Look and see the maps in your brain as you memorize them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Memorize",
                "Alternative": "Awake"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u307c, \u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself memorizing the sound of a cock crow and using it to play jokes on your fellow Vikings. Cock-a-doodle-doo!",
                "mnemonic": "Every morning, a {tooltip:Reading:cock} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304f}) crows and rouses the Vikings. Seeing this, one of the Vikings {tooltip:Kanji:memorize}s the cock crow so that he can mimic it and play pranks on his fellow Vikings."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You are all by your lonesome {tooltip:Radical:self} and you have to check {tooltip:Radical:twenty} {tooltip:Radical:rice paddie}s. The thing you have to check is the smell of all the rice paddies to see if they're ready for harvest. At each one, you open up your {tooltip:Kanji:nose} and smell deeply.",
            "hints": "Focus in on your nose. Your nostrils get huge, and your nose is huge. Smell the rice in your imagination. Your nose is amazing.",
            "meanings": {
