                        "reading": "\u305d\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u308f, \u305d\u3070",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Try saying {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u308f} out the side of your mouth like the leader of the shellfish and you'll probably say {span:lang=ja:\u304c\u308f} too. Don't stick a knife in your side though, we won't pay your medical bills when you complain to us that this mnemonic got you injured.",
                "mnemonic": "Because of this knife in his {tooltip:Kanji:side}, he can't pronounce certain words correctly. The most obvious one is when he says {span:lang=ja:\u5ddd} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u308f}), but it comes out of the side of his mouth as {span:lang=ja:\u304c\u308f}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you set a fish on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} and chop its {tooltip:Radical:fins} off with an {tooltip:Radical:axe}, you\u2019re probably a {tooltip:Kanji:soldier}. Only soldiers have access to axes, and you like to eat fish, but first you have to set it on the ground to chop its fins off.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to carve a fish with an axe. Probably not an easy thing to do. If you\u2019re a trained axe soldier, you\u2019d probably have an easier time with it. Picture yourself chopping off fins as an expert axe soldier.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Soldier"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
