                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine this soldier lighting a bale of hay on fire to cook his fish. The hay burns really fast, but it should be enough.",
                "mnemonic": "Uh-oh, it looks like this axe {tooltip:Kanji:soldier} was so excited about chopping the fins off his fish that he didn't think about how he was going to cook them. The only thing nearby to light on fire is a bale of {tooltip:Reading:hay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3044}). Well, it's not the best thing, but at least it will get these fish cooked."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What do you {tooltip:Radical:say} to a {tooltip:Radical:guard}? Your {tooltip:Kanji:theory} about how the thing he's guarding isn't even real. Yeah, you have this whole thing figured out. You have for a while. At this point, it's only fair that you tell your theory to the guard who's wasting his time.",
            "hints": "Imagine saying your theory out loud to a guard about how what he's guarding isn't even there. Imagine how he would react.",
            "meanings": {
