{
            "mnemonic": "You've seen {span:lang=ja:\u7f8e\u5473\u3057\u3044} by this point. This is the opposite of that. Instead of {span:lang=ja:\u7f8e} you have {span:lang=ja:\u4e0d} (not), so something that does {tooltip:Kanji:not} have {tooltip:Kanji:flavor} is something that doesn't taste good. i.e. something {tooltip:Vocabulary:bad tasting}. This can also refer to someone who's {tooltip:Vocabulary:unskillful} at something as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bad Tasting",
                "Alternatives": "Unappetizing, Unskillful",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307e\u305a\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u305a\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "7010-subject-7150.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u305a\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29836-subject-7150.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading doesn't follow any of the rules you've run into. It's {span:lang=ja:\u307e\u305a\u3044}. Think about how you're going through this really long {tooltip:Reading:maze} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u305a}) and how you're promised a really tasty wonderful treat at the end for getting through it (you're a lab rat or something). When you get to the end, there's your treat! What joy! You eat it and... oh man... it is so {tooltip:Vocabulary:bad tasting} you can't even believe it. Be sure to imagine the terrible taste and the terrible disappointment after going through that difficult maze only to get this... this... terribly {tooltip:Vocabulary:unappetizing} cheese.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u306a\u3093\u304b\u4e0d\u5473\u305d\u3046\u306a\u30b5\u30f3\u30c9\u30a4\u30c3\u30c1\u3060\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Those sandwiches look a bit unappetizing, don't they?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u5b57\u306f\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u4e0d\u5473\u3044\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "His handwriting is kinda bad, don't you think?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u3093\u306a\u306b\u4e0d\u5473\u3044\u5473\u564c\u6c41\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019ve never eaten such disgusting miso soup."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Remember how {span:lang=ja:\u7d00\u5143\u5f8c} is \"After death\" or \"AD\"? Well, this is the opposite because it has a {tooltip:Kanji:before} ({span:lang=ja:\u524d}) in it. It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:BC} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:Before Christ}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Before Christ",
                "Alternatives": "Bc, Bce, Before Common Era",
                "Word Type": "noun"
