                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29884-subject-3935.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are the ones you learned with the kanji. It's also like the vocab: {span:lang=ja:\u671d} is like the vocab version, {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3055} and {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u98ef} is like the word you learned, {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u306f\u3093}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u671d\u3054\u98ef\u306e\u7f8e\u5473\u3057\u305d\u3046\u306a\u306b\u304a\u3044\u306b\u9f3b\u304c\u3072\u304f\u3072\u304f\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My nose twitched when I smelled the delicious breakfast."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u308f\u304c\u5bb6\u306e\u671d\u3054\u98ef\u306f\u3001\u3054\u98ef\u3068\u5473\u305d\u3057\u308b\u3001\u7389\u5b50\u3084\u304d\u306b\u5e72\u3057\u9b5a\u3068\u6c7a\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Our family always has rice, miso soup, omelets, and dried fish for breakfast."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u306d\u3047\u3001\u3055\u3063\u304d\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u30b5\u30d7\u30e9\u30a4\u30ba\u671d\u3054\u306f\u3093\u30d1\u30fc\u30c6\u30a3\u30fc\u306e\u4e8b\u3092\u6559\u3048\u305f\u3067\u3057\u3087\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3048\u3063\uff01\u30b5\u30d7\u30e9\u30a4\u30ba\u3060\u3063\u305f\u306a\u3093\u3066\u77e5\u3089\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\uff01\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Did you just tell Koichi about his surprise breakfast party?\" \"Oh! I didn\u2019t know it was a surprise.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:thing} you {tooltip:Kanji:build} is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:building}. There aren't too many other things you build, at least not to this extent.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Building",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3066\u3082\u306e"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3066\u3082\u306e",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "7039-subject-3995.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3066\u3082\u306e",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29866-subject-3995.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is a bit weird. It's kun'yomi readings across the board, meaning your knowledge of {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u3066\u308b} hopefully can come into play here. A building is something you build, so how do you say \"to build\"? It's {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u3066\u308b} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3066\u308b}). Since it's a thing you build, it's a {span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3066\u3082\u306e}. This reading is a bit confusing, but hopefully after a while you'll get it if you get it wrong too many times! Maybe if you think about the building you're in and call it a {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u7269} a few times it'll sink in better?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3059\u3066\u304d\u306a\u30c7\u30b6\u30a4\u30f3\u306e\u5efa\u7269\u3067\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "This is very nicely designed building, isn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5efa\u3066\u3089\u308c\u3066\u304b\u3089\u307e\u3060\u4e00\u5e74\u3057\u304b\u305f\u3063\u3066\u306a\u3044\u306e\u306b\u3001\u3042\u306e\u5efa\u7269\u306f\u3082\u3046\u305a\u3044\u5206\u3088\u3054\u308c\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "It's only been a year since it was built, but this building is pretty dirty already, isn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3042\u306a\u305f\u3068\u305d\u306e\u5efa\u7269\u3092\u4e00\u7dd2\u306b\u898b\u306b\u884c\u304d\u305f\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3046\u306e\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3044\u3064\u304c\u3054\u90fd\u5408\u3088\u308d\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u3048\u3048\u3063\u3068\u3001\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u3054\u90fd\u5408\u306b\u5408\u308f\u305b\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"I\u2019d like to go see the building with you so when would be convenient for you?\" \"Well, I\u2019ll adjust my schedule accordingly.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

