                        "file": "29908-subject-3969.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. The last {span:lang=ja:\u60aa\u679c} gets the {span:lang=ja:\u60aa} shortened a little bit.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u679c\u60aa\u56e0\u60aa\u679c\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3046\u3060\u308d\uff1f\u5f53\u7136\u306e\u3080\u304f\u3044\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "They say \"evil begets evil\" right? So they just got properly punished."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u60aa\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3092\u3057\u305f\u3089\u3001\u60aa\u56e0\u60aa\u679c\u3067\u5f8c\u3005\u3072\u3069\u3044\u76ee\u306b\u3042\u3046\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "If you do something bad, you'll get in trouble later because evil breeds evil."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8056\u66f8\u306b\u306f\u3001\u696d\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u4f55\u3066\u66f8\u3044\u3066\u3042\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3063\u3051\uff1f\u60aa\u56e0\u60aa\u679c\u3068\u304b\u3060\u3063\u3051\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "What does the Bible say about karma? Was it like \"evil begets evil\" or something?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you make your {tooltip:Kanji:theory} {tooltip:Kanji:bright} (and clear and easy to understand) you must have come up with an {tooltip:Vocabulary:explanation} for it. Before it was dark and murky in everyone's mind. But, when you give your explanation, it gets bright and easy to understand! Yay!",
