                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29755-subject-4049.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are both kun'yomi vocab readings, probably because a {span:lang=ja:\u9f3b} is a body part, and body parts do that to jukugo words. You know {span:lang=ja:\u9f3b}'s reading from the kanji ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u306a}) and you know {span:lang=ja:\u6b4c}'s reading from the vocabulary word {span:lang=ja:\u6b4c} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u305f}). Combine them together and you have a very nice humming tune and reading, {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u306a\u3046\u305f}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u9f3b\u3092\u3075\u304f\u3089\u307e\u305b\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u9f3b\u6b4c\u3092\u6b4c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi was humming while making his nose swell."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u9f3b\u6b4c\u307e\u3058\u308a\u3067\u697d\u3057\u305d\u3046\u306b\u81ea\u8ee2\u8eca\u306b\u4e57\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet was happily riding his bicycle while humming."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7206\u7b11\uff01\u304a\u524d\u9f3b\u6b4c\u4e0b\u624b\u3059\u304e\u3060\u3063\u3064\u30fc\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "LMAO! You are just terrible at humming."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
