                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5468\u308a\u306e\u4eba\u304b\u3089\u3001\u7121\u77e5\u306a\u304f\u305b\u306b\u77e5\u3063\u305f\u304b\u3076\u308a\u3092\u3059\u308b\u3084\u3064\u3060\u3068\u601d\u308f\u308c\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3089\u3069\u3046\u3057\u3088\u3046\u3068\u5fc3\u914d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm worried people think of me as an ignorant know-it-all."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7121\u77e5\u304c\u539f\u56e0\u3067\u3001\u9593\u3061\u304c\u3044\u3092\u304a\u304b\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I made a mistake due to ignorance."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7121\u77e5\u3092\u3055\u3089\u3051\u51fa\u3057\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3063\u3066\u6065\u305a\u304b\u3057\u304c\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306a\u3093\u304b\u7121\u3044\u3088\u3002\u3042\u3044\u3064\u3089\u3053\u305d\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u305f\u3061\u306e\u7121\u77e5\u3092\u96a0\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u6065\u3058\u308b\u3079\u304d\u3055\u3002",
                    "en": "You shouldn\u2019t be ashamed of yourself after admitting your ignorance. They should be ashamed of themselves for hiding their own ignorance."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well. You can add {tooltip:Vocabulary:phantom} to the meanings as well, because phantoms are kind of like {tooltip:Vocabulary:illusion}s.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Illusion",
                "Alternatives": "Phantom, Apparition",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307e\u307c\u308d\u3057"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u307c\u308d\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6904-subject-3988.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307e\u307c\u308d\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29775-subject-3988.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: You look up to see a crazy {tooltip:Vocabulary:illusion}. You can't believe it's real. Master Roshi, from Dragonball, is standing in front of you (you thought he was a cartoon!). Then, he splits into a million versions of himself, creating a {tooltip:Reading:mob of Roshi}s ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u307c\u308d\u3057}). This mob goes on to train many people to fight.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u85ac\u3092\u98f2\u3080\u3068\u3001\u5e7b\u304c\u898b\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You'll be able to see apparitions if you take this drug."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5e7b\u306e\u9b5a\u3092\u3064\u304b\u307e\u3048\u305f\u305e\uff01",
                    "en": "I caught a phantom fish!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u604d\u60da\u72b6\u614b\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u30b5\u30fc\u30e2\u30f3\u306e\u5e7b\u3092\u4f55\u5ea6\u3082\u898b\u305f\u5f8c\u306b\u3001\u30d5\u30b0\u306f\u3088\u3046\u3084\u304f\u5f7c\u5973\u304c12\u5e74\u524d\u306b\u6b7b\u3093\u3060\u3053\u3068\u3092\u601d\u3044\u51fa\u3057\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u304c\u5e7b\u3092\u898b\u3066\u3044\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u3044\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After a series of ecstasy filled visions of Salmon, Fugu finally remembered she had been dead for 12 years, and he realized he was seeing an illusion."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:diagram} {tooltip:Kanji:theory} is an {tooltip:Vocabulary:illustration} that is used as an {tooltip:Vocabulary:explanatory diagram}. Just imagine a chalk board with all sorts of drawings of things, showing how they work, at least in theory.",
