                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29765-subject-3955.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are the kun'yomi readings. With {span:lang=ja:\u5074} you've already learned it. With {span:lang=ja:\u5185} you've also already learned the reading. Combine them together and you have {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3061\u304c\u308f}. In case you've forgotten, here's a mnemonic to help you remember that pesky {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3061} portion. What is it that's drawn you inside? \"{tooltip:Reading:Oo, chee}se!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3061}) Cheese has drawn you inside. You're so excited that you exclaim, \"Oo, cheese!\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u308a\u305d\u306a\u9280\u884c\u306e\u5185\u5074\u3067\u5f85\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'll wait for you inside Resona Bank."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u53f3\u306e\u5185\u5074\u306e\u304b\u304b\u3068\u306b\u30c8\u30b2\u304c\u3055\u3055\u3063\u305f\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I think I've got a splinter in my inner right heel."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30be\u30f3\u30d3\u3092\u4e2d\u306b\u5165\u308c\u306a\u3044\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u91d1\u5c5e\u88fd\u306e\u30b7\u30e3\u30c3\u30bf\u30fc\u3092\u4e0b\u308d\u3057\u3066\u3001\u5185\u5074\u304b\u3089\u9375\u3092\u639b\u3051\u308b\u5fc5\u8981\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We need to lower the metal shutters and lock them from the inside to shut the zombies out."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you're {tooltip:Kanji:ford}ing a stream, and you suddenly feel {tooltip:Kanji:dry} feelings around you, that doesn't make any sense for something wet. This dryness is an {tooltip:Vocabulary:interference}. It's an {tooltip:Vocabulary:intervention} trying to stop you from fording.",
