                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. You just have to remember that {span:lang=ja:\u4f1d} is read as {span:lang=ja:\u3067\u3093} in this case. Just imagine yourself sitting in your {tooltip:Reading:den} ({span:lang=ja:\u3067\u3093}) as you get cozy and listen to this theory about a great {tooltip:Vocabulary:legend}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30a4\u30eb\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u306e\u4f1d\u8aac\u306e\u82f1\u3086\u3046\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u308c\u3070\u3001\u3060\u308c\u3092\u601d\u3044\u3046\u304b\u3079\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "When you hear \"a legendary Irish hero,\" who comes to mind?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u524d\u3081\u3061\u3083\u304f\u3061\u3083\u30e2\u30c6\u308b\u306a\uff01\u30de\u30b8\u3067\u4f1d\u8aac\u7684\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Girls love you, man. You are legendary, seriously!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4f1d\u8aac\u306b\u3088\u308b\u3068\u3001\u3053\u306e\u6d77\u306b\u306f\u8c46\u8150\u3092\u98df\u3079\u308b\u30d5\u30b0\u304c\u4f4f\u3093\u3067\u3044\u308b\u305d\u3046\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "According to a legend, there is a fugu that eats tofu in this ocean."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

