                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u604b\u611b\u3057\u305f\u3089\u3001\u76f8\u624b\u306b\u5bfe\u3057\u3066\u3044\u3064\u3082\u611b\u60c5\u3092\u611f\u3058\u3059\u304e\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3046\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "When I'm in love, I'm usually way too into them."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3046\u3061\u306e\u5b50\u306f\u3001\u6700\u8fd1\u604b\u611b\u5c0f\u8aac\u3070\u304b\u308a\u8aad\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My kid has been reading romance novels all the time lately."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u604b\u611b\u3067\u306e\u5225\u308c\u969b\u306f\u3001\u5207\u306a\u304f\u3066\u7518\u9178\u3063\u3071\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Parting from someone you love is always painfully bittersweet."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you have {tooltip:Kanji:romance} you also have {tooltip:Vocabulary:love}! The romantic kind of mushy, gushy love. Be careful though. This word doesn't share its meaning with its kanji. But, that's how romance is. It gets all crazy and turns to love really fast.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Love",
                "Word Type": "independent noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6942-subject-3997.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29817-subject-3997.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: Your {tooltip:Vocabulary:love} isn't toward a person, it's toward this giant {tooltip:Reading:Koi} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3044}) fish you met the other day. The fish is just so... so... handsome! You get hearts popping above your head every time you think about this koi!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u307e\u3067\u3001\u604b\u306b\u604b\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3042\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u3060\u308c\u304b\u306b\u604b\u3057\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u7121\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I wanted to fall in love, but I'd never actually fallen for anyone until now."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b5\u30fc\u30e2\u30f3\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3001\u306a\u3093\u304b\u304b\u308f\u3044\u304f\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3088\u306a\u3002\u604b\u3059\u308b\u5973\u3063\u3066\u611f\u3058\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "Don't you think Salmon got prettier? I think it's because she's a woman in love, don't you?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u3053\u3068\u304c\u982d\u304b\u3089\u96e2\u308c\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3002\u3053\u308c\u3063\u3066\u604b\u306e\u59cb\u307e\u308a\u306a\u306e\u304b\u306a\uff1f",
                    "en": "I can\u2019t get Fugu out of my head! Is there love in the air?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": [
                {
                    "en": "to be in love",
                    "ja": "\u604b\u3092\u3059\u308b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "to fall in love",
                    "ja": "\u604b\u306b\u843d\u3061\u308b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "new love",
                    "ja": "\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u604b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                }
            ]
        }

