                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u5c0f\u8aac\u30de\u30b8\u3067\u5927\u597d\u304d\u3060\u308f\u3002\u3053\u308c\u306f\u30db\u30f3\u30e2\u30ce\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I seriously love this novel. This is legit."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u7236\u3055\u3093\u3001\u5c0f\u8aac\u304c\u58f2\u308c\u3066\u9f3b\u9ad8\u3005\u3060\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Dad is glowing with pride because his novel is selling well, huh?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u307b\u3089\u3001\u3053\u308c\u3067\u306a\u307f\u3060\u3068\u9f3b\u3092\u3075\u304d\u306a\u3088\u300d\u3068\u8a00\u3044\u306a\u304c\u3089\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u8aad\u3093\u3067\u3044\u305f\u5c0f\u8aac\u306e\u30da\u30fc\u30b8\u3092\u4e00\u679a\u3084\u3076\u3063\u3066\u3001\u30af\u30ea\u30b9\u30c6\u30f3\u306b\u308f\u305f\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "\u201cHere, wipe your tears and nose,\u201d Koichi said, ripping off a page of the novel that he'd been reading and handing it to Kristen."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that an {span:lang=ja:\u304a\u9858\u3044} is a request, and that {span:lang=ja:\u4e8b} is a \"thing\" or \"action.\" So, this is a \"request action,\" in a sense. A better way to say that is {tooltip:Vocabulary:one's wish} or a {tooltip:Vocabulary:prayer}, because that's what you're doing when you do the action of requesting something.",
