{
            "mnemonic": "What you {tooltip:Kanji:build} up in {tooltip:Kanji:front} of other people is your public image. This is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:public behavior}, how you act around others you don't really know. This concept is surprisingly important in Japan, so you'll hear it often enough despite being such a strange concept in other places. You'll have to think of this like you're building buildings of personality in front of you. These show off who you are on the outside, but it protects what's on the inside.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Public Behavior",
                "Alternatives": "Public Behaviour, Official Stance, Public Position, Public Face, Tatemae",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3066\u307e\u3048"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3066\u307e\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "6897-subject-3996.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u305f\u3066\u307e\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29788-subject-3996.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is pretty strange. It's a lot like {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u7269} in that it's read as {span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3066}, which is like the word {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u3066\u308b} even though the {span:lang=ja:\u3066} isn't showing here. So, you'll have to remember it's read like {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u3066\u308b} but the {span:lang=ja:\u3066} gets pushed into the kanji.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u672c\u97f3\u3068\u5efa\u524d\u3092\u4f7f\u3044\u5206\u3051\u308b\u306e\u304c\u4e0a\u624b\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet is good at separating his public and private selves."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3044\u3058\u3087\u3046\u304c\u7121\u3044\u3068\u3053\u3053\u306e\u533b\u8005\u306b\u307f\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3046\u306e\u306f\u5efa\u524d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Our official stance is that you can't see a doctor here without a letter of reference."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u304f\u300c\u672c\u97f3\u3068\u5efa\u524d\u300d\u306f\u65e5\u672c\u72ec\u7279\u306e\u6587\u5316\u3060\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u5b9f\u969b\u306f\u4e16\u754c\u4e2d\u306b\u5b58\u5728\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "It\u2019s often said that \"the contrast between one\u2019s personal feelings and public behavior\" is a characteristic unique to Japanese culture, but that exists all over the world."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:tie} up all the {tooltip:Kanji:fruit} because you're going to use them to make giant fruit letters. These giant fruit letters will show the {tooltip:Vocabulary:result} of the big monkey election.",
