                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}You've learned the {tooltip:Reading:\u304c\u308f} as the reading for this kanji, but when its used on its own as a vocabulary word, it is read as {tooltip:Reading:\u305d\u3070}. Here's a mnemonic to help you remember:\n{splitParent}Having a {tooltip:Reading:sober}({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3070}) person by your {tooltip:Vocabulary:side} is important when you're drunk. \n{splitParent}Think of other vocabulary words that use {tooltip:Reading:\u304c\u308f}. In these words, {tooltip:Kanji:\u5074} is a suffix, so it will have another kanji that comes before it. \n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
