                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You didn't learn this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u8a00} though, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}Nothing cuts through {tooltip:Vocabulary:silence} like a {tooltip:Reading:gon}g ({span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3093}). Once it's done gonging you really notice how silent the world around you is.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bce\u6669\u7121\u8a00\u96fb\u8a71\u304c\u304b\u304b\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Every night I get a silent prank phone call."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u793e\u54e1\u305f\u3061\u306f\u3001\u7121\u8a00\u3067\u3082\u304f\u3082\u304f\u3068\u4ed5\u4e8b\u3092\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u898b\u3048\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u5b9f\u306f\u30b9\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u3068\u3044\u3046\u30a2\u30d7\u30ea\u3067\u30c1\u30e3\u30c3\u30c8\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Tofugu workers seem to work silently, but they are actually chatting on an app called Slack."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u77e5\u3089\u306a\u3044\u30aa\u30c3\u30b5\u30f3\u304b\u3089\u6025\u306b\u6bcd\u89aa\u3063\u3066\u306e\u306f\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u5b50\u3069\u3082\u306b\u611b\u60c5\u3092\u611f\u3058\u308b\u3082\u306e\u3060\u308d\u3046\u3068\u304b\u8aac\u6559\u3055\u308c\u3066\u3055\u3041\u3001\u3073\u3063\u304f\u308a\u3057\u3066\u7121\u8a00\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Suddenly, some random guy started lecturing me about how mothers feel affection for their children, and it freaked me out so much I went completely silent."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Maybe you didn't know this, but if you're like everyone else learning a new language, you learn the cuss words first. {span:lang=ja:\u304f\u305d} is sh*t / garbage, though it's not really a \"bad\" word in Japanese like it is in English. So, what is your {tooltip:Kanji:nose} sh*t? It's your {tooltip:Vocabulary:snot} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:boogers}. Ewwww, stop eating them!",
