{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:failure}, but \"to failure\" doesn't make sense. What happens when you experience failure, though? Well you get defeated, and you're also unsuccessful. So, this verb is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be defeated} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be unsuccessful}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Defeated",
                "Alternative": "To Be Unsuccessful",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3084\u3076\u308c\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u3076\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "7058-subject-4005.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u3076\u308c\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29885-subject-4005.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: You have been defeated. You lay there on the ground, and the fans around the stadium are disgusted with your performance. Some hipster walks up to you and says: \"{tooltip:Reading:Yah, Boo}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3084\u3076}) referring to how poorly you did. \"No boo!\" you reply back. \"Yah boo\" they say again.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d6\u30eb\u30fc\u30b8\u30a7\u30a4\u30ba\u306f\u3001\u30ec\u30c3\u30c9\u30bd\u30c3\u30af\u30b9\u306b\u4e09\u5bfe\u4e00\u3067\u6557\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The Blue Jays lost the game to the Red Socks with a score of 1-3."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u307f\u3093\u306a\u304c\u4e88\u60f3\u3057\u3066\u3044\u305f\u901a\u308a\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u4eca\u56de\u3082\u306e\u3069\u81ea\u307e\u3093\u30b3\u30f3\u30c6\u30b9\u30c8\u3067\u6557\u308c\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "As we all expected, Koichi was defeated again in the singing contest."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30aa\u30ea\u30f3\u30d4\u30c3\u30af\u306e\u4e88\u9078\u7b2c\u4e00\u56de\u6226\u3067\u6557\u308c\u305f\u65e5\u672c\u4ee3\u8868\u306e\u30a2\u30a4\u30b9\u30db\u30c3\u30b1\u30fc\u30c1\u30fc\u30e0\u306b\u3001\u6012\u3063\u3066\u30ab\u30ec\u30fc\u3092\u6295\u3052\u3064\u3051\u305f\u7537\u306e\u8a71\u805e\u3044\u305f\uff1f",
                    "en": "Did you hear that a guy got upset with Japan\u2019s national ice hockey team when they were defeated in the first round of a preliminary game for the Olympics and threw some curry at them?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:courage} so the verb version is what happens when you have lots of it. Someone with courage is probably the kind of person {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be lively} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be encouraged}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Be Encouraged",
                "Alternatives": "To Be Lively, To Be In High Spirits, To Cheer Up, To Be Excited, To Be Inspired",
                "Word Type": "godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3055\u3080"
