                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29801-subject-3994.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is shared with {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u3066\u308b}, so if you know {span:lang=ja:\u5efa\u3066\u308b} then you should be able to read this word as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6771\u4eac\u306b\u306f\u3001\u65b0\u3057\u3044\u9ad8\u305d\u3046\u30d3\u30eb\u304c\u305e\u304f\u305e\u304f\u3068\u5efa\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "New high-rise buildings are being built one after another in Tokyo."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30db\u30ef\u30a4\u30c8\u30cf\u30a6\u30b9\u306b\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u3069\u3046\u305e\u3046\u304c\u5efa\u3061\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi's bronze statue was erected at the White House."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b5\u30fc\u30e2\u30f3\u3068\u50d5\u306f\u3001\u6d5c\u8fba\u306e\u5317\u7aef\u306b\u5efa\u3064\u5bb6\u3092\u8cb7\u304a\u3046\u3068\u76f8\u8ac7\u3057\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u79c1\u9054\u306b\u306f\u5024\u6bb5\u304c\u9ad8\u3044\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "Salmon and I are discussing buying a pre-built home at the north end of the beach, but it\u2019s a little expensive for us."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:sad} so the verb form of that is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be sad}. Boohoo.",
