                ],
                "hints": "Feel the pain of the tattoo needle as you get scooters tattooed onto your body. It might hurt now, but you\u2019ll be rewarded with great happiness later in life.",
                "mnemonic": "If you can't {tooltip:Kanji:attain} a scooter, attaining a {tooltip:Reading:tattoo} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3064}) of one is the next best thing. Might as well get two tattooed on because {tooltip:Kanji:plural} is always better. This is a surefire way to attain happiness. Get a tattoo."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:gambler} sets {tooltip:Radical:fire} to his home in order to {tooltip:Kanji:bake} some goods and {tooltip:Kanji:cook} a turkey. Setting his house on fire isn\u2019t exactly the brightest idea, but the gambler is taking a gamble that the things he baked and cooked in the fire will offset the cost of a new home. ",
            "hints": "Feel the fiery flames around you as you smell the smell of baked goods and cooked meat in your nostrils.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bake",
                "Alternatives": "Cook, Burn"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
