                "hints": "While many things in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} may not be created equal, the temples are, at least. ",
                "mnemonic": "The bamboo temple is also an {tooltip:Kanji:equal} distance away from the other temples in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. When you look at a map of {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} temples, you can measure them out and they'll all be perfectly equal."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:winter}, one can use a sliced up {tooltip:Radical:tree} as a {tooltip:Kanji:flat objects counter}. Since it\u2019s winter, all the leaves have fallen off the tree, so it\u2019s easy to cut into slats. These slats can be used as counters for flat objects, such as these slats.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself counting these flat objects in winter. It\u2019s super cold, but you have to count them. How many are there?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Flat Objects Counter",
                "Alternatives": "Flat Object, Counter For Flat Objects"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now imagine yourself counting on these mice you just smashed. They\u2019re freshly dead, so there\u2019s not much of a stench yet, but you still feel bad about using dead mice to help you count. Imagine yourself counting on these mice as you try to hold back tears from all the murder you just did.",
                "mnemonic": "While trying to count these slats of wood, a whole bunch of {tooltip:Reading:mi}ce ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u3044}) show up and start climbing all over the tree. This will not do, so you take two slats and start smashing and flattening all the mice. Now that the mice are flat too, you can also use them as a {tooltip:Kanji:flat objects counter}. Good job, mice."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:death} of your {tooltip:Radical:heart} will cause you to {tooltip:Kanji:forget} all of the most important things. People think memories are kept in your brain, but that's not true. Your heart is where all of your most precious memories are kept, and when it dies, you forget them all.",
            "hints": "Imagine someone close to you experiencing the death of their heart. They look right at you but they've already started to forget everything. I know this is not a fun thing to imagine, but use that emotion to help you remember this kanji, not forget it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Forget"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You know, that's probably why so many old people go bowling. They forgot everything else.",
                "mnemonic": "When someone {tooltip:Kanji:forget}s everything they're left with only one thing to do: go {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}). Bowling is easy, and there's nothing to forget. You pick up a ball. You drop it. Everything else is automatically taken care of."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Using {tooltip:Radical:flowers} to make a {tooltip:Radical:lip ring} is always going to end in {tooltip:Kanji:frustration}.",
            "hints": "Have you ever made a daisy chain? Try making a daisy lip ring. Just imagine your frustation as you try to make it small enough to fit through your lip piercing.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Frustration"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
