                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u4e08\u592b\u3060\u3088\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u4e88\u544a\u306a\u3057\u306b\u304b\u3044\u3053\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You'll be alright. Koichi won't fire you without prior notice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e09\u30f6\u6708\u5bb6\u3061\u3093\u3092\u305f\u3044\u306e\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u3001\u7acb\u3061\u306e\u304d\u3092\u4e88\u544a\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I left my rent unpaid for three months and then I was given an eviction notice."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bba\u4eba\u4e88\u544a\u3092\u544a\u3052\u308b\u624b\u7d19\u304c\u3001Tofugu\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u306b\u5c4a\u3051\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "A letter giving advance notice for a murder arrived at the Tofugu office."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:announce} something to a {tooltip:Kanji:wide} audience, you're just throwing your message out there for everyone to hear. This is just a big wide {tooltip:Vocabulary:advertisement}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Advertisement",
                "Alternatives": "Ad, Advert",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046\u3053\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3046\u3053\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30036-subject-4083.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3046\u3053\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20607-subject-4083.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Sorry, you learned the kun'yomi reading with {span:lang=ja:\u5e83}. So, think of it this way when you need to remember this word's meaning: You're {tooltip:Vocabulary:advertising} something. It's a big advertisement to advertise how terrible a person {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} is. Come up with some terrible things he's done so that you can imagine this crazy Koichi advertisement you made and ran on national TV.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u56f3\u66f8\u9928\u304b\u3089\u501f\u308a\u305f\u672c\u306b\u3001\u30b9\u30fc\u30d1\u30fc\u306e\u5e83\u544a\u304c\u4e00\u679a\u306f\u3055\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "In a book I borrowed from the library, there was a grocery store advertisement stuck between the pages."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30af\u30fc\u30dd\u30f3\u304c\u4ed8\u3044\u305f\u5e83\u544a\u3092\u5fd8\u308c\u305f\u306e\u3067\u3001\u5bb6\u306b\u3082\u3069\u3089\u306a\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3044\u3051\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I have to go back home because I forgot the ad with the coupon."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u3001\u30a2\u30e4\u304cTofugu\u306e\u5e83\u544a\u306b\u3082\u306e\u3059\u3054\u304f\u5909\u308f\u3063\u305f\u7d75\u3092\u63cf\u3044\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u544a\u3052\u53e3\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet informed Koichi that Aya created the strangest picture ever for Tofugu\u2019s advertisement."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3046} is \"to laugh.\" This is the noun version, because the {span:lang=ja:\u3046} in {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3046} turns to {span:lang=ja:\u3044} (so don't confuse this as an adjective). What is the noun version of \"to laugh\"? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:a laugh}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "A Laugh",
                "Alternative": "Laugh",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u308f\u3089\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u3089\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "7150-subject-4063.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u3089\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29903-subject-4063.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same as {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3046}, so just make sure you know that so you can know this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u3067\u306f\u30af\u30ea\u30b9\u30de\u30b9\u30c7\u30a3\u30ca\u30fc\u306b\u30b1\u30f3\u30bf\u30c3\u30ad\u30fc\u3092\u98df\u3079\u308b\u3068\u8a00\u3063\u305f\u3089\u3001\u306a\u305c\u304b\u7b11\u3044\u304c\u8d77\u304d\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Everybody laughed for some reason when I said that people eat KFC for Christmas dinner in Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3046\u304b\u308c\u81ea\u8eab\u591a\u5206\u4f55\u3092\u7b11\u3063\u3066\u308b\u306e\u304b\u5206\u304b\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u305f\u3060\u7b11\u3044\u304c\u6b62\u307e\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3046\u3058\u3087\u3046\u305f\u3044\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I feel like he probably doesn't even know what he's laughing at anymore, but he just can't help it."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6620\u753b\u3092\u898b\u3066\u6ce3\u304f\u306a\u3093\u3066\u3001\u304a\u524d\u3089\u3057\u304f\u306a\u3044\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u304b\u3002\u3044\u3064\u3082\u3069\u306e\u6620\u753b\u306e\u3069\u3093\u306a\u6df1\u523b\u306a\u30b7\u30fc\u30f3\u306b\u3082\u5927\u7b11\u3044\u3057\u3066\u308b\u306e\u306b\u3002",
                    "en": "It\u2019s not like you to cry at movies. You always laugh really hard when there are any serious scenes in them."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

