                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Don't confuse this with the same-sounding {span:lang=ja:\u6226\u8eca} though... unless you're washing your {span:lang=ja:\u6226\u8eca} in a {span:lang=ja:\u6d17\u8eca}...\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u8eca\u306e\u6d17\u8eca\u3092\u3057\u305f\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3046\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u305f\u3089\u3001hello@tofugu.com\u307e\u3067\u30e1\u30fc\u30eb\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "If there's someone out there who wants to wash Koichi's car, please email us at hello@tofugu.com."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6d17\u8eca\u304c\u7d42\u308f\u308b\u306e\u3092\u5f85\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u9593\u3001\u30ac\u30bd\u30ea\u30f3\u30b9\u30bf\u30f3\u30c9\u306e\u30d0\u30a4\u30c8\u304c\u305a\u3063\u3068\u30c0\u30e9\u30c0\u30e9\u8a71\u3057\u304b\u3051\u3066\u304d\u3066\u3001\u304b\u306a\u308a\u30a6\u30b6\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "While I waited for the car wash to finish, the part-timer kept yacking at me and it was really annoying."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8ab0\u304c\u30de\u30cd\u30fc\u30fb\u30ed\u30f3\u30c0\u30ea\u30f3\u30b0\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306b\u6d17\u8eca\u30d3\u30b8\u30cd\u30b9\u306a\u3093\u3066\u8cb7\u3046\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3046\u306e\u3055\uff1f",
                    "en": "Who would buy a car wash business to launder money?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You hopefully know that {span:lang=ja:\u8a3c\u660e} means \"proof.\" So, when the {tooltip:Kanji:proof} is {tooltip:Kanji:written} down, what kind of proof is it? It's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:certificate} of some kind. I'm going to need to see some {span:lang=ja:\u8a3c\u660e\u66f8} if you want to get in here, sir.",
