{
            "mnemonic": "You know how {span:lang=ja:\u5b88\u308b} is \"to protect,\" right? This is like that, but it's the noun version. It's not really \"a protection,\" though it kind of is. What things can you wear to protect you from things like bad luck, demons, and ancient aliens? That would be a {tooltip:Vocabulary:amulet} or an {tooltip:Vocabulary:charm}. You'll see these kinds of things sold at temples and such.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Amulet",
                "Alternative": "Charm",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u307e\u3082\u308a"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
