{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3046} is \"to laugh.\" This is a noun version of that, though it's not \"a laugh,\" (that's {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3044}). Add {span:lang=ja:\u304a} to that and you have the thing that makes you laugh. It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:comedy}. It's the {tooltip:Vocabulary:joke} that's elevated with {span:lang=ja:\u304a} because it made you laugh SOOOOO much. Haha!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Comedy",
                "Alternatives": "Joke, Funny Story",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304a\u308f\u3089\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u308f\u3089\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29964-subject-4060.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304a\u308f\u3089\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20724-subject-4060.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the same {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3046} or {span:lang=ja:\u7b11\u3044}. It's also the same as what you learned with the kanji.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30a4\u30b1\u30eb\u304c\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306b\u5165\u308b\u6642\u306b\u9593\u3061\u304c\u3048\u3066\u30e1\u30a4\u30f3\u5dde\u306e\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u306b\u5f15\u3063\u3053\u3057\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u4eca\u3067\u3082\u307f\u3093\u306a\u306e\u304a\u7b11\u3044\u8349\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When Michael got a job at Tofugu, he moved to Portland, Maine by mistake. It's still a funny story we laugh about to this day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u6bce\u65e5\u3001\u30de\u30a4\u30b1\u30eb\u304b\u3089\u304a\u7b11\u3044\u306e\u7279\u304f\u3093\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi gets intensive comedy training from Michael every day."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5922\u306e\u4e2d\u3067\u3001\u79c1\u306f\u304a\u7b11\u3044\u82b8\u4eba\u3067\u3001\u30c6\u30ec\u30d3\u3067\u304a\u5ba2\u3055\u3093\u306e\u524d\u3067\u30aa\u30ca\u30e9\u3092\u3057\u306a\u304f\u3061\u3083\u3044\u3051\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u3046\u307e\u304f\u3067\u304d\u306a\u304b\u3063\u305f\u306e\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3067\u3001\u305d\u306e\u756a\u7d44\u306e\u53f8\u4f1a\u3092\u52d9\u3081\u3066\u305f\u5148\u8f29\u82b8\u4eba\u306b\u3059\u3054\u304f\u6012\u3089\u308c\u305f\u306e\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "In my dream, I was a comedian and I had to fart on purpose in front of the TV audience, but I couldn\u2019t do it. Then I was scolded by the experienced comedians who hosted the show."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:paragraph} in {tooltip:Kanji:writing} is what you send someone when you want to submit a {tooltip:Vocabulary:complaint}. You want to make sure these are in writing, though, otherwise you don't have proof of your complaint. Also, don't make it longer than a paragraph, because that's too long and nobody cares about how you think the shop staff mistreated your dog Fluffy.",
