{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:equal}? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:equal} (and also {tooltip:Vocabulary:similar} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:equivalent}). That \"similar\" one is a bit weird, because \"similar\" is not equal, though I'd lean more towards equal.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Equal",
                "Alternatives": "The Same, Equivalent, Similar",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3068\u3057\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3072\u3068\u3057\u3044",
