                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. It will help to know the word {span:lang=ja:\u66dc\u65e5} as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u91d1\u66dc\u65e5\u306b\u98f2\u307f\u306b\u884c\u304f\u7d04\u675f\u3001\u5fd8\u308c\u3066\u306a\u3044\u3088\u306d\uff1f",
                    "en": "You haven't forgotten that we planned to go out for drinks Friday night, have you?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u3001\u6bce\u9031\u91d1\u66dc\u65e5\u306e\u591c\u306b\u3001\u60c5\u5831\u306e\u30d0\u30c3\u30af\u30a2\u30c3\u30d7\u3092\u4f5c\u6210\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet makes a backup of our data every Friday night."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u30b3\u30b9\u30c1\u30e5\u30fc\u30e0\u3067\u3059\u304c\u3001\u3044\u3064\u9803\u4ed5\u4e0a\u304c\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\u306d\u3048\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u91d1\u66dc\u65e5\u306e\u5348\u5f8c\u307e\u3067\u306b\u306f\u3067\u304d\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"When will my Fugu costume be ready?\" \"It\u2019ll be ready by Friday afternoon.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:friend} that you {tooltip:Kanji:attain} is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:friend}. This is the most common way to say \"friend,\" so learn it if you want to make any!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Friend",
                "Alternative": "Companion",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21333-subject-4151.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30067-subject-4151.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings for both of these are readings you haven't learned yet, though maybe you already know this word since it's fairly common. Think of it this way. You have your friend {tooltip:Reading:Tom} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3082}) Cruise. You like him, and he likes you. You're close enough friends that you can {tooltip:Reading:touch} ({span:lang=ja:\u3060\u3061}) each other too. Like, on the shoulder or on the hand or whatever, without it being awkward. So, you like to {tooltip:Reading:Tom touch} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3082\u3060\u3061}) when you can, because he has nice skin.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u304a\u53cb\u9054\u30ea\u30b9\u30c8\u306b\u79c1\u3092\u3064\u3044\u304b\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please add me to your friends list."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u53cb\u9054\u304c\u3001\u3053\u3053\u306f\u3061\u3085\u3046\u8eca\u7981\u6b62\u30a8\u30ea\u30a2\u3060\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "My friend told me that this is a no-parking area."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u5074\u306b\u3044\u3066\u304f\u308c\u3066\u3042\u308a\u304c\u3068\u3046\u3002\u300d\u300c\u4f55\u8a00\u3063\u3066\u308b\u306e\u3088\uff01\u53cb\u9054\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u306e\uff01\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Thank you for taking my side.\" \"What are you talking about? We\u2019re friends, aren\u2019t we?\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:silver} {tooltip:Kanji:seat} isn't some crazy kingdom where the king sits upon a silver seat. It is a famous place in Tokyo. Perhaps if you read the reading it will become more apparent what the meaning is (since they're the same). This silver seat place is {tooltip:Vocabulary:Ginza}.",
