                        "file": "40804-subject-8853.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u982d} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}They used to make you {tooltip:Vocabulary:kowtow} every single time you came to {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. That's full on head to floor kowtowing in front of everyone who is already in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} to prove that you appreciate being there. They might even make you do it these days too, if you're not being respectful enough while you're there.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u53e9\u982d\u3068\u306f\u3001\u3044\u308f\u3086\u308b\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u571f\u4e0b\u5ea7\u306e\u3053\u3068\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "\"Kowtow\" is what is called \"dogeza\" in Japan."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u90e8\u5c4b\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3044\u305f\u5168\u54e1\u304c\u3001\u738b\u306b\u5411\u304b\u3063\u3066\u53e9\u982d\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Everyone in the room kowtowed toward the king."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u7537\u306f\u3001\u53e9\u982d\u3092\u62d2\u5426\u3057\u305f\u305f\u3081\u3001\u5211\u52d9\u6240\u306b\u5165\u308c\u3089\u308c\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Since the man refused to kowtow, he was put into a jail."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
