                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21539-subject-4144.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the word {span:lang=ja:\u8aad\u307f} (like {span:lang=ja:\u8aad\u3080}) and the reading you learned for {span:lang=ja:\u8a13} combined, making {span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3093\u3088\u307f}. Sounds familiar? It's that {tooltip:Vocabulary:kun'yomi} reading you've heard so much about.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u6f22\u5b57\u306f\u3001\u8a13\u8aad\u307f\u3067\u3082\u97f3\u8aad\u307f\u3067\u3082\u8aad\u3081\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "This kanji can be read with either the kun'yomi or on'yomi readings."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u6f22\u5b57\u306f\u3001\u8a13\u8aad\u307f\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Do you know this kanji's kun'yomi?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3064\u3082\u8a13\u8aad\u307f\u3068\u97f3\u8aad\u307f\u3092\u9593\u9055\u3048\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "I mix up kun\u2019yomi and on\u2019yomi all the time."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The body part that lives between your {tooltip:Kanji:throat} and your {tooltip:Kanji:head} is your {tooltip:Vocabulary:larynx}. Otherwise known as the {tooltip:Vocabulary:voice box}, because your vocal cords live in there.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Larynx",
                "Alternative": "Voice Box",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046\u3068\u3046"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3046\u3068\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40714-subject-8851.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u3046\u3068\u3046",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "40802-subject-8851.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u982d} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}If you really want to get a {tooltip:Vocabulary:larynx} work out, go to {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. It's loud, it's crowded, and you have to yell the entire time to get people to hear what you have to say. You also know 18 levels of kanji and you really want to shout them all out, which makes your {tooltip:Vocabulary:voice box} tired (but makes you happy).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5589\u982d\u306f\u3001\u5589\u307c\u3068\u3051\u306e\u4e00\u90e8\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The larynx is one part of the Adam's apple."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5589\u982d\u30ac\u30f3\u306f\u305f\u3070\u3053\u3084\u98f2\u9152\u304c\u539f\u56e0\u3067\u8d77\u3053\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u591a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Laryngeal cancer is often caused by smoking and drinking."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5589\u982d\u708e\u3067\u606f\u3092\u3057\u305f\u308a\u3001\u6c34\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3060\u308a\u3059\u308b\u306e\u3055\u3048\u82e6\u3057\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Because of my laryngeal inflammation, it's painful for me to even breathe or drink water."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "At least way back in the day, things that {tooltip:Kanji:teach} {tooltip:Kanji:instructions} to people are things that teach a {tooltip:Vocabulary:lesson} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:moral}. Back in the day, lots of learning was done through storytelling, and storytelling taught lessons and morals, thus, this word.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lesson",
                "Alternative": "Moral",
