                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20779-subject-7702.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings for this word are all kun'yomi readings. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5b88} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}When you finish singing a {tooltip:Vocabulary:lullaby} to your child they always ask for {tooltip:Reading:more} ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u308a}). It doesn't matter how many you sing, they always want at least one more before they will fall asleep.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30af\u30ea\u30b9\u30c6\u30f3\u306e\u5b50\u5b88\u6b4c\u306f\u3001\u30d7\u30ed\u306e\u3044\u304d\u306b\u9054\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Kristen's lullaby has reached the professional level."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e1\u30ea\u30ab\u3067\u4e00\u756a\u6709\u540d\u306a\u5b50\u5b88\u6b4c\u306f\u4f55\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "What's the most popular lullaby in America?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5b50\u4f9b\u306e\u9803\u306b\u6b4c\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3063\u305f\u5b50\u5b88\u6b4c\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "It's a lullaby that was sung for me when I was little."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you categorize {tooltip:Kanji:people} into {tooltip:Kanji:type}s, you have different {tooltip:Vocabulary:races of people}. Or, you can categorize people as one type of \"people\" in this universe. If you did this, you'd call us {tooltip:Vocabulary:mankind}.",
