                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u5e74\u306e\u6625\u304b\u3089\u3001\u3080\u3059\u3081\u3092\u4fdd\u80b2\u5712\u306b\u3042\u305a\u3051\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u53ef\u80fd\u3060\u3068\u805e\u3044\u3066\u3001\u80f8\u306e\u3064\u304b\u3048\u304c\u4e0b\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Hearing that it would be possible for me to put my daughter in daycare this spring lifted a huge weight off my shoulders."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3082\u3046\u5c11\u3057\u5b9f\u3052\u3093\u53ef\u80fd\u306a\u304b\u3044\u6c7a\u3055\u304f\u3092\u3066\u3044\u3042\u3093\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please present a few more possible solutions."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306f\u5e74\u9593\u4e00\u5104\u30c9\u30eb\u3092\u7a3c\u3050\u3053\u3068\u306f\u5b9f\u73fe\u53ef\u80fd\u3060\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019d say earning a hundred million dollars a year is possible."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:writing} that you put on a {tooltip:Kanji:leaf} is like something else. Instead of a leaf, think about writing you put on a leafish sized item. A {tooltip:Vocabulary:postcard} perhaps?",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Postcard",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304c\u304d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u304c\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "7207-subject-4143.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u304c\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29942-subject-4143.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is kind of weird, sorry. The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u8449} is the {span:lang=ja:\u306f} you know and love. Then, {span:lang=ja:\u66f8} is {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304d} despite not having a {span:lang=ja:\u304d} on the end like you'd expect. So, it's weird. It's shortened like a postcard is a shortened letter, I suppose? Technically it is the {span:lang=ja:\u66f8\u304d} reading, but keep in mind that {span:lang=ja:\u66f8\u304d} gets rendaku'd.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3061\u3087\u3063\u3068\u305d\u306e\u8449\u66f8\u3092\u304a\u501f\u308a\u3057\u3066\u3082\u3044\u3044\u3067\u3059\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Could I borrow the postcard for a moment?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3086\u3046\u4fbf\u5c40\u3067\u8449\u66f8\u3092\u8cb7\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u304a\u91d1\u3092\u306f\u3089\u3063\u305f\u3042\u3068\u3001\u305d\u306e\u307e\u307e\u5fd8\u308c\u3066\u305d\u3053\u306b\u304a\u3044\u3066\u304d\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u307f\u305f\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "I bought postcards at the post office, but it seems that I left them there after paying."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304c\u5b9f\u306f\u3068\u3042\u308b\u79d8\u5bc6\u306e\u56fd\u306e\u738b\u5b50\u69d8\u3067\u3001\u306e\u3063\u3074\u304d\u306a\u3089\u306a\u3044\u7406\u7531\u306e\u305f\u3081\u30dd\u30fc\u30c8\u30e9\u30f3\u30c9\u30aa\u30ec\u30b4\u30f3\u3067\u8eab\u5206\u3092\u96a0\u3057\u3066Tofugu\u306e\u793e\u9577\u3068\u3057\u3066\u751f\u304d\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3044\u3046\u5947\u5999\u306a\u8449\u66f8\u3092\u53d7\u3051\u53d6\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I received a weird postcard saying that Koichi is actually the prince of a secret country, but he is living incognito as the Tofugu president in Portland, Oregon for some unavoidable reason."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

