                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u5831\u544a\u3057\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "Shouldn't we report this to Koichi?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3001\u30c8\u30fc\u30d5\u30b0\u306e\u5e74\u6b21\u5831\u544a\u3092\u3001\u793e\u54e1\u305f\u3061\u306b\u53e3\u982d\u3067\u5831\u544a\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi gave an oral report of Tofugu's annual report for the workers."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5f7c\u304c\u9003\u3052\u51fa\u3055\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u306b\u3001\u3081\u3061\u3083\u304f\u3061\u3083\u9762\u767d\u3044\u598a\u5a20\u306e\u5831\u544a\u65b9\u6cd5\u3092\u8003\u3048\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "I\u2019m thinking about the funniest way to inform my boyfriend that I\u2019m pregnant so that he won\u2019t run away from me."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:bake}d {tooltip:Kanji:bird} isn't just any bird, it's {tooltip:Vocabulary:roast chicken}. You may also know it by its romanized Japanese name: {tooltip:Vocabulary:yakitori}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Roast Chicken",
                "Alternatives": "Cooked Chicken, Yakitori",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3084\u304d\u3068\u308a"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u304d\u3068\u308a",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
