                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30018-subject-4117.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are the vocab kun'yomi readings. With {span:lang=ja:\u713c\u304d}, you can use the reading you learned with the kanji. With {span:lang=ja:\u9ce5} just remember back to the vocab word, {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u308a}. Combine and eat.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u713c\u304d\u9ce5\u306f\u79c1\u306e\u751f\u6d3b\u306b\u4e0d\u53ef\u6b20\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Yakitori is essential for my life."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e3b\u4eba\u306f\u713c\u304d\u9ce5\u5c4b\u306e\u3051\u3044\u3048\u3044\u304c\u5fd9\u3057\u3059\u304e\u3066\u3001\u3051\u3063\u3053\u3093\u8a18\u5ff5\u65e5\u306e\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3059\u3063\u304b\u308a\u5fd8\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My husband was too busy running his yakitori restaurant and he totally forgot about our wedding anniversary."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u305b\u3044\u306b\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3002\u3042\u306a\u305f\u306e\u713c\u304d\u9ce5\u306a\u3093\u304b\u98df\u3079\u3066\u306a\u3044\u308f\u3088\uff01",
                    "en": "Don\u2019t blame me! I didn\u2019t eat your yakitori."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Mmmmm, yum! Take some {tooltip:Kanji:meat} and {tooltip:Kanji:cook} it. Then you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:roast meat} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:cooked meat}. If you go to Japan look out for {span:lang=ja:\u713c\u8089} places (same meaning/reading). They are good, if you're into meat at least.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Roast Meat",
                "Alternatives": "Grilled Meat, Cooked Meat, Yakiniku",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3084\u304d\u306b\u304f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u304d\u306b\u304f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30005-subject-4118.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
