                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20613-subject-4118.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}{span:lang=ja:\u713c\u304d} uses the reading you learned with the kanji. {span:lang=ja:\u8089} does too. Put them on the grill and enjoy!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u713c\u304d\u8089\u5c4b\u306b\u30ab\u30e1\u30e9\u3092\u304a\u3044\u3066\u304d\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I left my camera at the yakiniku restaurant."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u53bb\u308b\u8005\u3088\u308a\u6b8b\u308b\u8005\u306e\u65b9\u304c\u3064\u3089\u3044\u3068\u3044\u3046\u306e\u306f\u3001\u713c\u304d\u8089\u3092\u98df\u3079\u3066\u308b\u6642\u306b\u306f\u5f53\u3066\u306f\u307e\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "They say it's harder for the person left behind than it is for the one who leaves, but this doesn't apply when we're eating grilled meat, now does it?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u304c\u7279\u306b\u30a4\u30e9\u30a4\u30e9\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3001\u713c\u304d\u8089\u3092\u30af\u30c1\u30e3\u30af\u30c1\u30e3\u97f3\u3092\u7acb\u3066\u3066\u98df\u3079\u308b\u4eba\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I find it really irritating when people chew yakiniku loudly."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Something {tooltip:Kanji:below} your {tooltip:Kanji:writing} isn't what you want to necessarily publish to the world. It's below your writing, after all. This is merely a {tooltip:Vocabulary:rough draft}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rough Draft",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u3059\u308b verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3057\u305f\u304c\u304d"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u305f\u304c\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30035-subject-4104.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3057\u305f\u304c\u304d",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20719-subject-4104.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is all kun'yomi vocab reading, as you can maybe guess from the hiragana sticking out. If you know the readings of the words {span:lang=ja:\u4e0b} and {span:lang=ja:\u66f8\u304f} separately, you should be able to combine them into one reading. Just don't forget the rendaku here!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3044\u3044\u8a18\u4e8b\u3092\u66f8\u304f\u305f\u3081\u306b\u306f\u4e0b\u66f8\u304d\u3092\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u5927\u4e8b\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "In order to write a good article, it is important to make a rough draft."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u306e\u3064\u304f\u3048\u306e\u5f15\u304d\u51fa\u3057\u306b\u306f\u3001\u9ad8\u6821\u306e\u6642\u306b\u66f8\u3044\u305f\u81ea\u4f5c\u306e\u8a69\u306e\u4e0b\u66f8\u304d\u304c\u5927\u5207\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3042\u308b\u3063\u3066\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u308b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Did you know Koichi keeps the rough draft for a poem he wrote in high school in his desk drawer in the office?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30e4\u3063\u3066\u3001\u3044\u3064\u3082\u6700\u521d\u306b\u925b\u7b46\u3067\u4e0b\u66f8\u304d\u3057\u3066\u308b\u306e\u304b\u306a\u3002\u305d\u308c\u3068\u3082\u3001\u4e0b\u66f8\u304d\u7121\u3057\u3067\u7d75\u3092\u63cf\u3044\u3066\u308b\u306e\u304b\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "I wonder if Aya usually makes a rough pencil draft first or if she just draws freehand."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:big} {tooltip:Kanji:height} of your {tooltip:Kanji:husband} makes everything {tooltip:Vocabulary:safe} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:all right}. Nothing you need to worry about when you have your super giant husband around to protect you. This is a really useful word, and it is used all the time. If someone asks: \"Are you alright?\" you could say in response \"{span:lang=ja:\u5927\u4e08\u592b}\" to mean you're doing all right.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Safe",
                "Alternatives": "All Right, Okay",
