                        "file": "40809-subject-8855.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word uses the kun'yomi reading for the first kanji and the on'yomi readings for the second two. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5de5} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}You want your {tooltip:Vocabulary:sugar sculptures} to be made into {tooltip:Reading:coo}kies ({span:lang=ja:\u304f})! Cookies are your other favorite snack, so having a cookie that's really just entirely made of sugar is the absolute best.\n{splitParent}Also, watch out for the rendaku on {span:lang=ja:\u7d30}, it's easy to miss if you're focusing on remembering this new on'yomi reading.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u7236\u306f\u98f4\u7d30\u5de5\u306e\u540d\u4eba\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My father is a master of sugar sculptures."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u98f4\u7d30\u5de5\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3042\u308b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Have you ever made sugar sculptures?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u91d1\u9b5a\u306e\u98f4\u7d30\u5de5\u306f\u3001\u5f62\u3082\u5473\u3082\u672c\u7269\u306e\u91d1\u9b5a\u306b\u305d\u3063\u304f\u308a\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3063\u3066\u3002",
                    "en": "Apparently, the sugar goldfish is similar to real goldfish in shape and taste."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When the {tooltip:Kanji:sun} {tooltip:Kanji:cook}s something, and that something is you, it is giving you {tooltip:Vocabulary:sunburn}.",
