        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:tea} {tooltip:Kanji:shop} where you {tooltip:Kanji:consume} (tea) is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:tea house}. Welcome! Sit down. Relax. Have some tea.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tea House",
                "Alternatives": "Cafe, Coffee House, Coffee Shop",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3063\u3055\u3066\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3063\u3055\u3066\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21319-subject-4088.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304d\u3063\u3055\u3066\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30058-subject-4088.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings are what you'd expect except for {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3064} getting shortened to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3063} and {span:lang=ja:\u8336}, which has this strange {span:lang=ja:\u3055} reading. To remember that it's {span:lang=ja:\u3055} instead of {span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3083}, think of this {tooltip:Vocabulary:tea house} you're going in. You think it's nice and pleasant, and it is for a while... until someone starts working a {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}) outside, ruining the atmosphere. BEWWEEEEHHHEEEHHHHHE gatatatatatat BWEEEHEEE.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30a2\u30a4\u30d5\u30a9\u30f3\u304c\u306c\u3059\u307e\u308c\u3061\u3083\u3063\u3066\u3055\u3002\u4eca\u3001\u55ab\u8336\u5e97\u306e\u96fb\u8a71\u3092\u501f\u308a\u3066\u304b\u3051\u3066\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "My iPhone was stolen, so I'm using the tea house telephone to call you now."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u55ab\u8336\u5e97\u3067\u30b3\u30fc\u30d2\u30fc\u3092\u98f2\u3093\u3067\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u30ec\u30b8\u306e\u4eba\u304c\u304a\u3064\u308a\u3092\u308f\u305f\u3057\u5fd8\u308c\u3066\u3066\u79c1\u3082\u305d\u308c\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u304b\u305a\u51fa\u3066\u304d\u3061\u3083\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3088\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I was drinking coffee at a cafe and the cashier forgot to hand me my change, but I also didn't notice and just left."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u53bb\u5e74\u3001\u30d6\u30e9\u30b8\u30eb\u306e\u55ab\u8336\u5e97\u3067\u5076\u7136\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u4f1a\u3063\u305f\u3088\u3002\u300d \u300c\u672c\u5f53\uff1f \u305d\u3046\u8a00\u3048\u3070\u3001\u9577\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3042\u3044\u3064\u306e\u9854\u898b\u3066\u306a\u3044\u306a\u3041\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Last year I ran into Koichi in a cafe in Brazil.\" \"Oh, really? Now that you mention it, I haven\u2019t seen him in years.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "An {tooltip:Kanji:institution} for {tooltip:Kanji:monk}s is going to be a {tooltip:Vocabulary:temple} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:monastery}. What a nice place to live, I'm sure!",
