                        "pronunciation": "\u3064\u3052\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29947-subject-4082.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: I'd like {tooltip:Vocabulary:to announce}... we're not having one baby, we're having {tooltip:Reading:two} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064}) babies!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u604b\u4eba\u306b\u5225\u308c\u3092\u544a\u3052\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I bid farewell to my girlfriend."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eca\u65e5\u306e\u671d\u4f1a\u3067\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u660e\u65e5\u304b\u3089\u3058\u3067\u5165\u9662\u3059\u308b\u3053\u3068\u3092\u793e\u54e1\u306b\u544a\u3052\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi announced to his employees at today's morning meeting that he would be hospitalized for hemorrhoids from tomorrow on."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u3001\u30de\u30df\u306f\u307f\u3093\u306a\u306e\u60f3\u50cf\u306e\u659c\u3081\u4e0a\u3092\u884c\u304f\u5909\u4eba\u3060\u3068\u544a\u3052\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Viet told Koichi that Mami is much weirder than everyone imagined."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know that {span:lang=ja:\u9054} means {tooltip:Kanji:attain}. So, when you add {span:lang=ja:\u3059\u308b} to it you make it a verb. Now it means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to attain}.",
