                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn this with the kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you out:\n{splitParent}When you get sick, your mom calls every day to ask, \"Are you better {tooltip:Reading:now} (\u306a\u304a)?\" How about NOW!? How about NOW!? Jeez Mom, just let me rest!\n"
