                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from the individual words {span:lang=ja:\u53d6\u308b} and {span:lang=ja:\u51fa\u3059}. Put them together and you should be able to read this word too.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5929\u624d\u5916\u79d1\u533b\u304c\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u8133\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u51fa\u3057\u3066\u3001\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306b\u3044\u690d\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "A genius surgeon took out Koichi's brain and transplanted it into Viet."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u9ed2\u3044\u670d\u3092\u7740\u305f\u7537\u304c\u3001\u30de\u30a4\u30b1\u30eb\u306e\u304b\u3070\u3093\u304b\u3089\u3055\u3044\u3075\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u51fa\u3059\u306e\u3092\u898b\u305f\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I saw a man in black clothes pick a wallet out of your bag, Michael."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30aa\u30fc\u30d6\u30f3\u304b\u3089\u30d5\u30b0\u3092\u53d6\u308a\u51fa\u3057\u3066\u304a\u3044\u3066\u304f\u308c\u306a\u3044\uff1f\u3042\u3068\u4e94\u5206\u3067\u7740\u304f\u304b\u3089\u3002",
                    "en": "Can you take the blowfish out of the oven for me? I\u2019ll be there in five minutes."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:pray} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to pray}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Pray",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u306e\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u306e\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30108-subject-4122.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u306e\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21330-subject-4122.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \"You gotta pray if you want Santa to bring you Christmas presents!\" \"{tooltip:Reading:I know} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u306e}), I know,\" you reply as you begin to pray to Santa. You should say this out loud to remember it better.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30cf\u30ea\u30b1\u30fc\u30f3\u306e\u3072\u304c\u3044\u8005\u306e\u305f\u3081\u306b\u7948\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I prayed for the hurricane victims."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u56fd\u5bb6\u8a66\u9a13\u306b\u7121\u4e8b\u5408\u683c\u3067\u304d\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u7948\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I will pray for your success on the national exam."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u56fd\u6280\u3067\u3042\u308b\u76f8\u64b2\u304c\u3001\u304b\u3064\u3066\u306f\u7c73\u306e\u8c4a\u4f5c\u3092\u7948\u308b\u5100\u5f0f\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3053\u3068\u3092\u77e5\u3063\u3066\u308b\u65e5\u672c\u4eba\u304c\u305f\u304f\u3055\u3093\u3044\u308b\u3068\u306f\u601d\u3048\u306a\u3044\u306a\u3002",
                    "en": "I don\u2019t think many Japanese people know Japan\u2019s national sport \"sumo\" used to be a ritual to pray for a bountiful rice harvest."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:prohibition} so the verb version means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to prohibit}.",
