{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:news report} so you could try to say \"to news report\" but that doesn't make sense. What does make sense is \"{tooltip:Vocabulary:to report on},\" however.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Report On",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046\u3058\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u307b\u3046\u3058\u308b",
