                        "file": "30159-subject-4107.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u304b\u304d\u306a\u304a\u3059",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21326-subject-4107.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The readings come from {span:lang=ja:\u66f8\u304f} and {span:lang=ja:\u76f4\u3059}. Know those and you'll know how to read this word too!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e3b\u4eba\u516c\u3092\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304b\u3089\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306b\u5909\u3053\u3046\u3057\u3066\u3001\u3053\u306e\u8a71\u3092\u66f8\u304d\u76f4\u3057\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Please change the protagonist to Viet instead of Koichi and rewrite this story."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8a66\u9a13\u7d42\u4e86\u9593\u304e\u308f\u306b\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3001\u53d7\u9a13\u756a\u53f7\u304c\u9593\u3061\u304c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u306b\u6c17\u3065\u3044\u3066\u3001\u3042\u308f\u3066\u3066\u66f8\u304d\u76f4\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I noticed that I wrote the examinee's number wrong at the very end of the exam period and rewrote it in rush."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u3053\u308c\u3092\u66f8\u304d\u76f4\u3059\u6642\u9593\u304c\u3042\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3046\uff1f\u300d\u300c\u79c1\u306f\u305d\u3046\u306f\u601d\u308f\u306a\u3044\u306d\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"Do you think we have enough time to rewrite this?\" \"I don\u2019t think so.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:sit} so the verb vocab version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to sit}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Sit",
                "Word Type": "intransitive verb, godan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3059\u308f\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u308f\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "7111-subject-7479.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3059\u308f\u308b",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "29896-subject-7479.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is unlike the kanji reading, so let's use a separate mnemonic to remember this. Just imagine yourself going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to sit} down. You sit down, and the ground collapses below you and you fall. When you land, you find yourself in a nasty, stinking {tooltip:Reading:sewer} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u308f}). It is so gross. Taste the sewage in your mouth. Smell it. Feel gross. You shouldn't have sat down on that spot, it was looking awfully dangerous, now that you think about it.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5927\u4e8b\u306a\u66f8\u985e\u306e\u4e0a\u306b\u5ea7\u3089\u306a\u3044\u3067\u3082\u3089\u3048\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
                    "en": "Could you not sit on the important documents?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3068\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u3044\u3064\u3082\u30d6\u30fc\u30d6\u30fc\u30af\u30c3\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u3067\u3044\u305f\u305a\u3089\u3059\u308b\u306e\u3067\u30aa\u30d5\u30a3\u30b9\u306e\u3044\u3059\u306b\u5ea7\u308b\u6642\u306f\u6c17\u3092\u3064\u3051\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi and Viet are always playing whoopee cushion pranks, so I'm always careful when I sit down on my office chair."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305a\u3063\u3068\u5ea7\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3068\u3001\u304a\u5c3b\u304c\u6c57\u3070\u3093\u3067\u304d\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "When I\u2019m sitting for a long time my butt gets sweaty."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:strike} or {tooltip:Kanji:beat}, so the verb version is {tooltip:Vocabulary:to strike} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to beat}.",
