                        "file": "40803-subject-8852.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You haven't learned this reading yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}When you're going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to strike} something over and over it makes a {tooltip:Reading:ta-ta} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u305f}) sound. Imagine you're about to beat a steel drum, for example. Now listen... {span:lang=ja:\u305f\u305f}! There! Did you hear it?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30c9\u30e9\u30e0\u3092\u53e9\u304f\u624d\u80fd\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "You have a talent for beating drums."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u958b\u3051\u308b\u524d\u306b\u3001\u30c9\u30a2\u3092\u53e9\u3044\u3066\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3063\u305f\u3088\u306d\uff01\uff1f",
                    "en": "Didn't I tell you to knock before opening the door?!"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u91d8\u30d0\u30c3\u30c8\u3067\u53e9\u304b\u308c\u308b\u306e\u3063\u3066\u3001\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u75db\u3044\uff01",
                    "en": "Being hit with spiked bats really hurts!"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
