                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. It will help to know the word {span:lang=ja:\u66dc\u65e5} as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c34\u66dc\u65e5\u306b\u3059\u308b\u3079\u304d\u3053\u3068\u306f\u3001\u5927\u304d\u304f\u5206\u3051\u3066\u4e09\u3064\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "We can split up what we have to do on Wednesday into three, big things."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6bce\u9031\u6c34\u66dc\u65e5\u306f\u3001\u5b66\u6821\u306e\u5f8c\u30d7\u30fc\u30eb\u306b\u884c\u3063\u3066\u6cf3\u3044\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Every Wednesday after school I go to the pool and swim."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c34\u66dc\u65e5\u306e\u591c\u3001\u5f7c\u306f\u304b\u306a\u308a\u9154\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3066\u3001\u30c8\u30e9\u30c3\u30af\u306b\u8f62\u304b\u308c\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3002",
                    "en": "He got drunk out of his mind Wednesday night and was run over by a truck."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

