                "hints": "Imagine yourself getting mixed up in this situation and the pterodactyl sized condor picking you up. Feel the condor\u2019s talons digging into your shoulders as it grabs you up and flies you towards the sun.",
                "mnemonic": "Just before the tsunami crashes over you, a {tooltip:Reading:con}dor ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3093}) swoops out of the sky and grabs you up. This condor must be a {tooltip:Kanji:mix} \u2013 a normal condor is not strong enough to pick up a human. The condor must be mixed with something else. Like a pterodactyl."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:sheep} loses its {tooltip:Radical:horns} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} so it picks them up in his {tooltip:Radical:mouth} to take them to a {tooltip:Kanji:morally good} doctor who is {tooltip:Kanji:good} enough to attach them back onto his head. This poor sheep lost his horns and now feels quite sad. Sheep don\u2019t have hands, so the sheep had to pick the horns up off the ground with his mouth. An evil doctor would just murder the sheep and steal his horns, so the sheep must find a morally good doctor to reaffix them.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself as the good doctor being approached by this forlorn sheep without horns. Hear the clack of the horns together as the sheep drops them out of his mouth onto the ground and lets out a pathetic bleat. \u201cBaa~aa~ah~\u201d",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Morally Good",
                "Alternative": "Good"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself using your Zen magic to heal this sheep. Place your hands on the sheep\u2019s horns and imagine returning them to their rightful location on the sheep\u2019s head. Feel the soft wool of the sheep as he bleats in happiness.",
                "mnemonic": "Since you are a {tooltip:Kanji:morally good} doctor, you decide not to murder the sheep and harvest its organs. Instead, as a practitioner of the {tooltip:Kanji:good} teachings of {tooltip:Reading:Zen} ({span:lang=ja:\u305c\u3093}) Buddhism, you decided to help the sheep out. Your Zen teachings have only increased the power of your healing abilities, so you fix the sheep up in no time."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "For a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} to make it into a {tooltip:Radical:river}, it must know the {tooltip:Kanji:sequence} and {tooltip:Kanji:order} of water flow. Geoducks usually live in the ocean, not in a river, so they must study the order of water flow in order to determine the best sequence for making it into a river.",
            "hints": "Imagine this geoduck mapping out a plan to get to the river. It\u2019s studying the sequence and order of water flow. See it sitting there, reading a book, reading glasses and all. It\u2019s quite odd.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Order",
                "Alternative": "Sequence"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "June has arrived. Imagine the geoduck making its way from the ocean to the river. Use whatever makes you think of June to link that month to this scene of the geoduck making his way to the river.",
                "mnemonic": "After extensive study of the {tooltip:Kanji:sequence} and {tooltip:Kanji:order} of water, the geoduck has determined that {tooltip:Reading:June} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3093}) is the best time to travel to the river. June is the best time for the temperature and atmospheric pressure to be just right for such a journey. In June, the geoduck will set out."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You use a {tooltip:Radical:roof} to keep yourself {tooltip:Radical:dry} and safe from {tooltip:Kanji:outer space}. Look outside, above your roof, and you'll see outer space stretching above you.",
            "hints": "You don't want to float up into outer space and get all wet, do you? No? Then you better make sure you have a roof above your head.",
