{
            "mnemonic": "This is a little confusing for someone who didn't grow up with the Japanese language. You have {tooltip:Kanji:fifty} {tooltip:Kanji:sound}s. Then, they're in a certain {tooltip:Kanji:order}. So, these fifty sounds are the Japanese syllabary. That's hiragana / katakana, probably from back in the day when there were more sounds than there are now. So, the \"fifty sounds in order\" makes up {tooltip:Vocabulary:aiueo order}, where the \"aiueo\" is {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3044\u3046\u3048\u304a} representing the five columns.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Aiueo Order",
                "Alternatives": "In Aiueo Order, Syllabary Order",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3054\u3058\u3085\u3046\u304a\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3054\u3058\u3085\u3046\u304a\u3093\u3058\u3085\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
