                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21371-subject-4229.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the two vocab words separately put together, just as you'd expect from a body-part related kanji. So, {span:lang=ja:\u732b} plus {span:lang=ja:\u820c} = {span:lang=ja:\u306d\u3053\u3058\u305f}. Just remember that {span:lang=ja:\u820c} is read here as {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u305f}, and not {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u305f}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u304c\u732b\u820c\u3060\u3063\u3066\u3053\u3068\u3001\u5fd8\u308c\u3066\u306a\u3044\uff1f",
                    "en": "Aren't you forgetting that I have an aversion to hot foods?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3054\u3081\u3093\u306a\u3055\u3044\u3002\u79c1\u3001\u732b\u820c\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm sorry. I can't eat hot things."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u732b\u820c\u306a\u306e\u3067\u3001\u30b9\u30fc\u30d7\u3092\u3075\u3046\u3075\u3046\u3057\u306a\u3044\u3068\u98df\u3079\u3089\u308c\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002\u672c\u5f53\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u5618\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "Koichi doesn\u2019t like hot food, so he can\u2019t eat soup without blowing on it. Is this true or false?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

