{
            "mnemonic": "Remember {span:lang=ja:\u7d30\u3044} and how it means \"thin.\" Well, this is another adjective that comes from the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u7d30} with a similar but different meaning (sorry!). If you think about something that's very thin, though, there isn't much surface area. In order to use this very thin thing (say, to put your favorite model railroad on) you have to zoom way in and get incredibly {tooltip:Vocabulary:detailed} with it. It's super {tooltip:Vocabulary:small} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:fine}, so get your magnifying lens out! You can remember that this one is \"detailed\" or \"fine\" because the {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044} makes you think of {tooltip:Reading:coy}otes. You put a ton of work into this detailed and fine model railroad on a very thin piece of land. Then, a coyote comes in and trashes it all, because you made the mistake of making it out of meat.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Detailed",
                "Alternatives": "Small, Fine, Trivial",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3053\u307e\u304b\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u307e\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30365-subject-4348.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3053\u307e\u304b\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21429-subject-4348.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This word has a different reading from the ones you've learned so far (sorry), so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}After the coyote wrecks your pretty train things he bites you on the head, sending you into an indefinite {tooltip:Reading:coma} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u307e}).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3058\u3083\u3042\u3001\u3053\u306e\u30ad\u30e3\u30d9\u30c4\u3092\u7d30\u304b\u304f\u304d\u3056\u3093\u3067\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Then, finely chop this cabbage please."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7d30\u304b\u3044\u304a\u91d1\u3057\u304b\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "I only have small change."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6728\u3092\u898b\u3066\u68ee\u3092\u898b\u305a\u3001\u3060\u305c\u3002\u7d30\u304b\u3044\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3070\u304b\u308a\u6c17\u3092\u3068\u3089\u308c\u305a\u306b\u3001\u3082\u3063\u3068\u5927\u304d\u3044\u30b9\u30b1\u30fc\u30eb\u3067\u7269\u3092\u8003\u3048\u3066\u304f\u308c\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You can\u2019t see the wood for the trees. Don\u2019t just focus on the details, look at the bigger picture."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

