                        "pronunciation": "\u3084\u3055\u3057\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30364-subject-4208.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Everything is so {tooltip:Vocabulary:easy} for you to do. Why? Because you don't do anything yourself. You ask others. You say things like \"Hey, can you get me some water?\" They say \"{tooltip:Reading:yassah!}\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3084\u3055}) very enthusiastically.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u8089\u3092\u3046\u3059\u304f\u5207\u308b\u306e\u306f\u3042\u307e\u308a\u6613\u3057\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3067\u306f\u3042\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "Slicing meat very thin isn't a simple thing to do."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304d\u3081\u306e\u7d30\u304b\u3044\u808c\u3092\u4fdd\u3064\u306e\u306f\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306b\u3068\u3063\u3066\u306f\u6613\u3057\u3044\u3053\u3068\u3060\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "It was easy for Koichi to maintain his delicate skin."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8a66\u9a13\u306e\u6642\u3001\u6613\u3057\u3044\u554f\u984c\u304b\u3089\u5148\u306b\u89e3\u3044\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3046\u65b9\u304c\u597d\u304d\u306a\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "During exams, I like solving the easy questions first."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you have {tooltip:Kanji:eight} {tooltip:Kanji:books} you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:eight books}. This is an example of how to count books, so if you have eight of them this is what you'd say.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Eight Books",
                "Alternative": "Eight Volumes",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3063\u3055\u3064"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3063\u3055\u3064",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30331-subject-4172.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306f\u3063\u3055\u3064",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21343-subject-4172.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. The {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3061} part gets shortened as it often does when put into situations like this, making it {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3063}. The {span:lang=ja:\u518a} is all normal, and to the \"book(s).\" Har!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5b66\u751f\u306f\u516b\u4eba\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3001\u6559\u79d1\u66f8\u306f\u516b\u518a\u5fc5\u8981\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Because there are eight students, we will need eight textbooks."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304a\u91d1\u304c\u306a\u304f\u3066\u3044\u3059\u304c\u8cb7\u3048\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u672c\u3092\u516b\u518a\u3064\u307f\u4e0a\u3052\u3066\u3044\u3059\u306e\u4ee3\u308f\u308a\u306b\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I have no money and I can't buy a chair, so I use eight books as a chair instead."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c0f\u8aac\u3092\u305f\u3063\u305f\u516b\u518a\u51fa\u7248\u3057\u305f\u304b\u3089\u3063\u3066\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u4e8b\u3092\u5c0f\u8aac\u5bb6\u3060\u306a\u3093\u3066\u547c\u3073\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3088\u3002\u4e94\u5341\u518a\u51fa\u7248\u3059\u308c\u3070\u3001\u3082\u3057\u304b\u3059\u308b\u3068\u305d\u3046\u547c\u3076\u304b\u3082\u3057\u308c\u306a\u3044\u3051\u3069\u306d\u3002",
                    "en": "I won\u2019t call myself a fiction writer after only publishing eight books. If I publish fifty books, then I\u2019ll call myself that."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know how {span:lang=ja:\u975e\u5e38} means {tooltip:Kanji:emergency} and how {span:lang=ja:\u53e3} can be some kind of doorway (like in {span:lang=ja:\u5165\u308a\u53e3}, for example)? Well, if that's the case, then you have an emergency doorway. Usually you run away from emergencies, though, making this an {tooltip:Vocabulary:emergency exit}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Emergency Exit",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3058\u3087\u3046\u3050\u3061"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3072\u3058\u3087\u3046\u3050\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30354-subject-4246.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3072\u3058\u3087\u3046\u3050\u3061",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21088-subject-4246.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is the words {span:lang=ja:\u975e\u5e38} and {span:lang=ja:\u53e3} combined together. The thing that makes this weird is that it's a mix of the kun and on'yomi readings. I guess things get all jostled up when you have yourself an emergency.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u975e\u5e38\u53e3\u306f\u305d\u3053\u306e\u901a\u8def\u3092\u5de6\u306b\u884c\u3063\u305f\u3068\u3053\u308d\u306b\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "You will see the emergency exit when you turn left at that corridor."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u4e0d\u826f\u9ad8\u6821\u751f\u304c\u30af\u30e9\u30b9\u3092\u30b5\u30dc\u3063\u3066\u304f\u3064\u308d\u3050\u5834\u6240\u3068\u8a00\u3048\u3070\u3075\u901a\u306f\u975e\u5e38\u53e3\u306e\u304b\u3044\u3060\u3093\u306e\u4e0b\u3067\u3059\u3088\u306d\uff1f",
                    "en": "When you think of a place where bad high schoolers skip class and hang out, it would be under the emergency exit staircase, right?"
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30fc\u30c8\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u30a2\u30e4\u304c\u63cf\u3044\u305f\u7d75\u3092\u96a0\u3059\u3068\u3001\u6ce5\u68d2\u306f\u975e\u5e38\u53e3\u304b\u3089\u3053\u3063\u305d\u308a\u3068\u629c\u3051\u51fa\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "After putting Aya\u2019s drawing under his coat, the thief slipped out through the emergency exit."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
