{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the word are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Flute",
                "Alternative": "Whistle",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3048"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3075\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30163-subject-4358.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3075\u3048",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21434-subject-4358.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: Pretend you're trying to {tooltip:Kanji:whistle}, but you can't. All that comes out is air. You make a \"{tooltip:Reading:Fuuuuuuueh}\" sound over and over, because you can't get the whole whistling thing down. Go ahead and pretend to do that (or do it for real).\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u7b1b\u306b\u306f\u3001\u30c4\u30bf\u304c\u7d61\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The flute was entangled in the vines."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u306f\u3068\u7b1b\u3001\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u304c\u304a\u307e\u3064\u308a\u3067\u8cb7\u3063\u3066\u304f\u308c\u305f\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "My mom bought this dove flute for me at a festival."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u306e\u7b1b\u3092\u6301\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u7537\u306e\u4eba\u304c\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3055\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "That guy holding the whistle is Mr. Koichi."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have {tooltip:Kanji:two} {tooltip:Kanji:flat objects} that make up your {tooltip:Kanji:tongue}. What kind of tongue is made up of two of anything? That's a tongue that's split, that's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:forked tongue}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Forked Tongue",
                "Alternative": "Duplicity",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u306b\u307e\u3044\u3058\u305f"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u307e\u3044\u3058\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20989-subject-4141.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u306b\u307e\u3044\u3058\u305f",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30347-subject-4141.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. That's the case for the first two kanji, but {span:lang=ja:\u820c} actually uses the kun'yomi. Not only that, it's read here as {span:lang=ja:\u3058\u305f}, and not {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u305f}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u653f\u6cbb\u5bb6\u9054\u306e\u4e8c\u679a\u820c\u306e\u653f\u3055\u304f\u306b\u306f\u3082\u3046\u3046\u3093\u3056\u308a\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm totally fed up with politicians' duplicitous policies."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3044\u3064\u306f\u4e8c\u679a\u820c\u3060\u304b\u3089\u6c17\u3092\u3064\u3051\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "He has a forked tongue, so you should be careful."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u25cb\u00d7\u30af\u30a4\u30ba: \u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306f\u7b49\u8eab\u5927\u306e\u521d\u97f3\u30df\u30af\u4eba\u5f62\u3092\u8cb7\u3046\u304a\u91d1\u3092\u5132\u3051\u308b\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u4e8c\u679a\u820c\u3092\u4f7f\u3063\u3066\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3092\u9a19\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\u25cb\u304b\u00d7\u304b\uff1f",
                    "en": "True or False Quiz: In order to get the money for a life-sized Hatsune Miku doll, Viet used his forked tongue to cheat Koichi. True or false?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This one's a little weird. You have a {tooltip:Kanji:group} of {tooltip:Kanji:cloth}. Think about this. If you group together a bunch of cloth into one big cloth, you have something nice and soft. What can you use this nice and soft cloth things for? Well, you can sleep on it. This is the Japanese word {tooltip:Vocabulary:futon}, which you may have heard in English before (though the Japanese futon is quite different from the American one). You can also translate this to {tooltip:Vocabulary:bedding} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:sleeping mat} too.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Futon",
                "Alternatives": "Bedding, Sleeping Mat",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3068\u3093"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3075\u3068\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20943-subject-4193.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3075\u3068\u3093",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30198-subject-4193.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. The reading for {span:lang=ja:\u56e3} is the secondary reading that went with the kanji, though, so watch out for that. If you can figure out the meaning of this word, chances are you already know how to spell it, so carry that over to Japanese.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u306e\u5e03\u56e3\u306e\u54c1\u3057\u3064\u306b\u306f\u3001\u3044\u304f\u3089\u304b\u6539\u5584\u304c\u898b\u3089\u308c\u308b\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "I think I can see some improvements in the quality of this bedding."
                },
                {
