                        "file": "21077-subject-4238.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u81ea\u52d5\u8a5e\u300c\u9032\u3080\u300d\u306e\u53ef\u80fd\u5f62\u306f\u3001\u300c\u9032\u3081\u308b\u300d\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The potential form of the intransitive verb \"to advance\" is \"something advances.\""
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u304c\u5927\u306e\u82e6\u624b\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306e\u4e00\u3064\u306b\u3001\u4ed6\u52d5\u8a5e\u3068\u81ea\u52d5\u8a5e\u306e\u4f7f\u3044\u5206\u3051\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "One of the things I really dread is using transitive and intransitive verbs properly."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u53d7\u52d5\u614b\u306b\u3067\u304d\u308b\u304b\u3069\u3046\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u3067\u5224\u65ad\u3059\u308b\u3068\u3001\u81ea\u52d5\u8a5e\u3068\u4ed6\u52d5\u8a5e\u304c\u7c21\u5358\u306b\u898b\u5206\u3051\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You can easily judge if it's an intransitive verb or a transitive verb when you think about whether or not you can change it to the passive form."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:add} and you {tooltip:Kanji:subtract}. This brings you back to zero. There was absolutely no point in doing those actions. Completely {tooltip:Vocabulary:pointless}. In fact, I'd say that was downright {tooltip:Vocabulary:irresponsible} of you. The extra {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3044} is there to mean \"good,\" as in \"good, you've figured out how pointless that was, now stop.\"",
