                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. The {span:lang=ja:\u8aac} gets shortened to {span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3063}.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3053\u308c\u4ee5\u4e0a\u8aac\u5f97\u306e\u3088\u5730\u306f\u7121\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "There is no room for persuasion anymore."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u3092\u8aac\u5f97\u3059\u308b\u306e\u306f\u5ca9\u3092\u624b\u3067\u308f\u308b\u306e\u3088\u308a\u3082\u3080\u305a\u304b\u3057\u3044\u3068\u8a00\u308f\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "They say it would be harder to persuade Koichi of something than it would be to break a rock with your hand."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306b\u4f4f\u3080\u305f\u3081\u306b\u3001\u307e\u305a\u6700\u521d\u306b\u81ea\u5206\u306e\u89aa\u3092\u8aac\u5f97\u3057\u306a\u304f\u3066\u306f\u3044\u3051\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "In order to live in Japan, the first thing I have to do is convince my parents to let me do it."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a food pretty specific to Japan, making it a slightly weird one to learn. You have a {tooltip:Kanji:Japanese Plum}. Then you have {tooltip:Kanji:dry}. So when the Japanese plum is dried, it's not a dried plum (that would be too easy), it is a {tooltip:Vocabulary:pickled plum} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:pickled ume}. If you know the name of this food, you can call it by that too: {tooltip:Vocabulary:umeboshi}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pickled Plums",
                "Alternatives": "Pickled Ume, Umeboshi",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3081\u307c\u3057"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3081\u307c\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30268-subject-4214.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3046\u3081\u307c\u3057",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21035-subject-4214.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this one, like the meaning, is kind of strange. It's the kun'yomi readings, so apologies in advance for that. You have {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3081} plus {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3057}, which comes from {span:lang=ja:\u5e72\u3059} though the {span:lang=ja:\u3057} is stuffed inside the {span:lang=ja:\u5e72} for some reason. It's also rendaku'd. Basically, everything is all screwed up, so you know, deal with it. This food is awesome, and common, so you have to learn it. I guess the pickling process has mangled the reading of this word. At least it tastes good.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6885\u5e72\u306f\u4e57\u308a\u7269\u3088\u3044\u306b\u304d\u304f\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "Umeboshi is good for motion sickness."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6885\u5e72\u306f\u4f55\u306b\u6df7\u305c\u3066\u98df\u3079\u3066\u3082\u7f8e\u5473\u3057\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Umeboshi can be mixed with anything."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3059\u307f\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3001 \u524d\u3092\u901a\u3089\u305b\u3066\u3082\u3089\u3063\u3066\u3082\u3088\u308d\u3057\u3044\u3067\u3057\u3087\u3046\u304b\u3002\u3042\u306e\u6885\u5e72\u3057\u304c\u5165\u3063\u305f\u5c0f\u74f6\u3092\u8cb7\u3044\u305f\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3002",
                    "en": "Excuse me. May I get through? I\u2019d like to buy that jar of pickled plums."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
