                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30329-subject-4225.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: The entanglement mess you're fixing is a couple of kids that got their hair tangled up. They were doing some sparring in their {span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3089\u3066} class and one thing led to the other and suddenly both their hair was entangled together.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u3063\u3071\u3089\u3063\u3066\u7d61\u3093\u3067\u304f\u308b\u3084\u3064\u304c\u5927\u304d\u3089\u3044\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I hate people who get drunk and then pick fights."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u307f\u306b\u30dc\u30bf\u30f3\u304c\u7d61\u3093\u3058\u3083\u3063\u3066\u53d6\u308c\u306a\u3044\u306e\u3002",
                    "en": "My hair got tangled around the button and I can't get it out."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6700\u60aa\uff01\u30cd\u30c1\u30e3\u30cd\u30c1\u30e3\u306e\u98a8\u8239\u30ac\u30e0\u304c\u91e3\u308a\u7cf8\u306b\u7d61\u3093\u3058\u3083\u3063\u305f\uff01\u3069\u3046\u3084\u3063\u3066\u53d6\u308c\u3070\u3044\u3044\u3093\u3060\u308d\u3046\u3002",
                    "en": "Oh no! Sticky bubblegum got tangled around my fishing line! How can I get it out?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji means {tooltip:Kanji:riot}, but this verb version word doesn't really mean \"to riot.\" It's more like {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be in disorder}. But if you think about it, when things are rioting and crazy, they definitely are in disorder, so you can think of it that way. You can differentiate this from the future word {span:lang=ja:\u4e71\u3059} because with {span:lang=ja:\u308c\u308b} you know it is {tooltip:Reading:rare} for it to be like this. You aren't doing it, but it just happens on occasion (rarely) so you take advantage of it.",
