                        "file": "43721-subject-8944.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word has okurigana (hiragana attached to the kanji) you know that it's probably going to be the kun'yomi reading, which you didn't learn with the kanji. Here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}We all want {tooltip:Vocabulary:to change something}. Probably {tooltip:Reading:a lotta} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3089\u305f}) things! Think about all the things you want to change. Your name? Your habits? Your plans? The rules? The government? I bet you can think of a lotta things you want to change.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u3092\u6539\u3081\u308b\u3053\u3068\u306b\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "We decided to change the date."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u306e\u8003\u3048\u65b9\u306f\u6539\u3081\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "You should correct that way of thinking."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8a71\u3057\u5408\u3063\u305f\u901a\u308a\u306b\u8a08\u753b\u3092\u4e00\u90e8\u6539\u3081\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Just as we discussed, we revised a part of the plan."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

