                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: What are you going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to take along}? Whoa. That much? Why in the world do you have {tooltip:Reading:two} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064}) of everything?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u5973\u3092\u9023\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
