                        "file": "21021-subject-4190.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u308f\u304b\u3081",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30315-subject-4190.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}{span:lang=ja:\u82e5\u3044} uses the same reading you learned with the kanji, but the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u5e03} is totally irregular. If you can figure out the meaning, you can use that to remember the reading (since they're the same), but here's a mnemonic to help you just in case:\n{splitParent}You're eating {tooltip:Vocabulary:wakame} and you suddenly spot a {tooltip:Reading:\u76ee} ({span:lang=ja:\u3081}) looking up at you. You didn't know seaweed had eyes!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u304b\u3093\u56fd\u3067\u306f\u305f\u3093\u751f\u65e5\u306b\u306f\u82e5\u5e03\u30b9\u30fc\u30d7\u3092\u98f2\u3080\u7fd2\u304b\u3093\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "In Korea, it's customary to have wakame soup on your birthday."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5fd9\u3057\u3044\u306e\u3067\u3001\u304b\u3093\u5358\u306b\u82e5\u5e03\u3068\u304d\u3085\u3046\u308a\u306e\u548c\u3048\u7269\u3092\u4f5c\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I'm busy so I simply made dressed wakame and cucumber."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u304a\u6bcd\u3055\u3093\u304c\u3001\u82e5\u5e03\u3068\u8c46\u8150\u306e\u304a\u5473\u564c\u6c41\u3092\u4f5c\u3063\u305f\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3001\u98df\u3079\u308b\uff1f",
                    "en": "My mom made a miso soup with wakame seaweed and tofu. Do you want some?"
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

