                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30725-subject-7763.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You haven't learned this reading for {span:lang=ja:\u60aa} yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}When you feel {tooltip:Vocabulary:disgust} for someone all you can manage to say when you see them is, \"{tooltip:Reading:Oh}... ({span:lang=ja:\u304a}), it's you.\" Feel the anger when you see their face, \"Oh, you again. Bleh.\"\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30af\u30ea\u30b9\u30c6\u30f3\u306f\u30af\u30a4\u30f3\u30fb\u30d9\u30ea\u30eb\u3092\u5acc\u60aa\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "Kristen hates Queen Beryl."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u5acc\u60aa\u306e\u76ee\u3067\u79c1\u3092\u306b\u3089\u3093\u3067\u304d\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi glared at me with a look of disgust in his eyes."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3042\u3044\u3064\u306e\u9854\u3092\u898b\u308b\u3060\u3051\u3067\u3001\u5acc\u60aa\u3092\u50ac\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "Just seeing his face makes me seethe with hatred."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You know the word {span:lang=ja:\u76bf} (plate) and the word {span:lang=ja:\u6d17\u3046} (to wash), right? You can probably guess dish washing is happening here, but this is a noun, so it's the idea of {tooltip:Vocabulary:dishwashing}, AKA {tooltip:Vocabulary:doing dishes}, or {tooltip:Vocabulary:washing dishes}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dishwashing",
                "Alternatives": "Doing Dishes, Washing Dishes",
