                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Notice that {span:lang=ja:\u5730} is read as {span:lang=ja:\u3058} instead of {span:lang=ja:\u3061}. You've seen this happen a few times before, so just try to remember that this is the case here.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65b0\u805e\u306f\u3001\u653f\u5e9c\u306e\u5730\u9707\u5bfe\u3055\u304f\u3092\u306f\u3052\u3057\u304f\u975e\u96e3\u3057\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The press severely criticized the government's earthquake preparedness."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u3075\u3060\u3093\u5730\u9707\u306e\u306a\u3044\u6240\u3067\u3054\u304f\u305f\u307e\u306b\u5730\u9707\u304c\u8d77\u304d\u308b\u3068\u8b66\u5bdf\u306b\u96fb\u8a71\u3057\u3066\u304f\u308b\u4eba\u304c\u51fa\u308b\u3002",
                    "en": "When an earthquake occurs in a place where they rarely have them, some people call the police."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u6628\u591c\u306e\u5730\u9707\u306b\u3064\u3044\u3066\u8a71\u3057\u305f\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002\u300d\u300c\u305c\u3072\u805e\u304d\u305f\u3044\u304b\u3089\u8a71\u3057\u3066\u3088\u3002\u300d",
                    "en": "\"I want to talk to you about the earthquake last night.\" \"I\u2019ll totally listen to what you have to say.\""
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "An {tooltip:Kanji:earthquake} {tooltip:Kanji:disaster} is just that, an {tooltip:Vocabulary:earthquake disaster}. These are no good.",
