                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u3067\u306f1950~1960\u5e74\u4ee3\u306b\u304b\u3051\u3066\u3001\u516c\u5bb3\u304c\u5927\u304d\u306a\u793e\u4f1a\u554f\u984c\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "In Japan, pollution became a huge societal problem between 1950 and 1960."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u9054\u306f\u307f\u3093\u306a\u3001\u516c\u5bb3\u306e\u52a0\u5bb3\u8005\u3067\u3059\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "We are all responsible for the pollution problems."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u606f\u5b50\u306f\u3001\u516c\u5bb3\u306b\u3088\u308b\u547c\u5438\u5668\u75be\u60a3\u306b\u82e6\u3057\u3093\u3067\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "My son is suffering from a pollution-triggered respiratory illness."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:One} {tooltip:Kanji:husband}, {tooltip:Kanji:many} {tooltip:Kanji:wives}. Sounds a bit sketchy. This is {tooltip:Vocabulary:polygamy}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Polygamy",
                "Alternative": "Polygyny",
                "Word Type": "noun, \u306e adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3063\u3077\u305f\u3055\u3044"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
                    {
                        "gender": "male",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3063\u3077\u305f\u3055\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "20997-subject-4282.ogg"
                    },
                    {
                        "gender": "female",
                        "pronunciation": "\u3044\u3063\u3077\u305f\u3055\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "30711-subject-4282.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word, which usually means on'yomi readings from the kanji. If you know the readings of your kanji you'll know how to read this as well. Just note that the {span:lang=ja:\u4e00} gets changed to {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3063} and the {span:lang=ja:\u592b} gets changed to {span:lang=ja:\u3077} from {span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3046} for some reason. You can imagine that this is because when you are the type that has many wives, you're probably the type who makes them clean up your {tooltip:Reading:poo} for you as well.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u3082\u304b\u3064\u3066\u306f\u4e00\u592b\u591a\u59bb\u304c\u307f\u3068\u3081\u3089\u308c\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Japan used to approve of polygamy too."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u300c\u4e00\u592b\u591a\u59bb\u305b\u3044\u3068\u304b\u3001\u3042\u308a\u3048\u306a\u3044\u3088\u306a\u300d\u3068\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u304c\u975e\u96e3\u3059\u308b\u3088\u3046\u306b\u8a00\u3046\u3068\u3001\u300c\u305d\u306e\u975e\u96e3\u3001\u81ea\u5206\u306b\u5411\u3051\u305f\u65b9\u304c\u3044\u3044\u3093\u3058\u3083\u306d\u3047\u304b\uff1f\u300d\u3068\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u304c\u7b11\u3063\u3066\u8a00\u3044\u8fd4\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "\"I can't believe polygamy exists,\" Viet said accusingly. \"You can turn that finger around,\u201d Koichi retorted with a smile."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u5168\u3066\u306e\u7537\u6027\u304c\u4e00\u592b\u591a\u59bb\u5236\u3092\u652f\u6301\u3059\u308b\u8a33\u3058\u3083\u306a\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "It\u2019s not like all men support polygamy."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:possible} ({span:lang=ja:\u53ef\u80fd}) {tooltip:Kanji:gender} is one of two things. This means there's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:possibility} you'll either be a boy or a girl. Or maybe something else! Who knows?! ",
