                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21415-subject-4320.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it should use the kun'yomi reading. When learning the kanji, you didn't learn that reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you with this word: When you come to confess your {tooltip:Vocabulary:sin} to me, you start claiming it wasn't you. You say it was some other version of you! What? How could this be? Well, you say \"there are {tooltip:Reading:two me}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u307f}) out there!\" One is doing the bad stuff, and the other is you, and you haven't done any sins!\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30de\u30df\u304c\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306e\u30d9\u30fc\u30b3\u30f3\u3092\u98df\u3079\u305f\u7f6a\u306f\u601d\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u4ee5\u4e0a\u306b\u91cd\u3044\u3002",
                    "en": "Mami's crime of eating Koichi's bacon is more serious than she thinks."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u79c1\u306e\u4f1a\u793e\u306e\u793e\u9577\u306f\u4f1a\u8a08\u3055\u304e\u306e\u7f6a\u3067\u6709\u7f6a\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "My company president has been found guilty of accounting fraud crimes."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u7f6a\u306a\u304d\u4e00\u822c\u5e02\u6c11\u3092\u6bba\u5bb3\u3057\u305f\u4eba\u306f\u96c7\u308f\u306a\u3044\u3068\u601d\u3046\u3088\u3002",
                    "en": "I don\u2019t think Koichi would hire anyone who has committed the crime of murdering innocent civilians."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": [
                {
                    "en": "to commit a crime",
                    "ja": "\u7f6a\u3092\u72af\u3059",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "sense of guilt",
                    "ja": "\u7f6a\u306e\u610f\u8b58",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "to admit guilt",
                    "ja": "\u7f6a\u3092\u8a8d\u3081\u308b",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                },
                {
                    "en": "to forgive a sin",
                    "ja": "\u7f6a\u3092\u8a31\u3059",
                    "partOfSpeech": "independent noun"
                }
            ]
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a single kanji with an {span:lang=ja:\u3044} on the end, meaning you know it's probably an adjective. What's the adjective form of {tooltip:Kanji:smoke}? It's {tooltip:Vocabulary:smoky}.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Smoky",
                "Word Type": "\u3044 adjective"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3080\u3044"
