                        "pronunciation": "\u3051\u3080\u3044",
                        "voiceActorId": 2,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21406-subject-4303.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You sort of did learn this reading with the vocabulary word {span:lang=ja:\u7159}, but this one is just different enough where we thought we should make a mnemonic for this one: \n{splitParent}All this {tooltip:Vocabulary:smoki}ness is from a terrible {tooltip:Reading:chem}ical ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3080}) spill that happened nearby. It was acid, so it burned everything up real good, causing the air to get pretty smoky.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u5c71\u706b\u4e8b\u306e\u305b\u3044\u3067\u753a\u4e2d\u304c\u7159\u304f\u306a\u3063\u3066\u3044\u308b\u3093\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The entire town is smoky now due to the wildfire."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u82b1\u706b\u304c\u7159\u304f\u3066\u3001\u3080\u305b\u3066\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The smoky fireworks made me cough."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u7159\u3044\u306a\u3042\uff01\u4e00\u4f53\u3044\u3064\u306b\u306a\u3063\u305f\u3089\u7159\u8349\u3084\u3081\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3088\uff1f\u672c\u5f53\u306b\u81ed\u3044\u3093\u3060\u3051\u3069\u3002",
                    "en": "It\u2019s so smoky! When the heck are you going to quit smoking? This really smells awful."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

