                        "voiceActorName": "Kenichi",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "21364-subject-4204.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You probably learned this reading with this verb's transitive other half {span:lang=ja:\u6539\u3081\u308b}, but here's a mnemonic anyway just in case: \n{splitParent}{tooltip:Vocabulary:To be renewed} you decide to go to a spa. You get in a bathtub and they pour in {tooltip:Reading:a lotta} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3089\u305f}) leeches and eels to help you to be renewed. Feel the fear. There are a lot of them! Alternatively, you can imagine them pouring in a lotta Maru cats, because that's way fuzzier.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u65e5\u672c\u306e\u5e74\u53f7\u304c\u3001\u8c46\u6cb3\u8c5a\u306b\u6539\u307e\u308a\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "The Japanese era name was altered to Tofugu."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u30d3\u30a8\u30c8\u306e\u751f\u6d3b\u305f\u3044\u5ea6\u304c\u6539\u307e\u3063\u3066\u3001\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u306f\u3068\u3066\u3082\u3088\u308d\u3053\u3073\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Koichi was very happy to see that Viet had reformed himself from his evil way of life."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u305d\u3046\u6539\u307e\u308b\u306a\u3088\u3002\u30b3\u30a6\u30a4\u30c1\u5927\u7d71\u9818\u306f\u3001\u3068\u3066\u3082\u6c17\u3055\u304f\u306a\u3093\u3060\u304b\u3089\u3002",
                    "en": "Don\u2019t be so formal! President Koichi is very friendly."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This word consists of kanji with hiragana attached. Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:crime} and the verb vocab version can mean {tooltip:Vocabulary:to commit a crime}, {tooltip:Vocabulary:to make a mistake}, or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to rape}, depending on the context.",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Commit A Crime",
