                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: If you're not doing the mixing, in order for things {tooltip:Vocabulary:to get mixed} you call your {tooltip:Reading:ma} ({span:lang=ja:\u307e}) up and ask her to mix it. What a terrible lazy child you are.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c34\u3068\u6cb9\u306f\u6df7\u3056\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\u3002",
                    "en": "Oil doesn't mix with water."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u8272\u304c\u6df7\u3056\u3063\u3066\u306b\u3058\u3093\u3067\u3057\u307e\u3044\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "Those colors mixed."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u307f\u3093\u306a\u306e\u4f1a\u8a71\u306b\u6df7\u3056\u308b\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3067\u304d\u306a\u304f\u3066\u3068\u3066\u3082\u60b2\u3057\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3057\u3001\u5bc2\u3057\u304b\u3063\u305f\u3088\u3002",
