{
            "mnemonic": "If you use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to point when you {tooltip:Radical:compare} things you're really just throwing around {tooltip:Kanji:criticism}. You should never need to point fingers when you're just comparing things. If you're pointing and picking and being mean, that's criticism.",
            "hints": "Some criticism is okay, as long as it's constructive and it helps the person get better. But when you start pointing fingers, it's time to step back and try to not be such a jerk.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Criticism"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Before you throw criticism around, imagine that embarrassed heat. You don't want to feel that way, so why would you do it to someone else? ",
                "mnemonic": "If you're having trouble not giving out {tooltip:Kanji:criticism}, just think about how you would react if someone criticized you. You'd feel an embarrassed {tooltip:Reading:he}at ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}) rise throughout your body. That heat will cover your whole face."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:lion} harvesting {tooltip:Radical:rice} uses an {tooltip:Radical:axe} to {tooltip:Kanji:cut off} the tops of the stalks. The lion is roaming the rice fields using his axe to harvest the rice. He does so by cutting off the part of the rice stalks he needs.",
            "hints": "Picture this lion on his hind legs, walking through a rice field. He\u2019s holding an axe in one hand and acting like a human. See him cut off the plants and hear the whoosh of the axe as he cuts.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cut Off"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
