                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "When dawn comes in Africa (it's a lion, so that's where he is) it gets too hot to be in the sun, so the lion gets cut off from his job of cutting things off.",
                "mnemonic": "The lion will {tooltip:Kanji:cut off} rice stalks until {tooltip:Reading:dawn} ({span:lang=ja:\u3060\u3093}). But at the first light of dawn, it will run and hide in the shade of the trees, cut off from the rice."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Both a {tooltip:Radical:leader} and a {tooltip:Radical:king} have a {tooltip:Kanji:duty} to protect their people. A good leader always protects his followers, and a good king always protects his subjects. This is their duty.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself being protected by your king and leader. They don\u2019t really like you, but it is their duty to protect you. See them fighting off evil doers and taking bullets for your sake.",
            "meanings": {
