                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine grabbing hold of the element that holds all life together and trying to wash it with soap. It's slippery so you keep dropping it and soap keeps going in your eyes.",
                "mnemonic": "You need to keep this {tooltip:Kanji:element} clean, so you make sure to wash it with {tooltip:Reading:so}ap ({span:lang=ja:\u305d}) every single day. This turns out to be pretty hard because the element is an invisible thread, but you do your best."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Seeing a {tooltip:Radical:mohawk} in the {tooltip:Radical:winter} means the {tooltip:Kanji:enemy} is nearby. You are from the dreadlock tribe and the mohawk tribe is your enemy. You\u2019re deep in the heart of battle and winter has fallen. Now is the time to take out the enemy.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself holed up in a winter encampment, waiting to strike at the mohawk wearing enemies. Feel the cold around you as you scan the horizon for mohawks.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Enemy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
