                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Establish weapons in sets or the people who use them won't be able to match each other.",
                "mnemonic": "Weapons have to be {tooltip:Kanji:establish}ed in {tooltip:Reading:sets} ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3064}). So you have to make another one that goes with it. Make them cohesive please."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You should {tooltip:Radical:say} \"{tooltip:Radical:peace}\" before you {tooltip:Kanji:evaluate} a situation. That way everyone will know where you\u2019re coming from. If you\u2019re honest and say \"peace\" before you evaluate a situation out loud, everyone will know where you stand.",
            "hints": "What situation would you like to evaluate? Be sure to say \"peace\" before doing so. Imagine yourself doing this out loud and think of what you would say.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Evaluate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself trying to explain a situation you\u2019re about to evaluate and your audience keeps shouting \u201cHeyo!\u201d every other sentence. Imagine how frustrating that would be. Get angry at your rude audience and how much they shout \u201cHeyo.\u201d",
                "mnemonic": "When you say \"peace,\" you end up making a really bad pun and you hear somebody say \u201c{tooltip:Reading:Heyo}!\u201d ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3087\u3046}) You look at the people around you and try to {tooltip:Kanji:evaluate} who said heyo, but you can\u2019t tell. You start talking again when somebody exclaims \u201cThat\u2019s what she said\u201d and another person shouts \u201cHeyo!\u201d once again, but you still can\u2019t evaluate who\u2019s saying these things."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:tree} with a {tooltip:Radical:squid} on it, so you get closer to {tooltip:Kanji:examine} it.",
            "hints": "As you examine the tree and the squid in it, you think, \"Huh, nope still weird.\" You should examine it further to find out what's going on.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Examine"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
