                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Zombie hands keep coming out of the ground, but as long as you wear the mask and increase the dirt on top of them, they won't be able to escape their earthly prison.",
                "mnemonic": "Use the dirt mask to {tooltip:Kanji:increase} the dirt around you. The {tooltip:Radical:zo}mbies ({span:lang=ja:\u305e\u3046}) are trying to escape, so you just keep increasing the dirt on top of them so they can't get out."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tree} is growing out of a {tooltip:Radical:top hat} you need to {tooltip:Kanji:inspect} it to find out why and how this happened. You should probably {tooltip:Kanji:investigate} the area too. I mean, how could a tree grow out of a top hat anyway? Seems suspicious.",
            "hints": "Inspect the tree. Inspect the top hat. Did you find anything?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Inspect",
                "Alternatives": "Investigate, Inspection, Investigation"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine stopping to inspect the tree after each minute of sawing. You'll find out why it's growing out of a top hat! Eventually!",
                "mnemonic": "In the middle of your {tooltip:Kanji:inspection} you realize you need to {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}) the tree open to come to a good conclusion. This seems a bit unnecessary, but no! No! For the sake of this {tooltip:Kanji:investigation} you must saw the tree in half!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "\"I'll cut that baby in {tooltip:Radical:half} with a {tooltip:Radical:knife} if you don't figure out custody,\" says the {tooltip:Kanji:judge}. Ah, the oldest judge trick in the book.",
            "hints": "Since you two can't make a decision on who gets custody of the baby, the judge now has to step in and judge for you. Will you figure it out for yourself, or let the baby get cut in half? What an effective judge.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Judge"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Han Solo the judge isn't a bad person... but he isn't so good either. He'll cut that baby in half if you don't figure things out. That's the kind of judge Han Solo is.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:judge} is {tooltip:Reading:Han} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}) Solo, so you know he's not going to back down."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're about to enter a {tooltip:Radical:roof} that has your {tooltip:Radical:number} on it so you can face the {tooltip:Kanji:judge}. You've been sitting here for what feels like hours, waiting for your number to come up. Finally the time has come\u2014the judge will see you now.",
            "hints": "Picture the judge sitting under the roof. Your number is sitting on his big desk, next to the gavel.",
