                        "reading": "\u304d\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your cyborg has been really great lately. Your wife loves it. It saved the world. It's nice of you to take this occasion to show the cyborg how much it means to you all with a festival.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:occasion} this time is to celebrate your wonderful {tooltip:Reading:cy}borg ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044}). It's about time you did something nice for it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:hat} comes to a {tooltip:Radical:stop}, thinking of a {tooltip:Kanji:plan}. The hat had been pacing around for a while, trying to think of how to get off the head he's resting upon and back into the house where it's nice and cozy, and came to the sudden realization of a plan. This caused the hat to stop.",
            "hints": "Imagine a hat walking about on your head, pacing back and forth deep in thought. See the hat stroke its chin in contemplation as it tries to think up a plan to get off your noggin and back inside.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Plan"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u308f\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as the hat begins to grin. This plan is so simple it\u2019s sure to work. Now watch as the hat obtains the key and enters the locked door. What sort of mischief will the hat get into once inside?",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:plan} that made this hat stop right in its tracks was very simple. First, obtain the {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) to the house. Then, use the key to get in the front door. How simple!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If there\u2019s {tooltip:Radical:grass} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} and {tooltip:Radical:fins} in your {tooltip:Radical:hand}, you need to {tooltip:Kanji:raise} that hand up to the sky. You\u2019re in the middle of a fisherman\u2019s ritual, which can only be performed on grassy ground. You take fish fins from the previous year, and raise them up to the sky in order to ensure a good fishing harvest.",
            "hints": "Feel the grass in your toes and the fins in your hand as you raise them up to the sky. See the sun glistening off the fins as you raise them up in the air.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Raise"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself going through the same process as before, only this time imagine yourself in Little Kyoto. Little Kyoto is really little, so make sure you're in the right spot.",
                "mnemonic": "This ritual only works in one part of the world however. It absolutely must be performed in Little {tooltip:Reading:Kyo}to ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087}). The way Little Kyoto lines up with the sun and the sky and all that astrological junk makes it the best place for you to {tooltip:Kanji:raise} fish fins up in the air."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What people {tooltip:Radical:say} to you will be carved by a {tooltip:Radical:blade} into your {tooltip:Radical:heart}, and the next time you see them, you'll immediately {tooltip:Kanji:recognize} them.",
            "hints": "Sometimes your brain won't recognize someone, but your heart will. That's because what they say draws that blade across your heart and leaves a mark, for better or for worse, forever.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Recognize"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "There's just something about Nintendo\u2014you'd recognize them and their games anywhere.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:recognize} places, names, and even games this way. But the thing that has the most real estate on your heart, the thing you recognize the most, is {tooltip:Reading:Nin}tendo ({span:lang=ja:\u306b\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:next} {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} will be yours, but this shellfish will be mine. These are the {tooltip:Kanji:resources} we have to share and distribute.",
            "hints": "Our resources are based around a system of trading shellfish. It's not that weird, plenty of ancient societies used shellfish as their main resource!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Resources"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Of course you're going to use your resources to get a sheep. You're living in a time when shellfish are used to trade for goods and services!",
                "mnemonic": "You save up all of your {tooltip:Kanji:resources} so you can buy a {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}). You bring a big sack of your shellfish resources to the market and finally get to pick out that sheep you've had your eyes on for months."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The kanji and the radical are exactly the same. That means they share meanings as well.",
            "hints": "If you know the radical, you will know the kanji as well!",
