{
            "mnemonic": "Remember how {span:lang=ja:\u81ea\u52d5\u8a5e} was \"intransitive verb\"? Intransitive verbs are when something just happens. You aren't doing the action to them. This word, however, is the other kind. A {tooltip:Vocabulary:transitive verb} is when you are directly doing something to something else. That's why it has {tooltip:Kanji:other} in there, because it's a {tooltip:Kanji:verb} ({span:lang=ja:\u52d5\u8a5e}) you do to an{tooltip:Kanji:other} thing, directly.",
