                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Some of the Vikings managed to fill their bathtubs with acorns and are trying to rub themselves clean with them instead of water...",
                "mnemonic": "The poor Viking trying to {tooltip:Kanji:manage} all the others keeps having to confiscate {tooltip:Reading:a}corns ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3044}). \"You can't take baths in acorns and wood, it has to be water!\" he shouts."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Can you look at the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} and know which {tooltip:Radical:direction} you need to go? Then you might be a {tooltip:Kanji:monk}. Monks have amazing skills like that. And I'm sure you've seen monks wandering around in lots of media. They don't need maps or smartphones. They just look at the dirt and let the earth guide them to where they need to be.",
            "hints": "Picture a monk walking through a large field in the middle of nowhere. He knows where to go, he's not afraid. The dirt will lead him in the right direction.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Monk"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a monk bowling in the middle of the road. Imagine your shock at how well he handles the ball. Also, imagine how heavy it must be for a monk to carry a bowling ball everywhere!",
                "mnemonic": "You want to know the {tooltip:Kanji:monk}'s trick so you hide behind him for a while as he walks. Finally the monk stops, looks around, takes out a {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) ball and starts bowling in the dirt. The bowling ball rolls off, the monk follows it, and then heads off in that direction."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you try to {tooltip:Radical:say} things with a {tooltip:Radical:knife}, the police will put you in a {tooltip:Radical:net} as your {tooltip:Kanji:penalty} for breaking the knife laws. You can't just go up to other people and say things with a knife out.",
            "hints": "Imagine getting so mad that you use a knife instead of words to say what you're trying to say. A net falls over you and pulls you down. The knife goes flying. This is your penalty for acting like a crazy person.",
