                ],
                "hints": "You can inhale a cucumber too, I suppose, but don't tell anyone I told you to.",
                "mnemonic": "Use this mouth ability to {tooltip:Kanji:suck} {tooltip:Reading:cu}cumbers ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3085\u3046}) into your mouth. Cucumbers are shaped like cylinders so you can suck them into your mouth like this. Just as nature intended."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "While riding on your {tooltip:Radical:scooter}, you grow a {tooltip:Radical:mustache} on top of the {tooltip:Radical:mustache} you already have in order to {tooltip:Kanji:surpass} the people around you. You're in a scooter race and your mustache is the only thing keeping you in the lead, but someone else has a mustache too! So you grow another mustache to surpass them once again!",
            "hints": "Picture yourself running on a scooter with a bunch of other people and closing your eyes tight, willing another mustache to sprout out of your face to surpass them all.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Surpass"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059, \u3042\u3084\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch helplessly as the car surpasses every single one of your scooters. Both of your mustaches droop in shame.",
                "mnemonic": "Suddenly, something else manages to {tooltip:Kanji:surpass} you all. It's a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b})! A car with two mustaches is also riding on a scooter and going way faster than you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Taking {tooltip:Radical:orders} from a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} will place you into enemy {tooltip:Kanji:territory}. Geoducks make terrible commanders, so if you take orders from one, expect to end up in unknown territory, potentially even enemy territory. Be prepared.",
            "hints": "Imagine this geoduck shouting orders at you to march into enemy territory. See its gross body as a mouth forms and starts shouting out orders.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Territory"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel yourself in the row boat as you imagine rowing away to safe territory. Hear the geoduck in the background shouting at you from shore, ordering you to return to land.",
                "mnemonic": "Not wanting to end up dead in enemy {tooltip:Kanji:territory}, you decide to escape this geoduck leader by getting on a {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat and rowing your way outta there. The geoduck commander orders you to halt your escape, but you still get in your row boat and row away."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The light of the {tooltip:Radical:moon} is shining on a {tooltip:Radical:guard} who's been on duty all night. The moon light makes him so warm and comfortable that he forgets where he is and starts to {tooltip:Kanji:undress}. He thinks he's home! Everyone is going to see him take off his clothes!",
            "hints": "Picture a sleepy guard, bathed in moonlight, starting to undress. No! Keep your uniform on guard! Don't undress outside in the middle of the night!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Undress"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine throwing darts at a guard who's undressing himself. Imagine trying to aim for his pants so they'll be nailed to his body.",
                "mnemonic": "You can't seem to get the guard to stop {tooltip:Kanji:undress}ing so you throw some {tooltip:Reading:darts} ({span:lang=ja:\u3060\u3064}) at him. You figure that even if the guard doesn't snap out of this weird sleepy trance, at least you can use the darts to stick his clothes to his body. Then maybe he won't be able to undress anymore. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take all of your {tooltip:Radical:thread} and {tooltip:Radical:allocate} them into one place to {tooltip:Kanji:unite} them. You wrap all the thread together into a giant thread ball. Now it's a big, united mess!",
            "hints": "Allocate all of your thread like you would your cash: by uniting it! Not at a bank, but in a big, intertwined lump.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Unite"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Try to do this yourself at home. Unite all of your thread and poof! There's {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}!",
                "mnemonic": "You're busy trying to {tooltip:Kanji:unite} all of your thread, twisting and tying and wrapping, and suddenly you look at the ball in your hands and see {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. You've united this thread into the shape of {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. There are even little pins for all the famous neighborhoods and tourist spots. This is strange, because you don't remember putting them there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} can {tooltip:Radical:fix} the {tooltip:Kanji:value} of certain goods and services. Leaders basically get to decide how much everything is worth in value, like rice or lamps or how much you get paid for the work you do.",
            "hints": "Imagine having a wonderful leader who values your work and time and so the value you get from working is high. Now imagine a terrible leader, who thinks you should be working at all times and doesn't find any value in what you do. Life will be a lot harder...",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Value",
                "Alternative": "Price"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306d, \u3042\u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine if you could fix the value of cheese to something. How much would you make it cost? If you were a dairy farmer you'd probably be pretty pissed about the leader making it this low.",
                "mnemonic": "This leader has fixed the {tooltip:Kanji:value} of {tooltip:Reading:chee}se ({span:lang=ja:\u3061}), making it \uffe51 permanently. One yen! That's, like, less than a penny! Unfortunately, the leader won't fix any of the other really expensive things... so now everyone only eats cheese."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} the {tooltip:Radical:leader} is in has the most {tooltip:Kanji:value}! He would only choose to fly the very best one, after all. That's why it's worth way more than the others. Actually, any helicopter he flies goes up in value. That's the amazing effect of a good leader.",
            "hints": "Can you understand the value of this helicopter? The leader flew it to war and back! So of course it's worth a lot!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Value"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine driving a valuable car with the leader's helicopter on top. Yeah!",
                "mnemonic": "To further increase the helicopter's {tooltip:Kanji:value}, the leader bought himself a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}) and then tied them together. Now it has the value of a helicopter AND a car! Wow!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "That {tooltip:Radical:scarecrow} with the {tooltip:Radical:knife} is the {tooltip:Kanji:vice} president. Yeah, I know how he looks, and I'm pretty sure he does some murdering on the {tooltip:Kanji:side}, but you didn't hear that from me.",
            "hints": "I don't know how we managed to get a knife-wielding scarecrow as a vice president, there's a side of politics I don't get, I guess. I mean, just look at him up there. If something happens to our president we're stuck with that thing.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Vice",
                "Alternative": "Side"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What's going on? Normally if a vice president yells f**k you there would be... I dunno... consequences? What's happening?!",
                "mnemonic": "It's the {tooltip:Kanji:vice} president's turn to speak at the podium and he just clears his throat and yells, \"{tooltip:Reading:F**k} ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u304f}) you!\" to the crowd, holding up his knife. They cheer."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There's an {tooltip:Radical:arrow} in a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} that you can {tooltip:Radical:see} in your {tooltip:Kanji:view}. The turkey seems to be viewing you too, from afar.",
            "hints": "View the turkey as the turkey views you. View the arrow stuck in it too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "View"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
