                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The {span:lang=ja:\u53cd} reading is all good and merry, but the {span:lang=ja:\u5fdc} reading gets a bit wonky, turning into {span:lang=ja:\u306e\u3046}. This is probably because it's just way easier to say than {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093\u304a\u3046} and sounds basically the same too. So, {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093\u304a\u3046} goes to {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093\u306e\u3046} and everyone's happy. Do you have {tooltip:Vocabulary:a response}? \n{splitParent}The reading {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093\u304a\u3046} is also going to be included since it's technically correct though a less common spelling.\n"
