                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your arms are nude, eh? That's why they look like snakes, you know. You should be more careful.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:arm} is exposed to the moon and the outside and you feel a chill. Where are your clothes? Ah, you're n{tooltip:Reading:ude, eh} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3067})?! I guess it is pretty common to sleep in the nude, eh?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:stand} in the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} and {tooltip:Radical:see} the {tooltip:Kanji:boundary}. The boundary between your home and your neighbors. The boundary between your town and the next. All you have to do to see it is stand in the dirt. It also helps that there is a boundary sign standing in the dirt that you can also see.",
            "hints": "Get off your computer and go stand outside in the dirt and see what boundaries you can see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Boundary"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
