                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself kicking the flag ten times. Count it off in your head and imagine each instance up to ten. Any more kicks after ten don\u2019t cause the table to do anything, but it does cause your leg to get sore.",
                "mnemonic": "The blackjack table does have a limit though of how many times it will {tooltip:Kanji:expand}, and that limit is {tooltip:Reading:ten} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3093}). You can only kick the flag to get the table to expand ten times."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Behind the {tooltip:Radical:flag} lies a {tooltip:Radical:mask}\u2014yet another {tooltip:Kanji:layer} of secrecy. You\u2019re standing in front of a crowd, giving a rousing speech. Hiding your face is the flag of your country, and behind that flag you\u2019re also wearing a mask, just in case the flag falls down. The extra layer of secrecy is just to be safe.",
            "hints": "These layers are meant to protect you. We all have layers we hide behind sometimes, you know? You can't be totally transparent with everyone.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Layer"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Everyone in the crowd is completely silent, staring at your soul, with all of its layers peeled off.",
                "mnemonic": "Someone jumps up on stage and starts peeling off your {tooltip:Kanji:layer}s! You stand there, first goes the flag, then the mask, then ... your {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) is laid bare. No, literally. You don't have a body, your soul was under that mask. And now it's floating there for all to see."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Radical:see} a {tooltip:Radical:spirit} you have to {tooltip:Kanji:look at} it. Look at it directly, because if you look away then it could disappear.",
            "hints": "Look at the spirit. Look at its shape and into its eyes. Just don't look away.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Look At"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you have to look at this sheep. Maybe the sheep was projecting the spirit... or maybe it's just a sheep. You'll have to look at it a bit longer to know for sure.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:look at} the spirit for as long as you can, until you hear a {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057}) sound. You look away for a second, see the sheep look at you, and when you look back the spirit is gone. Damn!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:king} is showing his people how to put a {tooltip:Radical:net} around a weird {tooltip:Radical:zombie} by walking around it in a {tooltip:Kanji:loop}.",
            "hints": "Watch as the king loops the net around and around and around the zombie, keeping it completely pinned down.",
