{
            "mnemonic": "If you leave a {tooltip:Radical:cross} on a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard}'s {tooltip:Radical:car} it's a sign that you'll {tooltip:Kanji:publish} everything if they try to drive. It's basically the universal symbol of, \"We're watching you, and we'll publish what you do, so don't drive drunk.\"",
            "hints": "Open your newspaper in the morning and you can see what's been published about all the drunkards who didn't pay attention to the crosses on their cars. They were all arrested and their stories were published for all to see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Publish"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
