                "mnemonic": "Once a year, when the {tooltip:Kanji:servant} wants to go home to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}, the leader follows. The servant isn't just there for the leader, they're companions, they support each other at all times. Even if that means heading home to {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} to see the fam."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:door} leading to the {tooltip:Radical:moon} can be broken down with one\u2019s {tooltip:Kanji:shoulder}. It\u2019s not a very sturdy door to the moon, so it\u2019s quite easy to drop your shoulder and ram it open.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself smashing through this door using your shoulder and seeing the moon on the other side. Hear the splintering of wood as your shoulder crashes through the door and feel the impact with your body.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shoulder"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
