                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's a really nice tie you use to apprehend the wolverine, so even though it's struggling and fighting, it can't get away.",
                "mnemonic": "You catch up with the wolverine and {tooltip:Kanji:apprehend} it by tying it down with the {tooltip:Reading:tie} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3044}) from around your neck!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have to fly in a {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} and use a {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer} to punch your {tooltip:Kanji:ballot}. The helicopter gets you far away from prying eyes, and the jackhammer makes you really try for whoever you're voting for on that thing. It's foolproof!",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to fill out your ballot while flying in a helicopter and using only a jackhammer to do it. Do you think you could do it? Do you think you could do it AND vote for the right person?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ballot"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You're starting to think this method of filling out ballots is rigged.",
                "mnemonic": "While using the jackhammer on the {tooltip:Kanji:ballot}, the helicopter pilot keeps yelling \u201c{tooltip:Reading:Heyo} ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3087\u3046}), don't mess up! Heyo! Watch out, don't let me see!\u201d as he flies the helicopter all over the place."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:mantis} sitting on a {tooltip:Radical:flag} and you know for a fact that it does not {tooltip:Kanji:belong} there. Insects should be in trees and on the ground. Not on flags. Insects belong in the wild!",
            "hints": "Look at that mantis, pretending it belongs here. What are you gonna do about it?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Belong"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305e\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your Bosozoku life has prepared you for this moment. Those who don't belong, shall be punished, you think to yourself.",
                "mnemonic": "Luckily for you, and unluckily for this mantis who doesn't {tooltip:Kanji:belong} on your flag, you're a Boso{tooltip:Reading:zoku} ({span:lang=ja:\u305e\u304f}) bike gang member, and you don't take crap from nobody. You climb the flagpole, punch the mantis and yell, \"YOU DON'T BELONG HERE!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "At your {tooltip:Radical:wedding} you use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to {tooltip:Kanji:catch} the wedding rings. And to catch the bouquet. And to catch the rice that everyone is throwing at you, ow, ow, hey stop! Weddings are really more about catching things than they are about whoever is standing across from you.",
            "hints": "Imagine being at a wedding and getting to catch a ton of things in your fingers.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Catch"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304b, \u3068\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself grumpily hoeing all the things you couldn't catch, and the dirt under it, and putting it into a big dumpster.",
                "mnemonic": "You're having a good time {tooltip:Kanji:catch}ing things until it's cleanup time and someone throws a {tooltip:Reading:hoe} ({span:lang=ja:\u307b}) at you. First of all, ow again, that was your face. Second, this is your wedding. You aren't supposed to have to hoe it all up. You're supposed to drop everything you caught and leave!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to grab this guy's {tooltip:Radical:foot} and {tooltip:Kanji:catch} him! Not physically though, you do grab his foot, but you close your eyes, and catch the idea of him in your mind just by touching your fingers to his foot.",
            "hints": "You don't really like the idea of touching your fingers to someone's foot, so you do it ever so slightly, and only catch the gist of what it's like.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Catch"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3089",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You wipe your eyes and look up, seeing that the person running from you is wearing socks with little pictures of the Torah on them. You were able to catch that in your brain but not the person. You must have touched those Torah socks and not his foot. You've been tricked!",
                "mnemonic": "As you touch his foot, you {tooltip:Kanji:catch} a glimpse of the {tooltip:Reading:Torah} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3089}) in your mind. Suddenly, you are able to grasp and understand every single thing written in the Torah. You fall to the ground."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} with a {tooltip:Radical:stick}, a {tooltip:Radical:hook}, and an {tooltip:Radical:arrow} is able to change the {tooltip:Kanji:climate} and {tooltip:Kanji:weather}. Not just the type of climate that causes sunny and rainy days though, the political climate too, because they're a political {tooltip:Kanji:candidate} too.",
            "hints": "Imagine this leader twirling his stick around with his hook so quickly it changes the actual weather. Then he shoots it into the sky with an arrow, changing the actual climate itself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Climate",
                "Alternatives": "Weather, Candidate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046\u308d\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ask {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} why he's changing the climate. He says more people do their WaniKani reviews when it's raining, so he decided to create climate change to make it more dangerous to go outside. \"This way, people will stay indoors and do their WaniKani reviews,\" he tells you.",
                "mnemonic": "Who is this {tooltip:Kanji:climate} and {tooltip:Kanji:weather}-changing {tooltip:Kanji:candidate} leader with the hook, stick, and arrow? It's none other than {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:criminal} that stole your {tooltip:Radical:car} was your {tooltip:Kanji:comrade}! You thought the two of you were friends, but you were probably wrong.",
            "hints": "Just because someone is your comrade doesn't mean they actually like you. Don't let your guard down and let them near your car.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Comrade"
