{
            "mnemonic": "Touch your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to your {tooltip:Radical:friend} to {tooltip:Kanji:extract} their friendship. Extract it with a high five. Extract it with a back rub. Extract it with an, \"Oh no, there's some lint on your shirt, let me get that for you.\"",
            "hints": "REMINDER: You are not allowed to touch any of your friends without their permission. If they say no to extracting, then you don't get to touch. End of story.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Extract"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3064, \u306f\u3064, \u306f\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306c",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "REMINDER: If someone asks you to extract their clothes to help them be nude, you don't have to do it unless you also want to! Choices and respect, people!",
                "mnemonic": "Your friend looks you in the eye and says, I want you to {tooltip:Kanji:extract} my clothes. I want to be {tooltip:Reading:nu}de ({span:lang=ja:\u306c}). Now you have to use your fingers on your friend to extract their clothes to help them be nude."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:fish} and {tooltip:Radical:sheep} are very {tooltip:Kanji:fresh} here. This is a great place to get fresh fish and fresh sheep. I kid you not.",
            "hints": "Imagine eating this fresh fish and fresh sheep. It\u2019s the freshest you\u2019ve ever tasted. Taste it on your tongue and experience how fresh it is.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fresh"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3056",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Can you imagine eating a fresh centaur? How weird would that be? Half of it is human-like, so you\u2019d be like, a half cannibal. Weird, huh?",
                "mnemonic": "This place also serves {tooltip:Kanji:fresh} {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}), but that\u2019s just weird. Centaur is endangered and you don\u2019t believe in eating endangered things. Even if they are incredibly fresh."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits these {tooltip:Radical:flowers} they'll {tooltip:Radical:both} become {tooltip:Kanji:full} of water. Tsunamis carry a lot of water, definitely enough to make both of these flowers full.",
            "hints": "Picture both of these little flowers, happily swaying in the breeze. Then the tsunami comes, leaves, and you look back and their little cup-heads are full to the brim with water.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Full"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Soon you have full color pages, full of stories about both of these tsunami-filled flowers and their adventures together. And when you're done, your heart is full as well. Awwww.",
                "mnemonic": "As you stare at the {tooltip:Kanji:full} flowers, you decide to write a {tooltip:Reading:man}ga ({span:lang=ja:\u307e\u3093}) about them. Your head is full of manga ideas!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:beggar} lies sprawled on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} so you {tooltip:Kanji:give} him some money. You feel bad for the beggar on the ground, so that\u2019s why you decided to give him something.",
            "hints": "See the beggar on the ground. He\u2019s writhing in agony and moaning for help. Imagine how sad and pitiful he looks.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Give"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now watch as the beggar plays with the yo-yo you just gave him. He\u2019s actually pretty good with it. See the beggar doing insane tricks with his new yo-yo as passersby give him change for his impressive yo-yo performance.",
                "mnemonic": "When you set the money down next to the beggar he shouts, \u201cNo! I want a {tooltip:Reading:yo}-yo ({span:lang=ja:\u3088})!\u201d so you go to the corner store and buy him a yo-yo with the money instead. You {tooltip:Kanji:give} the yo-yo to the beggar and he looks very happy."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Somebody got {tooltip:Radical:dirt} on your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} and {tooltip:Radical:dirt} on your {tooltip:Radical:toe}s so you're going to {tooltip:Kanji:hang} them upside-down and slap them with your dirty extremities.",
            "hints": "If someone got dirt all up in your finger and toe business wouldn't you want to hang them too?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hang"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044, \u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Don't get dirt on me, buddy. Or I'll hang you upside-down and hit you with my car. Then you'll be sorry.",
                "mnemonic": "You have this person {tooltip:Kanji:hang}ing upside-down but they don't seem to be suffering enough, so you hit them with your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). No mercy."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Behind a {tooltip:Radical:building}, a {tooltip:Radical:cleat}-wearing {tooltip:Radical:wolverine} is holding his {tooltip:Radical:heart} and trying to {tooltip:Kanji:hide}.",
            "hints": "You know the phrase, \"You can run, but you can't hide?\" This wolverine can't run anymore so he's trying to hide (even though he knows it probably won't work).",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hide"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Lucky wolverine! Inns are good for hiding. The staff isn't supposed to give out his room number, and there are tons of different rooms for him to hide in.",
                "mnemonic": "The wolverine looks up at the building he's trying to {tooltip:Kanji:hide} behind and sees it's an {tooltip:Reading:inn} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tree} grows next to a {tooltip:Radical:greenhouse} enclosing an {tooltip:Kanji:imitation} of the tree. The imitation greenhouse tree wants to be big and impressive like the tree outside, so it does its very best imitation of a real tree.",
            "hints": "Look at this greenhouse tree struggle to grow big and strong like the wild tree outside. Hear its leaves shake and timber creak. How cute.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Imitation"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082, \u307c",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hear the little tree moaning at its pitiful imitation of a real tree. The greenhouse tree sounds very sad and you actually start to feel bad for it. Moan along with the tree in sympathy.",
                "mnemonic": "The greenhouse tree realizes that its {tooltip:Kanji:imitation} will never be as good as the real thing. When it realizes this, the tree {tooltip:Reading:mo}ans ({span:lang=ja:\u3082}) aloud. The tree is still kinda tiny, so the moan isn\u2019t very loud, but it is still pretty strange to witness. Speaking of witnesses, {tooltip:Reading:Bo}bo ({span:lang=ja:\u307c}) the clown sees this greenhouse tree moaning and decides to take it for his next clown show. Surely this miniature moaning tree can be worked into Bobo's next clown act."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Now} your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} can {tooltip:Kanji:include} more words than ever before! With our new and improved \u201cMouth Now!\u201d program, your mouth will include more words than you ever thought possible!",
            "hints": "Imagine how your repertoire of new words will impress all your friends and family. Don\u2019t include them on your secret that you used the Mouth Now! program, just feel super smart with all the words you now know.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Include"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Since you bought the program, you also got the Gandhi books included with your order. Imagine yourself reading them and learning all about non-violent resistance. Fascinating.",
                "mnemonic": "If you buy now, we\u2019ll also {tooltip:Kanji:include} a handful of books by {tooltip:Reading:Gan}dhi ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3093}) himself. Gandhi didn\u2019t use our program, but we\u2019re sure if he\u2019d had the opportunity to, he would have used it. So buy now, and get the words of Gandhi in your hands as well as your mouth!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Be careful what you {tooltip:Radical:say} in {tooltip:Radical:public}, otherwise you might face a {tooltip:Kanji:lawsuit}. People will sue you for just about anything these days, so you really need to watch what you say in public, otherwise you might find yourself with a lawsuit on your hands.",
            "hints": "Think of all the things you could say in public that could get you stuck dealing with a lawsuit.{splitParent}Oh my gosh! How dare you think those things?! You're lucky you didn't say them out loud in public, or I'd file a lawsuit against you myself!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lawsuit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You better hope what you said wasn't about the Shougun, or he's really going to use this lawsuit to destroy you.",
                "mnemonic": "Any and all {tooltip:Kanji:lawsuit}s need to be brought before the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). Oh, you thought you'd get a judge or a jury? Nope, the Shougun decides your fate."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:building}'s {tooltip:Radical:root}s will {tooltip:Kanji:limit} the things under and around it.",
            "hints": "Picture the roots of a building: metal beams going into the ground. Now imagine trying to build something like a subway under there. It's not good! The building limits what can go under it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Limit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Genji tunneling under a building where a cute lady lives. He's trying to get in, but the building roots limit how far he can dig. No! Now how will he steal a secret kiss?!",
                "mnemonic": "The person who hates these {tooltip:Kanji:limit}s more than anyone else is {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}). He wants to be able to tunnel under buildings, sneak in, smooch ladies, and sneak back out. But all the building root limits make that impossible!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:moon} who stays in {tooltip:Radical:bed} all day every day will soon become {tooltip:Kanji:obese}. A healthy moon needs movement and exercise to stay fit and not become obese. If a moon stays in bed all day, they\u2019ll be sure to grow obese over time.",
            "hints": "Imagine this moon in bed, slowly getting bigger and bigger, becoming more obese every day. Hear the sound of the bed creaking and cracking as the moon grows larger and larger.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Obese"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053, \u3053\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the obese moon cozied up in bed with a heated blanket and hot cocoa.",
                "mnemonic": "Since the {tooltip:Kanji:obese} moon is in bed all day, and since the moon stays pretty cold, she needs some extra {tooltip:Reading:he}at ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}) to stay warm. A heated blanket should do the trick."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Music} {tooltip:Radical:beans} make farts {tooltip:Kanji:plentiful}. And lucky for you, music beans themselves are also plentiful, so you can eat plenty of them to power your musical bean toots.",
            "hints": "Imagine dancing to your own plentiful bean music as you gorge on beans.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Plentiful"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Be polite! Keep your plentiful farts at home.",
                "mnemonic": "Your music bean farts are too {tooltip:Kanji:plentiful} to leave your {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}). If you tried to leave your home you'd definitely fart all over people outside, so you keep your plentiful farts to yourself."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:husband} marries a {tooltip:Radical:husband} while the {tooltip:Radical:sun} goes down and the men {tooltip:Kanji:replace} their solitary lives with one of everlasting companionship. Instead of one husband and one wife, we have two husbands here. They shed their lives of bachelorhood and replace it with one of monogamy.",
            "hints": "See these two husbands as the sun sets under them. Listen to them each saying their vows, expressing how they could never replace one another.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Replace",
                "Alternative": "Exchange"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "See the husbands driving off into the sunset in their car. Hear the engine rumble as the car speeds off into the distance.",
                "mnemonic": "After the ceremony, the husband and his husband get in a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}) and drive off into the sunset. They\u2019ll never be able to {tooltip:Kanji:replace} this memory with anything. Truly it is the happiest day of these husbands\u2019 lives."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} rises over the {tooltip:Radical:capital} building, creating a breathtaking {tooltip:Kanji:scene}. The sun is so bright and warm as it crests over the capital building. It\u2019s quite the scene to behold.",
            "hints": "Picture this scene in your mind. Squint as the sun shines in your eyes and feel its warmth as it rises up and over the capital building.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Scene"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this scene again, but this time the sun is making the capital look like a big, fancy cake. Now take a bite!",
                "mnemonic": "The only way to make this {tooltip:Kanji:scene} better would be to add {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}). Now that you think about it... as you look at the scene in front of you, the capital kind of looks like a big cake."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:gladiator} only sees himself ({tooltip:Radical:oneself}) on those big {tooltip:Kanji:scroll}s they advertise the fights with. Gladiators don't get mirrors and there are no cameras or videos yet. The scroll drawings are all they get of themselves.",
            "hints": "Imagine being a gladiator. Your big fight is coming and you're the  main event! Look at the scroll for the fight and try to find yourself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Scroll"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "After a while of showing off the scroll, someone finally pulls you aside and says, \"That guy isn't you, it's the real Genghis Khan. He's coming to the event and he's against you. So. Nice knowing you.\"{splitParent}Oh.",
                "mnemonic": "When you look at the {tooltip:Kanji:scroll} you realize... you look just like Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093})! You excitedly fist pump and start showing everyone how cool you are."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You want to get your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} on the {tooltip:Radical:humble} {tooltip:Radical:stool}, so you dedicate your life to {tooltip:Kanji:search} for it. Wait, the humble stool? You know, like the holy grail or the ark of the covenant, but it's called the humble stool. It's from some bible or something, I promise.",
            "hints": "Now you have to search through a bunch of religious texts for this humble stool with your fingers. Don't go too fast and get paper cuts!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Search"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You dedicated your soul to searching, and now that your soul is free from its body, you can continue the search until you find it!",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:search} and you search and, unfortunately, you spend your entire life searching and you die without finding the humble stool. But don't worry, your {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) comes back and now you get to continue your search but with afterlife powers!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:lifeguard} will choose a {tooltip:Radical:tree} to {tooltip:Kanji:set up} the station where he'll {tooltip:Kanji:care} for the people on the beach and in the water. Trees provide the shade lifeguards need to take care of half-drowned kids and grannies with sand stuck in their bathing suits. That's why they set up their care stations here.",
            "hints": "Watch the lifeguard walk around the beach. He needs to pick a nice big tree for his set up, so he can provide the best care possible.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Set Up",
                "Alternative": "Care"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} setting up a care station. You hope you don't get in trouble in the water so you don't have to see how good he is at caring for people.{splitParent}Hint: when you see the \"lifeguard\" radical, the reading is probably going to be {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046}.",
                "mnemonic": "You look closer at the {tooltip:Kanji:set up} and realize the lifeguard is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}! You know he teaches Japanese but... is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} really qualified to care for people like this?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} rises over the {tooltip:Radical:capital}, shines down on your {tooltip:Radical:hair}, and casts a long {tooltip:Kanji:shadow} on the ground in front of you.",
            "hints": "Feel the heat of the sun on your back as you look down over your capital, your long hair blowing over your shoulder. Your shadow stretches in front of you and it's honestly pretty impressive.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shadow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3052",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What do you do? Keep standing here, admiring the view and casting this shadow on the acorn. Or do you move and let the acorn grow, becoming a tree that can cast its own shadow on your capital.",
                "mnemonic": "In the shade from your {tooltip:Kanji:shadow} you see a small {tooltip:Reading:a}corn ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3044}) laying on the ground. You're about to reach down and pick it up when you realize that your shadow is keeping this little acorn from growing up big and strong."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:thread} is {tooltip:Radical:mix}ed all around and begins to {tooltip:Kanji:strangle} you.",
            "hints": "Just imagine thread everywhere, mixing in with everything. It's all around, and no matter where you go you get more and more caught in this thread. Eventually it tightens because you're trying to escape, and you feel yourself having trouble breathing. Imagine the moment when you realize you're getting strangled.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Strangle"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057, \u3057\u307c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "In your final moments before you are totally strangled, you think you see a little thread come out of his butt. \"I should have done my WaniKani reviews\" is your last thought.",
                "mnemonic": "As you are {tooltip:Kanji:strangle}d you see who set this trap. (What else could it be, with all this thread everywhere?) It is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, who just watches you as you lose consciousness, tapping his fingers together."
            }
