                        "file": "31856-subject-4803.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: This {tooltip:Vocabulary:vivid} and {tooltip:Vocabulary:splendid} fresh fish is MINE! You grab the {tooltip:Reading:other} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3056}) one that's not as vivid and splendid. This one is mine.\n"
