                        "file": "44201-subject-8987.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. You haven't learned the on'yomi for {span:lang=ja:\u72fc} (wolf) yet, so here's a mnemonic to help you remember that, as well as which on'yomi to use for {span:lang=ja:\u4eba}:\n{splitParent}There's a {tooltip:Vocabulary:werewolf} in front of you wearing  {tooltip:Reading:jean}s and eating {tooltip:Reading:roe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093\u308d\u3046}). This is typical behavior for werewolves, as I'm sure you know.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u4eba\u72fc\u3092\u898b\u305f\u3053\u3068\u304c\u3042\u308a\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
