{
            "mnemonic": "You take some {tooltip:Radical:flowers} and some {tooltip:Radical:fruit} and you make a {tooltip:Kanji:cake} out of it. It\u2019s a very nice looking, flavorful cake. The fruit makes it taste great and the flowers make for great cake decorations.",
            "hints": "Look at this cake you have made. It\u2019s majestic. Now taste some of it. It is one great tasting cake. Imagine yourself eating the best cake in all of ever.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cake"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hear the roar of the car engine as you get splattered in the face with the cake. Wipe it off of your face just in time to see the car speeding off into the distance. Also, recall that this kanji shares a reading with the similar kanji, {span:lang=ja:\u679c}.",
                "mnemonic": "You\u2019re standing back, admiring your {tooltip:Kanji:cake} when you hear a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}) engine revving and before you know it your cake has been run over. The car came out of nowhere and ran your cake right over, spraying fruit cake bits and flowers all over the place. Stupid car!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "They {tooltip:Radical:say} using a {tooltip:Radical:measurement} device (like a ruler) is a good way to {tooltip:Kanji:chastise} someone. They do something bad? Chastise them by slapping their wrists, their feet, their eyes, ears, anything! They say something out of turn? CHASTISE THEM!",
            "hints": "Imagine being chastised with a measurement device. Think how horrible it would be getting hit on your knuckles, your nose, or the back of your head. It would be awful. Imagine this experience.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chastise"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "How could you say something in English while you're in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}?! After you went to all the trouble to learn all this kanji and Japanese? Geez, we almost think you deserve to be chastised...",
                "mnemonic": "You're being {tooltip:Kanji:chastise}d because you tried to say something in English in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. Everyone around you slowly turned around, eyes aflame and rulers in hand, ready to chastise you for uttering those forbidden words."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:old} {tooltip:Radical:winter} is to blame for today's {tooltip:Kanji:circumstance}. It is the {tooltip:Kanji:reason} things are bad now. ",
            "hints": "Imagine a poor, broken town. And, imagine the mayor of a town telling their people that things are bad because of that bad old winter. \"It's to blame for our circumstance!\" he yells.",
            "meanings": {
