                "mnemonic": "In reality, this {tooltip:Kanji:circumstance} was actually caused by a single {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053}), though. This kid went through town, destroying everything in their path."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your new {tooltip:Radical:car} doesn\u2019t {tooltip:Radical:mix} well with the other cars in your garage because its color is in stark {tooltip:Kanji:contrast} to the others. All of your other cars are pristine white in color, but this new car is a mix of lots of colors. It almost looks like a peacock or something it\u2019s so colorful. Such a contrast.",
            "hints": "Imagine this garage of yours with a sea of white cars. Now there is a new car that really sticks out like a sore thumb. Imagine yourself looking out over your cars and seeing this wacky car practically jumping out at you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Contrast",
                "Alternative": "Compare"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
