                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun'yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}When thinking about the {tooltip:Vocabulary:circumstance} of your current situation and the {tooltip:Vocabulary:reason} you're there (which is studying kanji and vocab). Whose fault is it? It's WaniKani's fault! But, your brain has been beaten to a mush from all the studying, so when you say \"it's your fault\" it comes out as \"it's {tooltip:Reading:yue} fault!\" Go ahead and say it out loud that way.\n"
