                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}I am going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to obey} you. I think your order is a bit of {tooltip:Reading:shit \u304c} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u305f\u304c}), I'll do it and obey you. \n{splitParent}(Little side note, did you know {span:lang=ja:\u304c} in the middle of a sentence can mean \"but\" in Japanese? Think of it as that meaning here.)\n"
