                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}Someone is trying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to shake something}. And unfortunately, that something is you. The most unfortunate thing here is that you're totally {tooltip:Reading:full} ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u308b}), and you throw up because of the shaking (and you're full, gross!).\n"
