{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:capital}, a broken {tooltip:Radical:dog} begins to {tooltip:Kanji:settle in}. This dog used to live in the country, but he kept getting caught in bear and fox traps which busted the poor dog up. The dog didn\u2019t want to live like this, so he decided to settle in the capital city where there aren\u2019t pesky animal traps to get caught in.",
            "hints": "Imagine this dog going to the capital and settling in. The poor dog looks pretty messed up though. The radical for dog in this kanji is a bit modified, so just remember that the dog in this story is all messed up.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Settle In"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch the broken dog settle in to his new shoes in his new home in the capital. The old dog can finally enjoy life!",
                "mnemonic": "In order to help the dog {tooltip:Kanji:settle in}, the capital cobbler makes him a pair of {tooltip:Reading:shoe}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}). The shoes help him walk on his hurt legs, but more importantly, they help him relax and feel like a dog again."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take your {tooltip:Radical:leather} and {tooltip:Radical:change} it into {tooltip:Kanji:shoes}.",
            "hints": "You start with a sheet of leather. Now imagine yourself going through the process of changing them to shoes. Smell the leather and feel it, too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shoes"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine some of these old coots busting into a modern shoe store and kicking over all the display stands and setting everything on fire because they hate non leather shoes so much. Hear the old coots screaming and babbling nonsense as they destroy the store.",
                "mnemonic": "Some {tooltip:Kanji:shoes} aren\u2019t made from leather anymore these days, but you know who always wears shoes made of leather? Old {tooltip:Reading:coots} ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3064}). Old coots are so old that the only shoes they wore growing up were made from leather so they refuse to wear any shoes that aren\u2019t made from leather. Crazy old coots."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Closing each {tooltip:Radical:eye} is something that the {tooltip:Radical:peoples} do before they {tooltip:Kanji:sleep}. The peoples can\u2019t sleep with both eyes open and they can\u2019t sleep with just one eye open either. Peoples have to close each eye before they can sleep.",
            "hints": "You are one of these peoples, so imagine yourself closing your eyes and sleeping. Go ahead and do it right now. Close one eye, and then the other. Now imagine yourself sleeping.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sleep"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306d\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Those other peoples were really mean to you. Imagine all the mean things they were saying to you. What did they say? Think about all these mean things as you close your eyes and drift off to sleep. Also keep in mind that this kanji has the same reading as {span:lang=ja:\u6c11}, which is included in this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "The reason you want to {tooltip:Kanji:sleep} is because all the other peoples were {tooltip:Reading:mean} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3093}) to you. They were so mean that the only way you could get over it was to close your eyes and sleep. You just want to sleep."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:sun} while holding a {tooltip:Radical:comb} in a {tooltip:Radical:cage} and sitting on a {tooltip:Radical:stool}, you comb your hair in your {tooltip:Kanji:spare time}. Since you\u2019re in a cage, you actually fashioned this comb yourself, so it\u2019s a little messed up, missing a prong. You\u2019re working on improving it in your spare time, and you also use it to style your mop.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself in your spare time, sitting on this stool in a cage in the sun. Feel the warmth of the sun on your body and feel the metal bars of the cage holding you in. You try to forget about your situation by combing your hair with the comb. The comb radical is a little modified, so be sure to remember that you made this comb yourself and it\u2019s a little wonky.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Spare Time",
                "Alternative": "Free Time"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u307e, \u3044\u3068\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself in this cage. You\u2019re going to be there for life because you\u2019d stolen too many cars. Feel the tears run down your face as you continue to comb your hair. You\u2019re going to die in this cage.",
                "mnemonic": "So how did you get in this cage? Well, before you used to comb your hair in your {tooltip:Kanji:spare time}, you used to steal {tooltip:Reading:ca}rs ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). You\u2019d stolen many a car in your day, but you finally got caught in the act of stealing a car, and now you\u2019re spending all of your spare time in that cage, just combing your hair."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Cut this {tooltip:Radical:comb} up with your {tooltip:Radical:weapon} and turn it into the {tooltip:Kanji:steps} for some {tooltip:Kanji:stairs}.",
            "hints": "When you think about it, a comb is like a ladder. So if you cut all the rungs off with your weapon and put them on the ground, they turn into stairs!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Steps",
                "Alternative": "Stairs"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine standing at the top of the stairs you made yourself, looking down at the entire town below you, as the light of dawn breaks and fills everything before you with light. And now more people can see this beautiful sight if they climb your steps.",
                "mnemonic": "You slowly work to create these {tooltip:Kanji:stairs}, you have to slice up a lot of combs, and at {tooltip:Reading:dawn} ({span:lang=ja:\u3060\u3093}) they are done!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you eat a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} the size of the {tooltip:Radical:moon}, your {tooltip:Kanji:stomach} is going to hurt. All the rice in a rice paddy the size of the moon is way too much rice for anyone to consume. If you do, your stomach is going to ache like crazy.",
            "hints": "Imagine having a whole rice paddy in your stomach. A rice paddy the size of the moon. Your stomach hurts a lot. You feel like you\u2019re going to throw up.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Stomach"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This eagle saw your stomach distress and decided to help by making you barf. Hear the screech of the eagle as it swoops down and rams you in the stomach.",
                "mnemonic": "From the sky, an eagle swoops down and flies right into your distended {tooltip:Kanji:stomach}. Bam! The {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) hits your stomach and you vomit up the entire moon sized rice paddy."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When someone is {tooltip:Radical:sick} in order to diagnose the {tooltip:Radical:correct} cause and treatment, you need to check their {tooltip:Kanji:symptom}s. You have to be especially careful too, because if you get a symptom wrong, you could kill them!",
            "hints": "If you know all of the symptoms for each and every sickness you'd be able to cure them all!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Symptom"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You get all up close and personal with the Shougun. Hmm, his symptoms are watery eyes, stuffy nose, angry shouting (wait no, that's not a symptom, is it?). Don't mess up!",
                "mnemonic": "You need to figure out the {tooltip:Kanji:symptom}s the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) is having. This is really serious too, so you better be correct about which sickness he has. If something bad happens to the Shougun it will be off with your head."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits while you're {tooltip:Radical:farming}, you'll have to wear really {tooltip:Kanji:thick} clothes to deal with it. The water is thick with fish and cars and other ripped-up debris too, which makes it even harder.",
            "hints": "Imagine putting on your thick farming suit as the tsunami comes at you. You hold onto your hoe and brace yourself for the wall of water.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Thick"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Thanks Nostradamus, now I'm in my nice, thick gear, struggling to hoe my fields through this wall of tsunami water. But I'm not dead and I'm not wet.",
                "mnemonic": "You knew to put on your {tooltip:Kanji:thick} tsunami-proof farming gear because {tooltip:Reading:No}stradamus ({span:lang=ja:\u306e\u3046}) warned you it was coming. He sent a message to your brain yesterday so you'd know what to wear today."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a special {tooltip:Radical:thread} in your {tooltip:Radical:towel} you can use to make it {tooltip:Radical:stand} up by {tooltip:Kanji:tighten}ing it.",
            "hints": "Imagine pulling this thread and watch as your towel tightens and goes rigid, standing up almost completely on its own (except that the thread did it).",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tighten"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "A tightened towel stands up for easy grease cleanup. No wiping on your pants, no dripping on the floor.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:tighten} your towel before you eat {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots every night. That way it stands up nice and straight next to your eating chair, ready for all that delicious tater tot grease that gets on your fingers."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:scooter} is {tooltip:Radical:white}. This color will {tooltip:Kanji:urge} and {tooltip:Kanji:compel} you to use it. Scooter companies use colors to get you to do what they want. Some would say they are trying to {tooltip:Kanji:coerce} you, even.",
            "hints": "Look at how white the scooter is. It urges you to use it. It compels you. You feel coerced...",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Urge",
                "Alternatives": "Compel, Coerce"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Really all marketing, advertising, and the like is just a hack of your brain.{splitParent}Hint: If you see {span:lang=ja:\u767d} in a kanji, there's a good likelihood the reading will be {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u304f}.",
                "mnemonic": "When they {tooltip:Kanji:urge}, {tooltip:Kanji:compel} and {tooltip:Kanji:coerce} you like this, they are {tooltip:Reading:hack}ing ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u304f}) your brain."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Someone just asked you to {tooltip:Radical:say} which {tooltip:Radical:direction} they should {tooltip:Kanji:visit}.",
            "hints": "You better think long and hard about where you think they should visit before you say so. They're relying on you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Visit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u305a, \u304a\u3068\u305a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your home is just over that direction, and it's your favorite place to visit, so why wouldn't this stranger want to visit your home too?! So come and visit my home, random person!",
                "mnemonic": "You end up saying, \"You should {tooltip:Kanji:visit} my {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}).\" How kind of you!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Taking a {tooltip:Radical:thread} and moving to the {tooltip:Radical:sound} of the music, a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} makes a {tooltip:Kanji:weave} through some fabric. He\u2019s using the thread to weave his clothes back together after he damaged them in a fall down the stairs. You know, because he\u2019s a drunkard.",
            "hints": "Imagine this drunkard bipping and bopping to the sound of the music as he weaves this thread through his clothes to repair them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Weave"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u304d, \u3057\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine this drunken Sheikh again, only this time he is moving to the sound of some Arabic music. You know what that sounds like, right?",
                "mnemonic": "This drunkard is actually a {tooltip:Reading:Sheikh} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u304d}) (an Arabic leader), but he\u2019s just fallen on hard times and has been hitting the bottle pretty hard lately. The piece of clothing he is using the thread to {tooltip:Kanji:weave} back together is one of his fancy formal robes."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If your {tooltip:Radical:soul} is lying in the {tooltip:Radical:grass} in a {tooltip:Radical:treasure chest}, you're going to {tooltip:Kanji:worry} about it. It's just sitting there, out in the open, waiting for anyone to come and open it.",
            "hints": "Picture your soul curled up inside this treasure chest that's just sitting out on the grass. Anyone could open it up and look inside, and this worries you quite a bit!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Worry"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You worry about what you'll find if you look directly at your soul. But you also worry about what will happen if someone else looks. So you're stuck in a constant state of worrying: nah or yah?!",
                "mnemonic": "Unfortunately, you also {tooltip:Kanji:worry} about opening it yourself. You stand in front of the chest and think, \"Should I open it? {tooltip:Reading:Nah, yah} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3084}). Wait. Nah. Yah. Dang, you can't make up your mind."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:flag} by the {tooltip:Radical:exit} letting you know to {tooltip:Kanji:yield}. There\u2019s cross traffic just outside the exit, and the flag lets you know that you need to yield to them.",
            "hints": "Look at this flag telling you to yield. Now look through the exit right by the flag. You can see a bunch of people out there walking. Imagine standing by the exit, yielding to the other people until you have an opening. Hear the hustle and bustle of the people as you wait.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Yield"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Darn coots! Forget the yield flag, it\u2019s time to exit. Imagine busting out of the exit, punching and pushing your way through the old coots. Hear them scream and shout \u201cAugh! My hip!\u201d as you plow through them.",
                "mnemonic": "Even though the flag told you to {tooltip:Kanji:yield}, you\u2019re starting to lose your patience. The people walking outside the exit are all a bunch of crazy old {tooltip:Reading:coots} ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3064})! These crazy coots keep walking right in front of the door, getting in the way. The old coots aren\u2019t even going anywhere, they just keep looping around to obstruct the way!"
            }
        }

