                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Gecki is attacking you now. He's hitting you over and over with his tiny car. He's yelling and smacking your ankles with his weapon. And all you can do is wait and let the attack happen, because you know you deserve it.",
                "mnemonic": "Right before the {tooltip:Kanji:attack} begins, you recognize the hand holding this weapon and driving this car. It's {tooltip:Reading:Gecki} ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u304d}), your long-lost gecko who you may or may not have let fly off into a really fierce tsunami. Oops. I think he may be here attacking you out of revenge."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "After a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}, you find an {tooltip:Radical:axe} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} next to some {tooltip:Radical:fins} on the {tooltip:Kanji:beach}. The tsunami was pretty violent, and it looks like this axe got blown into some fish and cut off their fins and now those things are just on the ground by the beach.",
            "hints": "See these things on the beach. It makes sense to see fins, as fins are usually in the ocean, so seeing them on the beach is logical. Pick up the stuff you find as you feel the beach sand between your toes.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Beach"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u307e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Pick up the hammer in your hand. It\u2019s pretty heavy. The tsunami must have been very strong to pick up such a heavy hammer.",
                "mnemonic": "Walking down the {tooltip:Kanji:beach} a bit more, you also find a {tooltip:Reading:hammer} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u307e}). Gosh, looks like the tsunami hit a workshop or a hardware store or something. First the axe, now a hammer."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:thread} is {tooltip:Radical:odd}, but that's what makes it {tooltip:Kanji:beautiful}. It's a little frayed, it's a little miscolored, but that's what makes it appealing to you.",
            "hints": "If something is a bit odd, it's usually beautiful in its own way, just like this beautiful thread.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Beautiful"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "To remember that there's a beautiful thread hidden away, you tie a not-as-beautiful thread to the end of the key.",
                "mnemonic": "You take this {tooltip:Kanji:beautiful} thread and lock it up with a {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}). You want to keep it all to yourself, you want its beauty to be for your eyes only!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are some {tooltip:Radical:horns} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} next to {tooltip:Radical:fins} on a {tooltip:Radical:plate} that are meant to {tooltip:Kanji:benefit} everyone. If you're a member of this town, one of your benefits is this little set up.",
            "hints": "You pick up the horns off the ground and put them on your head, then eat some fins off the plate. This is just one of many benefits to living here. You'll never go hungry!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Benefit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Okay, so using the {span:lang=ja:\u99c5} is probably a better benefit than eating cold fins off a plate on the ground, but you take what you can get. They're all free!",
                "mnemonic": "Another {tooltip:Kanji:benefit} is free {span:lang=ja:\u99c5} usage! Whenever you come back home from places on the train, this {span:lang=ja:\u99c5} is completely free."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Pointing your magic solar powered wishing {tooltip:Radical:stick} at the {tooltip:Radical:sun}, you attain the {tooltip:Radical:legs} of a {tooltip:Kanji:child}. You\u2019re old and want young legs to carry you around, so you took your wishing stick that\u2019s powered by the sun, and you wished for the legs of a child.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself getting new legs. Legs that belong to a child. They\u2019re limber and young and full of energy! Feel your legs of a child underneath you!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Child"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Say back to Jesus, \u201cI\u2019m not your child Jesus! And you\u2019re just jealous of my new legs! You wish you had the legs of a child, Jesus! Your legs are like super old!\u201d Actually say this out loud, and remember how Jesus wishes he could be a child again too.",
                "mnemonic": "As you delight in your new legs, {tooltip:Reading:Je}sus ({span:lang=ja:\u3058}) descends from the sky. \u201cMy {tooltip:Kanji:child},\u201d he says, \u201cwhy have you pointed the stick at the sun and wished for the legs of a child? You were already perfect, just as all of God\u2019s children are perfect.\u201d"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:roof} protecting your {tooltip:Radical:life} and the {tooltip:Radical:net} protecting your {tooltip:Radical:heart} are both protected by the {tooltip:Kanji:constitution}.",
            "hints": "The constitution makes it so that everything you hold dear is locked away, nice and safe on a piece of paper, and no one can change the rules or hurt you without your say so. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Constitution"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Ken standing in front of your constitution. But keep a close watch, cause wily ol' Nic Cage is in the business of thievin' on constitutions.",
                "mnemonic": "Your country's {tooltip:Kanji:constitution} is being protected by none other than {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai, hero for hire."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You got your {tooltip:Radical:ice} {tooltip:Radical:orders}. Of course, your ice orders are to make things {tooltip:Kanji:cool} and {tooltip:Kanji:cold}.",
            "hints": "Making things cool and cold are pretty much the only orders you'll hear from ice. Ice is very simple in that regard.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cool",
                "Alternative": "Cold"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3081, \u3072, \u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a cold ray coming out of your ray gun. Anything it touches becomes cold. \"Stay cool, bird boy,\" you say.{splitParent}Hint: when you see the radical {tooltip:Radical:orders} it's fairly likely the reading will be {span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3044}.",
                "mnemonic": "How will you make things {tooltip:Kanji:cool} and {tooltip:Kanji:cold}? You'll use a special {tooltip:Reading:ray} ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3044}) gun that shoots a cold ray."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:winter} {tooltip:Radical:table} would be an odd thing to {tooltip:Kanji:deal with}. Winter can be hard to deal with on its own, but turn your table into winter? Just dealing with your food getting cold would be the worst!",
            "hints": "Look at this winter table. How are you ever going to deal with it? Just think of your favorite warm food and then imagine it getting cold. Deal with it, dog.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Deal With"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3053\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel the relief of getting rid of this table. No more having to deal with it anymore. The circus show can have it.",
                "mnemonic": "This winter table is something you have to {tooltip:Kanji:deal with}, sure, but what if you just gave it to a circus {tooltip:Reading:show} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087})? They like weird stuff like this."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:loiter} on the {tooltip:Radical:mountain}, reading off the numbers of {tooltip:Radical:pi} on this {tooltip:Radical:winter} morning. Everything is so perfect, so mathematical here. You view it as {tooltip:Kanji:delicate}. Not in the sense that it will break apart at any moment, more in the sense that there are smaller, more subtle things to be enjoyed on this mountain, which is why you loiter here doing math.",
            "hints": "You'll have to imagine the things you consider to be \"delicate.\" Is that the snow falling on the branches? Is it the breeze? Is it something else? That's for you to decide, but imagine it vividly whatever it is.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Delicate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3073",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself looking at the bee, thinking how each hair on its body is so delicate. Maybe it has a delicate aroma to go with it. A faint smell of honey?",
                "mnemonic": "Ah! Of course! The {tooltip:Kanji:delicate} bumble {tooltip:Reading:be}e ({span:lang=ja:\u3073}), that is your epitome of delicate. It lands upon your finger, and you look at its every fiber of being."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} uses a {tooltip:Radical:stick} in the {tooltip:Radical:winter} made of {tooltip:Radical:hair} to enforce {tooltip:Kanji:discipline}. The leader uses the stick made of hair to discipline his followers. He hits them with it.",
            "hints": "Imagine the leader disciplining his people with the hair stick in the winter. Imagine him yelling \u201cDISCIPLINE!!\u201d with each hit of the stick as you feel the cold winter air around you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Discipline"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as the leader gets pelted with all sorts of types of shoes. Boots, high heels, baby slippers. They're all colliding with him as the people shout, \"Discipline solves nothing!\"",
                "mnemonic": "If the leader uses a stick to {tooltip:Kanji:discipline} his followers, eventually they'll fight back. The disciplined masses start to take off their {tooltip:Reading:shoe}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}) and throw them at the leader!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You wear a great big {tooltip:Radical:cross} on your chest and you attend a {tooltip:Radical:specialty} {tooltip:Kanji:exhibition} for {tooltip:Kanji:gambling}. The big cross on your chest is your badge for being admitted into the exhibition. Everyone at the specialty exhibition has a cross, and everyone is gambling.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself at this specialty exhibition. Feel the weight of the cross shaped badge on your chest as you continue gambling at the exhibition.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Exhibition",
                "Alternative": "Gambling"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304f, \u3070\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hack the gambling machines. Imagine the sounds of the exhibition around you as you work to hack the machines. Look at the computer parts and cables as you work.",
                "mnemonic": "You\u2019re not very good at {tooltip:Kanji:gambling}, but you are pretty good at cheating. You {tooltip:Reading:hack} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u304f}) the specialty {tooltip:Kanji:exhibition} gambling machines to pay out lots of cash just for you. You hack quickly and quietly, so luckily no one notices that you\u2019ve hacked the system."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:Grain} {tooltip:Radical:Mouth} {tooltip:Radical:King} pours grain from his mouth for you and his other subjects. You go to him and pull his finger. When you do this, grain pours from his mouth. But we were greedy. We didn't understand the {tooltip:Kanji:extent} to which we were harvesting his mouth wheat.",
            "hints": "Of course, you need to imagine pulling the Grain Mouth King's finger, to some extent. You can't just read what we write for you, without going to the imagination zone. Pull that finger real hard a couple times, and watch an extra large purge of grain pour forth.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Extent"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3069",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine hearing the rumors that the Grain Mouth King ran out of grain, so you go check the extent of his failure yourself. But tater tots taste pretty good too. Imagine eating one of his mouth tater tots and go ahead and comment about it to him.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:extent} to which we were harvesting grain from his mouth was too great. The Grain Mouth King has run out of grain. He worries he will lose power if he has no grain to offer, so he switches to barfing out {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots instead."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Sometime in the future, {tooltip:Radical:thread} of every {tooltip:Radical:color} will be faced with {tooltip:Kanji:extinction}. Eventually there will be nothing else to make thread out of, and thread of every kind and color will reach extinction.",
            "hints": "Imagine what the world would be like without thread. No thread of any color. How would you fix tears in clothes or make new ones? It would be a strange world where thread is extinct.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Extinction",
                "Alternative": "Die Out"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305c\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Pretend you have deadly zits. They\u2019re everywhere, not just your face. You can\u2019t pop them or you\u2019ll die, but they\u2019re all bulging and extremely painful. Now you\u2019re facing extinction. Lousy.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:extinction} of thread was brought on by a very strange thing. Deadly {tooltip:Reading:zits} ({span:lang=ja:\u305c\u3064}). These zits killed off all the producers of thread, and eventually the thread went extinct. Dang zits."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Ice} from the {tooltip:Radical:east} is {tooltip:Kanji:frozen}. Well, of course, all ice is frozen, but ice from the east is like, really super frozen.",
            "hints": "Imagine this super frozen ice from the east. You\u2019ve never seen anything quite like it before. It\u2019s so frozen, it\u2019s like it was frozen once and then frozen again. Twice frozen. Feel the ice and how freezing cold it is. It\u2019s super cold, guys.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Frozen",
                "Alternative": "Freeze"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u304a, \u3053\u3054",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} and seeing all this frozen ice. Hear people speaking Japanese all around you as you touch and feel the freezing twice-frozen ice.",
                "mnemonic": "Japan is a country in the east, and this ice was {tooltip:Kanji:frozen} in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} is really good at freezing frozen things, so it makes sense that this frozen ice came from there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:giant} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:giant} kanji are exactly the same! Massive!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Giant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "See Little Kyoto after the giant rampaged through it. It looks even smaller and more pathetic than ever. Look at all the smoldering rubble and smell the smoke with your nose.",
                "mnemonic": "Just recently, a {tooltip:Kanji:giant} rampaged through Little {tooltip:Reading:Kyo}to ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087}), so now it's even smaller than before. Poor Little Kyoto."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Only give {tooltip:Radical:grain}s to a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} if it's {tooltip:Kanji:immature}. Adult turkeys should be eating healthier things, like insects and grass. But immature turkeys don't care if they get fat, so they whine and whine and whine until you give them grains.",
            "hints": "Imagine an immature turkey complaining at you until you give it grains. Now it's taking selfies with the grains and posting pics to Instagram and hashtagging them #GRAINLIFE.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Immature"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a bunch of immature kids and turkeys eating cheese together.",
                "mnemonic": "Another thing {tooltip:Kanji:immature} turkeys (and people) love is {tooltip:Reading:chee}se ({span:lang=ja:\u3061}). Most of us non-immature people and birds still like cheese, but if you didn't have an immature cheese phase as a kid or teen, you won't be able to like cheese as a mature old person."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Super {tooltip:Radical:poop} is a super {tooltip:Radical:power} you have in {tooltip:Kanji:infancy}. Those in infancy have the power to poop at will, whenever and wherever they please. Infancy poop power!",
            "hints": "Infants poop a lot. There's poop everywhere. The powerful aroma overwhelms you. Eww.{splitParent}Also refers to childhood, when you still have some of your poop powers, but they're already starting to go away.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Infancy",
                "Alternative": "Childhood"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3055\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "See this infant gobbling up all the yogurt he can get his grubby little hands on. Soon, he begins to poop all over the place. Hear the infant screaming, \"Goo-goo! Yogurt poop power! I'm a baby! Wahhhh!!\"",
                "mnemonic": "In {tooltip:Kanji:infancy}, one eats a lot of soft foods, such as {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}). Yogurt is the food item above all others that grants superior pooping power."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You stick {tooltip:Radical:horns} in the {tooltip:Radical:ground} using them as {tooltip:Radical:spikes} and you {tooltip:Kanji:line up} the horns in a straight line. Horns are pretty much the same thing as spikes once you stick them in the ground, and you line these ones up precisely for optimal protection.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself lining up these horns in the ground. The spikes are sharp and you poke yourself with one. Ouch. Need to be more careful as you line these up.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Line Up"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3089, \u306a\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the hay in that bull's mouth as it chomps angrily, watching you line up horns in the ground. It probably wishes you were the hay.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:line up} these horns and stick them into the ground, you notice a bull munching on {tooltip:Reading:hay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3044}) nearby. It's staring at the horns you're lining up. Somehow it feels like it's munching that hay angrily. You gulp, looking at its horn as it grabs another mouthful of hay, and you feel pretty guilty."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you know the radical meaning {tooltip:Radical:lovely}, you know the kanji meaning {tooltip:Kanji:lovely} as well!",
            "hints": "You know what would make learning this radical lovely? Studying your radicals.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lovely"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
