                        "reading": "\u3044\u3055\u304e\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The area is SO pure that the ground absorbs the ketsup and now it's all pure... ketsup color.",
                "mnemonic": "After the tsunami pulls away, everything left is {tooltip:Kanji:pure} white. You hate this, so you run over and squirt {tooltip:Reading:ketsu}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3064}) all over the place to make it not so pure."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:gold} {tooltip:Radical:Wolverine} swam in the {tooltip:Radical:water} while his father made a {tooltip:Kanji:record} of it. Wolverine is gold in color because he just won the gold medal in swimming, so now he is gold. Way to go, Wolverine.",
            "hints": "See this gold Wolverine holding his gold medal after getting out of the water. His dad doesn\u2019t want to forget anything about this precious moment so he makes a record of it. Imagine him scribbling furiously in his notebook.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Record"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a pitiful Wolverine crying on the ground as each rock hits him. All he wanted was some recognition from his father. Poor guy. Imagine poor Wolverine like this as his dad just looks on and writes in his notebook.",
                "mnemonic": "Since Wolverine is actually a mutant, he is soon disqualified from his gold medal. His father makes a {tooltip:Kanji:record} of this also. One angry fan threw a {tooltip:Reading:rock} ({span:lang=ja:\u308d\u304f}) at Wolverine afterwards. Then another threw a rock. And another rock. Before you knew it, everyone was throwing rocks at Wolverine. Wolverine\u2019s dad didn\u2019t step in to help though, he just kept keeping records."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:scooter} takes you to the {tooltip:Radical:barracks}, {tooltip:Radical:drop}s you off, and then goes in {tooltip:Kanji:reverse} all the way back home in the {tooltip:Kanji:opposite} direction.",
            "hints": "Imagine riding your scooter to the barracks. It literally drops you on the ground when you get there, and then drives in reverse back the opposite way you came.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reverse",
                "Alternative": "Opposite"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
