{
            "mnemonic": "You don't say \"to aggression.\" When you do aggression on someone, you're probably doing something to hurt them in some way. This is an attack, making this word {tooltip:Vocabulary:to attack}. This refers to a planned attack, though. Think about what you're going to do. Plan it out. Then, {span:lang=ja:\u653b\u3081\u308b}!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "To Attack",
                "Alternatives": "To Assault, To Assail",
                "Word Type": "transitive verb, ichidan verb"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3081\u308b"
                    }
                ],
                "pronunciationAudios": [
