                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: Only for you, when you visit {tooltip:Reading:Nara} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3089}), the deer there are {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be lined up} for you to inspect, as you are the deer inspector. If you don't know about Nara and its deer, you should look it up, they're pretty awesome.\n"
