{
            "mnemonic": "A good {tooltip:Radical:leader} will use {tooltip:Radical:charcoal} to mark her {tooltip:Kanji:colleague}s. Sometimes if leaders aren't around all the time, people will get rebellious and act badly toward people who can get them in trouble. So when you mark them with charcoal you know that someone close with your leader is around and you should probably stop being a butt.",
            "hints": "Imagine seeing one of the leader's colleagues walking around, watching you. You'd get back to work and stop goofing around, right?",
