                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine goofing off in your row boat and then seeing one of the colleagues waiting on the shore for you. No! She's gonna take your row boat away!",
                "mnemonic": "You have to be good around her {tooltip:Kanji:colleague}s, because if you aren't your {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat permit will be taken away. Row boating is the only fun you ever get to have, besides learning kanji. So act as best you can around the leader's colleagues so you don't lose your row boat rights."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tree} is {tooltip:Radical:not} a {tooltip:Kanji:cup of liquid} or a {tooltip:Kanji:counter for cups}. Don\u2019t get them mixed up. The last time you tried making a cup out of a tree to count your throat got filled with splinters when you used it. There wasn't even any liquid in it.",
            "hints": "Imagine cutting a tree into a cup of liquid and focus on the pain in your throat when you try to actually use it. Instead you kick the tree and angrily count cups of liquid in your head, because they simply are NOT the same.",
            "meanings": {
