                        "reading": "\u305b, \u305d\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Say this haiku out loud. Memorize it and use this haiku to remember this kanji.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:back} hurts so much that the only way to properly explain the pain is in {tooltip:Reading:hai}ku ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3044}) form. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:horse} gets trapped in a small room with a {tooltip:Radical:stool} and an {tooltip:Radical:insect}, and together they create a very {tooltip:Kanji:boisterous} situation. The horse and the insect are both scrambling frantically to get out of the small room, knocking the stool around all over the place.",
            "hints": "Imagine the boisterous sounds coming from this small room. Hear the horse neigh and stomp his hooves, hear the insect buzzing loudly, and hear the wooden stool rattle around as the horse and insect try to escape the room.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Boisterous"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The horse gets even more frightened now that it killed the insect and saw an actual soul float by its head and it grows even more boisterous. ",
                "mnemonic": "At the height of their {tooltip:Kanji:boisterous} sounds, there's a sudden, awful CRONCH(!) and you see the {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) of the insect slowly rising out of the room, through the ceiling."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Radical:eat} you want to see the shape of your {tooltip:Radical:gun} from under a {tooltip:Radical:towel}, so you {tooltip:Kanji:decorate} your house with them.",
            "hints": "Just picture it: an entire home decorated top to bottom with guns covered in towels, so only the outline shows. As your guests try to eat you say, \"Guess what gun this is?! Haha, you got it wrong, pull the towel back.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Decorate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3056",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Maybe you should be more conscious of other people when you decorate. Or at least, don't shock people into fainting or yelling or leaving. Guns do that, you know?",
                "mnemonic": "If you actually {tooltip:Kanji:decorate} your house like this it will give people quite a {tooltip:Reading:shock} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u304f}). In fact, they might be so shocked they run out of there screaming."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you want to buy a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} you have to go to the bank {tooltip:Radical:beforehand} to {tooltip:Kanji:deposit} enough money. If you don't deposit your money you won't have enough in your account to buy even one! They're expensive, after all.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself depositing your money beforehand. Imagine the delicious geoduck you'll be able to buy now that the money has been deposited into your account!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Deposit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
