{
            "mnemonic": "Traveling in the {tooltip:Radical:direction} of the ocean, you take a {tooltip:Radical:gun} and shoot a {tooltip:Radical:crab}, then stick a {tooltip:Kanji:flag} in the beach and claim it as your own. The crab was the only thing standing in the way of you conquering the area. Now that the flag is in the ground, no one can dispute who it belongs to.",
            "hints": "Look at your flag and hear it flapping in the wind. Also hear your ears ringing a bit from when you shot that crab. Look at all the bits of exploded crab strewn around the area. Yowza.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Flag"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself locking this flag up with your key. Imagine turning the key in the lock and hearing the click when it is secured.",
                "mnemonic": "To make sure that no one removes your {tooltip:Kanji:flag}, you lock it to one of the lifeguard posts and you throw away the {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}). Since no one will have the key to unlock the flag, no one will be able to remove it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} knocks a {tooltip:Radical:cleat} off a {tooltip:Radical:child} and the shoe begins to {tooltip:Kanji:float} away in the water. This child was just out playing soccer, minding his own business, when the tsunami crashed in and knocked his cleats off his feet. Now the cleat is floating away with the tsunami.",
            "hints": "Your cleat is floating away but you\u2019re floating too. The water is really deep now, but you try and float towards your cleat to retrieve it. Imagine floating in this wet water reaching for your lost cleat.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Float"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046, \u3046\u308f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Say \u201cUwaaa~\u201d out loud a few times while you imagine an {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u306b} stabbing you as you float along with the tsunami water. What a day you\u2019ve had.",
                "mnemonic": "While you {tooltip:Kanji:float} in the water, an {tooltip:Reading:u}ni ({span:lang=ja:\u3046}) jabs into your foot. \u201c{tooltip:Reading:Uwa}aa~ ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u308f})\u201d you cry. That uni really hurts. They\u2019re all spikey and painful and junk. \u201cUwaaaa~\u201d"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:run} every day and soon you {tooltip:Radical:become} a human that can {tooltip:Kanji:go beyond} the normal speed limits of man. You run and you run and you run. This training allows you to become super human. You go beyond the limits of a normal human. You become a human who can run really fast.",
            "hints": "Run fast! Go beyond the limits imposed upon you by nature! Imagine yourself running faster than any human has ever run ever. Feel yourself cutting through the air, wind breaking across you as you break the sound barrier. Boom!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Go Beyond"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Etch these runes into your legs. Go ahead and run a finger over your legs and pretend to etch runes into them. These runes you etch will allow you to run fast forever.",
                "mnemonic": "To solidify your ability to {tooltip:Kanji:go beyond} the abilities of other humans, you {tooltip:Reading:etch} ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3064}) sacred runes into your legs to preserve your running abilities. Etching these runes makes sure that your skills will never deteriorate."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} is being {tooltip:Radical:call}ed on to {tooltip:Radical:boil} the earth by {tooltip:Kanji:illuminating} it.",
            "hints": "We don't want the earth to actually boil, but we do want some of that boiling hot sun light to illuminate all of the darkness of the universe and let us see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Illuminate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the Shougun calling out to the sun, asking it to illuminate our planet with its boiling hot rays. You better thank the Shougun the next time you see him for everything he does for you.",
                "mnemonic": "The person who calls the sun asking it to {tooltip:Kanji:illuminate} the earth is the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). It's very specifically the Shougun's responsibility to make sure the earth is illuminated every morning."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} rips a {tooltip:Radical:flag} off your house in the {tooltip:Radical:rain}, causing a {tooltip:Kanji:leak} where it was ripped out. The rain and the tsunami combined just tore the flag right off your house. The force was so strong that it actually removed part of the wall, and now you have a leak in your home.",
            "hints": "Look at this leak in your house and see the rain water coming in. Hear it drip drip dripping down the wall.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Leak"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Did you know that roe can plug any leak? It\u2019s true. If you don\u2019t mind wasting some, you should break a leak into your own house and then try to plug it back up again with some salmon roe.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:leak} is getting worse and worse and so is the tsunami, when you see something outside. It\u2019s a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:roe} ({span:lang=ja:\u308d\u3046}) floating in the waves. Using your quick thinking skills you scoop it up and shove it into the cracks where the water is leaking in. It works like a charm!"
