                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You come from a lineage of cake makers and eaters. No wonder you love cake so much! (And if you hate cake, no wonder your family doesn't like you.)",
                "mnemonic": "You trace your {tooltip:Kanji:lineage} back and realize that every single person in your family loved {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}). Most of them were cake bakers, too!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:servant} holding a {tooltip:Radical:gun} sits on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} to {tooltip:Radical:see} if he can find something to {tooltip:Kanji:look at}. The servant is on watch duty and has the gun to protect the perimeter. He patrols the grounds to look at the distance to see if there are any trespassers.",
            "hints": "Look at this servant. He\u2019s doing a great job. Oops, look like he sees you. Yup, he\u2019s pointing his gun at you. Imagine staring down the barrel of his gun as you slowly back away.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Look At"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3089\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Pretend you are Macho Man Randy Savage. Run at this servant guy, take his gun away, and beat him up. Ohhh yeaaahhh!",
                "mnemonic": "You start backing away, but then you realize that you are Macho Man {tooltip:Reading:Ran}dy ({span:lang=ja:\u3089\u3093}) Savage. Randy Savage backs away from no fight! I mean, {tooltip:Kanji:look at} this guy \u2013 this servant guy. Take away the gun and he\u2019s not much to look at. You can take him."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You meet a {tooltip:Radical:woman} from another {tooltip:Radical:clan} under the rising {tooltip:Radical:sun} to prepare for {tooltip:Kanji:marriage}. Your clan and her clan are standing together as the two of you watch the sun rise together.",
            "hints": "Marriage is a big deal and it's going to connect your two clans, so you have to do the ceremony in the sun in front of everyone so they can see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Marriage"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Do you want to go through with this marriage? You better hope you see a condor then! It's the official bird of love and unification, ya know. That's why so many people wait until they're older to get married these days, because there aren't as many condors thanks to deforestation.",
                "mnemonic": "For the {tooltip:Kanji:marriage} to be official, you need to wait for a {tooltip:Reading:con}dor ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3093}) to appear. If it doesn't show up before the sun goes down again, the marriage was a failure. You have to try again tomorrow with a different woman."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:soul} will {tooltip:Radical:cross} through your body and into the {tooltip:Radical:net} of your {tooltip:Radical:clothes} so that you'll be hit with {tooltip:Kanji:nostalgia} when you wear them again. Nostalgia for all the things that happened every single time you wore those clothes.",
            "hints": "When you put on an old piece of clothing, a shirt maybe, or some pants, feel the nostalgia that was embedded in it and left there by your soul.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Nostalgia"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel these nostalgic knots inside you. Now tie knots in the clothes that make you feel nostalgic so you don't wear them again.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:nostalgia} ties {tooltip:Reading:knots} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3064}) in your stomach and your chest. Even if the memories and feelings weren't particularly bad, there's something about the wistful feeling of nostalgia that knots up your insides."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You put your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} and an {tooltip:Radical:ear} on a {tooltip:Radical:stool} in the {tooltip:Radical:sun} so you can get your {tooltip:Kanji:photograph} taken. This is a glamour {tooltip:Kanji:photo}, so you have to be in one of these weird, cheesy poses for it to come out jusssst right.",
            "hints": "Imagine putting your fingers and your ear on a stool, now try to relax your head a little bit, and smile for the camera. This is a professional photograph, so you better do what you're told!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Photograph",
                "Alternative": "Photo"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
