{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:float}ing {tooltip:Kanji:world} {tooltip:Kanji:painting} is what you call an {tooltip:Vocabulary:ukiyo-e woodblock print} in Japan. The \"floating world\" refers to an evanescent world that is impermanent (floating), just as beauty and entertainment is. Back in the day, this type of art was made into woodblock prints and paintings. Unfortunately, we don't have a name for these in English because they're so unique and special, but they come up more than you'd think, so get used to ukiyo-e!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ukiyo-e",
                "Alternatives": "Ukiyo-e Woodblock Print, Ukiyo-e Painting",
                "Word Type": "noun"
            },
            "vocabReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "primary": true,
                        "reading": "\u3046\u304d\u3088\u3048"
