            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There\u2019s a {tooltip:Radical:comb} and what looks like the {tooltip:Radical:same} {tooltip:Radical:comb}, and you found them on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} next to some {tooltip:Radical:fins} you showed {tooltip:Kanji:interest} in. At first, the shiny fins on the ground caught your interest, but once you got closer to the fins you also noticed a pair of combs that are interesting too.",
            "hints": "Pick up these fins and the two combs. Feel their weight in each hand as you examine them with interest. Smell the fish smell and feel the teeth on the combs.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Interest"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046, \u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You've always had an interest in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}, so it makes sense that you'd be interested in things from {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} too.",
                "mnemonic": "Since the combs {tooltip:Kanji:interest} you more than the fins, you examine the combs more closely. Taking interest in where they were made, you discover they were made in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. Dang, {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} sure does make some nice combs."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you have a {tooltip:Radical:big} {tooltip:Radical:mouth} but a good {tooltip:Radical:heart}, people will recognize your {tooltip:Kanji:kindness}. Even if you blabber on with your big mouth, as long as everyone knows that your heart is filled with kindness, they will love and accept you.",
            "hints": "Share your kindness with the world. Use your big mouth to let people know what you\u2019re doing. \u201cI\u2019M TAKING OUT THE TRASH AND NOBODY EVEN ASKED ME!\u201d Y\u2019know, that sort of thing. Go ahead and say that out loud a few times.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Kindness"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine chopping up these onions. Smell the onion smell in the air as your eyes begin to sting from the onions. Your friend had better appreciate this kindness.",
                "mnemonic": "To further show your {tooltip:Kanji:kindness}, you chop up some {tooltip:Reading:on}ions ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u3093}) for a friend who always cries when they chop onions. The onions make you cry too, so it\u2019s a nice act of kindness that you\u2019re toughing it out for your pal."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you use a {tooltip:Radical:slide} to {tooltip:Radical:enter} a building, you'll be sliding for a {tooltip:Kanji:long time}.",
            "hints": "Imagine a never-ending slide that goes deep down inside a building. You can't see anything in the dark around you, you just plunge down and slide forever. And forever is a long time, my friend.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Long Time"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046, \u304f",
