                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine this group of Vikings rampaging through {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. See all the Japanese people running away and screaming as the group of Vikings comes busting in, swinging their axes and shouting loudly.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:party} has decided to raid {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. It\u2019s a large undertaking, but they have a large group of Vikings on the job. {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} doesn\u2019t stand a chance."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the {tooltip:Radical:canopy} comes {tooltip:Radical:beforehand}, it's a {tooltip:Kanji:preface} for the rest of the canopy.",
            "hints": "Although not necessarily a book preface, you can imagine a book made out of canvas pages. The canvas pages that came beforehand (i.e. in the beginning, before the book started) is the preface.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Preface"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
