                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Look at Zazu asking the turkeys random questions about miscellaneous trivia. You\u2019ve seen the Lion King, right? Zazu should be pretty easy to visualize here.",
                "mnemonic": "As if things couldn\u2019t get any more {tooltip:Kanji:random}, {tooltip:Reading:Zazu} ({span:lang=ja:\u3056\u3064}) from the Lion King flies into the tree and starts asking the nine turkeys {tooltip:Kanji:miscellaneous} trivia. Zazu always did have a thirst for knowledge, but this is kind of strange."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under a {tooltip:Radical:tree} sitting on the {tooltip:Radical:grass} is a {tooltip:Radical:woman} who loves {tooltip:Kanji:sakura}, or {tooltip:Kanji:cherry tree}, if you\u2019re an English speaker. This woman really likes to just chill out in the grass under these cherry trees and watch the sakura blossoms. It\u2019s very pretty.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself sitting under the tree in the grass with the woman. Smell the cherries and see the sakura blossoms falling down all around you. How whimsical.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sakura",
                "Alternatives": "Cherry Tree, Cherry Blossom"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3046, \u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u304f\u3089",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Sakura means cherry tree and sakura is the way to pronounce this kanji. Easy!",
                "mnemonic": "How do you say {tooltip:Kanji:cherry tree} in Japanese? {tooltip:Reading:Sakura} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u304f\u3089}). {tooltip:Kanji:Sakura} is Japanese for cherry tree. I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve probably heard this before, so it shouldn\u2019t be too hard to remember."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:roof} of a {tooltip:Radical:certain} {tooltip:Radical:mountain} shrouds its contents in {tooltip:Kanji:secrecy}.",
            "hints": "I can't even tell you which mountain it is, nor how to get in. That's what secrecy is all about.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Secrecy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
