                        "reading": "\u304d\u3073, \u304a\u3054\u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh Genji, if only you were as strict about using protection as you were on your elf child.",
                "mnemonic": "One of the {tooltip:Kanji:strict} parents of this elf kid is... {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093})?! Looks like he had another illegitimate kid... this time with an elf."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you're at your {tooltip:Radical:cottage} the only thing you do with your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} is {tooltip:Kanji:throw away} things. The cottage is for vacation. And vacation means being as lazy as possible. But you certainly don't want to live in filth, so you have to throw away your trash at least.",
            "hints": "Imagine sitting in your cottage. You throw away a banana peel. You throw away some used suntan lotion. You throw away all your cares in the world.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Throw Away"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3083",
