                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You're really happy this cat pirate welcomes gay people aboard. Whether that's because you're gay or just because you're a baseline decent human being is up to you.{splitParent}Also if you aren't the kind of person who would welcome gay people onto your cat pirate ship, you should just leave nyaow.",
                "mnemonic": "The cat pirate then launches into a speech about how they {tooltip:Kanji:welcome} all kinds of people. Especially {tooltip:Reading:gay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3044}) people. He puts a certain emphasis on gay, so you figure that the cat pirate either thinks you're gay or wants you to be."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:leader} has a {tooltip:Radical:gun} it's {tooltip:Radical:easy} to {tooltip:Kanji:wound} people. When you have a gun and a lot of responsibility it's easy to get carried away and mess up, wounding the people you were supposed to be protecting. You can even wound yourself.",
            "hints": "Picture how easy it would be for the leader of your country to wound someone if they had a gun. Scary, right?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wound"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
