                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3084\u3064, \u307f\u3055\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What happens to your soul, you ask? It gets covered in syrup. That's probably where the syrup fingers phrase came from in the first place.",
                "mnemonic": "If you want to {tooltip:Kanji:manipulate} someone else it's going to have a permanent effect on your {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}). Being manipulative isn't cool. And your soul will suffer forever for it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:bamboo} absorbed the {tooltip:Radical:moon}'s {tooltip:Radical:power}, and you want that power in your body, so you surgically insert them into your body to replace your {tooltip:Kanji:muscle}s and {tooltip:Kanji:tendon}s.",
            "hints": "Picture your new bamboo muscles glowing under your skin with the moon's power. You flex and feel the power coursing through you!",
