                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If someone who looks a little drunk comes up to you and starts with {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u308f\u3055}, there is a 100% chance what follows is gossip.",
                "mnemonic": "When you start to tell a {tooltip:Kanji:rumor} or spread {tooltip:Kanji:gossip}, you're a little drunk, so you slur you words. \"{tooltip:Reading:Ooo I saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u308f\u3055})...\" is how you start every rumor. It's got some southern drawl to it almost (Uuuwahsahw)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you grind a {tooltip:Radical:stone} down to more than just a {tooltip:Radical:few} pieces, it will become {tooltip:Kanji:sand}. Stones that get broken up enough will become sand, and you pick up a few grains in your hand.",
            "hints": "Feel these few grains of sand between your fingertips. Imagine the stones that they originally came from. Nature is crazy.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sand"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055, \u3057\u3083",
