                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Just remember that stones become sand and if you remember that this kanji means sand you\u2019ll remember how to pronounce it as well.",
                "mnemonic": "What\u2019s in your hand? A few grains of {tooltip:Reading:sa}nd ({span:lang=ja:\u3055})! {tooltip:Kanji:Sand}, sand, sand!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Keeping at a {tooltip:Radical:bamboo} {tooltip:Radical:interval} is the definition of {tooltip:Kanji:simplicity}. ",
            "hints": "Just one bamboo wide, over and over. That is simplicity.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Simplicity"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Simplicity is how he took over so much of the world. If he didn't stick to simplicity, there's no way he'd have been able to do what he did. ",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Simplicity} is what Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) always demanded. Everything he decided was based on simplicity."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you take the {tooltip:Radical:flowers} off some {tooltip:Radical:coral} and {tooltip:Radical:boil} them, {tooltip:Kanji:steam} comes out.",
            "hints": "Steam comes out of the coral flowers because they hold a lot of water. They're flowers, but they're coral flowers, so they came from the ocean. Of course there's water in them, and if you boil that water steam will come out.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Steam"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's weird that Jourm is so sensitive to the smell of steaming coral. He's lived as a farmhand nowhere near the sea all his life... at least that's what he told you. And now he's in your house breathing in the steam really deeply with his nose practically in the pot.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the {tooltip:Kanji:steam} coming off the coral flowers, someone appears behind you. It is {tooltip:Reading:Jou}rm ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087\u3046}), the big farmhand. \"Are you steaming coral?\" he asks. \"Smelled it a mile away. I love crunching me some coral.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:storehouse} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:storehouse} kanji meanings are the same. If you know the radical, you know the kanji!",
            "hints": "Your brain is like a storehouse, you know? Hopefully that's where you kept your storehouse knowledge.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Storehouse"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
