                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself as Sherlock Holmes, you inferred your way to freedom, swinging away on a conveniently-placed vine.",
                "mnemonic": "You were able to {tooltip:Kanji:infer} the turkey's plan, so now it's your turn. You look around and see the only way out... is to {tooltip:Reading:swi}ng ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3044}) to safety! How did I infer that, dear Watson? Why, isn't it obvious! There are vines here. Turkeys can't fly. So I shall swing my way to freedom!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:moon} {tooltip:Radical:storehouse} is another storehouse you own. Remember how your regular storehouse holds zombies (from the kanji {span:lang=ja:\u8535}?). Your moon storehouse is on the moon, and it is filled with {tooltip:Kanji:internal organs}.",
            "hints": "Your moon storehouse has internal organs because 1) you have to keep them far away from the zombies or they'll go berserk, and 2) you think it's funny to see them bounce around in low gravity. Boing, boing, boing, haha look at that internal organ.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Internal Organs"
