                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: What is most {tooltip:Vocabulary:valuable} to you? Of course it's your {tooltip:Reading:toe toe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u3068}). It's your big toe (the long {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046}) with another small toe growing out of it (short {span:lang=ja:\u3068}). Imagine your toe toe, and then imagine how valuable it is to you. So valuable! You can also think about {span:lang=ja:\u5c0a\u3044}, a similar word which means \"revered.\" It's a similar idea, and it has the same reading.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u547d\u3063\u3066\u306e\u306f\u30d9\u30fc\u30b3\u30f3\u3068\u540c\u3058\u304f\u3089\u3044\u8cb4\u3044\u3082\u306e\u306a\u3093\u3060\u3088\u3002",
