                "hints": "\nSee this eagle as it comes to deliver your order just for your sake. Scree! Hear its wings flap and your package plop down on your porch as it's delivered.",
                "mnemonic": "For the {tooltip:Kanji:sake} of convenience, companies will use {tooltip:Reading:ea}gles ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) for delivery jobs in the future. Just put in an order, and it'll be at your doorstep in no time flat. Eagles are like, super fast at delivery."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:ear} listens to your {tooltip:Radical:heart} and feels {tooltip:Kanji:shame}. Your heart is full of shame for how you\u2019ve lived your life and when your ear hears all the things you\u2019ve done, your ear feels shame too.",
            "hints": "Feel the shame. Feel the shame in both your ear and your heart. Imagine the things you\u2019ve done to make you feel so much shame.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shame"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f, \u306f\u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You\u2019re super embarrassed for bringing so much shame on yourself again. But then you think of another joke. \u201cHahaha!\u201d Better luck with the next Haj, I guess.",
                "mnemonic": "You must cleanse your spirit of this {tooltip:Kanji:shame}. You decide to complete {tooltip:Reading:Haj} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3058}). (Haj is the fifth pillar of Islam, and is a pilgrimage to Mecca during the month of Dhu al-Hijja). Upon arrival in Mecca, you think of a funny joke and bust out laughing. \u201c{tooltip:Reading:HA}HAHAHAHAHA!! ({span:lang=ja:\u306f}) HAHAHAHAHA!!!\u201d Oh man, you\u2019re in a temple and that was completely inappropriate. You feel even more shame than before."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Next to the {tooltip:Radical:scooter}, there's a {tooltip:Radical:flag} warning you that there are {tooltip:Radical:sheep} around here, so you should go {tooltip:Kanji:slow}.",
            "hints": "It's also a warning to the sheep that if they want to ride scooters they should also slow down, because as we all know, sheep are speed demons.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Slow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
