                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "So of all the boats out there, generally all of them have weapons, and generally Han Solo will be on one.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Generally} a boat with a weapon will be owned by {tooltip:Reading:Han} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}) Solo. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} comes, the {tooltip:Radical:brush} makes a good safe {tooltip:Kanji:haven}. Thick brush is a haven from tsunamis because the brush will break the tsunami water and keep you safe and dry.",
            "hints": "Imagine being in the haven of a brush while a tsunami strikes. Hear the water crash and rush all around you while you remain safe in your haven.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Haven"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Since there is room for two people in the brush, imagine yourself in the haven with one other person. They and you make two. The other person is a real whiner though - imagine them crying the whole time.",
                "mnemonic": "The only downside about this {tooltip:Kanji:haven} is that there\u2019s only room for {tooltip:Reading:two} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064}) people in the brush. The brush isn\u2019t big enough for more than two people, so unless you have a lot of brush, you won\u2019t be saving many people from the tsunami."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If someone is {tooltip:Radical:sick} feed them {tooltip:Radical:charcoal} to {tooltip:Kanji:heal} them. Okay, so maybe you shouldn't feed it directly to them, but charcoal has amazing water filtration powers. So put charcoal in their water and the water will heal them right up.",
            "hints": "Imagine being sick. Like sick as a dog sick. And then you take some charcoal, put it into your drinking water, and then you're healed!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Heal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself rowing your row boat into the lake with huge chunks of solid charcoal. You carefully break them up and toss them over the side, so you can heal everyone.",
                "mnemonic": "You aren't the only one that needs to be {tooltip:Kanji:heal}ed, so you take your {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat out onto the lake where your town gets its drinking water and you dump a bunch of charcoal into it! Now everyone will be healed when they drink."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "With a {tooltip:Radical:thread}, a {tooltip:Radical:lion} sews together all the {tooltip:Radical:rice} he'll {tooltip:Kanji:inherit} from his parents one day. He's convinced his parents are going to try to keep some of his inheritance from him, so he's linking it all together so it can't go anywhere.",
            "hints": "Picture this lion surrounded by the thousands of grains of rice he'll inherit from his parents. He's carefully threading them all together.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Inherit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I'd much rather inherit a cake than a ton of hard to keep track of rice, like this poor lion.",
                "mnemonic": "If you're going to {tooltip:Kanji:inherit} something from your parents, try to convince them to make it {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}), not rice. A single cake is much easier to keep track of and probably tastier (though it will be super stale by the time they die)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you go on a {tooltip:Radical:scooter}, anything {tooltip:Radical:valuable}, you need to {tooltip:Kanji:leave behind}.",
            "hints": "Rings, necklaces, wallets, phones? Don't take them on a scooter. Leave behind all that valuable stuff!",
