                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading for this vocabulary is the same as the reading you learned with the kanji. But! Some explanation about when to use {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3051} versus {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3083\u3051}.\n{splitParent}They're both technically right. But, typically when you refer to the living animal, you use {span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3051}, and when you refer to salmon as a food, it's more likely to be {span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3083\u3051} (but it can go either way). There might be some generational and regional differences, though.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
