                "hints": "Imagine yourself as you back away from the explosion. As you back away, see the fire dance and feel the heat of the explosion on your face.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the fire {tooltip:Kanji:explode}, you start to {tooltip:Reading:back} ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u304f}) away. I don\u2019t blame you. You need to back away or else you\u2019ll get caught in the violent explosion. Back away a little more just to be safe."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're holding a {tooltip:Radical:flag} on a {tooltip:Radical:stick} above your {tooltip:Radical:eye}s to imitate {tooltip:Kanji:eyebrows}. You can't grow any of your own, but you really love eyebrows, so this was the best you could do.",
            "hints": "Look at yourself in the mirror. You can see the stick holding up the flag and it's very clear you drew some eyebrows onto the flag with some markers, but you still look pretty good (in your opinion).",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Eyebrows"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f, \u3073",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3086",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine walking around town, holding your eyebrow flags. You can feel the meat sticking above your eyes. They stink and they're weirdly lukewarm, but you know your real eyebrows will grow under them any day now.",
                "mnemonic": "Underneath your fake {tooltip:Kanji:eyebrows} are two slabs of {tooltip:Reading:me}at ({span:lang=ja:\u307f}). Meat helps hair grow, according to many Internet specialists who also happen to sell meat. You're waiting for this meat to foster eyebrow hair, and when that sweet day comes you won't need these flags."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You carry a {tooltip:Radical:cross} across a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} with a {tooltip:Radical:heart} on it to return a {tooltip:Kanji:favor} for your friend. The heart needs to be purified so that\u2019s why you have it on the cross and your friend lives on a rice paddy farm so that\u2019s why you\u2019re running through that. The favor you are paying your friend back with is getting him this heart. He needs a new one and you\u2019re providing it.",
            "hints": "This is a pretty big favor. Imagine running through a rice paddy carrying a cross with a warm beating heart on it. Thump thump. Thump thump.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Favor"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048, \u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3050",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine how dumb you feel at this miscommunication. Eh? You don\u2019t feel dumb? Well you should!",
                "mnemonic": "You arrive at your friend\u2019s place and you can finally return the {tooltip:Kanji:favor} you owe him by presenting him with the heart. \u201c{tooltip:Reading:Eh} ({span:lang=ja:\u3048})? What\u2019s this? I didn\u2019t ask for this!\u201d \u201cEh!?!?\u201d you reply. Apparently he didn\u2019t want a real heart, he wanted a candy one. He wanted a Valentine!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} pushes all the {tooltip:Radical:fish} closer to land, making for some easy {tooltip:Kanji:fishing}. The tsunami starts out in the middle of the ocean and pushes all the fish towards the coast where everyone does their fishing. With all the fish pushed closer to land and closer together, it\u2019s very easy for people to go fishing in one spot and catch a lot of fish.",
            "hints": "Imagine going fishing for fish in a fishing spot after a tsunami. There are SO many fish here. Your hook barely touches the water and there\u2019s already a fish on it. Man, fishing like this is easy! Smell the smell of fish and sea air around you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fishing"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e\u3087, \u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Go! Go row! Go and row for the fishing! How do you go? You row! The row part should be pretty easy to remember since you gotta row your boat out to sea, but if you\u2019re having trouble with the go part, just remember that it has the same reading as {span:lang=ja:\u9b5a}.",
                "mnemonic": "To get to the best {tooltip:Kanji:fishing} spot you need to {tooltip:Reading:go} ({span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3087}) {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) out to the middle of the ocean. You go by means of rowing. To get to the fish and do the fishing, you need to go and row out to sea."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Grain} left in the {tooltip:Radical:sun} blossom and give off a wonderful {tooltip:Kanji:fragrance}. They smell fresh and delicious. There's nothing better than the fragrance of fresh, sun-kissed grain.",
            "hints": "Imagine this warm, grain fragrance. What does it smell like to you? Cooked rice? Gentle flowers? A warm summer's day?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fragrance"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046, \u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304a, \u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This fragrance was {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}'s armpits the whole time. You thought it was warm grains. Or... maybe he smells like... grains?",
                "mnemonic": "As you sniff this lovely {tooltip:Kanji:fragrance} you get lost in the smell. When you open your eyes again, you see a farming {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} standing in front of you. With... his... arm... up. \"Do you like my fragrance? I was genetically modified to have a unique fragrance compared to the other {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} dug out a chunk of the land and now it looks like a big {tooltip:Radical:red} {tooltip:Radical:bow}. It's a {tooltip:Kanji:gulf} now!",
            "hints": "Picture all the famous gulfs you learned about in geography class. Most of them look like someone pressed a bow into them and dug out the land. (And just imagine they're red because the earth is bleeding, making the sand red.)",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gulf"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch one tsunami come in and cut out a chunk of land, leaving behind a big, red gulf.",
                "mnemonic": "How many tsunamis does it take to make a {tooltip:Kanji:gulf}? Just {tooltip:Reading:one} ({span:lang=ja:\u308f\u3093}). If there were more, then no land would be left behind. It would all be taken into the sea."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:foot} heard an {tooltip:Radical:omen} and now it's making you {tooltip:Kanji:hop} over things.",
            "hints": "Imagine your foot hearing this omen, \"If you step on a crack, you'll break your mother's back.\" Now your foot hops over all of the tiny cracks in the street and the sidewalk and you look really silly.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hop"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068, \u306f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you're hopping away in fear from Mrs. Chou!",
                "mnemonic": "As you hop you start to hear an awful scream coming down the street. It's Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}) and she's running straight for you yelling, \"STEP ON MY STREET'S CRACKS! STOP HOPPING OR YOUR MOTHER WILL NEVER BREAK HER BACK!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} and {tooltip:Radical:wrap} them around another person. This is called a {tooltip:Kanji:hug}. Just make sure you include all the stuff attached to your fingers, like your hands and arms too, otherwise it's more of a squeeze, and we don't want to do that to people.",
            "hints": "Picture it like you're a baby who is new to hugs. You start with your fingers, spread them out and move forward. Now wrap all that stuff attached to your fingers around another person. You did it! You're hugging now!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hug"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060, \u304b\u304b, \u3044\u3060",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine getting a nice, big hug from your dad. Mm. It's cozy and feels like home.",
                "mnemonic": "Who do you love to {tooltip:Kanji:hug} the most? Your {tooltip:Reading:da}d ({span:lang=ja:\u3060})! He gives the best hugs. They're warm and big and tight and comforting. The kind of hug dads are really good at giving."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put the {tooltip:Radical:sun} in {tooltip:Radical:prison} and everything will always be {tooltip:Kanji:in season}. If the sun is in prison, the seasons can't change. Want to wear a giant weenie costume all year round? Put the sun in prison on Halloween. Now your weenie body is always in season because it's always the same {tooltip:Kanji:time of month}.",
            "hints": "You're welcome. Now you know how to keep everything in season. Lifehack!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "In Season",
                "Alternatives": "Time Of Month, Season"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3093, \u3058\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Jokes on them though. Halloween will be in season forever now. Soon it will be Halloween. Soon it will be time for candy. Soon June will end and people will forget about everything else.",
                "mnemonic": "When things are {tooltip:Kanji:in season} for too long, people are going to wonder what's going on. When's Christmas? When's Golden Week? {tooltip:Reading:Soon} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3093}), you say. Soon enough, it's {tooltip:Reading:June} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3093}) which is the middle of the year so everything is soon."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Radical:ear} is {tooltip:Radical:cross}ed with sound, it catches it like a {tooltip:Radical:net}, and sends it to your {tooltip:Radical:heart} for processing. Because you're using your heart to process this sound, it means you're giving it a proper {tooltip:Kanji:listen}.",
            "hints": "Imagine the whole process of sound going through your ear and to your heart, then the gears turning to really understand what someone is saying. It's a real listen, not a fake non-heart listen.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Listen"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Focus on listening, and focus on their message about Mrs. Chou. Feel afraid about the future because of it.",
                "mnemonic": "You are {tooltip:Kanji:listen}ing so well to what someone is saying. What are they telling you that is so important? They are telling you of the omen of Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}), who will destroy the earth."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You give your {tooltip:Radical:servant} a {tooltip:Radical:gun} along with some other {tooltip:Radical:products} to {tooltip:Kanji:look to}. You can\u2019t look to them yourself since you are very busy. You allow your servant to look to your gun and the other products.",
            "hints": "Imagine your servant as he looks to your gun and products. You can always look to him to take care of your menial tasks. You feel smug.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Look To"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e\u305e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine your servant as he looks to your car\u2019s o-ring. Hear him clinking and clanking around in the garage as he does so.",
                "mnemonic": "After your servant is done with your gun and other products you want him to {tooltip:Kanji:look to} your car\u2019s o-{tooltip:Reading:rin}g ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3093}). There\u2019s something wrong with the o-ring so you want your servant to look to that as well."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:omen} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:omen} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "If you know the omen radical, you know the omen kanji as well!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Omen"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3056",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You can clarify with the person telling you the omen several things: \"Do you believe in the omen about Mrs. Chou destroying the world?\" \"When will this omen about Mrs. Chou come true?\" etc. As long as you're associating omen with Mrs. Chou you should be good, so keep harping on that.{splitParent}Anyway, whenever you hear any kind of omen (omen is a radical in the kanji), there's a good chance it's going to be about Mrs. Chou.",
                "mnemonic": "You listen to the {tooltip:Kanji:omen}, in it, it tells of an event in the future when Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}) will destroy the world."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The weight of {tooltip:Radical:life} on your {tooltip:Radical:sword} is {tooltip:Radical:big} when you {tooltip:Kanji:pledge} to protect your city. That's the big, big weight of every single person's life in that city pressing down on you every time you take out that sword.",
            "hints": "Imagine holding up your sword and pledging to protect the lives of everyone in this city. It's a big deal!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pledge"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Would you pledge to give up cake to show everyone how serious you are about protecting life?",
                "mnemonic": "Until the city is safe, you {tooltip:Kanji:pledge} to give up {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}), your favorite food."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Destroy a {tooltip:Radical:lantern} with your {tooltip:Radical:knife} and you'll be {tooltip:Kanji:punish}ed.",
            "hints": "Even if it was your own lantern, why stab it with a knife? You could have recycled that. I will punish you for lantern stabbing and pollution!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Punish"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The next time you want to stab a lantern with a knife, think about how good cake tastes and stop. Remember, DARE (Don't Attack Reusable Electronics)!",
                "mnemonic": "I will {tooltip:Kanji:punish} you by taking away your {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044})! You'll never eat cake again. Not for birthdays, not for holidays. This is your punishment."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:greenhouse} is the newest {tooltip:Radical:power} of the city you decided to {tooltip:Kanji:recruit}. You\u2019re trying to recruit all the buildings in town and the greenhouse was the next on your list. It adds just a little bit of power to the town, but it's important nonetheless.",
            "hints": "Imagine what you had to do to recruit this greenhouse. Imagine schmoozing with the previous greenhouse owners to recruit them to your cause and sell you the greenhouse.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Recruit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Recruit Bobo the clown. Look at him. He\u2019s terrifying. Bobo will make for a great deterrent for entry to your greenhouse.",
                "mnemonic": "After you {tooltip:Kanji:recruit} the greenhouse, you recruit {tooltip:Reading:Bo}bo ({span:lang=ja:\u307c}) the clown to guard it for you. Bobo the clown has a terrifying amount of power so he\u2019ll make an excellent guard for the greenhouse."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} presents you with a {tooltip:Radical:prize} as {tooltip:Kanji:reparation} for his past deeds. This leader wronged you in the past and wishes to make amends. Therefore the leader presents you with a reparation in the form of a glittering prize.",
            "hints": "Imagine receiving your reparation prize. Feel the prize in your hand. It\u2019s all wrapped up but it\u2019s heavy and feels expensive. What could it be?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reparation"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3050\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine receiving your reparations from the Shougun himself. You're angry at him for threatening you, wounding people, and cutting off the heads of people who go against him, but you take it anyway.",
                "mnemonic": "The leader who presented you with this {tooltip:Kanji:reparation} is the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) of Japan. He's trying to make up for all the threats he made to you and some of the things you saw (which he's now trying to cover up for)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Everyone from your {tooltip:Radical:clan} puts their {tooltip:Radical:fingers} in the {tooltip:Radical:ground} as a way to {tooltip:Kanji:resist} their lords. Your clan is made of a bunch of peasants, but you aren't going to work the land for other people anymore. You're going to resist. This is a protest! Your fingers work for no one but yourselves from now on!",
            "hints": "Imagine your entire clan putting their fingers in the ground in unison as a form of resistance. It's a moving sight.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Resist"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You make your choice to resist. He orders his guards to pull your fingers out of the ground, chop them into the size of tater tots, and then deep fry them. After they're done, the lord pops one in his mouth and says, \"Oooh, resistance is delicious.\"",
                "mnemonic": "You're all {tooltip:Kanji:resist}ing with your fingers in the ground, when the lords appear, angry. \"You resist us by hiding your fingers with potatoes in the ground?! You want your fingers to be useless potatoes so badly? We'll chop them up and turn them into {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:door} is {tooltip:Radical:big} and you need to {tooltip:Kanji:return} it to its rightful owner. This door is too big and important looking to not belong to someone. You need to find its owner and return it to them.",
            "hints": "Heft this big door in your arms. It\u2019s very heavy. Feel your arms tire as you look for who to return the door to.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Return"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3069",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You\u2019re obsessed with returning this big door. Once you enter this mode, the only way to get out is to return the thing you have.",
                "mnemonic": "You are in {tooltip:Kanji:return} {tooltip:Reading:mode} ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3069}). When you enter this mode, you concentrate only on returning something. Nothing else matters in this mode. You\u2019re in full on return mode."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} {tooltip:Radical:call}s out to the earth by {tooltip:Kanji:shining} down on it.",
            "hints": "The sun doesn't have a voice, unfortunately, so it calls out the only way it can, with its shining rays.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shining"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the Shougun standing in the shining sunlight. He's so bright and beautiful!",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:shining} is aimed directly at the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). The sun is shining on the Shougun to not only show its support for his leadership, but to let him shine brighter than anyone else in Japan."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:skewer} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:skewer} kanji are exactly the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals, yo.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Skewer",
                "Alternative": "Spit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
