                "hints": "Imagine trying to use this cushy skewer. It's the right shape (long, thin, pointy at one end), but every time you try to put something on it it squishes in on itself like a long marshmallow.",
                "mnemonic": "Uh oh, this {tooltip:Kanji:skewer} is really... {tooltip:Reading:cushy} ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3057}). It's so soft and cushy you can't get any meat or vegetables onto it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "At this {tooltip:Radical:gate} you're trying to get some {tooltip:Radical:beans} through, but the {tooltip:Radical:measurements} were off and you're starting to {tooltip:Kanji:struggle}. No matter how you push or pull these beans, they're just too big to get through the gate.",
            "hints": "\"I'm really struggling here, I thought you said you measured these beans?\" you ask the bean seller. \"I did! I mean, I struggled with the measurements, I'm not very good at math...\" Ugh.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Struggle"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u305f\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"How am I supposed to sell my beans if you struggle this much just to get them into {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}!\" the bean seller shouts. It's making you struggle more, and beans start falling on your head, ripping their way out of their sack.",
                "mnemonic": "You continue to {tooltip:Kanji:struggle} because you need to get these beans to the other side of the gate and into {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. You usually struggle a little when people want to bring things through the gate to {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}, but this is ridiculous."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Happiness} is a {tooltip:Radical:circle} that's {tooltip:Kanji:tenacious}. In other words, we're all in this circle/cycle where we do whatever we can to grab onto happiness and hold it as tightly as we can.",
            "hints": "Be tenacious about happiness in your life. No matter how many times it slips away, don't give up. Keep going after it, because it will absolutely come back if you're tenacious enough.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tenacious"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046, \u3057\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Will someone take the shoe sometimes? Yeah, but the shih tzu doesn't give up. That's how you need to be with happiness. Kids, be tenacious!",
                "mnemonic": "Happiness is as {tooltip:Kanji:tenacious} as a {tooltip:Reading:shih tzu} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3064}) with a {tooltip:Reading:shoe} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}). That little dog does not want to give up on the shoe, no matter what's happening around it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:foot} is a little {tooltip:Radical:red} and you can see {tooltip:Kanji:traces} of ink streaked on it. Where did these traces come from?",
            "hints": "You look closer at your foot, examining the traces of red ink, and slowly the night before comes back to you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Traces"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
