                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as clusters of pins fall when the bowling balls hit them. You back up and peek through one of the other doors in the cluster and it also houses a bowling alley. Huh.",
                "mnemonic": "After you make it through the door, you come across another {tooltip:Kanji:cluster} of doors. Which one to choose? There's a loud thunderous sound coming from behind one and you decide to open it. Behind it, there's an entire {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) alley and people bowling, loudly!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tiger} needs to {tooltip:Radical:think} and {tooltip:Kanji:consider} its actions before it attacks. Tigers are smart hunters, so they need to consider all options and really think through a situation.",
            "hints": "Look at this tiger as it approaches you. Think what things it has to consider. It has to consider how big of a threat you are and so on. You need to consider how you\u2019re going to escape from this tiger.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Consider"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082\u3093\u3071\u304f, \u304a\u3082\u3093\u3071\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Consider this! Tigers look great in robes.",
                "mnemonic": "It's {tooltip:Kanji:consider}ing you for so long that it takes out a {tooltip:Reading:ro}be ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087}), a pipe, and an armchair and starts puffing away, staring intently at you. You didn't even know tigers could wear robes, but this one seems to use it to help itself think."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "They {tooltip:Radical:say} if you put things on a {tooltip:Radical:slide}, {tooltip:Radical:seven} things to be exact, that\u2019s the best way to {tooltip:Kanji:consign} goods to someone. They say if you consign seven things to someone, you should send them over on a slide. Slide \u2018em on down. All seven of \u2018em.",
            "hints": "Imagine what seven things you consign over to this other person for safekeeping. Visualize them in your head as you slide each one down the slide.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Consign"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Let\u2019s imagine what it would be like to hit this tack while sliding on the slide. It would hurt. Good thing you are consigning it over to someone. Probably safer for everyone that way.",
                "mnemonic": "One of the seven things you {tooltip:Kanji:consign} over to this guy is a {tooltip:Reading:tack} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u304f}). It\u2019s the sharpest tack you\u2019ve ever seen. You slide the tack down the slide. Good thing no one is on the slide now, sitting on that tack would hurt."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Past} {tooltip:Radical:stamp}s usually depict images {tooltip:Kanji:contrary} to current views.",
            "hints": "Look at this stamp. There's Columbus being hugged by a bunch of South American natives. Yikes, that's contrary to how things went, that's for sure.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Contrary"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
