{
            "mnemonic": "When you see {tooltip:Radical:flowers} in a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} you can't help but use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to {tooltip:Kanji:draw} them. Have you ever seen rice paddy flowers? They're beautiful. And if you can draw them you can capture that beauty and show it to everyone.",
            "hints": "Imagine using your fingers to draw these rice paddy flowers. Don't worry about how well you can draw, this is so beautiful, anyone could capture it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Draw"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b, \u3048\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "To be fair, would you want to look at a drawing that makes you constantly smell stinky B.O.? I didn't think so.",
                "mnemonic": "Even though you tried to {tooltip:Kanji:draw} the flowers as best you could, whenever someone looks at it they smell {tooltip:Reading:B.O.} ({span:lang=ja:\u3073\u3087\u3046}). Maybe it's because you were drawing for a really long time and kept sweating. Maybe it's because you are just a stinky person. But no one wants to look at your drawing for long because all they can smell is B.O."
            }
        }

{
