                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the cape (the land mass that sticks out into water) but it's shaped just like your old cyborg. Weep a single tear.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:cape} below looks just like your {tooltip:Reading:cy}borg ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044}). Or rather, the cyborg you once had, before you had to give him up. It's kinda cross-shaped, it has a slide part, and lots of little fleshy bits. Ah, the memories."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tree} {tooltip:Radical:crab} breaks into your games cabinet and steals a {tooltip:Kanji:chess piece}. He\u2019s trying to impress all his tree crabs back home by showing how not afraid of humans he is. Plus the rest of the tree crabs need one last chess piece to complete their set.",
            "hints": "Imagine finding this tree crab in your games cabinet trying to make off with your chess piece. This tree crab is big and you weren\u2019t expecting to find it in your games cabinet so you\u2019re kind of terrified. You scream in horror.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chess Piece"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You put the key in your pocket and call animal control. They unlock the cabinet with the key and remove the tree crab from your home. But who\u2019s to say he won\u2019t be back??",
                "mnemonic": "Before the tree crab can make it out with the {tooltip:Kanji:chess piece}, you shut the door to the games cabinet and lock it with a {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}), trapping the tree crab inside. Now what?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Radical:say} \"{tooltip:Radical:Nurse}!\" you're ready to {tooltip:Kanji:defer} to them.",
            "hints": "If you say \"nurse\" you're asking something of a nurse. For this story, pretend like you don't know what to do, so you're going to defer to their skill and let them take over.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Defer"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u305a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It makes sense to defer to the knowledge of a medical professional. When going through this story, imagine yourself trying to revive Jourm, but nothing you do works. That's why you defer to the nurse. \"Save Jourm,\" you say. \"He's just a simple, kinda weird, ten foot tall farmhand with nine toes.\"",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:defer} to the nurse because you're trying to save the local farmhand, {tooltip:Reading:Jou}rm ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087\u3046}), and you can't do it. He's bleeding a lot, and you don't know what to do."
            }
        }

{
