                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this old hermit fighting this centaur in a duel. Who do you think is gonna win? Hear the hermit screaming in agony as the centaur demolishes him.",
                "mnemonic": "One day the {tooltip:Kanji:hermit} was leading the mountain goats around and he ran into a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur {span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}. The centaur said that he was the rightful leader of these mountain goats so the centaur challenged the hermit to a duel."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are {tooltip:Radical:three} {tooltip:Radical:slide}s sticking out of this {tooltip:Radical:building} that lead to your {tooltip:Kanji:home country}. The rest of the slides go to other places, but three are yours. ",
            "hints": "Imagine standing at the top of the building and looking down at the three slides that stretch off toward your home country. It takes a few hours to slide all the way there, but at the end you'll be home.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Home Country"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u306b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Even if you move, even if you haven't been back in years, your home country will always be your home in some way, deep down.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:home country} is your {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046})!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:loiter} around with a {tooltip:Radical:gun} while your friend tries to {tooltip:Radical:correct} a {tooltip:Radical:stamp} to make it more {tooltip:Kanji:honorable}. Someone messed with the stamp machine and your friend is trying to correct the error. You\u2019re loitering around with a gun since you\u2019re his bodyguard. To have an error on the stamp would not be honorable, so that\u2019s why your friend is going to correct it.",
            "hints": "Feel the weight of the gun in your hands as your friend works to make the stamp honorable again. Listen to your friend complain about how there are so few people left in the world that are honorable. Also keep in mind that the correct radical is a little different with the vertical line going through the top, so just think of that as the error trying to be corrected.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Honorable"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054, \u304e\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a, \u304a\u3093, \u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You run, leaving your friend and Godzilla to their honorable battle. A single tear runs down your cheek.",
                "mnemonic": "Just as you\u2019re pondering what it means to be {tooltip:Kanji:honorable}, your friend gets shot by {tooltip:Reading:Go}dzilla ({span:lang=ja:\u3054}). Godzilla must have been the one who ruined the stamp! \"Go, go, save yourself, Godzilla got me!\" your friend cries."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When someone wants to view the {tooltip:Radical:reality} of your {tooltip:Radical:soul}, show it with {tooltip:Kanji:humility}. Because the reality is... our souls are all a little dirty. And we haven't been the best versions we could be. So make sure when you show all of yourself you do so with some humility.",
            "hints": "Focus on the feeling of humility here. You're putting it all out there, you know? With nowhere to hide.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Humility"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3064\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine humility literally moving through your shins. Can you still stand or do you need to fall to your shins, in humility?",
                "mnemonic": "As {tooltip:Kanji:humility} washes over you, you feel a shaking in your {tooltip:Reading:shin}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}). Humility lives in your shins, so now they're shaking and trying to bring you down to the ground."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You use your {tooltip:Radical:foot} to kick {tooltip:Radical:Wolverine} in the face so a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} can {tooltip:Kanji:leap} to freedom. This turkey is trying to escape from Wolverine by leaping over a fence. Wolverine doesn\u2019t want the turkey to escape, but you kick him with your foot and the turkey is then free to leap to safety.",
            "hints": "Imagine kicking Wolverine in the head with your foot as the turkey makes turkey sounds in the background. He\u2019s taller than you so you must leap as you kick.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Leap"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3069",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Leap! Leap onto the yak. Feel the yak fur beneath you as you ride away to safety, wind in your hair.",
                "mnemonic": "After you kick Wolverine and the turkey is safe, you {tooltip:Kanji:leap} onto a {tooltip:Reading:yak} ({span:lang=ja:\u3084\u304f}) to make your getaway. This yak is really fast so you\u2019ll have no problem outrunning Wolverine while riding it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "They {tooltip:Radical:say} {tooltip:Radical:Mona Lisa} had more {tooltip:Kanji:modesty} than any other woman at the time.",
            "hints": "Leonardo da Vinci picked her for her modesty. She's so modest she shows no emotion.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Modesty"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Have you met Ken the samurai in person? He never smiles, and will never show you his emotions. He's too modest for that.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:modesty} of Mona Lisa inspired {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai to become more modest."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:drop} of rain falls on a {tooltip:Radical:bear} leaning up against a {tooltip:Radical:cross} stuck into a {tooltip:Kanji:mound}. The drop wakes the bear up and he rolls down off the mound. After the bear rights himself, he assumes that the cross pushed him off the mound so he charges into the cross atop the mound and knocks it over.",
            "hints": "Imagine this whole scene. A drop of water rouses the bear and he becomes enraged after he rolls down the mound. Hear the bear roar with anger as he charges up the mound and violently smashes the cross into the ground.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mound"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now look at the bear sitting atop the mound with his head in his paws, looking like a fool filled with regret. This bear feels like a fool for attacking the cross like he did.",
                "mnemonic": "Once the bear fully wakes up he realizes that he just rolled down the {tooltip:Kanji:mound} on his own and the cross was not to blame. What a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}) this bear was. He knows it too. The bear feels pretty foolish."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:one sided} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:one sided} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals, yo!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "One Sided"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a one sided situation that you've had. Now imagine the winning side with a catapult. For example, a baseball game where one team is destroying the other. That's because instead of a pitcher, they have a catapult.",
                "mnemonic": "Think of anything that is {tooltip:Kanji:one sided}. A battle. A sports game. A relationship. What makes them so one sided? One side always has a {tooltip:Reading:cata}pult ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u305f})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Construction} for {tooltip:Radical:geoduck}s doesn't require as much paperwork as construction for humans, but you still need to write at least a {tooltip:Kanji:paragraph} to explain what you're doing.",
            "hints": "Actually imagine yourself writing one paragraph of explanation to the city so you can get the permits to construct housing for your geoducks. On the form, it specifies you should only write a paragraph.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Paragraph"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "In that paragraph, you praised {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} for being a great emperor, and you said that this construction project would help you to have more time to do your WaniKani reviews. Clearly you were pandering to Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} when you wrote it. But hey, it worked!{splitParent}Hint: When you see {span:lang=ja:\u5de5} in a kanji it will often take the {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046} reading.",
                "mnemonic": "You turn in your {tooltip:Kanji:paragraph}, and it is given to Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, who insists on being involved in all construction projects. Surprisingly, he approves your construction project, thanks to that paragraph you wrote in the application."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Criminal} {tooltip:Radical:writing} is always {tooltip:Kanji:patterned}. That is to say, there is a pattern to it, lots of ARGS and GONNA STAB YAs, but it's also patterned beautifully, with a collage of cut out letters.",
            "hints": "Can you see the patterns in the writing this criminal did? It looks like a quilt or some plaid. It's almost beautiful, the way those death threats are arranged!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Patterned"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture an eagle patterned out of cut out letters. What the words say isn't important (though it is asking for a ransom on your grandma), but the underlying image is gorgeous.",
                "mnemonic": "As you look closer at the {tooltip:Kanji:patterned} writing you realize that it forms the shape of an {tooltip:Reading:eagle} ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}). The most American bird of them all! Maybe this guy isn't a criminal after all!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:building} in {tooltip:Radical:winter} will allow {tooltip:Radical:life} to have {tooltip:Kanji:prosperity}. Before we had buildings it was impossible to have any prosperity in winter because everything was cold and most of us died. ",
            "hints": "Picture a dark, bleak winter landscape. No life anywhere. Now turn around and look at the prosperity on display in the building you're in. Everyone is happy and eating food and not freezing to death.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Prosperity"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ryu's prosperity has made him realize that having things isn't always enough. Now he's looking wistfully outside at the winter weather, missing the rough times.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:prosperity} isn't good for everyone though. You look over and see Ryu ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3085\u3046}) from Street Fighter sitting in the corner. He's got everything he could ask for. He's won the tournament, he's got money, he's got this nice big building, but now he's depressed."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} contains a {tooltip:Radical:scroll}, which you pull out and look at. On the scroll is a map, showing the {tooltip:Kanji:range} of the {tooltip:Kanji:sphere} of your mouth.",
            "hints": "On the map, there is a circle drawn around your mouth showing what range your mouth exists in. Thankfully, your tongue and teeth are within that sphere.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Range",
                "Alternative": "Sphere"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Everything else on the map was accurate, so you take a close look in the mirror, and there he is: a tiny Ken the samurai, protecting the range that is your mouth. He gives you a small nod and goes back to his post.",
                "mnemonic": "Looking at the {tooltip:Kanji:range} of your mouth on the map, you notice a tiny samurai marked near your molars. It is {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There\u2019s an {tooltip:Radical:arrow} in that {tooltip:Radical:turkey} and you do everything in your {tooltip:Radical:power} to {tooltip:Kanji:recommend} that we don\u2019t eat the turkey. There\u2019s an arrow in this turkey. The arrow looks a little broken, so there\u2019s probably splinters all up inside that turkey. I know you\u2019re all hungry but I can\u2019t recommend eating this bird.",
            "hints": "You can\u2019t recommend this turkey. It\u2019s probably dangerous. Imagine sending this turkey back in a restaurant, very upset with everything. Also keep in mind that the arrow is half buried in the turkey and looks a little broken since the arrow radical is a bit off.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Recommend"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Welp, I guess if Genghis Khan recommends eating food with weapons still in them, you're okay with recommending it too. Eat up, everyone.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:recommend} the Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) special instead of this arrow-tainted turkey! When it comes out, your heart sinks. Genghis Khan apparently ate a cow with an arrow broken off in it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Show your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to a {tooltip:Radical:giant} to show you {tooltip:Kanji:refuse} him. Giants are very big. So big that when you talk they can't really hear what you're saying. Hold up all your fingers so that he can see what you mean.",
            "hints": "Imagine holding up your fingers to show a giant you're refusing to let him do something. Yeesh, you're brave!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Refuse",
                "Alternative": "Refusal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3070",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine standing in front of a giant, refusing to let him crush Little Kyoto. I hope he doesn't stomp on you instead.",
                "mnemonic": "What do you {tooltip:Kanji:refuse}? You refuse to let him stomp all over Little {tooltip:Reading:Kyo}to ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087}). Little Kyoto is your home! And if the giant comes any closer he's going to destroy all the little buildings and shrines and soba noodle shops."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:grain} stuck in your {tooltip:Radical:cleat} had a {tooltip:Radical:former} life. In that life it was a {tooltip:Kanji:rice plant}. It was a happy little rice plant, minding its own business, when it was yanked up and cleaned up and put in a bag for people to buy and cook and eat. That was so long ago. Now it's just a sad grain in the bottom of your shoe.",
            "hints": "When you look at a grain of rice, you should think of its former life as a rice plant, not where it ended up.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rice Plant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u306d, \u3044\u306a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You decide to bring the grain back to where all of the other rice plants are, and they all chant {span:lang=ja:\u3044\u306a\u3001\u3044\u306d} as you return it to its home. You did a good thing today.",
                "mnemonic": "The grain of rice, as it thinks about its {tooltip:Kanji:rice plant} life too, mutters, \"{span:lang=ja:\u3044\u306a\u3001\u3044\u306d}.\" Yes little grain, it was a really nice life. I'm sorry."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:big} {tooltip:Radical:turkey} has to {tooltip:Radical:measure} a safe before he can {tooltip:Kanji:rob} it. If the safe is too big it won\u2019t fit in his getaway van and the robbery will have been a failure. So before the turkey robs the place he needs to measure the safe.",
            "hints": "Imagine this turkey as he tries to rob this safe. See him with the tape measure as he determines whether or not the safe is too big.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Rob"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3070",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the size of this uber big safe. What could be inside? Probably something good.",
                "mnemonic": "The safe that the turkey is trying to {tooltip:Kanji:rob} ends up being {tooltip:Reading:uber} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3070}) big. Like, really uber big. So uber big that the turkey can\u2019t even measure it with his tape measure. There\u2019s no way he\u2019s gonna be able to rob this place."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You come across a {tooltip:Radical:gold} {tooltip:Radical:hill}. You think you hit it big! You start digging, only to find out that it is merely a paper-thin layer of gold covering a hill of {tooltip:Kanji:steel}.",
            "hints": "Dig out many other spots. Every time, it's just steel under there.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Steel"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304c\u306d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"I suppose I can use this steel, even if it is not a hill of gold,\" he says. \"We will make steel weapons, which we will use to subjugate other nations. The whole world will learn kanji using the WaniKani system!\"",
                "mnemonic": "You report your findings about the {tooltip:Kanji:steel} you found to Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. He is displeased that it is a hill of steel."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:turtle shell} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:turtle shell} kanji are exactly the same!",
            "hints": "Cowabunga!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Turtle Shell"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046, \u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Because this is WaniKani, {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} has probably set the turtle shell on fire, too. \"Burn those turtle shells, burn those kanji!\" he yells.",
                "mnemonic": "With a {tooltip:Kanji:turtle shell} on his back, imagine {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are {tooltip:Radical:hot peppers} hiding in this {tooltip:Radical:dirt}, so you build a {tooltip:Kanji:wall} to protect yourself from them. Have you ever stepped on a really hot pepper? The oils bleed into your shoes and burn your feet! You don't want anyone stepping on these so you wall them up.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself walking around and seeing a wall around some dirt. You look inside and there are some hot peppers hiding just below the surface. Phew! Good thing this wall was here to protect you from them. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wall"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3079",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture some corn cobs. Now picture some hot peppers. Put a wall between them.",
                "mnemonic": "On the other side of this {tooltip:Kanji:wall} there are much less threatening {tooltip:Reading:cob}s ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3079}) of corn. Corn isn't spicy. It's delicious and sweet, so it's free from being walled in."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:spirit} {tooltip:Radical:stop}s protecting you, you'll have to go on {tooltip:Kanji:welfare}. If you can't rely on your family spirit, you'll have to have the help and protection come from somewhere else.",
            "hints": "The next time you see someone on welfare, be nice. Their spirit stopped protecting them, so they need a little more help right now.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Welfare"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
