{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} have to {tooltip:Radical:stand} up straight, to protect you from being {tooltip:Kanji:abduct}ed, or {tooltip:Kanji:pull}ed away against your will.",
            "hints": "You're convinced someone is trying to abduct you, so you need to keep your fingers standing at all times, ready to defend yourself. Your fingers are feeling pretty stiff, but you still keep them standing, just in case.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Abduct",
                "Alternative": "Pull"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3089",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Luckily, your fingers were standing to attention and you were able to fight off the mighty Ra. He won't try to abduct you again in a hurry. Thank goodness for those standing fingers.",
                "mnemonic": "Suddenly, someone really is trying to {tooltip:Kanji:abduct} you. They're {tooltip:Kanji:pull}ling you away. It's the ancient Egyptian god {tooltip:Reading:Ra} ({span:lang=ja:\u3089}). Help!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Every} {tooltip:Radical:winter} you are {tooltip:Kanji:alert} for danger. Everyone knows that the worst monsters come out in the winter so you need to be alert if you want to survive.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself out in the winter wilderness. You hear twigs snapping, growling, leaves rustling. You\u2019re incredibly alert and aware of everything going on around you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Alert"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Listen to the sasquatch rumble on by as you continue to smell the smelly smells of this putrid bin you\u2019re in.",
                "mnemonic": "Being the {tooltip:Kanji:alert} fellow you are, you hear a sasquatch approaching and dive into a trash {tooltip:Reading:bin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3073\u3093}) to hide. The bin smells really bad and you are keenly alert to all the various stenches and smells currently penetrating your nostrils, but at least you are safe."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You attempt to expel wind out of your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} but {tooltip:Radical:lack} the breath to {tooltip:Kanji:blow} out any. You\u2019re using your mouth and trying to blow out some air, but you are failing to do so.",
            "hints": "Blow some air out of your mouth. It\u2019s easy, right? Imagine what could cause you to fail at this activity.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Blow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Attempt to blow air out of your mouth while covering it with your hand. It\u2019s hard to do, right? Only a fool would try to blow air out of their mouth this way.",
                "mnemonic": "You silly {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}), the reason you couldn\u2019t {tooltip:Kanji:blow} any air out of your mouth is because your hand was over it. You can\u2019t blow air out that way. You silly fool, you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "It's time to do the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} {tooltip:Radical:sun} {tooltip:Radical:sun} {tooltip:Kanji:chant}. That's when you use your mouth to chant sun sun, sun sun, sun sun, over and over until the sun appears.",
            "hints": "Open your mouth and practice the chant right now! Sun sun, sun sun, sun sun!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The Shougun is glaring intently at you as you chant. Open your mouth as wide as you can, get all those \"sun suns\" out, and pray that the sun will appear.",
                "mnemonic": "You're doing this {tooltip:Kanji:chant} because the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) ordered you to. The sun hasn't been shining on him as much lately, and he's displeased. So now you have to chant for him."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you try to {tooltip:Radical:go} somewhere but you're too {tooltip:Radical:heavy} you'll {tooltip:Kanji:collide} with everything. Cars, people, houses. You're too heavy to dodge them, so you collide with it all.",
            "hints": "Imaging being too heavy to go anywhere without colliding with things.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Collide"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The Shougun is glaring at you from the ground. \"You've been colliding with my entire city and now you collide into ME?!\" Smoke blows out his nostrils.",
                "mnemonic": "You're going around the town, you {tooltip:Kanji:collide} with a bunch of things, when all of a sudden you collide with the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046})! Oh no! The shogun looks really mad."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} issued {tooltip:Radical:twenty} {tooltip:Kanji:commandment}s to his people.",
            "hints": "He basically just made up a bunch of commandments to order all the other drunkards around and decided having twenty (twice the amount of that other religion he heard about) would be a good number.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Commandment"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u307e\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Commandment 1: Thou shalt not touch my kayak\n{linebreak}Commandment 2: Thou shalt not look at my kayak\n{linebreak}Commandment 3: Thou shalt give me beer to put in my kayak{splitParent}It goes on like that for a while...",
                "mnemonic": "The drunkard is yelling out his twenty {tooltip:Kanji:commandment}s to the others at the bar, but they're all about {tooltip:Reading:kay}aks ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:Mona Lisa} is in front of you. \"You must all paint the Mona Lisa {tooltip:Kanji:concurrently},\" says your art class teacher.",
            "hints": "Pay close attention to the students around you. Don't go too fast or too slow, or you won't finish concurrently.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Concurrently"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's a nice painting, the frown is just right, and you finished concurrently with everyone else, but you're probably going to fail this class.",
                "mnemonic": "Your entire class finishes {tooltip:Kanji:concurrently}. You look at your finished result. Wait, that's not the Mona Lisa. You painted {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:flowers} are being worked upon by a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} with a {tooltip:Radical:specialty} for knowing how to {tooltip:Kanji:dilute} things. The tsunami can dilute the flowers by pouring itself onto it. A tsunami can dilute things because it is made of water. You could say that it\u2019s its specialty.",
            "hints": "Look at the flowers as they begin to dilute. Their color and fragrance and dimensions become weaker and more spread out. It\u2019s really trippy to witness.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dilute"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "As you continue to watch the flower dilute due to the water being poured onto it by the tsunami, imagine what techniques this tsunami is using to hack nature. Is the tsunami a super cyborg from the future? Maybe.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the flower {tooltip:Kanji:dilute}, you determine that this is obviously a nature {tooltip:Reading:hack} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u304f}). You\u2019ve never seen anything like this before, so you think the tsunami found out how to hack nature and that\u2019s how it got so good at diluting things. By hacking nature."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you're driving, you may notice the {tooltip:Radical:flag}s in the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} near the {tooltip:Radical:exit}s. These flags mark the {tooltip:Kanji:ditch} running along the side of the road. You won't want to try to exit the road here or you'll end up stuck in one.",
            "hints": "Picture the flags in the dirt. Picture the ditch just over the edge of them. Now look for another way to exit this road, cause that way is just not a good idea.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ditch"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's a pun, get it? Holy. Hole-y. The ditch is a long hole. See? It's funny.",
                "mnemonic": "If you do end up veering into a {tooltip:Kanji:ditch} you'll find yourself yelling, \"{tooltip:Reading:Holy} ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u308a}) crap!\" Then you'll go hurtling into the ditch."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Simultaneous}ly, you throw your {tooltip:Radical:knife} at another person who's throwing a knife at you and you both get a {tooltip:Kanji:dose} of your own medicine. Literally, there's poison on these knives and now you've both been stabbed.",
            "hints": "Watch as the dose of poison sinks into your body through the knife that's in your chest, as it simultaneously happens to the other guy too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dose"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3056\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you're begging them for a dose of the xylophone drug. Just a taste, you want to live!",
                "mnemonic": "\"I need a {tooltip:Kanji:dose} of the antidote!\" you yell, and the other guy looks you dead in the eyes. They slowly pull a tiny {tooltip:Reading:xy}lophone ({span:lang=ja:\u3056\u3044}) out of their pocket, play a few notes, and then eat it. \"Ah, you'd like a dose of the xylophone cure, wouldn't you?\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:fang} on a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} is {tooltip:Kanji:elegant}. Most turkeys do not have fangs, so this turkey with a fang is quite elegant and dignified. This turkey is special.",
            "hints": "Look at this turkey with a fang. It\u2019s elegant, but also frightening. See the fanged turkey staring at you menacingly.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Elegant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture this elegant gargoyle sitting in front of you. Reach out your hand and feels its hard, elegant stone gargoyle body.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:elegant} fang makes the turkey look more like a {tooltip:Reading:ga}rgoyle ({span:lang=ja:\u304c}) than a turkey. In fact, you haven't seen it move at all. Maybe it is just an elegant gargoyle!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Teacher}s are all around us. Those who came before us are our teachers, so it's important to respect them. This is the basic idea of {tooltip:Kanji:filial piety}.",
            "hints": "Respect your elders, for they have much to teach us. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Filial Piety"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I am so ignorant and have much to learn. I must show filial piety to my father, {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, so that he may teach me.",
                "mnemonic": "With {tooltip:Kanji:filial piety} in mind, you decide to go visit your father, who is {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:walk} by a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} a {tooltip:Kanji:frequent} amount. This geoduck really intrigues you, so you can\u2019t help but frequent the area the geoduck is in and walk around.",
            "hints": "Imagine walking around near this geoduck. This is the best area to frequent when you want to look at the geoduck. Just keep looking at it as you walk.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Frequent"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
