                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The tires screech, the horse neighs, BAM! Total destruction everywhere. Bystanders scream in horror. That horse will never gallop again. It\u2019s a sad day for all horsekind.",
                "mnemonic": "Then the horse {tooltip:Kanji:gallop}s into the road and gets hit by a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). Oh man, there\u2019s blood everywhere. This horse is never going to gallop again. That car totally destroyed it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} of all the {tooltip:Radical:spider}s is a {tooltip:Kanji:genius}! Spiders are already pretty smart. They can weave complex homes and traps in one web. They even know where not to step so they don't get caught. But the leader knows everything. It made itself a little webbed computer and everything!",
            "hints": "Imagine seeing the leader of the spiders weaving it's own little spider computer. Doing spider math, and spider chemistry. It's a genius!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Genius"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Soon we'll be slaves to the genius spiders. Soon we'll be the flies. ",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the spider {tooltip:Kanji:genius} you realize that {tooltip:Reading:soon} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3093}) spiders will take over the humans. They're just way smarter than us. Soon we'll be the bugs."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:woman} is {tooltip:Radical:rejoic}ing. She must be {tooltip:Kanji:glad} and {tooltip:Kanji:happy} to rejoice out loud in front of you like this.",
            "hints": "Picture a woman rejoicing loudly. She's got a big smile on her face and she wants you and everyone else to see how glad she is.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Glad",
                "Alternative": "Happy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u308c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You'd be happy too if you'd just found your lost keys. Though maybe you wouldn't shout it for the entire world to hear.",
                "mnemonic": "\"I'm so {tooltip:Kanji:glad}!\" the woman shouts, \"Because I found the {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d})!\" You immediately start to wonder what \"the key\" is. The key to life? The key to learning Japanese? Then you see she's holding up some car keys."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There\u2019s {tooltip:Radical:grass} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} and the {tooltip:Radical:fins} there {tooltip:Radical:say} you have no {tooltip:Kanji:honor}. The fins are left over from the fish you dismembered and they do not believe it was an act of honor. Now they are just sitting on the ground on the grass, calling you out for having no honor.",
            "hints": "Listen to what the fins have to say as they flop around on the ground in the grass. Hear them swish about as they flop, brushing up against the blades of grass.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Honor"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine taking your yo-yo out to do this. Feel the string tighten around your finger as you unleash the yo-yo and silence all the fins.",
                "mnemonic": "Being one of little {tooltip:Kanji:honor}, you decide to squash these vocal fins with your {tooltip:Reading:yo}-yo ({span:lang=ja:\u3088}). You take out your yo-yo and start bashing each fin with it until they stop talking about what little honor you have."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take {tooltip:Radical:flowers} down a {tooltip:Radical:slide} to a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} that you picked from your {tooltip:Kanji:luxuriant} garden. You picked the flowers from the luxuriant garden, not the drunkard, mind you. Also the drunkard has a cane, but not flowers. That\u2019s why you picked some from your luxuriant garden and slid down your cool slide. Now the drunkard has a cane and some flowers.",
            "hints": "Imagine picking these flowers from your luxuriant garden then shooting down the slide. There are so many flowers that you are simply overwhelmed by their aroma. Now hand your flowers to the drunkard and watch his face light up as he excitedly thanks you for the gift.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Luxuriant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3052",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hear the drunkard moan as he rubs the flowers all over his body. You\u2019re really weirded out. This is the last time you give him flowers from your luxuriant garden, that\u2019s for sure.",
                "mnemonic": "The drunkard is so happy to receive flowers from your {tooltip:Kanji:luxuriant} garden that he begins to {tooltip:Reading:mo}an ({span:lang=ja:\u3082}) with pleasure. The moans are getting louder and more erotic. You\u2019re kind of creeped out. You really want him to stop moaning."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under the same {tooltip:Radical:flag}, all the people get {tooltip:Radical:together} to present a new {tooltip:Radical:weapon} to your {tooltip:Kanji:lord}. You all bow and say, \"{tooltip:Kanji:Milord}, this gift is for you.\" Because that's the proper way to address your lord.",
            "hints": "When you address your lord you better say \"milord,\" otherwise you might get beheaded with the weapon you're all giving him.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Milord",
                "Alternative": "Lord"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
