        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Every} {tooltip:Radical:winter} the {tooltip:Radical:thread} fields become {tooltip:Kanji:overgrown}. Yes, thread grows in fields these days. And the thread grows the most in the winter because reasons. The thread gets so overgrown that you can\u2019t even walk through it without cutting the thread down with a machete.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to wade through this overgrown field of thread. It\u2019s really difficult, and also it\u2019s really cold because it\u2019s winter. You shiver. Imagine chopping the thread down with your machete. Chop chop chop!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Overgrown"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
