{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:fire} in the {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} burns down the {tooltip:Kanji:field}. The rice paddy fire spreads out from the paddy and consumes the field next to it. This rice paddy fire has ravaged your entire farm!",
            "hints": "Look at this fire burning the rice paddy and the surrounding field. Smell burnt rice in the air as you see the flames dance before your eyes.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Field"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u305f\u3051, \u306f\u305f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine running around this hot cay as you try to put out the fire in your field. The fire is ravaging the entire hot cay, so it takes you a while to put it out. Man those flames are hot.{splitParent}Also, this kanji can have the reading {span:lang=ja:\u306f\u305f} for the kun'yomi as well. If you learn the longer version ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u305f\u3051}) it will be easier to just shave off a kana to remember the shorter version.",
                "mnemonic": "Your rice paddy farm and {tooltip:Kanji:field} are on a cay. A cay is a small, sandy island, and since your farm is on fire, this cay has turned into a hot cay. Or as Mario would say, that\u2019s one-a {tooltip:Reading:hot-a cay}! ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u305f\u3051}) Mama mia!"
            }
        }

{
