                "hints": "If you aren't mourning enough, when the soul comes out of the person's body, it will get really mad. \"What, I'm not worth a few tears? Really?\" And then the soul will haunt you. So you better mourn like you mean it.",
                "mnemonic": "As the {tooltip:Kanji:mourning} continues, the {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) of the dead person rises out of the cross. The soul looks around at all of the mourners and nods. Yes, your mourning has pleased it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:thread} {tooltip:Radical:hill}, but the hill is a bit weird looking (take a look at the hill radical in this kanji). It's not any normal hill, it's a weird lumpy hill that isn't quite right. That's because it is a thread hill of {tooltip:Kanji:netting}, and parts of the nets have caught things, like fish and cats, so there's weird abnormal lumps in them.",
            "hints": "You'll need to differentiate this from {span:lang=ja:\u7db1}, which uses the same radicals (though {span:lang=ja:\u7db1} has a real hill radical). Just remember that the weird \"hill\" has stuff caught in it because it is {tooltip:Kanji:netting}.",
