{
            "mnemonic": "Look at the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} at {tooltip:Radical:dawn} and you'll be able to see all the {tooltip:Kanji:hedge}s growing in the area really well. At any other time of day, hedges tend to blend into their surroundings. But at dawn, the shadows the sun makes really helps them stand out.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself leaning over a balcony at dawn, looking at all the hedges appear and their shadows stretch over the ground.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hedge",
                "Alternative": "Fence"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
