{
            "mnemonic": "You need to make a {tooltip:Radical:measurement} of an area so you take two clumps of {tooltip:Radical:dirt} to {tooltip:Kanji:seal in} each side of your measuring tape, so it stays on the ground. This is the way people used to seal things back in the day, back when we didn't have fancy things like tape and glue.",
            "hints": "Picture sealing other things with dirt. Like the bricks in your wall. Or the hole in your floor. Dirt can seal in anything.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Seal",
                "Alternatives": "Seal In, Closing"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
