{
            "mnemonic": "Ah yes, {tooltip:Kanji:wet} {tooltip:Kanji:clothes} must be wet clothes-NOT! This used to mean \"wet clothes\" a long, long time ago, but these days it's used for {tooltip:Vocabulary:false accusations}. Think of it this way: if you make false, baseless accusations, it's like you're dumping water all over someone for no reason. ",
