                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}The reading is a little different from {span:lang=ja:\u7fa4\u308c\u308b}, though. There's an extra {span:lang=ja:\u3089} in there. That being said, it's pretty similar, so you should be able to use one to remember the other after a few reps. You can also think about it this way: Everyone is flocking together in one place. Strange thing is, it's to a small {span:lang=ja:\u6751} ({span:lang=ja:\u3080\u3089}). There's a {span:lang=ja:\u6751} reunion going on, that's why.\n"
