{
            "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:conceal}, but as a verb, this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to go under} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to pass through}. Most commonly, this word means {tooltip:Vocabulary:to dive underwater} or {tooltip:Vocabulary:to go underground}. Can you see why the kanji for conceal kind of makes sense in these cases? If you're underwater or underground, no one can see you!",
