                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "36101-subject-6945.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}\u6f5c\u308b has two possible readings: {span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3050\u308b} and {span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3050\u308b}. The first is used when you mean to dive underwater or go underground.  The second is used when you pass through or under something, sometimes with difficulty, such as crawling under a fence. We want you to focus on {span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3050\u308b}, so here's a mnemonic to help you:\n{splitParent}Why are you trying to dive underwater again and again? It's to get {tooltip:Reading:mo' goo} ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3050}) to sell on the black goo market. Who knew that sea goo was such a commodity?\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u30e2\u30b0\u30e9\u304c\u571f\u306e\u4e0b\u306b\u6f5c\u3063\u3066\u884c\u304f\u3068\u3053\u308d\u3092\u898b\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "I saw a mole going underground."
                },
                {
                    "ja": "\u6c34\u306e\u4e2d\u306b\u3069\u306e\u3050\u3089\u3044\u306e\u9593\u6f5c\u3063\u3066\u3044\u3089\u308c\u307e\u3059\u304b\u3002",
