                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself deciding to do this. First step is to get a ridiculously long measuring tape. Then, you go up to the {tooltip:Reading:sun} and start measuring. You immediately start getting burned. Feel the pain of the heat from the {tooltip:Reading:sun}. Think about how this really probably wasn't a good idea. You still go forward, though, doing your best to {tooltip:Kanji:measure} the sun. Ouch, ouch, ouch.",
                "mnemonic": "You want to {tooltip:Kanji:measure} something... something that will make you famous. You decide you'll measure the biggest mass in our solar system. We're talking about the {tooltip:Reading:sun} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:tree} has an {tooltip:Radical:omen} growing from it, one single {tooltip:Kanji:peach} that is the size of a house. Inside is a child who will save the village from demons.",
            "hints": "Of course, this tree omen of a {tooltip:Kanji:peach} refers to momotaro, the little boy who was born from a peach (you should look it up if you don't know this children's story).",
            "meanings": {
