                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It grows bigger everytime you say \"MORE MORE\" twice. If you say it just once, it stays the same.",
                "mnemonic": "If {tooltip:Reading:momo}taro ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3082}) wasn't enough, think about the {tooltip:Kanji:peach} growing larger and larger. You want it to grow bigger, so you yell at it: \"{tooltip:Reading:MO}RE! {tooltip:Reading:MO}RE!\" ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3082})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:grain} you cut off a {tooltip:Radical:tree} with a {tooltip:Radical:knife} is a {tooltip:Kanji:pear}. I don't know if you've ever seen Asian pears, but they're pretty big and sturdy. You can't just pick them off of the tree, you need the help of a knife. That's why this is a pear, and not an apple or peach or something else.",
            "hints": "Imagine standing below a tree full of pears. You take your knife and carefully cut them all down, one by one.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pear"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
