{
            "mnemonic": "Looking up to the {tooltip:Radical:cliff}, you see the {tooltip:Radical:tree}s, and the {tooltip:Radical:sun} shining down on them. Using the sun and the trees (up there on the cliff), you've devised a method to tell what time of the year it is, based on where the shadow from the trees fall. After a while, you develop a bigger system. This system is a whole {tooltip:Kanji:calendar}.",
            "hints": "Look at the different shadow patterns. Know what they all mean. This is your very own calendar system.",
            "meanings": {
