                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Normal kids would probably try to juke cram school, since it's hard and it's more school than they think they need. But you're a good kid who want to cram, so you juke the circle instead.",
                "mnemonic": "The sock circle seems to have a bit of a gravitational pull, so to make sure you get to {tooltip:Kanji:cram school} on time you have to {tooltip:Reading:juke} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u304f}) around it every day, to make sure you can get past it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "From the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of your {tooltip:Radical:older brother} comes... a {tooltip:Kanji:curse}!",
            "hints": "Imagine him cursing you. He's not a fan of you, since you are siblings, but to think he'd go so far as to put a curse on you? You can't believe it. What kind of curse did he put upon you?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Curse"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3085",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e\u308d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "In your mind, walk around the area where you live. Think about the places you can go that aren't roads. If you try to walk on a road, you can't. This is the {tooltip:Reading:no ro}ad curse, after all.",
                "mnemonic": "Turns out, he put the {tooltip:Reading:no ro}ad ({span:lang=ja:\u306e\u308d}) curse on you, meaning you can never walk on roads."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "After the {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} the {tooltip:Radical:sun} comes out again and shines on these {tooltip:Radical:spikes}. They were super wet before, but you figure the sun probably dried them off. You lean down to touch them and nope, they's still {tooltip:Kanji:damp}.",
            "hints": "The sun did a little bit of work, so they aren't wet, but they aren't dry either. They're damp.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Damp"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3081",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Luckily the shih tzu is kinda pinned between the spikes, so it isn't dead or anything, but it's definitely stuck. You try to help it out, but you slip because it's so damp and you fall in too! Imagine the sound of your cries mixing in with the shih tzu's as you both struggling to get out but can't because of how damp everything is.",
                "mnemonic": "As you're looking at the {tooltip:Kanji:damp} spikes, a {tooltip:Reading:shih tzu} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3064}) prances over, slips on the damp ground, and falls right on the spike! Oh nooo!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:grain}s you have stored in your {tooltip:Radical:house} reflect on your {tooltip:Kanji:earnings}. If you earn a lot of money, you have more grains.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking at the grains in the houses of people who make vastly different earnings. The poor artist has only a few sacks of grain. The rich samurai has an extra house just for holding his grain. That's how you know he has much higher earnings than the artist.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Earnings"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture your own earnings. Can you afford a lot of grains and a car?",
                "mnemonic": "Another way to check someone's {tooltip:Kanji:earnings} is to see if they have a {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). Would someone who doesn't make a lot of money have a car? No!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "I have {tooltip:Radical:sick} in my {tooltip:Radical:skin}. Just look at it, it doesn't look too good. Whenever I have sickness in my skin, I know that I'm probably {tooltip:Kanji:exhausted}.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself being really, really exhausted. Then look at your skin. It's all sickly looking.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Exhausted"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine exercising so much that your body gets all {tooltip:Kanji:exhausted} and {tooltip:Reading:hea}ted ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}) up.",
                "mnemonic": "When you're {tooltip:Kanji:exhausted}, your muscles are all probably worn out. Being this worn out, you can probably imagine that your body is all {tooltip:Reading:hea}ted ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}) up, from all the exercising."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:sheep} with {tooltip:Radical:feathers} (and presumably wings, too) is able to {tooltip:Kanji:fly}.",
            "hints": "Imagine the sheep with feathers taking off and flying around. It's an odd sight, but makes sense, kind of.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fly"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3051, \u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ha HA! Everyone knows sheep love cake. Works every time. Now this flying sheep is yours!",
                "mnemonic": "Using this sheep that can {tooltip:Kanji:fly}, you're going to get rich! But there's a problem... you have to catch the sheep. So, you get some {tooltip:Reading:cake} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3051}) and use it to lure the sheep to your trap, where you catch it!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "I'm putting all my {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} on {tooltip:Radical:someone}, hoping they'll win the race! This is a {tooltip:Kanji:gamble} and you're gambling.",
            "hints": "Remember, shellfish used to be used as money. So if you're betting shellfish on someone, you're just gambling. And you probably won't get any of those shellfish back.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gamble"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
