                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u308b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I think he maybe got too friendly with some raccoons and beavers and went crazy. Watch out for him if you live in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}, rabies is no joke.",
                "mnemonic": "You might see that {tooltip:Kanji:crazy} {tooltip:Kanji:lunatic} hanging around the outskirts of {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. He'll lurk near your trash cans and scream, \"I AM THE ANIMAL KING!\" and run away with some orange peels."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:woman} who is a {tooltip:Radical:nurse} should be called {tooltip:Kanji:miss}.",
            "hints": "Compare this to a man who is a nurse. You should probably call him mister. That's why you know a woman who is a nurse is \"miss.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Miss"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046",
