{
            "mnemonic": "This is a bit of a weird word. The kanji is {tooltip:Kanji:char}, and a previous word you learned ({span:lang=ja:\u7126\u3052\u308b}) is \"to be burned.\" This, on the other hand, is \"to be in a hurry\" or \"to be impatient.\" I guess if you're getting burned or have that feeling, you're going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be in a hurry} and you're going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be impatient}. You can tell that this is that word because it only has one kana, {span:lang=ja:\u308b}, which stands for {tooltip:Reading:ru}de. You're feeling someone is being rude (or maybe you are), which is why you have this feeling of impatience and hurrying.",
