                        "voiceActorId": 1,
                        "voiceActorName": "Kyoko",
                        "voiceDescription": "Tokyo accent",
                        "file": "36459-subject-6883.ogg"
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This kanji uses the kun'yomi readings for each kanji, for some reason. You learned the kun'yomi reading for {span:lang=ja:\u6238}, but in this case it's rendaku'd so it becomes {span:lang=ja:\u3069} instead of {span:lang=ja:\u3068}. You didn't learn the kun'yomi version of {span:lang=ja:\u4e95} with the kanji. Think of this {tooltip:Vocabulary:well}, and look inside. There you see an {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}), stuck inside. As you pull it out, it scratches your eyes out.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
                {
                    "ja": "\u3088\u304f\u51b7\u3048\u305f\u4e95\u6238\u6c34\u3092\u98f2\u3080\u3068\u3001\u51b7\u305f\u3044\u30a2\u30a4\u30b9\u30af\u30ea\u30fc\u30e0\u3092\u98df\u3079\u305f\u6642\u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\u982d\u304c\u30ad\u30fc\u30f3\u3068\u75db\u307f\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002",
                    "en": "When I drank cold water from the well, I got brain freeze like when I ate cold ice cream."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

