                "mnemonic": "Be careful that you don't spill {tooltip:Kanji:black ink} on anyone or anything. If you do, you have to own it. Imagine spilling black ink on someone, and when they confront you, you yell, \"Yeah I got black ink on you, so {tooltip:Reading:sue me} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u307f})!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:eye} gets kicked with a {tooltip:Radical:cleat} that came careening toward your {tooltip:Radical:forehead} when it popped off someone doing a {tooltip:Radical:dance}, and you {tooltip:Kanji:blink}.",
            "hints": "Well, of course you blink, you can't control that. And when a cleat come hurtling toward your eye it blinks automatically.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Blink"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u305f\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Soon the person who's cleat hit you is running over and trying to apologize and stop your crying, but it's too late.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:blink} and blink and {tooltip:Reading:soon} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3093}) there are tears coming out of them too. You try to blink them away but it's not working. Soon you're crying and blinking and crying some more."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} {tooltip:Radical:wrap}s around itself, the resulting wave will create a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:bubbles}. You know how tsunamis wrap around once gravity kicks in, right? Well when that wave crashes, a whole lot of bubbles are created.",
            "hints": "Picture the bubbles bursting out of the wrapped up tsunami as it crashes down. The air that the tsunami sucked in while it was wrapping up come out as bubbles big and small.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bubbles"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
