                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The dormitory row boat leaks a little too, so by the time you get back you really need to light the charcoal and heat up!",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:dormitory} is on an island, so when you go out to get the charcoal you have to take a {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat. You row and row and row until you reach the shed with all the charcoal. Then you row and row and row it back to the dormitory."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There are {tooltip:Radical:nine} {tooltip:Radical:bird}s and one of them is a {tooltip:Kanji:dove} and another is a {tooltip:Kanji:pigeon}. These nine birds are a flock of all kinds, but the dove and the pigeon are the leaders.",
            "hints": "Look at these nine birds strutting down the street like they own the place. The dove and pigeon are out in front because they are the most important. Hear them chirping and fluttering their feathers about.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dove",
                "Alternative": "Pigeon"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Devour it. You love pigeon hearts. Discard the rest, keep the heart.",
                "mnemonic": "Take a look at the {tooltip:Kanji:pigeon} in front of you. Now, grab it, tear it in half, and grab the {tooltip:Reading:heart} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3068}) from its little body. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Make {tooltip:Radical:barracks} out of {tooltip:Radical:gold} and they will get {tooltip:Kanji:dull} quickly. Gold is soft, it's okay for jewelry and delicate things that aren't used much, but barracks for soldiers? Those are used constantly, and they get worn out easily. What was once shiny gold will go dull in days.",
            "hints": "Picture a huge barracks made of dull, almost brown, gold. Maybe you should have picked a better material.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dull"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3069\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b\u3076, \u306e\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You stand cowering in front of the don as he inspects how dull the gold barracks are. You don't wanna be off'd for this just because the don was dull enough to make you use gold!",
                "mnemonic": "As you stare sadly at the {tooltip:Kanji:dull} barracks, the {tooltip:Reading:don} ({span:lang=ja:\u3069\u3093}) shows up out of nowhere, and he's pissed. He turns his angry gaze toward you and says, \"How did my barracks get so dull? Are you at fault? This is bad, this is very bad. Someone will pay for this.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You want to turn your {tooltip:Radical:gold} {tooltip:Radical:comb} into a {tooltip:Radical:weapon}, so you throw it into the {tooltip:Kanji:forge}.",
            "hints": "Once the gold comb has melted down in the forge, you can forge it into whatever weapon you want.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Forge"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
