                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Tap this bone china plate with your knuckle. Hear the pleasant tap as you continue to view all the fancy lanterns around you at the festival.",
                "mnemonic": "The plate part you found at the {tooltip:Kanji:lantern festival} (and put on the {tooltip:Kanji:tray}) is made out of {tooltip:Reading:bone} ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3093}) china. How fancy. Is bone china made from real bones? Bones found in China? Probably not, huh."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're standing under a {tooltip:Radical:canopy} when you see something strange sticking out of the {tooltip:Radical:dirt}. You pull it, but it won't budge. You pull harder and harder until the dirt starts rumbling and a giant {tooltip:Kanji:manor} starts rising out of the ground with you on top!",
            "hints": "Picture yourself on top of this manor that rose out of the ground. The canopy is still above you and it seems to be attached to the roof.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Manor"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being chased by an angry shougun all through his giant, luxurious manor. You barely have time to admire the interior design with him gaining on you like this!",
                "mnemonic": "The beautiful {tooltip:Kanji:manor} begins to shake and the {tooltip:Reading:shou}gun bursts out of the front door. \"WHO HAS UNEARTHED MY SECRET MANOR?!\" he screams."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "An {tooltip:Radical:animal} that {tooltip:Radical:kick}s {tooltip:Radical:dirt} into people's {tooltip:Radical:mouth}s is a {tooltip:Kanji:monkey}. Monkeys are naughty little things. You should be happy it was just dirt it kicked into your mouth, and not something worse.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking at a monkey at the zoo. Aww, it's so cute. But then it turns around and kicks some dirt right into your aww-ing mouth. Yuck! Why monkey, why?!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Monkey"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u308b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the monkey saluting you as you spit dirt out of your mouth. Taste the bitter dirt and the bitter shame. You were played by a monkey.",
                "mnemonic": "You spit the dirt out of your mouth and look back at the {tooltip:Kanji:monkey} to see that it's {tooltip:Reading:salu}ting ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u308b}) you. Is... is it mocking you?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There\u2019s a {tooltip:Radical:tree} in the {tooltip:Radical:east} that looks like a {tooltip:Kanji:pillar}. The tree is tall and straight and does not have any leaves or branches. The tree is basically a big wooden pillar that just happens to be alive still.",
            "hints": "Look at this big tree pillar over in the east. You always know where east is because of it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pillar"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
