                "mnemonic": "Your eyes follow the {tooltip:Kanji:cash}, and you watch as the penguin stuffs it, towel and all, into a {tooltip:Reading:hay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3044}) stack. What a smart penguin, people don't look for cash in hay, they're too busy looking for needles."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You give {tooltip:Radical:bamboo} to {tooltip:Radical:someone} and they make them into {tooltip:Kanji:chopsticks}. They are very talented at turning bamboo into bamboo chopsticks. This someone is an expert at their profession.",
            "hints": "Watch this person take ordinary bamboo and transform it into chopsticks right before your eyes. Hear the whooshing and whittling sounds as they form the bamboo into chopsticks with expert speed and precision.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chopsticks"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3083\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine trying to pick up hash browns with your chopsticks. They would be really hard to eat if you didn't have these handy eating tools!",
                "mnemonic": "Now use those {tooltip:Kanji:chopsticks} to eat some delicious {tooltip:Reading:hash} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3057}) browns! That's what chopsticks were made for. That's what they're always made for."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Rub {tooltip:Radical:charcoal} under your {tooltip:Radical:eye}s if you want to see {tooltip:Kanji:clear}ly. Sports players also rub charcoal under their eyes to see nice and clear in the bright sun.",
            "hints": "You can even rub charcoal in your eyes if you really want to clear them up, but you should probably only do this under the supervision of your eye doctor.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Clear"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine how dangerous it would be not to have clear vision while you row around in a row boat. You might even smack yourself in the face with your own oars.",
                "mnemonic": "You have to have {tooltip:Kanji:clear} vision because you're about to go out in your {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat. The light off the water shines right into your eyes and you need the charcoal to clear that up for you. Otherwise you'll end up crashing into the shore or going over a waterfall to your death."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a {tooltip:Radical:mountain} on top of a bunch of {tooltip:Radical:dirt} with a steep {tooltip:Radical:cliff}. This is a bit redundant, but the mountain and the dirt just make the {tooltip:Kanji:cliff} even bigger and steeper and scarier.",
            "hints": "Imagine a cliff. Now add two big helpings of dirt and a mountain to the top. It's still a cliff, it's just more cliff than before.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cliff"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304c\u3051",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine falling down this huge cliff and the last words you have to hear before you splat on the ground is someone yelling \"Guy\" at you over and over. What a way to go.",
                "mnemonic": "As you\u2019re peering over this tall {tooltip:Kanji:cliff}, somebody behind you shouts, \u201cHey, {tooltip:Reading:guy} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3044})!\u201d This startles you and you tumble down the cliff. Apparently so did he, because you can hear him saying, \"Hey guy! OOF! Are you okay? OOF! Guy? Guy!!!\u201d as you both fall."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Without a {tooltip:Radical:fire}, you will {tooltip:Radical:lack} the ability to {tooltip:Kanji:cook} anything. You really need a fire to cook properly. Having a fire will make sure any cooking endeavors you attempt will not fail.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself as you cook with a fire very confidently. Knowing you cannot fail, feel the heat and hear the crackling embers of the fire. Smell the delicious smell of whatever you are cooking as well.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cook"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine swinging this meal over the fire. Feel the flames licking at your fingertips as you cook this meal by swinging it back and forth over the fire.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:cook} your meal evenly by {tooltip:Reading:swi}nging ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3044}) it back and forth over the fire. You swing it left, you swing it right. You swing it to, you swing it fro. All this swinging ensures a properly cooked meal."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Sitting safely under your {tooltip:Radical:canopy} you take {tooltip:Radical:rice} and {tooltip:Radical:dirt}, mix it up, and create unique {tooltip:Kanji:cosmetics} for your face.",
            "hints": "Imagine mixing dirt and rice together to make some cosmetics that best fit your skin tone and type. No one will see you doing it under this canopy too, so the secret formula you come up with will be safe.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cosmetics"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine meeting the Shougun with your new cosmetics all over your face. You look amazing! Stunning! The shougun wants to know where you got that foundation, you're glowing!",
                "mnemonic": "You need these {tooltip:Kanji:cosmetics} because you have a meeting with the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) coming up. You want to impress him, and you don't want anyone to copy your look."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:pig} with {tooltip:Radical:horns} runs into a {tooltip:Radical:building} and makes it fall into the {tooltip:Radical:dirt}. This makes a loud {tooltip:Kanji:crash} sound. I mean, how could it not? The building literally crashed to the ground when the horned pig attacked it.",
            "hints": "Picture a pig with horns crashing into a building and both of them crashing into the dirt. Uh oh, is the pig dead?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Crash"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine walking around the crash site yelling \"Sooey! Sooey!\" over and over. You'll never know if the pig survived the crash if you don't.",
                "mnemonic": "You're worried about the pig, that was a pretty big {tooltip:Kanji:crash}, after all. So you yell, \"{tooltip:Reading:SOOEY} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3044})!\" Here pig pig pig. SOOEEEYYY! You know\u2014the universal call for pigs"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:crab} will try to hide what it {tooltip:Radical:lack}s with {tooltip:Kanji:deceit}. Lying, stealing, faking things\u2014no type of deceit is too much for a crab.",
            "hints": "Covering things up with deceit is pretty much the worst thing you can do, so don't be like this crab.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Deceit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3056\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the crab with its head, er, front half? Whatever, it's in the guillotine and it's screaming, \"You've been deceived! I never deceived anyone, you're all sheep!\"",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Deceit} can only take you so far, and soon the crab is caught, tried for its crimes and coverups, and sentenced to death via {tooltip:Reading:gui}llotine ({span:lang=ja:\u304e})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits your {tooltip:Radical:mohawk} and it begins to {tooltip:Kanji:drip}. The water from the tsunami continues to drip from your mohawk long after the tsunami has passed. There\u2019s a lot of water in your hair now, so it\u2019s probably going to drip for a while.",
            "hints": "Imagine having all this tsunami water in your hair. Hear it drip from your mohawk. Drip\u2026 drip\u2026 drip\u2026",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Drip"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u305f\u305f, \u3057\u305a\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel the weight of this dryer helmet on your head as you listen to it whirr away. The dripping has finally stopped! Success!",
                "mnemonic": "Luckily, you\u2019re a self-proclaimed {tooltip:Reading:techie} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u304d}), so you develop a device to stop the {tooltip:Kanji:drip} drip dripping. This techie device of yours is like a hair dryer helmet. You put it over your mohawk, it does its thing, and your hair is dry! Being a techie sure does have its benefits."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} there are {tooltip:Radical:flag}s and {tooltip:Radical:horns} lined up with a {tooltip:Radical:lantern} attached to them, making a {tooltip:Kanji:fence}. It's a little weird looking, but these things are definitely supposed to fence something in.",
            "hints": "Can you see the fence made of horns and flags through the light of the lantern?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fence"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself climbing over this fence (that you're definitely not supposed to climb based on all these flags and horns) and falling into the piles of hay. It's a little scratchy, but otherwise pretty comfy!",
                "mnemonic": "You want to know what this {tooltip:Kanji:fence} is fencing in, so you take a step closer. As the light from the lantern gets brighter you see that the fence is around a ton of {tooltip:Reading:hay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3044})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "It's {tooltip:Radical:rain}ing on your {tooltip:Radical:spear} that has {tooltip:Radical:winter} {tooltip:Radical:power}. When the warm rain hits your cold, winter spear, it creates {tooltip:Kanji:fog}.",
            "hints": "When warm water touches a cold spear, fog billows out and covers everything.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fog"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You walk toward the kirin through the fog. When you get close, the image before you becomes clear: it's two cans of Kirin beer on a slide.{splitParent}Next time you see fog, keep your eyes peeled for the real kirin in the kiri.",
                "mnemonic": "Through the {tooltip:Kanji:fog} you see the shape of a mythical {tooltip:Reading:kiri}n ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u308a}). You can only see the outline through the fog, but you know it's there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "After passing through a {tooltip:Radical:door}, you use a {tooltip:Radical:feather} to put the finishing touches on a {tooltip:Kanji:folding fan}. The door leads to your folding fan workshop where you make all your folding fans. This folding fan is now complete that you\u2019ve added a feather to it. How lovely it is.",
            "hints": "Use this folding fan to fan your face. Feel the refreshing breeze as you admire the gorgeous feather you just added. What a fashionista you\u2019ve become.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Folding Fan"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3046\u304e, \u3042\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine handing this newly made folding fan to the centaur. See his face light up with delight as he examines your fine craftsmanship and starts fanning himself with it. Another satisfied customer!",
                "mnemonic": "Your biggest {tooltip:Kanji:folding fan} customer is a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}). This centaur just loves your folding fans and this one you just made with the feather was for the centaur\u2019s latest order. You go back out your door and deliver this folding fan to the centaur."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:door} a {tooltip:Radical:criminal} will get into is the {tooltip:Kanji:front door}. Now hold on, you may be thinking, wouldn't they go for the back door? No! 99% of home invasions happen when you leave your own front door unlocked!",
            "hints": "You better check the locks on your front door right now, because odds are you left it open and didn't even notice. It's the perfect door for a criminal to get access to your home.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Front Door"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3073\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine how you'd heat up your front door. A hot iron? A blow torch? A small fire? It doesn't matter how, as long as the heat makes it all the way through your front door and hurts any criminals trying to get into it.",
                "mnemonic": "To protect your {tooltip:Kanji:front door} from criminals you plan to fill it with {tooltip:Reading:hea}t ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}). Oh yeah, we're gonna Kevin McCallister this."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:soul} will only inhabit a {tooltip:Radical:root} if it's holding a {tooltip:Kanji:grudge}. Have you ever seen a nice, haunted tree? No! They're always angry and trying to get someone back for something.",
            "hints": "Don't die with a grudge, or your soul might end up angry and trapped in some roots.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Grudge"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a tree with the soul of a condor with a grudge in it before you. You feel bad about being so wasteful with paper and chopsticks now, huh?",
                "mnemonic": "If you see one of these {tooltip:Kanji:grudge} trees, it's probably inhabited by the soul of a {tooltip:Reading:con}dor ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3093}). Humans tend to kill condors and take their trees away to build houses and make toilet paper. So condors hold pretty bad grudges against us, and so their souls end up stuck in a lot of trees."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take a {tooltip:Radical:towel} and wrap it around your head to keep the {tooltip:Radical:sun} out of your {tooltip:Radical:eye}s. You've invented... the {tooltip:Kanji:hat}!",
            "hints": "A hat is just a piece of cloth or a towel you get to stay on your head. Extra points if it protect your eyes from the sun.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hat"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine bowling with hats. Thankfully, they work as bowling balls just as well as they work as hats. You're so innovative!",
                "mnemonic": "People see you wearing this fancy new {tooltip:Kanji:hat} thing and start asking you to share. You grab all your extra towels, roll them up, and {tooltip:Reading:bow}l ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) them down the street toward everyone who asks for one."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:soul} {tooltip:Radical:mask} helps you to see the deepest part of anyone's soul. You look around and in all the people you only see {tooltip:Kanji:hate}.",
            "hints": "You're supposed to see all the emotions, so why do you only see hate inside everyone?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305e\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Zombies are pretty filled with hate, so it makes sense that you'd see a bunch of hate if you used the soul mask on them.",
                "mnemonic": "It turns out you're not looking at normal people. You see so much {tooltip:Kanji:hate} because all the people you're looking at are actually just a group of {tooltip:Reading:zo}mbies ({span:lang=ja:\u305e\u3046})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} of a {tooltip:Radical:narwhal} {tooltip:Radical:construction} crew needs all the {tooltip:Kanji:help} he can get. The narwhals are beginning construction on an underwater city. The leader knows the narwhals are hard construction workers, but they\u2019ll need some help building this city.",
            "hints": "Imagine being the narwhal leader and asking others for help. Ask a shark for help. Ask a whale for help. Ask a shrimp for help. Go on, ask.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Help"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine using this saw and realizing how big of a help it is. Hear the saw sawing away as you and your fellow narwhals get to work.",
                "mnemonic": "Then you discover a {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}) who would be a great big {tooltip:Kanji:help}. This saw is very strong and would help you and your narwhal construction team out a lot. You should make use of this saw right away."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have {tooltip:Radical:fingers} in the {tooltip:Radical:thousand}s and while looking up at the {tooltip:Radical:sun} you decide you want to {tooltip:Kanji:insert} them in there.",
            "hints": "Hold your thousand+ fingers up to the sun and imagine inserting them into the sun's super-hot ... s-sun lava. (That's what it is, right? Yeah, let's go with that.)",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Insert"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Since you have a thousand fingers too many, you decide to insert them all into the sun and watch as their souls pop out. You listen to the little souls scream at you.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:insert} one finger, it burns up immediately, and its {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) comes flying out screaming for a moment before it disappears. Hmm. You insert another finger and as it burns up, another little soul comes out screeching, \"WHY WOULD YOU INSERT ME IN THERE!\" and is gone."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} and {tooltip:Radical:Wolverine} take a {tooltip:Radical:slide} to {tooltip:Kanji:Italy}. Wolverine\u2019s leader is Professor X, and they are both sliding down a big slide to Italy. How fun!",
            "hints": "Imagine Wolverine and his leader Professor X going down this slide to Italy. Hear them wooping and cheering as they ride down the slide. Whee~",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Italy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine this eagle carrying Professor X away from Italy and out over the ocean. You can also remember this reading easily because Italy starts with the letter I. Super simple stuff.",
                "mnemonic": "Before Professor X can get off the slide into {tooltip:Kanji:Italy}, a large {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) swoops down and plucks him right out of his wheelchair. That eagle is very strong. Goodbye, Professor X!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "They {tooltip:Radical:say} the {tooltip:Radical:key} to telling a {tooltip:Kanji:lie} is to totally believe the lie yourself. They say that if you believe your own lie, others will believe it as well. This is key.",
            "hints": "Imagine an actual key going from you to another person. This key is the lie. You gotta believe in the lie for it to reach the other person and unlock their understanding. Visualize this visual lie.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lie"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3064\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine trying to lie your way out of this. He saw you steal his saw. He caught you red handed. What sort of lie can you spin to get yourself out of this situation?",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:lie} you told was about not stealing your buddy\u2019s {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}). You actually did steal his saw. He saw you steal his saw, but now you are trying to lie your way out of it. It\u2019s not going well."
