                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}This is a jukugo word that uses the on'yomi readings of the kanji. Well, at least most of it does. To remember the reading for {span:lang=ja:\u54c0} imagine some {tooltip:Vocabulary:pathetic} person who lost their home. They may be {tooltip:Vocabulary:pitiful} but at some point after losing their home they decided that the hood of your car would make a fine place to live. You can't help but ask them, \"{tooltip:Reading:Why} ({span:lang=ja:\u308f\u3044}) my car?\" There are so many other cars this pathetic person could be camping out on, but they chose yours.\n"
            },
            "contextSentences": [
