                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Ha ha!\" Paste paste. \"Ha ha ha!!\" PASTE PASTE PASTE.",
                "mnemonic": "You're a little crazy, which is why you decided to use {tooltip:Kanji:paste} to paste your entire fortune to these shellfish, and as you paste each one you yell out, \"{tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f})!\" Paste."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sunlight} shines on your {tooltip:Radical:forehead} in your {tooltip:Radical:car} with a great {tooltip:Kanji:radiance}. The car you are in is a convertible, so the sunlight shines right onto your big bald forehead. The sun has a pretty powerful radiance as it is, but the sheen from the sunlight hitting your forehead is the most powerful radiance ever witnessed by man.",
            "hints": "Imagine this radiance emanating from your shiny dome. The radiance is blinding!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Radiance"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304c\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Point your shiny forehead, filled with radiance, at your car. Hear the engine start and jump to life as you power it with the reflected sunlight from your forehead.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:radiance} is the {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) to powering your car. Your car runs on reflected solar energy, and the radiance coming from your forehead is the most powerful source of radiant sunlight ever imagined. Your forehead is a perfect key for this car."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Radical:soul} has an {tooltip:Radical:idea} it's just a {tooltip:Kanji:recollection} of something you already know. Only your brain can have original ideas, so when your soul tries to come up with one, it's just a recollection of something you thought before now.",
            "hints": "When you have a recollection of some idea or thing in the past, it's just your soul saying, hey remember this? Let's not forget this.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Recollection"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine recollecting a past life in Oklahoma. Life was simple and nice. You should consider taking this as a sign to move there again!",
                "mnemonic": "Your soul is sending you a {tooltip:Kanji:recollection} right now of... your past life as a farmer in {tooltip:Reading:Ok}lahoma ({span:lang=ja:\u304a\u304f}). You see yourself farming and sweating and living a wonderful life. Hmm, maybe you should move to Oklahoma and live the simple life again."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you try to put your {tooltip:Radical:soul} into {tooltip:Radical:every}thing, you'll {tooltip:Kanji:regret} it. It's not so much that putting your soul into things is bad, but every single thing? You'll burn out immediately. You won't be able to be good at any of those things. And you'll regret all the time you wasted trying to be the best at everything.",
            "hints": "Imagine if you went full force into everything you've ever even thought of doing. Imagine how burnt out your soul would be. Imagine all the regret you'd have that you didn't just stick to one thing and do it well.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Regret"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3084, \u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Throw everything you regret away. Only kayak from now on.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:regret} is too strong for you to ignore, so you decide to drop everything but {tooltip:Reading:kay}aking ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044}). If there's one thing you refuse to regret, it's your bright orange kayak and all the friends you made at kayaking club."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take a {tooltip:Radical:rake} in for a {tooltip:Radical:measurement} but it is {tooltip:Kanji:resistant}. The rake doesn\u2019t want to have its measurements taken. The rake is resistant to have any measurement taken because it feels inferior to the other rakes and doesn\u2019t want to be embarrassed if it ends up being smaller than the others.",
            "hints": "Try and move this rake over to the measurement table. It is resistant so you have a hard time moving it. Imagine the rake struggling and resisting endlessly.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Resistant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "See yourself tying the tie around the rake and attaching it to the measurement table. The rake is still jostling around, but the tie keeps it from moving about too terribly much.",
                "mnemonic": "Because the rake is persistently {tooltip:Kanji:resistant}, you eventually tie it to the table with your neck {tooltip:Reading:tie} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3044}). The tie won\u2019t hold for long, so you need to take each measurement quickly."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On a {tooltip:Radical:cliff}, the {tooltip:Radical:pope} is holding a {tooltip:Kanji:shield}. The pope is near the edge of the cliff and is using the shield to fend off demons. The demons want to shove the pope off the cliff, but the pope is using his holy shield of popery to fend them off.",
            "hints": "Imagine the shield glowing brightly as hymns play in the background. The demons try to get close to the pope to shove him off the cliff but the holy shield is too bright and popey.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shield"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3066",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This pope would have been in a lot of trouble if June's summer sun hadn't risen at just the right moment. His shield would have become useless and he might have been shoved off the cliff if it was a less sunny month.",
                "mnemonic": "The light of the pope's {tooltip:Kanji:shield} begins to fade. The shield's holy power is waning! Just as the demons are about to push him off the cliff, the sun begins to rise. That's right! It's {tooltip:Reading:June} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3093}) and summer has just begun. The pope's shield reflects the power of June's bright sun into the eyes of the demons, casting them off the cliff behind him and back into hell!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is an {tooltip:Radical:insect} on the {tooltip:Radical:roof} in a {tooltip:Radical:spoon}. It's there for the eating, and it's how you plan to attract a {tooltip:Kanji:snake} to your roof.",
            "hints": "Snakes love insects, especially when they're ready to eat on a spoon. But, snakes don't usually go on top of the roof, so that's why you have to tempt one with an insect in a spoon.",
            "meanings": {
