{
            "mnemonic": "If {tooltip:Radical:someone} wants to {tooltip:Radical:boil}, you let them {tooltip:Kanji:boil}!",
            "hints": "There's someone in your face yelling about how they want to boil! You yell back, \"Okay, if you want to boil, just boil!\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Boil"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3083",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Once your knee is done boiling, the person kneels down in front of you and presents it on a platter, mocking you, since you can't kneel anymore. You should pay more attention to what's going on from now on or you could find yourself in... HOT WATER. Ohohoho.",
                "mnemonic": "Welp, the pot is at a rolling {tooltip:Kanji:boil} and your {tooltip:Reading:knee} ({span:lang=ja:\u306b}) is in there. The person wasn't saying they wanted to boil, they said they wanted to boil someone. And that meant you. Well, your knee anyway."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} {tooltip:Radical:loiter}s near a {tooltip:Radical:black hole} then it's going to {tooltip:Kanji:capsize}. I mean, yeah, it's not a boat, but just look, that's what's happening! That helicopter is going down!",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to cover up a black hole so that the helicopter doesn't capsize. It's one or the other, dude. Cover or capsize. You decide.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Capsize",
                "Alternative": "Cover"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u304a, \u304f\u3064\u304c\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Man, f**k you you, black hole. F**k you you. Making that helicopter capsize and then refusing to be covered?",
                "mnemonic": "You're doing your best to {tooltip:Kanji:cover} the black hole to stop the helicopter from {tooltip:Kanji:capsiz}ing but it's not working! \u201c{tooltip:Reading:F**k} you ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u304f}) black hole!\" you shout. You just want to cover it up! You just want to do the right thing!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:horse} who can write a {tooltip:Radical:paragraph} gets to be a {tooltip:Kanji:chess piece}. Only the most erudite of horses gets selected to be a chess piece. The knight\u2019s chess piece is represented by a horse, and for a horse to earn this honor, they must first write a paragraph explaining why they deserve the honor.",
            "hints": "Imagine a horse trying to write a paragraph about why it deserves to be a chess piece. See the horse struggle with his hooves to write out a paragraph as he neighs in nervous frustration.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chess Piece"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u307e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "See this horse in its coma. You feel bad that it will never be able to be a chess piece, but this is a bit dramatic.",
                "mnemonic": "Upon being told that he will never be a {tooltip:Kanji:chess piece}, the horse slips into a {tooltip:Reading:coma} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u307e}). The horse will never awaken from this coma as he knows he will never fulfill his dream of becoming a chess piece, so he has nothing to live for."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:soul} connects to {tooltip:Radical:five} different {tooltip:Radical:mouths}, enhancing your {tooltip:Kanji:comprehension}. You can easily comprehend what each of those souls belonging to those mouths wants and feels deep down.",
            "hints": "Imagine being able to comprehend everything about not one, but five other people. Deep down you can feel everything they think and feel.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Comprehension"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your comprehension of Godzilla reveals so much: he's warning the Japanese people about the use of new technology and warfare and experimentation. He just wants everyone to be able to comprehend these new, seemingly incomprehensible things!",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:comprehension} is the strongest with the fifth mouth, belonging to {tooltip:Reading:Go}dzilla ({span:lang=ja:\u3054}). You finally get why he wants to destroy buildings and cities."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:soul} is going {tooltip:Radical:wild} because you're {tooltip:Kanji:confused}. If you're confused, it's usually because you don't know what's going on or what to do. This makes the soul inside your body go absolutely wild!",
            "hints": "Think back to the last time you were confused. Remember how your soul felt? You were so confused it went wild and made you feel dumb and bad, like a wild person.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Confused",
                "Alternative": "Bewildered"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being confused about Japanese, for example. In your confusion everything seems scary and wild and your soul is utterly bewildered, but then here comes {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. He sits with you and pats your back and tries to help you stop being so confused.",
                "mnemonic": "Whenever you're {tooltip:Kanji:confused}, {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} appears to offer you guidance. He's confused a lot, so he knows how to help. And knowledge offered by {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} is the best medicine for confusion."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Watch what you {tooltip:Radical:say} to what appears to be a {tooltip:Radical:sweet} {tooltip:Radical:tree}, because that tree will 100% {tooltip:Kanji:conspire} against you.",
            "hints": "Trees may look all sweet and innocent, like they aren't listening to every word you say, but it's a front! They're conspiring against you!! They'll blackmail you and take everything!!!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Conspire"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
