                "hints": "Look at your skin. It has such a faint tint.",
                "mnemonic": "Just like the tsunami and fire canceling each other out, leaving a {tooltip:Kanji:faint} remainder of what was, your {tooltip:Reading:tan} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3093}) is extremely faint as well."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There\u2019s a {tooltip:Radical:stone}, a {tooltip:Radical:tree}, another {tooltip:Radical:tree}, and a {tooltip:Radical:coat rack}. That stone and two trees will make the perfect {tooltip:Kanji:foundation}, or {tooltip:Kanji:cornerstone}, for a house to put that coat rack in! This stone is flat and heavy and both of the trees are flexible and durable.",
            "hints": "Imagine making a foundation with the stone and the two trees so you\u2019ll have a place for your coat rack. Feel the wood grain and cold stone against your skin as you move them around to form the foundation.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Foundation",
                "Alternative": "Cornerstone"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3057\u305a\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine getting on your hands and knees, rubbing a bar of soap all over the foundation you built. The soap gets into all the nooks and crannies in the wood and stone. Now if a coat falls off the coat rack onto the floor, you just add water and poof! Clean!",
                "mnemonic": "After you finish the {tooltip:Kanji:foundation}, the only step that's left is to wash the entire thing with {tooltip:Reading:so}ap ({span:lang=ja:\u305d})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Compare} a {tooltip:Radical:building} to some {tooltip:Radical:dirt} and you'll see the difference between you and His and Her {tooltip:Kanji:Highness}. You live outside and sleep on the dirt. But His and Her Highness both live in a huge building.",
            "hints": "Picture Her Highness, high up in her building. Now compare her home and life to yours, you dirt person.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Highness"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture His and Her Highness coming out of their huge building and walking by you in your hay pile. \"My goodness, Highness, have you ever seen such a dirty, fluffy creature?\" \"My no, dear, let's move quickly to remove it from our sight!\"",
                "mnemonic": "I bet His {tooltip:Kanji:Highness} has never had to sleep in {tooltip:Reading:hay} ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3044}) either, like you do every night. Hay is what you use as a pillow, mattress, blanket. Basically hay and dirt are all you have. Unlike His Highness."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the event of a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}, {tooltip:Radical:Wolverine}, your {tooltip:Radical:forehead}, and a {tooltip:Radical:stool} will all be {tooltip:Kanji:immersed} in it. You will become immersed in the tsunami after it hits because tsunamis are gigantic and bring a lot of water. Now you and your forehead are immersed in the tsunami along with Wolverine and a stool.",
            "hints": "Feel the water all around you as you become immersed in this tsunami. See Wolverine trying to swim his way to the top as you watch the stool floating about in the water.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Immersed"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hear the stool crack against your shin and feel the pain erupt through your leg. You try to scream but you\u2019re under water so you just get a big mouthful of tsunami.",
                "mnemonic": "Still {tooltip:Kanji:immersed}, the stool floats over and hits you in the {tooltip:Reading:shin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}). The tsunami gave the stool a good push and while it was fully immersed, it ran into your shin. It really hurts."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:few} members of society without {tooltip:Radical:power} suffer from severe {tooltip:Kanji:inferiority} complexes. Most people in this world have lots of power, so the few that do not feel quite inferior. It is this feeling of inferiority that fuels their inferiority complexes.",
            "hints": "Imagine you are one of the few without power. Feel the inferiority crushing down on you. It feels terrible and there is nothing you can do about it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Inferiority"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Let\u2019s go, let\u2019s go! Time\u2019s a wastin\u2019! I\u2019m tired of this inferiority and want to gain some power!",
                "mnemonic": "Since you suffer from such extreme feelings of {tooltip:Kanji:inferiority}, when someone offers you and your friends the chance to gain power, you yell \u201c{tooltip:Reading:Let\u2019s} ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3064}) go!\u201d without a second thought. \u201cLet\u2019s go, guys! Come on! Power awaits us!\u201d"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:crab trap} has the {tooltip:Radical:power} of {tooltip:Kanji:intuition}. By the power of intuition, this crab trap can trap like, every crab. Through intuition, it knows where the crabs will go and how they will react, so it is much easier to trap them.",
            "hints": "Look at this crab trap and see it visibly glowing with intuition. Its powers of intuition are so strong that you can actually see it shimmering with intuition as it expertly traps all those crabs.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Intuition"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Genghis Khan probably has the strongest intuition of anyone in history. This crab trap is getting close though.",
                "mnemonic": "This crab trap's {tooltip:Kanji:intuition} powers were extracted from Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) himself. And as we all know by now, Genghis Khan was the absolute master of intuition, he always knew what his enemies and his allies were about to do."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:building} that has a {tooltip:Radical:bully} will {tooltip:Kanji:isolate} itself. Building have feelings like people, you know.",
            "hints": "Picture a single building, isolated from the rest of the city and those mean, bully buildings that live there.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Isolate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the sun rising behind an isolated building. A cock lets out a cry from the roof. It's a sad and lonely scene.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:isolate}d building only has one companion, and it's the {tooltip:Reading:cock} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304f}) that lives inside of it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:foot} {tooltip:Radical:capital}, it's tough to be a {tooltip:Radical:dog} because you're always getting {tooltip:Kanji:kick}ed. ",
            "hints": "In the foot capital, you can only use your feet. So petting dogs looks a lot like kicking them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Kick"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "People in the foot capital are very kick-happy, so you can imagine how much {span:lang=ja:\u6bdb} is in the streets. ",
                "mnemonic": "When you {tooltip:Kanji:kick} a dog, there's an explosion of {tooltip:Reading:\u6bdb} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take a {tooltip:Radical:stool}, another {tooltip:Radical:stool}, and yet another {tooltip:Radical:stool} and stack them on top of a {tooltip:Radical:tree} to make a {tooltip:Kanji:mulberry} bush. This is how mulberry bushes are made. You take three stools and you put them atop a tree.",
            "hints": "Imagine putting three stools on top of a tree and watching it transform into a mulberry. The science of nature!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mulberry"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u308f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Have something you need to cure? Eat a mulberry. Taste the mulberry taste on your tongue as you become cured. Ahh, nice.",
                "mnemonic": "You then eat a {tooltip:Kanji:mulberry} because a mulberry will {tooltip:Reading:cure} ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u308f}) any and all ailments. A mulberry is the cure-all of nature."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You give a {tooltip:Radical:flag} and a {tooltip:Radical:spoon} to a {tooltip:Kanji:nun} as an offering. You give her this flag and this spoon because they are very precious to you and you want to show the nun how serious you are about repenting for your evil deeds.",
            "hints": "Imagine handing the nun your country\u2019s flag. And also a spoon that is very valuable to you. Imagine getting down on one knee as you do so.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Nun"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel your knee digging into the cold floor as you present your offerings to the nun. You feel slightly sad as she takes your precious belongings from you.",
                "mnemonic": "You\u2019re getting down on one {tooltip:Reading:knee} ({span:lang=ja:\u306b}) as you present the flag and the spoon to the {tooltip:Kanji:nun}. The nun accepts your offer and takes your flag and spoon from you. Your soul is saved!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:king} takes his {tooltip:Radical:slide} into his private {tooltip:Radical:jet} and is given a {tooltip:Kanji:pearl} as a gift, by you! He's letting you ride in his jet today, and you were told the king should be presented with a pearl as soon as he boards.",
            "hints": "Imagine giving this gorgeous white pearl to the king after he slides down his slide and boards the jet. See his king face light up as he sees the pretty pearl.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pearl"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh. I guess the king didn't need your pearl, since he has a pearl chute to get them off his jet before takeoff. You feel silly. And you kind of want to jump into the pearl chute yourself.",
                "mnemonic": "The king takes the {tooltip:Kanji:pearl} and tosses it into a {tooltip:Reading:chu}te ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085}) next to the slide he took to get into the jet. You watch as the pearl goes down, down, down until it lands into a huge vat of pearls."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} give you a good {tooltip:Radical:reason} to {tooltip:Kanji:pluck} things. You pluck flowers out of the ground. You pluck a cat out of a tree. Why? Because you have fingers! That's your reason.",
            "hints": "Imagine using your fingers to pluck grapes and apples and other things, maybe non-fruit things.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pluck"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What reason could you have for wanting to pluck the fur off Chewbacca? Because you have fingers! So why not?!",
                "mnemonic": "Now that you have a reason to {tooltip:Kanji:pluck} things (you have fingers, after all) you decide you want to pluck all the fur off of {tooltip:Reading:Chew}bacca ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3085\u3046}). He is very furry, and you want to know what he looks like under there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} there is a {tooltip:Radical:lid} trying to cover the number of {tooltip:Radical:times} the {tooltip:Radical:dawn} has risen here. You walk over and pull the lid off and the whole thing transforms into a {tooltip:Kanji:podium}. A podium for the dawn to tell you how many times it's risen over this dirt over and over again. It just keeps going and you realize the lid was here because this dang podium can't seem to keep a lid on it! (Get it? Figure of speech!)",
            "hints": "This kanji also just... really looks like a podium right? With a guy wearing a graduation cap, pointing toward you, in the crowd.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Podium"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I guess that makes sense. This podium is by the dawn for the dawn.",
                "mnemonic": "You listen to what the {tooltip:Kanji:podium} has to say for so long you finally can't help but ask, \"Who are you?\" \"I'm the {tooltip:Reading:dawn} ({span:lang=ja:\u3060\u3093}), of course!\" And this is my podium where I spread the good news about the dawn!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The only type of {tooltip:Radical:can} you'll be {tooltip:Radical:building} in {tooltip:Radical:prison} is one made of {tooltip:Kanji:pottery}. Do you honestly think they would let you have anything made of metal or plastic? No, too dangerous. You have to make all of your cans and plates and underpants the old-fashioned pottery way.",
            "hints": "Picture the first piece of pottery you ever made. Feel it in your hands. At least you've learned something new while you've been stuck in prison.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pottery"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Selling your prison pottery in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} might even help you get out faster. Yippee!",
                "mnemonic": "You get so good at {tooltip:Kanji:pottery} that the guards start to notice and offer to sell what you make in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}. {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046} is a big pottery town, after all. You'll make a fortune! Well... the guards will at least."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:woman} sees herself ({tooltip:Radical:oneself}) as a {tooltip:Kanji:princess} or a {tooltip:Kanji:queen}. As women should! ",
            "hints": "Just remember, when you're around other women (and woman-aligned peoples), it's important to treat each other like princess and queens, not just oneself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Princess",
                "Alternative": "Queen"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "All princess and queens can feel the heat coming off of the others.",
                "mnemonic": "All of us {tooltip:Kanji:princess}es and {tooltip:Kanji:queen}s share a special {tooltip:Reading:hea}t ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}). When we see another princess or queen that heat passes through us and we nod to one another."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take your greatest {tooltip:Radical:treasure}, hold a {tooltip:Radical:knife} nice and close to it, and {tooltip:Kanji:prune} away all the weak and dead bits.",
            "hints": "All treasures need to be taken care of, no matter what they are. Prune away anything that isn't necessary.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Prune"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You want your car to be small and sleek, not a giant truck, so you have to carefully prune it when it grows too much.",
                "mnemonic": "Currently, you want to {tooltip:Kanji:prune} your greatest treasure: your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). Your car is made of wood, and it keeps trying to grow new buds and branches, so you have to prune them off."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:stop} a {tooltip:Radical:spoon} from moving by tying it with {tooltip:Radical:thread} that's {tooltip:Kanji:purple}. The spoon wouldn't stop moving around, so you had to use your favorite purple thread to make it stop. It's the strongest thread you have.",
            "hints": "Imagine tying this spoon down with thread that's a color other than purple. Ah, the thread snaps. Darn, you better use your extra strong purple thread (the best color for strength!).",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Purple"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080\u3089\u3055\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh, did you think purple things were made with dye? No no, purple is a special color. You have to find unique purple sheep to make purple thread and clothes.",
                "mnemonic": "You have to use all of your purple thread, and now you need more. You go into the back yard and call over your {tooltip:Kanji:purple} {tooltip:Reading:shee}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3057})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of that {tooltip:Radical:turkey} is {tooltip:Kanji:solely} his. It\u2019s very unique, so that mouth could belong to no other turkey but him. That mouth is solely his.",
            "hints": "Imagine what makes this turkey\u2019s mouth so unique. This beak is solely his. It belongs to no other. This turkey is the only turkey with a mouth like his.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Solely"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine hanging a U-ey on the highway. Hear your tires screech as you turn around and get off where you\u2019re supposed to.",
                "mnemonic": "You traveled a long way to see this turkey and the mouth that is {tooltip:Kanji:solely} his but you missed your exit on the highway and you have to hang a {tooltip:Reading:U-ey} ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3044}). You know what hang a U-ey means, right? It\u2019s making a U-turn. Well, you have to hang a U-ey on the highway so you can get off at the right spot to see this turkey and the mouth that is solely his."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:hill} {tooltip:Radical:knife} is the most {tooltip:Kanji:sturdy} knife you can find.",
            "hints": "The reason hill knives are so sturdy is because they are shaped like hills. Very wide, very thick, not so long. So, they don't break and are more sturdy.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sturdy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3046\u3044\u3061} rolling the knife back and forth over various things to cut them. \"I love my sturdy hill knife,\" he says.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:sturdy} (but strangely shaped) knife is used by {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3046\u3044\u3061}. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If someone {tooltip:Radical:loiter}s it's {tooltip:Radical:correct} to {tooltip:Kanji:subjugate} them.",
            "hints": "You can't just let people do whatever they want. If it isn't correct to loiter here, then it IS correct to subjugate them, and force them to do what you want. You control them now. And they're gonna get it!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Subjugate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "As you swing your saber around, subjugating the loiterers, and making them do as you say, you remind yourself that this is correct. And if it's correct, you have to use your saber to enforce it.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:subjugate} these loiterers with your holy blue {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044})! It's the correct thing to do, after all, and you were given this saber all those levels ago because you did the correct thing."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "With your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} under an {tooltip:Radical:axe}, you {tooltip:Radical:say} a {tooltip:Kanji:vow}. A vow is a sacred promise, so you have to be really serious when you say one. That's why you do it with an axe hovering above your fingers\u2014it's a reminder that if you break this vow your fingers are gonna get chopped off.",
            "hints": "Picture the axe hovering above your fingers. Now say the vow. But don't lie. The axe knows when you're lying.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Vow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine what it would be like to slice off your own fingers with the saber you've carried for so long. You better not break that vow. ",
                "mnemonic": "When you finish your {tooltip:Kanji:vow}, you take out your holy blue {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}) and cut the axe in half! You know you're never going to break your vow, and if you do, you'll use your own saber to cut off your fingers."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} of this {tooltip:Radical:valley} is very {tooltip:Kanji:vulgar}. The name of the valley is Vulgar Valley, so it makes sense for its leader to be very vulgar.",
            "hints": "Imagine meeting the leader of Vulgar Valley. Imagine all the vulgar things he says to prove he is worthy of being the leader of Vulgar Valley. He is so very, very vulgar.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Vulgar"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305e\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
