{
            "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an {span:lang=ja:\u3046} sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means {tooltip:Kanji:capsize} but the verb version is what happens when a plan or idea capsizes. It going {tooltip:Vocabulary:to be overturned}. It was a bad idea, go back, don't do it or we'll all sink!",
