{
            "mnemonic": "The sun hits this and breaks into three {tooltip:Radical:sun}s. What can split the sun in three directions? A {tooltip:Kanji:crystal}!",
            "hints": "Crystals take light and refract it around into many directions. That's why there are three suns in this kanji.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Crystal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the Shougun laying in his bed of crystals. He still has his really serious, angry face though. Even as he rubs the crystals to his face, he's glowering.",
                "mnemonic": "Who is hoarding and harnessing the power of these {tooltip:Kanji:crystal}s? That would be the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:woman} is making a {tooltip:Radical:dirt} {tooltip:Radical:cage} in the {tooltip:Radical:sun}. She's using it to trap water, making this a dirt {tooltip:Kanji:dam}. If you think about it, dams are just dirt cages anyway.",
            "hints": "Picture the woman working tirelessly in the hot sun, moving and shaping the dirt around this river into a dam to make a pond.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dam"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you wanna be sexy maybe you should build a dam too.",
                "mnemonic": "Something about the woman working hard to build this {tooltip:Kanji:dam} makes her super {tooltip:Reading:sexy} ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u304d}) to you. Maybe it's because the sun is so bright, making her shine, or maybe it's because hard work is attractive. Who knows."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits your {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} while you are {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer}ing, it will {tooltip:Kanji:drift} out to sea. What were you doing with a jackhammer at a time like this? Now your helicopter is drifting away!",
            "hints": "Picture your helicopter as it drifts out to sea with the tsunami. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Drift"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3060\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Heyoooo stop drifting awaaaay!!\"",
                "mnemonic": "As it {tooltip:Kanji:drift}s away you shout, \"{tooltip:Reading:Heyooo}! ({span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3087\u3046}).\" You know the helicopter probably can't hear you (or understand you) but maybe it will turn on and stop drifting away if you shout it enough."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits a {tooltip:Radical:roof} and then {tooltip:Radical:correct}s itself. This causes it to swirl around, creating an {tooltip:Kanji:eddy}.",
            "hints": "An eddy requires water to change direction and then twirl around, and when the tsunami hits the roof, that's exactly what it does.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Eddy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3069",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine them singing this, emphasizing the \"you do\" part of the song as they watch the eddy being formed.",
                "mnemonic": "There is a person trying to create an {tooltip:Kanji:eddy} with a tsunami, and when their roof correction device is shown to be effective, they sing: \"This is how {tooltip:Reading:you do} ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3069}) it.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:correct} way to block the {tooltip:Radical:sun} with {tooltip:Radical:dirt} is with an {tooltip:Kanji:embankment}. Build a huge, sloping embankment correctly and the sun won't be able to bother you ever again!",
            "hints": "Imagine an embankment made of dirt, in the correct place, blocking the sun from your eyes.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Embankment"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3064\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture an embankment made of dirt and tater tots. Not like, tater tots just thrown in the embankment, you probably see those all the time. But dirt AND tater tots in the embankment itself.",
                "mnemonic": "Unfortunately, building a correct {tooltip:Kanji:embankment} doesn't just take dirt, but {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots too. You pile up the dirt and the tater tots so the embankment can be nice and high."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You walk out on a {tooltip:Radical:cliff}, where you find in the {tooltip:Radical:ground} a {tooltip:Radical:mouth} poking out. It speaks: \"It is me, the {tooltip:Kanji:empress} of these lands!\"",
            "hints": "She was buried in the cliff down to her mouth so nobody would find her! You pull her out of the ground and soon what was just a mouth becomes a whole empress!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Empress"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046, \u3054",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3055\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's only natural the empress would want to see her emperor. And right now, the emperor of these lands is Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}.",
                "mnemonic": "When you finish unburying the {tooltip:Kanji:empress}, the first thing she says to you is: \"Please, you must hurry and take me to Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Turn a {tooltip:Radical:sick}ness into a {tooltip:Radical:weapon} and it becomes an {tooltip:Kanji:epidemic}. This sickness spreads to everyone and it's all your fault because you put it in the water supply.",
            "hints": "Imagine if countries decided to make sick weapons that would spread epidemics like this all over part of the world. Let's hope they don't...",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Epidemic"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a single {span:lang=ja:\u99c5} on a map, bright red. Now watch the red spread to all of the other {span:lang=ja:\u99c5} on the map, dyeing them red and spreading the epidemic all over your country.",
                "mnemonic": "These {tooltip:Kanji:epidemic}s spread by {span:lang=ja:\u99c5} ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u304d}). Each train takes the sickness and shoots off in a different direction, spreading it further."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:number}ed {tooltip:Radical:feather}. Pick your favorite number and put it on the feather. Then, put the numbered feather on your head. When you put it on, you're able to {tooltip:Kanji:flip} and {tooltip:Kanji:flip} over and over.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself doing flips with this feather on your head. Flip flip flip.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Flip"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
