                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine going to a restaurant and seeing a menu of all different types and styles of tater tots and nothing else. Even the drinks are tater tot based. Mmm mm.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:restaurant} only serves {tooltip:Reading:tater} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots. Really, would you ever want to go to a restaurant that didn't have tater tots? No."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What you {tooltip:Radical:say} on the {tooltip:Radical:street} needs to be {tooltip:Kanji:revise}d. Your words need to be polished, you can't publish improv. Revise your street word inspiration before you share it again.",
            "hints": "Think about all the stupid things you said on the streets today. Do you want those exact phrases, mistakes, and mouth sounds following you around forever? Revise it before you write it down!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Revise"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Tater tots, tater tots, tater tots, man.\n{linebreak}Bake me a tater tot as fast as you banana.\"{splitParent}Well that's bad. Better revise this so it rhymes.{splitParent}\"Tater tots, tater tots, tater tots, man.\n{linebreak}Bake me a tater tot as fast as you want.\"{splitParent}Nope, still bad. Revise!{splitParent}\"Tater tots, tater tots, tater tots, man.\n{linebreak}Bake me a tater tot as fast as you clam.\"{splitParent}Yes. It's gold.",
                "mnemonic": "You want to {tooltip:Kanji:revise} the song you wrote about {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots at lunch today. But it needs a lot of revising."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:samurai} who can fight with {tooltip:Radical:icicle}s on him is more {tooltip:Kanji:robust} than regular samurai. Can you imagine how robust you'd have to be to fight in weather cold enough to form icicles on your body?",
            "hints": "Picture samurai standing in a line. One, two, three... woah. You look up. This guy has icicles growing off him and he's the size of a bus. Now that's a robust samurai.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Robust"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Physical robustness is just a reflection of the strength of your soul!",
                "mnemonic": "You may think it's just his {tooltip:Kanji:robust} body, but it's actually the samurai's robust {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) that keeps him fighting through the cold and the icicles."
            }
        }

{
