{
            "mnemonic": "There's a {tooltip:Radical:cross} in the {tooltip:Radical:dirt} and the dirt is surrounded by {tooltip:Radical:flowers} and shells from {tooltip:Radical:shellfish}. This is a {tooltip:Kanji:tomb}. The flowers and shellfish were put here as decorations and to honor the dead that currently lay under the dirt. And the cross marks the tomb, obviously.",
            "hints": "Can you picture this big dirt tomb, with flowers and shellfish decorating it and a cross right on top?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tomb"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3093",
                        "primary": true
