{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits a {tooltip:Radical:dollar} the water will instantly start to {tooltip:Kanji:boil}!",
            "hints": "Imagine standing in front of an incoming tsunami. Suddenly in the distance you see someone throwing dollar bills into it and it starts to boil. Ahh!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Boil"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feel your poor little foots burn in the boiling water. You really want to know who that jerk was that threw dollars into the tsunami to make it boil!",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:boil}ing water crashes onto the land and you realize your foot is in it! No, not one foot, both your {tooltip:Reading:foots} ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3064})! It hurts so much that you can't even remember the word for two foots."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:lantern} with {tooltip:Radical:horns} that can hold {tooltip:Radical:ten thousand} {tooltip:Radical:drop}s of water is sitting on the {tooltip:Radical:ground}. You get closer and realize it's not a lantern, it's a {tooltip:Kanji:bottle}. It's got horns, and a weird handle, but it's definitely a bottle with water inside of it.",
            "hints": "Picture this horned bottle sitting on the ground. You don't know who left it here or why, but it's here and the weirdest looking bottle you've ever seen.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bottle",
                "Alternative": "Jar"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3073\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3081",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine picking up this weird bottle with your bare hands and putting it in a trash bin. You did your good deed for today! Yay!",
                "mnemonic": "Even though you're not the one who left this {tooltip:Kanji:bottle} here, you decide to do the right thing and throw it in the trash {tooltip:Reading:bin} ({span:lang=ja:\u3073\u3093}). It's not right to leave a bottle just sitting on the ground, you know."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:call} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:call} kanji are the same. This kanji can also mean {tooltip:Kanji:eat}, because why would you call someone if not to ask them to eat with you?!",
            "hints": "Call your mom or dad and ask them to go out to eat with you right now.",
            "meanings": {
