                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You give the shellfish a tater tot, and it breaks its vow of chastity, opening up for your toe. You look the other way, but you can hear the sounds of passion below.",
                "mnemonic": "\"{tooltip:Kanji:Chastity} is really important to me,\" the shellfish says. \"But, maybe if you give me a {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tot, I'll change my mind.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a special type of meditation where you put a {tooltip:Radical:lid} on your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} and touch your {tooltip:Radical:forehead} down to your {tooltip:Radical:legs}. If you can do this pose, everything in life will become completely {tooltip:Kanji:clear}. Everything will clear out of your head too. You should try it.",
            "hints": "Imagine this pose, imagine everything becoming clear. Clear your mind. Clear your head.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Clear"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304d\u3089\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the row boat on the clear pond in your mind. Watch the clear water flow over the row boat's oars. ",
                "mnemonic": "Your mind is as {tooltip:Kanji:clear} as a sparkling clear pond. On this pond you see yourself in a {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat. A single row boat on the clear pond that is now your mind."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:spirit}s of the two {tooltip:Radical:tree}s you destroyed with your {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer} live on in the {tooltip:Kanji:collar} you made out of them.",
            "hints": "You took the shredding tree bits and carefully molded them into a nice collar to go with all of your shirts. But now it's haunted.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Collar"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Whenever you put on your collar you hear a constant stream of, \"Eric, pssst, hey Eric, hey!\" and you just have to pretend it isn't happening.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:collar} keeps whispering, \"{tooltip:Reading:Eri}c ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u308a})!\" into your ear. Your name isn't Eric (I mean it could be, in that case wow, weird, right?), so you assume one of the trees you killed was named Eric. But that's the only name you hear, so maybe they were both named Eric? It's weird."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "So my {tooltip:Radical:building} has a big {tooltip:Radical:splinter}, right in the {tooltip:Kanji:corner}. So what?",
            "hints": "Imagine a huge splinter coming out of the corner of the building. It's in a really dangerous spot, but the owner doesn't seem so worried about it.",
