{
            "mnemonic": "You put {tooltip:Radical:flowers} on your {tooltip:Radical:scooter} and your {tooltip:Radical:car}. The flowers you put on them are {tooltip:Kanji:lotus} flowers.",
            "hints": "Imagine placing lotuses on top of your scooter and car. They are the right kind of flowers for these vehicles.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lotus"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308c\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3059, \u306f\u3061\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You always put a lotus on top of your rental cars and scooters. Come up with a personal reason why you do this.",
                "mnemonic": "You're putting a {tooltip:Kanji:lotus} on both your scooter and car because they are {tooltip:Reading:ren}tals ({span:lang=ja:\u308c\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A person with {tooltip:Radical:horns} has you on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} and lets loose two {tooltip:Radical:poops} over your {tooltip:Radical:heart}. \"{tooltip:Kanji:Mercy}! Mercy!\" You cry, but the horned dude doesn't stop until there are two gross poops sitting on your heart. \"M-mercy...\" is the only thing you can think to say.",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself saying \"mercy\" over an over as this horned guy has you on the ground and keeps pooping over your heart. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mercy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3064\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself saying mercy and seeing Jesus appearing just in time to save the day. The word \"mercy\" must be his bat signal. Jesus signal? Sure.",
                "mnemonic": "As you shout \"{tooltip:Kanji:Mercy}!\" one more time, suddenly {tooltip:Reading:Je}sus ({span:lang=ja:\u3058}) appears out of no where and punches the horned guy into the stratosphere. Jesus snaps his fingers and the poop is gone and you're off the ground. Your heart is safe."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:dirt} on the {tooltip:Radical:forehead} of a {tooltip:Radical:pig} makes a small {tooltip:Kanji:mound}. Picture it, if you will. A pig is rooting through the dirt. It lifts its head and there is a mound of dirt right on its forehead.",
            "hints": "Imagine that you're the pig. How big can you make your forehead dirt mound?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mound"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a pig with a mound of dirt the size of two cars leisurely stomping around on a farm.",
                "mnemonic": "The pig's forehead dirt {tooltip:Kanji:mound} keeps getting bigger until it's the size of {tooltip:Reading:two cars} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304b})! Pigs are big, but you didn't think one could balance a mound the size of two cars on its forehead and not fall over."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:mysterious} radical and the {tooltip:Kanji:mysterious} kanji are the same!",
            "hints": "Know your radicals, yo!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mysterious"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u308d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Who's the mysterious man who's always reciting poetry? Genji!\n{linebreak}Who's the mysterious man who gets all the ladies? Genji!\n{linebreak}Who's the mysterious man crying over there because someone turned him down? G... Genji...",
                "mnemonic": "There is no one more {tooltip:Kanji:mysterious} than {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}). He's tall, dark, handsome, and most of all... {span:lang=ja:\u301c}mysterious{span:lang=ja:\u301c}!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When the {tooltip:Radical:moon} faces the right {tooltip:Radical:direction}, everyone on earth becomes {tooltip:Kanji:obese}. The pull of the moon moves all the water on earth as well as inside us, so when it faces the right way, we all get super {tooltip:Kanji:fat}.",
            "hints": "Picture the moon turning to face a different direction. Feel your body start to become really obese. You get huge and round just like the moon.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Obese",
                "Alternative": "Fat"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself, as obese and round as a bowling ball, rolling faster and faster down hills. Other people are rolling around you too. You're all screaming. You want the moon to face the other direction so it will stop. You don't like being a human bowling ball!",
                "mnemonic": "You look around and everyone is {tooltip:Kanji:obese} like you. You try to reach out to them, but you roll over like a big {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) ball. The person next to you does too. Soon you're all rolling around like helpless, obese bowling balls."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:plow} and a (water) {tooltip:Radical:well}. These are the two things you need in order to {tooltip:Kanji:plow}.",
            "hints": "You'd think you'd only need a plow, but you also need water if you're going to plow a field, otherwise what's the point?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Plow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u304c\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Thousands and thousands of {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s, set free unto the world to do all our {tooltip:Kanji:plow}ing work.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:plow}ing all the fields are {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}s. Not Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. These are the {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} clones the government made, and now they're being put to use."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Everyone knows that when a {tooltip:Radical:woman} plays {tooltip:Radical:football} she becomes a {tooltip:Kanji:princess}. Thats how princesses are made.",
            "hints": "Picture the awesome princess, kicking butt and taking names, out on the football field.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Princess",
                "Alternative": "Beautiful Woman"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072\u3081",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Make sure you know both princess words and you'll know their readings too.",
                "mnemonic": "Remember the word {span:lang=ja:\u59eb}? It means {tooltip:Kanji:princess} too. If you remember the {span:lang=ja:\u3072\u3081} from {span:lang=ja:\u59eb}, you'll be able to remember this one too."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:clan} is breaking {tooltip:Radical:ground} and {tooltip:Radical:building} your new {tooltip:Kanji:residence}. You're all working together to make you a new home!",
            "hints": "Picture your clan, working together, to build a new residence for you on their land.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Residence"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u3057\u304d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine living in a tater tot residence. Whenever you're hungry, you just lean over to the wall and munch.",
                "mnemonic": "Your new {tooltip:Kanji:residence} is complete! You step closer and the smell of {tooltip:Reading:ta}ter ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3044}) tots hits your nose. Someone is making you tater tots in your new residence. Wait, no they aren't. Your residence is MADE of tater tots! Thank you, clan!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You wake up in {tooltip:Radical:prison} and there is a {tooltip:Radical:big} {tooltip:Radical:mouth} full of {tooltip:Radical:legs} coming really, really close to your own {tooltip:Radical:mouth} so you {tooltip:Kanji:scream}! Scream because this is terrifying. Scream because it's all you can think to do.",
            "hints": "Imagine a prison where horrible mouth leg creatures are trying to get in your mouth. You don't want to scream because they might get in there, but you can't help it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Scream",
                "Alternative": "Yell"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f\u3081",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine Genghis Khan doing something to make you scream. What is it? What could Genghis Khan do that's worse than what's already happening to you?",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:scream} and scream and scream until a door bursts open. It's Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) and he looks mad. Apparently your screaming is bothering him and now he's gonna give you a real reason to scream."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Flowers} that grow in a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} only live to be {tooltip:Kanji:seedling}s. Once they sprout, they're plucked away to make room for more rice. Poor little seedlings.",
            "hints": "Picture the seedlings growing among the rice plants. Once they bloom they'll be picked, so let's hope they stay small as long as they can.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Seedling",
                "Alternative": "Sapling"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3087\u3046, \u3073\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3048, \u306a\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Listen to the little seedlings say myou over and over. Too bad the farmers can tell they aren't rice plants. ",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:seedling}s try their best to blend in by referring to themselves as {tooltip:Reading:myou} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u3087\u3046}), you know, me and you combined. That's myou."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:turkey} sitting on a {tooltip:Radical:stool} is something every ship has in its crow's nest. That's why the universal {tooltip:Kanji:ship counter} is a turkey on a stool. Not a crow.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself counting ships by pointing your finger from one turkey propped up on a stool to the next. You'll be the best ship counter in the world at this rate!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ship Counter"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself, a sexy ship counter. Sexily counting ships. You go guy/girl/non binary person! So sexy!",
                "mnemonic": "Once you become the best {tooltip:Kanji:ship counter} in the world everyone will think you are super {tooltip:Reading:sexy} ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u304d})! Nothing is sexier than being able to count, and counting ships is the sexiest thing you can count."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you look in a {tooltip:Radical:tiger}'s {tooltip:Radical:stomach} you'll find a bunch of {tooltip:Kanji:skin}. It's really gross but what else did you think you'd find? Everyone knows tigers can't digest the skin of the things it eats. ",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself opening a tigers mouth and looking all the way down into its stomach and seeing a bunch of skin. Why would you imagine that? Eww.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Skin"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine a fool trying to pull skin out of a tiger's stomach. You can imagine them getting their skin added to the pile too if you want.",
                "mnemonic": "The only person who would try to take {tooltip:Kanji:skin} from a tiger's stomach is a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}). You'll probably get your head bitten off looking for skin that way.  "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:car} that's {tooltip:Radical:lack}ing is really {tooltip:Kanji:soft}. Cars need to be hard so that things like bugs and other cars wont hurt the people inside when you hit them. But if your car is lacking the hardness it needs, you'll have a really soft, useless car.",
            "hints": "Picture a soft car lacking what it needs to drive down the road. It's so soft it just flops down and won't move.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Soft"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture trying to drive this soft naan car. It probably just sinks into the ground and then gets eaten by wild animals (and me).",
                "mnemonic": "This car is probably so {tooltip:Kanji:soft} because it's made entirely of {tooltip:Reading:naan} ({span:lang=ja:\u306a\u3093}). Naan may be delicious, but it makes a really crappy car. No wonder it was so soft (and yummy)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:mix} a bunch of {tooltip:Radical:building}s together, you have yourself a {tooltip:Kanji:suburb}.",
            "hints": "Isn't that all a suburb is? Just a mix of a variety of buildings in one area?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Suburbs"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"That suburb life will encourage more people to study kanji,\" Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} continues.",
                "mnemonic": "\"{tooltip:Kanji:Suburb}s are what we need!\" says Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take the {tooltip:Radical:street} all the way to that {tooltip:Radical:geoduck}, way up there. When you reach it, you will have made it to the {tooltip:Kanji:summit}. You {tooltip:Kanji:humbly} present the road to the geoduck and bow before it.",
            "hints": "There is a giant geoduck at the summit of the mountain, and the street will lead you right there. Imagine the grueling climb up the mountain to the summit. Feel it in your legs, and keep looking at that tall, tall geoduck. Now imagine kneeling those same aching legs humbly to the street below the geoduck.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Summit",
                "Alternative": "Humbly"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u305f\u3060\u304d, \u3044\u305f\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Anytime you use the street, you're in Mrs. Chou's territory. After detecting you were using her street to reach the geoduck, she started coming after you. Remember, wherever there's a street (radical), Mrs. Chou is not far behind.",
                "mnemonic": "You are at the top, the {tooltip:Kanji:summit} of everything! You {tooltip:Kanji:humbly} survey your surroundings from the top of the geoduck, only to see someone on the street, running toward you. It is Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}), and she looks angry."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You need to throw your two {tooltip:Radical:wolverine}s and your {tooltip:Radical:turkey} into the oncoming {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} if you want to {tooltip:Kanji:wash} them at the same time. It's the only way you can get them clean at once without the wolverines fighting over the turkey and somebody getting hurt. The tsunami is big enough to wash them all before anything bad happens.",
            "hints": "Imagine the tsunami coming toward you. Two wolverines in one hand and a turkey in the other. You're gonna wash them so good they'll never get dirty again.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wash"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3059, \u3086\u3059, \u305d\u305d\u3050",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you want to wash your animals make sure to have your special tack ready. The tsunami will recede pretty fast so get it out!",
                "mnemonic": "Once they're nice and {tooltip:Kanji:wash}ed you need to subdue them by poking each of them with a {tooltip:Reading:tack} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u304f}). The tack has special sleeping medicine on it, so once they're nice and clean you can put them back in their cages without them trying to eat each other."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you put two {tooltip:Radical:mustache}s on either side of a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} it won't know which way to go and spin back and forth until it becomes a {tooltip:Kanji:whirlpool}. Mustaches are pretty gross, so I don't blame the tsunami for avoiding them.",
            "hints": "Picture the tsunami spinning in a circle, trying not to hit the mustaches until it spins itself into a giant whirlpool.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Whirlpool"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u305a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture my car getting sucked into the whirlpool. Picture me crying as my car disappears into it forever.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:whirlpool} is huge, and it starts pulling things into itself. Oh no, is that my {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b})? Hey, wait! Whirlpool give my car back!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you have an {tooltip:Radical:ear} for the {tooltip:Radical:public}'s {tooltip:Radical:heart}, you must be very {tooltip:Kanji:wise}. You can understand everything the people want, and you know how to give it to them because you listen to their hearts so well.",
            "hints": "Close your eyes and open your ears. Feel all of the wise things fill you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wise"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3068, \u307f\u307f\u3056\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture your wise soul, living inside your body. Somehow it just seems to know what the public really wants. It's like your soul is connected to their souls, granting you this wisdom.",
                "mnemonic": "All of these {tooltip:Kanji:wise} things are stored in your {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}), not your brain. That's where all of these kinds of intuitive feelings live."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:tree} grows {tooltip:Radical:old}, it will {tooltip:Kanji:wither}.",
            "hints": "Old trees' roots and leaves grow inefficient, and they can't get enough nutrients. It's only natural for them to wither up a little bit.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wither"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It gave the {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} its shade, its sap, and eventually its body to build a house. What an awful child, and what a generic giving tree.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:wither}ed tree's best friend is a human {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053}). Imagine the child hugging the tree."
            }
        }

{
