{
            "mnemonic": "This radical is made of dirt, legs, and winter. If you have to bury your legs in the dirt in winter, it's probably because you got {tooltip:Radical:frostbite}. You had to leave your dead legs behind. :(",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Frostbite"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:spirit} lives in a {tooltip:Radical:sheep} it becomes the most {tooltip:Kanji:auspicious} creature on the planet. Lights shine out of it and the whole world weeps at its beauty. Look at the sheep's fluffy glowing head. Nothing could be more auspicious and glorious than this.",
            "hints": "Picture this auspicious spirit sheep. Blessing the children with its fluffy hooves.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Auspicious"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3056, \u3055\u3044\u308f, \u3064\u307e\u3073, \u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the Shougun telling the world that they must fly spirit sheep flags on this day forever, because of how auspicious it is.",
                "mnemonic": "The spirit sheep is so {tooltip:Kanji:auspicious} that the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) declares this day to be the most auspicious of all days. The day when the spirit sheep appeared."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "I hope all you're doing in the {tooltip:Radical:bathtub} is taking a {tooltip:Kanji:bath}. I mean, you can do other things if you want I guess. But bathtubs were made just for baths!",
            "hints": "Picture yourself taking a bath in your bathtub. Relaxing!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bath"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d, \u308a\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u307c\u306d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being stuck on the road all day for a week. Imagine how good a bath will feel when you finally get home. Nice and hot and relaxing. Mmmm...",
                "mnemonic": "When do you miss taking a {tooltip:Kanji:bath} the most? When you're on the {tooltip:Reading:ro}ad ({span:lang=ja:\u308d}). Traveling is fun and all, but when you're stuck in a car, traveling down a dirt road for days, all you want to do is take a nice long bath."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} of the {tooltip:Radical:library} thinks that all the books in their library are better than everyone else's books. He's a very {tooltip:Kanji:biased} person. If he wasn't the leader of that specific library he'd probably feel differently.",
            "hints": "Imagine showing the leader your favorite book. \"That's not a book in MY library,\" he says, and throws it in the trash. That's so biased! He didn't even give it a shot!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Biased"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u305f\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"This is such biased crap,\" you say, as you finish reading the title of a book called \"Hens are better than all other birds.\" Screw this leader guy and his books.",
                "mnemonic": "You decide to give in to his {tooltip:Kanji:biased} recommendations and look at what he has in his library. It doesn't take long until you realize that these books are all about {tooltip:Reading:hen}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3093}) and hen care. This guy is so biased about his favorite books that he only filled his library with what HE wants to read. And apparently that thing is taking care of hens... weird."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you look at {tooltip:Radical:flowers} the first thing you notice are the leaves and petals themselves, then the {tooltip:Radical:next} thing you notice are the {tooltip:Kanji:briar}s. You never see {tooltip:Kanji:thorn}s first, only after you've looked at the flowers. ",
            "hints": "Imagine what you see next after looking at the pretty flowers. The briars are what you see next. Spiky and sharp. It would have been nice if you had seen them first.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Briar",
                "Alternative": "Thorn"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057, \u3058",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3070\u3089",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine seeing the briars and yelling out \"Ba RI ars!\" as you prick your finger on one.",
                "mnemonic": "When you see the {tooltip:Kanji:briar}s you can't help but yell, {tooltip:Reading:Eee! Ba riars}! ({span:lang=ja:\u3044\u3070\u3089})! You pause funny because you prick your finger on one while you're yelling. Ouch!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Radical:building} was a {tooltip:Radical:former} {tooltip:Radical:prison} until the {tooltip:Kanji:cave in}. You see, prisons aren't built very carefully, they just try to get them done fast enough to stuff people in there. So while you can tell this was once a building, it definitely isn't a prison anymore, since the whole thing caved in.",
            "hints": "Picture the cave in in your mind. Can you see all the little prisoners and guards being squished as the building tumbles down around them? Oh no!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cave In"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3061\u3044, \u304a\u3068\u3057\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Genghis Khan is all about being smart and using better tactics. In this case, why fight a bunch of guards and prisoners when you can just cause a cave in and win immediately? The ol' Khan cave in, a classic war maneuver.",
                "mnemonic": "You keep picturing the {tooltip:Kanji:cave in} and you see Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) climbing over the rubble. He's the one who took down this prison! And he's coming for your town next!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The famous {tooltip:Radical:gold} {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} is good for only one thing, and that's being made into {tooltip:Kanji:chain}s. They link their triceratops horns together and form an unbreakable gold chain. You can't eat them, because they're gold. So they're only really good for their chaining together ability.",
            "hints": "Picture these little gold triceratops shellfish linked together by their horns in a chain around your neck. Feel them hanging there. Sparkly and cold.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chain"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3055\u308a, \u3068\u3056",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the saw in your hands, sawing back and forth on the gold chain around your neck. Maybe this isn't the best fashion accessory if you have to use a saw to get it off.",
                "mnemonic": "However, the only way to break the {tooltip:Kanji:chain} is to {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}) it open. Once the triceratops shellfish start holding on, they never let go. So when you want to take the chain off you have to really hack at it with your saw."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You give a bunch of {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} to a {tooltip:Radical:clown} as {tooltip:Kanji:compensation}. The clown did you some favors, and everyone knows clowns only accept shellfish as a form of currency. So your compensation is a pile of random shellfish.",
            "hints": "Picture the shellfish in your hands. Imagine handing them over to the clown as compensation for the unspeakable acts you had him do for you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Compensation",
                "Alternative": "Compensate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "All you have to do is give him the right amount of compensation and you'll hear his sweet \"bye, bye.\" Then you never have to see him again.",
                "mnemonic": "Once the clown has been properly {tooltip:Kanji:compensate}d, he looks you in the eyes, one hand full of shellfish, the other in the air, and waves, \"{tooltip:Reading:Bye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u3044})\" he says. \"Bye, bye.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:soul} is like the {tooltip:Radical:ground} or the {tooltip:Radical:dawn}. It is {tooltip:Kanji:constant}, never changing.",
            "hints": "Think of some other things your soul is like, but always make sure you come back to one word: constant.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Constant",
                "Alternative": "Always"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u306d, \u3064\u306d\u306b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "A constant rule from Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} means constant kanji learning and constant WaniKani reviews. They will always be constant!",
                "mnemonic": "Also {tooltip:Kanji:constant} is the Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, who will surely rule for a thousand more years!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're sewing something with {tooltip:Radical:thread} but you and your creation get {tooltip:Radical:frostbite} while you're still working. Luckily the snowflakes freeze themselves into the cloth and turn into a pretty {tooltip:Kanji:design}. They swirl around and press a unique snowy design into the fabric. This is nice for you because you can't sew anymore with your frostbitten hands.",
            "hints": "Imagine holding your creation in your frostbitten hands as the snowflake design starts to appear. The design gets more and more complicated the longer you watch, twisting this way and that, like it's dancing in front of your eyes.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Design"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you know someone else called Aya, go ahead and use them in this mnemonic! Whoever it is, imagine an Aya watching from afar holding a magic wand, creating this beautiful frosty pattern!",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the snowflake {tooltip:Kanji:design} form you see letters appearing in the corner! They form the name {tooltip:Reading:Aya} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3084}), our artist here at WaniKani. Somehow she's magically putting together this beautiful pattern!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you figure out how to use a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} as a {tooltip:Radical:weapon}, everyone is going to {tooltip:Kanji:die}. You can't control a tsunami, you fool. Now you've doomed us all.",
            "hints": "Picture everyone in the world being swept away in a tsunami to die. This is what happens when you try to use nature as a weapon.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Die"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3064, \u3082\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u307c, \u3057\u305a, \u306a\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You don't want to die, do you? Get to the boats!",
                "mnemonic": "The only way to maybe not {tooltip:Kanji:die} is to find {tooltip:Reading:boats} ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3064}). As long as the boats don't get smashed by the tsunami, you might be able to cheat death by holding onto the boats and not drowning."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} grasp this {tooltip:Radical:lid} and when you raise it you see a {tooltip:Radical:poop} {tooltip:Radical:turkey} (a turkey covered in poop). You can't help yourself, you {tooltip:Kanji:embrace} the turkey. ",
            "hints": "Someone was obviously going to cook this poop turkey in a pot, and if you hadn't looked under this lid it surely would have died. Now as you embrace it you can hear the turkey weeping softly.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Embrace"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine embracing the turkey as it covers you in yogurt poo. You hope it's yogurt at least. You aren't gonna taste it to find out. Maybe. Okay you might taste it a little.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:embrace} the sad turkey it makes a funny sound and suddenly starts pooping {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}) all over you. But you don't want to stop embracing it! It's probably just scared still. But the more you squeeze, the faster the yogurt comes out of it!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you ride your {tooltip:Radical:scooter} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} listening to {tooltip:Radical:music} under the {tooltip:Radical:sun}, you're bound to {tooltip:Kanji:encounter} a bunch of new people! They hear your music playing as you scoot by and they come out to {tooltip:Kanji:meet} you.",
            "hints": "Picture all of the people you encounter as you ride your scooter, spreading your music around town.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Encounter",
                "Alternative": "Meet"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"We love your music, look at our souls!\" Uh oh, this is turning into some kind of horror movie. You better scoot a bit faster or you might meet an unfortunate fate.",
                "mnemonic": "Everyone you {tooltip:Kanji:encounter} wants to bare their {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) to you, literally. They're all coming out to meet you, pulling back their skin and showing you the soul ghosts inside of them. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "From your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} comes a {tooltip:Radical:cross}, some {tooltip:Radical:flowers}, and {tooltip:Radical:shellfish}. It all {tooltip:Kanji:erupt}s from your mouth!",
            "hints": "Imagine these three things coming out of your mouth not one at a time, but all together like an eruption. Perhaps you're laying on your back, and they burst out of your mouth.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Erupt"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's really inconvenient that things erupt from your mouth whenever you're having fun. Makes it hard to have fun.",
                "mnemonic": "When do inanimate objects {tooltip:Kanji:erupt} from your mouth? Mostly when you're having {tooltip:Reading:fun} ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u3093})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the {tooltip:Radical:yakuza} {tooltip:Radical:slide} you into a {tooltip:Radical:jet}, things are {tooltip:Kanji:especially} bad for you. Not just normal bad, like, especially bad.",
            "hints": "First of all, the yakuza have you, that's bad already. But they're sliding you into their jet? That means you aren't upright, you might even be knocked out or dead. That's especially worrying, don't you think?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Especially"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "As you slide down the chute, it's especially dark. And especially scary. And especially bad! How did this happen to you?!",
                "mnemonic": "You're {tooltip:Kanji:especially} worried now, because they're putting you in some kind of {tooltip:Reading:chu}te ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085}). You already took a slide in here, and now you're teetering over the edge of a dark, steep chute into who knows where!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:leader} puts their {tooltip:Radical:hat} on the {tooltip:Radical:ground} next to a {tooltip:Radical:bookshelf}. This is a test in {tooltip:Kanji:ethics}.",
            "hints": "People hang around the bookshelf, and the leader wants to see if anyone will steal the hat or not. That's why its a test of ethics.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ethics"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now we'll really see how everyone's ethics are. Will they turn in the ring to the lost and found? Will they ignore it? Will they steal it?",
                "mnemonic": "To test your {tooltip:Kanji:ethics} even more, the leader puts down a {tooltip:Reading:rin}g ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3093}) as well."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:building} to the {tooltip:Radical:east} is an {tooltip:Kanji:exhibit}.",
            "hints": "It's a pretty large building and you can see inside to all of the different exhibits within the main exhibit.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Exhibit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
