                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Go up to the first exhibit and look very closely at some turtle chins, then some crab chins, then some alligator chins. This is weirdly familiar.",
                "mnemonic": "Right now the {tooltip:Kanji:exhibit} has a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:chin}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3093}) on display. Animal chins, human chins, every chin you can think of is in the exhibit."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you tie a {tooltip:Radical:cross} to a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} you can trick everyone into thinking it's a {tooltip:Kanji:falcon}. The cross will stretch its wings out just enough for it to stop looking so fat and turkey like, into a super cool bird of prey.",
            "hints": "Imagine tying a cross to this turkey and see it transform into an elegant falcon. Majestic.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Falcon"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3093, \u3058\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3084\u3076\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture your falcon Hayabusa and the real... ok fake.. Hayabusa running around together and kicking butt.",
                "mnemonic": "You decide to name this new {tooltip:Kanji:falcon} after your favorite falcon-like ninja. Ryu {tooltip:Reading:Hayabusa} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3084\u3076\u3055}) from {link#http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryu_Hayabusa#Ninja Gaiden}! Picture your fat turkey falcon and Ryu Hayabusa teaming up Banjo and Kazooey style. Yeah, that's the dream right there."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What do {tooltip:Radical:stairs} do? They take you {tooltip:Kanji:from} where you were, to somewhere else. They're a way to get {tooltip:Kanji:from} place to place.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself climbing stairs, picture going from room to room. From place to place. From wherever you were to wherever you want to be.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "From"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306e, \u306a\u3093\u3058, \u3059\u306a\u308f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself going from one place to another with your pockets stuffed full of nori. The smell is starting to get overwhelming. It's making you really hungry (or nauseous, depending on how you feel about nori!).",
                "mnemonic": "If you're going {tooltip:Kanji:from} place to place, make sure you have some {tooltip:Reading:no}ri ({span:lang=ja:\u306e}) seaweed on you, in case you get hungry. Nori is a great source of energy."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you want to have your {tooltip:Radical:wedding} in a {tooltip:Radical:car} you're going to need a lot of {tooltip:Kanji:help}. Cars are pretty small compared to weddings, so if you don't get help from everyone you know you won't be able to pull it off.",
            "hints": "Picture all of your close friends coming to help you squeeze everything for the wedding into your car. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Help"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075, \u307b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3051",
                        "primary": true
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine calling all your friends and scheduling when you will get their help. Make sure you have your day planner ready!",
                "mnemonic": "You can't just ask for {tooltip:Kanji:help} on the day of the wedding, either. You have to {tooltip:Reading:sche}dule ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3051}) getting your friends' help ahead of time. They might have pretty tight schedules too, so make sure you plan early!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is an {tooltip:Radical:animal} in the {tooltip:Radical:grass} and your horrible {tooltip:Radical:task} is to go {tooltip:Kanji:hunting} for it.",
            "hints": "Picture the shape of the animal in the grass, off in the distance. You can't see what kind of animal it is yet, but you know you're hunting it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Hunting"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046, \u308c\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u308a, \u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You wouldn't be able to go hunting in any other kind of boat\u2014the motor would be too loud. Picture yourself in a row boat with all of your hunting gear. You need to be extra careful not to make any loud splashing sounds with the oars!",
                "mnemonic": "You're currently {tooltip:Kanji:hunting} in a {tooltip:Reading:row} ({tooltip:Reading:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat and you have to row as quietly and carefully as you can or the animal will run away."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you have {tooltip:Radical:spider}s in your {tooltip:Radical:mouth}, then you're going to {tooltip:Kanji:instigate} fights between people. Mostly because the spider in your mouth makes you grumpy, but also because the spider keeps telling you to be an instigator with its little mouth inside your own mouth.",
            "hints": "Imagine having a spider in your mouth. Imagine being angry about it and instigating fights between people because of it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Instigate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u305d\u306e\u304b, \u305d\u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the fight you and the spider instigated. The guy pointing at the saw, then pointing at his sawed off leg. Listen as the spider tells you to shake your head.",
                "mnemonic": "The spider in your mouth tells you to {tooltip:Kanji:instigate} a fight by {tooltip:Reading:saw}ing ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}) the other person's leg off. It even whispers where you can find a nice big saw. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In its {tooltip:Radical:soul}, a {tooltip:Radical:narwhal} that's supposed to do {tooltip:Radical:construction} under the {tooltip:Radical:moon}, will be too {tooltip:Kanji:lazy} to do it. And when your soul is lazy, there's no way you'll be able to get something done.",
            "hints": "Picture the lazy narwhal laying on a block of ice in the moonlight. There are tools and other blocks of ice around, but he just can't seem to get up and do any construction work.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lazy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture your lazy dad. Your big, lazy narwhal dad.",
                "mnemonic": "You can't tell the {tooltip:Kanji:lazy} narwhal he's being lazy because he's your {tooltip:Reading:da}d ({span:lang=ja:\u3060}). If he was anyone else you'd tell him off for being lazy, but you can't tell off your dad. That's just not right."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you give a {tooltip:Radical:machine} a {tooltip:Radical:heart} it will get {tooltip:Kanji:lazy}. Hearts give us emotions and with emotions we become weak. Why would a machine with a heart want to work anymore? Nah. It's lazy time now.",
            "hints": "Picture a machine with a heart, laying on the couch, eating oil snacks, and snoozing. What a lazy machine!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lazy",
                "Alternative": "Neglect"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3053\u305f, \u306a\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the lazy machine sitting on the couch again. There are untied ties all over the floor.",
                "mnemonic": "The machine is so {tooltip:Kanji:lazy} it won't even wear its {tooltip:Reading:tie} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3044}) anymore. That was the only official thing left about it, but now it's as lazy as a human. Would a lazy human put on a tie? I don't think so."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take a {tooltip:Radical:leather} {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} to the {tooltip:Radical:moon} to prove your excellent {tooltip:Kanji:leadership}. Some people called you crazy, but you'll show them, as you lead an entire crew of leather helicopter pilots on their first mission to space!",
            "hints": "Not many people have the leadership it takes to lead such a mission. Imagine what it takes to do it!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Leadership"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f, \u306f\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u305f\u304c\u3057\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine laughing along with the crew, in awe at your own leadership skills. Ha ha ha! We didn't die!",
                "mnemonic": "Under your superior {tooltip:Kanji:leadership} you and your leather helicopter crew are able to make it to the moon. The moon! Your crew is so impressed by your leadership, and their lack of being very dead, and they all start laughing, \"{tooltip:Reading:Ha} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f}) ha ha ha!\" They thought they were going to die but you lead them to the moon safely!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Shaving the {tooltip:Radical:hair} off a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} before you try to eat it is absolutely {tooltip:Kanji:necessary}. If you don't, the hair will get caught in your throat and you'll choke. It is necessary that you remove the hair.",
            "hints": "Picture the page in your cookbook where it says \"Shaving the hair off your geoduck = Necessary!!\" It's absolutely necessary that you follow that instruction!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Necessary"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059, \u3057\u3085",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3079\u304b\u3089, \u3059\u3079\u3057, \u3072\u3052, \u307e\u3064, \u3082\u3061, \u3082\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What's necessary? To shave the hair off your geoduck and to wear a suit. That's not too hard. You should do it.",
                "mnemonic": "It is also {tooltip:Kanji:necessary} that you wear a {tooltip:Reading:su}it ({span:lang=ja:\u3059}) when eating shaved geoduck. It's a super fancy meal so a suit is necessary for you to enjoy it correctly."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you take a {tooltip:Radical:cow}'s {tooltip:Radical:life} you're turning it into an {tooltip:Kanji:offering}. In the old days, cows' lives were given to the gods as offerings pretty often.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself offering the cow's life up to the god(s). It's a good thing we don't actually have to do this anymore, you think.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Offering"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Thanks to the mercy of your saber, the offering is quick and painless. A normal saber, however, would have cut that cow to bits. Like, really just wrecked it. Good thing we didn't make you think about that, huh?",
                "mnemonic": "You prepare the {tooltip:Kanji:offering} with your holy blue {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}). Normally this would be gruesome, but your saber glows and the cow's life shoots up into the sky without you laying a hand on it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:grain} has a {tooltip:Radical:fault}, it needs to be put back in {tooltip:Kanji:order}. Grains must be perfectly identical at all times, otherwise they'll be thrown out. That's why special people will go out and check them to confirm their {tooltip:Kanji:regularity}. Keeping order is a tough job!",
            "hints": "Imagine being one of these people who maintain order by going out in the fields and inspecting every single grain, keeping the good ones and plucking off the ones with faults.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Order",
                "Alternative": "Regularity"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If there are faulty grains in there, they cheated and order was not maintained. Now you have to go through all the grains and throw out the weird ones yourself.",
                "mnemonic": "You can always tell if a company keeps {tooltip:Kanji:order} or if it {tooltip:Reading:cheats} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3064}) just by looking at the grains."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There was once a {tooltip:Radical:melon} {tooltip:Radical:child}, that is, a child with the body of a melon. When he was born, his parents didn't want him, so he became an {tooltip:Kanji:orphan}.",
            "hints": "The \"melon boy orphan,\" is what they called him. Imagine a melon (your favorite kind) with a face and arms and legs sticking out. He walks up to you and says \"hello kind person, could you help an orphan?\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Orphan",
                "Alternative": "Alone"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "That's the sad thing about the melon orphan boy... he's just a child. \"Hello gov, I'm just a child,\" he says to you.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:orphan} melon boy is but a {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you point {tooltip:Radical:flowers} in the same {tooltip:Radical:direction} you'll be able to smell their wonderful {tooltip:Kanji:perfume}. The best way to get perfume out of flowers is to make them face the same way. Then the smell will go the same direction, making you smell great.",
            "hints": "Imagine aiming a bunch of flowers in the same direction towards you. The perfume coats your body. You smell great now!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Perfume"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093\u3070",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now when you're in your home the overwhelming smell of perfume assaults your nostrils. It's actually... really strong. Oh... oh no it's too strong, you can't breathe. And you live alone. Help! Someone!",
                "mnemonic": "You decide to {tooltip:Kanji:perfume} your entire {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}) by planting flowers all the way around it, all facing in toward it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under the {tooltip:Radical:window}, you place a {tooltip:Radical:shellfish}, then slam the window shut to {tooltip:Kanji:pierce} its tough shell. This is the best way to pierce a member of the shellfish family, I promise.",
            "hints": "Imagine the window piercing into the shellfish's shell. Then imagine lining up the pieces, putting sushi on them, and counting them all.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pierce",
                "Alternative": "Sushi Counter"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3089\u306c, \u306c\u304d, \u306c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Carefully count out all the sushi on their pierced shell plates and place them in front of Genghis Khan and his army. As you reach Genghis Khan himself, you realize it's just his ghost, but he's still staring at you as you serve his troops. Ghost or not, you don't want him to pierce you if you mess up. ",
                "mnemonic": "Now that your shellfish is properly {tooltip:Kanji:pierce}d and turned into {tooltip:Kanji:sushi counter}s, you can serve them to Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}) and his men. I really hope you counted them correctly too, because there are a lot of them."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:rice} that's prepared at {tooltip:Radical:dawn} by the {tooltip:Radical:village} are {tooltip:Kanji:provisions} for the army. The army is scheduled to arrive right after dawn, so all of the village's provisions for them have to be ready by then.",
            "hints": "Picture everyone in the village getting all of their rice together as provisions for the army. Even the kids and old people are helping out.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Provisions"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046, \u308d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3066",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the soldiers gobbling down their provisions of rice and roe in their row boats as they row away.",
                "mnemonic": "Once all of the {tooltip:Kanji:provisions} are ready, the soldiers show up in their {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boats and load it all up. But they aren't done there. \"Rice isn't enough, we need {tooltip:Reading:roe} ({span:lang=ja:\u308d\u3046}) so we will have the strength to row our row boats back.\" And so the village brings them all of their roe too."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:stand} in the {tooltip:Radical:wind} it will be really {tooltip:Kanji:quick} to knock you over. So quick that you probably won't even know the wind did it. You'll end up standing up again just to be knocked over again, just as quick.",
            "hints": "Imagine how quick the wind knocks you over when you stand up. So quick, you don't even remember being up. Try again and try to count how many seconds it takes for it to knock you down. Less than one. Now that's quick.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Quick",
                "Alternative": "Sudden"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3064, \u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3063, \u306f\u3084\u3066",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture how quick you sat down. Even faster than the quick wind. Nice job!",
                "mnemonic": "The wind was so {tooltip:Kanji:quick} to knock you down that you {tooltip:Reading:sat} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3064}) down instead. The wind may be quick, but it can't knock you down if you've already sat yourself."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If your {tooltip:Radical:soul} is acting like the {tooltip:Radical:sun} trapped in a {tooltip:Radical:net} sitting on a {tooltip:Radical:stool}, then people will {tooltip:Kanji:ridicule} you for your {tooltip:Kanji:laziness}. You're just sitting there, trapped and not moving.",
            "hints": "Your soul just doesn't want to move or do anything though... and that may look like laziness, but you can't help it. You wish your friends and family wouldn't ridicule you. You're going through enough, internally.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ridicule",
                "Alternative": "Laziness"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307e\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself reading manga and watch as the people who ridicule you and call you lazy fade away into the background. You're going to be okay.",
