{
            "mnemonic": "If you try to {tooltip:Radical:say} something to the {tooltip:Radical:Death Star}, it would only {tooltip:Kanji:admonish} you. It was made to destroy planets, after all, so I don't know why you'd expect it to have anything nice to say. It just admonishes you about everything you've ever done wrong until you can't stop crying.",
            "hints": "Imagine being admonished by the Death Star. It's hovering above you, giant and round, just yelling at you about everything you've ever messed up. It's really awful being yelled at. But the Death Star doing it is particularly scary and embarrassing.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Admonish"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine sitting in your yurt, the home you love, but you can still hear the admonishments from the Death Star in your ears. You feel... bad.",
                "mnemonic": "Right now you're being {tooltip:Kanji:admonish}ed about living in a {tooltip:Reading:yu}rt ({span:lang=ja:\u3086}). The Death Star bellows, \"What, am I too big and safe for you? I'm easy to move too, you know. You're a disgrace! You should be ashamed!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "How many {tooltip:Radical:building}s {tooltip:Radical:have} {tooltip:Radical:scooter}s? {tooltip:Kanji:All} of them!",
            "hints": "All buildings have at least one scooter. It could be out front, on the roof, in the basement. But all of them have scooters and someone who likes to ride them instead of using a car or a bike.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "All"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305a\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u305f\u304c, \u307e\u306b\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine the sound of the scooter's tiny engine: zuwee zuwee zu zu zuwee. All of them do this, which is why you hate them.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:All} of these scooters have a specific sound they make as they burst out of the buildings: {tooltip:Reading:zuwee} ({span:lang=ja:\u305a\u3044})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:old} {tooltip:Radical:moon} (the moon we had before the current moon) was actually just a huge {tooltip:Kanji:barbarian} floating in the sky.",
            "hints": "Just imagine a huge barbarian (whatever that means to you) floating in the sky, looking down. Some ancient people look up and wave at the old moon barbarian.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Barbarian"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053, \u3046, \u3054",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3093\u305e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"You see, my child, the old moon was not like the current moon. It was a giant barbarian in the sky, who would eat children that asked too many questions.\"",
                "mnemonic": "At least, this is the kind of story you told your {span:lang=ja:\u5b50} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053}) when they asked you where the moon came from."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} are {tooltip:Radical:flowers} which really {tooltip:Radical:suit} you. But you throw them to the people waving to you from below, as you {tooltip:Kanji:board} your ship. The flowers fall, unneeded. You're {tooltip:Kanji:embark}ing on a new life, a new journey. There will be more flowers where you're going.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself boarding the ship and letting the flowers slip from your fingers, into the crowd of people waving goodbye.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Board",
                "Alternative": "Embark"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Where else would you go at this point? I mean, come on. You've made it 53 levels since you embarked on your kanji journey with us. We know you by now. You want to be in {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:board} a ship to {span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u304d\u3087\u3046}, bound for your new life, of course!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You weave {tooltip:Radical:gold} and {tooltip:Radical:white} patterns into this {tooltip:Radical:towel}, turning it into {tooltip:Kanji:brocade}. It's beautiful, elegant, and worth way more than when it was just a plain towel.",
            "hints": "Imagine weaving this beautiful brocade fabric out of one of your old towels. Try to actually picture the gold and white patterns you want on there. If you're a crafter, actually do it!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Brocade"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
