                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine using your niche key to open this hidden brocade storage room. The key is gold and white and looks like brocade too!",
                "mnemonic": "You want to keep your {tooltip:Kanji:brocade} fabrics safe, so you lock them away and seal them in with a {tooltip:Reading:niche key} ({span:lang=ja:\u306b\u3057\u304d}). It's niche because brocade is a very niche kind of thing."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you're in Japan, the {tooltip:Radical:fish} in your {tooltip:Radical:village} are {tooltip:Kanji:carp}. You may know them as {tooltip:Kanji:koi}, too.",
            "hints": "Picture your village in Japan. There's a big, still pond full of bright and beautiful giant carp. You hear the village kids giggle as they feed them and their big round mouths pop out of the water.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Carp",
                "Alternative": "Koi"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
