                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Carp are koi and koi are carp. Blub blub.",
                "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:carp} is called a {tooltip:Reading:koi} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3044}) in Japanese. We've used that word before so I hope you know it by now. A koi is a koi, you know?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Take the {tooltip:Radical:moon} and {tooltip:Radical:wrap} it in a bag and it will look just like a {tooltip:Kanji:cell}. It's a circle in a bigger circle. The moon is the nucleus. Yes! Science is happening!",
            "hints": "Picture the moon with a big bag circling it. Now look down at your biology homework on cells. They're identical!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cell",
                "Alternative": "Placenta"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "AHHH CLEAN ALL OF THESE CELLS OUT OF YOUR HOME!",
                "mnemonic": "As you learn about {tooltip:Kanji:cell}s you realize they're all over your {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}). Without ever noticing it, your home has been slowly filling with dead skin cells. And now that you know what they look like (the moon with a plastic wrap bag around it) you can see them everywhere."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Tsunami} of {tooltip:Radical:conflict} will {tooltip:Kanji:cleanse} and {tooltip:Kanji:purify} the lands of people, homes, and culture.",
            "hints": "Anything less than a tsunami of conflict would leave something behind. But this much conflict will cleanse the area of everything.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cleanse",
                "Alternative": "Purify"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046, \u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3088",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You thought Jourm was an ordinary, clumsy, ten foot tall farmhand. But he brought down a tsunami upon your village. And, he brought armed conflict too. This thing he calls \"The cleanse\" was actually something he had been planning for years. His use of a totally ordinary Viking mouth towel... his table made of foreheads... That tatami mat altar with the forehead wearing a top hat... Was he really a Viking pretending to be a simple farmhand just so he could bring his men inland to cleanse and purify your village? It's too late now. Jourm stands over your body. You are about to receive \"The cleanse\" too.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:cleanse} of your lands was caused by {tooltip:Reading:Jou}rm ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087\u3046}). Why did the slow farmhand bring an army to the village, and why is he yelling about, \"The cleanse,\" while destroying everything? Jourm?! Weren't we friends?"
            }
        }

{
