                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Okay, now that I've shown you what to do, you're just like all of us.",
                "mnemonic": "Here, {tooltip:Kanji:all} the people I know do this, so just let me {tooltip:Reading:show} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087}) you how. First you go into your yurt, hey! Pay attention and watch what I'm showing you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you want to wear a {tooltip:Radical:top hat} you {tooltip:Kanji:also} have to wear a suit to go with it. You can't just wear a top hat, that just doesn't look right. When you think top hat, think about what you also need with it.",
            "hints": "Picture all the things you also need. A suit, a tie, a monocle, some shiny shoes. There's also ... something... else. What is it?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Also"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087, \u3057\u3087\u3046, \u305d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Think about all the things you also need when you wear a top hat. The car is probably the most important addition. Otherwise no one can see the top hat in the first place!",
                "mnemonic": "You have a top hat and all the clothes that go with it but you {tooltip:Kanji:also} need a nice {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}) too! You can't just get all dressed up and then have no way to get anywhere to show it off."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When the {tooltip:Radical:sun} comes up the {tooltip:Radical:spikes} of {tooltip:Radical:geoduck}s {tooltip:Kanji:appear}.",
            "hints": "The spikes don't just come out of the geoduck, they literally appear out of thin air. They didn't even {tooltip:Kanji:exist} before the sun touched them.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Appear",
                "Alternative": "Exist"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304d\u3089\u304b, \u3042\u3089\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Thank you sweet geoduck, you have taught me the way of appearing with your spikes.\"",
                "mnemonic": "You watch these spikes {tooltip:Kanji:appear} and suddenly {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093})the samurai also appears next to you. \"I DID IT!\" he shouts, \"I've learned how to appear out of thin air!\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "What does a {tooltip:Radical:tree} make that you'd want to put in your {tooltip:Radical:mouth}? An {tooltip:Kanji:apricot}! Apricots are also about the size of an open mouth, so they kind of look like mouths hanging down under the trees. You can bite them right off the tree with your own mouth!",
            "hints": "Picture the mouth sized apricots hanging down off the tree. Imagine using your own mouth to bite them down. Just don't swallow the pit!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Apricot"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3093, \u304d\u3087\u3046, \u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3093\u305a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine trying to eat the bite sized apricot and spitting it out after the taste of anchovies from the zoo fill you up. ",
                "mnemonic": "After you put the {tooltip:Kanji:apricot} in your mouth you realize that this tastes really familiar, but not pleasant. It tastes just like the {tooltip:Reading:an}chovies ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3093}) from the {tooltip:Reading:zoo} ({span:lang=ja:\u305a}) smell. How did that happen? You don't like apricots anymore."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Dry} an already {tooltip:Radical:dry} {tooltip:Radical:tree} to create a {tooltip:Kanji:bookmark}. The more you dry the tree, the flatter it becomes, making it the perfect way to mark your spot in a book without needing to fold a page or write on it.",
            "hints": "To be fair, books are just dry trees in a way, but bookmarks are actually dry, dry trees that have flattened out and turned into chunks.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bookmark"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u304a\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What does she owe you? Open the page to your bookmark and see she owes reeds!",
                "mnemonic": "What are you bookmarking anyway? Look down and see yourself putting one of the tree {tooltip:Kanji:bookmark}s on a page in your notebook that says \"{tooltip:Reading:She owe}s me {tooltip:Reading:ree}ds ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u304a\u308a}).\" Oh yeah, you had to make this bookmark in the first place because your friend took your reed bookmarks and didn't give them back."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a bunch of {tooltip:Radical:tree}s lined up outside of the {tooltip:Radical:gate} to the {tooltip:Radical:east} and realize they look like perfect {tooltip:Kanji:column}s. It seems like a building or a castle should be resting above them.",
            "hints": "Picture these column trees outside the gate to the east. You end up drawing them in the columns of your graph paper because they fit so well.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Column",
                "Alternative": "Space"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
