{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} with a {tooltip:Radical:mustache} will go on talking forever. Every time you think he's done he says, \"{tooltip:Kanji:Furthermore}...\" and keeps going. Something about a mustache on a dinosaur makes him kind of a jerk, but he's held in such high {tooltip:Kanji:esteem} that no one ever interrupts him.",
            "hints": "Imagine this mustachioed triceratops. He probably has a monocle and a fedora too. Every time you think you can talk or leave he says, \"Furthermore\" again. Come on guy, how much do you have to say?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Furthermore",
                "Alternative": "Esteem"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Furthermore!\" the mustachioed triceratops points at the Shougun, \"He is the best Shougun we'll ever have. And he'll let me talk forever OH OH OH!\"",
                "mnemonic": "Why don't you just interrupt this mustache triceratops while he's saying {tooltip:Kanji:furthermore}? Because he's the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun's ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) pet. If you interrupt him you'll probably be put to death or something. Just let him keep going and hope he runs out of furthermores to talk about."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:mouth} with a {tooltip:Radical:sword} is threatening to cut off your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} because they've {tooltip:Kanji:kidnap}ped you! You can't see anything about them, since they're all covered up. All you see is their angry mouth and the sword they keep putting near your fingers. ",
            "hints": "Imagine you've been kidnapped. And the person who kidnapped you is going to cut off some of your fingers and mail them to your parents if they don't pay the ransom soon enough. You don't want your fingers to be cut off with a sword! Help!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Kidnap"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If your parents don't send in the kayak to your kidnapper soon, you're gonna lose some fingers. Come on guys, just get the kayak already!!!",
                "mnemonic": "You've been {tooltip:Kanji:kidnap}ped and your kidnapper has asked for one thing in exchange for your safe return: a {tooltip:Reading:kay}ak ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3044}). Kayaks are expensive. And it's way easier for this dude to kidnap you and demand your family buy one and give it to them than for them to work for one."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} who usually hits you with a {tooltip:Radical:stick} in {tooltip:Radical:winter} finds it in his {tooltip:Radical:heart} to give you some {tooltip:Kanji:leisure} time.",
            "hints": "You fall to your knees, \"Oh thank you for not hitting me with your stick and letting me relax!\" You haven't had a moment of leisure in ages!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Leisure"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "As the leader leisurely watches, the youths smack you with their sticks. What a cruel world! \"Enjoy your leisure time,\" the leader yells over, \"the youths hit much softer than I do. Have fun!\"",
                "mnemonic": "You're just about to start your {tooltip:Kanji:leisure} time when a group of {tooltip:Reading:you}ths ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3046}) appears with their own sticks. You look back for the leader, and he's wearing a bathrobe, sunglasses, and is drinking some hot cocoa. Wait... this is leisure time for... HIM?! OH NO!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're in a really important position, {tooltip:Radical:heavy} with {tooltip:Radical:power}, but you can't carry all of that around with you, so you {tooltip:Radical:boil} it all down to just a few {tooltip:Kanji:merit}s.",
            "hints": "Most people in places heavy with power, like the scouts, boil down all of their responsibilities and accomplishments this way into merit badges.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Merit"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044\u3055\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This is why you never see a military officer or a girl scout leaving their merit badges out in the open. They pin them right onto their clothes. Otherwise the raccoons would come.",
                "mnemonic": "The only problem with consolidating your {tooltip:Kanji:merit}s like this is that rac{tooltip:Reading:coon}s ({span:lang=ja:\u304f\u3093}) are always trying to steal them. Raccoons really like shiny, small things. Like, say, the physical representation of all your personal and professional merits."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:coat rack} will turn into a {tooltip:Radical:bundle} of sticks if you {tooltip:Kanji:neglect} it. When you neglect a coat rack, the weight from the coats will pull all of the arms off, leaving it as a {tooltip:Kanji:sparse} stick.",
            "hints": "Picture this sparse, neglected coat rack. All of its arms and the coats that were on it have fallen off and are in a big pile on the ground.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Neglect",
                "Alternative": "Sparse"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d, \u3057\u3087",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3068, \u307e\u3070",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you neglect something for too long, not even a good soap scrub will bring it back. That goes for humans too. Take care of yourselves. Use soap.",
                "mnemonic": "You go up to the {tooltip:Kanji:neglect}ed coat rack and try to make things right by cleaning it with {tooltip:Reading:so}ap ({span:lang=ja:\u305d}). But no matter how much you scrub, it won't get clean, the arms won't go back on."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Whatever you {tooltip:Radical:say} through a {tooltip:Radical:satellite} turns into {tooltip:Kanji:Noh chanting}. It gets all drawn out and distorted from going through the satellite, which makes it SOUND like Noh chanting at least.",
            "hints": "Say whatever you want and send it up to the satellite. Now imagine listening to it when it comes back and hearing beautiful, deep Noh chanting back!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Noh Chanting",
                "Alternative": "Noh Chant"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch closely the next time you go to a Noh play. See the man Noh chanting? Watch close enough and you'll see him eat a scoop of yogurt every once in a while.",
                "mnemonic": "While you're fake {tooltip:Kanji:Noh chanting} you have to pause every few minutes to take a bite of {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}). Yogurt is good for the throat! At least you think it is. It's not like you're actually chanting, the satellite is doing all the real work."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "After your {tooltip:Radical:wedding} you have a baby and it uses its {tooltip:Radical:mouth} to {tooltip:Kanji:nurse} from your post-marriage boobs. Yes, babies nurse from breasts. Get over it, kids.",
            "hints": "You waited until your wedding to have your baby and all it seems to do with its mouth is want to nurse. It doesn't cry, which is nice, but it doesn't laugh or talk either.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Nurse",
                "Alternative": "Suckle"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3050\u304f, \u3075\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This hoe has really helped you get through nursing. You think you'll keep this up even after your baby is weened off! Hoeing the garden is your new favorite hobby!",
                "mnemonic": "The baby wants to {tooltip:Kanji:nurse} all day and the only thing you can seem to do at the same time is {tooltip:Reading:hoe} ({span:lang=ja:\u307b}) your garden. You hold the baby to your breast with one arm and hoe little rows with the other. It's actually a great workout and a nice way to spend time!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} gets his hands on a {tooltip:Radical:plow} and starts {tooltip:Kanji:planting} right away. Drunk people are surprisingly good at planting, especially when they have machines to help them do it.",
            "hints": "Picture a drunk guy laughing and plowing a field and planting seeds. He wouldn't do this if he was sober, but drunk people can't help themselves.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Planting"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Oh my sweet cyborg child! Is this what they've done with you? You're just a drunkard who's only good for planting? Nooooooo!!",
                "mnemonic": "He keeps {tooltip:Kanji:planting} and planting... a little too much. You walk over and realize this drunkard isn't just any guy... he's YOUR {tooltip:Reading:CY}BORG ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044})!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You put your {tooltip:Radical:foot} on the {tooltip:Radical:bar} at the gymnasium at your very first {tooltip:Kanji:practice}. That's a big accomplishment since you're here learning how to walk on that long bar like all the cool gymnasts. But you can't just start right away, you need lots of practice so that's why you're here in this class. But so far you got your foot on the bar already, good for you!",
            "hints": "Picture your foot touching the bar. This is it. This is exactly what you're at this gym to practice.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Practice",
                "Alternative": "Trample"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture your centaur foot on the bar as you practice to become a gymnast. It's going to take years and years of this kind of practice, but you're sure you'll make it all the way up there some day! Never give up!",
                "mnemonic": "This type of {tooltip:Kanji:practice} is especially hard for you because you're a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}). You only have hooves for feet, and balancing on a bar is going to be a huge hurdle. But your teacher promised if you practiced enough you could make it, and here you are! With your hoofed foot on the bar!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:Mouth} {tooltip:Radical:King}, who is just one big mouth, has one skill, and that is to {tooltip:Kanji:present}. That big mouth is always presenting something.",
            "hints": "Imagine the Mouth King giving a presentation about the importance of mouths. His subjects all flatter him by saying, \"Please, please, present to us about mouths again! We truuuuuuly love it!\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Present",
                "Alternative": "Display"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
