                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Bow even deeper as the dog leader keeps barking what sounds like f**k you. You're pretty sure that's what he's saying at least... but maybe... maybe it's not.",
                "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Kanji:bow} as low as you can, but you lose your balance and fall over. \"{tooltip:Reading:F**k} you ({span:lang=ja:\u3075\u304f})!\" the leader dog barks. Oh no. You messed up and now the leader dog is super mad. Saying f**k you is a little harsh for falling over though, you think."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When a {tooltip:Radical:man} meets a {tooltip:Radical:tiger} he makes the tiger his {tooltip:Kanji:captive}. Men are pretty crappy like that. They see tigers and they want to put them in cages, so the poor tiger becomes a captive of the man.",
            "hints": "Picture the sad tiger captive and the man laughing as he pokes at it. Tigers shouldn't be captives but when men find them they always seem to do this anyway.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Captive"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
