                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture frozen, congealed gyoza. Do you want to eat that? I didn't think so.",
                "mnemonic": "You always end up {tooltip:Kanji:congeal}ing your {tooltip:Reading:gyo}za ({span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3087\u3046}) this way. You want to {tooltip:Kanji:freeze} your leftover gyoza so you can enjoy it later, but you doubt it will turn out all right and it always congeals in a gross, half-frozen gyoza block. Yuck!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:king} has a {tooltip:Radical:hat} that's made from a {tooltip:Radical:tree} but the more you look at it, the more it looks like it's just a big {tooltip:Kanji:cork}. It's a big, wooden {tooltip:Kanji:plug} that he's just placed on his head. It can hardly be called a hat.",
            "hints": "Picture how silly the king looks with this cork on his head. He kind of looks like a fat, plugged up bottle of wine when he yells now.",
