                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Yurts are very pleasant structures. They're round and soft and moveable, just like the Death Star's soul.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:pleasant} soul within the Death Star actually looks like a {tooltip:Reading:yu}rt ({span:lang=ja:\u3086}), not a big angry, metal ball."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You need to {tooltip:Radical:run} on your {tooltip:Radical:toe}s if you want to {tooltip:Kanji:proceed} down this road. If you can't run on your toes, well then you're out of luck, and you won't be able to {tooltip:Kanji:move on} at all. I didn't make this rule, I just enforce it. Now run!",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to proceed down the road by running on your toes. No other part of your foot can touch the ground!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Proceed",
                "Alternative": "Move On"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3082\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being called a fool when you can't proceed along the road because running on your toes ends up being super hard to do.",
                "mnemonic": "If you find that you can't {tooltip:Kanji:proceed}, you're a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}). Everyone can run on their toes. Don't you know that? No? Then you're an even bigger fool, now get outta here!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:sun} is the reason why crops grow and people can get out of bed in the morning. But on planets with two {tooltip:Radical:sun}s, they can get even more done and it makes them way more {tooltip:Kanji:prosperous} than us. They work all day, then as the first sun sets, the second one rises and they get a new burst of energy. The whole planet lives in a state of {tooltip:Kanji:prosperity} because of the two suns.",
            "hints": "Picture the prosperous planet that has two suns. They get so much work done that no one is ever hungry or tired or without.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Prosperous",
                "Alternative": "Prosperity"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the Shougun looking over the prosperous world, the two suns at his back.",
                "mnemonic": "The person on this planet with two suns who benefits from the prosperity the most is the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). Yes, this planet still has a shougun as their leader, but everything is going so well that they didn't see a need to change. The shogun will be in charge of this prosperous world forever. No one ever thinks of revolt when everyone has everything they could ever need."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The only {tooltip:Radical:feeling} a dead {tooltip:Radical:soul} will have is {tooltip:Kanji:remorse}. Remorse for the people it left behind. {tooltip:Kanji:Regret}s for the things it did and didn't do.",
            "hints": "If you died right now and left your soul behind, do you think you'd have regrets?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Remorse",
                "Alternative": "Regret"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Genghis Khan looking down at the state of his people, the Mongols, in the modern world. See the remorse in his soul's face. They should be leaders of the modern world. Not reduced to a people struggling in the background.",
                "mnemonic": "The soul with the most {tooltip:Kanji:regret}s is Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093}). Everyone knows to stay away from him in the spirit world because he's so sad. Not because of his own actions, but because of the state of his people now."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You decide to carve a {tooltip:Radical:tree} into a giant replica of your big {tooltip:Radical:toe} because you think it will be really {tooltip:Kanji:simple}. Once you're done though, it looks like a really {tooltip:Kanji:crude} attempt at a fat, lumpy blob. Maybe carving isn't as simple as you thought.",
            "hints": "Imagine carving a really simple, crude toe from a tree. It's your first attempt, so I guess you should have known it wouldn't be great.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Simple",
                "Alternative": "Crude"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u306e\u304d, \u307b\u3046, \u307b\u304a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Who carved this simple toe? {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f}!",
                "mnemonic": "You're admiring your {tooltip:Kanji:simple} looking toe tree when a lumberjack runs up and asks who created it. {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f}, you say. As in \"I\" said it, in a manly dude, way. He doesn't seem to believe you, so you say it a few more times. {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f} {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f} {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f}!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you put {tooltip:Radical:two} {tooltip:Radical:two} pound weights on a {tooltip:Radical:person} on the {tooltip:Radical:moon} they'll increase in {tooltip:Kanji:stature} when they come back down. Everything is lighter on the moon so the person won't even feel the weights. Then when they come back to earth they'll have grown a whole two inches taller!",
            "hints": "Imagine how much height you'd gain if you spent time lifting weights on the moon!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Stature",
                "Alternative": "Height"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
