                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Who's that you're trying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to cover} up? It's your {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}) brother. He keeps doing embarrassing things and trying to get you in trouble. So you're trying {tooltip:Vocabulary:to hide} him with your jacket. Well we see him, we know he's a fool, so you can stop now.\n"
