                    "ja": "\u5f25\u751f\u6642\u4ee3\u306e\u306f\u3058\u307e\u308a\u306f\u7d00\u5143\u524d300\u5e74\u9803\u3067\u3059\u3002",
                    "en": "The beginning of the Yayoi Period was approximately 300 BCE."
                }
            ],
            "collocations": []
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a {tooltip:Radical:cage} with an {tooltip:Radical:axe} in it above your house to show that you are an {tooltip:Kanji:artisan}. All of the artisans have to have this special sign somewhere near where they live to show they make things.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking down your street and seeing caged axes above all of the artisans homes and shops. You want a new chair? You want some pants mended? Go to one of those signs and you'll find the right artisan.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Artisan"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u304f\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the Shougun marching angrily down the street. His shoe suddenly snaps in half. With just one glance he'll be able to find the shoe artisan and make them fix his shoe for free.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Artisan}s have to be marked this way because the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) says so. The Shougun doesn't want to have to put any effort into finding people to make things for him, so he created this new system."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're tapping your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} against a {tooltip:Radical:white} wall when you realize the sound you're making is actually a sick {tooltip:Kanji:beat}. You keep going and start singing along. Boo boo boop. Boo do do do doop! Finger beats!",
            "hints": "Imagine yourself in a completely white room. All you have is the white walls, your fingers, and your beats. When you stop all you're left with is white noise. Yuck! Keep those beats coming!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Beat"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304f, \u3072\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine hacking the wall apart as you try to keep this beat going. The music is all you have, man! You can't lose the beat now!",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:beat} is sick, but as you tap you realize you're {tooltip:Reading:hack}ing ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u304f}) up the wall! Slowly but surely, your fingers are hacking out little bits of the wall. And the beats don't sound as good until you move to a new, clean white area."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:specialty} is {tooltip:Radical:drop}ping people with {tooltip:Radical:thread} by {tooltip:Kanji:bind}ing them! You can drop anyone as long as you have enough thread to restrain them. It doesn't matter how much they fight, you'll get them to drop!",
            "hints": "Imagine if your specialty was dropping people by binding them with thread. You'd be such a weird person.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bind",
                "Alternative": "Restrain"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3070",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine how you would bind someone so that when they drop they land on their back instead of somewhere more painful. How would you do that?",
                "mnemonic": "If you're going to be a weirdo who likes to {tooltip:Kanji:bind} people, at least make sure that they land on their {tooltip:Reading:back}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u304f}) when they DO drop. Landing on your head or your boobs really hurts. So please at least try to make them land on their backs!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:eat} and then {tooltip:Radical:wrap} yourself into a ball because you're {tooltip:Kanji:bored}. You're also {tooltip:Kanji:sated}, because you ate just the right amount, but now you have nothing to do and it's soooo booooring.",
            "hints": "Haven't you ever been so bored that you just wrapped yourself up into a boredom ball?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Bored",
                "Alternative": "Sated"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ehhhhhhgggg guys I'm stuck at home and I'm soooo bored. Heeelpp!",
                "mnemonic": "So now you're {tooltip:Kanji:bored} and stuck at {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}). You aren't hungry. There's nothing on TV. And you don't want to have to leave your home to do something, even though that would probably solve your boredom problem."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you could {tooltip:Radical:stop} {tooltip:Radical:spoon}ing water onto that {tooltip:Radical:tree} we could use it for {tooltip:Kanji:brushwood}. But if you don't stop, then it will be too wet to burn at all! Stop already!",
            "hints": "We need to use that brushwood to make a fire! So stop spooning water on it!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Brushwood",
                "Alternative": "Firewood"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3044, \u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3070",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Shiba inu's come from setting brushwood on fire! That must have been how they got their name!",
                "mnemonic": "You finally set the {tooltip:Kanji:brushwood} on fire and suddenly a {tooltip:Reading:Shiba} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3070}) Inu jumps out of the flames. So that's why they named this wood after them or... or vice versa?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:insect} that is amongst all the {tooltip:Radical:world}'s {tooltip:Radical:tree}s is the {tooltip:Kanji:butterfly}. They are always hanging around trees, those butterflies.",
            "hints": "Imagine any tree in the world with different kinds of butterflies fluttering around. Then go to another tree in the world that looks completely different. Once again, butterflies! They really are fluttering around every tree in the world.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Butterfly"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "She grabs another butterfly and starts pulling off wings again, though this time you can see her evil face looking at you while she does it. \"I hate butterflies,\" she says. \"They are always dying in my tea.\"",
                "mnemonic": "As you look at a {tooltip:Kanji:butterfly}, fluttering around a tree, a hand reaches out from the tree and grabs it, then starts plucking the wings off. An evil laugh comes from inside the tree, and you know it's Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}). "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:mysterious} sound that comes from a {tooltip:Radical:bow}string when you pluck it is called a {tooltip:Kanji:chord}. It's still a {tooltip:Kanji:bowstring} though. You need strings to make chords, after all.",
            "hints": "Every time you touch a bowstring, listen to the chords it plays.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chord",
                "Alternative": "Bowstring"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3052\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u308b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "GASP! Genji is finally singing chords of love to you! Your dreams have come true and the most handsome, romantic man ever is finally yours!",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:chord} you're hearing right now is being played by {tooltip:Reading:Gen}ji ({span:lang=ja:\u3052\u3093}). He's sitting under your window plucking bowstrings and singing."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're trying to open the {tooltip:Radical:lid} of a manhole that's covered in {tooltip:Radical:ice} by {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer}ing it a bunch of {tooltip:Radical:times} but it's not working because it's just too {tooltip:Kanji:cold}. It's so cold that your jackhammer is starting to ice up too. But you need to get this lid open so you try time after time after time!",
            "hints": "Imagine if it was sooo cold that no matter how many times you tried to jackhammer the ice of the lid for this manhole, it wouldn't crack open. ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Cold"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3073\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If it wasn't so darn cold you wouldn't have to hear this horrible high pitched ringing sound because there wouldn't even be any ice to jackhammer through!",
                "mnemonic": "Each time the jackhammer hits the freezing {tooltip:Kanji:cold} ice it makes a high pitched {tooltip:Reading:rin}ging ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3093}) sound. It's actually really annoying to listen to but you really need to crack this ice open so you have to keep listening to it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under this {tooltip:Radical:canopy} you have a {tooltip:Radical:brush} and a {tooltip:Radical:task} to complete with it. This is totally {tooltip:Kanji:common}. ",
            "hints": "This type of thing is common for almost every class or job you'll ever have. They sit you down under the canopy, put a brush in your hand, and say, \"Here complete this task. I'll be over there.\"",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Common"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "As you eat the yogurt you think about how common yogurt is too. It's just a normal food, common in everyone's fridge.",
                "mnemonic": "This is so {tooltip:Kanji:common} and familiar to you that you finish your task early and eat some {tooltip:Reading:yo}gurt ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046}) while you wait for the guy to come back."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you drive a {tooltip:Radical:car}, everyone under your {tooltip:Radical:roof} is putting their {tooltip:Radical:life} in your hands, even if they don't say it with their {tooltip:Radical:mouth}\u2014it's still under your {tooltip:Kanji:control}.",
            "hints": "It's really important to remember how many things are under your control when you operate a vehicle. It isn't just the people in your car either, it's everyone and everything in your way too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Control"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u3055\u3073",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you don't want to think about hitting adorable cats with your car, you better maintain control. You're responsible!",
                "mnemonic": "You have to maintain {tooltip:Kanji:control} of your car or you'll hit a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:cats} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3064}). The roads are full of cats at all times. And if you lose control of your car for just a second, you'll hit at least two or three cats."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you can {tooltip:Radical:guard} your {tooltip:Radical:soul} from bad things you'll always feel {tooltip:Kanji:delight} and {tooltip:Kanji:joy}. It's hard to guard your soul from everything though, so take all the joy you can, while you can.",
            "hints": "Imagine guarding yourself from all the bad things in the world. No more politics, religion, internet trolls debating the two, it's all guarded from your precious soul. Ahhh, it's so joyous to be unburdened.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Delight",
                "Alternative": "Joy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3048\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u308d\u3053",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture joy etched on your own face. No one can get you down.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:delight} you feel is so great that it becomes permanently {tooltip:Reading:etch}ed ({span:lang=ja:\u3048\u3064}) in your soul and even your face."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put a {tooltip:Radical:hole} in someone's {tooltip:Radical:body} with a {tooltip:Radical:bow} and they'll become {tooltip:Kanji:destitute}. You put a hole in them. They can't work. They can't take care of their house or their kids. They've lost it all.",
            "hints": "Picture a destitute person wandering in the streets with a hole in their body.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Destitute"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3085\u3046, \u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture a destitute person, sitting on the street, holding a cucumber. Putting the cucumber in their hole. Crying.",
                "mnemonic": "You see this {tooltip:Kanji:destitute} person and decide to give them a {tooltip:Reading:cu}cumber ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3085\u3046}). They don't even remember that they're supposed to eat those, so they shove it in the hole you made with your bow."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If when you speak it sounds like the {tooltip:Radical:power} of a {tooltip:Radical:drum} is coming out of your {tooltip:Radical:mouth}, then people will hold you in high {tooltip:Kanji:esteem}. Anyone who has a loud, booming, powerful voice will be held in high esteem in this day and age. Look at all those awesome musicians who have booming voices!",
            "hints": "Imagine hearing someone speak and it's so powerful and loud that it sounds like they have a drum booming out of their mouth. You'll love them! You'll hold them in the highest esteem!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Esteem",
                "Alternative": "Praise"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3044, \u3088\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you hold someone in high esteem you give me your- give them your car. Gimme!",
                "mnemonic": "You hold them in such high {tooltip:Kanji:esteem} that you give them your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}). I ... I said you give them your car! Give them your car. Hey, hey!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Twenty} {tooltip:Radical:penguin}s together are always {tooltip:Kanji:evil}. Penguins are seen in groups a lot, sure, but did you know that any time there are exactly twenty penguins in a group they're plotting evil things? Evil things like global warming. And how to eat all the fish in the world so humans can't have any.",
            "hints": "Imagine walking around in the arctic when you stumble upon an evil group of penguins. They'd be cute if they weren't holding papers with \"Kill All Humans\" on them and tiny guns in their penguin hands.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Evil"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3078\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Only someone or, in this case, something truly evil would kill someone and hide their remains under some hay. That's really disrespectful and, well, evil.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:evil} penguins can't let you tell the other human's what you've seen, so they murder you and hide your body in a {tooltip:Reading:hay}stack ({span:lang=ja:\u3078\u3044}). Your family will never know what happened to you. The penguins will get away with their evil plans."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There is a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} that is a {tooltip:Radical:satellite}, but it is {tooltip:Kanji:far off} and {tooltip:Kanji:far away}.",
            "hints": "Look up into the sky. That little moving light is the scooter satellite. It's just scooting along, far away from here.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Far Off",
                "Alternative": "Far Away"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u308b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The scooter satellite's only purpose is to make a \"har har har\" sound that is audible from far away. It's quite obnoxious.",
                "mnemonic": "The scooter satellite is {tooltip:Kanji:far off}, but you can still hear it's horn go \"{tooltip:Reading:har} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u308b}) har har.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} {tooltip:Radical:together} with another tsunami is going to cause a massive {tooltip:Kanji:flood}.",
            "hints": "More than one tsunami will definitely result in a flood. Imagine the floody aftermath of more than one tsunami, arriving together.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Flood"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"This flood was caused by you! It is because you did not believe in the holy Crabigator! It is because you didn't do your kanji reviews. It's because you used ignore scripts and reordering scripts and you sinned, sinned, sinned!\" {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} says to the scared, cold, now homeless people.",
                "mnemonic": "After the terrible {tooltip:Kanji:flood}, Emperor {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} comes to survey the destruction and offer hope to his people. But, instead he just tells the people that this flood happened because they didn't believe in the Crabigator's words, and because they weren't doing their kanji reviews."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:thread}s are {tooltip:Radical:humble} and that makes you a perfect {tooltip:Kanji:gentleman}. You don't have to have fancy clothes to be a gentleman, just humble ones that don't stand out and show off too much. That shows how polite you are.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself as the perfect gentleman. You may not have a fancy top hat and tie, but you're humble about what you wear and you're kind to everyone.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gentleman"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "But you're a gentleman, so you don't kick their shins back, you smile and hold in the pain. No matter how bad your shins hurt, you never fight back!",
                "mnemonic": "Unfortunately, as a {tooltip:Kanji:gentleman} who dresses humbly, you're always getting kicked in the {tooltip:Reading:shin}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3093}) by rude kids (and occasionally rude adults)."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You've learned that you can {tooltip:Radical:catapult} things to {tooltip:Kanji:give} them to other people! Don't catapult rocks at buildings and walls, catapult gifts to the people you love.",
            "hints": "If you want to give someone something, use a catapult!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Give"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304f\u308c, \u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You give Godzilla old used cars, chunks of old buildings, and sometimes hamburgers. Godzilla is so happy you're giving him food, he doesn't destroy anymore!",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Give} food to your new friend {tooltip:Reading:Go}dzilla ({span:lang=ja:\u3054}) with the catapult! You and Godzilla understand each other now. He's just hungry."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:samurai} hits the {tooltip:Radical:forehead}s of {tooltip:Radical:grain}s with his {tooltip:Radical:weapon} so the {tooltip:Kanji:grain}s will pop off and into his mouth. He doesn't want to kill the plants, so he's just skimming the grain's foreheads so they'll fall off and he can eat them.",
            "hints": "Picture the samurai taking out his weapon and spinning in a lightning fast circle. The forehead grains pop off and come raining into his open mouth.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Grain"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "These grains aren't even cooked, they're just hard and raw, so the Coke really helps wash them down.",
                "mnemonic": "Phew, all of this {tooltip:Kanji:grain} is making the samurai thirsty, so he reaches in his bag and pulls out an ice cold, refreshing {tooltip:Reading:Coke} ({span:lang=ja:\u3053\u304f})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} in your {tooltip:Radical:ear}s when there's an {tooltip:Radical:explosion} {tooltip:Kanji:in addition} to all the other things you were told to do. You have to crouch under a desk, you have to stay away from windows, you have to close your eyes. But in addition to that, you need to protect your ears!",
            "hints": "Pretend you're in a class in the mid-20th century, watching a video on bomb explosion safety. In addition to putting your fingers in your ears, you have to do a bunch of other stuff. You can't just stop after the first step!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "In Addition"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3064, \u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3055, \u304b\u306d, \u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "In addition to ears, you have a lot of sets on your body to worry about. Sets of eyes, nostrils, legs, you get the picture.",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:In addition} to all the steps you have to take to protect yourself, you can't forget that ears come in {tooltip:Reading:sets} ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3064}). You can't just stick one finger in one ear and have that be the end. You have a set of ears to worry about!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "On the {tooltip:Radical:roof} {tooltip:Radical:above}, is a {tooltip:Radical:small} {tooltip:Radical:stool}. Anyone who sits in that stool will be {tooltip:Kanji:lonely}.",
            "hints": "Imagine sitting on this small stool, waaaaay up there above the roof. You can't see anyone and you can't talk to anyone. You feel this awful emptiness inside. That's what it's like to be lonely.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lonely"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3083\u304f, \u305b\u304d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3073, \u3055\u307f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You're so busy talking to Jack, you don't hear the voices from below, \"Aren't you lonely up there, miss? Do you want us to get a jack to get you down? Hello? I don't think she can hear us...\"",
                "mnemonic": "You're so {tooltip:Kanji:lonely}, you make up an imaginary friend: {tooltip:Reading:Jack} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3083\u304f}). Jack doesn't get rid of the lonely feeling because he isn't real, but he is a distraction at least."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:roof} is {tooltip:Radical:spicy} because you're the {tooltip:Kanji:manager}. You're always testing new recipes in your house to share with everyone who works under you, but that makes all the spice stick to your roof (since it doesn't have good ventilation like a restaurant or a lab would).",
            "hints": "Picture yourself as the manager of a restaurant or a science lab. You have to test all of your managerial methods at home before you can bring them to work. And if you were to lick that roof of yours... it would be spicy from all of your experiments.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Manager"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Unfortunately, you couldn't figure out how to make non-spicy cyborgs, but that's okay because you're going to be the best cyborg manager ever! No one will ever take them away from you again.",
                "mnemonic": "You've finally done it. You're now the {tooltip:Kanji:manager} of a bunch of spicy new {tooltip:Reading:cy}borgs ({span:lang=ja:\u3055\u3044}). You've been toiling away for over a year, but you've finally replaced the cyborg you lost, and now you can manage them properly without anyone getting in the way. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The only {tooltip:Radical:building} you'll get {tooltip:Radical:frostbite} in is a {tooltip:Kanji:mausoleum}. Mausoleums and {tooltip:Kanji:tomb}s weren't made for living people, so they aren't insulated from the cold. No one cares if a dead body gets frostbite.",
            "hints": "Unfortunately, you're realizing this because you thought a mausoleum would be a good hiding place from the winter cold. Spoilers, it's not.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mausoleum",
                "Alternative": "Tomb"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3055\u3055\u304e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine taking your frostbitten fingers and trying to get away from the mausoleum in this row boat. It looks like it was made of bones and it is not very seaworthy. But you row with all your might, because you don't want to end up a permanent fixture in this tomb!",
                "mnemonic": "You need to escape this {tooltip:Kanji:mausoleum} now but the only way out is on a {tooltip:Reading:row} ({span:lang=ja:\u308a\u3087\u3046}) boat over a creepy frozen pond. You've heard of these mausoleum row boats before, and you're pretty sure they're cursed."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You go to buy a {tooltip:Radical:table} but it looks it has water damage from {tooltip:Radical:drop}s of water hitting it. This makes it a pretty {tooltip:Kanji:mediocre} table. The water drops haven't really damaged it that much, it still stands and you can use it, but it's kinda ugly, so it's just mediocre.",
            "hints": "You didn't expect to see water drop damage on this table so now your mood is mediocre too.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mediocre"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3093, \u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3046\u3088, \u304a\u3088, \u3059\u3079",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine having a bone to pick with someone because they're trying to sell you something mediocre and they just won't listen. Now you have a bone to pick with the person who recommended this guy to you!",
                "mnemonic": "You weren't expecting to see such a {tooltip:Kanji:mediocre} table so you go up to the guy who's selling it and say, \"Hey, I have a {tooltip:Reading:bone} ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3093}) to pick with you!\" But he doesn't think there is a bone to pick at all, he doesn't think the table is mediocre like you do."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Who loves their {tooltip:Radical:flag}, using {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer}s, and precise {tooltip:Radical:measurement}s? Your {tooltip:Kanji:military officer}! He's always saluting the flag, jackhammering near all the new recruits to test them, and checking the measurement between the floor and their pants. Who else could it be?",
            "hints": "Picture a military officer doing all those things.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Military Officer",
