                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084\u3059",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Yes! Peaceful blue radicals standing in a row. What's that? YES you do want more radicals added to the site. Well okay then, if it will keep you at peace, sure!",
                "mnemonic": "Now if someone asks you if the color blue makes you {tooltip:Kanji:peaceful} you should say \"{tooltip:Reading:YES}! ({span:lang=ja:\u3084\u3059})\" And you'll have us to thank for that! All those peaceful blue radicals. They're the easiest thing on the site, and if someone asks you if radicals make you feel peaceful say YES again!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When {tooltip:Radical:small} {tooltip:Radical:drop}s of water work {tooltip:Radical:together} they gain {tooltip:Kanji:respect} for one another. If you end up working with someone long enough, and they end up being really great, you'll respect them too! ",
            "hints": "Imagine being a small drop of water and seeing other drops of water come to help you by working together. You'd really respect them, right?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Respect"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3084\u3046\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine respecting someone so much that you'll cheer ooh yankees over and over even though they're kind of a crappy team. ",
                "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Kanji:respect} someone enough you'll even take up their hobbies. The person you respect most loves the Yankees. You don't really feel the same, but you respect that about them so you chant, \"{tooltip:Reading:Ooh Ya}nkees, {tooltip:Reading:Ooh Ya}nkees {span:lang=ja:\u3046\u3084\u3046\u3084} with them during each game."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take some {tooltip:Radical:thread}, put your {tooltip:Radical:scooter} up to a {tooltip:Radical:signpost}, and {tooltip:Kanji:sew} them together. You don't have a lock, so sewing your scooter up to the signpost to keep it safe is all you can think of.",
            "hints": "Imagine slowly sewing your scooter to the signpost, passing the thread back and forth through the signpost's metal holes and your scooter's handles.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sew"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307b\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Hopefully, if your scooter is still here later you'll be able to start sewing outside of your home more often from now on!",
                "mnemonic": "You usually only {tooltip:Kanji:sew} at {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}), so this is a big exception for you. You're usually worried that if you sew in public people will judge your stitches, so this is a big step for you!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:boat} that's {tooltip:Radical:white} isn't just a boat, it's a {tooltip:Kanji:ship}.",
            "hints": "Boats don't need to be a bright white color. But, ships do! They're dangerous and big, so they paint them nice and white.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ship"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u304f",
