{
            "mnemonic": "You give a {tooltip:Radical:bow} and a {tooltip:Radical:stick} to your friend's family. This is because your friend died, and he loved bows and sticks. You give this to his family, to give our {tooltip:Kanji:condolence}s.",
            "hints": "Imagine looking at the bow and stick as you slide them over to your deceased friend's family. This won't do enough, but it is a little condolence at least.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Condolence"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3061\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3076\u3089, \u3068\u3080\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine her saying, \"My condolences,\" as Mrs. Chou does him in.",
                "mnemonic": "More than a {tooltip:Kanji:condolence}, you want to avenge your friend's death. He was killed by Mrs. {tooltip:Reading:Chou} ({span:lang=ja:\u3061\u3087\u3046}), and she broke his stick and bow, which is why you got the family a new set."
            }
        }

