                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This may not be a happy thing to think about, but it will help you remember this kanji better. Imagine your dad fighting a degenerative disease. Imagine helping him fight through this. Everything will be okay eventually. I promise.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the building {tooltip:Kanji:degenerate}, you can't help but think of your {tooltip:Reading:da}d ({span:lang=ja:\u3060}). You had to watch him waste away the same way of a degenerative disease. Why do people have to die, dad?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You take a {tooltip:Radical:drum} and a {tooltip:Radical:branch} and... well, what else would you do? You would {tooltip:Kanji:drum} or {tooltip:Kanji:beat} them together.",
            "hints": "A branch is just like a drumstick, so of course you're going to drum them together.",
