{
            "mnemonic": "To the {tooltip:Radical:mountain}s you took your {tooltip:Radical:horned} {tooltip:Radical:husband} for you two to get married. (Society wouldn't accept a horned husband!) To hide even more from the prying eyes of society, you take your horned husband into a {tooltip:Kanji:ravine}.",
            "hints": "Imagine walking up the mountain in your wedding clothes so you can get married without anyone trying to stop you. Then, because you're still worried, you go into a ravine where you are read your marriage vows.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ravine"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
