                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You're sitting at home, and there is a knock at the door. A man in a suit, hat, and dark sunglasses hands you a briefcase full of money. \"Here's your spring salary. Enjoy the dry weather.\"{splitParent}\"T-thanks?\"{splitParent}Welp, have fun at home with your stacks of early salary cash.",
                "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Kanji:salary} is sent straight to your {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}) instead of the bank. Okay, something is definitely fishy here."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you put your {tooltip:Radical:spoon} in the {tooltip:Radical:sun} while you're in {tooltip:Radical:prison}, a {tooltip:Radical:mouth} will appear to {tooltip:Kanji:scold} you. You can never see who the mouth belongs to, but considering you're in prison it's probably a guard. Either way, that person doesn't like what you're doing and they keep scolding you when you put your spoon out into the sun.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to reflect some precious sunlight into your prison room with a spoon. Now imagine a mouth appearing in the way of the sunlight and it scolds you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Scold"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3064",
