                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "WHAT KIND OF WORLD IS THIS THAT YOU'RE IN A PRISON WHERE CATS SCOLD YOU?!",
                "mnemonic": "One day you finally get fed up. You need to know who the mouth of the person who's {tooltip:Kanji:scold}ing you is. You stick your spoon out into the sun and the mouth appears, scolding you right on time. You reach out and grab them. But in your hand is a pile of {tooltip:Reading:cats} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3064})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have a {tooltip:Radical:net} of {tooltip:Radical:thread} for catching a {tooltip:Radical:turkey}. But, it must be {tooltip:Kanji:spread out} and you must {tooltip:Kanji:arrange} it first.",
            "hints": "The reason you'd use a net made of thread is because it's hard to see. But, it's only that way when you spread out the net. It's important to spread out and arrange your net otherwise the turkey will see it.",
            "meanings": {
