                "hints": "Take a walk around your home right now. Can you find the best place to sprout flowers? Remember, it has to be nice and bright! Not dark and damp. Don't put them in your closet.",
                "mnemonic": "You want to grow these {tooltip:Kanji:sprout}s in your {tooltip:Reading:ho}me ({span:lang=ja:\u307b\u3046}), not outside. So you need to find the windows in your house that are the brightest."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tree} melts into the {tooltip:Radical:ground} after listening to loud {tooltip:Radical:music} in the hot {tooltip:Radical:sun}, so you have to find a nice big {tooltip:Kanji:tank} to scoop the melted tree into. The music made the tree vibrate at juuust the right frequency that it, combined with the hot sun, made the tree turn into a puddle. You can't just leave it being all blobby on the ground, so you find a tank for it.",
            "hints": "Imagine scooping a melted tree into a tank. It's a very strange sensation.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Tank",
                "Alternative": "Vat"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075\u306d",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Um, okay?\" you reply to the soul, and walk away from the tank. \"W-wait! Tanks can't move? Come back, let me haunt you with my tree soul!\"{splitParent}It's a good thing there weren't wheels on that tank!",
                "mnemonic": "You're staring at the big {tooltip:Kanji:tank} when an eerie sound comes out, \"Oooh I am the {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) of the tree! You've trapped me in this tank and now I'm going to haunt it!\" You don't want to be haunted by a tank with a soul stuck in it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The amount of {tooltip:Radical:dirt} you need to get some {tooltip:Radical:peace} is a {tooltip:Kanji:two mat area}. Two tatami mats, that is. This is a pretty common measurement in Japan, so you should get really familiar with the amount of space that two tatami mats take up together.",
