{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:building} {tooltip:Radical:clown} is the only clown allowed to {tooltip:Kanji:accompany} you. You hate all clowns, and so does the rest of your town. But this clown is really good at building buildings, and he's allowed to leave his part of town and accompany you while you fix buildings together.",
            "hints": "I know it's been a long time, but try not to mix this one up with \t{span:lang=ja:\u90e8}, if you can. Remember, the clown building is in another part of town and the clowns aren't supposed to leave. But the building clown is okay to accompany you through the rest of the city.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Accompany"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Wave bye to the clown, he'll accompany you on your building job tomorrow, but right now he has to go home and be with the rest of his clown people. He can't accompany you after dark.",
                "mnemonic": "He can only {tooltip:Kanji:accompany} you for so long though and soon it's time to say {tooltip:Reading:bye} ({span:lang=ja:\u3070\u3044}) again."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} on your {tooltip:Radical:husband} to {tooltip:Kanji:aid} him. There's something about a spouse's touch that just makes you feel better. Have you ever had someone rub your back while you were hurt or sick or sad? It's nice, right?",
            "hints": "Imagine rubbing your husband's back with your fingers to aid him. You want him to feel better. You want him to get that comforting feeling that this kind of touching gives.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Aid"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "That's true love, my friend.",
                "mnemonic": "Unfortunately, your husband wouldn't need your {tooltip:Kanji:aid} if he wasn't such a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}). He walks into doors, he falls down the stairs, he touches the plate when the waiter says it's hot. And every single time your fool husband hurts himself, you aid him."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When your {tooltip:Radical:scooter} has a {tooltip:Radical:fault}, you need to get an {tooltip:Kanji:alternate}. Hopefully your insurance will cover it too.",
            "hints": "You have a scooter that you drive every single day, but if you notice a fault, you need to send it in to get it fixed. That's when you break out your alternate scooter.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Alternate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3066\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine riding on your alternate {span:lang=ja:\u9244} scooter. Feel the hard iron under your bum and the loud sounds it makes as you scoot down the street. I hope your normal scooter is fixed soon.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:alternate} scooter is made entirely of {span:lang=ja:\u9244} ({span:lang=ja:\u3066\u3064}). It's hard and cold and not very comfortable when you sit on it. That's why you chose to keep it as an alternate and not as your everyday scooter."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:husband} was wearing his {tooltip:Radical:cleats} when he accidentally stepped on a {tooltip:Radical:bird}. Luckily this particular bird is a {tooltip:Kanji:chicken}, and chickens are really durable!",
            "hints": "Picture the sad, stepped on chicken. It's angrily clucking and chasing your husband around your yard for what he did.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Chicken"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u308a, \u306b\u308f\u3068\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "This cake was for your husband, but now he gets nothing. The chicken gets to eat all of the cake in front of him instead.",
                "mnemonic": "The only way to stop the {tooltip:Kanji:chicken} from putting on your husband's cleats and stepping on him to death in revenge is to feed it the {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044}) you were making."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:king} {tooltip:Radical:rake}d all the {tooltip:Radical:mountain}s down into flat land so he could see everyone in the kingdom from his castle windows. You should share your {tooltip:Kanji:congratulations} with him. Now, quick tell him this was a great idea.",
            "hints": "Imagine saying \"Congratulations!\" to a king who just ordered his servants to rake down all the pretty mountains in his kingdom.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Congratulations"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3044, \u305a\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u305a, \u3057\u308b\u3057",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine how hollow your congratulation sounds when you really miss those mountains. This king doesn't deserve your nice words.",
                "mnemonic": "The moment you say \"{tooltip:Kanji:Congratulations}!\" you've already started to {tooltip:Reading:miss} ({span:lang=ja:\u307f\u305a}) those beautiful mountains. But you can't let missing them ruin your congratulations! Don't let the king know!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Gambler}s usually only see the {tooltip:Radical:sun} at {tooltip:Kanji:dawn}. They gamble all day and through the night, and if they leave it's at the crack of dawn to get home, clean up, and then go back. I haven't known a gambler who's seen the sun ... well ever!",
            "hints": "Imagine being a gambler and seeing the bright dawn sun when you come out of the casino or pachinko parlor. It burns your eyes! Evil dawn, get back inside quick!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Dawn"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046, \u304e\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304b\u3064\u304d, \u3055\u3068",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine getting up at dawn and seeing the {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304b\u3064\u304d} in the sky near the sun. It's so beautiful!",
                "mnemonic": "If you're up at {tooltip:Kanji:dawn} you'll also see the {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304b} (red) {span:lang=ja:\u3064\u304d} (moon). The {span:lang=ja:\u3042\u304b\u3064\u304d} only happens as the sun comes up at dawn so usually only gamblers see it. But if you get up early, you can see it too!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:clown} takes a {tooltip:Radical:knife} and {tooltip:Kanji:divide}s himself. First he divides himself into two pieces, then he's in four pieces, then... oh why won't he stop?!",
            "hints": "Instead of dying, the clown divides into slightly thinner clowns.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Divide"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The many clowns crash to the floor as the bowling ball plows through their... his(?) divided bodies. You can't bear to look anymore.",
                "mnemonic": "The clown finally stops trying to {tooltip:Kanji:divide} himself, and you can't stand to look at all of him. You grab a {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) ball and bowl all of his divided parts over!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you touch {tooltip:Radical:ice} for too long you'll get {tooltip:Radical:frostbite} and that's a really hard thing to {tooltip:Kanji:endure}. A lot of people can't, and die. Then again, you managed to endure touching ice long enough to get frostbite in the first place, so maybe this is baby stuff for you.",
            "hints": "Imagine having to endure the pain of frostbite because you were a jerk who put his hand on ice for a few hours.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Endure"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u306e",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine if you were one of these cool Shinobi ninjas that could endure the extreme cold and pain of frostbite!",
                "mnemonic": "The best people in the world at being able to {tooltip:Kanji:endure} the pain are the {tooltip:Reading:shino}bi ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u306e}) ninjas! They train by hanging out in frozen areas all the time and don't complain at all. Maybe if the pain gets to be too much you can go ask them for advice."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You have to reach a certain {tooltip:Radical:number} of {tooltip:Radical:flowers} and {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}s hits to become a legitimate {tooltip:Kanji:fiefdom}. At least in the old days. If you don't meet one of these conditions, like if you get hit by tsunamis all the time but you only have two or three flowers that will grow, you can't be your own fiefdom.",
            "hints": "Imagine being the person who has to check whether each fiefdom has enough flowers and tsunamis per year to keep their status.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fiefdom"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture Han Solo flying around Japan checking to make sure all the fiefdoms are up to code.",
                "mnemonic": "The most famous {tooltip:Kanji:fiefdom} checker is {tooltip:Reading:Han} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}) Solo. He takes his Millennium Falcon and swoops around checking for flowers and signs of past tsunamis and then he'll either say you can or cannot be your own fiefdom. Thanks Han Solo!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you {tooltip:Radical:say} the {tooltip:Radical:lineup} of your family members that have lived on this earth under the {tooltip:Radical:sun}, you're really explaining your {tooltip:Kanji:genealogy}.",
            "hints": "Say the line up of what happened under the sun. It's the genealogy of your family or the score of your game!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Genealogy",
                "Alternative": "Score"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3075",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your family genealogy and your game's score aren't even close to being the same thing. Memorize these or everyone will think you're a fool.",
                "mnemonic": "if you can't tell the difference between your {tooltip:Kanji:genealogy} and a game's {tooltip:Kanji:score} you're a {tooltip:Reading:foo}l ({span:lang=ja:\u3075}) and I can't help you. You aren't a fool, are you? You know the difference."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:king} wants you to make a {tooltip:Radical:rocket} that looks {tooltip:Kanji:glassy}. It won't be very stable, and it probably won't work, but making it glassy and pretty is the only way to make the king approve.",
            "hints": "Imagine a king who won't accept a rocket that isn't made of glassy material. He's not very smart...",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Glassy"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308a",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture the king admiring himself in the glassy surface and then his face contorts. He smashes his fist through the rocket and rips out the reeds. \"REEDS AREN'T GLASSY!\" he cries, and starts hitting you with them.",
                "mnemonic": "You take the {tooltip:Kanji:glassy} rocket and try to stuff some thin {tooltip:Reading:reed}s ({span:lang=ja:\u308a}) inside to support it. But because it's clear and glassy the king sees them at the last second."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You can only manage to avoid a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} by standing {tooltip:Radical:above} it on a {tooltip:Radical:small} {tooltip:Radical:stool} if you are very {tooltip:Kanji:graceful}. If you aren't graceful enough the tsunami will knock you and the stool over and you'll be swept away like everyone else.",
            "hints": "Imagine being graceful enough to balance on a small stool above a raging tsunami! Sooo cool!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Graceful"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3068",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It doesn't matter how badly the stool shook, you stayed graceful and didn't fall! ",
                "mnemonic": "No matter how {tooltip:Kanji:graceful} you are, the still tsunami {tooltip:Reading:shook} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u304f}) the small stool. That's where your gracefulness came in. The stool shook, but you didn't. You balanced yourself and refused to go down. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} does a {tooltip:Radical:dance} on top of the {tooltip:Radical:tree} to show his {tooltip:Kanji:greatness} to everyone around. If he dances all the way up there on top of the tree, then no one can deny his {tooltip:Kanji:excellence}!",
            "hints": "\"Look upon your leader's greatness!\" he shouts, doing a jig around on the branches.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Greatness",
                "Alternative": "Excellence"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3050",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Oh leader, your greatness is so... great!\" you shout up at him. He's holding the ketsup bottle over your head and staring into your eyes as he dances in the tree. He isn't sure if he wants to dump it on you yet. He isn't sure if you really recognize his excellence.",
                "mnemonic": "If you don't recognize the leader's {tooltip:Kanji:greatness} he will throw {tooltip:Reading:ketsu}p ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3064}) all over you (it's a special mix of ketchup and catsup). And it's ketsup because it looks like blood. The blood he'll spill if you don't look up and clap at his great dancing."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:samurai} puts his {tooltip:Radical:forehead} on the {tooltip:Radical:table} next to his {tooltip:Radical:weapon}. He is just a {tooltip:Kanji:husk} of his former self. This {tooltip:Kanji:shell} of a samurai has nothing left.",
            "hints": "He's just sitting there, he can't even pick up his weapon or raise his head anymore.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Husk",
                "Alternative": "Shell"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u304f, \u3053\u304f, \u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3089, \u304c\u3089",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"Co co co co cooooock!\" the cock screams, shocking the samurai back into his lifeless shell. You did it!",
                "mnemonic": "The only way to bring a {tooltip:Kanji:husk} of a samurai back to life is to have a {tooltip:Reading:cock} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u304f}) crow right in his ear."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "This is a {tooltip:Radical:gold} {tooltip:Radical:roof}, {tooltip:Radical:correct}? It's important to {tooltip:Kanji:lock} it up, then.",
            "hints": "It's only natural that you'd want to lock a gold roof so nobody can steal it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lock"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "He's the big farmhand who turned out to be an undercover Viking in your town, only to pillage and destroy everything. Under the gold roof is where he locked up all your village's valuables, after wiping you all out.",
                "mnemonic": "The person who {tooltip:Kanji:lock}ed the gold roof was {tooltip:Reading:Jou}rm ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3087\u3046})."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:sweet} {tooltip:Radical:woman} sits under a {tooltip:Radical:tree} and works as a {tooltip:Kanji:mediator}. If you're having a fight with someone, bring them to the sweet woman under the tree and she'll mediate for the two of you. Problem solved! Thanks sweet lady!",
            "hints": "Imagine the sweet tree woman being a mediator for you and your arch rival. What she says fixes everything between you two!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Mediator"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306a\u3053\u3046\u3069",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine her refusing to let you pay her for her mediator services and just saying \"bye\" over and over until you leave. Weird.",
                "mnemonic": "You go to pay the woman for being your {tooltip:Kanji:mediator} for you two but she just says, \"{tooltip:Reading:Bye} {span:lang=ja:\u3070\u3044}).\" You try to hand her some money and she stares into your eyes. \"Bye.\" Oh... okay, bye then."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} gets into a {tooltip:Radical:net} that's im{tooltip:Radical:prison}ing a bunch of {tooltip:Radical:insect}s, the insects are going to get all {tooltip:Kanji:muddy}. The net gets dragged along with the tsunami water and the insects can't escape, so they just get covered in the yucky stuff.",
            "hints": "Picture a net prison full of insects being dragged by a tsunami getting muddier and muddier. Poor buggles!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Muddy",
                "Alternative": "Impure"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3060\u304f, \u3058\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
