{
            "mnemonic": "The only {tooltip:Radical:tree} a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} will live in is an {tooltip:Kanji:oak} tree. They really only do this because oak trees have really yummy acorns and turkeys loooove acorns.",
            "hints": "Imagine seeing a turkey sitting in an oak tree munching on acorns. You didn't even know turkeys could fly, but it got up there somehow.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Oak",
                "Alternative": "Oak Tree"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3044, \u3059\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046, \u3064\u3061",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine standing in a grove of oak trees and yelling SOOEY! SOOOOOEY! Now watch as hundreds of turkeys come flying at your face! They think you have more acorns for them. RUN!",
                "mnemonic": "If you see a bunch of {tooltip:Kanji:oak}s but no turkeys just yell, \"{tooltip:Reading:SOOEY} ({span:lang=ja:\u3064\u3044})!\" and they'll all come jumping out! Just because you can't see a turkey in there doesn't mean there isn't one!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you spill something {tooltip:Radical:red} on yourself in {tooltip:Radical:winter} you should {tooltip:Kanji:pardon} yourself immediately and try to find something else to wear. It's very dangerous to wear red in winter, and even if it seems rude, make sure you pardon yourself right away and get that taken care of!",
            "hints": "Imagine spilling red wine or red paint down your shirt. Quickly pardon yourself and get changed now!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pardon"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3083",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine not pardoning yourself fast enough and having the winter shaman spirit away whatever you got red on. That's embarrassing.",
                "mnemonic": "If you don't {tooltip:Kanji:pardon} yourself fast enough the winter {tooltip:Reading:sha}man ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3083}) will burst in and cast a spell on you, taking away all the clothes that have red on them! Now you have to pardon yourself for being naked!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Throw a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} in a cage with a {tooltip:Radical:tiger} and some {tooltip:Radical:spikes} and the tiger will have the time of its life {tooltip:Kanji:play}ing with them! Think of all the tiger play time possibilities! ",
            "hints": "If you were the tiger how would you play with the drunkard? ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Play"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e, \u3052",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3056, \u3058\u3083, \u305f\u308f\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "What would you rather watch? A guillotine at work or a tiger playing like this?",
                "mnemonic": "If you aren't the tiger, watching it {tooltip:Kanji:play} is a little like watching someone's head get cut off with a {tooltip:Reading:gui}llotine ({span:lang=ja:\u304e}). In fact, you don't want to watch it play at all anymore."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If someone gives you a {tooltip:Radical:sock} you should {tooltip:Kanji:receive} it and thank them. You can't just say no or put the sock on the ground and walk away. You should always receive a sock properly, with both hands, when it's handed to you.",
            "hints": "Imagine Dobby reaching out to receive his first sock. Don't you want to be happy like that too?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Receive"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046, \u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine standing in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068} and receiving sock after sock. People just keep giving and you keep receiving!",
                "mnemonic": "The best place to {tooltip:Kanji:receive} a sock is in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. They're famous for their sock stores and schoolgirls who have too many socks. If you walk down the street someone is bound to try to hand you a sock in {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}, and you should receive it happily."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you want to take a {tooltip:Radical:flag} out of the {tooltip:Radical:mouth} of a {tooltip:Radical:mantis} you have to make a formal {tooltip:Kanji:request} first. Mantises don't like to just give things away, and they're kind of mean so if you try to steal the flag it will probably bite you. So make a formal, polite request if you want it.",
            "hints": "Imagine trying to request a flag from a scary mantis that has it sitting in it's mouth. Will it give it to you? Will it bite you? You'll have to wait and see.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Request",
                "Alternative": "Entrust"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u304f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u304f, \u305f\u306e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine your shock at finding out the mantis not only understood your request, but agreed! This is great but also makes you wonder what other creatures can understand you...",
                "mnemonic": "After you {tooltip:Kanji:request} the mantis give you its flag it {tooltip:Reading:shock}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u304f}) you by actually spitting it out of its mouth at your feet. You didn't think your request would work, or even if the mantis understood human speech, but it shocked you by doing exactly what you asked!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:triceratops} standing in front of a full {tooltip:Radical:moon} and you can't help but see a really strong {tooltip:Kanji:resemblance}. The triceratops has that round frill thing behind its horns and it looks just like the round full moon. Who knew that a triceratops would resemble the moon!",
            "hints": "Look at the triceratops. Now look at the moon. See the resemblance? Uncanny, don't you think?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Resemblance"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3084\u304b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine being the Shougun and seeing the resemblance between a triceratops and the moon for the first time. You'd put that on all your stuff too, if you were him.",
                "mnemonic": "The first person to see this {tooltip:Kanji:resemblance} was the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}). That's why he decided to put a triceratops head with the moon behind it on his mon (family crest). Now he's known as the full moon dinosaur shogun, and he's very famous."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:soul} on a {tooltip:Radical:cross} covered in {tooltip:Radical:flowers} with {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} at its feet and you suddenly {tooltip:Kanji:resent} them. It's not like you want to be the one up there on the cross, but so many people left flowers and shellfish for them. It should have been you...",
            "hints": "Picture the soul on the cross, flowers all around it and shellfish at its feet. Feel your resentment grow.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Resent"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
