                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word is made up of a single kanji, it probably uses the kun'yomi reading. You did not learn this reading, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}{tooltip:Vocabulary:Shell}s come from ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3089}) living animals. You can't have a shell \u2014 or a {tooltip:Reading:cara}pace ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3089}) \u2014 unless something was once in there. They have to come from something.\n{splitParent}This word isn't limited to animal shells though! It covers seed shells, or husks, too. \ud83c\udf31\n"
