                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3080\u3064",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine only letting this guy start to introduce himself with {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f} before walking the heck outta there. Just because he was acting friendly doesn't mean he was actually your friend.",
                "mnemonic": "This {tooltip:Kanji:friendly} guy comes up to you and start to introduce himself, \"{span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f}-\" but you stop him. He's been getting way too friendly with your womb and you don't want to hear who he is. He can {span:lang=ja:\u307c\u304f} at someone else, you're out."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you stay up for so long that you get to watch the {tooltip:Radical:moon} go down and the {tooltip:Radical:dawn} come, then people will say you have serious {tooltip:Kanji:guts}. Staying up that late is really hard, and not everyone can do it. If you don't have the guts to stay up, you'll just fall asleep and never see the moon and the sun switch places in the sky.",
            "hints": "Imagine the guts you'd have to have to stay up for so long that you see the moon and the sun switch places! A lot of guts!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Guts"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3082",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine having the guts to stay outside to watch the moon and the sun and then getting a really deep tan from it.",
                "mnemonic": "You were outside for so long, proving you had {tooltip:Kanji:guts}, that you also got a sweet {tooltip:Reading:tan} ({span:lang=ja:\u305f\u3093}) out of it! It's a really deep tan though, and you probably need more guts if you ever want to do all that again."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You try to use your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} to cast {tooltip:Radical:doubt} on people by using them to {tooltip:Kanji:imitate} each other. Right now you're using your fingers as finger puppets, imitating one of your friends to the others.",
            "hints": "Picture your angry friend standing up next to your fingers, shouting, \"I'm the real me! That's just an imitation!\" The rest of your friends look nervously at each other. They doubt this person is real now.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Imitate"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
