                "hints": "Imagine using a zoo saw to cut down a Japanese birch tree. What's a zoo saw? It's a saw that's used in zoos, to build all the animal enclosures. And to cut down spicy trees.",
                "mnemonic": "You can only cut down a {tooltip:Kanji:Japanese birch} using {tooltip:Reading:a zoo saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u305a\u3055}) because a regular saw can't handle how spicy these trees are."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} hits a {tooltip:Radical:tree} and your {tooltip:Radical:hat} protects you from the {tooltip:Radical:water}, but the hat itself is now covered in {tooltip:Kanji:lacquer}. You take it off and see that it's shiny and hard and protected.",
            "hints": "Picture your hat and all of the other things the tsunami + tree water touched. It's all been hardened with a thick coating of the lacquer.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lacquer",
                "Alternative": "Varnish"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u308b\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Watch as your shih tzu tries to bite your now lacquered chair. It gets its teeth around the leg, but it's hard as a rock. The shih tzu starts sneezing and spitting, letting go. Looks like it tastes bad too. Perfect!",
                "mnemonic": "You decide to scoop up the rest of the {tooltip:Kanji:lacquer} water and use it on your furniture to protect it from your {tooltip:Reading:shih tzu} ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3064}). Now it can't bite or scratch or ruin any of your things anymore!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see a {tooltip:Radical:gate} with a {tooltip:Radical:tree} growing through it and it reminds you that you need more {tooltip:Kanji:leisure} time. You walk up to the gate tree and curl up under its branches. No one will bother you because the tree is blocking the gate from being used.",
            "hints": "Imagine spending your leisure time curled up under a tree that's growing through a gate. It's so cozy and secluded!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Leisure"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "But wait. Isn't Genghis Khan dead now? He winks at you, \"Leisure time is for the dead.\" He smiles, and fades away, disappearing into the tree.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:leisure}ly nap, you hear a gruff voice, \"Ah, you're done too, huh?\" It's Genghis {tooltip:Reading:Khan} ({span:lang=ja:\u304b\u3093})! He's spending his leisure time relaxing under this abandoned gate just like you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:soul} {tooltip:Radical:stand}s in the {tooltip:Radical:village} you {tooltip:Kanji:long for}. It's the village you're from, and no matter how far you go, no matter how old you get, your soul is still there, and you {tooltip:Kanji:yearn} for it.",
            "hints": "Have you ever been away from your village? Maybe you're far away right now, studying Japanese alone. Can't you feel your body longing for your soul back home?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Long For",
                "Alternative": "Yearn"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046, \u3068\u3046, \u3069\u3046",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u3053\u304c",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You long for a cougar to leave you alone! You yearn for a cougar to bother someone else!",
                "mnemonic": "No matter how much you {tooltip:Kanji:long for} it, you can't go back because {tooltip:Reading:a cougar} ({span:lang=ja:\u3042\u3053\u304c}) is in the way. Whenever you try to return to your village to be reunited with the soul you yearn for, a cougar is back, and won't let you in."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:drop} to the ground in a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy}, and then {tooltip:Radical:drop} down in front of the {tooltip:Radical:cross} you keep on you because you're trying to make yourself as {tooltip:Kanji:lowly} as you can in front of God. He said to lower yourself and this is the only way you can interpret that.",
            "hints": "Imagine dropping down in a rice paddy, then again in front of your cross. Be as lowly as you can make yourself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Lowly",
                "Alternative": "Base"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
