                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You try to push the key back into your body. Back into your eye, you even try to swallow it, but it comes back out. Finally you look down at your mourning heart and try the key there. It clicks. And opens.",
                "mnemonic": "While you're in {tooltip:Kanji:mourning}, you feel a sharp pain in your crying eyes. A {tooltip:Reading:key} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d}) comes sliding out with your tears. You look around wildly, but you're still alone. Is this... the key of mourning?"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When under{tooltip:Radical:ground} {tooltip:Radical:music} makes it out into the light of the {tooltip:Radical:sun} (the public), it finally becomes {tooltip:Kanji:official}. Music isn't really real unless people hear it outside of those secret underground concerts.",
            "hints": "Think of all that music you listened to underground but not in the light of the sun. None of that was official music. None of it!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Official"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046, \u305e\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u304b\u3055, \u3068\u3082\u304c\u3089, \u3078\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The official music penetrates into your soul, instead of just your ears, and it's affecting everyone else's souls too! Oh no... wait that's too many people. This was your song! No, it's too popular now, stop your souls from liking it! Ahhh!",
                "mnemonic": "Once the music is {tooltip:Kanji:official}, you'll feel it in your {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}). When you listen to it outside, under the bright sun, your soul gets to finally hear it too."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you're on a {tooltip:Radical:mountain} looking from {tooltip:Radical:above} to {tooltip:Radical:below} that means you're on the {tooltip:Kanji:peak} of the mountain.",
            "hints": "Imagine standing right at the peak of a mountain looking at down from above and everything down below. You're really, really high up!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Peak"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3068\u3046\u3052",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture yourself sitting on a mountain peak in Tokyo and watching a little Tokyo gecko run up and down on them. It's adorable and totally worth the climb.",
                "mnemonic": "It's only on this type of mountain {tooltip:Kanji:peak} that you'll be able to find the rare and adorable {tooltip:Reading:To}kyo {tooltip:Reading:ge}cko ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u3046\u3052}). These tiny little critters can only be found on the ridges going above and below the mountains in Tokyo. There are like six mountains in Tokyo, so the next time you're scaling the ridges keep your eyes open for the Tokyo gecko!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "We want you to say things with your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} right {tooltip:Radical:now} because it's {tooltip:Kanji:recital} time! Go, perform please. What do you mean you didn't know the recital was right now? Well, tough luck. Recite!",
            "hints": "The recital is happening now. So open your mouth and start already!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Recital"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304e\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Drink gin before all your recitals! It'll help!",
                "mnemonic": "Here, if you are too afraid to start the {tooltip:Kanji:recital} now drink this {tooltip:Reading:gin} ({span:lang=ja:\u304e\u3093}) to get your courage up. But once you're done drinking it the recital starts!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:stone} that looks like a {tooltip:Radical:turkey} {tooltip:Radical:boil}ing underwater is just a {tooltip:Kanji:reef}.",
            "hints": "It may seem like there are a bunch of turkeys under there, but it's just the shape the reef takes. Though I guess if you're looking from above the water it really does look like a bunch of turkeys freaking out.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reef"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You don't know if the Shougun likes the reef because he likes the beauty of the ocean, or if he's fantasizing about turkeys boiling. He's a... complex man.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:reef} is the {tooltip:Reading:Shou}gun's ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3087\u3046}) favorite place to be nowadays. He sits next to the water, and stares down into it for hours."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "People think {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}s are only made of water but they have a {tooltip:Radical:few} pieces of {tooltip:Kanji:sand} in there too. There's actually more sand in the ocean than most people think. And tsunamis can't just have water and sharks in them. A few grains of sand will always slip in.",
            "hints": "Imagine how those few grains of sand feel to get swept up into a tsunami. They didn't ask for this. They just wanted to stay at the bottom of the sea.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Sand"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055, \u3057\u3083",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u306a, \u3088\u306a\u3052\u308b",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "I saw the sand, stop doubting me!",
                "mnemonic": "How do I know there's {tooltip:Kanji:sand} in there? Because I {tooltip:Reading:saw} ({span:lang=ja:\u3055}) them! "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In a {tooltip:Radical:flowers} {tooltip:Radical:net} a {tooltip:Radical:drunkard} {tooltip:Radical:slide}s down like a {tooltip:Radical:drop}. There they stay, an icon of {tooltip:Kanji:scorn} and {tooltip:Kanji:neglect}.",
            "hints": "It's embarrassing to fall down a flowers net while drunk. Despite that, there you are. Everyone who goes by scorns you or neglects you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Scorn",
                "Alternative": "Neglect"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3079\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3055\u3052\u3059",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You try to get up, but no matter how much you \"bets you\" someone that you can get up, you slide back down the flowers net. \"I bets you I can do it next time,\" you say.",
                "mnemonic": "Every time you receive {tooltip:Kanji:scorn} and {tooltip:Kanji:neglect} from someone walking by, you say in your drunken voice: \"I {tooltip:Reading:bets you} ({span:lang=ja:\u3079\u3064}) I can get up if I want. I bets you I can.\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} that's heading for your village is {tooltip:Radical:fat} you should try to {tooltip:Kanji:select} a different one to hit instead. You don't want to select fat tsunamis because they do more damage.",
            "hints": "Imagine being at the tsunami store and selecting the least fat one there.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Select"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f, \u305f\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304a\u3054, \u306b\u3054, \u3088\u306a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "While you select the tsunami that's right for you. Keep an eye out for those fat taco-eating ones. And then stay away from them!",
                "mnemonic": "If you're having trouble {tooltip:Kanji:select}ing which one is the least fat just check to see which tsunamis are eating {tooltip:Reading:ta}cos ({span:lang=ja:\u305f}). Only fat tsunamis will be eating them, so just look for one without a taco."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Move {tooltip:Radical:thread} in the right {tooltip:Radical:direction} and you'll end up {tooltip:Kanji:spinning} it into yarn. Then you can spin that yarn into a sweater or a scarf with your favorite half tofu half fugu mascot on it!",
            "hints": "Imagine spinning thread into whatever your imagination wants.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Spinning",
                "Alternative": "Spin"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3080",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Picture all of these thread-made bowling items. You're a really big bowling fan, huh?",
                "mnemonic": "While you're {tooltip:Kanji:spinning} you realize that you've always wanted to make your own {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) ball. And bowling ball cover. And bowling ball shoes."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Going from a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} to a {tooltip:Radical:helicopter} that's {tooltip:Radical:big} even for yourself ({tooltip:Radical:oneself}), is huge {tooltip:Kanji:transition}.",
            "hints": "It's an upward transition, so that's nice, but it's still going to take you a long time to get used to using a big helicopter instead of a scooter.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Transition"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u3064, \u307f\u3084\u3053\u304c\u3048",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "A centaur is just a human halfway between transitioning into a horse, so it isn't even that hard to do!",
                "mnemonic": "You decide one {tooltip:Kanji:transition} isn't enough, so you transition to a {tooltip:Reading:cen}taur ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3093}) too. Now you're a big half horse-half human creature and you'll fit in the big helicopter better."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "There were lots of things that were {tooltip:Radical:above} you when you were {tooltip:Radical:small} that you would need a {tooltip:Radical:stool} to reach, so you just asked your {tooltip:Kanji:aunt} or {tooltip:Kanji:uncle} to get them for you.",
            "hints": "Your parents didn't want you having those things, which is why they put them up high, but your aunt and uncle would always spoil you and get them for you.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Uncle",
                "Alternative": "Aunt"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "\u304a",
                        "primary": true
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You aren't supposed to wear your obi unless it's a special occasion, but your aunt and uncle don't know that. Now you can run around with it on your head and your parents can't stop you by putting it up high!",
                "mnemonic": "You ask your {tooltip:Kanji:aunt} and {tooltip:Kanji:uncle} to help you reach your special {tooltip:Reading:o}bi ({span:lang=ja:\u304a}) from high up in the closet. "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Making a mnemonic for a {tooltip:Radical:crab trap} is {tooltip:Kanji:VERY} hard. So hard that I couldn't come up with one. But it's very possible that one of you will!",
            "hints": "How hard is it to come up with a good mnemonic for a crab trap? Very hard!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Very",
                "Alternative": "Great"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u306a\u306f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "How many sentences can you make with very and jeans? More than me I hope.",
                "mnemonic": "You know what else is {tooltip:Kanji:very} something? {tooltip:Reading:Jean}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3093}). Jeans are very expensive. Jeans are very tight. Jeans are very popular. Jeans are very a lot of things."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} that is {tooltip:Radical:good}. This fabled creature has never been seen, but you {tooltip:Kanji:wander} the lands in search of it.",
            "hints": "You wander everywhere, with no particular direction in mind.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Wander"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Wherever the good tsunami goes, it leaves delicious fish roe behind. That's what makes it a good tsunami.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:wander}, you come across a clue. It is fish {tooltip:Reading:roe} ({span:lang=ja:\u308d\u3046}). "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under the {tooltip:Radical:mountain}'s {tooltip:Radical:roof} are people using {tooltip:Radical:jackhammer}s to {tooltip:Kanji:worship} the gods. The noise from their jackhammering echos up through the mountain and up toward the sky where the gods live. As long as each person uses their own jackhammer, the sound will be loud enough to reach them.",
            "hints": "Man your own jackhammer! (And worship the gods.)",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Worship",
                "Alternative": "Revere"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3059\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u304c",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You try to argue that you can't sue someone for the way they choose to worship, but they say they're all deaf now, all the animals have gone, and no one sleeps anymore because of the shaking. Yikes, they might have a case!",
                "mnemonic": "Unfortunately, the people who live around here can also hear you and the others {tooltip:Kanji:worship} in the mountain and they're going to {tooltip:Reading:sue} ({span:lang=ja:\u3059\u3046}) you for the noise. "
            }
        }

{
