{
            "mnemonic": "You should {tooltip:Kanji:congratulate} a person who speaks lots of {tooltip:Kanji:dialect}s because they have to be a really {tooltip:Vocabulary:strong person}, just like Mr. {tooltip:Vocabulary:Benkei} was. You think learning Japanese is hard now, just wait till you hear Osaka-ben and Hokkaido-ben. It takes a really strong person \u2014 a Benkei \u2014 to learn all those dialects, so congratulate them and tell them how strong they are!",
            "hints": "",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Benkei",
                "Alternative": "Strong Person",
