                "mnemonic": "\n{splitParent}Since this word consists of a kanji with hiragana attached, you can bet that it will use the kun'yomi reading. You didn't learn that reading with this kanji, so here's a mnemonic to help you: \n{splitParent}Your mourning is especially {tooltip:Vocabulary:unpleasant} because it's your pet {tooltip:Reading:ea}gle ({span:lang=ja:\u3044}) you're mourning for. Your parents wouldn't let you bury him so you're just staring at his week old, dead eagle body. It's super {tooltip:Vocabulary:disgusting}, actually.\n"
