                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Look at that guy now. What a loser.",
                "mnemonic": "Once you {tooltip:Kanji:censure} them and they lose all their power, they'll be just another {tooltip:Reading:guy} ({span:lang=ja:\u304c\u3044}). A normal guy with everything lost to him. HAHAHA!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you think a {tooltip:Radical:tree} looks {tooltip:Radical:sweet} you have to be {tooltip:Kanji:certain} before you bite into it. Trees are really hard, and usually pretty bitter (believe me) so if you don't want a mouthful of broken teeth, sap, and sadness, you really need to be sure it's the one before you start munching.",
            "hints": "Which tree do you think is sweet? That one? Or that one? Are you absolutely certain? I hope you are!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Certain",
                "Alternatives": "One, That Person"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u308c\u304c\u3057, \u306a\u306b\u304c\u3057",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "So now let me ask you again, are you certain, or would you like to try the bowling ball test?",
                "mnemonic": "If you really want to be {tooltip:Kanji:certain}, and not just guess, take out your {tooltip:Reading:bow}ling ({span:lang=ja:\u307c\u3046}) ball and roll it as hard as you can into the tree. If its the right one it will let out a sweet smell, if it's not the tree will punch you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "An {tooltip:Radical:arrow }is shot from {tooltip:Radical:heaven} and hits right between your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} and your {tooltip:Radical:mustache} to {tooltip:Kanji:correct} your crooked smile. It also {tooltip:Kanji:straighten}s your teeth and the crooked cut of your mustache too. Who told you that looked good? Well, it doesn't matter. The heaven arrow corrected it for you.",
            "hints": "An arrow from heaven will correct all your problems!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Correct",
                "Alternative": "Straighten"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "If you want someone to correct your teeth or mustache, just wander around {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}, staring up at the sky. Then when you see an arrow, run for it and try to catch it with your face!",
                "mnemonic": "These heavenly {tooltip:Kanji:correct}ing arrows actually come from {span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3087\u3046\u3068}. They hate seeing people with crooked mustaches, so they shoot them out on the regular. It just looks like they're coming from heaven because they fall out of the sky."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Inside this giant {tooltip:Radical:mouth} is a {tooltip:Radical:person}, trapped, because they're a {tooltip:Kanji:criminal}. They did something bad (they touched the mouth of another person without consent) and now they're in mouth jail for criminals.",
            "hints": "Picture the criminal, trapped inside the mouth. They don't even look sorry!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Criminal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
