                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You learned this reed technique from a group of ninjas who use them to breathe underwater, and you never thought you'd use them like this.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:diarrhea} is here. It's happening. And it smells so awful you can't breathe. You have to take some hollow {tooltip:Reading:reed}s ({span:lang=ja:\u308a}) and shove them up your nose and out the bathroom door so you can get some fresh air in you."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If you ride a {tooltip:Radical:scooter} with your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} around an {tooltip:Radical:axe} you're going to {tooltip:Kanji:die}. I mean, probably. There's a 99% chance you'll die.",
            "hints": "Picture someone else riding a scooter with an axe in their fingertips. That's so dangerous! One bump, one bad turn, and that axe slips and they'll die.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Die"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305b\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3044, \u3086",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Your holy blue saber died for you. It saved you from certain death and now it died. After all you've been through together. All 60 levels. This is the end.",
                "mnemonic": "You slip. The axe collides with your face. You {tooltip:Kanji:die}. But... wait! There's a bright, blue glow and suddenly you're un-dead. You watch in slow motion as your holy blue {tooltip:Reading:sa}ber ({span:lang=ja:\u305b\u3044}) brings you back to life and takes the hit from the axe instead."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:animal} that hangs out in {tooltip:Radical:melon} patches is the elusive {tooltip:Kanji:fox}! They like to steal melons then come back into town disguised as human melon sellers. Foxes are tricky like that.",
            "hints": "Imagine seeing a red fox scampering through a melon patch trying to take melons with it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Fox"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
