                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304d\u3064\u306d",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine buying kits that neigh and putting them around your melon patch to warn you when foxes are around.",
                "mnemonic": "If you want to stop {tooltip:Kanji:fox}es from stealing your melons you can get one of those {tooltip:Reading:kits} that {tooltip:Reading:neigh} ({span:lang=ja:\u304d\u3064\u306d}) when one is around. The kits neigh when they sense a fox, but because it sounds like a horse the fox won't run. But you'll be able to get out there and take your melons back!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're stuck in your {tooltip:Radical:car} during a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} and all you have to break out is an {tooltip:Radical:axe}. You whack and whack but you're only {tooltip:Kanji:gradually} making progress. You thought an axe would be an easy way to get out of a car but it's not working like you'd planned! You have to make more than gradual progress if you don't want to drown. ",
            "hints": "Imagine gradually denting your car door open with an axe while you're trapped in a tsunami. This isn't fast enough! ",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Gradually",
                "Alternative": "Steadily"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305c\u3093",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3088\u3046\u3084, \u3084\u3084",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "YO YANKEES! Gradually yelling that saved your life!",
                "mnemonic": "As you're {tooltip:Kanji:gradually} making your door open with the axe you look up to see the New York Yankees floating by on top of their bus. You yell, \"{tooltip:Reading:YO YA}NKEES ({span:lang=ja:\u3088\u3046\u3084}) to get their attention. They see your gradual progress and start throwing balls at your car to help dent it open."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You see {tooltip:Radical:twenty} {tooltip:Radical:slide}s lined up like a {tooltip:Kanji:grid}. You don't know who put them here, but they almost look like the grid paper you do your maths homework in. But who would use a slide as grid paper?",
            "hints": "Picture twenty slides laid out in a grid system.",
