                    }
                ],
                "hints": "\"N-no?\" you respond. \"Wrong! I hid all the time. There's nothing wrong with hiding, you're doing a great job.\" he says, and disappears.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:hide} the ghost of {tooltip:Reading:Toku}gawa ({span:lang=ja:\u3068\u304f}) Ieyasu appears before you, inside the cage! His arms are crossed and he's shaking his head at you. \"Do you think I managed to become the first shougun of Japan by hiding?\""
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You {tooltip:Radical:say} something to a {tooltip:Radical:boot} when you want to be {tooltip:Kanji:humble}. You're down there because you're bowing in front of the person you're humbling yourself before. Because of that, your face is really close to their boots and you're speaking directly at them, instead of at the person's face, so it's more {tooltip:Kanji:discreet}.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself trying to be humble. You're down on the ground talking to a pair of boots. You don't dare raise your eyes past that.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Humble",
                "Alternative": "Discreet"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
