        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Put a {tooltip:Radical:yakuza} member in a {tooltip:Radical:prison} on the {tooltip:Radical:sun} and he'll become a {tooltip:Kanji:martyr} to all the other yakuza still on earth. He died up there so the rest of them wouldn't have to. Because they definitely aren't getting caught now, if the penalty is a burning death in the new sun prison.",
            "hints": "Imagine all the yakuza coming out into the streets and holding up signs saying this guy was a martyr. A hero to all who do bad stuff in bad groups but don't wanna get caught.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Martyr"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3058\u3085\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Really, it's not the fault of the people who put him there that he's become a martyr. It's the month of June. PUNISH JUNE! PUT JUNE IN THE SUN PRISON! (Is what I assume those yakuza are shouting.)",
                "mnemonic": "The only reason he ended up a {tooltip:Kanji:martyr} in the first place is because they put him up there in {tooltip:Reading:June} ({span:lang=ja:\u3058\u3085\u3093}). Everyone knows the sun is way too hot for humans in June. It's summer!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "In the {tooltip:Radical:dirt}, you find a {tooltip:Radical:lid} under the {tooltip:Radical:table}. You lift it to reveal a deep {tooltip:Kanji:pit}. Why is there a {tooltip:Kanji:hole} under your table?",
            "hints": "You pull away the lid and crawl inside. There is a ladder that takes you deep into the pit.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Pit",
                "Alternative": "Hole"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3053\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "After you've nursed {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} back to health, he explains that he was put here by a clone {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}\u2013the very same {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061} who became emperor. He tells you he can think of around 61-70 different pain levels of revenge, but also that \"it probably wouldn't be worth it, so let's just hang out for a while instead. Ooh, are those cookies?\"",
                "mnemonic": "When you reach the bottom of the {tooltip:Kanji:pit}, you hear someone scuffling around and the sounds of chains. You light a match and inch closer to see what it is. In the darkness, you see {span:lang=ja:\u3053\u3046\u3044\u3061}, starved and chained in a pit under your table."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're in a {tooltip:Radical:net} but you have the {tooltip:Radical:ability} to quit playing along and {tooltip:Kanji:leave} at any time. ",
            "hints": "Your captors think they have you trapped, but you know you can leave whenever you feel like it.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Quit",
                "Alternative": "Leave"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3084",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "As the heat spreads you decide to leave. You hop out of the net and watch the shock spread in your captors eyes.",
                "mnemonic": "You don't know if you want to {tooltip:Kanji:quit} this charade until you feel an uncomfortable {tooltip:Reading:hea}t ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}). You look down and the net you're in is being hung above a large fire."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "If the {tooltip:Radical:death} of a {tooltip:Radical:woman} occurs it's because she was being {tooltip:Kanji:reckless}. People don't just die out of nowhere! They have to have done something super crazy to cause it. Right? Yes... right.",
            "hints": "Picture yourself watching the news about a woman's death. The word RECKLESS?! pops up on your screen and keeps flashing. Huh, she must have been, you think to yourself.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Reckless"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082\u3046, \u307c\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307f\u3060",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine what reckless thing that woman had to have done to die while mowing the lawn. Eww.",
                "mnemonic": "As you watch the news about this {tooltip:Kanji:reckless} woman you find out that she died from {tooltip:Reading:mow}ing ({span:lang=ja:\u3082\u3046}) her lawn. You're not sure how, but now you really believe that she had to be doing it really recklessly to die doing it."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:flowers} that wash up on shore in {tooltip:Radical:tsunami}s that we make into {tooltip:Radical:syrup} is {tooltip:Kanji:seaweed}. Okay, so it's more like soup or tea than syrup, but you can make them both out of seaweed.",
            "hints": "Seaweed is the flower of the sea!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Seaweed"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305d\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3082",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Feed your soul with seaweed and it will thank you. Promise! <3",
                "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Kanji:Seaweed} is true {tooltip:Reading:sou}l ({span:lang=ja:\u305d\u3046}) food. Which means it's good for your soul. Didn't you ever read those books about chicken soup being good for your soul? Well that was a lie. Miso soup with seaweed is what's really good for your soul."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Tsunami}'s have a {tooltip:Radical:certain} tendency to {tooltip:Kanji:secrete} things as they go back out to sea. When they bash themselves onto the land they just throw a bunch of sea water around, but there are only certain things that they'll secrete when they're leaving.",
            "hints": "Certain tsunami secretions are dangerous. Can you think of any?",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Secrete"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3072, \u3072\u3064",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The next time someone asks you what does a tsunami secrete? You'll say heat!",
                "mnemonic": "Most tsunami's {tooltip:Kanji:secrete} {tooltip:Reading:he}at ({span:lang=ja:\u3072}). It takes a lot of energy for a tsunami to crash onto the land so the water is really really hot, and it has to secrete that heat as it's going back out to sea."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Use your {tooltip:Radical:mouth} to sing and a {tooltip:Radical:shellfish} to stroke your shamisen, and you'll be performing a {tooltip:Kanji:shamisen song} just like that! Yes, it's that easy. Just go find a shell, open your mouth, and you'll be singing one too in no time!",
            "hints": "Imagine using your mouth to sing and a shell to play the shamisen to perform your shamisen song!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shamisen Song"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3070\u3044",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3046\u305f",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "A shamisen song is a song, yay!",
                "mnemonic": "A {tooltip:Kanji:shamisen song} is just an {span:lang=ja:\u6b4c} ({span:lang=ja:\u3046\u305f}) but with a shamisen. They're still songs so they're said the exact same way!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "{tooltip:Radical:Half} of a {tooltip:Radical:rice paddy} is always on the {tooltip:Kanji:shore}. Japan is surrounded by water, after all. So it only makes sense that half of every rice paddy is right next to the ocean shore, right?",
            "hints": "Picture a rice paddy. Half of it is trailing off into the shore. Hear the seagulls. Feel the ocean breeze!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Shore"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u306f\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3042\u305c, \u304f\u308d, \u307b\u3068\u308a",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine laying on the shore with Han Solo. Enjoying a cool drink. Smelling the fragrance of the rice paddy behind you. Yeah, this is the life!",
                "mnemonic": "You decide to walk along this {tooltip:Kanji:shore} when you see {tooltip:Reading:Han} ({span:lang=ja:\u306f\u3093}) Solo lounging in the sand. He's waving for you to join him! You get to lay on the shore with Han!!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:leader} {tooltip:Radical:squid} tells all of its squid people to be {tooltip:Kanji:thrifty}.",
            "hints": "Imagine the leader squid giving a speech about how you shouldn't buy new things, and how you should live with a roommate to save money. Every squid yen counts!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Thrifty",
                "Alternative": "Frugal"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3093",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3064\u3065\u307e\u3084\u304b, \u3064\u307e",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Ken's squid is always shaking his head at Ken the samurai's obsession with wearing all silk. He should visit Thrifty Threads, the second hand shop, and get some cotton clothes that would do the job just fine.{splitParent}Hint: Whenever there's a squid, remember that Ken ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai is nearby.",
                "mnemonic": "Who is a {tooltip:Kanji:thrifty} squid? {tooltip:Reading:Ken} ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3093}) the samurai's squid buddy, who gets carried around in a bucket and never pays rent."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You put your {tooltip:Radical:fingers} in the {tooltip:Radical:coffin} to tickle the {tooltip:Radical:beggar} inside. What you're doing is a new form of {tooltip:Kanji:torture}.",
            "hints": "First, you put them in a coffin to make them think they're going to die. Then you tickle them with your fingers. There is no greater psychological + physical torture than this.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Torture"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3054\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "He keeps screaming: \"STOP THIS TICKLE TORTURE. I CAN'T TAKE IT JUST BURY ME.\"",
                "mnemonic": "The beggar you will coffin tickle {tooltip:Kanji:torture} is {span:lang=ja:\u3054\u3046\u3044\u3061}, a.k.a. Grandpa Koichi. He is a frail old man, and doesn't like to be tickled."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Give {tooltip:Radical:alcohol} to a {tooltip:Radical:demon} and you'll see how {tooltip:Kanji:ugly} it really is. Demons need to concentrate to keep their disguises going. Even if it looked pretty when you met it, like super handsome, give it a few drinks and its facade will slide off and reveal its super gross demon face.",
            "hints": "Picture the drunk demon as its pretty face drips off revealing the ugly crap piled underneath.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Ugly"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3085\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u3053, \u307f\u306b\u304f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "The demon drinking alcohol out of its nasty shoes is the ugliest scene you've ever seen.",
                "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Kanji:ugly} demon is drunk and taking off his {tooltip:Reading:shoe}s ({span:lang=ja:\u3057\u3085\u3046}) and swinging them around his head. And, oh no, he's drinking more alcohol out of the shoes."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Your {tooltip:Radical:forehead} is in the {tooltip:Radical:sun}, and you start seeing those creatures with {tooltip:Radical:lid}s for heads and  {tooltip:Radical:fins} for feet again. Where on earth did they come from? They must have come from the {tooltip:Kanji:underworld}. Nothing like that exists in this life.",
            "hints": "Imagine the heat of the sun on your forehead as you watch these horrible creatures with lid-heads and fin-feet. There's no doubt that these are creatures from the underworld. You get out of the sun as fast as you can.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Underworld"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3081\u3044, \u307f\u3087\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "You make a mental note to always avoid the sun in May.\n",
                "mnemonic": "The sun is unusually hot for the month of {tooltip:Reading:May} ({span:lang=ja:\u3081\u3044}), which must be why those underworld creatures are running around."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "The {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} swept away one of the {tooltip:Radical:cleat}s your {tooltip:Radical:husband} just bought and creates an entire {tooltip:Kanji:valley} with it.",
            "hints": "Watch as the tsunami rakes your husband's cleat across the mountain, carving a valley and an easier path for itself. Nature is brutal.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Valley"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3051\u3044",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u305f\u306b, \u305f\u306b\u304c\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Imagine yourself eating cake with your husband in this newly formed valley. You both agree that this should be called Cake Valley!",
                "mnemonic": "When the water clears, you and your husband go to the {tooltip:Kanji:valley} to look for the cleat and instead you find a bunch of {tooltip:Reading:ca}ke ({span:lang=ja:\u3051\u3044})! Maybe this is the tsunami's way of saying, \"Thanks for letting me steal your cleat so I could make this valley shortcut.\" "
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "When you see a {tooltip:Radical:tsunami} coming {tooltip:Radical:courage} {tooltip:Kanji:well}s up inside you and you gain the power to save everyone you meet before they get washed away! Feel that courage {tooltip:Kanji:boil} and spread throughout all your limbs. You feel like you have super strength. This tsunami isn't going to hurt anyone while you're alive to stop it!",
            "hints": "Imagine what it feels like to have courage well up inside you. Courage in the face of certain death!",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Well",
                "Alternative": "Boil"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3086\u3046, \u3086, \u3088\u3046",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u308f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Who wells up with courage? You do!",
                "mnemonic": "Who does that courage {tooltip:Kanji:well} up inside? {tooltip:Reading:You} ({span:lang=ja:\u3086\u3046})! In fact, YOU feel like there is a never ending well of courage bursting out of you now. You are going to be a hero!"
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "Under your own {tooltip:Radical:roof}, a {tooltip:Radical:geoduck} jumps out of the {tooltip:Radical:ground} with a {tooltip:Radical:sword} and stabs your husband/wife/marriage partner to death. Now you're a {tooltip:Kanji:widow}.",
            "hints": "Imagine the geoduck laughing and screaming, \"Now you're a widow! Now you're a widow!\" flailing the sword around. It's awful.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Widow"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u304b",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "It's just you and your car now, living the widow life, driving on into the sunset and forgetting your past.",
                "mnemonic": "You may be a {tooltip:Kanji:widow}, but that doesn't make you weak. You run outside, jump into your {tooltip:Reading:ca}r ({span:lang=ja:\u304b}), and run your entire house and the geoduck over."
            }
        }

{
            "mnemonic": "You're walking in a {tooltip:Radical:greenhouse} when you see a {tooltip:Radical:small} {tooltip:Radical:drop} of water fall and it makes you {tooltip:Kanji:yearn for} the person you {tooltip:Kanji:adore}. You haven't seen them in so long. But something about being in this greenhouse and seeing that tiny water droplet made your heart burst with longing. ",
            "hints": "Imagine how it feels to yearn for someone else when you see the small water drop. Imagine how your heart feels.",
            "meanings": {
                "Primary": "Yearn For",
                "Alternative": "Adore"
            },
            "kanjiReadings": {
                "readings": [
                    {
                        "name": "On\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u307c",
                        "primary": true
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Kun\u2019yomi",
                        "reading": "\u3057\u305f",
                        "primary": false
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Nanori",
                        "reading": "None",
                        "primary": false
                    }
                ],
                "hints": "Now you yearn for being somewhere Bobo is not.",
                "mnemonic": "As you {tooltip:Kanji:yearn for} that person from your past, you look back at the drop and see... {tooltip:Reading:Bo}bo ({span:lang=ja:\u307c}) the clown?! Uhg. Apparently Bobo dropped that small drop of water."
            }
        }

{
